Alan Osborne,/users/56eef3cb0000ff000a1054a9,GB,35.0,2024-09-08 21:53:06+00:00,1.0,Have Amazon no sense of responsibility for Sub Suppliers,"I never use Amazon because of a bad experience several years ago (Hair Dryer burst into flames and Amazon didn't want to know). However, my daughter has used Amazon consistantly, being reasonably satisfied. However, experience this week has changed her opinion. She ordered a Power Washer. When it arrived, the cardboard box it was in appeared to have been opened and very roughly resealed. On opening the box, two of the main components were missing, namely the gun and handle. On phoning Amazon, we were told that we had to deal directly with the supplier. Complaining about this, after over 40 minutes on the phone, we got a promise of a refund. We asked for that to be confirmed in an email. Email arrived stating we had to deal directly with supplier! Phoned back but got nowhere. You would have thought that, considering the disgraceful condition the Washer was delivered in, Amazon would have wanted to be involved.",2024-09-08 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,8.0,922,158,56,9,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,never use amazon bad experience several year ago hair dryer burst flame amazon didnt want know however daughter used amazon consistantly reasonably satisfied however experience week changed opinion ordered power washer arrived cardboard box appeared opened roughly resealed opening box two main component missing namely gun handle phoning amazon told deal directly supplier complaining minute phone got promise refund asked confirmed email email arrived stating deal directly supplier phoned back got nowhere would thought considering disgraceful condition washer delivered amazon would wanted involved,0.07841248769814176,0.9215875123018582,0.0886146943353898,0.2,0.778516695018007,77.8516695018007,High Trust
