Unfiltered Unfiltered by ME,/users/66e3819222038d6026335464,PR,1.0,2024-09-13 02:04:42+00:00,1.0,I didn’t want to give any stars,"I didn’t want to give any stars; however I gave 1 because it was the only option I had. A third party where a family member resides in Florida about 2 months ago as a favor purchased 2 items I had asked my son to purchase for me. I sent the Photographs so he would know what items they were. I didn’t have knowledge that they would both be purchased at Amazon. They were a Tough Light 400 and an Eton Emergency Radio. I only know that my son indicated that the lamp was double the price advertised, no issue with the price of the Eton Radio. The items were carefully packaged with Bubble wrap and foam and mailed to me in Puerto Rico. Upon arrival, the Tough Light 400 although it looked perfect never turned on. I followed the advice of the manufacturer and nothing worked. The radio was operating well, however I noticed that there were scuff marks on one side and the screw where the Lithium battery was looked like it had been tampered with. I called Amazon first since I didn’t have a receipt or the address where the products were shipped to. Amazon immediately responded that I had to have proof of purchase to return and that after 30 days I needed to take the issue to the manufacture. Tough Light never responded to a message I left them and after sending an email expressing the diverse issues, there position was that in order to return and replace I needed to have proof of purchase. I know that every product sold has a unique number and ToughLight could have easily verified if the product I have was sold through Amazon m. That ended the story! However, the Eton Radio was not charging properly solar or with furnished plug to charge in an electrical outlet. The response was 180 degrees from Amazon and ToughLight! I explained the predicament I was in; not having proof of purchase and not acquainted with the person who purchased the products. People are reluctant to furnish credit card information to a person they don’t know, but I am very grateful for the gesture regardless. Eton, simply requested my address and committed to sending a shipping label. After they receive the Radio, they will send a new product. Therefore, my first experience with Amazon and last… I don’t have an exact date, however I do know the products were purchased and sent to me about a few weeks afterwards. By the time I got around to opening the package, my guesstimate is that 1 and 1/2 to 2 months time period from this date. ",2024-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,13.0,2429,442,31,7,59.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,didn’t want give star however gave option third party family member resides florida month ago favor purchased item asked son purchase sent photograph would know item didn’t knowledge would purchased amazon tough light eton emergency radio know son indicated lamp double price advertised issue price eton radio item carefully packaged bubble wrap foam mailed puerto rico upon arrival tough light although looked perfect never turned followed advice manufacturer nothing worked radio operating well however noticed scuff mark one side screw lithium battery looked like tampered called amazon first since didn’t receipt address product shipped amazon immediately responded proof purchase return day needed take issue manufacture tough light never responded message left sending email expressing diverse issue position order return replace needed proof purchase know every product sold unique number toughlight could easily verified product sold amazon ended story however eton radio charging properly solar furnished plug charge electrical outlet response degree amazon toughlight explained predicament proof purchase acquainted person purchased product people reluctant furnish credit card information person don’t know grateful gesture regardless eton simply requested address committed sending shipping label receive radio send new product therefore first experi