Brenda Takko,/users/657aac3e30352f00112fe73a,US,3.0,2024-09-03 21:07:07+00:00,1.0,Customer Relations Failure,"The Amazon customer service I received today was one of too many unsatisfactory experiences with their representatives. Amazon's failure to provide reasonable responses or solutions to my issues has been a big problem for me and countless other angry and disappointed customers. Their non-refundable food and pet food, or easily replaceable damaged item/s policies are examples of many unfavorable reasons why I have ended my Prime membership and chosen to shop elsewhere. Hopefully, other dissatisfied customers will follow my lead and cancel their Prime membership. Do yourself and local businesses a big favor. Stop feeding the machine. CANCEL AMAZON NOW! You will be so glad you did. THANK YOU! Dissatisfied Customer.",2024-09-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,3.0,721,111,26,3,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer service received today one many unsatisfactory experience representative amazon failure provide reasonable response solution issue big problem countless angry disappointed customer nonrefundable food pet food easily replaceable damaged item policy example many unfavorable reason ended prime membership chosen shop elsewhere hopefully dissatisfied customer follow lead cancel prime membership local business big favor stop feeding machine cancel amazon glad thank dissatisfied customer,0.31192032051700097,0.6880796794829991,0.062254627033090294,0.2,0.6564907651481175,65.64907651481175,Medium Trust
Terry Wiltorn,/users/5570609e0000ff0001c3af67,GB,25.0,2024-09-03 17:56:44+00:00,1.0,Dangerous and disinterested ,"Whilst connecting a smart TV to the ‘in built’ Amazon Prime, I was asked to go to Amazontv. on doing this I was directed to another page which asked me to call 08003213437. A individual answered and started to give me pass codes, then started to ask me about renewing prime for 2 years at a reduced rate. I became very concerned at this and hung up. When opening my email there was one, allegedly from amazon, thanking me for purchasing a £70 gift card, on checking my account I noticed 2 items in the basket, gift card at £70 and a game boy at £100. I immediately removed these, changed my password and attempted to contact customer service, impossible to find a phone number so ended up on their chat, this is when the problem really started, transferred 4 times eventually told not to answer any emails or txt , nothing remotely to do with my problem. After 59 minutes I gave up. So please use extreme caution as this appears to be a rather complex scam. Incidentally, I never gave any passwords or bank details.",2024-09-02 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,3.0,1015,187,28,3,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,whilst connecting smart tv ‘in built’ amazon prime asked go amazontv directed another page asked call individual answered started give pas code started ask renewing prime year reduced rate became concerned hung opening email one allegedly amazon thanking purchasing £ gift card checking account noticed item basket gift card £ game boy £ immediately removed changed password attempted contact customer service impossible find phone number ended chat problem really started transferred time eventually told answer email txt nothing remotely problem minute gave please use extreme caution appears rather complex scam incidentally never gave password bank detail,0.045773929078222114,0.9542260709217779,0.10487941671340438,0.2,0.7980889188035698,79.80889188035698,High Trust
Chris Rogers,/users/55283a720000ff0001b7845b,GB,28.0,2024-09-03 17:46:49+00:00,2.0,Prime delivery isn't prime,"Delivery is appalling these days. Items stolen due to being left on doorstep, constant changes to estimated delivery times, and the number of items stated next day for prime members that end up being delivered 2 or 3 days later. Standards have really gone downhill.",2024-09-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,3.0,265,45,26,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,delivery appalling day item stolen due left doorstep constant change estimated delivery time number item stated next day prime member end delivered day later standard really gone downhill,0.020844245181501846,0.9791557548184981,0.025238362310712283,0.4,1.0946255498713915,109.46255498713914,High Trust
Chris,/users/628d473ca677f30012ecd6c2,GB,5.0,2024-09-03 17:23:11+00:00,2.0,Definitely not what it used to be.,"I have been an Amazon customer for more than twenty years. I was usually happy with the service but recent experiences have given me pause. For example, I recently ordered a time sensitive spare timer  to control my immersion heater and was not once, but twice delivered the wrong item (despite assurances by the increasingly inept customer service it wouldn’t happen again). To round it off the replacement order was delayed. I guess we are sort of stuck with Amazon but I would encourage everyone to consider buying at other shops as well or Amazon’s dominance will only increase and with it our dependence on this one company.",2024-09-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,9.0,3.0,629,108,34,7,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon customer twenty year usually happy service recent experience given pause example recently ordered time sensitive spare timer control immersion heater twice delivered wrong item despite assurance increasingly inept customer service wouldn’t happen round replacement order delayed guess sort stuck amazon would encourage everyone consider buying shop well amazon’s dominance increase dependence one company,0.020045582180077074,0.9799544178199229,0.06057206954570948,0.4,1.1020916228191033,110.20916228191034,High Trust
