A.B,/users/66c206bd8a6e868a5fab515c,US,1.0,2024-08-18 16:46:11+00:00,1.0,"Used to be my go-to for books and movies, now unuseable.","Amazon, which was once the most convenient services on the internet, has become almost completely unusable. You pay monthly fee for faster shipping, but then theres a 99% chance your item will be damaged from mishandling by drivers / shippers, or were in damaged, unsellable condition to begin with. I've seen drivers throw packages at people's doors! Shippers dont bother to even think about what they're packing so there will be insufficient padding to protect from drivers' mishandling or their intentional damage when throwing items. I cant order anything that i want to arrive in brand new unbroken condition. The only things i can order are things that can handle a little bit of a beating in transit, but thats barely anything. Order a ""brand new"" blu ray, receive a previously opened blu ray that was shrinkwrapped and melted with a heat gun. Order a brand new book, get a book that was completely destroyed from bouncing around in a box 3x its size with no padding or all messed up from being in a soft bubble wrap envelope, and that is if they arent completely destroyed by the shipper/fullfillment center. Believe it or not, but amazon used to have special packaging for books and movies so that they dont get damaged but nobody in this self-serving megacorporation cares anymore. 98% of items are off-brand chinese products that belong at a 99 cent store that are priced as high as the real brand-name products they're disguising themselves as. These products break either right away or very shortly after return windows. They typically ship with some type of offer for gift cards in exchange for reviews, padding up the reviews of their inferior products. The product page makes them appear as a brand name product, but the item comes in a generic unsealed box. You would get better at five below but it was priced at $40. This is pretty much the entire store. Trusted brands with names like, ""gOOprOO"", ""WYdaiBother"" are amazons recommended choice. It is no longer worth doing business with amazon, who are obviously unwilling to address the issues customers are complaining about with a too-big-to-fail attitude. If they continue operating like this and are incapable of listening to their customers they should deservedly go under. This is not a company that consumers should do business with.",2024-07-30 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,8.0,18.0,2309,389,56,11,19.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,amazon convenient service internet become almost completely unusable pay monthly fee faster shipping there chance item damaged mishandling driver shipper damaged unsellable condition begin ive seen driver throw package people door shipper dont bother even think theyre packing insufficient padding protect driver mishandling intentional damage throwing item cant order anything want arrive brand new unbroken condition thing order thing handle little bit beating transit thats barely anything order brand new blu ray receive previously opened blu ray shrinkwrapped melted heat gun order brand new book get book completely destroyed bouncing around box x size padding messed soft bubble wrap envelope arent completely destroyed shipperfullfillment center believe amazon used special packaging book movie dont get damaged nobody selfserving megacorporation care anymore item offbrand chinese product belong cent store priced high real brandname product theyre disguising product break either right away shortly return window typically ship type offer gift card exchange review padding review inferior product product page make appear brand name product item come generic unsealed box would get better five priced pretty much entire store trusted brand name like gooproo wydaibother amazon recommended choice longer worth business amazon obviously unwilling address issue customer complaining toobigtofail attitude continue operating like incapable listening customer deservedly go company consumer business,0.007818249788751772,0.9921817502112482,0.21817162086371283,0.2,0.8397251992783668,83.97251992783667,High Trust
SandyG,/users/64fdeb935e734d0011224412,US,4.0,2024-08-18 14:16:22+00:00,1.0,"Sold used, gray market broken laptop","We called HP, and found out Amazon sold us a gray market used laptop. HP will not honor the warranty, because it apparenty has been modified outside of the HP's technical specifications, which is why the computer is crashing all the time. HP tech told me this computer will not work with 32 gigs of ram. HP said it is only built to handle 16 gigs of ram. It also apparently is pre-owned, since the bitlocker key is on the previous owner's microsoft account. My microsoft account showed no bitlocker key. HP was kind enough to reset everything from the previous owner, even though I had no warranty. I knew nothing of this until we called HP's tech support. They are concerned and will be investigating these gray market HP laptops through Amazon. These laptops should never be modified; Amazon is breaking them by messing with the technology.In the mean time, I am returning this laptop. THEY SOLD ME A USED COMPUTER THAT THEY MODIFIED (in direct violation of HP's technical specifications) TO CAUSE CONSTANT CRASHING!!!! Amazon's a bunch of crooks. ",2024-08-17 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,8.0,18.0,1050,181,36,6,1.0,0,4,2,1,Suspicious,called hp found amazon sold u gray market used laptop hp honor warranty apparenty modified outside hp technical specification computer crashing time hp tech told computer work gig ram hp said built handle gig ram also apparently preowned since bitlocker key previous owner microsoft account microsoft account showed bitlocker key hp kind enough reset everything previous owner even though warranty knew nothing called hp tech support concerned investigating gray market hp laptop amazon laptop never modified amazon breaking messing technologyin mean time returning laptop sold used computer modified direct violation hp technical specification cause constant crashing amazon bunch crook,0.9453475493757818,0.054652450624218196,0.10151430173864273,0.2,0.34762908565983763,34.762908565983764,Low Trust
