From Maine,/users/669d8eda9e4801782efa738c,US,2.0,2024-07-26 11:36:37+00:00,1.0,Amazon is demanding all my personal info.,"Amazon ""Limited"" my account after I updated my credit card information and placed a small order.  They cancelled the order and sent a weird email to ""verify my account""They need a picture of my drivers license, a bank statement, credit card statement and so much more.  All uploaded to a sketchy cloud service!OK Amazon.  I need a customer support phone number and a way verify the identity of the employee and the email I received before sending you my sensitive information.  Your turn.",2024-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,7.0,26.0,488,83,41,7,2.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,amazon limited account updated credit card information placed small order cancelled order sent weird email verify accountthey need picture driver license bank statement credit card statement much uploaded sketchy cloud serviceok amazon need customer support phone number way verify identity employee email received sending sensitive information turn,0.037788038698700094,0.9622119613012999,0.04655075715086932,0.2,0.7904161320808238,79.04161320808238,High Trust
Ian Latus,/users/5c90d39956e1116116cc5027,GB,5.0,2024-07-26 10:31:54+00:00,1.0,I wish I could give no stars,"I wish I could give no stars. Buying off Amazon is a nightmare. If the package arrives at all, it's usually damaged and in a gigantic box, delivered by someone who is so stressed they're either surly or ready for a breakdown. Some eBay purchases are delivered by Amazon Logistics. They are also a nightmare. Out of five eBay purchases delivered by Amazon Logistics, only one has arrived. To my neighbour. The tracking shows packages reaching my post town, then 'being rejected' - by who? There's no tracking showing it going to my village, so it gets to the hub and they can't be bothered with it because I'm at a remote location. Then there's selling on Amazon. That makes the buying experience like heavenly bliss. Amazon treat their vendors so badly that I'm surprised there are any left. Clearly this is lucrative though, otherwise Mr Bezos wouldn't look so happy. Amazon just sucks. It sucks so much I can't express it strongly enough. ",2024-07-26 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,7.0,26.0,941,164,28,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wish could give star buying amazon nightmare package arrives usually damaged gigantic box delivered someone stressed theyre either surly ready breakdown ebay purchase delivered amazon logistics also nightmare five ebay purchase delivered amazon logistics one arrived neighbour tracking show package reaching post town rejected there tracking showing going village get hub cant bothered im remote location there selling amazon make buying experience like heavenly bliss amazon treat vendor badly im surprised left clearly lucrative though otherwise mr bezos wouldnt look happy amazon suck suck much cant express strongly enough,0.013289337277789503,0.9867106627222105,0.09197980931015143,0.2,0.8117512932231356,81.17512932231355,High Trust
