Peter Rotondo,/users/66a230fdda573706d1d68d35,US,1.0,2024-07-25 13:03:34+00:00,1.0,I looked on the internet for Verizon…,"I looked on the internet for Verizon prepaid phones.  Up pops ""cheap Verizon prepaid phones"".  Click, look at items, all of which are labeled ""Total by Verizon"".  Unaware that Total is a completely different company, I bought one.I saved the phone until my current phone started going downhill, being on a very fixed income and not wanting to waste.Unfortunately, I didn't open the phone until after the return period passed.Discovered (was told by Verizon) that my phone wasn't compatible with my plan.Asked via virtual chat if I could return it,  and got nothing.Time has nothing to do with it.  The phone hasn't been used and Amazon, I feel, misled the consumer (me).  I will be very wary of ordering anything from now on.A decent customer service rep would have gotten a manager to approve the return.  She couldn't be bothered.""Try the retailer"". (Pardon, I thought YOU were the retailer).  Total wanted more than the phone costs to unlock it.Screw Amazon.",2024-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,7.0,25.0,961,160,37,7,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,looked internet verizon prepaid phone pop cheap verizon prepaid phone click look item labeled total verizon unaware total completely different company bought onei saved phone current phone started going downhill fixed income wanting wasteunfortunately didnt open phone return period passeddiscovered told verizon phone wasnt compatible planasked via virtual chat could return got nothingtime nothing phone hasnt used amazon feel misled consumer wary ordering anything ona decent customer service rep would gotten manager approve return couldnt botheredtry retailer pardon thought retailer total wanted phone cost unlock itscrew amazon,0.016523870880923303,0.9834761291190767,0.08973639932697701,0.2,0.8096853444249337,80.96853444249336,High Trust
