Rach,/users/5f107b2b755aa4bb4318146a,US,5.0,2024-07-02 16:55:08+00:00,1.0,3rd Party Purchaser,"I recently purchased an item from a third-party seller on Amazon, which was advertised with a 30-day return guarantee. However, my attempt to return the item has been an incredibly frustrating experience. The third-party seller refused to provide a return slip, leaving me at a loss for how to proceed.In an effort to resolve the issue, I reached out to Amazon customer service five times via chat and phone. During each interaction, I was assured that I would receive a refund within 48-72 hours. Unfortunately, these promises never materialized. On my final attempt to contact Amazon, I was shocked to learn that they were unsure why I had been repeatedly told I would receive a refund, as the item apparently cannot be returned. When I pointed out the 30-day return guarantee clearly stated on the website, I was told this information was incorrect.This experience has left me feeling misled and disappointed. As a Prime member, I expected better support in resolving this issue. Instead, I've wasted countless hours trying to address the problem, only to be told that Amazon cannot assist further. I'm now left with an unwanted product and over $300 out of pocket.This situation raises serious concerns about Amazon's policies regarding third-party sellers and their commitment to customer satisfaction. Why would Amazon allow third-party businesses on their platform if they cannot comply with Amazon's stated policies? Moreover, why isn't Amazon willing to work with customers and sellers to resolve disputes fairly? This system seems to open up opportunities for third-party sellers to potentially scam Amazon purchasers.I would appreciate if Amazon could clarify their policies regarding third-party sellers and returns, improve their customer service to provide accurate information, and implement better measures to ensure third-party sellers comply with Amazon's policies. This experience has significantly diminished my trust in Amazon's marketplace and their commitment to customer satisfaction.",2024-04-12 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,7.0,2.0,2008,307,19,3,81.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,recently purchased item thirdparty seller amazon advertised day return guarantee however attempt return item incredibly frustrating experience thirdparty seller refused provide return slip leaving loss proceedin effort resolve issue reached amazon customer service five time via chat phone interaction assured would receive refund within hour unfortunately promise never materialized final attempt contact amazon shocked learn unsure repeatedly told would receive refund item apparently cannot returned pointed day return guarantee clearly stated website told information incorrectthis experience left feeling misled disappointed prime member expected better support resolving issue instead ive wasted countless hour trying address problem told amazon cannot assist im left unwanted product pocketthis situation raise serious concern amazon policy regarding thirdparty seller commitment customer satisfaction would amazon allow thirdparty business platform cannot comply amazon stated policy moreover isnt amazon willing work customer seller resolve dispute fairly system seems open opportunity thirdparty seller potentially scam amazon purchasersi would appreciate amazon could clarify policy regarding thirdparty seller return improve customer service provide accurate information implement better measure ensure thirdparty seller comply amazon policy experience significantly diminished trust amazon marketplace commitment customer satisfaction,0.0027545139062792098,0.9972454860937208,0.17218171620863712,0.2,0.8330590862885878,83.30590862885879,High Trust
