Queen Riser,/users/66712e53290ae64945112fad,GB,1.0,2024-07-01 14:36:31+00:00,1.0,BIG CON ARTIST PROFESSIONAL THEIVES,"They deserve 0 stars. Please be aware that Amazon is using unethical and immoral practices to con people out of money. They state that if you order goods totalling 35.00 or more, your order is eligible for free delivery. I ordered some essential oils from the same seller. I checked each order to verify that it was eligible for free delivery. When I proceeded to checkout, I skipped Prime, and I was still being charged 4.99 for postage. This is because Amazon had a bottle of the essential oils ticked for premium delivery to arrive tomorrow, which I did not tick.  Customer services were useless as I was told that 3 of the oils were coming directly from a 3rd party seller and not Amazon. This is despite ordering all of the oils from the same seller and all of them being eligible for free delivery. I removed the oil that had the premium delivery cost added to it and attempted to check out. However, a different oil came up for next day delivery. This happened 3 times with the oils that were previously listed for free delivery, now showing a premium delivery cost. There was no option to untick the premium delivery cost as Amazon automatically applies this to your order.This breaches advertising and trading standards and is clearly fraudulent. The customer service adviser stated that the reason for this was that information in baskets changed as orders were updated, and the seller would change the information to reflect what was in stock.  I guess she thought I imagined it all and that I did not know what I was talking about. I will be reporting Amazon to the requisite body as this does need investigating.  It is such a long and frustrating process and a total waste of time. With this big online fraudster.  Your track record is disgusting as you are just interested in profits over people. You should be totally ashamed, but I guess this is something that you are accustomed to. You believe you are above the laws, and you will continue to con your sellers. A big round of applause to you!",2024-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,7.0,1.0,2011,358,35,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,deserve star please aware amazon using unethical immoral practice con people money state order good totalling order eligible free delivery ordered essential oil seller checked order verify eligible free delivery proceeded checkout skipped prime still charged postage amazon bottle essential oil ticked premium delivery arrive tomorrow tick customer service useless told oil coming directly rd party seller amazon despite ordering oil seller eligible free delivery removed oil premium delivery cost added attempted check however different oil came next day delivery happened time oil previously listed free delivery showing premium delivery cost option untick premium delivery cost amazon automatically applies orderthis breach advertising trading standard clearly fraudulent customer service adviser stated reason information basket changed order updated seller would change information reflect stock guess thought imagined know talking reporting amazon requisite body need investigating long frustrating process total waste time big online fraudster track record disgusting interested profit people totally ashamed guess something accustomed believe law continue con seller big round applause,0.0151816815352604,0.9848183184647396,0.20078519349411106,0.2,0.832566197931192,83.2566197931192,High Trust
