Mary,/users/5f6ed76cf29944f10ffbfb72,GB,13.0,2024-06-29 14:24:48+00:00,1.0,Unhappy Customer,"I have been an Amazon customer for many years, I’ve extremely disgruntled to learn the minimum order requirement to get free delivery has risen from £25.00 to £35.00, an absolute disgrace, which is a 40% increase, to expect customers to buy more is shocking especially in the current times of need. Forcing customers to add unnecessary items to their basket just to avoid a delivery fee feels like a slap in the face & a way to increase sales. It may also force customers to pay for Prime. I won't be agreeing to prime, I will order goods to the value of £35 and return items free of charge to get a refund. I will also use a family members prime to get free delivery if required. DISGUSTED",2024-06-29 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,29.0,690,128,16,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer many year i’ve extremely disgruntled learn minimum order requirement get free delivery risen £ £ absolute disgrace increase expect customer buy shocking especially current time need forcing customer add unnecessary item basket avoid delivery fee feel like slap face way increase sale may also force customer pay prime wont agreeing prime order good value £ return item free charge get refund also use family member prime get free delivery required disgusted,0.011373852904162061,0.988626147095838,0.0717891194615816,0.2,0.8086708974402352,80.86708974402353,High Trust
