Geoff de Moll,/users/5911c1df0000ff000a96219c,GB,56.0,2024-06-28 17:46:07+00:00,1.0,Allowing companies that are not trading to sell on their website,"I ordered a garden shed on Amazon when it’s arrived it was too ugly to go into my garden. I contacted Amazon to get a return label and when I carried the shed that weigh 30 kg plus to the post office they told me that the postage was not covered, I contacted Amazon. They assured me they would get back to the seller who would contact me within two days to arrange return of the goods. Now six weeks later, I am being told by Amazon that The order was placed under a different email address and they can only deal with that person. I have pointed out to them that there must be 100 orders before and since that order all placed under the same email address the same delivery address using the same card. I have spent over 50 hours trying to get my money back I’ve been told on two occasions that they would force the third-party to return my money within seven days which hasn’t happened. I have wrote three letters to their managing director and finally I had an answer over the phone this evening.. The person on the phone has given me absolute no confidence of me getting my money back. He’s saying it can’t be looked at under GDPR The order was placed under a different email address and I’m asking him how that’s happened when all the other orders are showing placed under the right email address. I’ve also asked him when when I applied to return the goods why it came out off my orders on the app making it very difficult for me to take the matter up with their customer services. I am also very concerned that the third-party that I placed my order with on the Amazon website have ceased trading and why Amazon allowing companies that do not trade to sell on their website. The guy on the telephone could not answer that question said he would report it, but I would hear nothing back as it would stay an internal matter. this is clearly not good enough and they as they are not protecting their customers.",2024-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,28.0,1914,361,64,11,45.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered garden shed amazon it’s arrived ugly go garden contacted amazon get return label carried shed weigh kg plus post office told postage covered contacted amazon assured would get back seller would contact within two day arrange return good six week later told amazon order placed different email address deal person pointed must order since order placed email address delivery address using card spent hour trying get money back i’ve told two occasion would force thirdparty return money within seven day hasn’t happened wrote three letter managing director finally answer phone evening person phone given absolute confidence getting money back he’s saying can’t looked gdpr order placed different email address i’m asking that’s happened order showing placed right email address i’ve also asked applied return good came order app making difficult take matter customer service also concerned thirdparty placed order amazon website ceased trading amazon allowing company trade sell website guy telephone could answer question said would report would hear nothing back would stay internal matter clearly good enough protecting customer,0.017789129475183435,0.9822108705248166,0.20246775098149186,0.2,0.8315989854587067,83.15989854587067,High Trust
Karen & Dave,/users/6533015a0044c500138e53b2,GB,2.0,2024-06-28 17:42:15+00:00,1.0,What customer service?,"At the start of the week I ordered a dishwasher with installation and removal of the old appliance. I was given a delivery slot of Friday 7am to 7 pm. As I could not be at home before 12 I telephoned to alter the delivery. I was told the delivery instructions had been changed and that the delivery would be after 12. When despatch confirmation was sent, again it said 7am to 7pm so I once again phoned and was assured delivery was after 12.At 9:30am of the day of delivery I received a txt saying they had tried to deliver but there was no one there. Surprise surprise!So I once agai telephoned and was given the run around on 3 separate occasions each time I was told that the dishwasher was due for delivery anytime before 7 although on their own web site it stated that it had been returned to the depot. The most surprising thing is all is that all 3 call agents insisted that there was no manager available for me to discuss these issues with. Unbelievable that a company the size of Amazon doesn’t have a supervisor or manager on call to help resolve customer issues.",2024-06-28 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,28.0,1074,201,22,3,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,start week ordered dishwasher installation removal old appliance given delivery slot friday pm could home telephoned alter delivery told delivery instruction changed delivery would despatch confirmation sent said pm phoned assured delivery day delivery received txt saying tried deliver one surprise surpriseso agai telephoned given run around separate occasion time told dishwasher due delivery anytime although web site stated returned depot surprising thing call agent insisted manager available discus issue unbelievable company size amazon doesn’t supervisor manager call help resolve customer issue,0.09274620457117806,0.9072537954288219,0.11273135165451487,0.2,0.7761731680453139,77.61731680453138,High Trust
