Denis USA,/users/606320b8631c39001a03800d,US,4.0,2024-06-27 20:30:39+00:00,1.0,Fake reviews and crazy searching algorithms ,"I don’t support Amazon since it’s faking reviews and pushing sellers to hunt for reviews. It’s unfair for sellers and buyers, and this review race has to stop. Their algorithms are showing just their click-promoting items and not the criteria I am looking for. Why show me shoes of size 10 if I am looking for size 13? It’s such a waste of time. I don’t buy there, only on eBay, where there’s an optimistic atmosphere and sellers can leave feedback for buyers in return. Sellers don’t pay for clicks to show their products in search but pay a percentage from the sold price. eBay shows me only the products matching my search criteria. Other marketplaces such as Walmart, Target, etc. are much better too, with fast and free shipping as well.I am not going to pay for this Prime subscription—I am fine with longer shipping. For urgent items, I can pick them up on my way home from the store. Walmart can sometimes ship the next day with their $35+ order free shipping service. All other marketplaces have similar return policies.",2024-06-27 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,27.0,1029,182,44,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,don’t support amazon since it’s faking review pushing seller hunt review it’s unfair seller buyer review race stop algorithm showing clickpromoting item criterion looking show shoe size looking size it’s waste time don’t buy ebay there’s optimistic atmosphere seller leave feedback buyer return seller don’t pay click show product search pay percentage sold price ebay show product matching search criterion marketplace walmart target etc much better fast free shipping welli going pay prime subscription—i fine longer shipping urgent item pick way home store walmart sometimes ship next day order free shipping service marketplace similar return policy,0.010839926755449592,0.9891600732445505,0.10207515423443635,0.2,0.8149950674691625,81.49950674691625,High Trust
