Sheryl 'Massoth' Andrews,/users/6679b45c5f04c53ec6c50ece,US,1.0,2024-06-24 20:01:15+00:00,1.0,Deceptive electronics selling practices,"Just wanted to share an Amazon issue I had today in case you may be unaware of this selling practice.I received a Canon printer as a Christmas gift.  I had a problem with it over the weekend that I could not solve using Canon's online support.  I called Canon this morning as the printer has a 1 year warranty.  Canon said the number of the printer I gave them was not a valid number and I told them that is what is stamped on the front of the printer.  They asked where it was purchased and I told them Amazon.  Canon told me Amazon sent me a Canadian product and therefore the warranty is not valid in the US.  They told me my only recourse was to call Amazon.Amazon did not want to do anything about it since it was after the 30 day return period.  After a rather heated discussion with them about deceptive selling practices they did agree to refund after I return the item.  I got an email from them with shipping instructions and an estimated refund which was 20% less (for a restocking fee).  Another discussion followed and I have to call them after they receive the return for the 20% to be refunded.  They also did not want to refund me for 2 unused ink cartridges I had ordered but they finally agreed after I expressed my opinion on that.  So, after 1 hour and 5 minutes on the phone with Amazon today I get to call them back again for the 20%.Tip of the day:  Don't order electronics from Amazon.",2024-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,24.0,1409,266,39,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wanted share amazon issue today case may unaware selling practicei received canon printer christmas gift problem weekend could solve using canon online support called canon morning printer year warranty canon said number printer gave valid number told stamped front printer asked purchased told amazon canon told amazon sent canadian product therefore warranty valid u told recourse call amazonamazon want anything since day return period rather heated discussion deceptive selling practice agree refund return item got email shipping instruction estimated refund less restocking fee another discussion followed call receive return refunded also want refund unused ink cartridge ordered finally agreed expressed opinion hour minute phone amazon today get call back tip day dont order electronics amazon,0.005947898087595421,0.9940521019124046,0.14918676388109928,0.2,0.8268634037324222,82.68634037324222,High Trust
