M K Maury,/users/6374f644a46a1e0013e4dd8c,US,3.0,2024-06-02 00:53:13+00:00,2.0,"If there's a delivery policy, stick to it and don't lose deliveries!!!","Amazon makes sure a customer can't get in touch when they claim that a delivery has been made to my door or to the porch. First problem: there's no porch. Second problem and the reason for my complaint: THERE'S NO SIGN OF A DELIVERY OF ANY SORT ANYWHERE TO BE FOUND!!! And Amazon makes sure that I will never get it!!! They say to use their chat, only the chat isn't available!!! There were two failed deliveries priced at $8.20 and $11.28. Neither order arrived. I have given the most explicit instructions; maybe I have to draw a photo map as well?!?!?!? Now I worry that all the orders I place are going to be left just anywhere and I'll just pay for things that I'll never receive. I notice that direct interaction is not possible. That forces me to file complaints elsewhere, which is what I am doing now because I am given no alternative. And I don't appreciate lying of any sort. No, it was not delivered to my door. Funny that Walmart managed to deliver to me with no problem. Amazon has failed me. There's no other way to describe it. I feel sick now. This is what is done to a disabled senior male these days. I'll just post my complaint everywhere possible; I have no other alternative. Some possibility of making contact with a human being should be available; when no possibility is made available, ripping off a customer is child's play. If I have to go out and lead the delivery person by the hand to get to my door, TELL ME SO IN PLAIN ENGLISH, A LANGUAGE IN WHICH I HAVE WRITTEN AND PUBLISHED!!! Amazon has a publication of mine on record, so they can't say my instructions aren't clear. What burns me most is the lying. Delivery was not made. The app gives me no way to make contact. Maybe they assume I'll die before a delivery is made. I give up. I have no way of guessing anymore. If Walmart made a delivery to my door, Amazon should have been able to do the same thing -- maybe. Normally, they store large deliveries in lockers on the property here and give the customer codes to log into the lockers. Instead, they claimed to deliver them to my door when there was nothing to be found. I faxed them about this development and received no notice of change in my favor.",2024-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,2.0,2190,409,70,12,1.0,0,15,2,1,Suspicious,amazon make sure customer cant get touch claim delivery made door porch first problem there porch second problem reason complaint there sign delivery sort anywhere found amazon make sure never get say use chat chat isnt available two failed delivery priced neither order arrived given explicit instruction maybe draw photo map well worry order place going left anywhere ill pay thing ill never receive notice direct interaction possible force file complaint elsewhere given alternative dont appreciate lying sort delivered door funny walmart managed deliver problem amazon failed there way describe feel sick done disabled senior male day ill post complaint everywhere possible alternative possibility making contact human available possibility made available ripping customer child play go lead delivery person hand get door tell plain english language written published amazon publication mine record cant say instruction arent clear burn lying delivery made app give way make contact maybe assume ill die delivery made give way guessing anymore walmart made delivery door amazon able thing maybe normally store large delivery locker property give customer code log locker instead claimed deliver door nothing found faxed development received notice change favor,0.9999999736129843,2.638701568358215e-08,0.22938867077958497,0.4,0.6458777473494248,64.58777473494249,Medium Trust
Frances Jones,/users/65146d7794ad3b0011021b20,US,2.0,2024-06-02 00:42:07+00:00,1.0,Incredibly rude customer service ,"Amazon used to be incredibly reliable, consistent, and user-friendly, however lately there's been an exponential increase in wrong deliveries, falsely reported deliveries, and stolen deliveries. I understand things happen, but I believe that when they do, particularly if one customer is experiencing this frequently, the customer should be penalized as little as possible. When voicing these concerns after not receiving the fourth delivery within a month, I was met with condescension and a lack of consideration. I have found their customer representatives to be snarky, demeaning, and unwilling to actually fix the issue or offer compensation. Even their apologies are rude. Sad because this business used to be hospitable and efficient. Seems this conglomerate has gotten larger than they can handle. ",2024-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,2.0,806,121,33,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon used incredibly reliable consistent userfriendly however lately there exponential increase wrong delivery falsely reported delivery stolen delivery understand thing happen believe particularly one customer experiencing frequently customer penalized little possible voicing concern receiving fourth delivery within month met condescension lack consideration found customer representative snarky demeaning unwilling actually fix issue offer compensation even apology rude sad business used hospitable efficient seems conglomerate gotten larger handle,0.015965946576415747,0.9840340534235843,0.06786315199102635,0.2,0.8055896571099973,80.55896571099973,High Trust
Darien Stelling,/users/66514cbbd11b29dad62dc389,GB,4.0,2024-06-01 23:03:42+00:00,3.0,Overall Amazon experience.,"My experience is purely based on the website and processes, but overall amazon with get a 3/5.Purely because a lot of products are the site can 3rd party and made with cheap material while sellers sell products at a high price.However amazon do plenty of offers on normal everyday products and I've not had much issue when contacting them if I have problems.My only gripe would be that sometimes some products are sent out via other couriers such as Evri, DPD, Royal Mail etc, and I wish they would state on the order on the website that this chosen courier is delivering my parcel instead of an amazon courier.",2024-05-29 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,1.0,611,109,26,3,3.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,experience purely based website process overall amazon get purely lot product site rd party made cheap material seller sell product high pricehowever amazon plenty offer normal everyday product ive much issue contacting problemsmy gripe would sometimes product sent via courier evri dpd royal mail etc wish would state order website chosen courier delivering parcel instead amazon courier,0.020519429765072393,0.9794805702349276,0.061132922041503085,0.6,1.4019668695257643,140.19668695257644,High Trust
David Noble,/users/665b719b9e5419a1dd7b263a,US,1.0,2024-06-01 21:08:26+00:00,1.0, “Customer disservice” ,"The title “Customer service” must mean something different to Amazon employees than to other businesses. I needed to apply a gift card balance to my Amazon account, but the online reply was that it was “invalid” though it has never been used.Since the online Customer service department suggested it would be best to “chat“ with a representative, I enter a summary of the problem I was having to make it easier for my customer service representative.After one hour of waiting for a representative to respond online, Aman Joined the chat and asked if there was anything he could do. Clearly he had not bothered to read my summary, so I copied all of the information and reposted it in my reply. After another 10 minutes, I asked Aman to escalate this conversation to his superiors as a complaint and ended the session that had wasted more than one hour of my time.I am sure that it comes as no surprised anyone but, Jeff Bezos and his Amazon crew seem to only care about taking easy money as there is absolutely no interest in providing any true “customer service.”",2024-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,6.0,1.0,1064,188,23,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,title “customer service” must mean something different amazon employee business needed apply gift card balance amazon account online reply “invalid” though never usedsince online customer service department suggested would best “chat“ representative enter summary problem make easier customer service representativeafter one hour waiting representative respond online aman joined chat asked anything could clearly bothered read summary copied information reposted reply another minute asked aman escalate conversation superior complaint ended session wasted one hour timei sure come surprised anyone jeff bezos amazon crew seem care taking easy money absolutely interest providing true “customer service”,0.015625383601432834,0.9843746163985672,0.105440