ds asf,/users/5ec7d9fb82bffbf88077e30b,NL,36.0,2024-05-20 20:08:54+00:00,1.0,Lies and broken promises ,"I had a very bad experience with Amazon.deI ordered multiple pairs of Falke socks in the promotion in different colours. Since you could only order 4 pair of any colour at the same time, I also placed multiple orders.On the Amazon website it stated that these socks were all to be delivered within a week or maximum 14 days to the Netherlands.I received the largest part of my orders within 14 days, however Amazon could not ship 8 pair of socks at that time and I was given an indication of another 2-3 weeks for delivery.After waiting patiently for these socks for 3 weeks, I received a message from Amazon (the day before these socks were set to be shipped) that they were cancelling the order.I contacted the Amazon helpdesk to ask what happened. They told me the colour could not be found in the warehouse and therefore they would cancel my order. I asked them if it would be possible to get a different colour (at the time of ordering multiple other colours were also available for the promotional price).After some discussion Amazon agreed to sell me 8 pair of socks in a colour of my choice. They even promissed me an additional discount of 10% and refund of the shipping costs because of all the hassle.They told me I had to cancel my orders and order these socks at the current price. They would than refund me the difference in price once I received the orders, as well as the 10% discount and the shipping costs.To make sure I understood correctly I even send them a calculation of what refund the would be giving me (the price was more than double compared to the promotional price). They confirmed I understood everything correctly and I wouldn't have to worry.So I ordered 8 pair of socks and send Amazon an message to receive the refund. However, Amazon refused to give me the promised refund.I have had long message conversations as well as 2 phone calls for over an hour with the help desk. During these calls the Amazon employees agreed with me and promised me to arrange the refund. Afterwards I got written messages that I have been misinformed and that they can't/won't give me the refund.Finally, I have returned the 8 pair of socks to get my money back. It was impossible to get Amazon to keep their word and you should be aware that the promises they make mean nothing.",2024-05-18 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,20.0,2294,412,25,4,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,bad experience amazondei ordered multiple pair falke sock promotion different colour since could order pair colour time also placed multiple orderson amazon website stated sock delivered within week maximum day netherlandsi received largest part order within day however amazon could ship pair sock time given indication another week deliveryafter waiting patiently sock week received message amazon day sock set shipped cancelling orderi contacted amazon helpdesk ask happened told colour could found warehouse therefore would cancel order asked would possible get different colour time ordering multiple colour also available promotional priceafter discussion amazon agreed sell pair sock colour choice even promissed additional discount refund shipping cost hasslethey told cancel order order sock current price would refund difference price received order well discount shipping coststo make sure understood correctly even send calculation refund would giving price double compared promotional price confirmed understood everything correctly wouldnt worryso ordered pair sock send amazon message receive refund however amazon refused give promised refundi long message conversation well phone call hour help desk call amazon employee agreed promised arrange refund afterwards got written message misinformed cantwont give refundfinally returned pair sock get money back impossible get amazon keep word aware promise make mean nothing,0.01398778316197148,0.9860122168380285,0.2310712282669658,0.2,0.8392203540724075,83.92203540724074,High Trust
