Will Murch,/users/6109b201f4ba290012d61bda,GB,2.0,2024-05-11 13:00:11+00:00,1.0,Used to love Amazon and when Prime…,"Used to love Amazon and when Prime started it was great. The issues started when Amazon began to Make their own in house deliveries since then in over 12 months every delivery has been late or delivered to entirely the wrong address on my road. With complaint after complaint doing nothing to resolve this. Customer services are a joke asking if I have canvassed the local neighbours if they have received it. I would appreciate that if I were in the middle of nowhere  but with two blocks of flats I am not spending hours doing the delivery drivers job for them. Or straight up marking packages as attempted on the week when I am home all day.In short prime is a waste of money for several reasons;1) video has gone from a streaming service to having poor choice with most items being pay to rent or buy. Those available are now saddled with a premium service within a premium service with adverts throughout.2) prime next day delivery is hopeless the drivers either lie and mark deliveries as complete when they haven't tried or are too clueless to find an address (royal mail and other providers manage just fine,)3) over priced rubbish with little benefit ",2024-05-11 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,11.0,1160,205,35,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used love amazon prime started great issue started amazon began make house delivery since month every delivery late delivered entirely wrong address road complaint complaint nothing resolve customer service joke asking canvassed local neighbour received would appreciate middle nowhere two block flat spending hour delivery driver job straight marking package attempted week home dayin short prime waste money several reason video gone streaming service poor choice item pay rent buy available saddled premium service within premium service advert throughout prime next day delivery hopeless driver either lie mark delivery complete havent tried