Home Owner FUJB,/users/630812179e069800133c4b45,US,3.0,2024-05-11 00:36:39+00:00,1.0,VIOLATIONS OF FEDERAL FAIR TRADE…,"VIOLATIONS OF FEDERAL FAIR TRADE COMPETITION LAW The FTC and states allege Amazon’s anticompetitive conduct occurs in two markets—the online superstore market that serves shoppers and the market for online marketplace services purchased by sellers. These tactics include:Anti-discounting measures that punish sellers and deter other online retailers from offering prices lower than Amazon, keeping prices higher for products across the internet. For example, if Amazon discovers that a seller is offering lower-priced goods elsewhere, Amazon can bury discounting sellers so far down in Amazon’s search results that they become effectively invisible.Conditioning sellers’ ability to obtain “Prime” eligibility for their products—a virtual necessity for doing business on Amazon—on sellers using Amazon’s costly fulfillment service, which has made it substantially more expensive for sellers on Amazon to also offer their products on other platforms. This unlawful coercion has in turn limited competitors’ ability to effectively compete against Amazon.Amazon’s illegal, exclusionary conduct makes it impossible for competitors to gain a foothold. With its amassed power across both the online superstore market and online marketplace services market, Amazon extracts enormous monopoly rents from everyone within its reach. ",2024-05-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,11.0,1322,183,33,5,10.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,violation federal fair trade competition law ftc state allege amazon’s anticompetitive conduct occurs two markets—the online superstore market serf shopper market online marketplace service purchased seller tactic includeantidiscounting measure punish seller deter online retailer offering price lower amazon keeping price higher product across internet example amazon discovers seller offering lowerpriced good elsewhere amazon bury discounting seller far amazon’s search result become effectively invisibleconditioning sellers’ ability obtain “prime” eligibility products—a virtual necessity business amazon—on seller using amazon’s costly fulfillment service made substantially expensive seller amazon also offer product platform unlawful coercion turn limited competitors’ ability effectively compete amazonamazon’s illegal exclusionary conduct make impossible competitor gain foothold amassed power across online superstore market online marketplace service market amazon extract enormous monopoly rent everyone within reach,0.006206291222160195,0.9937937087778398,0.10263600673022995,0.2,0.8174240557349659,81.7424055734966,High Trust
