Peter Harris,/users/639c4d83e430720013e99dfb,GB,7.0,2024-05-08 10:11:14+00:00,1.0,Very bad service for business owners,"Amazon is becoming very unreliable now. I've been dealing with them for nearly years. At the end of last year, I was ordering products for my business. When they stopped arriving. I contacted Amazon but no response so, I contacted the seller and still no response. I tried over 20 times with no success. Amazon made 3 mistakes in 3 days and they got away with it. Amazon became the weak link in my business so, I had no hesitation in dealing with eBay. I would not recommend anyone to deal with Amazon. ",2023-11-08 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,8.0,503,93,36,6,182.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon becoming unreliable ive dealing nearly year end last year ordering product business stopped arriving contacted amazon response contacted seller still response tried time success amazon made mistake day got away amazon became weak link business hesitation dealing ebay would recommend anyone deal amazon,0.0011693608785885462,0.9988306391214115,0.05215928210880538,0.2,0.8098471759824667,80.98471759824668,High Trust
Derek Nigh,/users/65f5d2645f0bc8001294a9d1,US,1.0,2024-05-08 07:35:26+00:00,1.0,Amazon Customer Service: non-existent,"I’ve been buying products from Amazon for over 10+ years. I have thousands of photos in Amazon Photos, I have other paid services with them also. I changed phone numbers and forgot to change the two-step verification. I have followed the process for removing my two-step verification phone number for over 30 days - with no response. I’ve called spoken to several managers with no resolution in sight. I have lost all confidence in Amazon. This is the worst customer experience ever. I’m considering contacting an attorney to get access to my photos and videos. Avoid this poorly run operation - at least don’t use their other services by placing videos and photos in their care. So frustrating. They are not serious about customer service. They are inept and lazy. ",2024-05-07 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,8.0,766,130,37,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,i’ve buying product amazon year thousand photo amazon photo paid service also changed phone number forgot change twostep verification followed process removing twostep verification phone number day response i’ve called spoken several manager resolution sight lost confidence amazon worst customer experience ever i’m considering contacting attorney get access photo video avoid poorly run operation least don’t use service placing video photo care frustrating serious customer service inept lazy,0.02231996015251622,0.9776800398474838,0.07291082445316882,0.2,0.8034221848143757,80.34221848143757,High Trust
Jules Angebault,/users/663aebfcf763a3dc7f8c54a9,NZ,1.0,2024-05-08 05:05:42+00:00,1.0,Amazon's Customer Service Nightmare: A Saga of Salt and Incompetence,"Let me regale you with the tale of my recent descent into the abyss of Amazon's incompetence. Picture this: I'm locked out of my account because, surprise, surprise, I no longer have access to my phone number. So, what's Amazon's brilliant solution? Use a credit card. Sounds straightforward, right? Wrong! Apparently, the geniuses at Amazon haven't yet grasped the concept of credit card expiration dates.In my quest to untangle this mess, I attempted to reach out to their esteemed customer service. But alas, the phone numbers provided might as well have led to the Bermuda Triangle, because they were utterly useless from my corner of the world in New Zealand.It's mind-boggling that a company swimming in cash like Scrooge McDuck hasn't managed to figure out basic customer service protocols. And so, in a fit of exasperation, I was forced to resort to the drastic measure of creating a whole new account just to make a simple purchase. Bravo, Amazon, for turning what should've been a routine transaction into a Shakespearean tragedy of errors. If you value your sanity, steer clear of this tech behemoth's abyss of ineptitude.",2024-05-08 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,8.0,1133,187,68,10,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,let regale tale recent descent abyss amazon incompetence picture im locked account surprise surprise longer access phone number whats amazon brilliant solution use credit card sound straightforward right wrong apparently genius amazon havent yet grasped concept credit card expiration datesin quest untangle mess attempted reach esteemed customer service ala phone number provided might well led bermuda triangle utterly useless corner world new zealandits mindboggling company swimming cash like scrooge mcduck hasnt managed figure basic customer service protocol fit exasperation forced resort drastic measure creating whole new account make simple purchase bravo amazon turning shouldve routine transaction shakespearean tragedy error value sanity steer clear tech behemoth abyss ineptitude,0.027599487898080883,0.9724005121019191,0.10487941671340438,0.2,0.8071761393936404,80.71761393936404,High Trust
