melinda gardener,/users/59a845990000ff000ac28e48,GB,37.0,2024-05-05 15:13:18+00:00,1.0,My 65 year old Father who has Sciatica,"My 65 year old Father who has Sciatica, blood clots and anxiety was attacked, thrown to the grown causing injury to his back and punched in his face by one of your drivers. He was sleeping in his house when the delivery man came to delivery a package to his next door neighbour. Then the delivery man pressed down on my dad’s bell holding his finger on the bell for a prolonged amount of time. Which started my dad and he got up to go to the door. The delivery man then tried to give him the package and he said it was not his. My dad then told him to press the number 2 bell, the driver said he alll could not find it and my father said it was on the middle of the door right I in front of the drivers face if the driver had cared to look. At this point the driver started shouting, knock my elderly father to the floor causing him to fall straight back into the house hitting his lower back in the step as he fell. The driver then came over him to punch him in his face, threw the package that he had came to delivery for next door toward their door and ran out before my father could get up to get the registration of the van. My dad has been undergoing man diagnostic test since January of this year and is not a very Will man health wise. I find it appalling that your drivers would attack an old man for staying the obvious to them. The man park directly outside the house and also has a lady sitting in the passenger seat which I know is slaps not allowed during work hours in your vans.  My dad has report the incident to the police and has a cad number which we will like to share with you when you get back to us. The incident happened at his address at 4pm ish on 02/05/2024. You driver has left My Dad in pain, stiffness and worsening his sciatica symptoms and his anxiety. This was appalling and you must see to it that the driver is fully reprimanded and that you share his details with the police. We have the details of the package he was delivery to identify which drivers van it was loaded on m. So you can identify, pull up and reprimand the correct driver. We will share this info with you once you get back to us.",2024-05-02 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,5.0,2134,422,38,8,3.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,year old father sciatica blood clot anxiety attacked thrown grown causing injury back punched face one driver sleeping house delivery man came delivery package next door neighbour delivery man pressed dad’s bell holding finger bell prolonged amount time started dad got go door delivery man tried give package said dad told press number bell driver said alll could find father said middle door right front driver face driver cared look point driver started shouting knock elderly father floor causing fall straight back house hitting lower back step fell driver came punch face threw package came delivery next door toward door ran father could get get registration van dad undergoing man diagnostic test since january year man health wise find appalling driver would attack old man staying obvious man park directly outside house also lady sitting passenger seat know slap allowed work hour van dad report incident police cad number like share get back u incident happened address pm ish driver left dad pain stiffness worsening sciatica symptom anxiety appalling must see driver fully reprimanded share detail police detail package delivery identify driver van loaded identify pull reprimand correct driver share info get back u,0.054170897876237516,0.9458291021237625,0.23667975322490184,0.2,0.8202505017068616,82.02505017068617,High Trust
