Sharon Gat,/users/6637797d731b500012115841,IL,1.0,2024-05-05 14:20:20+00:00,1.0,The great Amazon believes that our time…,"The great Amazon believes that our time is unimportant, and their written resolutions are not obligatory. I purchased an item and was supposed to receive it after two weeks. After four weeks, I didn't receive the item. I contacted customer service and tried to cancel since I had already bought an additional item. I couldn't cancel the order but I was promised a full refund without returning the item. More than two additional weeks passed, and finally, the item arrived. I contacted customer service again to proceed with what I was promised( and got an email confirmation regarding such a resolution). A refund was issued. I have waited for dates for the confirmation, which I didn't receive, so I contacted customer service once again. Once again, I was promised a refund and even received an email confirmation. Again, days passed, and nothing happened. Once again, I contacted customer service and passed from one representative to another, even asking for phonecall which I was promised and didn't receive; after more than two hours, I asked for a supervisor who explained that with no return, no refund could be issued and maximum promotional is less than a half of the original sum. After all this time and confirmation, this is Amazon's answer? Are you serious you can't handle less than 90 USD? Well, dear Amazon, I am done with you after years of purchase. ",2024-05-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,5.0,1370,232,40,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,great amazon belief time unimportant written resolution obligatory purchased item supposed receive two week four week didnt receive item contacted customer service tried cancel since already bought additional item couldnt cancel order promised full refund without returning item two additional week passed finally item arrived contacted customer service proceed promised got email confirmation regarding resolution refund issued wa