Raimonds,/users/630744fe08df9c0012172409,GB,6.0,2024-05-03 18:10:42+00:00,1.0,Amazon is braking in my order of life,"I had to create a new account because Amazon wouldn't assist me in recovering an account I had used for years. They also refused to delete my old account, preventing me from creating a new one with my personal email where I could easily find my regular purchases. Eventually I registered my new account using my telephone number to the new Amazon account which resulted silently adding my work email to the Amazon shopping account. I view this situation with Amazon as highly disrespectful. I see this is like someone is entering my home, rearranging everything, and dictating how I should live.",2024-05-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,3.0,595,102,37,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,create new account amazon wouldnt assist recovering account used year also refused delete old account preventing creating new one personal email could easily find regular purchase eventually registered new account using telephone number new amazon account resulted silently adding work email amazon shopping account view situation amazon highly disrespectful see like someone entering home rearranging everything dictating live,0.011205708217304882,0.9887942917826951,0.05720695457094784,0.2,0.8058385368055371,80.5838536805537,High Trust
Timothy,/users/6634fb60731b500012103015,US,1.0,2024-05-03 16:57:46+00:00,1.0,"$1,000+ in pre-authorizations??? Get Real!!!!","I made a purchase for office supplies on April 30th, 2024. Today, May 3rd, 2024, I reviewed my credit card statement online, and saw that I had three pending charges. The office supplies cost me $562.34, but the other two charges were for $567.16. I have no record of the $567.16 charge(s). I spoke with an Amazon Customer Service Representative, who said that the initial charge of $567.16 was a pre-authorization, but couldn't answer as to why I was charged that amount twice. They refused to let me submit a suggestion to a help desk, so I am leaving my review here. If I only had a $1,000 or $1,500 credit limit and I relied on that card for fuel, I would be in a serious bind. How dare Amazon tie up over a thousand dollars of my credit.",2024-05-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,5.0,3.0,742,139,45,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,made purchase office supply april th today may rd reviewed credit card statement online saw three pending charge office supply cost two charge record charge spoke amazon customer service representative said initial charge preauthorization couldnt answer charged amount twice refused let submit suggestion help desk leaving review credit limit relied card fuel would serious bind dare amazon tie thousand dollar credit,0.028553520952978407,0.9714464790470216,0.07795849691531127,0.2,0.801314938906573,80.1314938906573,High Trust
