Timothy Gillis,/users/663036f078f40e0012bd643f,US,1.0,2024-04-30 02:10:34+00:00,1.0,Don't Believe The Promised Delivery Date,"I've found that Amazon can't be trusted to keep their word, and many of their product listings are outright deceptive. I ordered a product on Friday, the listing said ""Free delivery tonight if ordered within 2 hours."" I completed the order within 10 minutes. While paying, the details said ""delivery tomorrow."" What? Why did that change? Okay, so I paid for the order. The email confirmation said, ""Delivery by Sunday."" Really? It keeps changing at every step. The clincher was when I later got a notification that said ""Your item will be delivered on Monday."" The shipping details on their website are a complete bait and switch to get people to buy. My last four orders from them have followed this same pattern, and two of those orders were delivered to the wrong address. Amazon delivery service has gone downhill terribly in the last couple of years.",2024-04-25 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,30.0,855,147,40,6,5.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ive found amazon cant trusted keep word many product listing outright deceptive ordered product friday listing said free delivery tonight ordered within hour completed order within minute paying detail said delivery tomorrow change okay paid order email confirmation said delivery sunday really keep changing every step clincher later got notification said item delivered monday shipping detail website complete bait switch get people buy last four order followed pattern two order delivered wrong address amazon delivery service gone downhill terribly last couple year,0.006276193020341901,0.9937238069796581,0.08244531688166012,0.2,0.813350966866161,81.3350966866161,High Trust
