Ashley Smith,/users/662d54cde957d20011add037,US,1.0,2024-04-28 09:31:08+00:00,1.0,"Amazon stole my money, and probably yours too. Check all refunds received from them.","I ordered a product for $299.00 from amazon, the day it was supposed to arrive I checked to see if the order was out for delivery, at which point I got an alert that the product was damaged in route. I contacted the company I ordered the product from and was told that was an amazon issue not their issue. I spoke to amazon about the order and they said I could not request a new product but they would refund my money in 5-7 days. 5-7 days later I get a refund for $289.98. Now don't get me wrong I know $9.02 isn't a lot of money but I DIDNT GET THE PRODUCT AND WASNT GIVEN THE CHOICE TO REPLACE THE ITEM. When contacting amazon to find out why they didn't refund the whole amount they stated that promotional credits are non refundable. How does that make any sense at all? Amazon stole my money plain and simple. THEN, when I tried to leave a review about my experience with this order i was told and I am quoting exactly from the email I received from them, that they couldn't post my review for the following reasons: ""Please edit and resubmit your review Hello Ashley, We couldn't post your review because it focuses on one or more of these topics: Sellers Delivery Packaging Pricing Availability Why isn't that allowed? These aspects vary by order and won't be relevant to all customers. That said, we want your feedback about sellers and packaging, just not in product reviews. Please edit and resubmit your review. Before you do, make sure it meets all of our community guidelines."" So, where should I leave a review about my feedback relating to sellers and packaging then? I cant even give other consumers an accurate review of my experience, I'm guessing because amazon stole my money. I will never order from them again, and hope this will prevent a few people from making the same mistake. ",2023-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,28.0,1805,330,84,14,275.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered product amazon day supposed arrive checked see order delivery point got alert product damaged route contacted company ordered product told amazon issue issue spoke amazon order said could request new product would refund money day day later get refund dont get wrong know isnt lot money didnt get product wasnt given choice replace item contacting amazon find didnt refund whole amount stated promotional credit non refundable make sense amazon stole money plain simple tried leave review experience order told quoting exactly email received couldnt post review following reason please edit resubmit review hello ashley couldnt post review focus one topic seller delivery packaging pricing availability isnt allowed aspect vary order wont relevant customer said want feedback seller packaging product review please edit resubmit review make sure meet community guideline leave review feedback relating seller packaging cant even give consumer accurate review experience im guessing amazon stole money never order hope prevent people making mistake,7.794733062793343e-05,0.9999220526693721,0.1850813236118901,0.2,0.8369772910570641,83.69772910570641,High Trust
