James Layne,/users/5887d6150000ff000a70072c,US,7.0,2024-04-21 07:45:46+00:00,1.0,How far the Mighty Amazon has Fallen ,"I can't begin to describe how far Amazon has fallen over the years.  I was a customer from the beginning.  I was with Prime shortly after it came out.  I seriously thought it was the best company in the world, until it wasn't.  Then it wasn't even close.  Amazon now has among the worst customer service I encounter anywhere.  It rivals Comcast and Verizon Fios for the worst service you can even conceive of.  There's literally no way to describe the thousand ways Amazon fails at basic stuff.  It's service is a nightmare now.  You're sent off to a foreign country, with people who are supremely unhelpful, with the simplest issues taking hours to resolve.  I'm over it.  I no longer trust Amazon.  It's that simple.  Most recent case in point: I called Synchrony Bank, the issuer of the Amazon store card, to pay my bill.  It said the balance was over $400, so I thought I'd go through to a live person and see what the purchases were, to make sure nothing was unauthorized.  I recognized every purchase, except one.  There was an $11 charge for Amazon digital services.  I knew I hadn't authorized any digital purchases, so told them to put me through to Amazon.  The Indian man I spoke with was completely unhelpful.  Mind you, I mean him or anyone else no disrespect for being foreign.  He spoke with a thick accent likely because English was his second language.  GOOD FOR HIM.  It's something to be proud of.  But it also makes it very difficult to take care of issues that have any degree of complexity at all. He insisted I definitely ordered Amazon Music Unlimited, because I played [unintelligible] on my Alexa device.  What was the name of it?  ""It was [unintelligible]""  HUH?  SAY THAT AGAIN SLOWLY?  Literally, his accent was so thick I couldn't tell at all what he was saying.  After repeating it a fourth time, I made out the word ""noise.""  It hit me that Amazon was charging me $11 a month to play ""brown noise"" on my bedroom Alexa device.  I've played that as a background sleep noise for YEARS.  Didn't start in December.  I've literally played it for about 3-5 years, every single night.  Suddenly it apparently started charging me for it in December.  I never heard it ask me ANYTHING about a subscription and certainly never agreed to any such thing.  But that didn't convince this Amazon rep, who apparently could read my mind and insisted I absolutely did order it.  I grew increasingly annoyed, especially as he kept going silent for 20, 30, 40 seconds at a time without saying a word, no hold or anything.. just silence.  Finally I told him, ""why are you being silent?  I don't know what you're doing.""  He then hung up on me.  So much for customer service.  I called angrier now and spoke with a second rep.  She was so very sorry the first rep hung up on me.  If I would just take more time out of my Saturday night to explain everything all over again and verify myself again... which I had no choice but to do.  She took a complaint on the last rep, but said she couldn't help me.  I'd have to be transferred to Amazon music.  Mind you, by this time it's nearly 1 am in the morning on a Sunday morning.  She puts me on hold... and I wait and I wait and wait some more.  About 15 minutes she comes back and says ""I'm sorry for the long wait.  I'm still in the queue to speak with Amazon music.""  I told her I would wait.  She puts me back on hold... 20 minutes pass... 30 minutes pass... 40 minutes pass.  Finally I had to give up.  She never came back on the line to say anything.  Just the same canned music playing over and over and over and over on a loop.  Called again.  Asked for a supervisor, but my phone died because I'd been held on the line so long.  He didn't call back.  I gave up because I had to give up.  Otherwise, I'd have a stroke from my anger and high blood pressure.  Amazon, you suck. Every single time I have a problem now, this is what I encounter.  Amazon is no longer a great company.  It's a company that will cut every corner, that disrespects its customers and their time, and that cares only about its bottom line.  It will go the way of Sears because it deserves to.  ",2024-04-20 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,21.0,4131,758,37,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,cant begin describe far amazon fallen year customer beginning prime shortly came seriously thought best company world wasnt wasnt even close amazon among worst customer service encounter anywhere rival comcast verizon fios worst service even conceive there literally way describe thousand way amazon fails basic stuff service nightmare youre sent foreign country people supremely unhelpful simplest issue taking hour resolve im longer trust amazon simple recent case point called synchrony bank issuer amazon store card pay bill said balance thought id go live person see purchase make sure nothing unauthorized recognized every purchase except one charge amazon digital service knew hadnt authorized digital purchase told put amazon indian man spoke completely unhelpful mind mean anyone else disrespect foreign spoke thick accent likely english second language good something proud also make difficult take care issue degree complexity insisted definitely ordered amazon music unlimited played unintelligible alexa device name unintelligible huh say slowly literally accent thick couldnt tell saying repeating fourth time made word noise hit amazon charging month play brown noise bedroom alexa device ive played background sleep noise year didnt start december ive literally played year every single night suddenly apparently started charging december never heard ask anything subscription certainly never agreed thing didnt convince amazon rep apparently could read mind insisted absolutely order grew increasingly annoyed especially kept going silent second time without saying word hold anything silence finally told silent dont know youre hung much customer service called angrier spoke second rep sorry first rep hung would take time saturday night explain everything verify choice took complaint last rep said couldnt help id transferred amazon music mind time nearly morning sunday morning put hold wait wait wait minute come back say im sorry long wait im still queue speak amazon music told would wait put back hold minute pas minute pas minute pas finally give never came back line say anything canned music playing loop called asked supervisor phone died id held line long didnt call back gave give otherwise id stroke anger high blood pressure amazon suck every single time problem encounter amazon longer great company company cut every corner disrespect customer time care bottom line go way sears deserves,0.005033645042460101,0.9949663549575399,0.4251261918115536,0.2,0.8825084158410806,88.25084158410806,High Trust
Rosalind Smith Cross,/users/65204b6bb151090011f3bf23,US,2.0,2024-04-21 04:57:44+00:00,5.0,Today I received a package from Amazon,"Today I received a package from Amazon, but it was empty -- the adhesive had slipped on the envelope and the contents probably fell out in the truck. I used the automated system through the website and was immediately connected to an agent who resolved the problem in about 30 seconds. Highly impressed with the efficiency of the company, and the great service from the customer service rep!",2024-04-20 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,21.0,391,68,38,7,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,today received package amazon empty adhesive slipped envelope content probably fell truck used automated system website immediately connected agent resolved problem second highly impressed efficiency company great service customer service rep,0.21894233803316493,0.781057661966835,0.03813796971396523,1.0,1.8981564249262104,189.81564249262104,High Trust
Amunet Amun,/users/6624365ace8f9100112370b1,US,5.0,2024-04-20 23:41:56+00:00,1.0,Amazon Unprofessional employees and overcharges,"On April 16, 2024, I received an Amazon Prime charge of $9.99. On April 15, 2024, I received an Amazon Prime charge of $16.53.I reached out to Amazon and was told by an Amazon rep that they could not see a charge for $9.99 when both charges are clearly seen on my bank statement. I filed a BBB complaint on April 16, 2024. Amazon reached out to me via email on April 19, 2024, totally ignoring my BBB complaint which is where I expected communication. I do not appreciate it when business circumvent BBB in order to avoid the complaints being listed on their website.The public has the right to know how all businesses conduct their business including when they are ripping off consumers and being unprofessional.I contacted my bank but I am not satisfied with Amazon's response to my complaint. I attached the BBB complaint, my bank statement double Amazon charges, and the emails from Amazon for your viewing.",2024-04-16 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,20.0,911,160,47,5,4.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,april received amazon prime charge april received amazon prime charge reached amazon told amazon rep could see charge charge clearly seen bank statement filed bbb complaint april amazon reached via email april totally ignoring bbb complaint expected communication appreciate business circumvent bbb order avoid complaint listed websitethe public right know business conduct business including ripping consumer unprofessionali contacted bank satisfied amazon response complaint attached bbb complaint bank statement double amazon charge email amazon viewing,0.029820891915306215,0.9701791080846938,0.08973639932697701,0.2,0.8030368339077422,80.30368339077421,High Trust
