Dave Johnson,/users/5b4c78084de5666d34c73bb1,GB,3.0,2024-04-13 18:55:41+00:00,1.0,First I'll start with the good stuff,"First I'll start with the good stuff. Shopping, quick delivery, Prime Video, Prime Music. Now the bad stuff. With the introduction of an extra £2.99 per month as a separate payment for Prime Video to remove adverts, I find it hard to trust Amazon anymore. When I signed the contract and paid for a year's subscription it stated advert-free movies and TV series. How can they suddenly decide that that is no longer true and you will now have to pay an extra fee? Now I'm wondering what else they are going to charge extra for, next-day delivery, Amazon Music, and Photo storage. My trust in Amazon has gone.",2024-04-13 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,13.0,606,109,36,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,first ill start good stuff shopping quick delivery prime video prime music bad stuff introduction extra £ per month separate payment prime video remove advert find hard trust amazon anymore signed contract paid year subscription stated advertfree movie tv series suddenly decide longer true pay extra fee im wondering else going charge extra nextday delivery amazon music photo storage trust amazon gone,0.016730834594756605,0.9832691654052435,0.061132922041503085,0.2,0.8038611671109223,80.38611671109223,High Trust
