Yusuf Aly,/users/660f97822ed44a0012c24a42,GB,1.0,2024-04-05 08:22:22+00:00,1.0,Amazon security is rubbish,"Amazon security is rubbish. Our family Amazon account has been fully hacked, and our hacker easily managed to change our account phone number, email and password on our Amazon account without a single barrier stopping that hacker. Now our hacker has access to our home address and bank cards in our Amazon account, which is really worrying. We received an email from Amazon that our old email address A has been changed to the new email address B, which was shocking because we never changed our email address. Amazon could have send us a link in that same email to give an option to undo this email change if it wasn't us, something that all big companies have for their customer account like gmail. Or Amazon could have send a code to our phone number or old email address that our hacker needed access to before that hacker could change our account email address or password so basically some sort of security barrier, but clearly Amazon thought that there was no need for any of these barrier even if everyones Amazon account contains peoples bank card and personal details plus our hacker can freely order stuff on our account and properly will do other suspicious acts. Who ever made Amazon website have clearly lacked some simple security standards. I called Amazon customer service (which Amazon customer service was hard to find because we didn't have access to our Amazon account) and they said that they cannot close our account that has been hacked because the email and phone number has been changed by our hacker and we also can no longer access it.",2024-04-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,5.0,1563,273,26,4,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon security rubbish family amazon account fully hacked hacker easily managed change account phone number email password amazon account without single barrier stopping hacker hacker access home address bank card amazon account really worrying received email amazon old email address changed new email address b shocking never changed email address amazon could send u link email give option undo email change wasnt u something big company customer account like gmail amazon could send code phone number old email address hacker needed access hacker could change account email address password basically sort security barrier clearly amazon thought need barrier even everyones amazon account contains people bank card personal detail plus hacker freely order stuff account properly suspicious act ever made amazon website clearly lacked simple security standard called amazon customer service amazon customer service hard find didnt access amazon account said cannot close account hacked email phone number changed hacker also longer access,0.018327652398157705,0.9816723476018423,0.1531127313516545,0.2,0.821458720071252,82.14587200712519,High Trust
