Todd Brogowski,/users/66071746fd25b100113601c0,US,4.0,2024-03-29 21:40:04+00:00,1.0,Counterfeit goods and long delays,"I have been struggling with Amazon since the pandemic started five years ago. I live in rural America and rely on Amazon as it eliminates hours of driving to stores. However, lately, I can't seem to avoid counterfeit products with them, such as sneakers, batteries, and lightbulbs. Delivery has gotten slower and slower; I'm now averaging two weeks' delivery time, which means that it's actually more convenient to go to the store. That's *with* Amazon Prime membership, which, for $130/year, does not seem to provide the same fast shipping it used to. Given Amazon's horrible labor practices, its non-responsive customer service, and the frequency of counterfeit goods, I am going to try to stay away from them as much as I can.",2024-03-28 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,29.0,729,122,33,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,struggling amazon since pandemic started five year ago live rural america rely amazon eliminates hour driving store however lately cant seem avoid counterfeit product sneaker battery lightbulb delivery gotten slower slower im averaging two week delivery time mean actually convenient go store thats amazon prime membership year seem provide fast shipping used given amazon horrible labor practice nonresponsive customer service frequency counterfeit good going try stay away much,0.021592759603910147,0.9784072403960898,0.06842400448681997,0.2,0.8028884210954089,80.2888421095409,High Trust
