Manickam Hellmuth,/users/6603d17244935e00127e3b6c,US,1.0,2024-03-27 09:57:53+00:00,1.0,I've been a pretty frequent amazon…,"I've been a pretty frequent amazon customer over at least the last two decades. The downfall started with a decision to purchase a macbook pro for around $3000. A large purchase, but I had confidence that if anything went wrong amazon would right things quickly. I received a one time passcode or OTP as they refer to it. I greeted the amazon delivery person, I gave him the passcode several times- he kept repeating it back incorrectly. I took the package and remarked to my girlfriend that man they make macs light these days. I opened the package to find an obviously used and abused macbook box. I opened the box with an ever increasing heart rate as I knew at this point my worst fears were about to be realized. It was EMPTY! My girlfriend rushed out the door to the driver who was just down the street. He stated you want to look in the back of my truck? Nothing I can do, call amazon support. Of course I called right away. I sat on hold for at least 30-40 mins. Amazon's first attempt at resolving the issue was to tell me there was nothing that could be done since I gave them the OTP- they stated I should call the police???!!!! When I refused and stated I had already wasted my day with this whole situation they put me on hold again for many minutes. They finally returned and refunded my order. This person refunded me with the most disgust I've ever experienced in my years of customer service. She quickly said bye, none of the usual thanks for being an amazon customer... Little did I know the issues would only continue from here. Later that evening I received an email stating my account had most likely been hacked and all my orders were cancelled. Next I came to find out that any order around $100+ would require a OTP- meaning they send you a passcode via email a couple hrs before your order arrives that you're forced to give to the delivery person- meaning you have to be present all day long if you actually want to receive your order. That's exactly the opposite of what amazon was designed to be. I called in multiple times to have this obstruction / inconvenience removed. One person from logistics stated maybe I should buy my macbook from apple like he did? I asked if he ever bought anything on amazon for $100+ he stated no. After talking to several more people from all over the world one person agreed to give me a partial refund of around $79 of the $139 I was so exhausted I agreed to it. I now realize that it makes no sense, given it's only almost April 1st and a prorated refund would be $100+??? This has been a pretty ridiculous experience to say the least. I repeated my grievances multiple times and I don't think one person understood once, much less did they try and correct it or provide any kind of customer service. PS I'm still waiting for my $79 refund... ",2024-03-26 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,27.0,2808,520,35,6,1.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,ive pretty frequent amazon customer least last two decade downfall started decision purchase macbook pro around large purchase confidence anything went wrong amazon would right thing quickly received one time passcode otp refer greeted amazon delivery person gave passcode several time kept repeating back incorrectly took package remarked girlfriend man make mac light day opened package find obviously used abused macbook box opened box ever increasing heart rate knew point worst fear realized empty girlfriend rushed door driver street stated want look back truck nothing call amazon support course called right away sat hold least min amazon first attempt resolving issue tell nothing could done since gave otp stated call police refused stated already wasted day whole situation put hold many minute finally returned refunded order person refunded disgust ive ever experienced year customer service quickly said bye none usual thanks amazon customer little know issue would continue later evening received email stating account likely hacked order cancelled next came find order around would require otp meaning send passcode via email couple hr order arrives youre forced give delivery person meaning present day long actually want receive order thats exactly opposite amazon designed called multiple time obstruction inconvenience removed one person logistics stated maybe buy macbook apple like asked ever bought anything amazon stated talking several people world one person agreed give partial refund around exhausted agreed realize make sense given almost april st prorated refund would pretty ridiculous experience say least repeated grievance multiple time dont think one person understood much less try correct provide kind customer service p im still waiting refund,0.8945480207148034,0.10545197928519656,0.2916432978126753,0.2,0.41105464920513335,41.105464920513334,Low Trust
