damian ritter,/users/6602f7999dd6780011ae3b82,US,1.0,2024-03-26 18:28:20+00:00,1.0,Fraud scam and defamation ,I bought this pc 3 weeks ago from Amazon. Its supposed to be an i7 with an rtx 3060 it came in with a i5 I wrote a review and sent it back. Got accused of switching the cpu and denied my refund. They then removed the 831 reviews since novemeber most of which pointing out power issues (they shut down n won't turn back on) I'm now being told by Amazon they will not honor their guarantee and have backed the seller claiming that I switched the cpu. I will be suing the company and looking into a lawsuit against Amazon as well for covering up the third parties actions. The saler was pro refurbished the model was from tech magnet and so is their support line. Do not buy from them. Also any suggestions for legal actions I'm talking to a lawyer but since they deleted the reviews I'm not sure I have much of a case unless we could push for data on the reviews if there's a back up anywhere,2024-03-26 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,26.0,890,174,26,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,bought pc week ago amazon supposed rtx came wrote review sent back got accused switching cpu denied refund removed review since novemeber pointing power issue shut n wont turn back im told amazon honor guarantee backed seller claiming switched cpu suing company looking lawsuit amazon well covering third party action saler pro refurbished model tech magnet support line buy also suggestion legal action im talking lawyer since deleted review im sure much case unless could push data review there back anywhere,0.013284488289855697,0.9867155117101443,0.0975883342680875,0.2,0.8128754227086896,81.28754227086897,High Trust
