Susan Larson,/users/6601f8cc830fec001289c096,CA,1.0,2024-03-26 00:51:59+00:00,3.0,Sharp decline in service,"Sharp decline in service. When I started using Amazon about a year ago my main concern was if I could return items if they didn't work out. I tore up my knee and can't get out to do my purchases and Prime seemed to be a good option aat that time. I could use Prime video and returns were easy. I could take my return to the UPS store half a blck away and they would print my label, scan the item and done!  Recently everything has changed for the worse. They no longer use the same courier company and all the options for drop off are too far for me due to the mobility issues. The free pick up option looks good until you spend the entire day waiting for the pick-up only to get notified at 9pm that you have been rescheduled for the next day. This goes on for days sometimes. I'm sorry, you wanted to shower or take your dog out to pee? Too bad. Most recently I recieved the okay from customer service to leave my pick up at the door and when I got out of the shower they had only picked up one of the two items that were in the same box. By the way, contacting customer service is almost impossible. Good luck finding the link to request a call or actually talking to a person. The AI call doesn't give you the option to talk to a person, you have to know to say ""talk to a person"". The chat doesn't actually chat, it is just more self help. They don't want to know what their customers think.Then there is Prime Video. All the shows I was watching suddenly came with a price tag. The garbage that was left has comercials and isn't worth watching. I haven't watched anything on Prime for weeks. I bought one movie that I will say goodbye to if I cancel but it may be worth it.As for the products, hit or miss as usual. If I am familiar with a brand and it works for me it is usually a safe bet. Otherwise it definitely is a gamble.",2024-03-25 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,26.0,1834,363,24,4,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,sharp decline service started using amazon year ago main concern could return item didnt work tore knee cant get purchase prime seemed good option aat time could use prime video return easy could take return ups store half blck away would print label scan item done recently everything changed worse longer use courier company option drop far due mobility issue free pick option look good spend entire day waiting pickup get notified pm rescheduled next day go day sometimes im sorry wanted shower take dog pee bad recently recieved okay customer service leave pick door got shower picked one two item box way contacting customer service almost impossible good luck finding link request call actually talking person ai call doesnt give option talk person know say talk person chat doesnt actually chat self help dont want know customer thinkthen prime video show watching suddenly came price tag garbage left comercials isnt worth watching havent watched anything prime week bought one movie say goodbye cancel may worth itas product hit miss usual familiar brand work usually safe bet otherwise definitely gamble,0.05252643180772223,0.9474735681922778,0.2035894559730791,0.6,1.4144546752907545,141.44546752907544,High Trust
GuBeFa,/users/5f454423768213cf90f0f539,DE,12.0,2024-03-25 22:22:29+00:00,1.0,Amazon astonishing requests to modify one's PW,"I've had an Amazon account for years but, at times they send codes via discontinued phone numbers. I called Amazon where I was asked for my full name, email and street address, and the last 4 of my credit card number. I would have thought these data identified me but oh no.! there were more questions: last purchases during the last 3 months; items you  placed in 'keep for later'; etc. It took several calls and over 2 hours to reset my PW and remove the two-step verification. Let's hope it stays that way!   ",2024-03-23 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,25.0,512,94,46,7,2.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,ive amazon account year time send code via discontinued phone number called amazon asked full name email street address last credit card number would thought data identified oh question last purchase last month item placed keep later etc took several call hour reset pw remove twostep verification let hope stay way,0.22760186513987177,0.7723981348601282,0.05272013460459899,0.2,0.6967430943509839,69.6743094350984,Medium Trust
Priscilla,/users/63deda869ee43700121979b6,US,2.0,2024-03-26 19:04:00+00:00,1.0,It’s a scam now,"I have been an Amazon Prime member for numerous years. I am well aware of the purchase and return process. However, about three months ago, I have noticed a huge change in the return process. I ordered a small piece of furniture, worth $181.00. The item was damaged upon opening. I quickly filed a return on Amazon. I went to UPS, with the affixed label that I was provided, and they explained, I had to pay $240.00 in order to ship it back. The return label was not paid for by Amazon. I only had the item for less than a week and it was damaged. Why would any company expect me to pay that amount to ship it back? I have called Amazon at least a dozen times and every time I talk to someone new, I get a new answer. It’s a third party seller and we don’t get involved in that. After waiting three weeks with getting absolutely nowhere, I filed a dispute with American Express. Thank gosh for them because I would have never received a refund. I made the mistake and gave Amazon another try and ordered a bathingsuit a month ago. Here we go again! I returned it via post office per Amazon, with a delivery address to New Jersey, and item was delivered but no refund. Again, a third party seller. Even though, return address is in New Jersey. I had to call Amazon ten times so far and the A - Z process is ridiculous! They act like they are helping but they don’t! I am cancelling my Prime Membership and will never deal with this nonsense again! I heard that Amazon company sold off to third party sellers so buyers beware!! It’s scan now, if you ask me!",2024-01-24 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,26.0,1555,297,15,4,62.0,0,7,1,0,Genuine,amazon prime member numerous year well aware purchase return process however three month ago noticed huge change return process ordered small piece furniture worth item damaged upon opening quickly filed return amazon went ups affixed label provided explained pay order ship back return label paid amazon item less week damaged would company expect pay amount ship back called amazon least dozen time every time talk someone new get new answer it’s third party seller don’t get involved waiting three week getting absolutely nowhere filed dispute american express thank gosh would never received refund made mistake gave amazon another try ordered bathingsuit month ago go returned via post office per amazon delivery address new jersey item delivered refund third party seller even though return address new jersey call amazon ten time far z process ridiculous act like helping don’t cancelling prime membership never deal nonsense heard amazon company sold third party seller buyer beware it’s scan ask,0.9929218085481681,0.007078191451831861,0.16657319125070105,0.2,0.3368537339760561,33.68537339760561,Low Trust
