Maureen,/users/658cbab7f554990012728e17,US,2.0,2024-03-24 21:57:31+00:00,1.0,Amazon issuing gift cards instead of refunds for returns,"I ordered and returned a number of items from Amazon.com in the month of February. Instead of the refunds being returned to the credit card I'd used to purchase them, Amazon took it upon themselves to open an Amazon gift card for me. This is so unethical it leaves me speechless. I was never notified that they were doing this, so if I hadn't placed an order in March I wouldn't have known I had several hundred dollars sitting on a gift card with my name on it. The customer service person did his best to transfer the refunded money back to my credit card but it will take another week for it to show up on my credit card -- so Amazon has had the use of my money for a month and I'm paying interest on money that should have gone back onto my credit card. I'd have given them 0 stars, if that were possible.",2024-03-23 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,24.0,809,158,56,9,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered returned number item amazoncom month february instead refund returned credit card id used purchase amazon took upon open amazon gift card unethical leaf speechless never notified hadnt placed order march wouldnt known several hundred dollar sitting gift card name customer service person best transfer refunded money back credit card take another week show credit card amazon use money month im paying interest money gone back onto credit card id given star possible,0.013829090536038003,0.986170909463962,0.0886146943353898,0.2,0.810808393599059,81.0808393599059,High Trust
Reasonably Real,/users/65dbfd5723fcd900124275bc,US,5.0,2024-03-24 21:49:50+00:00,3.0,Consumer Positive and a Seller Negative,"Once upon a time, in the magical land of Amazon.com, I embarked on a quest to buy a variety of items and even sell some of my own. Little did I know that this journey would be filled with both laughter and bewilderment.As a buyer, my experience has been mostly positive. Amazon's vast selection of products and speedy delivery make it a convenient choice for all your shopping needs. However, there have been times when I've encountered the occasional weirdness with returns. It's like trying to find a needle in a haystack while blindfolded and hopping on one foot.But fear not, dear reader, for I have discovered a hidden treasure! On rare occasions, I've managed to summon a human customer service representative. These elusive creatures are surprisingly pleasant and possess the power to make your problems disappear with a wave of their magical wand.Now, let's talk about the dark side of Amazon: the seller experience. As a small business owner, I must warn you that Amazon is a greedy and ridiculous platform. It's like a dragon hoarding all the gold and leaving you with just a few measly coins. Their policies are designed to maximize their own profits, leaving sellers feeling like they're on a never-ending quest for fairness.To all aspiring merchants out there, I would advise you to tread carefully in the treacherous realm of Amazon. Offer your products on their platform to reach a wider audience, but don't put all your eggs in this basket. Instead, create your own enchanted website and offer your wares at a slightly lower price. It's like offering a secret discount to those who dare to venture beyond the Amazon kingdom.In conclusion, dear reader, Amazon.com is a land of contrasts. As a consumer, you'll likely have a good experience, but as a seller, be prepared for a wild and unpredictable journey. So, gather your courage, sharpen your wit, and may the odds be ever in your favor!",2024-03-23 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,24.0,1905,324,39,6,1.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,upon time magical land amazoncom embarked quest buy variety item even sell little know journey would filled laughter bewildermentas buyer experience mostly positive amazon vast selection product speedy delivery make convenient choice shopping need however time ive encountered occasional weirdness return like trying find needle haystack blindfolded hopping one footbut fear dear reader discovered hidden treasure rare occasion ive managed summon human customer service representative elusive creature surprisingly pleasant possess power make problem disappear wave magical wandnow let talk dark side amazon seller experience small business owner must warn amazon greedy ridiculous platform like dragon hoarding gold leaving measly coin policy designed maximize profit leaving seller feeling like theyre neverending quest fairnessto aspiring merchant would advise tread carefully treacherous realm amazon offer product platform reach wider audience dont put egg basket instead create enchanted website offer ware slightly lower price like offering secret discount dare venture beyond amazon kingdomin conclusion dear reader amazoncom land contrast consumer youll likely good experience seller prepared wild unpredictable journey gather courage sharpen wit may odds ever favor,0.0652914015602538,0.9347085984397462,0.18171620863712842,0.6,1.4036975409472987,140.36975409472987,High Trust
Jim Ruiz,/users/5c94176ecececa8076c09150,US,3.0,2024-03-24 21:49:04+00:00,1.0,Amazon Switching Customer Payment Methods for Financial Gain,"I have been a Prime customer for years. Apparently, their new CEO is using tactics to increase shareholder wealth. I ordered a faucet and charged it to my Mastercard. When the order was shipped, I noticed it was charged to my Amazon Card. I didn't even open the package and returned the item for this reason thinking I would get a credit to my Amazon Card. I found out they gave me an Amazon Gift Card and my next two orders that I charged to my Visa were charged to my Amazon gift card. Now they say I can't get a credit to my Amazon Card because these last two orders were charged to my gift card. I now owe something I do not own, and they are charging me interest for nonpayment on my Amazon Card. Unacceptable for Amazon to switch my payment methods for their financial gain. I have a paper trail to prove this. That's what happens with Monopolies.",2024-01-11 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,24.0,853,162,60,8,73.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,prime customer year apparently new ceo using tactic increase shareholder wealth ordered faucet charged mastercard order shipped noticed charged amazon card didnt even open package returned item reason thinking would get credit amazon card found gave amazon gift card next two order charged visa charged amazon gift card say cant get credit amazon card last two order charged gift card owe something charging interest nonpayment amazon card unacceptable amazon switch payment method financial gain paper trail prove thats happens monopoly,0.004358193036175454,0.9956418069638245,0.09085810431856421,0.2,0.8159925243456251,81.5992524345625,High Trust
