Matt Thompson,/users/63765bbe9b534e00138dbc9e,MT,6.0,2024-03-24 15:41:40+00:00,1.0,Some of the worst customer service i've…,"Some of the worst customer service i've ever experienced just trying to log in to my account. When logging in they send you a verification text. I didn't receive this text message so tried again. No luck. So I attempted To reach customer service. To do this is like cracking the enigma code and after the fourth person I spoke to I was told they couldn't verify me as I had only bought kindle products and not had anything delivered to my door in the past few months!? Any other company would have a simple re-verification process like asking you two security questions you set up when signing up and confirming your address, but not Amazon, you need to have had something delivered to your door!? I've used your service so why can't you verify who I am? These companies get so big and monopolise their space that the customer no longer becomes important to them - only the shareholders, which I was one of, but as on Monday will no longer be. ",2024-03-24 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,24.0,944,173,40,7,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,worst customer service ive ever experienced trying log account logging send verification text didnt receive text message tried luck attempted reach customer service like cracking enigma code fourth person spoke told couldnt verify bought kindle product anything delivered door past month company would simple reverification process like asking two security question set signing confirming address amazon need something delivered door ive used service cant verify company get big monopolise space customer longer becomes important shareholder one monday longer,0.28823438435041865,0.7117656156495813,0.09702748177229388,0.2,0.6752883041792495,67.52883041792495,Medium Trust
