Michael Winkler,/users/65fb82f1ae740b0011982ead,US,1.0,2024-03-21 02:49:18+00:00,1.0,"Decline of Amazon, WTH?","Over the past two years, the service at Amazon has steadily declined.  I've had multiple gifts that were ordered, not make it in time for birthdays or Christmases. These were not spur of the moment orders, but orders made several weeks in advance. It seems to become the norm for delivery dates to be changed after the orders are made. I had been waiting on a product that Amazon told me was out for delivery today, just to be told now that it is delayed in transit and won't arrive for seven more days. How is that even possible?! This will cause me to miss an event I was looking forward to take part in.I've been a Prime member for several years now and the little perks that used to be enjoyed are also going away. Programs with commercials is the latest downgrade as of late. Really starting to question why I'm a Prime member any more.  People wonder why so many Americans order from Chinese businesses, and the answer is becoming crystal clear. ",2024-03-20 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,21.0,952,174,23,4,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,past two year service amazon steadily declined ive multiple gift ordered make time birthday christmas spur moment order order made several week advance seems become norm delivery date changed order made waiting product amazon told delivery today told delayed transit wont arrive seven day even possible cause miss event looking forward take part inive prime member several year little perk used enjoyed also going away program commercial latest downgrade late really starting question im prime member people wonder many american order chinese business answer becoming crystal clear,0.028194602375362636,0.9718053976246374,0.0975883342680875,0.2,0.8054203656659362,80.54203656659362,High Trust
