Dazza smith,/users/5d5d7fd621e4e32ba9d33afb,GB,5.0,2024-03-20 16:14:24+00:00,1.0,Attempted to reinform customer service…,"Attempted to reinform customer service today, and at least expected to receive some Tech Support for prolific hacking of my paid Music Unlimited and paid Prime Video accounts.This had been reported to Police and Action Fraud, for some time now.Been a paying customer since 2015.This involved hijacking of my account through my devices and the downloading of movies and music from individuals I had identified, to the authorities.The fraudulent linking of much equipment such as a Fire-stick which I have never owned, in the registered devices menu.On calling customer service to end these paid services due to this intrusion, I received a Scottish Lady who seemed helpful but when she informed me I was being passed onto tech support I was left on and then hung up on.Second call to customer services involved attempting to communicate with a sarcastic female who did not seem interested, gave long deliberate hmmmms and asaaahs and told me tech support wasn't on call.I asked why and she just repeated the same answer.I then received an email from this agent informing me that she was ending my services, deleting all accounts and data records from my memberships of paid Prime services with Amazon.I had not requested this and found this suspicious, considering the continuous hacking and downloading of data from Music  unlimited and Prime video account of mine, which I had paid for and as I had reported.Third operator seemed marginally interested enough to correct this involuntary action by the previous operator.It seems a dark cloud has descended on Amazon on multiple levels and I won't be paying for any more services untill this has lifted.",2024-03-20 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,20.0,1652,271,39,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,attempted reinform customer service today least expected receive tech support prolific hacking paid music unlimited paid prime video accountsthis re