Norberto Montesino,/users/65b7a91eb3888d0012534a4a,US,5.0,2024-03-16 17:50:48+00:00,1.0,Don't Trust Replacements,"On October 15, 2023 I had purchased at Amazon a BARWING Adjustable Weight Bench. I notice that the box was damaged and heard like moving broken pieces inside the box. After opening the box, the plastic seal cap was broken in pieces, and the center folding alloy Steel where the plastic seal cap is attached was bended. I contacted Amazon customer service regarding this issue and was told that there was no need to return the item, that I could keep it or give it to someone or to discard it, and a replacement was sent. Now On March 11, 2024 I was charged again and it has been posted to my banc card. Now Amazon is justifying and saying that the return window date has been closed and they can't refund the damaged merchandise. I have summited the complaint to my card member services claims department for damaged merchandise, and waiting for this refund resolution. My advice is, if you opt for a replacement don't do it, rather return the item and purchase it again.",2023-10-15 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,16.0,971,176,24,3,153.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,october purchased amazon barwing adjustable weight bench notice box damaged heard like moving broken piece inside box opening box plastic seal cap broken piece center folding alloy steel plastic seal cap attached bended contacted amazon customer service regarding issue told need return item could keep give someone discard replacement sent march charged posted banc card amazon justifying saying return window date closed cant refund damaged merchandise summited complaint card member service claim department damaged merchandise waiting refund resolution advice opt replacement dont rather return item purchase,0.0035134888188235454,0.9964865111811765,0.09871003925967471,0.2,0.8179852634425232,81.79852634425232,High Trust
