"Cha, Cha, Cha Chia Chia",/users/616ebeb1272e970013c8f8e3,US,7.0,2024-03-13 04:03:16+00:00,1.0,Amazon's Seller Policies Facilitate Fraud and Exploit Sellers,"As a seller on Amazon's platform, I must express my utter disappointment and frustration with their blatant disregard for the well-being of their sellers. It's evident that Amazon prioritizes profit over the integrity of its marketplace, as they consistently side with consumers even in cases of obvious fraud, leaving sellers to bear the brunt of the consequences.One of the most egregious issues plaguing Amazon's marketplace is their lenient approach towards fraudulent claims made by customers. Despite ample evidence proving that customers have received the items they ordered, Amazon readily refunds them at the expense of the sellers. This not only results in financial losses for sellers but also creates an environment ripe for exploitation.The fact that Amazon retains the fees they charge sellers, even in cases of fraudulent refunds, highlights their complete lack of accountability. Sellers invest their time, resources, and efforts into the platform, only to be met with indifference and exploitation by Amazon.Unlike on my own website, where stringent policies deter fraudulent activities, Amazon's lax approach enables customers to exploit the system with impunity. The frequency of such occurrences is alarming and severely undermines the profitability of selling on Amazon.It's evident that Amazon's policies are designed to prioritize market share over the well-being of sellers. Their relentless pursuit of dominance in the e-commerce industry has led them to sacrifice the livelihoods of countless sellers in the process. It's high time that sellers unite and hold Amazon accountable for their unethical practices.In conclusion, Amazon's facilitation of fraud and exploitation of sellers is unacceptable. Their policies not only undermine the integrity of the marketplace but also pose a significant threat to the livelihoods of sellers. It's imperative that sellers take a stand against such injustice and demand accountability from Amazon.",2024-03-12 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,13.0,1962,290,61,8,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,seller amazon platform must express utter disappointment frustration blatant disregard wellbeing seller evident amazon prioritizes profit integrity marketplace consistently side consumer even case obvious fraud leaving seller bear brunt consequencesone egregious issue plaguing amazon marketplace lenient approach towards fraudulent claim made customer despite ample evidence proving customer received item ordered amazon readily refund expense seller result financial loss seller also creates environment ripe exploitationthe fact amazon retains fee charge seller even case fraudulent refund highlight complete lack accountability seller invest time resource effort platform met indifference exploitation amazonunlike website stringent policy deter fraudulent activity amazon lax approach enables customer exploit system impunity frequency occurrence alarming severely undermines profitability selling amazonits evident amazon policy designed prioritize market share wellbeing seller relentless pursuit dominance ecommerce industry led sacrifice livelihood countless seller process high time seller unite hold amazon accountable unethical practicesin conclusion amazon facilitation fraud exploitation seller unacceptable policy undermine integrity marketplace also pose significant threat livelihood seller imperative seller take stand injustice demand accountability amazon,0.006472663692210358,0.9935273363077897,0.16264722378014582,0.2,0.8292931129099239,82.92931129099239,High Trust
Thegrandcanyon Izegypt,/users/623ba3d003b9d60012210f5b,US,6.0,2024-04-03 04:24:01+00:00,2.0,disgusting used items sold as new,"i ordered another blanket from amazon & got another 1 that is SMELLY, SOILED & clearly USED, its also shrunk, like its been washed. I should have known better when i got a drill kit w/ food stains on it & they replaced it  w/ another used product w/  half the drill bits missing. Things have really taken a turn for the worse since they changed to foreign CEOs. This appears to be the new standard. I have to wonder if their underwear, baby clothes etc are being sold under “lightning deals”, which actually means their selling you used filthy  items. ",2024-03-13 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,4.0,3.0,552,101,33,6,21.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered another blanket amazon got another smelly soiled clearly used also shrunk like washed known better got drill kit w food stain replaced w another used product w half drill bit missing thing really taken turn worse since changed foreign ceo appears new standard wonder underwear baby clothes etc sold “lightning deals” actually mean selling used filthy item,0.007289271049248127,0.9927107289507519,0.056646102075154234,0.4,1.1076845848904067,110.76845848904067,High Trust
