CM,/users/5c72d51cfb89ee597e4b170d,US,2.0,2024-03-12 18:49:05+00:00,1.0,Amazon NOT honoring DEFAULT addresses,"I've been an Amazon customer from the beginning - when people were afraid to put their cc# online. However in the past 9-12 months, Amazon is no longer honoring DEFAULT addresses. It will randomly send shipments to other addresses in your address book, even if the last 5 went to your default. I called customer service and they said it's because I ordered it BUY NOW. But, it says in their fine print that Buy Now orders go to default payment + address. Customer service used to be amazing, but now is abysmal. I think it's time to cut the cord. There are plenty of other companies who want my business. I do hope the lawyers add this DEFAULT address issue to their class action suit against Amazon for charging Prime members fees to remove commercials. A quick Google of the issue shows that it's a major problem. Default addresses have worked until the past year, so trust it's just another money grab. ",2024-03-11 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,12.0,906,163,37,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ive amazon customer beginning people afraid put cc online however past month amazon longer honoring default address randomly send shipment address address book even last went default called customer service said ordered buy say fine print buy order go default payment address customer service used amazing abysmal think time cut cord plenty company want business hope lawyer add default address issue class action suit amazon charging prime member fee remove commercial quick google issue show major problem default address worked past year trust another money grab,0.007467605534520703,0.9925323944654793,0.09141895681435783,0.2,0.8145499885956112,81.45499885956113,High Trust
Patrick,/users/63f60b4ad24cee00122a7d6c,GB,6.0,2024-03-12 14:26:09+00:00,1.0,Amazon disapponts,"Amazon encourages the customer to use pick-up points. And so I did. In September 2023 I purchased a book to pick up at a pick-up point. The book is set to be delivered in April 2024. That is 7 months later. In January I ordered 2 books, both are set to be delivered at a pick up point in August. Again, 7 months later. This morning I ordered 2 books. First I selected the pick up point. It said that they would be delivered in December. I reconsidered and selected my home address. Now it says that they will be delivered next week. WHAT SCAM ARE THEY RUNNING? I contacted customer support. After some waffling (what a waste of time), they said they couldn't do anything about it. I was offered the option of premium (came with a £4 cost) and then -please sit down for this- the books would be delivered in September. SO DISAPPOINTED.",2024-03-12 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,12.0,834,156,17,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon encourages customer use pickup point september purchased book pick pickup point book set delivered april month later january ordered book set delivered pick point august month later morning ordered book first selected pick point said would delivered december reconsidered selected home address say delivered next week scam running contacted customer support waffling waste time said couldnt anything offered option premium came £ cost please sit book would delivered september disappointed,0.013036025808582647,0.9869639741914173,0.08749298934380258,0.2,0.8109805849644691,81.09805849644691,High Trust
