Laura K,/users/65ee5eb0c64a540012541730,US,1.0,2024-03-11 03:32:30+00:00,1.0,Reconsider your loyalty to this company.,"I have been a loyal customer to Amazon for 10+ years. My household items are practically all ordered on Amazon. I have never missed a return window. I started a return 2 weeks ago and then had a very stressful time with my family. I realized I missed bringing my items to UPS by a few days and contacted Amazon Customer Service for support. Customer service had me wait for 90+ minutes (first via a lost help chat and then via phone with long hold times and a transfer to a new team), only to tell me that there was nothing they would do for me.",2024-03-10 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,11.0,545,106,40,6,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,loyal customer amazon year household item practically ordered amazon never missed return window started return week ago stressful time family realized missed bringing item ups day contacted amazon customer service support customer service wait minute first via lost help chat via phone long hold time transfer new team tell nothing would,0.0054199957146256654,0.9945800042853743,0.05945036455412227,0.2,0.8091800750535116,80.91800750535117,High Trust
Teresa Neighbors,/users/65ee2b035a9c7700114ce025,US,1.0,2024-03-10 23:50:04+00:00,1.0,Amazon cheats and steals,"Amazon has resorted to cheating and illegal tactics.  They receive and accept items for return, process the return, and then weeks later, charge you for the return, citing that you must upload your photo identification, even though they accepted and received your items already, with no mention of that requirement anywhere in their policy.  And, at times, they insist that an item is not eligible for return, even if it says that it is eligible on the website and in your order details.",2024-03-09 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,10.0,487,83,24,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon resorted cheating illegal tactic receive accept item return process return week later charge return citing must upload photo identification even though accepted received item already mention requirement anywhere policy time insist item eligible return even say eligible website order detail,0.01792264110935753,0.9820773588906425,0.04655075715086932,0.2,0.8003488308754951,80.03488308754952,High Trust
Sara,/users/63ff7342fbfb53001255e45a,US,3.0,2024-03-10 23:33:23+00:00,1.0,File complaint with BBB if ARC does not respond,"Tired of waiting for ARC (Amazon Claims Department) to process my claim, I filed a complaint with the Better Business Bureau.  Within 12 HOURS I got two phone calls and an email from the lawyer representing ARC, expressing his wish to settle.  The next day, I got another email or phone call from the same lawyer. In the email he stated he agreed to what I had claimed.  And I gave the lawyer permission to cut the check by email. I am sharing this because I am so surprised at how expediently they want to avoid a lawsuit.  It must not look good to have high numbers of lawsuits filed against Amazon to report in their Annual Report to their shareholders.  ""Claim # AMZ.  Christina is the person handling the case.On a rainy day, an Amazon driver attempted to back out of my driveway, skidding down and running over my mailbox.  The van got stuck on the mailbox post, and a tow truck was called to pull out the van.  The damage to the lawn and the mailbox is well documented in video and photos, which ARC received.  Most recently, ARC stated that since I had filed for lawn damage 3 years ago, this is a repeat claim.   And demands that I submit a photo of the lawn repair from three years ago because the present lawn damage may be a replicated claim.  And I quote Christina from ARC representing Amazon.com.   ""As for the previous damages and showing the repairs, this is a new policy that has been put in place. Unfortunately this alerts us to people who have filed multiple times for damages.""  My argument is when new damages are inflicted by Amazon drivers,  Amazon should pay for damages no matter when it occurs.  When I sent her the email from three years ago, which never mentioned a photo she was using to reject the claim, she stated that she would look into it.  It is impossible to produce a photo from three years ago that was not taken or requested.  It is such a nonsense to reject a claim.  And Christina will ignore me until I bug her again; this has been going on for over THREE months!    It is utterly surprising that Amazon has resorted to this kind of CUSTOMER UNFRIENDLY practice.  Amazon.com is NOT a customer-friendly company!  I will file a claim with the small claims court.  I am so disappointed at how awful Amazon has turned out.  Seeing the same type of claim as mine here shows that this is not just one ARC representative who has gone rogue. It is Amazon's policy. ",2024-03-07 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,10.0,2402,438,47,9,3.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,tired waiting arc amazon claim department process claim filed complaint better business bureau within hour got two phone call email lawyer representing arc expressing wish settle next day got another email phone call lawyer email stated agreed claimed gave lawyer permission cut check email sharing surprised expediently want avoid lawsuit must look good high number lawsuit filed amazon report annual report shareholder claim amz christina person handling caseon rainy day amazon driver attempted back driveway skidding running mailbox van got stuck mailbox post tow truck called pull van damage lawn mailbox well documented video photo arc received recently arc stated since filed lawn damage year ago repeat claim demand submit photo lawn repair three year ago present lawn damage may replicated claim quote christina arc representing amazoncom previous damage showing repair new policy put place unfortunately alert u people filed multiple time damage argument new damage inflicted amazon driver amazon pay damage matter occurs sent email three year ago never mentioned photo using reject claim stated would look impossible produce photo three year ago taken requested nonsense reject claim christina ignore bug going three month utterly surprising amazon resorted kind customer unfriendly practice amazoncom customerfriendly company file claim small claim court disappointed awful amazon turned seeing type claim mine show one arc representative gone rogue amazon policy,0.1430407098959046,0.8569592901040954,0.24565339315759954,0.2,0.7776103236835675,77.76103236835675,High Trust
