A Adams,/users/595276470000ff000aa8ac14,GB,6.0,2024-03-03 04:56:48+00:00,1.0,Amazon is a plague on the planet earth,"It is a textbook example of capitalism gone mad. Squeeze out the competition to such a degree that you're answerable to no-one. Become such a monopoly that cities outbid each other to offer tax-incentives to build one of their modern day slavery 'fulfilment' centres in their locality. And when something goes wrong who is there to talk to? Chatbots, phonebots and livechat with Indians who have no authority to do anything but read out scripts. There is no accountability. And all the while we sit here addicted to plastic tat, fuming at delivery drivers who are paid peanuts per parcel, powerless as Amazon evades tax on an industrial scale while valued at multiple trillions of dollars. How are the state schools doing in your area? Hospitals? Police force well funded? Roads in good nick? No, they're not in my neighbourhood either. That's thanks to mega-corps like Amazon whose stock price has rocketed while your teachers and nurses go to food banks. ",2024-03-03 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,3.0,957,161,38,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,textbook example capitalism gone mad squeeze competition degree youre answerable noone become monopoly city outbid offer taxincentives build one modern day slavery fulfilment centre locality something go wrong talk chatbots phonebots livechat indian authority anything read script accountability sit addicted plastic tat fuming delivery driver paid peanut per parcel powerless amazon evades tax industrial scale valued multiple trillion dollar state school area hospital police force well funded road good nick theyre neighbourhood either thats thanks megacorps like amazon whose stock price rocketed teacher nurse go food bank,0.025234202874872755,0.9747657971251272,0.09029725182277061,0.2,0.8054423489271177,80.54423489271177,High Trust
