M E,/users/65e1f344251ec30012dd3aa0,US,1.0,2024-03-01 17:25:05+00:00,1.0,Try Before You Buy,"On Jan 21, I purchased an item with the ""Try Before You Buy"" program. On Jan 29, I returned the item as instructed to Amazon. There were two items in the box (also as instructed). The other item was received and  returned by the system on Feb 1. On Feb 18, I received an email informing me that the other item was not returned yet and if it did not get it returned by Feb 22, I would be charged for the item. I immediately contacted Amazon to inform them the item was already returned, but they told me they could not do anything until I my credit card was charged. My card was charged on Feb 23. I contacted Amazon immediately, and was told that the credit would happen. Two weeks later and over a dozen more conversations with Amazon, I finally got the credit today. Nightmare! If I had not stayed on top of this and been persistent, I would have paid for something I do not have. Will never use this service again.",2024-03-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,1.0,917,176,18,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,jan purchased item try buy program jan returned item instructed amazon two item box also instructed item received returned system feb feb received email informing item returned yet get returned feb would charged item immediately contacted amazon inform item already returned told could anything credit card charged card charged feb contacted amazon immediately told credit would happen two week later dozen conversation amazon finally got credit today nightmare stayed top persistent would paid something never use service,0.09887555865860417,0.9011244413413958,0.09871003925967471,0.2,0.7703042285226328,77.03042285226329,High Trust
