Me,/users/57deba260000ff000a457be0,US,57.0,2024-02-20 04:47:34+00:00,1.0,New and improved scammy behavior,"So I ordered an item, they sent me the wrong variation of the item obviously on purpose since they have started scamming even their prime customers as featured in business insider ""No more free ride"" article. In order to return my item they literally wanted to rob me of half the cost of the item and I did not know it until post purchase which is known as lying by omission. So that would mean if I wanted the color I actually ordered they would get half the money from me returning the wrong one they sent me and them a whole orders worth of money from the second order and act like I'm stupid and don't know what they are up to. Also the whole ""verify by a third party"" to see if you qualify for amazon prime access program. That option doesn't exist and even if I was interested I would not give a scammy billion dollar company that has no respect for their customers or employees my sensitive documents. They want to play stupid games, the best thing is to let them have the dummy prize of not having our business or so much less business that it hurt them. I called them out on this in my review of the item and they refuse to post it, so they know what they are doing. We have been hurting since covid and the inflation. The only way not to lose more money is to not shop at places where they are actively trying to find new and creative (lying by omission is an old tried and true, not creative) ways of trying trying to rob people of their money in this heavily inflated ""economy."" Shop where you know your getting a good/great deal and not constantly having to fight not to be parted with money that you know is yours. Amazon thrives from wearing their customers down to the point of making them give up on refunds and returns. One of their best scams is messing up people's orders or them not getting delivered at all and then claiming a person has had too many returns. I personally am not the one.",2024-02-17 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,20.0,1910,365,32,5,3.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered item sent wrong variation item obviously purpose since started scamming even prime customer featured business insider free ride article order return item literally wanted rob half cost item know post purchase known lying omission would mean wanted color actually ordered would get half money returning wrong one sent whole order worth money second order act like im stupid dont know also whole verify third party see qualify amazon prime access program option doesnt exist even interested would give scammy billion dollar company respect customer employee sensitive document want play stupid game best thing let dummy prize business much less business hurt called review item refuse post know hurting since covid inflation way lose money shop place actively trying find new creative lying omission old tried true creative way trying trying rob people money heavily inflated economy shop know getting goodgreat deal constantly fight parted money know amazon thrives wearing customer point making give refund return one best scam messing people order getting delivered claiming person many return personally one,0.035335216503469706,0.9646647834965303,0.2047111609646663,0.2,0.8232746239411984,82.32746239411985,High Trust
