"David in Austin, TX",/users/5f0faa9b0f0f841d2dfc75ba,US,3.0,2024-02-15 06:12:19+00:00,1.0,Amazon Key Installer Damaged Our Locks,"Amazon Business Key installer came out our multifamily condo complex at 11:21pm and decided they would disassemble the two postal style locks on our gate control box and cut the added chain to gain access to our control panel and install their hardware. This is ridiculous at best. Who the f$#k do they think they are? We are considering pressing charges as it is all on recorded camera footage. First to come out at 11:20pm is a bit shady, and then to damage our locks and cut out chain and twist and bend the (brand new!!) gate control box cover is just uncalled for. Amazon Business Key is nothing to begin with. For our property,  the driver still has to enter a code on his/her phone (or something similar) to send to the gate controller to open the gate. It takes no longer amount of time for the driver to reach out the window and enter a four digit code to open gate. Amazon has gone too far this time. Showing up at 11:20 in the dark of night to cut our chains and damage our locks is not acceptable.",2024-02-07 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,15.0,1009,190,38,6,8.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,amazon business key installer came multifamily condo complex pm decided would disassemble two postal style lock gate control box cut added chain gain access control panel install hardware ridiculous best fk think considering pressing charge recorded camera footage first come pm bit shady damage lock cut chain twist bend brand new gate control box cover uncalled amazon business key nothing begin property driver still enter code hisher phone something similar send gate controller open gate take longer amount time driver reach window enter four digit code open gate amazon gone far time showing dark night cut chain damage lock acceptable,0.2113844413906303,0.7886155586093697,0.1065619742007852,0.2,0.7156201741448418,71.56201741448417,Medium Trust
Wayne Carpenter,/users/5fee4acffadb0900197a21cf,US,5.0,2024-02-15 05:03:53+00:00,1.0,Poor Customer Service,"I called because a product could not be shipped to me at my address in the US although another product by the same manufacturer could. I had to ""battle"" with the IVR (Automated phone thing) and was eventually connected to a person who had to validate me. After he did, at around seven minutes, he just ""disappeared"" and said nothing on the phone. I called again and ""battled"" with the IVR. A man answered but could not explain properly why the problem I had occurred---it didn't make sense, so I disconnected the call.",2024-02-14 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,15.0,518,93,21,3,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,called product could shipped address u although another product manufacturer could battle ivr automated phone thing eventually connected person validate around seven minute disappeared said nothing phone called battled ivr man answered could explain properly problem occurredit didnt make sense disconnected call,0.051774298107678696,0.9482257018923212,0.05215928210880538,0.2,0.7845447073679216,78.45447073679216,High Trust
Julie Gross,/users/65cd77d8304c3200128205dc,US,1.0,2024-02-15 04:37:39+00:00,1.0,Avoid Purchasing from Third Party…,"Avoid Purchasing from Third Party Sellers on AmazonI recently purchased an item through Amazon that was sold by a third party seller. During shipping, the carrier marked the package as ""incorrect address"" without attempting delivery and said it would be returned to sender.After weeks of trying to get this resolved, neither the carrier nor third party seller could deliver the item or provide a refund. When I complained to Amazon, their customer service repeatedly passed the buck back to the third party seller rather than helping as the merchant of record.I offered extensive documentation, screenshots, and spent hours on calls trying to reach a solution. Amazon refused to step in and resolve the situation themselves, even after it was clear the package was lost. They would only say they ""notified the seller on my behalf"" but took no responsibility.It is unacceptable that Amazon sold this item but then refused to remedy their inability to fulfill the purchase as promised. After threatening chargebacks and complaints, Amazon still denied a refund and closed the case. They clearly have no intention of standing behind third party transactions that go wrong.I will never purchase something sold by third parties on Amazon again after this nightmare experience. Amazon has proven they are unwilling to protect customers when issues arise beyond our control. It is a waste of time to work with their customer service, who will only pass you off endlessly without resolving the problems their marketplace creates. Buyer beware of this risk if using third party sellers on Amazon!",2024-02-14 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,15.0,1587,255,34,5,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,avoid purchasing third party seller amazoni recently purchased item amazon sold third party seller shipping carrier marked package incorrect address without attempting delivery said would returned senderafter week trying get resolved neither carrier third party seller could deliver item provide refund complained amazon customer service repeatedly passed buck back third party seller rather helping merchant recordi offered extensive documentation screenshots spent hour call trying reach solution amazon refused step resolve situation even clear package lost would say notified seller behalf took responsibilityit unacceptable amazon sold item refused remedy inability fulfill purchase promised threatening chargebacks complaint amazon still denied refund closed case clearly intention standing behind third party transaction go wrongi never purchase something sold third party amazon nightmare experience amazon proven unwilling protect customer issue arise beyond control waste time work customer service pas endlessly without resolving problem marketplace creates buyer beware risk using third party seller amazon,0.017452254770140115,0.9825477452298599,0.1430173864273696,0.2,0.819877349900404,81.9877349900404,High Trust
