Janette Levey,/users/5fdb87a040335e001bcd3f9b,US,3.0,2024-02-06 21:39:39+00:00,1.0,Amazon -- when you absolutely need it next month,"I ordered a rollator walker for my 91-year old mother on 2/5/24. I was promised delivery by 9 p.m. 2/6/24. At about noon on 2/6/24 I went to track shipment and saw that the delivery date was now changed to 2/27/24 by 9 p.m -- even though it was picked up from a carrier facility 7 miles from the delivery address. I was back and forth with customer service chat who didn't want to tell me why it would be an extra day to deliver an item 7 miles away. They deflected and gave me UPS's number. UPS told me that it told Amazon last night that it wouldn't be able to deliver it today.Meanwhile, Amazon stopped the chat while I was holding with UPS and I had to start again. For a $250 item they wanted to offer me a $10 gift card. Then they offered instead a month off my prime membership -- and cut off the chat again. I called customer service but apparently they said they were the promotion department. They said as a gift and an apology they'd offer me a $100 voucher but I would have to pay for the shipping and handling. I pointed out that it's not a gift if I have to pay shipping and handling. The rep said he wasn't charging for the voucher just the shipping and handling. I told him that's not the way to treat a loyal prime customer. He kept saying ""OK you're not interested"" and I said that wasn't true I just didn't feel I should have to pay shipping and handling. He hung up on me.I called again and got through to customer service and he said he couldn't give any compensation, then said he could give $5. I told him that I had saved the previous chats and I was offered a month of free membership (about $12). He said Amazon can't do that which I know isn't true. I asked for an email address to send the chat and he wouldn't give me an email address. He then hung up.This is Amazon's idea of customer service. You are warned.If you want to order from Amazon, don't order anything big that you really need at a specific time -- and when they promise you something don't believe them.",2024-02-06 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,6.0,1996,385,48,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered rollator walker year old mother promised delivery pm noon went track shipment saw delivery date changed pm even though picked carrier facility mile delivery address back forth customer service chat didnt want tell would extra day deliver item mile away deflected gave upss number ups told told amazon last night wouldnt able deliver todaymeanwhile amazon stopped chat holding ups start item wanted offer gift card offered instead month prime membership cut chat called customer service apparently said promotion department said gift apology theyd offer voucher would pay shipping handling pointed gift pay shipping handling rep said wasnt charging voucher shipping handling told thats way treat loyal prime customer kept saying ok youre interested said wasnt true didnt feel pay shipping handling hung mei called got customer service said couldnt give compensation said could give told saved previous chat offered month free membership said amazon cant know isnt true asked email address send chat wouldnt give email address hung upthis amazon idea customer service warnedif want order amazon dont order anything big really need specific time promise something dont believe,0.02087870509592706,0.979121294904073,0.21592821088053843,0.2,0.8327462896281441,83.27462896281442,High Trust
