D A,/users/65c1bf9ba52d830012ba7024,US,1.0,2024-02-06 07:12:17+00:00,1.0,Where do I even begin,"Where do I even begin? My encounter with Amazon's customer service was nothing short of a nightmare. It's as if they go out of their way to make your life difficult.Firstly, getting in touch with a representative is like navigating a maze blindfolded. The automated system seems designed to frustrate and confuse you at every turn. And don't even think about trying to find a direct line to speak with a real person – it's like searching for a needle in a haystack.When I finally did manage to connect with someone, they were about as helpful as a broken pencil. It's like they're trained to provide the least amount of assistance possible. Instead of resolving my issue, they passed me from one department to another, each time repeating the same tiresome process of explaining my problem from scratch.And let's not forget about the wait times. I could have watched the entire Lord of the Rings trilogy twice over while waiting for a response. It's almost as if they take pleasure in making you wait endlessly, dangling the hope of resolution like a carrot on a stick.To top it all off, when a resolution was finally offered, it was so inadequate that I might as well have been talking to a brick wall. It's clear that Amazon's customer service is more concerned with closing tickets than actually solving problems.Save yourself the headache and frustration. Avoid Amazon's customer service like the plague. It's an experience you'll regret – one that will leave you questioning why you ever chose to do business with them in the first place.",2024-02-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,6.0,1543,265,21,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,even begin encounter amazon customer service nothing short nightmare go way make life difficultfirstly getting touch representative like navigating maze blindfolded automated system seems designed frustrate confuse every turn dont even think trying find direct line speak real person – like searching needle haystackwhen finally manage connect someone helpful broken pencil like theyre trained provide least amount assistance possible instead resolving issue passed one department another time repeating tiresome process explaining problem scratchand let forget wait time could watched entire lord ring trilogy twice waiting response almost take pleasure making wait endlessly dangling hope resolution like carrot stickto top resolution finally offered inadequate might well talking brick wall clear amazon customer service concerned closing ticket actually solving problemssave headache frustration avoid amazon customer service like plague experience youll regret – one leave questioning ever chose business first place,0.00951097863577303,0.990489021364227,0.14862591138530568,0.2,0.8249696929591747,82.49696929591747,High Trust
R G,/users/65c1b7803d9bf40012c960f0,US,1.0,2024-02-06 06:37:29+00:00,1.0,Ordered a vanity set for my daughter…,Ordered a vanity set for my daughter and the item is defective. It came damaged and cannot put it together. their customer service is terrible and would not allow me to return bc I was past a 30 day return window that I wasn't aware of. I was told they would send me manufacturers info by email but the link in the email was bad and was for an entirely different product and customer service keeps giving me the run around. Terrible customer service and a waste of $200,2024-02-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,6.0,469,89,37,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered vanity set daughter item defective came damaged cannot put together customer service terrible would allow return bc past day return window wasnt aware told would send manufacturer info email link email bad entirely different product customer service keep giving run around terrible customer service waste,0.02550333348552987,0.9744966665144701,0.04991587212563096,0.2,0.7972315076823613,79.72315076823612,High Trust
