Rodrigo Braga,/users/6552e09387f65600123f2d4f,BR,2.0,2024-01-30 22:17:51+00:00,1.0,Experience as a seller,"As a seller, its a nightmare. Even when I solve a buyers request (even when they don't have the legal right of it) I still get punished by Amazon unfairly... There was a ""A to Z warranty"" case that I HAVE ACCEPTED the return and paid for it (free of costs for the buyer) before the claim was filled and still, Amazon marked as ODR impact... Not to mention several cases where there's a post office mistake, strike which causes delays. Still, all the blame's on sellers, even if evolves things that we can not control.----Amazon itself has a 85% satisfaction rate from customers in Brazil (ReclameAqui)And at trustpilot, less than 2 stars...But they demand sellers to be perfect and having a 99% perfection rate (you can't have ""ODR - order defect rate"" higher than 2%)...",2024-01-29 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,30.0,771,136,22,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,seller nightmare even solve buyer request even dont legal right still get punished amazon unfairly z warranty case accepted return paid free cost buyer claim filled still amazon marked odr impact mention several case there post office mistake strike cause delay still blame seller even evolves thing controlamazon satisfaction rate customer brazil reclameaquiand trustpilot less starsbut demand seller perfect perfection rate cant odr order defect rate higher,0.041475624377261884,0.9585243756227381,0.07627593942793046,0.2,0.7945173756969551,79.45173756969551,High Trust
