may mcpherson,/users/63701bb824bd0d0012e054be,CA,7.0,2024-01-10 23:17:00+00:00,1.0,A SENIORS Shopping with Amazon & Prime,"l have been ordering from Amazon for awhile with no problems, until NOW!!!..l am a Senior 89yrs, & during the Xmas season found it very useful.However some of the items, (4, to be exact) had to be returned..The returns were initiated at different times, firstly 2 items, then l more, with no problem..Intel picked them up...The last item was refused with a pickup, and had to have a label to be returned, l do not have a printer, neither does anyone l know...l am now trying to figure out how to do this, the item cost $85.79...In the past l have not returned that many items, so why has Amazons policy changed ?..How many items are you allowed to return, and how often ?..Any orders l have returned were thru UPS with no issues, they printed the label & it was returned without dispute...l guess my question is HAS AMAZON & PRIME changed their RETURN POLICY ? How does a Senior without a printer, return an Item ? Where does a person go to get a LABEL printed ? Someone told me the Library, how does this work when the instructions are on my laptop ? l know l am looking for an EXCEPTION due to my AGE, which will probably not be recognized by either Amazon or Prime...For all the times l would use a printer, it is not feasible for me to buy one !!! l am looking for suggestions as there is no reason for me to keep the item in question...(DOESN""T FIT ME EITHER)..l will most certainly have to consider my online shopping with Amazon or Prime in the Future.. It was a convenient way for me to shop, due to my advanced age & capability of getting around physically...There are other companies for me to shop at, but l have had issues returning things to WISH, LITE INTHEBOX too far away in China, only once or twice but until NOW felt quite satisfied with both Amazon & Prime...Will never feel the same about ONLINE SHOPPING...",2024-01-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,10.0,1828