Rick,/users/5a2ffe0c0000ff000aeffdb3,US,3.0,2024-01-06 00:06:31+00:00,1.0,Amazon's customer service has totally…given overseas customer service that although they pormise they never do or understand how to give delivery instructions to the delivery driver,"Amazon's customer service has totally let me down. After having an article stolen and another taken by animals I bought a box for the delivery driver to put the stuff in on the advise of Amazon's customer service personnel. She told me to contact customer service with delivery instructions and the driver would correctly put my stuff into the box.I've literally spent around 1 ½ hours trying to get the overseas customer service dept to set up delivery instructions. The first agent kept me on the phone 45 minutes without figuring out how to set up the instructions even though I tried many times to get her to connect me with supervision with the thought that they may know how to do this. Finally she sent me to her supervisor who assured me that the instructions were properly set up.The first delivery was wrong and I went through the same phone conversations again, only to have the second delivery not delivered in the box again.Trying to figure out how to get Amazon to get this done is seemingly impossible.Although I saw a story recently about Bezos calling his own customer service , he obviously was pleased with what he found judging by the result. This is the third delivery not placed into the container that customer service twice told me had been arranged. Seems like if there's a possibility that a porch pirate stealing your goods than think twice about ordering from Amazon.",2024-01-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,6.0,1395,243,181,26,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer service totally let article stolen another taken animal bought box delivery driver put stuff advise amazon customer service personnel told contact customer service delivery instruction driver would correctly put stuff boxive literally spent around ½ hour trying get overseas customer service dept set delivery instruction first agent kept phone minute without figuring set instruction even though tried many time get connect supervision thought may know finally sent supervisor assured instruction properly set upthe first delivery wrong went phone conversation second delivery delivered box againtrying figure get amazon get done seemingly impossiblealthough saw story recently bezos calling customer service obviously pleased found judging result third delivery placed container customer service twice told arranged seems like there possibility porch pirate stealing good think twice ordering amazon,0.0034120923424615823,0.9965879076575385,0.13628715647784634,0.2,0.8255513851243385,82.55513851243384,High Trust
Steven Mannion,/users/5ee5f0b8da76514608b4a5a0,GB,6.0,2024-01-05 18:38:25+00:00,1.0,Too high on their own hubris.,"When I signed up for prime, parcels got delivered on time and usually with a reliable delivery slot. Then, over time,  the delivery time occasionally changed to 'Today by 10PM'. Fair enough, sometimes things go wrong. But then this happened again and again to the point where it became standard practice. I don't work for Amazon and I didn't pay for Prime so that I could wait around for eight to ten hours a day until they could deign to provide the service I was paying them for. When I phoned up at 3pm on a friday (the same day as posting this review) to complain about it regarding an order which was marked as 'Out for delivery' since 9AM, instead of solving the problem, the agent on the phone said that ""actually, that's in a queue and might not be there until Sunday"". If that was the case, why was it showing as 'Out for delivery'? This combined with the reduction in selections to the point of being really quite pathetic on Amazon Fresh, and raising prices to cover the amount of money they have wasted on Prime Video just makes the company as a whole both complacent and arrogant to the point where they no longer deserve anybody's business. In fact, it got to the point where just dealing with Amazon literally just felt like being in an abusive relationship, which is why I cancelled my subscription. There is a popular phrase: 'fluff' around and find out.Amazon do the 'fluffing' around. Their customers do the finding out.",2024-01-05 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,5.0,1439,259,29,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,signed prime parcel got delivered time usually reliable delivery slot time delivery time occasionally changed today pm fair enough sometimes thing go wrong happened point became standard practice dont work amazon didnt pay prime could wait around eight ten hour day could deign provide service paying phoned pm friday day posting review complain regarding order marked delivery since instead solving problem agent phone said actually thats queue might sunday case showing delivery combined reduction selection point really quite pathetic amazon fresh raising price cover amount money wasted prime video make company whole complacent arrogant point longer deserve anybodys business fact got point dealing amazon literally felt like abusive relationship cancelled subscription popular phrase fluff around find outamazon fluffing around customer finding,0.013160182654903596,0.9868398173450964,0.14526079641054404,0.2,0.822472067954657,82.2472067954657,High Trust
