Very Upset Customer,/users/60feed7df54aad0012de2af3,GB,3.0,2024-01-06 22:16:54+00:00,1.0,Breach of the Data Protection Act 2018 - Theft of Intellectual Property,"I’ve written to Amazon’s CEO, Andy Jassy and his Executive Relations team on numerous occasions about Amazon’s breach of the Data Protection Act 2018 (DPA) and theft of its customer’s intellectual property.  I stated in an e-mail to Mr Jassy, among other things, that I’m complaining about Amazon’s unlawful delivery policy.Amazon UK Services Limited (Amazon) continues to breach the Data Protection Act 2018 (DPA) and is deliberately intruding on its customer's privacy and stealing their intellectual property by taking photos/images of their person and of their private property (location) without their express permission and Amazon is not transparent with how its processing, sharing and storing such data and is exacerbating its misconduct resorting to evasive tactics to avoid the issue, which is totally unacceptable.As far as I’m aware the conditions of purchase on all of my orders thus far, DID NOT include me having to give up my rights and allow Amazon to violate my privacy and take my intellectual property in exchange for delivering my parcels. If that were the case, I would certainly not have bought anything from Amazon. Amazon's fulfillment of contract is to simply deliver the parcels and ask for the recipient's name and signature which is legally sufficient for proof of delivery and which I would oblige if the drivers presented me with that option, but they don’t. They quickly snap a photo of you as soon as you open the door, drop the parcel off and walk away, even despite the large security notice on my front door clearly stating, ""THIS IS PRIVATE PROPERTY, NO PHOTOS OR VIDEOS ALLOWED!""It is clear that Amazon needs to urgently address its delivery policy and give customers an option to sign for their deliveries and it must train its drivers to understand and respect PRIVATE PROPERTY and the right of privacy.Below, are some of the evasive tactics that Mr Jassy and team have responded following my Complaint and Request for “Right of Erasure” (SARs)[OPEN Quote] This is Jassy with Amazon's Executive Relations team.By corresponding with me, you have reached the highest level of customer service within our company. The Executive Relations' Department is the most senior department to which an issue may be escalated within Amazon.co.uk. This department liaises with customers on behalf of Amazon's most senior business executives, including the Amazon.co.uk Managing Director, the Amazon.co.uk Director of Customer Service, and our CEO.Your request was sent from an email address that is different from the one we have on file for you. I realise that you're concerned about deleting the photos or videos. It's never our intention to prolong this process, but in order to protect your privacy we can only send account information to the email address associated with your account. Please send this request from that email address.[END QUOTE]So according to his request I sent Mr Jassy my Complaint via the email associated with my Amazon account and this is the slippery response I received:[OPEN QUOTE]  “Hello,This is Gaurab with Amazon Executive Relations.I'm sorry but I couldn't find an Amazon.co.uk account under the e-mail address from which you've written.[END QUOTE]Consequently, I sent Mr Jassy and team step-by-step screenshots of me logging into my Amazon account via the email associated with my account which Gaurab above claimed s/he could not find and this is the evasive response I received on that attempt:[OPEN QUOTE] Dear Nicola,This is with Amazon's Executive Relations team.I was hoping to speak with you directly, on the number listed on your account, but unfortunately I was unable to reach you nor leave a voice message confirming my call.I hope you’ll first accept my apologies for the frustration and inconvenience you’ve experienced. [END QUOTE]These are many such examples of Amazon’s evasive tactics.I still haven’t received a satisfactory response from Amazon and as a result, I have no knowledge of how my personal data, photos/images are being processed, shared and stored as Amazon continues to arrogantly breach the Data Protection Act 2018.",2024-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,6.0,4111,656,71,12,2.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,i’ve written amazon’s ceo andy jassy executive relation team numerous occasion amazon’s breach data protection act dpa theft customer’s intellectual property stated email mr jassy among thing i’m complaining amazon’s unlawful delivery policyamazon uk service limited amazon continues breach data protection act dpa deliberately intruding customer privacy stealing intellectual property taking photosimages person private property location without express permission amazon transparent processing sharing storing data exacerbating misconduct resorting evasive tactic avoid issue totally unacceptableas far i’m aware condition purchase order thus far include give right allow amazon violate privacy take intellectual property exchange delivering parcel case would certainly bought anything amazon amazon fulfillment contract simply deliver parcel ask recipient name signature legally sufficient proof delivery would oblige driver presented option don’t quickly snap photo soon open door drop parcel walk away even despite large security notice front door clearly stating private property photo video allowedit clear amazon need urgently address delivery policy give customer option sign delivery must train driver understand respect private property right privacybelow evasive tactic mr jassy team responded following complaint request “right erasure” sarsopen quote jassy amazon executive relation teamby corresponding reached highest level customer service within company executive relation department senior department issue may escalated within amazoncouk department liaises customer behalf amazon senior business executive including amazoncouk managing director amazoncouk director customer service ceoyour request sent email address different one file realise youre concerned deleting photo video never intention prolong process order protect privacy send account information email address associated account please send request email addressend quoteso according request sent mr jassy complaint via email associated amazon account slippery response receivedopen quote “hellothis gaurab amazon executive relationsim sorry couldnt find amazoncouk account email address youve writtenend quoteconsequently sent mr jassy team stepbystep screenshots logging amazon account via email associated account gaurab claimed could find evasive response received attemptopen quote dear nicolathis amazon executive relation teami hoping speak directly number listed account unfortunately unable reach leave voice message confirming callus hope you’ll first accept apology frustration inconvenience you’ve experienced end quotethese many example amazon’s evasive tacticsi still haven’t received satisfactory response amazon result knowledge personal data photosimages processed shared stored amazon continues arrogantly breach data protection act,0.024501569726592762,0.9754984302734072,0.3679192372406057,0.2,0.8613330625848248,86.13330625848248,High Trust
Angie cook,/users/5f74709aa3275c6915ac8731,GB,26.0,2024-01-04 22:03:29+00:00,1.0,Ordered an item that didn’t work,"Ordered an item that didn’t work. Have to send it back for a refund, I have to pay for the return even though the Amazon advisor assured me I wouldn’t. It’s going to cost me £10 to return the large item. Customer service is awful, many items are defective or knock offs. I’ve seen many items that Amazon sell on temu for 80% cheaper. Delivering used to be next day or 2 days at most now they’re taking up to 2 weeks. It’s really gone down hill. Now they’re sending me emails saying they’re putting adverts on prime video even though I’m paying £8.99 a month. Well Amazon, you’re going to lose a lot of customers. Good luck.",2023-12-01 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,4.0,623,118,32,6,34.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered item didn’t work send back refund pay return even though amazon advisor assured wouldn’t it’s going cost £ return large item customer service awful many item defective knock offs i’ve seen many item amazon sell temu cheaper delivering used next day day they’re taking week it’s really gone hill they’re sending email saying they’re putting advert prime video even though i’m paying £ month well amazon you’re going lose lot customer good luck,0.02502459376840598,0.9749754062315941,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.800723822016526,80.0723822016526,High Trust
