Ed,/users/64641645498f6800126e57bd,US,10.0,2024-01-03 12:33:51+00:00,1.0,"Monopolies get lazy, arrogant, and oppressive.","You can type in anything you want in the Search bar.  Amazon will give you what they want you to see, not what you are looking for.  They will even ignore specific search terms if they want to.  You can even put double quotes around a word and Amazon will still ignore it if they want you to buy something else.  It is very frustrating that I cannot rely on a simple search function to find the items I am looking for.Also, when you have to return some items, they often make you put each item into a separate box/package and charge you $7.99 for each one.  Why won't they allow us to put several small items in one larger box and charge us $7.99 for only that one box?  It seems as though this ""return fee"" is being used to ""punish"" customers who dare return any items.In addition, when you are trying to find an item that has specific properties that you need, you cannot isolate such items using the selection bar on the left side of the screen.  They give you some selections, but they are vastly incomplete and often irrelevant.",2024-01-02 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,1.0,3.0,1033,193,46,6,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,type anything want search bar amazon give want see looking even ignore specific search term want even put double quote around word amazon still ignore want buy something else frustrating cannot rely simple search function find item looking foralso return item often make put item separate boxpackage charge one wont allow u put several small item one larger box charge u one box seems though return fee used punish customer dare return itemsin addition trying find item specific property need cannot isolate item using selection bar left side screen give selection vastly incomplete often irrelevant,0.008817591994431035,0.991182408005569,0.10824453168816602,0.2,0.8172401103404177,81.72401103404177,High Trust
