Steve Tessier,/users/657bf132a9248200126f6ab3,CA,11.0,2024-02-28 21:19:47+00:00,1.0,Amazon is the worst company on earth,"Amazon is the worst company on earth. Their prices are overly inflated. You think you are getting a deal, you’re not. They offer coupons with large rebates but the total price is always higher then elsewhere. Example: I purchased 3D Pinter with a $150.00 coupon off. I got the same printer elsewhere for $180.00 less.Second is replacement parts. I found that parts listed as compatible with your items often don't fit. Mostly these are from China. This wastes your time. When a Amazon item shows up on Google, search again on Amazon because there are multiple sellers with different prices. At least on eBay you can select the lowest price. Lastly, leaving your package at your door when you are home is stupid. Ring the doorbell. Jeff Bezos is the problem. ",2023-12-31 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,2.0,28.0,758,131,36,7,59.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon worst company earth price overly inflated think getting deal you’re offer coupon large rebate total price always higher elsewhere example purchased pinter coupon got printer elsewhere lesssecond replacement part found part listed compatible item often dont fit mostly china waste time amazon item show google search amazon multiple seller different price least ebay select lowest price lastly leaving package door home stupid ring doorbell jeff bezos problem,0.004012743111515731,0.9959872568884842,0.07347167694896242,0.2,0.8126879638340346,81.26879638340347,High Trust
