Michael S Alexander,/users/5f34665ef8dc552a1cbc7976,US,29.0,2024-01-01 17:58:31+00:00,1.0,Amazon ignorant incompetent disrespectful,"Wow I'm not quite sure where to begin. Amazon along with the Representatives just don't have the sense that GOD gave cabbage. I mean I seriously do believe that whoever is hiring such incompetent people have literally went blindly into the night snatching whomever throwing them into a giant room with phones and computers and saying get to work. Managers, supervisor's, Representatives all that work there or at least 97 % aren't paddling with both ores in the water.  It's like someone shot the dots of their dice years ago. I'm a nice person however when you pay for Amazon prime and then sometimes pay extra to have same day delivery, what that really means is haha we got cha again. Cause ya don't receive your package.  Amazon has adopted the moto you'll get it when we're damn good and ready to deliver it and if we want to will also use it and still send it. When you do get the notification that your package has been delivered, best believe their saying haha got cha again. Cause it's been delivered to the wrong place. Then you call, excuse me my package says delivered but it's not at my house. Umm excuse me sir have you checked the outside perimeter in the bushes also have you walked next door to check with your neighbors have you called other family members and have you walked up and down your street yelling has anyone seen my package.  Ummm excuse me Amazon Representatives last time I checked it wasn't my responsibility to track down something that I paid not only for you to deliver it but also I'm paying for prime as well plus the cost of whatever it is that I bought. You think you get just GPS it right the first time or maybe just do the job you applied for and got and getting paid to do. No instead you wanna scream threaten just get down right ignorant and hang up and then send a email asking for feedback on how great of a job you did