Mark Burnett,/users/6591cf55a6ef86001238783e,GB,2.0,2023-12-31 22:35:42+00:00,1.0,Dear oh dear Amazon,"Dear oh dear Amazon. I wanted to do a review about your fire stick so when I logged on to trust pilot I could not believe my eyes when I saw all the negative reviews you have not just on .com but right across the world including my country the UK. What's even more shocking is that you don't respond to any of them. In the world of commerce and business that would make me seriously worried when buying from you in fact I wouldn't, why because it means you don't care. So onto my problem then. The fire stick which I bought. Absolutely aweful, pedestrian, slow, glitchy as hell, even freezes in mid program often and I have to reset the thing, do you know how frustrating that is. It is a complete and utter waste of money. I will be throwing it away. So the question is do you care. I don't hold out much hope in your responding. My advice to people I think would be that if a company only cares about taking your money and doesn't want to take Care of your problem when it arises, then I can only think they are on the slippery slope down. Think first before you buy people and a wise word to you if I may Mr Bezos it's time to start caring.",2023-12-31 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,31.0,1143,225,19,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,dear oh dear amazon wanted review fire stick logged trust pilot could believe eye saw negative review com right across world including country uk whats even shocking dont respond world commerce business would make seriously worried buying fact wouldnt mean dont care onto problem fire stick bought absolutely aweful pedestrian slow glitchy hell even freeze mid program often reset thing know frustrating complete utter waste money throwing away question care dont hold much hope responding advice people think would company care taking money doesnt want take care problem arises think slippery slope think first buy people wise word may mr bezos time start caring,0.020385597