SM,/users/63cb8c2d08738d0013e0291d,US,19.0,2023-12-31 03:18:01+00:00,1.0,Exploitation at it's Finest,"Amazon is the type of company that will offer an array of products from brands, but values money over ethics. They may seem friendly with their interface and show convenience through services. It's all a facade.However, that's a totally different story when it comes to communication and treatment towards employees.Reviews on the site are sometimes fake with scammers acting as sellers while authentic opinions are being suppressed. I noticed the number of bots frequenting there as well. Also users/buyers can find their reviews being removed and discover themselves being banned from contributing for ""unusual reviewing activity"" by Amazon.  The moderators really have poor judgement behind their monitors. Another example is when employees that opperate in warehouses experience awful working conditions, the bosses there give the employees little time for a break. If you're an employee that have a problem, your boss is not going to show any mercy for your mental anguish.Pathetically enough, workers resorted in using pee-pee bottles if they need to urinate instead of going to the bathroom.Workers in that environment usually breakdown mentally and become severely exhausted. The most ludicrous resolve Amazon has to offer was coping spaces in 2021. These are mental health booths known as ""AmaZen.""In the Summer of 2023, Amazon decided to lock one of its customers, Brandon Jackson of Baltimore, Maryland, from his home connected with the smart home devices because a delivery driver allegedly heard a derogatory term through his doorbell. This has made news in my country.Apparently, no one was home at the time as evident and Amazon finally granted access to the man's residence and his accounts without explanation.I'm not going to deal with a business that tries to control its customers in an abusive manner. I have pity for the workers who are delivery drivers and warehouse employees that have to endure such an unhealthy workplace. I share a better relationship with Ebay and Walmart customer services long before this! Ebay and Walmart are more ethical businesses I would use as a customer. I would not recommend Amazon.",2023-12-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,31.0,2138,339,27,4,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon type company offer array product brand value money ethic may seem friendly interface show convenience service facadehowever thats totally different story come communication treatment towards employeesreviews site sometimes fake scammer acting seller authentic opinion suppressed noticed number bot frequenting well also usersbuyers find review removed discover banned contributing unusual reviewing activity amazon moderator really poor judgement behind monitor another example employee opperate warehouse experience awful working condition boss give employee little time break youre employee problem bos going show mercy mental anguishpathetically enough worker resorted using peepee bottle need urinate instead going bathroomworkers environment usually breakdown mentally become severely exhausted ludicrous resolve amazon offer coping space mental health booth known amazenin summer amazon decided lock one customer brandon jackson baltimore maryland home connected smart home device delivery driver allegedly heard derogatory term doorbell made news countryapparently one home time evident amazon finally granted access man residence account without explanationim going deal business try control customer abusive manner pity worker delivery driver warehouse employee endure unhealthy workplace share better relationship ebay walmart customer service long ebay walmart ethical business would use customer would recommend amazon,0.02631016824561851,0.9736898317543815,0.19012899607403252,0.2,0.8248707150919973,82.48707150919972,High Trust
Claudia Jones,/users/65908a0c162e7d00121dd54c,US,1.0,2023-12-30 23:22:38+00:00,1.0,Amazon’s A+ for outrageously bad customer service,"I ordered a Fire TV Stick 4K and the remote control did not work properly. It was depleting the batteries within 24 hours of replacing them. Amazon agreed to replace the items so I returned the remote and the fire stick. Instead of replacing it with the fire stick and the remote, they only sent the fire stick. I called customer service and was told I would have to purchase a remote and request a refund. Ridiculous, anti consumer response. I sent them the remote and fire stick and they replace it with a fire stick and no remote.  In other words I now have a product that is unusable. I’ve been a Prime customer for many years and make very frequent purchases. That stops now!!!",2023-12-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,30.0,682,126,49,7,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,ordered fire tv stick k remote control work properly depleting battery within hour replacing amazon agreed replace item returned remote fire stick instead replacing fire stick remote sent fire stick called customer service told would purchase remote request refund ridiculous anti consumer response sent remote fire stick replace fire stick remote word product unusable i’ve prime customer many year make frequent purchase stop,0.8517593416762032,0.14824065832379685,0.07066741446999439,0.2,0.38825381205589726,38.82538120558973,Low Trust
