Gail Kucher,/users/60f5e94d260ab40013a1a812,US,4.0,2023-12-29 05:14:10+00:00,1.0,False Advertising,"Amazon shipped my order via UPS, got all the tracking, product picked up by UPS, but after a 2 week wait, all of a sudden my product is "" out of stock "", so what? After 2 weeks on board UPS truck my order is refunded!  I DIDN'T WANT A REFUND, want my order that's in transit. Funny same thing happened in a year with same item. Fraud, false advertising. Then the ( all) customer service agents can't speak English, all of a sudden. Rip off fake Amazon.",2023-12-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,29.0,452,88,17,2,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon shipped order via ups got tracking product picked ups week wait sudden product stock week board ups truck order refunded didnt want refund want order thats transit funny thing happened year item fraud false advertising customer service agent cant speak english sudden rip fake amazon,0.08750983267203284,0.9124901673279672,0.049355019629837356,0.2,0.7661160875899511,76.6116087589951,High Trust
Linda Couch,/users/658e255ef49a3a0012cb07e7,US,1.0,2023-12-29 03:48:32+00:00,1.0,BUYER BEWARE,"BUYER BEWARE. As a Prime Member, Amazon did NOT make good on an order even though they didn't follow delivery instructions asked for at the time of order. As a result, and as a possible theft, Amazon did NOT provide a refund or replacement order even after completing every required step stated by reps. Beyond the financial loss, be aware most reps are hard to understand, don't listen, don't bother to refer to file notes (if there are any). They seem to use the same scripts not related to a question or to the information just provided. Example: I tried to explain the local police referred us to the Sheriff’s Office to file a possible theft report as they have the law enforcement jurisdiction at our rural address. No question or acknowledgement but repeatedly stating, “You must file a police report.” Finally, when I asked to speak to a supervisor, the rep hung up!  Also, as in my case, you will never speak to the same rep again. Even after your claim reportedly goes to “escalation,” you must call the general customer service number and start over, which includes reexplaining EVERYTHING as if it’s the first time you called.  Maddening! Still, I did EVERYTHING required, even repeatedly.  I was finally reassured by one phone rep that he saw my PDF report on file, that all had been done including talking to the USPS. He said our claim would be resolved quickly after he sent all to Escalation and not to worry about the deadline since we had completed everything required by that date. Yet on the “deadline date,” I called and spoke to 2 reps. I was told by the first rep after placing me on an extended hold, that he had called the police department and they had no record of a report from me on file, therefore there was nothing Amazon could do.  I again explained I had sent a PDF of a Sheriff’s Department report due to law enforcement jurisdiction as instructed by the local police department three times! He just repeated the same thing again with no acknowledgement of what I just said.  I begged him to listen and not hang up. I asked what ""police"" number he had called to verify he had called the Sheriff's Department; he said he couldn’t share that information due to privacy. I verbally stated the phone number of the Sheriff’s Department and asked if he had called that number - he wouldn't answer. I then asked to speak to his supervisor and was assured the supervisor would give me the same information he had. After an extended hold, someone new got on the phone. With a rude demeanor, he repeated that they had no police report on file; therefore, there would be no further support – refund or reorder. When I insisted it was there, again explaining that the jurisdiction was with the Sheriff’s office, he stated it did not contain all the information required. With witness at my side, I asked repeatedly for him to provide specifics of what was not included as I had referred to their email requirements, emailed those requirements to the Sheriff's Department, and saw the report with my own eyes, confirming all requirements met. He would not answer my question and provided no details. Finally, he said it was an “initial report” and not a “final report.” I told him this was the first I heard this as required to which he insisted they had provided me this information. Their email information had said to call Amazon during the police's office hours so their rep could verify information and I did this. (As soon as my call ended, I called the Sheriff’s Department myself and got immediately through. The gentleman in the report/records department told me no one from Amazon had called. They also said the rep doesn’t understand law enforcement investigations because if they don’t have a suspect as in my case, it is considered an open case with no final report written or available.) Bottomline: I have wasted significant time and effort – for nothing. I’ve taken a big financial loss on goods not delivered and paid at the same time a Prime Member fee to experience this type of treatment. (I also unfortunately ended up in the ER due to the stress of this all with heart issues.) Almost humorous, as you are on hold, Amazon’s recording speaks of their desire to have the best world class service. I am not a rude or unreasonable person. I used to be the Sr. V.P. in charge of customer service for a large company where we strived to protect the company but be fair with our customers. Trust me, Amazon's service is the worst. It’s inexcusable and I’m surprised there hasn’t been a class action lawsuit over inconsistent and unfair practices. Even if you’ve heard positive things about Amazon or you haven't had a problem yourself, just wait. Your turn may be coming. And it may be a horrific experience like mine.",2023-12-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,29.0,4755,840,12,2,15.0,0,3,1,0,Genuine,buyer beware prime member amazon make good order even though didnt follow delivery instruction asked time order result possible theft amazon provide refund replacement order even completing every required step stated rep beyond financial loss aware rep hard understand dont listen dont bother refer file note seem use script related question information provided example tried explain local police referred u sheriff’s office file possible theft report law enforcement jurisdiction rural address question acknowledgement repeatedly stating “you must file police report” finally asked speak supervisor rep hung also case never speak rep even claim reportedly go “escalation” must call general customer service number start includes reexplaining everything it’s first time called maddening still everything required even repeatedly finally reassured one phone rep saw pdf report file done including talking usps said claim would resolved quickly sent escalation worry deadline since completed everything required date yet “deadline date” called spoke rep told first rep placing extended hold called police department record report file therefore nothing amazon could explained sent pdf sheriff’s department report due law enforcement jurisdiction instructed local police department three time repeated thing acknowledgement said begged listen hang asked police number called verify called sheriff department said couldn’t share information due privacy verbally stated phone number sheriff’s department asked called number wouldnt answer asked speak supervisor assured supervisor would give information extended hold someone new got phone rude demeanor repeated police report file therefore would support – refund reorder insisted explaining jurisdiction sheriff’s office stated contain information required witness side asked repeatedly provide specific included referred email requirement emailed requirement sheriff department saw report eye confirming requirement met would answer question provided detail finally said “initial report” “final report” told first heard required insisted provided information email information said call amazon police office hour rep could verify information soon call ended called sheriff’s department got immediately gentleman reportrecords department told one amazon called also said rep doesn’t understand law enforcement investigation don’t suspect case considered open case final report written available bottomline wasted significant time effort – nothing i’ve taken big financial loss good delivered paid time prime member fee experience type treatment also unfortunately ended er due stress heart issue almost humorous hold amazon’s recording speaks desire best world class service rude unreasonable person used sr vp charge customer service large company strived protect company fair customer trust amazon service worst it’s inexcusable i’m surprised hasn’t class action lawsuit inconsistent unfair practice even you’ve heard positive thing amazon havent problem wait turn may coming may horrific experience like mine,0.2424669925271841,0.7575330074728159,0.4711160964666293,0.2,0.7729897230297338,77.29897230297338,High Trust
Adam D'Agostino,/users/6571da9c14a9680012a2b074,US,2.0,2023-12-29 03:45:22+00:00,1.0,The WORST customer support I’ve ever experienced,"Every time I speak to an Amazon agent in chat, they always tell me they have to transfer me to the appropriate ‘department’ which I’ve come to learn is a total BS excuse for them to not have to do their job. I end up having to re-explain my situation to 3-5 agents per request.Usually, their English is horrible and they show zero desire to actually help you as the customer.If only this company didn’t have such a massive grip on the world, this level of standard would never be accepted for any new and rising company. They’d fail in a heartbeat because they treat their customers like literal trash.",2023-12-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,29.0,602,110,48,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,every time speak amazon agent chat always tell transfer appropriate ‘department’ i’ve come learn total b excuse job end reexplain situation agent per requestusually english horrible show zero desire actually help customerif company didn’t massive grip world level standard would never accepted new rising company they’d fail heartbeat treat customer like literal trash,0.03951667585283195,0.9604833241471681,0.06169377453729669,0.2,0.7925804169810434,79.25804169810434,High Trust
Brady,/users/5f1a7d8d02b0ef8a58b0afb5,ZA,3.0,2023-12-29 03:29:30+00:00,1.0,Amazon Closed My Account Without Notice,"On Sun, 24 Dec I received an email from Amazon saying, ""We have temporarily placed your Amazon account on hold and canceled any pending orders or subscriptions because we detected unusual activity on it. To restore access to your account, sign in and follow on-screen instructions.""I signed in and followed the instructions to the letter. Yet on Mon, 25 Dec, I received another email from Amazon saying, ""We have closed your Amazon account because we were not able to confirm that you are authorized to use the payment method associated with your account. Your pending orders have been canceled. If you believe this is a mistake, please contact Customer Service.""I tried tweeting them only to be told by their support on Twitter that I must reply to the email about my account being close. I told them it came from a ""no-reply"" address so I could not reply to it. Their support person said I could reply to it.Yet when I did reply to it, I got an email back saying, ""You've written to an address that does not accept incoming e-mails, but we have provided links to help answer some common questions."", and that I must try the links on their Help page. All those links require a login, but they have closed my account, so I can't log in.I finally managed to find a button on an Amazon page that let me chat to an associate. He kept me waiting 20 minutes, asked me to wait longer, then closed the chat without any answers.",2023-12-25 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,29.0,1420,256,39,6,4.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,sun dec received email amazon saying temporarily placed amazon account hold canceled pending order subscription detected unusual activity restore access account sign follow onscreen instructionsi signed followed instruction letter yet mon dec received another email amazon saying closed amazon account able confirm authorized use payment method associated account pending order canceled believe mistake please contact customer servicei tried tweeting told support twitter must reply email account close told came noreply address could reply support person said could reply ityet reply got email back saying youve written address accept incoming email provided link help answer common question must try link help page link require login closed account cant log ini finally managed find button amazon page let chat associate kept waiting minute asked wait longer closed chat without answer,0.021680900257812174,0.9783190997421878,0.1435782389231632,0.2,0.8178751976557266,81.78751976557265,High Trust
Lola,/users/658e0568d4085500119ce9ac,US,1.0,2023-12-29 01:32:33+00:00,1.0,Inability to Communicate with Customer Service,"Two items that I ordered on Amazon were never delivered, and when I look at the order status on Amazon, it says ""Your package may be lost.""  This has happened a number of times with other orders.  I called Customer Service to get my lost items replaced, and I spoke with a rep who was nice and polite, but I simply could not understand what she was saying to me.  I had to ask her to repeat what she was saying many, many times, and when she did, I often still could not understand her.  I realize that providing overseas customer support has financial advantages for Amazon, but it is at the expense of customers.  On almost every customer service call I have made to Amazon, I have had a great deal of trouble communicating with the rep.  And I have often received information that is completely incorrect.  I remember when Customer Service reps were based in the U.S., and they were great and I was able to communicate with them.  My heart sinks every time I have to call Customer Service and I hear someone answer with a heavy accent because I know the interaction is going to be difficult and stressful.  I love  Amazon because of their huge and varied inventory and the ease of ordering from them, but I hate their Customer Service and Amazon delivery services.  Before Amazon created their own delivery service and delivery was handled by Fedex and UPS and a few others, I never had a problem with delivery.  But now I've had multiple problems, with my items being delivered to the wrong address (when my address is clearly posted on my house), with my items not being delivered at all but being ""lost,"" and with my items being delivered late.  I miss the old Amazon and have definite mixed feelings about the current one.",2023-12-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,29.0,1729,312,46,6,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,two item ordered amazon never delivered look order status amazon say package may lost happened number time order called customer service get lost item replaced spoke rep nice polite simply could understand saying ask repeat saying many many time often still could understand realize providing overseas customer support financial advantage amazon expense customer almost every customer service call made amazon great deal trouble communicating rep often received information completely incorrect remember customer service rep based u great able communicate heart sink every time call customer service hear someone answer heavy accent know interaction going difficult stressful love amazon huge varied inventory ease ordering hate customer service amazon delivery service amazon created delivery service delivery handled fedex ups others never problem delivery ive multiple problem item delivered wrong address address clearly posted house item delivered lost item delivered late miss old amazon definite mixed feeling current one,0.004652869906986014,0.995347130093014,0.17498597868760515,0.2,0.832670760784028,83.2670760784028,High Trust
