Tiffany DeWall,/users/6579515d0cd51300120cbd39,US,1.0,2023-12-27 09:01:14+00:00,1.0,So ordered $295.50 worth of Christmas…,"So ordered $295.50 worth of Christmas gifts. Showed delivered but pictures are not my apartment door. Contacted consumer service and the rep said refund was processed. 12 hours later, and most of that time on the phone or chat found out it was a lie. Filled out multiple incident reports. Now they want police report. Did call police and not much they can do. Amazon refuses to give me corporate number and email and refuses to do anything even though I have proof if what my door looks like. It clearly was delivered to wrong address. I guess my kids don't get Christmas presents this year. Filed police report, told me will refund then. Sent it to them and said it is an invalid police report, like what. Told customer service rep to call police department. She said if they can verify then can get refund. Gets back on phone and said that they did verify it but since they could not tell her if I made the report they could not verify my identity. Funny how it changed again. Called a manager and he said the police report is valid and before report is a signed form from me to get police report verifying it is me plus he said legally rep is not suppose ask for my identity. He tried to put in refund and a different department denied it. Then got an email saying I went against their refund policy and they are restricting my account to only digital purchases. Funny how Amazon is ignoring all of these negative reviews.",2023-12-10 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,27.0,1425,263,38,6,17.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered worth christmas gift showed delivered picture apartment door contacted consumer service rep said refund processed hour later time phone chat found lie filled multiple incident report want police report call police much amazon refuse give corporate number email refuse anything even though proof door look like clearly delivered wrong address guess kid dont get ch