Anoeschka,/users/6573d9e651045c0012bf9883,AU,1.0,2023-12-09 05:08:10+00:00,1.0,I would give it a 0/5 star rating if I…,"I would give it a 0/5 star rating if I could as their Accessibility, ease of use and neurodiverse options are limited when you ask for help for Prime Video. It is very confusing to have to click a whole bunch of tabs and then find out they don't have a message box or email address. Amazon also has no formal complaint process that is easy to find. False advertising that you can email them. I went through every drop-down bar, and not once did the email light up. I did not want people contact today as it is my day to watch series or read my ebooks and wanted to report a strange IT glitch by email/message that I felt confused me and didn't really fit any of their drop down bars. Not Amazon Video, Kindle or main website provide help message boxes or email addresses. You only have the option to speak on chat and mobile. The help page takes 5-8 clicks. You type in Binge contact us and their email address is easy to find in Google. Paramount has their easy to access email address on their international website, Everand has I think either easy to find email address through google search or a message box. Use these websites. They have more user-friendly, easy help service for streaming, ebooks and audibles.",2023-12-09 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,9.0,1216,224,39,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,would give star rating could accessibility ease use neurodiverse option limited ask help prime video confusing click whole bunch tab find dont message box email address amazon also formal complaint process easy find false advertising email went every dropdown bar email light want people contact today day watch series read ebooks wanted report strange glitch emailmessage felt confused didnt really fit drop bar amazon video kindle main website provide help message box email address option speak chat mobile help page take click type binge contact u email address easy find google pa