Janice Yee,/users/64eb7207ab8cdf00124e140e,US,8.0,2023-12-02 16:10:44+00:00,1.0,Resolving problems with Amazon is a headache,"Like a lot of people, I gravitate to Amazon when I need to buy something because of their massive inventory.  The convenience of one stop shopping is very alluring to me. However, my recent experience makes me rethink my Amazon shopping habit.  In a nutshell, I believe I was overcharged $115.00 by them and rather than go through the enormous hassle of trying to resolve it through a human representative, I am going to pay the $115.00.  To me it’s not worth the frustration of trying to deal with such a huge uncaring behemoth and probably end up paying the money anyway.  I suppose I am letting them get away with suspect behavior by not further investigating the overcharge, but my response is that I prefer to look into buying from other sellers from now on and not automatically throw all my business and hard earned money to them.",2023-12-02 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,2.0,837,149,44,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,like lot people gravitate amazon need buy something massive inventory convenience one stop shopping alluring however recent experience make rethink amazon shopping habit nutshell believe overcharged rather go enormous hassle trying resolve human representative going pay it’s worth frustration trying deal huge uncaring behemoth probably end paying money anyway suppose letting get away suspect behavior investigating overcharge response prefer look buying seller automatically throw business hard earned money,0.03359111339877893,0.966408886601221,0.08356702187324734,0.2,0.79991784767526,79.991784767526,High Trust
