Bob&Cindy Coleman,/users/6569f403f4c8fe0012948863,US,1.0,2023-12-01 16:56:20+00:00,1.0,Reduce theft of in route product,"The driver dropped a 'Prime"" bag in our garage but the bag was cut open down the entire side.  There was no product in the bag.  How can the driver not see this?? Amazon should add a step to their handling of product delivery.  Why can't the boxed/bagged product barcode indicate the weight of the package and upon last movement to the Prime delivery truck it is weighed again. The weight should match the original package weight that is provided in the bar code.  If the weight doest match - that's a process Amazon would need to figure out. This would reduce theft and would help identify where the theft is taking place. Would be also a huge win for customer service.",2023-11-29 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,1.0,670,122,32,6,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,driver dropped prime bag garage bag cut open entire side product bag driver see amazon add step handling product delivery cant boxedbagged product barcode indicate weight package upon last movement prime delivery truck weighed weight match original package weight provided bar code weight doest match thats process amazon would need figure would reduce theft would help identify theft taking place would also huge win customer service,0.01828885194380447,0.9817111480561955,0.06842400448681997,0.2,0.8045403749254618,80.45403749254618,High Trust
