Leo Dsilva,/users/5a564eb20000ff000afebdc5,GB,71.0,2023-11-28 09:14:27+00:00,1.0,Bad sales stunt by Amazon,"**Title: Deceptive Sales Stunt - An Unfulfilled Promise**I recently had the unfortunate experience of participating in what was advertised as an ""invite-only"" tele event on Amazon, and the entire ordeal has left me deeply dissatisfied. It's disheartening to realize that what was initially presented as an exciting opportunity turned out to be nothing more than a sales stunt, and the lack of transparency in this process is concerning.The concept of an exclusive tele event piqued my interest, and I eagerly engaged with the promotion in the hopes of securing an invite. Unfortunately, like many others, my anticipation turned into frustration as the promised invitations never materialized. It's hard not to feel misled when a company as prominent as Amazon engages in what seems to be a calculated marketing strategy that falls short of delivering on its promises.Transparency is the bedrock of trust between consumers and companies, and in this instance, Amazon's approach has left a lot to be desired. If the intention behind the promotion was to generate excitement and engagement, it backfired for a substantial number of participants who were left empty-handed and disillusioned.I believe that it's essential for a company of Amazon's stature to uphold a higher standard when it comes to marketing practices. Customers invest their time and enthusiasm in these promotions, and the least they deserve is clear communication and fulfillment of promises. This experience has undoubtedly left me questioning the integrity of Amazon's promotional activities.I sincerely hope that Amazon takes this feedback to heart and reevaluates its approach to such promotions in the future. Clear communication and a commitment to fulfilling promises will not only prevent customer disappointment but also contribute to a more positive and trusting relationship between Amazon and its customers.",2023-11-27 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,28.0,1886,288,25,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,title deceptive sale stunt unfulfilled promisei recently unfortunate experience participating advertised inviteonly tele event amazon entire ordeal left deeply dissatisfied disheartening realize initially presented exciting opportunity turned nothing sale stunt lack transparency process concerningthe concept exclusive tele event piqued interest eagerly engaged promotion hope securing invite unfortunately like many others anticipation turned frustration promised invitation never materialized hard feel misled company prominent amazon engages seems calculated marketing strategy fall short delivering promisestransparency bedrock trust consumer company instance amazon approach left lot desired intention behind promotion generate excitement engagement backfired substantial number participant left emptyhanded disillusionedi believe essential company amazon stature uphold higher standard come marketing practice customer invest time enthusiasm promotion least deserve clear communication fulfillment promise experience undoubtedly left questioning integrity amazon promotional activitiesi sincerely hope amazon take feedback heart reevaluates approach promotion future clear communication commitment fulfilling promise prevent customer disappointment also contribute positive trusting relationship amazon customer,0.07970773871271988,0.9202922612872801,0.16152551878855861,0.2,0.7924512344013518,79.24512344013517,High Trust
Jeral,/users/656558f640646e00124c72ef,US,1.0,2023-11-28 05:17:43+00:00,2.0,Just disappointed,"I pay for Amazon Prime particularly for the free 2 day shipping and more often than not, my packages are not delivered when the website says it was. Usually I have this problem when I order on Friday for Sunday delivery. I had an okay experience with customer service until the last time. I felt the rep was rude. I was assured this wouldn't happen again and the carrier team would be in touch with me and no one called. I was issued a refund but am completely dissatisfied with their delivery process.",2023-10-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,28.0,502,93,17,2,29.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,pay amazon prime particularly free day shipping often package delivered website say usually problem order friday sunday delivery okay experience customer service last time felt rep rude assured wouldnt happen carrier team would touch one called issued refund completely dissatisfied delivery process,0.008638185586572178,0.9913618144134279,0.05215928210880538,0.4,1.106112763628475,110.6112763628475,High Trust
