P,/users/6507159b9d6ef90012fc6cd1,US,2.0,2023-11-23 13:58:52+00:00,1.0,Prime service is a joke…,"I’m closing my Prime membership  after repeated shipping issues.  Prime delivery is a joke. Allegedly, as a Prime member, you can receive expedited shipping on some items. Time and again, my items don’t show by the expected date. This week my holiday was ruined because items that were allegedly out for delivery never showed. This happened twice on different items all in the same week- and a week where I needed Amazon to come through. Amazon is not convenient, poor logistics, and no real customer service.",2023-11-22 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,23.0,509,86,24,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,i’m closing prime membership repeated shipping issue prime delivery joke allegedly prime member receive expedited shipping item time item don’t show expected date week holiday ruined item allegedly delivery never showed happened twice different item week week needed amazon come amazon convenient poor logistics real customer service,0.013121043570747547,0.9868789564292525,0.04823331463825014,0.2,0.8030861411422763,80.30861411422762,High Trust
Sascha Wagner,/users/5b0daa0a4de5666d34b70f00,DE,2.0,2023-11-23 13:39:03+00:00,1.0,"Oh my, just ignore the customer","For starters: 1 star only, because I can not enter a 0 value. As for the Service: Free 1 day delivery. Nope. Repeated issues with holding the timeline. Well, thas nothing new. After a number of days, the amount gets refunded automatically, without priorly requesting consent. Not good for a number of reasons I won't discuss here. The support, likely somewhere in India (Punjab maybe) has some serious issues with using the german (german account) language properly. Thats ok. That was o be expected. After more then 20 Minutes of discussion and repeated iterations of ""this is what we do"" , I asked for the line manager. And to be clear, not a Karen, but if after more then 20 Minutes nothing is moving, I push a level up. Thee request was ignored. The service personel just returned with, quote: ""Soeben habe ich Ihre Anfrage mit meinem Führungskraft diskutiert."" - so he talked to the manager. Not me, as I requested. That was the point where I thought, lets keep them busy, to I made a formal request for Data Access based on GDPR. Which was commented with a link to the pricacy policy. Not quite the reaction. Looking forward on how this might develop in the comming days. By now I am 1h hour in and essentially being kept waiting.",2023-11-23 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,23.0,1236,221,31,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,starter star enter value service free day delivery nope repeated issue holding timeline well thas nothing new number day amount get refunded automatically without priorly requesting consent good number reason wont discus support likely somewhere india punjab maybe serious issue using german german account language properly thats ok expected minute discussion repeated iteration asked line manager clear karen minute nothing moving push level thee request ignored service personel returned quote soeben habe ich ihre anfrage mit meinem führungskraft diskutiert talked manager requested point thought let keep busy made formal request data access based gdpr commented link pricacy policy quite reaction looking forward might develop comming day h hour essentially kept waiting,0.012186252905880195,0.9878137470941198,0.12394840157038699,0.2,0.8186965538611373,81.86965538611372,High Trust
Mr David Morgan,/users/534d123a00006400016e5ebb,GB,50.0,2023-11-23 13:00:36+00:00,3.0,Used To Be Excellent.,"Used To Be Excellent.I have been with Amazon and Amazon Prime for over a decade and they have been excellent in every way a few hitches but it’s to be expected and was dealt with .The last couple of years the service has got steadily worse , prices are in some cases ( majority) very much higher , I recently return ed items which basically were not fit for purpose and received from Amazon an email threatening to close my account for returning to much but if you send me clearly used goods or goods which are not as shown I shall return them but Amazon are not interested, the deliveries are good on the whole but had things throw over fences dumped on car bonnet .. I have cctv so know when the driver lies .Prime is not really worth it as a lot of the films are just really cheap budgeted movies you wouldn’t watch anyway . After the last email threatening to close a very active account I am thinking now to take the lead and pull the plug on Amazon.Once they were excellent but I think they have now grown to big and offer very poor value for money",2023-11-22 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,23.0,1054,203,21,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used excellenti amazon amazon prime decade excellent every way hitch it’s expected dealt last couple year service got steadily worse price case majority much higher recently return ed item basically fit purpose received amazon email threatening close account returning much send clearly used good good shown shall return amazon interested delivery good whole thing throw fence dumped car bonnet cctv know driver lie prime really worth lot film really cheap budgeted movie wouldn’t watch anyway last email threatening close active account thinking take lead pull plug amazononce excellent think grown big offer poor value money,0.09408766862555838,0.9059123313744416,0.11385305664610207,0.6,1.375726777016441,137.5726777016441,High Trust
Catherine O,/users/612cd0310dfad80012d0b053,GB,5.0,2023-11-23 11:38:34+00:00,1.0,Absolutely impossible to enforce your…,Absolutely impossible to enforce your statutory rights under UK consumer law. Policies provided to “customer” service agents in foreign countries are inadequate at best and misleading at worst. They have no knowledge or understanding of The Consumer Rights Act 2015. Managers and “teams” are unable to communicate outside of the provided script which does not include consumer laws. Even getting contact to notify them of intended prosecution for failing to uphold consumer rights over a product is impossible. You end up in a loop of quoting your statutory rights and being advised the product is out of warranty to find out your statutory rights and links to trading standards. This is all deliberately designed so that Amazon does not have to fulfil their legal obligations to consumers.,2023-11-21 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,23.0,790,127,38,5,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,absolutely impossible enforce statutory right uk consumer law policy provided “customer” service agent foreign country inadequate best misleading worst knowledge understanding consumer right act manager “teams” unable communicate outside provided script include consumer law even getting contact notify intended prosecution failing uphold consumer right product impossible end loop quoting statutory right advised product warranty find statutory right link trading standard deliberately designed amazon fulfil legal obligation consumer,0.043525410409488256,0.9564745895905118,0.071228266965788,0.2,0.7924829481884135,79.24829481884134,High Trust
Alex Nicholas,/users/655f18abd5ae36001295890e,GB,4.0,2023-11-23 11:21:59+00:00,1.0,Lying delivery drivers and poor service,"I ordered a lego set as an early Christmas present. The item was not delivered yet the courier had said the item was handed to the recipient, this was a lie. Instead of refunding me Amazon is making me wait 2 weeks meaning I can't replace the item and the person I am buying for won't get their Christmas present. I am not going to use Amazon anymore and will now shop at Very instead",2023-11-17 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,23.0,384,75,39,6,6.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered lego set early christmas present item delivered yet courier said item handed recipient lie instead refunding amazon making wait week meaning cant replace item person buying wont get christmas present going use amazon anymore shop instead,0.026863788223308493,0.9731362117766915,0.04206393718452047,0.2,0.7949808933252499,79.49808933252498,High Trust
