Don Phillips,/users/655cbb0956038b0012a830bd,US,2.0,2023-11-21 16:13:45+00:00,1.0,Amazon inhumane treatment,"UPS ,in error, returned my generator to Amazon. I received notice of delivery from UPS had received shipment. Amazon won't return my generator. Amazon agrees they accepted delivery. For a month I have spoken with numerous supervisors and when I push them for a determination as to the generators location, they place me on hold until the phone goes dead. Clearly, this is an internal policy to avoid responsibility. I am a 78 year old widower, with cancer. I live alone and need the generator to insure that my home medical services work. These are the most callus, uncaring group of customer service representatives I've ever met.",2023-10-20 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,21.0,631,107,25,3,32.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ups error returned generator amazon received notice delivery ups received shipment amazon wont return generator amazon agrees accepted delivery month spoken numerous supervisor push determination generator location place hold phone go dead clearly internal policy avoid responsibility year old widower cancer live alone need generator insure home medical service work callus uncaring group customer service representative ive ever met,0.011897552535604664,0.9881024474643954,0.06001121704991587,0.2,0.8060534671421808,80.60534671421809,High Trust
