Avner Falk,/users/58f6710b0000ff000a8e73d7,IL,27.0,2023-12-06 07:55:19+00:00,1.0,AMAZON IS LYING ABOUT ITS SHIPPING,"This review was written on November 2, 2023 and updated on December 6.  A new order I placed on November 15 was PURPORTEDLY shipped on November 24, but I received two notices of delayed delivery, the last one saying I would only receive my shipment on January 6 — 52 days after placing my order. On November 24 the tracking information for my November 15 order said, “Carrier picked up package at Los Angeles International Airport. Shipment is on its way to destination country.” Ten days later the carrier’s website still said, “November 24, 2023: Package is on the way to destination country.” Now, on January 6, it says, ”December 5, 2023: Carrier picked up package at Buena Park, CA.” THIS MEANS THAT THE FIRST TRACKING INFO WAS A LIE. Another order that I placed in early September only reached me in late November. Amazon used to hire good carriers like FedEx, UPS or DHL Express. Now it is making millions of dollars on its shipping charges by using the cheapest and slowest carriers in the world while charging its customers high shipping fees and LYING TO THEM. My messages to Amazon’s CEO Andy Jassy about this are always answered by a standard bureaucratic replies claiming unforeseen circumstances and other delays but never addressing the content of my messages. I have asked Jassy, “Is this Amazon or Alibaba?!” He has never replied. Amazon calls itself “Earth’s most customer-centric company.” That is a sad joke.",2023-11-02 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,12.0,6.0,1428,244,34,6,34.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,review written november updated december new order placed november purportedly shipped november received two notice delayed delivery last one saying would receive shipment january — day placing order november tracking information november order said “carrier picked package los angeles international airport shipment way destination country” ten day later carrier’s website still said “november package way destination country” january say ”december carrier picked package buena park ca” mean first tracking info lie another order placed early september reached late november amazon used hire good carrier like fedex ups dhl express making million dollar shipping charge using cheapest slowest carrier world charging customer high shipping fee lying message amazon’s ceo andy jassy always answered standard bureaucratic reply claiming unforeseen circumstance delay never addressing content message asked jassy “is amazon alibaba” never replied amazon call “earth’s customercentric company” sad joke,0.11645071141355517,0.8835492885864449,0.13684800897363994,0.2,0.7691442460879505,76.91442460879504,High Trust
