S. B.,/users/59d3bd450000ff000ad08836,GB,15.0,2023-11-10 20:47:09+00:00,1.0,Amazon lied and cost me £150.,"I contacted customer service a few weeks ago to ask whether or not I would be reimbursed for expensive postage fees on a return I was making, and customer service told me more than once that yes, absolutely, I would be reimbursed up to £150 for postage costs. With this in mind I purchased postage via UPS which ended up costing £177.30. Now, however, Amazon is refusing to reimburse me, and every time I contact customer service to find out why and how to get my money back, they end the chat and ignore my issue. I've literally been lied out of £150 by a multi-billion dollar company. This is shameful and I will without a doubt be closing my account after this. I have told my friends and family about this and many of them have agreed that this was the last straw and that they will also no longer be using Amazon. You've got billions of pounds to play with, but you'll refuse to give me £150 that you promised me? Catch yourself on.",2023-11-10 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,10.0,937,176,29,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,contacted customer service week ago ask whether would reimbursed expensive postage fee return making customer service told yes absolutely would reimbursed £ postage cost mind purchased postage via ups ended costing £ however amazon refusing reimburse every time contact customer service find get money back end chat ignore issue ive literally lied £ multibillion dollar company shameful without doubt closing account told friend family many agreed last straw also longer using amazon youve got billion pound play youll refuse give £ promised catch,0.02183842176616609,0.9781615782338339,0.09871003925967471,0.2,0.8088227969688518,80.88227969688518,High Trust
