MEI TAN,/users/65457474038939001163061a,US,1.0,2023-11-04 00:30:22+00:00,1.0,Amazon website policy says as long as…,"Amazon website policy says as long as the Customers buy more than $35, we will get free delivery, but actually when i bought two items from two sellers, the total price is more than $35, but they still charge the delivery fee for one item, the other item has no delivery fee, i called their customer service, they said that you got to be prime members, we can get free delivery, which is not their website saying, scam",2023-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,4.0,418,78,38,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon website policy say long customer buy get free delivery actually bought two item two seller total price still charge delivery fee one item item delivery fee called customer service said got prime member get free delivery website saying scam,0.005377571580767436,0.9946224284192325,0.04374649467190129,0.2,0.8060605131439965,80.60605131439965,High Trust
David,/users/654551fbfa2e5e0011d7493c,US,1.0,2023-11-03 22:11:26+00:00,1.0,first,"first, I have been a satisfied amazon.com customer for over fifteen years.   This review involves an issue with an amazon.com approved return.   I purchased a product from amazon which turns out I didn't need.  So, I put in for a return, placed a copy of the original invoice in a sturdy shipping box, taped it up using 3M shipping grade tape then dropped it off with our shipping clerk for pick-up by UPS.   Day before UPS was scheduled to pick-up the package, an amazon.com delivery driver takes the package from our shipping clerk and leaves no receipt or tracking number.   This made it impossible for me to prove that amazon.com had picked up the package for return.   The next day, UPS attempted pickup and to their credit left a shipping label along with a tracking number with our front desk shipping clerk.   amazon.com refuses to acknowledge the pick-up for return and refuses to provide a refund ($99.99).   I'm headed to the Washington state Attorney General's office along with the Federal Trade Commission to see what they have to say about the problem.",2023-02-07 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,11.0,3.0,1067,182,5,1,269.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,first satisfied amazoncom customer fifteen year review involves issue amazoncom approved return purchased product amazon turn didnt need put return placed copy original invoice sturdy shipping box taped using shipping grade tape dropped shipping clerk pickup ups day ups scheduled pickup package amazoncom delivery driver take package shipping clerk leaf receipt tracking number made impossible prove amazoncom picked package return next day ups attempted pickup credit left shipping label along tracking number front desk shipping clerk amazoncom refuse acknowledge pickup return refuse provide refund im headed washington state attorney general office along federal trade commission see say problem,0.00034429971182777674,0.9996557002881722,0.10207515423443635,0.2,0.8202428809909733,82.02428809909733,High Trust
