Jerry Camps,/users/65412a611cef31001249ca45,US,1.0,2023-10-31 18:25:15+00:00,1.0,I bought a water heater and some other…,"I bought a water heater and some other stuff from Amazon. They broke the order up into 4 different deliveries. The first box had a car manifold in it. it was all labeled right with my name but i didn't order it. I called them to PU the item. After 2 days 2 other boxes came on separate trucks. They left them by my door and never PU the manifold box. The third truck arrived and Instead of picking up the car manifold, they PU the water heater they delivered that morning. I came home from work and called to see what happened and again I got some third-world person that I could hardly understand but this time I heard a baby crying in the background. I tried to explain and all their they answers were they were reading from some flowchart. They are told what to say word for word. They kept saying it was impossible that could have happened. I tried a few more times and I would get the same answers. After months of calling I gave up, now out 450 dollars. Then I figured maybe I could get some money back I lost so I told them to PU the manifold which was over 300 dollars. My name and address were all over the box. They said I'm sorry, you never ordered that Item and we can't give you credit. Now I'm stuck with a Ford 2012 manifold and out 450 dollars. Don't call or try to reason with customer service. They are completely useless. Better yet, save yourself a lot of aggravation. Don't bother ordering from Amazon. Does anybody have a use for a 2012 Ford manifold?",2022-11-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,31.0,1473,282,39,8,335.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,bought water heater stuff amazon broke order different delivery first box car manifold labeled right name didnt order called pu item day box came separate truck left door never pu manifold box third truck arrived instead picking car manifold pu water heater delivered morning came home work called see happened got thirdworld person could hardly understand time heard baby cry background tried explain answer reading flowchart told say word word kept saying impossible could happened tried time would get answer month calling gave dollar figured maybe could get money back lost told pu manifold dollar name address box said im sorry never ordered item cant give credit im stuck ford manifold dollar dont call try reason customer service completely useless better yet save lot aggravation dont bother ordering amazon anybody use ford manifold,8.316907686080696e-05,0.9999168309231392,0.15816040381379698,0.2,0.8315904962243289,83.15904962243289,High Trust
Clara Jarvis,/users/65168c74e531bc0012675854,GB,5.0,2023-10-31 15:59:24+00:00,1.0,"Amazon creates an environment where damaged products are acceptable, they'll give you refunds, but it's a hassle to even bother with in the first place.","In the start, amazon used to be really good and I could rely on them. I read a lot but the books I like can't be bought in most book stores, or I want new releases that will take months to come out in bookstores. I've had books come in pristine condition so the odd £30 I've paid for them has been worth it. But recently, sellers have been sending out books that are so dirty they can't be cleaned or removing the dirt damages the books and they see this as an okay thing to do. There is never holes in the packaging, the packaging is bent but even then how is this much dirt getting on the books?In the end, I've come to the conclusion that sellers are just selling really dirty books and nobody cares if you send it back or not, because the majority of the time people won't send them back or they'll forget. Thankfully, these specific books can be bought in bookstores for £3 more and they actually take care of them.It's pathetic that amazon thinks this is okay. However, they also seem to have a tendency to sell you broken ram sticks   costing almost £40 that just do not work on computers.I'm not paying for damaged items, and the reviews always say they're wonderful, but I still get damaged products.",2023-10-31 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,31.0,1209,227,152,25,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,start amazon used really good could rely read lot book like cant bought book store want new release take month come bookstore ive book come pristine condition odd £ ive paid worth recently seller sending book dirty cant cleaned removing dirt damage book see okay thing never hole packaging packaging bent even much dirt getting booksin end ive come conclusion seller selling really dirty book nobody care send back majority time people wont send back theyll forget thankfu