Robert McIntyre,/users/5e289d146167816b76866814,GB,7.0,2023-10-27 23:34:38+00:00,1.0,Horrendous,"Horrendous. Not a single member of their customer care team knows anything about GDPR. I have spent the last 9 days calling/emailing/chatting with Amazon representatives asking them to delete my dormant account. I have countless emails telling me the account has been deleted (in 48 hours). Each time I check, it's still there. There is nothing more I can do. They do not respond to complaints. Their webchat staff are just hopeless. I now have no option but to file a report against Amazon with the Information Commisioners office. Amazon is storing my personal data without my consent. They believe they are accountable to no-one.",2023-10-27 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,27.0,632,105,10,1,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,horrendous single member customer care team know anything gdpr spent last day callingemailingchatting amazon representative asking delete dormant account countless email telling account deleted hour time check still nothing respond complaint webchat staff hopeless option file report amazon information commisioners office amazon storing personal data without consent believe accountable noone,0.03703312852222788,0.9629668714777722,0.05888951205832866,0.2,0.7932613381505518,79.32613381505517,High Trust
J. L. Askew,/users/61773ee39e777d0013744b95,US,3.0,2023-10-27 20:06:07+00:00,2.0,Cancelled by Amazon,"I have been posting book reviews on Amazon for many years, always buying the books at the site to get the cachet of “Verified purchase”. My efforts resulted in more than thirty reviews appearing on Amazon, many rated as either “Top Positive Review” or “Top Critical Review”. But when I submitted a review of “The Last Politician” by Franklin Foer, I got a terse email from Amazon that it could not be posted “because it doesn’t meet our guidelines for one or more of these reasons: Profanity, Harassment, Hate Speech, Sexual Content, Illegal Activity, Private Information”. This had never happened before, and I was quite surprised. I went to the link that showed the “Community Guidelines” and read all six pages, scratching my head, trying to figure what I’d done wrong and then I realized the issue was politics. The person checking my review was apparently an extreme liberal so I made some changes that I thought might let my piece “pass” and I resubmitted it. But I soon realized this was a waste of time because I could make changes piecemeal again and again, but without knowing exactly what in my 850 word review was the ”problem”, my efforts would be fruitless.How could I get the nameless and faceless Amazon person behind the “wizard’s curtain” to tell me what to do? I remembered seeing on my “Author’s Page” a place where I could recommend books. I’d never used this feature before but now got the idea to cite Franklin Foer’s book as a “Recommendation”, writing in the comments, “I wrote a review of this book that did not pass the Amazon Moderator and I hope they will tell me what to change.” This was an act of desperation because I truly wanted to get my review posted and I was willing to make rewrites but had to have some guidance, sort of like we got from our high school English teacher who would take a red pencil and underline the problem.Apparently, my ploy with Amazon backfired because I soon got an email saying my post was “outside of our guidelines” and “consider this to be a first warning.” Amazon’s ire was about the book recommendation I’d put on my author’s page (specifically the comments showing Amazon in a bad light) since this was the only “post” I’d ever made other than book reviews.This was going nowhere, and I was not going to play Amazon’s games. I replied to the email, saying, “if you cannot tell me what I am doing wrong I will cancel my book advertising, Amazon Prime, and the Amazon prime credit card and quit making purchases from Amazon.” Six days later I got a reply email saying, “You have repeatedly posted content that violates our Community Guidelines . . . [and therefore] we’ve removed your ability to participate in Community features.” This was untrue because I’d only made one post, the one where I said, “I hope they [Amazon Moderator] will tell me what to change [in the review that had been rejected].”Unfortunately, all the book reviews I’d posted on Amazon over the years were deleted. This was quite disappointing because I’d spent hundreds of dollars on dozens of books, reading them closely over countless hours in order to write honest and informed book reviews and now my work had come to naught. I truly doubt that anyone has put more effort(both in the reading and the writing) into creating a book review than I have. Amazon’s actions have not only hurt me but are a disservice to millions of readers who rely on quality reviews to make wise decisions in their book purchases.As I said earlier, I’ve submitted critical assessments of other books to Amazon and never had a problem and I must conclude the current issue is over politics, simply having a different opinion. While I did say some positives about the author, I also faulted him for being almost sycophantic toward Biden. What he wrote was an uncritical fluff piece and I called it as such. The review, as written, would be passable to any reasonable person and there is nothing out of bounds in it. I read the book thoroughly and wrote an honest, critical review with no malice or evil intent. For anyone interested, a google search of “book reviews of ‘The Last Politician’” will take you to Goodreads where you’ll find my piece and you can decide for yourself.",2023-10-18 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,27.0,4201,739,19,3,9.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,posting book review amazon many year always buying book site get cachet “verified purchase” effort resulted thirty review appearing amazon many rated either “top positive review” “top critical review” submitted review “the last politician” franklin foer got terse email amazon could posted “because doesn’t meet guideline one reason profanity harassment hate speech sexual content illegal activity private information” never happened quite surprised went link showed “community guidelines” read six page scratching head trying figure i’d done wrong realized issue politics person checking review apparently extreme liberal made change thought might let piece “pass” resubmitted soon realized waste time could make change piecemeal without knowing exactly word review ”problem” effort would fruitlesshow could get nameless faceless amazon person behind “wizard’s curtain” tell remembered seeing “author’s page” place could recommend book i’d never used feature got idea cite franklin foer’s book “recommendation” writing comment “i wrote review book pas amazon moderator hope tell change” act desperation truly wanted get review posted willing make rewrite guidance sort like got high school english teacher would take red pencil underline problemapparently ploy amazon backfired soon got email saying post “outside guidelines” “consider first warning” amazon’s ire book recommendation i’d put author’s page specifically comment showing amazon bad light since “post” i’d ever made book reviewsthis going nowhere going play amazon’s game replied email saying “if cannot tell wrong cancel book advertising amazon prime amazon prime credit card quit making purchase amazon” six day later got reply email saying “you repeatedly posted content violates community guideline therefore we’ve removed ability participate community features” untrue i’d made one post one said “i hope amazon moderator tell change review rejected”unfortunately book review i’d posted amazon year deleted quite disappointing i’d spent hundred dollar dozen book reading closely countless hour order write honest informed book review work come naught truly doubt anyone put effortboth reading writing creating book review amazon’s action hurt disservice million reader rely quality review make wise decision book purchasesas said earlier i’ve submitted critical assessment book amazon never problem must conclude current issue politics simply different opinion say positive author also faulted almost sycophantic toward biden wrote uncritical fluff piece called review written would passable reasonable person nothing bound read book thoroughly wrote honest critical review malice evil intent anyone interested google search “book review ‘the last politician’” take goodreads you’ll find piece decide,0.004516439607563357,0.9954835603924367,0.414469994391475,0.4,1.1806357790745134,118.06357790745135,High Trust
Anthony Cox,/users/6536fd471ba5c40012fbaf61,US,2.0,2023-10-27 17:53:08+00:00,1.0,I can't believe Amazon's customer service and how bad it is they think they can steal from me please don't mind my spelling in the story and what Amazon's doing to me,I have never been treated like this in my life by a company lied to hung up on told one thing and then another different thing the next time I call I had to go to the length of recording my last conversations with the customer service at Amazon because of the lying I didn't return because they sent me a drone and I did not know that the Drone they sent me was the wrong drone it was a $240 drone when I ordered a $490 room they tried telling me that it's been too long to return it and I told them well I didn't even know until a friend of mine showed me his drone which we both ordered the same drones at the same time he got a totally different one than me and then looking it up it was a $200 less drone they told me that I was just out of luck and I'm put to what bite the ball and let them keep my $200 no so I'm fighting it finally I got a manager to agree to the return this was a month ago so I returned the item took 6 days for them to get the Drone back I know this for a fact because I tracked the package the first person I talked to about it I told them look on your website it says returns will be processed when item is received 1 to 5 business days that's exactly what it said on the return policy for that drill I called them they said it was not there and they did not receive it then I double checked with ups and they said it was there I called the next day and the gentleman that answered the next day said it was there and I had to wait for it to be processed okay perfect at least I know it's there I wait about 5-6 days I call back and I talked to a lady and I say okay so why hasn't my return gone through yet why haven't you guys refunded my money and she says well the drones not there and I said the gentleman yesterday told me it was there and he could see it was at the facility and I told her so I'm getting copies of all this and once I told her I was getting copies of all the tracking she hung up on me so I was a little frustrated and irritated about 3 days later I had another claim for A to Z claim that was put to be processed that the people never even put in I don't know if they're just pretending to type so that you hear typing or what but three different times they did that on this separate order I still haven't received anything from that and I'm going on over 3 weeks but back to the Drone so the next day when I called in they were trying to make excuses of why I wasn't receiving the money due to not being able to return to drone even though the manager said I could return it because they gave me the wrong item and it wasn't my fault and I didn't notice it till I saw my friends drone so they told me okay you know what you'll get the money and one to three days I was like oh cool finally you know it's been almost 3 weeks now and that time went by nothing called again spoke with someone else they said that nothing hasn't even been done they don't even see where that person put in that information in the computer I told him don't you guys record these conversations can't you see this and at that point is when I started thinking you know what I better start recording it so they don't have any clue where the packages what they're doing and where my return money is they've had the item for over a week now so now two weeks pass still have the item I've been calling every two days asking what's going on no one can tell me anything they're not entering any information on their computer so I'm screen recording our conversations with the guys and they don't have a clue about anything they're telling me I can't return that item and I'm sitting there arguing with them that they already have the item they've had it for 2 weeks now finally I get someone at customer service after I wait another two days to call I talked to someone for a month in now he says you know what I know you probably really need your money back and we've had the Drone for a long time and I'm going to see what I can do about this I won't let you hang up till I get this fixed so I'm recording all this so I have all these conversations now he's telling me that he can't make it happen it won't work it won't let him and I'm not understanding are you guys ripping me off and stealing my money now is Amazon ripping people off and still in their money so he says that he's going to go a different route and try to return other items if I cancel my return return other items to make the amount of the Drone so now he's put money back on like a prepaid gift card that I lose money on every time I spend money on it and so forth and so he gave me a $170 just remember now it's a $497 drone and that's it and that was after waiting three days again to get that money so now I'm just at Whitson and I can't believe Amazon would screw people over like this I don't know who they have running customer service but I'm at the point where I'm ready to never use Amazon again and boycott them for all the lying and thieving that they're doing right now it must be Amazon's new policies to lie,2023-09-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,27.0,5019,1025,166,32,31.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,never treated like life company lied hung told one thing another different thing next time call go length recording last conversation customer service amazon lying didnt return sent drone know drone sent wrong drone drone ordered room tried telling long return told well didnt even know friend mine showed drone ordered drone time got totally different one looking less drone told luck im put bite ball let keep im fighting finally got manager agree return month ago returned item took day get drone back know fact tracked package first person talked told look website say return processed item received business day thats exactly said return policy d