Jim McPherson,/users/653a7766ebe69a00129e5f2a,CA,1.0,2023-10-26 16:28:01+00:00,1.0,Many things Amazon fails in customer service,"Many things. The album I ordered was supposed to be new. Instead it was used with scratch marks and the cover was bent and coffee stained. It took many months of back and forth before I was refunded. Then to top it off, I order another album and all of sudden they were billing me for Amazon Prime which my wife's pays for on her account. I tried to get reimbursed for this charge and it was once again a miserable experience. I cancelled the prime membership and Amazon account and the Amazon MasterCard through MBNA. Worst experience ever.",2023-10-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,26.0,541,99,44,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,many thing album ordered supposed new instead used scratch mark cover bent coffee stained took many month back forth refunded top order another album sudden billing amazon prime wife pay account tried get reimbursed charge miserable experience cancelled prime membership amazon account amazon mastercard mbna worst experience ever,0.02663472226449072,0.9733652777355093,0.055524397083567024,0.2,0.797787518284468,79.7787518284468,High Trust
Mark Price,/users/5ac0cbfb4de5666d349f882a,GB,7.0,2023-10-26 16:15:31+00:00,1.0,Where do I start,"Where do I start, Amazon, I buy hundreds of items off Amazon as a buyer for the company I work for and usually they are okish. However lately they have become a nightmare! I could run you through the brash emails the hanging up of the phone or the weird decisions they seem to be making but whats the point you will all have your own versions of that to relate to. What I will say is that Amazon has become so big the tail is wagging the dog! Items dont arrive, refunds dont arrive, returns do arrive but then are deemed to be wrong by Amazon so further charges are applied to accounts. Do yourself a favour and shop about, there are better and even cheaper options out there its a little more work but when you get to the point of spending thousands a year Amazon should be your last choice not your first!",2023-10-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,26.0,807,156,16,4,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,start amazon buy hundred item amazon buyer company work usually okish however lately become nightmare could run brash email hanging phone weird decision seem making whats point version relate say amazon become big tail wagging dog item dont arrive refund dont arrive return arrive deemed wrong amazon charge applied account favour shop better even cheaper option little work get point spending thousand year amazon last choice first,0.7286809705189841,0.27131902948101594,0.08749298934380258,0.2,0.45315811260926847,45.31581126092685,Low Trust
Brian Raburn,/users/5ec75d9aee8f29435ad70e68,US,3.0,2023-10-26 15:50:59+00:00,1.0,A couple of years ago I had a problem…,"A couple of years ago I had a problem with my Amazon membership and was able to get through right away to someone who could speak good clear English and it was taken care of in less than a minute. This time I just got a notice saying that my order of light bulbs was attempted but not left. No explanation why, no nothing. Tried calling customer service got put on hold by someone who I could not understand 3 times then the phone on their end hung up after time. Their customer service has done a 180 not for the good.",2023-10-25 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,26.0,519,102,38,9,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,couple year ago problem amazon membership able get right away someone could speak good clear english taken care less minute time got notice saying order light bulb attempted left explanation nothing tried calling customer service got put hold someone could understand time phone end hung time customer service done good,0.014993969684448463,0.9850060303155516,0.05720695457094784,0.2,0.8039444060719654,80.39444060719654,High Trust
C G Eastwood,/users/548db07400006400019d7347,GB,33.0,2023-10-26 11:05:13+00:00,1.0,Buyer beware.,"Buyer beware.Amazon are increasingly touting themselves as ""A Marketplace Seller"".  A recent experience with a USA book seller is something I will strive to avoid from now on.Basically I ordered a used book on Excel spreadsheet programming etc.  The order was completed early... but the contents were a book called 'AUTOCAD 2020'.Something I have zero use for.I am now in the process of returning a hefty book to California, USA.I will bear the cost of a return post.The really bad news is that 'Amazon' will not refund MY money until the seller informs them of receipt.  This would be the same seller, that Amazon now tells me, has NO STOCK of the original book I ordered... leaving me to conclude that a book known to be misnamed on their stock inventory may have been shipped.Bottom line; this is a lot less like 'good service' than I would like.  The tick-box systems of so many businesses these days offers NO obvious clues that Amazon are likely to do much more than refer me to the task of reading their (no doubt) extensive T&C's which will justify their lax attitude to putting right the mistakes THEIR contacts have made.The one star refers to this issue.  I freely acknowledge that I find that their 'own sales' are in pretty good shape for most purchases.",2023-10-25 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,26.0,1267,221,13,2,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,buyer bewareamazon increasingly touting marketplace seller recent experience usa book seller something strive avoid onbasically ordered used book excel spreadsheet programming etc order completed early content book called autocad something zero use fori process returning hefty book california usai bear cost return postthe really bad news amazon refund money seller informs receipt would seller amazon tell stock original book ordered leaving conclude book known misnamed stock inventory may shippedbottom line lot less like good service would like tickbox system many business day offer obvious clue amazon likely much refer task reading doubt extensive tc justify lax attitude putting right mistake contact madethe one star refers issue freely acknowledge find sale pretty good shape purchase,0.014776060513809969,0.98522393948619,0.12394840157038699,0.2,0.8174016500571724,81.74016500571723,High Trust
