Kristina Kress,/users/65317dc6dd063d001247d32b,US,1.0,2023-10-19 21:04:46+00:00,1.0,Don’t Believe Them,"I ordered a telescoping pole which turned out to be too wobbly. When I requested a return, I received notification that I could not take it to a store to return it. They would send someone to pick it up on October 19 and it would be picked up between 10AM and 8 PM. The day before pickup, I received notification that someone had to be there in person when they came to pick it up. I had a doctors appointment that I had to cancel in order to be here. A person did come to pick it up and I ran outside and asked why I had to be home for when he picked it up. He told me that was incorrect. Why would Amazon tell someone they had to be home and then give them a bloody 10 hour window? What kind of business model is this? Maybe they should skip their space ideas and focus on customer service.",2023-10-19 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,19.0,792,161,18,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered telescoping pole turned wobbly requested return received notification could take store return would send someone pick october would picked pm day pickup received notification someone person came pick doctor appointment cancel order person come pick ran outside asked home picked told incorrect would amazon tell someone home give bloody hour window kind business model maybe skip space idea focus customer service,0.026789861558852747,0.9732101384411472,0.09029725182277061,0.2,0.8046645195851277,80.46645195851278,High Trust
