NS Ferris,/users/652e9323778a70001281d3d7,US,1.0,2023-10-17 16:03:45+00:00,1.0,No more big ticket items,"For big ticket items, Amazon apparently has a policy that refunds can take up to 30 days. Now, I've been a regular customer (who isn't). Between me and my husband, we probably buy something from Amazon 2-3 times a week. Then one day we buy a big ticket item ($350), return it, and this happens. It certainly leaves a bad taste in my mouth about this company, but more, I am so disheartened because I have really loved Amazon. Calling customer service is something I've rarely done. I don't even mind the song-and-dance scripted responses. I know the call center people are just doing their jobs, and they're honest people just like us. I am always polite when I speak to them, but the clincher for me was when I asked to speak to the supervisor, the guy practically told me in not so many words, 'If I transfer you, ma'am, I guarantee he will tell you the same thing anyway.' Through polite insistence, I managed to make him transfer me to his lead guy, who seemed to be more polished in language and demeanor. After more song-and-dance exchange, the bottom line is the lead person couldn't even override the system to plead my 'proven and very legitimate' case. But he at least gave me a viable excuse. They received my package through UPS a week ago, yet my app dashboard does not reflect that. Apparently, the communication breakdown comes from the return center, who has not processed the return. I am exasperated. The $382 refund is not going to bankrupt me, sure, but what this tells me is this: it's only going to get worse as this mega shopping platform gets even bigger.",2023-10-17 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,17.0,1579,284,24,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,big ticket item amazon apparently policy refund take day ive regular customer isnt husband probably buy something amazon time week one day buy big ticket item return happens certainly leaf bad taste mouth company disheartened really loved amazon calling customer service something ive rarely done dont even mind songanddance scripted response know call center people job theyre honest people like u always polite speak clincher asked speak supervisor guy practically told many word transfer maam guarantee tell thing anyway polite insistence managed make transfer lead guy seemed polished language demeanor songanddance exchange bottom line lead person couldnt even override system plead proven legitimate case least gave viable excuse received package ups week ago yet app dashboard reflect apparently communication breakdown come return center processed return exasperated refund going bankrupt sure tell going get worse mega shopping platform get even bigger,0.004745829097365841,0.9952541709026341,0.15928210880538418,0.2,0.8294835072123938,82.94835072123938,High Trust
