ono egbedi,/users/5e583f836ca715303185a7dd,GB,10.0,2023-10-15 22:03:35+00:00,1.0,Zero star if I could,"Zero star if I could based on the level of service.I have been with Amazon Prime membership for as long as it started and the actions of this customer service literally put the nail on this coffinI was being charged twice since september 2021, i pay annually for my subscription and noticed an added monthly subscription of 8.99 as well. When I called the customer service to call this out and also let them know they charged both my debit and credit card...i was concerned my bank card might have been hacked and  the customer service staff laughed at me for complaining, his tone was rude and was dismissive of my claims, he wasn't aware of their product either. I demanded to speak to the Manager who was not far off. I asked to raise a complaint and he asked ""why?"" ""Do you want the service personnel fired?"" I was shocked and said a complaint is to ensure the right training is provided where necessary. Needless to say, he refused to provide a reference number or followup details, stating it is an internal affair????Long story short, the manager managed to request a year's worth of the double payment and I decided to end my subscription with Amazon....I no longer wish to have this service, there are alternatives.",2023-10-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,15.0,1224,217,20,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,zero star could based level servicei amazon prime membership long started action customer service literally put nail coffini charged twice since september pay annually subscription noticed added monthly subscription well called customer service call also let know charged debit credit cardi concerned bank card might hacked customer service staff laughed complaining tone rude dismissive claim wasnt aware product either demanded speak manager far asked raise complaint asked want service personnel fired shocked said complaint ensure right training provided necessary needless say refused provide reference number followup detail stating internal affairlong story short manager managed request year worth double payment decided end subscription amazoni longer wish service alternative,0.023871083036766813,0.9761289169632332,0.12170499158721257,0.2,0.8124054567990591,81.2405456799059,High Trust
Consumer,/users/5eaaac1d0c79cdf03bc85591,US,2.0,2023-10-16 23:34:32+00:00,1.0,"Unreliable, as always","For the fifth time, after of course Amazon raised the yearly price… I place an order that says if I order now it will be In tomorrow. After the order is placed it changes it to the day after. Then when the day arrives at 10 at night I get the we are sorry your order is late bs and I get it the next day or so times a day after that. Glad they raised prime, offer next to nothing for free movies on prime video, and deliver significantly later then promised. Now I was supposed to get my order Saturday, didn’t arrive, then Sunday, didn’t arrive, then today, didn’t arrive. I bet next they lost it and I’ll get a refund, all the time wasted waiting for it but just apology and refund.",2023-10-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,16.0,684,135,21,3,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,fifth time course amazon raised yearly price… place order say order tomorrow order placed change day day arrives night get sorry order late b get next day time day glad raised prime offer next nothing free movie prime video deliver significantly later promised supposed get order saturday didn’t arrive sunday didn’t arrive today didn’t arrive bet next lost i’ll get refund time wasted waiting apology refund,0.013987911936158991,0.986012088063841,0.07571508693213685,0.2,0.8081490614183477,80.81490614183477,High Trust
Mrs Margaret Ross,/users/60b4e3942a6599001abf61b3,GB,4.0,2023-10-15 14:35:10+00:00,1.0,I noticed the Amazon Prime van was…,"I noticed the Amazon Prime van was parked in one of the disabled bay spaces outside my sheltered housing accommodation. He had taken up 1 and 1/2 of the only 2 disabled bays for the building which has 27 flats. I was unable to park my car due to the limited space that was left. I was entering my building as he was exiting. I asked him if he was aware that he'd parked in disabled bay to which he replied"" So what,there's worse things to complain about!"" I told him how inconsiderate this was as I couldn't park my car in the space he had left me. Also there was other spaces he could have parked his van.His reply"" Well tell folk in your building not to order stuff then"" I asked for his name as I was not happy with his attitude, very unprofessional. He wouldn't give me his name. He walked away and made fun of me saying "" Ooh go ahead and report me then spekky!"" This happened at 1pm on Saturday 14th October 23. I feel this kind of attitude towards an elderly disabled person is totally unacceptable.  Does Amazon not do a Customer Service training course for these drivers? If not its about time they did! I am absolutely furious with this driver moreso when other drivers have been very courteous and professional towards every service user who depend on Amazon for their needs. I'd like to think that this review would be taken seriously and dealt with appropriately.",2023-10-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,15.0,1376,255,35,7,1.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,noticed amazon prime van parked one disabled bay space outside sheltered housing accommodation taken disabled bay building flat unable park car due limited space left entering building exiting asked aware hed parked disabled bay replied whattheres worse thing complain told inconsiderate couldnt park car space left also space could parked vanhis reply well tell folk building order stuff asked name happy attitude unprofessional wouldnt give name walked away made fun saying ooh go ahead report spekky happened pm saturday th october feel kind attitude towards elderly disabled person totally unacceptable amazon customer service training course driver time absolutely furious driver moreso driver courteous professional towards every service user depend amazon need id like think review would taken seriously dealt appropriately,0.7215130333084397,0.27848696669156026,0.1430173864273696,0.2,0.467846960631254,46.7846960631254,Low Trust
Jonathan Parent Lévesque,/users/5da5f49e7e2251d8a4147a5e,CA,10.0,2023-10-15 13:18:14+00:00,1.0,The art of creating hurdles to prevent reclamations.,"At the recommendation of my post-graduate supervisor, I commanded ""Marketing Accountability: A New Metrics Model to Measure Marketing Effectiveness"" by Malcolm McDonald on Amazon on September 21, 2023.Since the delivery was expected between October 3 and October 16, I didn't pay too much attention as I was expecting an email on delivery.Today (October 14, 2023), I decided to check on my Amazon account what was happening with my delivery. It turns out that the focal item was supposedly delivered on September 27 - at least one week before the expected delivery range. Yet, as I look at my email, I never received any notification that the shipping was delivered...For God's sake, how is a normal customer supposed to do their due diligence with their shipping if the goods are delivered outside of the expected date range and the carrier doesn't even bother to notify the recipient that the delivery has been done?Naturally, being a post-graduate student living with less than $12,000 of yearly income, I try to request refunding. No way to chat with customer support and the chatbot says banality about it is the seller’s problem and not theirs. Then, I requested a phone call and yet another automatic voice-robot saying the exact same banality. With no other choice, I tried to contact the vendor via their system and didn’t even get an email proving that I contacted them so I could make a reclamation to my credit card provider under the “Consumer Protector Act”.Exasperated, I wrote a bad review on the product describing the exact same problem, which naturally was silenced by their moderation team.Good job Amazon on making it impossible for the poorest people in society to get a refund and doing such a good job managing your reputation on your own platform (owned media). It’s a shame that there are independent platforms on which exasperated customers can do negative eWOM without your interference, though…",2023-10-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,15.0,1923,318,52,8,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recommendation postgraduate supervisor commanded marketing accountability new metric model measure marketing effectiveness malcolm mcdonald amazon september since delivery expected october october didnt pay much attention expecting email deliverytoday october decided check amazon account happening delivery turn focal item supposedly delivered september least one week expected delivery range yet look email never received notification shipping deliveredfor god sake normal customer supposed due diligence shipping good delivered outside expected date range carrier doesnt even bother notify recipient delivery donenaturally postgraduate student living less yearly income try request refunding way chat customer support chatbot say banality seller’s problem requested phone call yet another automatic voicerobot saying exact banality choice tried contact vendor via system didn’t even get email proving contacted could make reclamation credit card provider “consumer protector act”exasperated wrote bad review product describing exact problem naturally silenced moderation teamgood job amazon making impossible poorest people society get refund good job managing reputation platform owned medium it’s shame independent platform exasperated customer negative ewom without interference though…,0.01576365106863769,0.9842363489313624,0.1783510936623668,0.2,0.8277883931981544,82.77883931981545,High Trust
David Galloway,/users/53590f4100006400016fd62c,GB,44.0,2023-10-15 07:31:13+00:00,1.0,Poor customer service and support,"Well, I never thought I would be writing a negative review about Amazon. After many years as loyal customers, and being a Prime member for many years, spending a lot of money, I find myself writing a negative review.Whilst being Prime members we have never had problems with faulty, not as described, not received goods, etc. Now we have cancelled out Prime membership, the customer service and customer support has become sub-standard. It just shows that you are not treated equally and there is no equality.If we had a problem with an item, the money was refunded either as soon as the item was returned or within a very quick period of time. Now we have cancelled our Prime membership, we have had nothing but trouble getting a simple refund for an item that was clearly sold '!s new' but was infact 'ex-display' and not as described. This is a clear cut case and should have warranted an immediate refund.After contacting the seller and getting no response, then one response, and no further response, we contacted Amazon. There was excuse, after excuse. They eventually said they would refund the money and said it will be in your account, but it wasn't.So bearing in mind they said they had refunded it! Two days later they send a message saying, ""your A-Z claim has been successful and we will be refunding you payment."" So the initial refund they said they had refunded, they had not actually refunded it. Now I will have to wait another 7 days for a refund. In total that will be 15 days from the item being received back by the seller.Why would you receive lesser customer service than a Prime member? Surely, all customers should receive the same customer service, after all we are all customers. Why is a non-prime member discriminated against? We are disgusted and disappointed in the service we have paid for, and this is not the experience we have become accustomed to over the many years with amazon.We have spend thousands of pounds with Amazon over the years. This will probably the last time we purchase from Amazon, and we will be closing both of our accounts with Amazon.",2023-10-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,15.0,2092,366,33,5,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,well never thought would writing negative review amazon many year loyal customer prime member many year spending lot money find writing negative reviewwhilst prime member never problem faulty described received good etc cancelled prime membership customer service customer support become substandard show treated equally equalityif problem item money refunded either soon item returned within quick period time cancelled prime membership nothing trouble getting simple refund item clearly sold new infact exdisplay described clear cut case warranted immediate refundafter contacting seller getting response one response response contacted amazon excuse excuse eventually said would refund money said account wasntso bearing mind said refunded two day later send message saying az claim successful refunding payment initial refund said refunded actually refunded wait another day refund total day item received back sellerwhy would receive lesser customer service prime member surely customer receive customer service customer nonprime member discriminated disgusted disappointed service paid experience become accustomed many year amazonwe spend thousand pound amazon year probably last time purchase amazon closing account amazon,0.22452399548386298,0.7754760045161371,0.2052720134604599,0.2,0.7287924049501606,72.87924049501606,Medium Trust
Robert Acker,/users/5e6fd104062aad63d1c79f61,US,3.0,2023-10-15 01:56:23+00:00,2.0,Amazon customer support is becoming…,"Amazon customer support is becoming progressively worse. You strugle to get a human, then you get someone that speaks English as a 3rd language (barely).  They are located in the Philippines or S. America.  Since they cannot understand you, or you them, resolving anything the least bit complicated is a struggle.  And for this you pay $179/yr?",2023-10-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,15.0,344,57,36,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer support becoming progressively worse strugle get human get someone speaks english rd language barely located philippine america since cannot understand resolving anything least bit complicated struggle pay yr,0.029828626362204097,0.9701713736377959,0.03196859226023556,0.4,1.0914794052709451,109.1479405270945,High Trust
