daisy7909,/users/541ea31400006400018bb085,GB,10.0,2023-10-14 21:12:48+00:00,1.0,Terrible and total lack of customer service,I have been waiting for a delivery this afternoon. I kept checking for updates. It eventually said delivered through letterbox. I don't know which one but not mine. I contacted them and said this is the second time running this has happened. I eventually managed to bypass the computerised moron and got through to alleged customer service team. I said what had happened again and they said for me to give them till Tuesday. I told them I am disabled hence my using them but doubtful for future now. Such good customer service that they can't even give you a call you back. If I could leave a minus rating it would be a minimum 5. Terrible service and no interest in their customers.,2023-10-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,14.0,683,124,43,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,waiting delivery afternoon kept checking update eventually said delivered letterbox dont know one mine contacted said second time running happened eventually managed bypass computerised moron got alleged customer service team said happened said give till tuesday told disabled hence using doubtful future good customer service cant even give call back could leave minus rating would minimum terrible service interest customer,0.018614681350329638,0.9813853186496704,0.06954570947840717,0.2,0.8046018012205166,80.46018012205167,High Trust
RNR,/users/638e595e39ac4d0013fef5ad,US,2.0,2023-10-14 20:17:15+00:00,1.0,Do not allow customer service to access your devices!,"I gave a customer service rep access to both of my Kindle Fires due to a problem (that I later figured out wasn't actually related to Amazon) and he deleted a few hundred bookmarks.  4 phone calls later and I still haven't gotten them back. One person told that my only option was a  factory reset which I had been trying to avoid because it's a total PITA.  According to the settings menu this should have restored all of my data; it didn't.  The last person I spoke to told me that the info in the settings menu about factory resetting your Kindle is ""wrong."" He wasn't able to tell me why it was never addressed.  When I told him that when I purchased my second Kindle all of my bookmarks were downloaded from my backup, which means my info is stored somewhere, he told me my Kindle must be defective.  Oh. And this was supposedly a supervisor I was speaking to.  I've sent a registered letter off to their main office but am not expecting any response.",2023-09-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,14.0,956,178,53,9,14.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,gave customer service rep access kindle fire due problem later figured wasnt actually related amazon deleted hundred bookmark phone call later still havent gotten back one person told option factory reset trying avoid total pita according setting menu restored data didnt last person spoke told info setting menu factory resetting kindle wrong wasnt able tell never addressed told purchased second kindle bookmark downloaded backup mean info stored somewhere told kindle must defective oh supposedly supervisor speaking ive sent registered letter main office expecting response,0.011702066526401943,0.9882979334735981,0.09983174425126191,0.2,0.8141153155870514,81.41153155870514,High Trust
