Stephanie Copeland,/users/610d5d36024a570012d4eb5f,US,2.0,2023-10-12 05:15:27+00:00,1.0,Buyer Beware,"I have shopped at Amazon for years. I’ve spend thousands of dollars with their company and always had good customer service up until now. I ordered some curtains from a third-party seller which didn’t look anything like they did in the picture. I asked Amazon for a refund and they told me to contact the third party seller first. The third-party seller refused to give me a prepaid shipping label until I provided pictures. Which I did. After that I never heard from them again. I contacted Amazon again and was told that I could keep the curtains and that I would be receiving a refund within 3 to 5 business days. Well a week goes by and nothing. I call Amazon again and they tell me that that the first customer service representative shouldn’t have told me that and that the best they can do is open up a claim and in the meantime I should just try and send the curtains back myself and they’ll refund me the shipping cost. I go to UPS and they tell me that it’s gonna cost $600 bucks to send these curtains back. Then I receive an email from Amazon denying me on the claim. I call them yet again and tell them look, I can’t afford to send these curtains back for $600 bucks. They tell me not to worry they will send me a prepaid shipping label and I will get refunded for the curtains. This time I ask for an email confirming this. Which they send me. The representative also files an appeal on the first claim. I received another email telling me that the appeal has  been denied on the grounds that I did not contact the third-party seller within 30 days. I call Amazon AGAIN and send them screenshots proving that I got in touch with the third-party seller within a week and that their own representatives had told me I would be getting a prepaid label. When they finally get back in touch with me they tell me that both of their representatives shouldn’t have said that and they will train their employees better in the future but since both appeals were denied they can’t do anything. So what they’re telling me is that they allow their own customer services representatives to lie to you just to get you off of the phone and also sorry not sorry your just out $200 bucks for the curtains you can’t return. I ended up canceling my prime membership and opening up a claim with the Better Business Bureau, no matter what happens though I’ll never shop with them again. I would rather spend extra money on shipping than give money to a company that knowingly lies to me.",2023-10-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,10.0,12.0,2478,460,12,2,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,shopped amazon year i’ve spend thousand dollar company always good customer service ordered curtain thirdparty seller didn’t look anything like picture asked amazon refund told contact third party seller first thirdparty seller refused give prepaid shipping label provided picture never heard contacted amazon told could keep curtain would receiving refund within business day well week go nothing call amazon tell first customer service representative shouldn’t told best open claim meantime try send curtain back they’ll refund shipping cost go ups tell it’s gonna cost buck send curtain back receive email amazon denying claim call yet tell look can’t afford send curtain back buck tell worry send prepaid shipping label get refunded curtain time ask email confirming send representative also file appeal first claim received another email telling appeal denied ground contact thirdparty seller within day call amazon send screenshots proving got touch thirdparty seller within week representative told would getting prepaid label finally get back touch tell representative shouldn’t said train employee better future since appeal denied can’t anything they’re telling allow customer service representative lie get phone also sorry sorry buck curtain can’t return ended canceling prime membership opening claim better business bureau matter happens though i’ll never shop would rather spend extra money shipping give money company knowingly lie,0.01168143973415862,0.9883185602658414,0.2579921480650589,0.2,0.8457577097459325,84.57577097459324,High Trust
