Bob Angeli,/users/6510bab2892f9600125fccfd,US,1.0,2023-09-25 00:45:24+00:00,1.0,"Beware the ""promised"" $10 promotional credit","On more than one occasion I've been ""promised"" a $10 promotional credit as compensation for poor customer experiences such as my packages being delivered to other homes in my area, or in some cases not at all.  These ""promises"" are made over the phone by customer service reps as well as by e-mail confirmation  when I've asked for that. Yet, the credit is never issued and there's no way of knowing until the next purchase (on items sold by Amazon themselves only) when no such credit is applied.  There is no way to see these credits in the customer account section.  It's hard for me how to see that this isn't deliberate, with the thinking being, ""Tell the customer they'll get the credit, but don't apply it and they'll just forgot about it.""  Any REAL credit should be readily visible in the customer account section, along with a case number and description of the reason for the credit.  Period.  Stop the DECEPTION!",2023-09-18 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,25.0,924,162,44,6,7.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,one occasion ive promised promotional credit compensation poor customer experience package delivered home area case promise made phone customer service rep well email confirmation ive asked yet credit never issued there way knowing next purchase item sold amazon credit applied way see credit customer account section hard see isnt deliberate thinking tell customer theyll get credit dont apply theyll forgot real credit readily visible customer account section along case number description reason credit period stop deception,0.023205204557512845,0.9767947954424872,0.09085810431856421,0.2,0.8065690185849563,80.65690185849563,High Trust
