Paul Howe,/users/64380897077a9c0013023664,US,2.0,2023-09-15 00:38:05+00:00,1.0,Amazon not so Prime anymore,"I have been a long time member of Amazon Prime. I used to place orders and always received them within 1-2 days. Once the pandemic hit, it apparently gave businesses an excuse to slack off on customer service. The 2 day guarentee changed to a 2 day approximate, and we would get items that ran a day or 2 late once a month or so. Back in August 2023 I ordered 2 laptops, not a cheap order it was about $2700. They were both ordered from the same amazon store and delivery to the same address. On day 2 one laptop arrived, but not the other. Although it was odd since they should have shipped together I let it slide since my account said it was delayed in transit to be delivered the next day. I contacted them on chat at the end of day 3 when it said delayed in transit again. They promptly lied to me and said it was in the system and would be dropped off on day 4. At the end of day 4 I was told after a very lengthy chat with 2 CS reps that ""they didn't know where the item was but not to worry this happens sometimes"" I told them I was going to be out of town on business over the weekend but the amazon store still had the item in stock saying it could be there the next day. They said they couldn't do that because the other one had shipped even though they didn't know where it was. They said there was nothing they could do just give it another day. So day 5 comes no delivery CS reps 5 and 6 both lie to me but I finally get CSR 6 a ""supervisor"" to ""put a stop on the order and refund my money withing 48 hours"" I ordered the same item from walmart+ and received it in less than 2 days. The refund that was supposed to be returned in 48 hrs took CS rep #7 on day 15 to finally process the refund. I saved all of the chat logs and highlighted where CS reps would tell me that the last rep lied to me on 5 different occassions. Amazon is not so prime anymore. Walmart+ rocked my delivery in about 36 hours though.",2023-09-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,15.0,1921,389,27,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,long time member amazon prime used place order always received within day pandemic hit apparently gave business excuse slack customer service day guarentee changed day approximate would get item ran day late month back august ordered laptop cheap order ordered amazon store delivery address day one laptop arrived although odd since shipped together let slide since account said delayed transit delivered next day contacted chat end day said delayed transit promptly lied said system would dropped day end day told lengthy chat c rep didnt know item worry happens sometimes told going town business weekend amazon store still item stock saying could next day said couldnt one shipped even though didnt know said nothing could give another day day come delivery c rep lie finally get csr supervisor put stop order refund money withing hour ordered item walmart received less day refund supposed returned hr took c rep day finally process refund saved chat log highlighted c rep would tell last rep lied different occassions amazon prime anymore walmart rocked delivery hour though,0.004400722802588784,0.9955992771974113,0.21817162086371283,0.2,0.8414339627714482,84.14339627714482,High Trust
Jackie Romero,/users/65038823f26646001346be15,US,1.0,2023-09-15 00:24:55+00:00,1.0,Amazon doesn't honor their promises,"The card that gets charged for my amazon prime membership expired and I had unfortunately not updated it to the new card in time, so instead of amazon contacting me by phone or email, they charged a random card that I had used to purchase something a long time ago. That card is linked to a checking account I don't really use anymore so I was overdrafted and got a $30 overdraft fee from the bank. The bank wouldn't refund since the prime charge was legitimate so I went on to amazon's online customer service chat to see if they could help. One woman passed me to a supervisor named Fatima. Fatima apologized and said that she would refund August's charge to the card that shouldn't have been used and to make up for the $30 bank fee, she would refund me for June and July's charges as well. Obviously I was at that point a happy customer, until... Two weeks later and not one refund had been received. So I call this time, instead of using the online chat. I don't know the name of the man I talked to, but after placing me on hold twice, he lets me know that even though HE COULD SEE the convo I had with Fatima, he couldn't honor her promise because it was ""against policy"". I can't believe he was able to see the convo I had where a supervisor stated that she'd refund me and was still unwilling to resolve the issue. I was so disgusted I cancelled my account with them. Honestly, I hardly watch anything on prime video nor do I really order anything anymore, so my membership won't be missed. That company doesn't deserve a single dime from anyone if that's how it's going to operate.",2023-09-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,15.0,1591,299,35,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,card get charged amazon prime membership expired unfortunately updated new card time instead amazon contacting phone email charged random card used purchase something long time ago card linked checking account dont really use anymore overdrafted got overdraft fee bank bank wouldnt refund since prime charge legitimate went amazon online customer service chat see could help one woman passed supervisor named fatima fatima apologized said would refund august charge card shouldnt used make bank fee would refund june july charge well obviously point happy customer two week later one refund received call time instead using online chat dont know name man talked placing hold twice let know even though could see convo fatima couldnt honor promise policy cant believe able see convo supervisor stated shed refund still unwilling resolve issue disgusted cancelled account honestly hardly watch anything prime video really order anything anymore membership wont missed company doesnt deserve single dime anyone thats going operate,0.006225669816084536,0.9937743301839155,0.16769489624228828,0.2,0.8304261443404154,83.04261443404154,High Trust
