Keith green,/users/6083172d2e5a09001b22db48,GB,8.0,2023-09-11 20:32:06+00:00,1.0,Purchase an item on the 24th aug 2023,"Purchase an item on the 24th aug 2023 , item was being sold by Amazon eu and advertised as in stock at time of sale . After sale I was informed delivery time to be confirmed. Nearly every day since purchase item has been advertised as in stock by Amazon eu . After contacting Amazon I was informed that the item was not in stock and also told that (in stock ) does not mean the item is in stock . Hear is what happened on 11/8/23 , the item said 13 in stock and while speaking the phone a Amazon advisor was able to tell me that there was now only 12 available while we were speaking, I asked the advisor could I not have one of the 12 and was told that is not how it works (lol) . So I pay for the item and Amazon won't deliver it but won't deliver it when it is clearly in stock and can't provide a delivery date . So if you see a item you like and is in stock, understand that the term (in stock ) written on a advertisement on Amazon platform does not actually mean (in stock) and what it does mean is very unclear.",2023-09-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,11.0,1019,209,37,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,purchase item th aug item sold amazon eu advertised stock time sale sale informed delivery time confirmed nearly every day since purchase item advertised stock amazon eu contacting amazon informed item stock also told stock mean item stock hear happened item said stock speaking phone amazon advisor able tell available speaking asked advisor could one told work lol pay item amazon wont deliver wont deliver clearly stock cant provide delivery date see item like stock understand term stock written advertisement amazon platform actually mean stock mean unclear,0.027056845659313378,0.9729431543406866,0.11721817162086372,0.2,0.809915211494516,80.9915211494516,High Trust
O O,/users/64cad44db14e590011960e40,US,6.0,2023-09-11 19:49:06+00:00,1.0,AMAZON FRAUD!!!!!!!!!!!,"my credit card company says amazon is claiming not to have received return of goods although I have considerable proof to the contrary from Amazon's website(1) emails from amazon employees stating that Amazon has received items(2) more than 15 screen shots showing progress of returns including: tracking of return, carrier scan of goods, Amazon scan and receipt of return. Amazon 'refund issued"" is shown on website, although the actual monies were never returned to me.(3) My credit card claims, on recorded lines, that Amazon says that the item was not returned.  This is false.  I provided (1) emails from Amazon employees stating that they had received the returned item, (2) provided tracking proving receipt of goods from vendor (3) showed screenshots from the vendor website showing carrier scan, vendor scan of goods received, and vendor ""refund issued"".(4) Amazon has alternately listed the refund (screenshots on different dates) as the amount of tax $31.16, (which is the amount of the tax for the item) and refund due $359.16 (combined amount of the subtotal and tax).  There is no explanation of why Amazon only issued the amount of tax to Capital One, but the fact that they did substantiates the fact that they received the item as a return.  I have screenshots which I sent to credit card company showing that the ""return has been issued"" for both 31.16 and 359.16 (which makes no sense), and this is listed as August 28, which is the same date as what is listed on the email from the employee.  It is now September 11, and I still don't have a refund for goods returned July 25.(5) Amazon refunded my card $31.16 which is just the amount of tax, which substantiates that the item was returned but doesn't explain why I was not refunded the subtotal of the returned item.  This is Fraud. I have reached out more than a dozens of times via recorded calls and emails, I have gotten nothing but robotic answers and form letter responses. I have spent untold hours on this. I sent over 15 screenshots to Capital One and returned the paperwork via mail that they requested.  I have spent literally hours on the phone with Amazon and Capital One and sent dozens of emails to both.  Capital One sent me a link which I sent back (ending 7849) On September 7, on a recorded line, the Capital One agent told me that the link they sent me would not suffice, and I would have to re-send all of the information.  This is egregious that I have to spend 15-20 hours to get a refund that is proven with screenshots, emails and has theoretically been credited because the vendor credited the tax and is in error with the amount.  This is FRAUD!",2023-09-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,11.0,2644,463,23,2,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,credit card company say amazon claiming received return good although considerable proof contrary amazon website email amazon employee stating amazon received item screen shot showing progress return including tracking return carrier scan good amazon scan receipt return amazon refund issued shown website although actual monies never returned credit card claim recorded line amazon say item returned false provided email amazon employee stating received returned item provided tracking proving receipt good vendor showed screenshots vendor website showing carrier scan vendor scan good received vendor refund issued amazon alternately listed refund screenshots different date amount tax amount tax item refund due combined amount subtotal tax explanation amazon issued amount tax capital one fact substantiates fact received item return screenshots sent credit card company showing return issued make sense listed august date listed email employee september still dont refund good returned july amazon refunded card amount tax substantiates item returned doesnt explain refunded subtotal returned item fraud reached dozen time via recorded call email gotten nothing robotic answer form letter response spent untold hour sent screenshots capital one returned paperwork via mail requested spent literally hour phone amazon capital one sent dozen email capital one sent link sent back ending september recorded line capital one agent told link sent would suffice would resend information egregious spend hour get refund proven screenshots email theoretically credited vendor credited tax error amount fraud,0.04923700783805001,0.95076299216195,0.2596747055524397,0.2,0.827316437191463,82.73164371914629,High Trust
