katt reed,/users/64ff41e0599be50011a091a2,US,1.0,2023-09-11 18:35:53+00:00,1.0,Amazon Customer Service Lacking Big Time!!,"An item I ordered was destroyed in transit and USPS returned item to Amazon.  According to their webpage, it stated that a credit would be issued.  9 days later, still no credit.  Contacted Amazon Customer Service via text and the disaster started.  First, the person couldn't understand why I was requesting a refund (remember damaged in transit and returned to Amazon by USPS).  Then would NOT REFUND the tax amount assessed to the product.  He could not understand why I was requesting that either.  I tried to explain all items are assessed tax and that is also part of the refund.  He refused.  I then asked to speak to a Supervisor and he responded to me ""he's going to say the something so why bother!!""  Is this a new policy?  Amazon DOES NOT REFUND SALES TAX on return items??  I am thoroughly disgusted as this guy was rude and unwilling to get a supervisor involved.  I was refunded the price of the product that's all which is 100% wrong!!",2023-09-08 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,11.0,951,169,42,6,3.0,0,4,1,0,Genuine,item ordered destroyed transit usps returned item amazon according webpage stated credit would issued day later still credit contacted amazon customer service via text disaster started first person couldnt understand requesting refund remember damaged transit returned amazon usps would refund tax amount assessed product could understand requesting either tried explain item assessed tax also part refund refused asked speak supervisor responded he going say something bother new policy amazon refund sale tax return item thoroughly disgusted guy rude unwilling get supervisor involved refunded price product thats wrong,0.6254565035671982,0.3745434964328018,0.09478407178911946,0.2,0.5062285625742248,50.62285625742248,Medium Trust
