Stuart Cheeseman,/users/64feb87f45a83e0012c50be5,NZ,1.0,2023-09-11 08:49:53+00:00,1.0,When things go wrong it’s a nightmare!,"With Amazon USA as long as nothing goes wrong with your order everything is fine. However, the test is always how a company performs when things go wrong, sadly with Amazon this is where they need a substantial improvement.of recent times I have had numerous orders go missing or damaged in transit.In the latest example I received a notice that the item was ‘undeliverable’. The message advised that a refund would follow in 5 days (or sooner).Well after the 5 days I used the Amazon chat to enquire why the item was undeliverable. The chat response was that the item had been damaged in transit and had been returned to Amazon. A refund was promised.10 days later with no sign of a refund I enquired again using chat. This time I was told I had to wait 2 more days before I could ask for a refund as the delivery time had not expired. What on earth? No point trying to talk reason with the person on their chat. It’s already been well over 5 days and, anyway, why make me wait longer when they have already confirmed the item was returned to them.",2023-09-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,11.0,1049,194,38,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon usa long nothing go wrong order everything fine however test always company performs thing go wrong sadly amazon need substantial improvementof recent time numerous order go missing damaged transitin latest example received notice item ‘undeliverable’ message advised refund would follow day soonerwell day used amazon chat enquire item undeliverable chat response item damaged transit returned amazon refund promised day later sign refund enquired using chat time told wait day could ask refund delivery time expired earth point trying talk reason person chat it’s already well day anyway make wait longer already confirmed item returned,0.0030153881985672906,0.9969846118014327,0.10880538418395962,0.2,0.8202533827375083,82.02533827375082