Carol Olson,/users/64fc56ba5bd27400120d76dc,US,1.0,2023-09-09 13:28:10+00:00,1.0,"Why give me shipping options, when you can't deliver?","This review has nothing to do with products bought they were fine and intact. This is a shipping review.Not the first time I was told my package would be at my home at a certain time, and IT WAS NOT. Then in an email sent to me says, if I would like to cancel my order for a refund I could, but there is no where in the message sent to do that. Package was to arrive between 7AM and 10AM. The package arrived at 7:00 PM. Why give the options? Why not just say it will arrive on this day by end of day? They give you 3 options to choose from and can't deliver on their options. I like Amazon and I can almost always find what I am looking for and get it in a few days of ordering. But the thing that bugs me the most is when you say it's going to deliver by a certain time and or day, and you do not. I pay for prime every month and I don't get prime shipping. Because you don't hold up your end of the options bargain.",2023-09-08 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,9.0,9.0,918,192,53,9,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,review nothing product bought fine intact shipping reviewnot first time told package would home certain time email sent say would like cancel order refund could message sent package arrive package arrived pm give option say arrive day end day give option choose cant deliver option like amazon almost always find looking get day ordering thing bug say going deliver certain time day pay prime every month dont get prime shipping dont hold end option bargain,0.007882978575988343,0.9921170214240117,0.1076836791923724,0.2,0.8175952465504803,81.75952465504804,High Trust
