js,/users/64f22ff9471b15001172e24b,US,1.0,2023-09-01 20:40:07+00:00,1.0,amazon prime video,"amazon prime video: two separate problems--1) extremely horrible customer service and the deliberate intention to make it difficult to even get through to them. the online chat bot takes you in circles. it's difficult to get a live chat agent. if you do, they can't understand your issue or solve the problem. if you call, the auto-prompt bot is just infuriatingly awful, doesn't even acknowledge the number prompts entered then terminates the call by stating the call is being ended because there was no response entered. last month, when i finally got a call through to a live agent, we were on the phone an hour, and the problem was not resolved, so the same problem came up again this month. on the last issue i called about, the customer-service agent was so rude and disrespectful, i just gave up on the call.2) called two months in a row about same problem regarding prime-subscription-included content (free, no-additional-charge content) downloaded to my ipad suddenly requiring payment. example: downloaded a season to watch at later time offline. was watching the series offline (wifi off), but had to run an errand, tried to resume a bit later. the series i had been watching just an hour earlier, but had to pause, suddenly is blocked from further viewing unless paid for. right in the middle of an episode, but now no longer free, payment is required. they were already downloaded and being viewed. in one case, i was on the next-to-last episode, so couldn't find out the ending without paying for the whole season i'd almost completed. the only thing that had changed was i was watching the downloads offline (wifi off), then tried to continue watching at a neighbors house with wifi on. think it's a technical issue but the customer-service rep would not even let me state the problem, kept cutting me off and overtalking me. they don't really know anything other than reading from a script, 