Shannon,/users/60240339b2252d001ad58216,US,2.0,2023-08-28 04:08:58+00:00,1.0,"Amazon support is the worst, and THAT is a FACT!","Amazon support is the worst. I got a defective item and it stopped working just days after the return window. The seller said they would send a replacement and to have amazon support help me with getting the shipping handled since their products are in amazons warehouse. The agents refused to listen or help and just copy and paste the same responses. They refuse to help and then lie to customers. One amazon agent told me that sellers have sent replacements to customers in the past, so that meant for a FACT that this seller also has a personal warehouse. Literally said it was a fact, but then when I asked if that seller for a fact has a warehouse because the agent knew of some sellers having their own warehouses? the agent refused to respond and just kept changing the subject. I asked the agent how they could know for a fact that the agent had a warehouse? Refused to answer. So I asked if they lied about knowing for a fact that the Seller had a warehouse, and the agent said that they could not confirm or deny that.... Wow amazon. Went from stellar support to almost one star reviews on trust pilot... Not to mention stores like costco (their membership costs less than amazons even) offers 90 day returns. Walmart, with NO membership offers 90 day returns as well and I have never had issues with their support either. You spend days trying to get help and get no resolutions. With all the money amazon generates, put some money BACK into customer service, and stop outsourcing the work to people who could not give less of a damn about the customers or their experience.",2023-08-27 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,28.0,1586,287,48,10,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon support worst got defective item stopped working day return window seller said would send replacement amazon support help getting shipping handled since product amazon warehouse agent refused listen 