Tim,/users/5b95de554de5666d349543bd,US,6.0,2023-08-24 14:58:12+00:00,1.0,You did it for you.,"They claimed they charged their Amazon Store Card that charges 29.99% FOR ME when my favorite 2.5% rewards credit card had been swapped by my bank and they changed the expiration from 05/25 to 06/25 causing bank to decline the purchase because of the data error. They did this for AMAZON. I did not want this. That's quite an ego Amazon to do something that makes me mad and claim you did it for me. DON'T TRUST THEM WITH A 2ND BUYING SOURCE. They will use it when you don't want them too and claim they did it for you. As if they couldn't have sent me an email saying the purchase was declined and I couldn't have fixed it 30 seconds after they had let me know what happened. Or as if the purchase arriving a day, a week, or a month later because clearing the card transaction was delayed was a problem for me. Not everyone is an addict in need of their shopping fix. No Amazon, you did it for you. Now you don't have me ever sharing a second funding source with you ever again.They should do a study of their data of customers that has a second funding source and no longer do. Then look to see what was the impulse for the customer removing the 2nd funding source. Charging a 2nd funding source should be a feature that can be turned on or off. Even if it was on by default, I should have the option to turn it off and not play such a stupid game. But I guess the customer is less important to them than the purchases we make.",2023-08-22 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,24.0,1429,278,19,5,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,claimed charged amazon store card charge favorite reward credit card swapped bank changed expiration causing bank decline purchase data error amazon want thats quite ego amazon something make mad claim dont trust nd buying source use dont want claim couldnt sent email saying purchase declined couldnt fixed second let know happened purchase arriving day week month later clearing card transaction d