Melissa De Clercq,/users/5a0c6dfc0000ff000ae2e751,US,4.0,2023-08-16 02:33:38+00:00,1.0,HORRIBLE CUSTOMER SERVICE,"Oh, my Goodness! Outsourced customer service! Hard to understand the rep. They always seem to be half asleep. Ask a specific question, they just repeat themselves over and over. No concern for customer’s issues. Try returning something. You either have to take time out of your busy day, to drop off at a UPS store, OR pay $7.99 for UPS to pick up the package from your home. Bull ….! You should NEVER have to pay ANYTHING to return a defective product! Fight enough like I did today, and last time I had this issue, and the outsourced rep will “comp” you the return fee, which you should never even been asked to pay in the first place! Horrible!",2023-08-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,16.0,647,119,25,3,1.0,0,6,2,1,Suspicious,oh goodness outsourced customer service hard understand rep always seem half asleep ask specific question repeat concern customer’s issue try returning something either take time busy day drop ups store pay ups pick package home bull … never pay anything return defective product fight enough like today last time issue outsourced rep “comp” return fee never even asked pay first place horrible,0.9951685371796973,0.004831462820302668,0.06674144699943915,0.2,0.3157640208100392,31.57640208100392,Low Trust
Joe Rogers,/users/5a1ca1000000ff000ae87e05,US,2.0,2023-08-16 01:53:11+00:00,1.0,Amazon no longer gives a damn,"Ultimately, Amazon has gone down hill as a business over the last couple of years. Whether it be silly mistakes like I'm ordering wood, smoking pellets and receive dog food and I don't have a dog; or most recently my wife orders some headphones doesn't like the fit, returns them and they proceed to tell us that we returned the wrong item. So they got rid of the item they received and are not going to refund us. Spent 2 days trying to work on that problem only to be brushed off and basically told they don't care or pass the buck to some other department that turns around and passes it to somebody else. $150 problem could have been fixed and a long loyal customer could have been kept. Now they're going to lose a heck of a lot more than $150 with my business going elsewhere on top of the fact that I'm going to bad mouth them as much as I possibly can and tell my story to everyone that will listen. Only further causing them lost revenue in the long run. Great business model Amazon, keep it up.  From here on in I'll just find other alternatives. Whether it's ordering direct or through Walmart or Target or going in person for a change.",2023-08-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,16.0,1147,217,29,6,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ultimately amazon gone hill business last couple year whether silly mistake like im ordering wood smoking pellet receive dog food dont dog recently wife order headphone doesnt like fit return proceed tell u returned wrong item got rid item received going refund u spent day trying work problem brushed basically told dont care pas buck department turn around pass somebody else problem could fixed long loyal customer could kept theyre going lose heck lot business going elsewhere top fact im going bad mouth much possibly tell story everyone listen causing lost revenue long run great business model amazon keep ill find alternative whether ordering direct walmart target going person change,0.011623336704412793,0.9883766632955872,0.12170499158721257,0.2,0.8185293299652361,81.8529329965236,High Trust
