Tee,/users/64d5b302227c1e0012892f75,US,1.0,2023-08-11 06:03:41+00:00,1.0,"Just got off the phone with ""Customer…","Just got off the phone with ""Customer Service"" regarding a change to an order I placed in July and still have not received. Checked the order status and noticed that not only had the brand of product I ordered been changed, but had been replaced by a brand I've never heard of at 4X the price of the one I ordered. I am absolutely sure it isn't what I ordered, as I have checked it's status repeatedly since then. The product name, picture, and price are different than what has been there EVERY OTHER TIME I've checked. Their response? ""We will give you a refund, send it back when you get it."" I said ty but I'm a little more concerned with being billed and shipped things that are not what I ordered. ""I'll pass it along to my supervisor."" Really? Ok, so I explained my concern with the 'report to my supervisor' not really addressing the issue I have, which is how exactly did this happen?? They respond with some mumbo jumbo about the seller changing it and that they will do this and that....hello? I ordered it thru AMAZON, I expect AMAZON to handle ANYONE or ANYTHING even attempting to change my order WITHOUT consent. I have been a frequent and long time customer of Amazon. Until now, I've had no issues whatsoever. This however is a deal breaker. I just ordered expensive pc parts yesterday. Are they now gonna be swapped to top of the line $10k parts I don't need and can't afford??? Intolerable. No help whatsoever beyond the BS i got from CS. I'm aware I can get a refund, THAT IS NOT THE ISSUE I contacted them about, and I clearly outlined the issue I had with their supposed 'resolution' but they just refused to address the fact that MY ORDER WAS NOT MY ORDER AND I'M PAYING FOR IT. When I filled out a customer service complaint review, they emailed me that they refused to post it, so here I am.",2023-08-10 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,11.0,1816,338,38,7,1.0,