Kb,/users/64a6b59778beea00116ad97d,US,4.0,2023-08-10 23:54:00+00:00,1.0,terrible experience with Amazon,"I had a terrible experience with Amazon. I returned a product that didn't meet my expectations and chose the free UPS pickup option. However, UPS didn't show up on the scheduled day; they arrived two days later and mistakenly took the wrong package from my front yard. They didn't even attempt to notify me by knocking or ringing the bell. I only found out about it through a notification on the app while I was at work. I immediately contacted customer care, and they assured me they would retrieve my package from UPS. It's been 10 days now, and they're saying it's difficult to resolve the issue. They even mentioned the option of legal action, but cautioned against expecting a positive outcome. This situation contradicts Amazon's customer obsession principle. No one is taking responsibility for their mistake. It's disappointing to see Amazon not living up to their claims. The customer service representatives keep ending calls without a solution, and there seems to be no clarity on how to escalate the matter. The tracking number shows that the package is in Amazon warehouse.",2023-07-23 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,10.0,1086,182,31,4,18.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,terrible experience amazon returned product didnt meet expectation chose free ups pickup option however ups didnt show scheduled day arrived two day later mistakenly took wrong package front yard didnt even attempt notify knocking ringing bell found notification app work immediately contacted customer care assured would retrieve package ups day theyre saying difficult resolve issue even mentioned option legal action cautioned expecting positive outcome situation contradicts amazon customer obsession principle one taking responsibility mistake disappointing see amazon living claim customer service representative keep ending call without solution seems clarity escalate matter tracking number show package amazon warehouse,0