Jonas,/users/64d403e2e93bdd00124d5172,US,1.0,2023-08-09 23:24:03+00:00,1.0,Prime not what it claims to be/very difficult to cancel,"I recently tried out Amazon Prime for a free trial, but I was disappointed with the experience. The free shipping was the only real benefit for me, and I often had to wait a week or more for items to arrive. On average it was at least two to three weeks and I  never once received same-day or next-day delivery.The cancellation process was also incredibly frustrating. I had to go through multiple options to find the option to cancel, and I was asked about a dozen times if I was sure I wanted to do it. At times, the cancel option received no response. I had to click cancel about six time before the website would accept my cancel option.Even after I finally canceled, I was still reminded several times that I was about to lose my membership and to continue to the cancellation process. I understand that Amazon was recently sued by the FTC in June 2023 for making it difficult for users to cancel their Prime memberships. The FTC alleged that Amazon used ""dark patterns"" to trick consumers into staying subscribed.As a result of this experience, I cannot recommend Amazon Prime. In summary, Amazon Prime is not worth the hassle. The free shipping is the only real benefit, and the cancellation process is incredibly frustrating. I would recommend looking for a different online retailer with free shipping if you're not interested in the other Prime perks.",2023-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,9.0,1361,238,55,10,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently tried amazon prime free trial disappointed experience free shipping real benefit often wait week item arrive average least two three week never received sameday nextday deliverythe cancellation process also incredibly frustrating go multiple option find option cancel asked dozen time sure wanted time cancel option received response click cancel six time website would accept cancel optioneven finally canceled still reminded several time lose membership continue cancellation process understand amazon recently sued ftc june making difficult user cancel prime membership ftc alleged amazon used dark pattern trick consumer staying subscribedas result experience cannot recommend amazon prime summary amazon prime worth hassle free shipping real benefit cancellation process incredibly frustrating would recommend looking different online retailer free shipping youre interested prime perk,0.014342324258992603,0.9856576757410074,0.1334828939988783,0.2,0.8195254166702794,81.95254166702794,High Trust
