camille curinga,/users/602c43e2109f75001ae19b87,US,5.0,2023-08-09 16:30:43+00:00,1.0,Amazon is running a re-charge scam,"Amazon is running a re-charge scam. You return an item via ups and they issue you a credit. A month later they recharge your card saying that you did not ship it back.I contacted Amazon support and this is there response;“I have checked the details and I am really sorry to inform you that as the return info was not updated that is why you were charged for the item. But no worries, I have updated the info and initiated a full refund for the item and it will be credited within 3-5 business days.”Now if you are not one to regularly check your email you might not catch these emails.Now you think this is a handled matter. But it’s NOT!!5 months later they RE-CHARGE your card AGAIN!!!They send the same response!!I can only assume their game is to bean count how many millions of consumers don’t CATCH IT!!To date this has happened 18 times to my account!!!",2023-08-08 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,8.0,9.0,860,158,34,6,1.0,0,12,2,1,Suspicious,amazon running recharge scam return item via ups issue credit month later recharge card saying ship backi contacted amazon support response“i checked detail really sorry inform return info updated charged item worry updated info initiated full refund item credited within business days”now one regularly check email might catch emailsnow think handled matter it’s month later recharge card againthey send responsei assume game bean count many million consumer don’t catch itto date happened time account,0.9999988871570883,1.11284291171021e-06,0.0886146943353898,0.2,0.31772349528853383,31.772349528853383,Low Trust
