Rick,/users/5d29df2579b4f523bc0f23c9,US,3.0,2023-07-30 06:36:55+00:00,1.0,Don’t buy valuable items from Amazon,"I ordered this printer 4 days ago with a 2 days delivery from Amazon at a good price (-21% + 50$ added discount). I am a loyal prime customer since 8 years, at least, with a lot of purchases.TBA307871694897As I was supposed to provide the 1-time pin code to the driver for delivery of this amazing printer, and the tracking was showing delivery between 2pm and 4pm initially,  I had organized my day to stay home.At 4pm , I was ""next stop"" on the map and the driver was 2 blocks away from my house. At 4.30pm, not seeing anybody, I checked again, the driver was still at the same place and the delivery moved to 7pm, while he was still 2 blocks away….At 5.30pm, I see now the driver is in Simi Valley, CA  at an Amazon center location, 30 miles away from my house. I phone the customer service, who literally just says what I can read on my screen…. So not useful at all.The day after I go to this center in Simi Valley, CA where they tell me to go complain in Chatsworth, CA as they cannot help locally. Well ….the driver obviously stopped here and had the printer loaded in the van there. So why cannot they help ? Being now in Chatsworth , we check, and printer is tagged as ""missing"" in the system. We phone together Amazon customer service over the phone, same thing again, not useful at all, we are even told it is not missing and it will be delivered this same day for sure.Now today saturday 07/29/23, same status as 3 days ago. The information are not even updated on the tracking. I phone the customer service where I am being told to wait until the 11th of august (in 15 days) to ask for a solution if I have not been delivered in the meantime. After saying I didn’t agree , I did ask to speak to a supervisor, who finally told me literally "" I cannot do anything else and I will hang up"", that he did while I was continuing speaking.I phoned again 2 hours ago , after having selected ""cancel this delivery"" , and spoke to another lady to whom I explained the whole story. This lady, this time, was courteous but told me she cannot tell me anything about this sad situation and will escalate the issue….and I cannot even order another 1 at the same price that I ordered !Now if I check the delivery status, informations have magically changed :  I can read that I refused the delivery because the order was canceled before. What ??!!? So now Amazon is changing the story line ?To summarize , basically my printer was loaded in the van, the driver stopped 2 blocks away for a while and for any reason it did last, then he decides not to deliver me and goes back to the Amazon center 30 miles away. The van stays overnight and suddenly the printer is missing, but in the end it is me refusing delivery because the order was canceled !?!?Something is definitely wrong but it is being cover-up obviously. Leaving aside the fact I was hang-up by an Amazon associate representing the management, and all other associates telling me what I could read !As it is not an isolated case, aside from huge money losses (and in this case how is it handled with Epson…),  it says a lot about the ""Customer experience"" or ""Customer centricity""  mindset being practiced at Amazon:- customer being held hostage if the ordered item has suddenly disappeared- customer being hung-up if not satisfied- customer unsatisfied left unsatisfied- customer is not a priority, Amazon decides to hang-up as they don’t have any solution, and decides that you have to wait the period of time they decide- customer is being handled by low cost countries personal , just repeating what they learned and not customizing their answer to your own concern. In the end the service is more expensive, being paid for…..nothing except providing informations you already have on your screenObviously, Amazon is not set to handle expensive orders/ items that can suddenly disappear, and for which you can be held hostage for a while. I know now that I will prioritize Amazon for cheap items but not for pricier ones where I will go in a store, or order straight from more serious companies (bestbuy….).It was not like this in the past, so Amazon has taken definitely a wrong turn, probably being the result of short-term cash only oriented decisions. But this is another story….",2023-07-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,30.0,4243,769,36,6,2.0,0,6,1,0,Genuine,ordered printer day ago day delivery amazon good price added discount loyal prime customer since year least lot purchasestbaas supposed provide time pin code driver delivery amazing printer tracking showing delivery pm pm initially organized day stay homeat pm next stop map driver block away house pm seeing anybody checked driver still place delivery moved pm still block away…at pm see driver simi valley ca amazon center location mile away house phone customer service literally say read screen… useful allthe day go center simi valley ca tell go complain chatsworth ca cannot help locally well …the driver obviously stopped printer loaded van cannot help chatsworth check printer tagged missing system phone together amazon customer service phone thing useful even told missing delivered day surenow today saturday status day ago information even updated tracking phone customer service told wait th august day ask solution delivered meantime saying didn’t agree ask speak supervisor finally told literally cannot anything else hang continuing speakingi phoned hour ago selected cancel delivery spoke another lady explained whole story lady time courteous told cannot tell anything sad situation escalate issue…and cannot even order another price ordered check delivery status information magically changed read refused delivery order canceled amazon changing story line summarize basically printer loaded van driver stopped block away reason last decides deliver go back amazon center mile away van stay overnight suddenly printer missing end refusing delivery order canceled something definitely wrong coverup obviously leaving aside fact hangup amazon associate representing management associate telling could read isolated case aside huge money loss case handled epson… say lot customer experience customer centricity mindset practiced amazon customer held hostage ordered item suddenly disappeared customer hungup satisfied customer unsatisfied left unsatisfied customer priority amazon decides hangup don’t solution decides wait period time decide customer handled low cost country personal repeating learned customizing answer concern end service expensive paid for…nothing except providing information already screenobviously amazon set handle expensive order item suddenly disappear held hostage know prioritize amazon cheap item pricier one go store order straight serious company bestbuy…it like past amazon taken definitely wrong turn probably result shortterm cash oriented decision another story…,0.9777105370343404,0.02228946296565959,0.43129556926528323,0.2,0.39740384533588646,39.740384533588646,Low Trust
Joanne “Josie Girl Productions,/users/64c5a41f600fdb00126196d1,US,1.0,2023-07-30 01:43:42+00:00,1.0,Awful service,"Awful service. Colin, my agent was very nice but couldn’t do anything to help me. Not one supervisor lucked up. Two weeks plus to receive a script. Insane! Quitting today. Good riddance!",2023-07-29 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,30.0,186,32,13,2,1.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,awful service colin agent nice couldn’t anything help one supervisor lucked two week plus receive script insane quitting today good riddance,0.7107623189442714,0.28923768105572856,0.0179472798653954,0.2,0.44820829650094335,44.82082965009433,Low Trust
Evange Who,/users/5ee1820b63833f448d088f31,US,6.0,2023-07-30 04:07:34+00:00,1.0,"Don't use them, beware of so called easy returns...","The ironic thing is that despite (especially on this site) the number of negative reviews, this site will still sell a lot of stuff, making the jerk, greedy, selfish Bezos, VERY rich.  Important thing to add on, under federal law the FTC says that if you receive a wrong package, you are entitled to keep it WiTHOUT having to pay for it, that is why they kept wanting me to send the pic,  If they sent you the wrong package I suggest EVERYONE make it as difficult as possible for them in not sending the package back and disputing the charge. I was THREATENED that if I sent it back without the photo first, the package might get ""lost"" and I wouldn't get a refund.I had ordered an Ipad Air and wanted it in Silver, and by accident ordered the color Slate Gray and when it came realized it was wrong color.  Called cus. serv. was told it had to be shipped back and not brought in, thought that agent was processing refund, but didn't called to get shipping info and the very, VERY nice CSA, (shall be called nameless for a reason) offered to send it back and when I tried to tell her what to write (that I got the wrong color, she told me not to say anything and now I know why.)  A few days later, my second order arrived, correctly ordered and the color was STILL wrong, starlight, instead of silver.  I wanted to  reorder again but this time I wanted to ask the sellers first  if they had the correct color, but on Amazon you have to use a chat bot and I didn't know how long it would take to get a reply, called them  to see if they could call sellers. Due to complications with the website, had to talk to a supervisor and for some reason, before they accept the return I would have to take a photo as proof, which I NEVER had to do and determine whether I could get a refund. I never had to go through that before EVER, and everyone I talk to doesn't want to explain why and just quickly hangs up. They must be getting a lot of negative feedback on this. After the initial conversation, I quickly started an online return WHERE item was accepted and should have just sent it back, but I foolishly called to ask why I needed to send photo when you don't have to send if you return it with online processing and was threatened that if I didn't send a photo first, they may refuse it at the warehouse and if it gets lost, I won't get my money back.  I don't know if they legally can do that, and even those it's a hassle I will send the photo, but I don't like the idea that they have to ""approve"" the return and the logic behind that if I didn't call in to ask what I wanted to originally ask, none of this would have happened, no need to send photos and no one I know has ever been asked to send photos. I read somewhere that I should not have said wrong item but item not as described (wrong color) and maybe that would have made a difference, but they wouldn't change it, I know now why the nice CSA told me not to give a reason which is why I won't name her, BE WARNED-if you don't want hassle don't buy in first place, but if you do return, do ONLINE only.The naughty part of me says take a photo of bricks that you got instead of a computer, who's to say that you didn't get it, you got the proof.",2023-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,30.0,3207,627,51,9,5.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ironic thing despite especially site number negative review site still sell lot stuff making jerk greedy selfish bezos rich important thing add federal law ftc say receive wrong package entitled keep without pay kept wanting send pic sent wrong package suggest everyone make difficult possible sending package back disputing charge threatened sent back without photo first package might get lost wouldnt get refundi ordered ipad air wanted silver accident ordered color slate gray came realized wrong color called cu serv told shipped back brought thought agent processing refund didnt called get shipping info nice csa shall called nameless reason offered send back tried tell write got wrong color told say anything know day later second order arrived correctly ordered color still wrong starlight instead silver wanted reorder time wanted ask seller first correct color amazon use chat bot didnt know long would take get reply called see could call seller due complication website talk supervisor reason accept return would take photo proof never determine whether could get refund never go ever everyone talk doesnt want explain quickly hang must getting lot negative feedback initial conversation quickly started online return item accepted sent back foolishly called ask needed send photo dont send return online processing threatened didnt send photo first may refuse warehouse get lost wont get money back dont know legally even hassle send photo dont like idea approve return logic behind didnt call ask wanted originally ask none would happened need send photo one know ever asked send photo read somewhere said wrong item item described wrong color maybe would made difference wouldnt change know nice csa told give reason wont name warnedif dont want hassle dont buy first place return online onlythe naughty part say take photo brick got instead computer who say didnt get got proof,0.007511417431525222,0.9924885825684748,0.35165451486259114,0.2,0.8665751942567556,86.65751942567556,High Trust
