Kirk McFarland III,/users/64c2c338e9782d0012f311d0,US,1.0,2023-07-27 21:19:32+00:00,1.0,"Delivery issue, customer service problems","I recently ordered a few items from Amazon.com.   The order was placed on Monday and was to be delivered by 8pm on Tuesday.  About that time I tracked the package to see where it was.  Amazon's tracking function indicated that the package was out for delivery and the visual graphic showed it to be very close to being delivered.   Checking again about 30 minutes later, the tracker indicated that the package was on its way but running late.  The next check informed me that the expected delivery date was as late as Saturday.  I was quite puzzled by this.  How could a package that seemed to be virtually on my door step suddenly be up to four days away?  I waited to see if the package would arrive the next day (Wednesday) before trying to contact Amazon.com.  It did not, so once again I tracked it.  This time, the package was was apparently not even out for delivery. Perplexed and frustrated,  I tried various avenues to contact Amazon.com to inquire about what had happened.   I finally got ahold of a person in customer service and explained the situation to him.  I gave him the information he needed and he said he'd check into it and be right back.  The call was terminated about 3 minutes later.  I never got a return call.As of 11:30am Thursday, the package is still not out for delivery. This has been a frustrating and disappointing experience.   I have been somewhat of an Amazon junkie for several years now.   I tell my coworkers, ""If you can't find it on Amazon,  it doesn't exist."".  I've experienced prompt deliveries most of the time. A few late ones now and again, but this one is strange.   I have been happy with with the majority of products I have received  and have had no problems returning any items.My experience with customer service in the present situation has been very frustrating trying to get past the Inflexible, canned and recorded  messages to speak to,  or chat with, a real person.  It would be a major improvement if some of the automation were removed and direct access to real people was possible.",2023-07-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,27.0,2045,360,41,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently ordered item amazoncom order placed monday delivered pm tuesday time tracked package see amazon tracking function indicated package delivery visual graphic showed close delivered checking minute later tracker indicated package way running late next check informed expected delivery date late saturday quite puzzled could package seemed virtually door step suddenly four day away waited see package would arrive next day wednesday trying contact amazoncom tracked time package apparently even delivery perplexed frustrated tried various avenue contact amazoncom inquire happened finally got ahold person customer service explained situation gave information needed said hed check right back call terminated minute later never got return calla thursday package still delivery frustrating disappointing experience somewhat amazon junkie several year tell coworkers cant find amazon doesnt exist ive experienced prompt delivery time late one one strange happy majority product received problem returning itemsmy experience customer service present situation frustrating trying get past inflexible canned recorded message speak chat real person would major improvement automation removed direct access real people possible,0.006251912987666637,0.9937480870123334,0.20190689848569826,0.2,0.8372554232033064,83.72554232033063,High Trust
Notarized translation,/users/5ff61258f5568e001bce0c02,GE,25.0,2023-07-27 21:01:14+00:00,3.0,Support service is just terrible and buyer is hardly ever protected,"Prices are very high, buyers are hardly ever protected, especially international customers using freight company address for shipping-just like me. Amazon allows drop shipper sellers who are not aware what they are dispatching. If your item is not as described you are experiencing monetary loss. Regarding customer service: it used to be very good back in the years but now most of them are sleepy and I even have a feeling that they did not understand English and they are using some online dictionary to see what you wrote, frequently they provide with irrelevant answers. Not all of them but most do. Amazon VS eBay-better buy on eBay, eBay has unbeatable prices at least.",2023-07-22 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,27.0,676,114,67,11,5.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,price high buyer hardly ever protected especially international customer using freight company address shippingjust like amazon allows drop shipper seller aware dispatching item described experiencing monetary loss regarding customer service used good back year sleepy even feeling understand english using online dictionary see wrote frequently provide irrelevant answer amazon v ebaybetter buy ebay ebay unbeatable price least,0.016767476817453466,0.9832325231825465,0.06393718452047112,0.6,1.4044036984953672,140.44036984953672,High Trust
