Stephen Powell,/users/64bf808c0d13ea001242315f,US,1.0,2023-07-25 09:58:18+00:00,1.0,Amazon Refuses To Honor Their Prime Member Agreement,"Amazon advertizes “Building a better future”. How, by cheating and lying to your customers? Its funny how my daughter can get an order to her house in two days and I live 50 miles from her and if I order the exact same thing it takes over a week to get to me and I am a prime member. The thing is I complained to customer service and when I was getting my orders in two days they suddenly went to taking a week. Amazon has no problems still charging me for my membership even though they refuse to fulfill their end of the agreement. That is nothing more than stealing. Amazon has joined in with the rest of these big companies and could care less about customer service. So what if a customer stops shopping, they will never notice. I asked customer service which warehouse my order is being shipped from and they said they didn't have that info. Yet last night I had a customer service rep tell me. How could she tell me if they don't have that information. The thing is, the rep that told me last night said I was shipped from the same warehouse as my daughter was. That tells me Amazon has marked my account to be shipped with a big delay in retaliation for me complaining. No other way to explain it considering I use to get my orders in two days and all of a sudden it stopped and add in the fact I am shipped from the same warehouse as my daughter and she can get the exact same order in two days. To hell with these big companies offering all these big discounts only to stop giving them and end up lying to their customers. Over the past 4 weeks I have been told no less than four times they were giving me a promo credit of $10 and was told that again tonight. My thing is when they give this to you it can never be seen by the customer. They say it will just show up on you next order that Amazon sells and ships. ell over the past four weeks I was never given credit from the promo money and when I asked the rep tonight what was my promo balance he said just the $10 he just put in there. That is why Amazon does not let you see the balance because most of the time it is really never given like they told you it would be and if for some reason they do they hope you forget about it and eventually they let it just disappear. Wake up folks, Amazon could care less about their customers. They will do what they have to, say what they have to just to get as much money as they can from you in exchange for as little as they can. I myself am talking to an attorney to see what I can do for Amazon refusing to live up to their end of the Prime agreement.",2023-07-25 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,25.0,2563,510,52,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon advertizes “building better future” cheating lying customer funny daughter get order house two day live mile order exact thing take week get prime member thing complained customer service getting order two day suddenly went taking week amazon problem still charging membership even though refuse fulfill end agreement nothing stealing amazon joined rest big company could care less customer service customer stop shopping never notice asked customer service warehouse order shipped said didnt info yet last night customer service rep tell could tell dont information thing rep told last night said shipped warehouse daughter tell amazon marked account shipped big delay retaliation complaining way explain considering use get order two day sudden stopped add fact shipped warehouse daughter get exact order two day hell big company offering big discount stop giving end lying customer past week told less four time giving promo credit told tonight thing give never seen customer say show next order amazon sell ship ell past four week never given credit promo money asked rep tonight promo balance said put amazon let see balance time really never given like told would reason hope forget eventually let disappear wake folk amazon could care less customer say get much money exchange little talking attorney see amazon refusing live end prime agreement,0.00654153329037712,0.9934584667096229,0.2860347728547392,0.2,0.8539361879257593,85.39361879257594,High Trust
