Annie,/users/64ba90bf22461500111c3752,US,1.0,2023-07-21 16:06:04+00:00,1.0,Amazon suspended my account without explanation,"Amazon locked my account without explanation. All I ever did was purchase some Kindle books using gift cards and my debit card. I lost access to my Kindle library. When I replied to their email and asked them to explain what exactly I did wrong, they said I ""may have provided inaccurate information to Amazon or otherwise used the account in violation of the Amazon conditions of use policy"". But I never did anything like that. And it's obvious that they aren't even sure I did. I'll never buy any digital content from Amazon again.",2023-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,21.0,534,95,47,6,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon locked account without explanation ever purchase kindle book using gift card debit card lost access kindle library replied email asked explain exactly wrong said may provided inaccurate information amazon otherwise used account violation amazon condition use policy never anything like obvious arent even sure ill never buy digital content amazon,0.0054803671350859475,0.9945196328649141,0.0532809871003926,0.2,0.8079160138525355,80.79160138525356,High Trust
Cat,/users/611920be05fd280012a25806,GB,9.0,2023-07-21 15:06:55+00:00,1.0,PLEASE READ - ACCOUNT HACKED,"I just had the most horrible Amazon experience yet. My account was hacked into as I started seeing order confirmation emails arrive in my inbox for flags and pillowcases worth around 500 GBP. In a panic I logged into my account and started deleting orders and deleting my card information. While I was doing this, the scammer entered fake bank details with my name on them and continued to order hoping probably that the ,,invalid payment details"" would prompt me to enter real ones. I successfully managed to change my password which seemed to stop any outside editing. The stores from where these orders were placed had just been created and had long word store names that were obviously fake. So Amazon, you have scammers creating fake shops, hacking into people's accounts and placing orders to their shops worth hundreds of pounds, do you not do any checking whatsoever on these before activating them? I had to fight a sea of bots before actually speaking to human beings, 1 who hung up on me, 2 passed me to other colleagues and another 2 that did not know how to help me. After I told them I was hacked I was told I would be contacted within 24h, after 1h I received a no-reply email stating the account seemed fine. I ended up having to do everything myself and when I tried to close down the account, an error message came up and I was unable to do so. Again I contacted customer service, was passed around from person to person until someone reluctantly said he raised a ticket to close the account and that it should be done within 5-7 days although I did not receive any email confirmation of this so I am again assuming you tell your employees to not help with these requests because you want to force people to stay on your platform and continue shopping. I am now watching my account like a hawk to make sure nothing else happens until it closes down, hopefully. This horrid experience plus constant missing packages for past real orders that were marked by drivers as ,,delivered"", needless to say I will never use you again, I can't wait until the account is closed and I never have to deal with you again.",2023-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,21.0,2124,384,28,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,horrible amazon experience yet account hacked started seeing order confirmation email arrive inbox flag pillowcase worth around gbp panic logged account started deleting order deleting card information scammer entered fake bank detail name continued order hoping probably invalid payment detail would prompt enter real one successfully managed change password seemed stop outside editing store order placed created long word store name obviously fake amazon scammer creating fake shop hacking people account placing order shop worth hundred pound checking whatsoever activating fight sea bot actually speaking human being hung passed colleague another know help told hacked told would contacted within h h received noreply email stating account seemed fine ended everything tried close account error message came unable contacted customer service passed around person person someone reluctantly said raised ticket close account done within day although receive email confirmation assuming tell employee help request want force people stay platform continue shopping watching account like hawk make sure nothing else happens close hopefully horrid experience plus constant missing package past real order marked driver delivered needless say never use cant wait account closed never deal,0.009181482285306073,0.990818517714694,0.2153673583847448,0.2,0.8384827305342959,83.8482730534296,High Trust
