Greater is He,/users/63755ced41e557001110f627,US,3.0,2023-07-21 06:52:21+00:00,1.0,I Absolutely Love Amazon,"I Absolutely Love Amazon! It was the seller that I had the issue with. I purchased and upgraded 132-hole bubble machine gun, and along with my delivery I received a coupon from the seller. It states that if I wrote a 5 star review, take a screenshot of the posted review, and my order ID, and email it to them I would receive a $30 Amazon egift card. I never received it. I wish trustpilot allowed photo uploads because I still have the coupon. Amazon won't allow my review to be posted ""especially with the coupon upload."" I can honestly say: I don't blame them. There would be a massive amount of complaints. Customers would demand Amazon to honor the $30 as a result of that seller's false advertisement, because that’s exactly what I did. Yes, they honored it. This specific merchant is bad business, and it is not a good look for a well-known successful company such as Amazon. I shared this with them as well. And Thank You, Trustpilot for allowing me to share my experience on your site!",2023-03-31 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,21.0,994,181,24,4,112.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,absolutely love amazon seller issue purchased upgraded hole bubble machine gun along delivery received coupon seller state wrote star review take screenshot posted review order id email would receive amazon egift card never received wish trustpilot allowed photo uploads still coupon amazon wont allow review posted especially coupon upload honestly say dont blame would massive amount complaint customer would demand amazon honor result seller false advertisement that’s exactly yes honored specific merchant bad business good look wellknown successful company amazon shared well thank trustpilot allowing share experience site,0.10792826126181754,0.8920717387381825,0.10151430173864273,0.2,0.7663387297168197,76.63387297168197,High Trust
