Mir Arad Navidi,/users/64b1a5d36c3c990012419818,US,1.0,2023-07-14 21:45:29+00:00,1.0,Worst customer service,"The worst part of my experience with Amazon was getting my money back. They kept it for more than six weeks before discovering that the money had actually been paid to another customer.Even after that, I had to phone them repeatedly for hours at a time, and they were never able to fix the issue.Instead than continuing to wait for Amazon to resolve the issue and refund my money, I wish I could just call my bank to request a refund.This $900 transaction remained on my credit card because they were unable to resolve their issue.I hope the management notices this and takes action. This is apparently a common problem on Amazon.com.Unbelievable.",2023-07-13 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,14.0,647,112,22,3,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,worst part experience amazon getting money back kept six week discovering money actually paid another customereven phone repeatedly hour time never able fix issueinstead continuing wait amazon resolve issue refund money wish could call bank request refundthis transaction remained credit card unable resolve issuei hope management notice take action apparently common problem amazoncomunbelievable,0.013732908453990394,0.9862670915460096,0.0628154795288839,0.2,0.8056966416787815,80.56966416787816,High Trust
Anca Nitu,/users/64b1923b39ef6900116f3de7,CA,2.0,2023-07-14 21:44:26+00:00,1.0,Email sent to Amazon.com,"Email sent to Amazon.comTo whom it may concernSince June 8 2023 I have been receiving unwanted packages through Amazon.comThe senders are unknown to meTo my knowledge I don't  even have an Amazon.com account, I do have one with Amazon.caAmazon.com and Amazon.ca potentially share the client databaseInitially the volume of unwanted packages scared me and I have contacted the RCMP ( Canadian police) about itI submitted a few unopened packages to them as evidenceThe RCMP returned the packages to me in a while saying there is not muchthey can do about this harassment but it's safe to open the packages and dispose of themAfter that I opened the packages  some had a return slip inside  and it turns out that they are packages sent through Amazon.comHere are some order ID numbersXxxxxYou could start investigating which account placed these ordersIf you notify the Police they can call the xxxx RCMP quoting file number xxxx to verify the veracity of this statement and ask for information if neededI will certainly not pay for return of any packagesI have called Amazon.com several  about this already: one time I was told it is a glitch which will be fixed, second time I talked with Leo, who explained he can do  nothing but will escalate the problemJeff ,a few days later , tried to gaslight me these are not Amazon ordersThe fourth time I called I was told some supplier is using my name and address to peddle their wares and has my address as a return addressThis seems to be a plausible explanation, I have since reached out to some senders whose ph # I found through an internet search by address and they seem to confirmThey allegedly take 7 business days to provide a response,  meanwhile I keep receiving an average of 4- 5 packages a day, of which I am refusing all I  canAmazon will not cancel the fraudulent account, I don't  have the password or the email address or the phone number for itI strongly advise people to cancel their Amazon.com account since security issues can create a world of problemsI have anxiety,stress, have spent hours on the phone to no avail, and who knows what the financial damage will be in the future. Might lose some weight cause I can't  eat because of stress LOLI am presently fighting UPS as well for customs duty bills they keep sending to me for these b COD packages they abandoned at my door without knockingAlso Amazon is letting me wait the usual time for their resolution.  I will have to call them for it because they are afraid to provide a written answer",2023-07-05 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,14.0,2513,439,24,4,9.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,email sent amazoncomto may concernsince june receiving unwanted package amazoncomthe sender unknown meto knowledge dont even amazoncom account one amazoncaamazoncom amazonca potentially share client databaseinitially volume unwanted package scared contacted rcmp canadian police iti submitted unopened package evidencethe rcmp returned package saying muchthey harassment safe open package dispose themafter opened package return slip inside turn package sent amazoncomhere order id numbersxxxxxyou could start investigating account placed ordersif notify police call xxxx rcmp quoting file number xxxx verify veracity statement ask information neededi certainly pay return packagesi called amazoncom several already one time told glitch fixed second time talked leo explained nothing escalate problemjeff day later tried gaslight amazon ordersthe fourth time called told supplier using name address peddle ware address return addressthis seems plausible explanation since reached sender whose ph found internet search address seem confirmthey allegedly take business day provide response meanwhile keep receiving average package day refusing canamazon cancel fraudulent account dont password email address phone number iti strongly advise people cancel amazoncom account since security issue create world problemsi anxietystress spent hour phone avail know financial damage future might lose weight cause cant eat stress loli presently fighting ups well custom duty bill keep sending b cod package abandoned door without knockingalso amazon letting wait usual time resolution call afraid provide written answer,0.007058647218757226,0.9929413527812427,0.24621424565339317,0.2,0.8457135255213,84.57135255213,High Trust
Olga M,/users/64b1a1104aa3bd00128dc693,UA,1.0,2023-07-14 21:27:54+00:00,1.0,They blatantly lie about the delivery date!,"I placed my order on July 11th and my Amazon Prime delivery date was July 13th, which date was fine for me at the time of ordering. When the order was already placed and I received a tracking number for my order, I saw a new delivery date - July 17th. And in fact, I received my order on July 14, which is 1 day later than the scheduled delivery date (July 13). If I had known that my order would be delivered on July 14th or later, I would not have placed the order. Now when I contact their support, they say that my date was July 17th, and I received my order on July 14th, which is 3 days earlier lol. They blatantly lie about the delivery date when they fail to deliver on time, they just change the delivery date without notice and make you look like an idiot.",2023-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,14.0,766,152,43,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,placed order july th amazon prime delivery date july th date fine time ordering order already placed received tracking number order saw new delivery date july th fact received order july day later scheduled delivery date july known order would delivered july th later would placed order contact support say date july th received order july th day earlier lol blatantly lie delivery date fail deliver time change delivery date without notice make look like idiot,0.017156064958241964,0.982843935041758,0.08524957936062816,0.2,0.8084718833930047,80.84718833930047,High Trust
