George D,/users/5b93d29b4de5666d34789e33,GB,2.0,2023-07-08 11:01:19+00:00,1.0,Amazon stole my £500,"Absolutely NO customer protection at all.This is my -£500 sad experience with Amz.Earlier this month I have noticed a transaction for an expensive mobile phone and a smart band, in my account, but for some guy in US. At that time, there was a tracking number and I could see that that order didn't arrive yet. I have let Amz know immediately, and all they did was to reset my password and delete those orders from my account. Therefore, now I can't even see where those items were bought from, what merchant?!Anyway, I have asked Amz about the refund, since this is an unauthorized order, but they told me to request it from my card issuer. These guys, after looking into it, have also refused to refund me, probably because they considered to be an Amazon internal issue. I can only think of someone/somehow accessing my account and ordering something for themselves - and sadly there's no customer protection for that, as it was proven to me. Probably that's why the bank didn't process the refund and instead sent me back to Amazon.Numerous times I've contacted them and explain again and again, only to be assured that this will be processed the right team and only to get the same no-reply email advising me to contact my back and ask them for refund.So I got tired and eventually told Amazon to just send me those items, so I can recover some loss at least. After all, I've let them know as soon as possible, and those things haven't reached the hacker's address. Surely they have contacted the shipping company and told them to return the order, because the tracking number still shows undelivered.In a nut-shell: Amazon took my money somehow, and gave me nothing in return.",2023-06-01 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,7.0,8.0,1681,296,20,4,37.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,absolutely customer protection allthis £ sad experience amzearlier month noticed transaction expensive mobile phone smart band account guy u 