Diane Hartley,/users/52bcb79b00006400015bb50a,GB,10.0,2023-06-17 11:51:48+00:00,1.0,Amazon Pallets are a scam!,"We decided to order one of the ""Amazon [electronics package] Pallets"" priced at £39. It was a ""lucky dip"" type package (a promotion Amazon offered after the bad press they had regarding destroying perfectly good stock, rather than at least donating it to charity). It promised great value advertising pictures of watches, phones, laptops etc. The package took weeks to deliver (eventually arrived from CHINA!!) and contained an unbranded Bluetooth earpiece (the closest BRANDED one we found was £20), a useless lead (maximum price found online for BRANDED one was £7) and a USB charger lead (priced online at £1.98). This was the HIGHEST value we could get the contents up to!!! To add insult to injury, because the items were not deemed to be faulty (although we did not test them, as the quality was total rubbish regardless if they functioned to begin with), we had to PAY to return the package to Amazon!",2023-06-13 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,6.0,17.0,908,155,26,5,4.0,0,6,1,0,Genuine,decided order one amazon electronics package pallet priced £ lucky dip type package promotion amazon offered bad press regarding destroying perfectly good stock rather least donating charity promised great value advertising picture watch phone laptop etc package took week deliver eventually arrived china contained unbranded bluetooth earpiece closest branded one found £ useless lead maximum price found online branded one £ usb charger lead priced online £ highest value could get content add insult injury item deemed faulty although test quality total rubbish regardless functioned begin pay return package amazon,0.9889535852767046,0.011046414723295372,0.08693213684800898,0.2,0.32290963473124945,32.29096347312495,Low Trust
