Mads,/users/6146e7c769847500121e1efd,DK,14.0,2023-06-09 21:08:18+00:00,1.0,This company (Olsen Store GMBH) is as…,"This company (Olsen Store GMBH) is as unscrupulous as you can possibly get. first they postponed delivery, then they started delivery with a T&T number which we have been able to follow and the item was ready for delivery today, June 9. then on the same day we received a message from Amazon that the package would not be delivered and that there would be a new date.How on earth can you not send a package when you provide the T&T number to the customer and it has been on the way, it smells far away of SCAM.This company should in no way be allowed to sell their product on Amazon.",2023-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,6.0,9.0,583,111,38,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,company olsen store gmbh unscrupulous possibly get first postponed delivery started delivery tt number able follow item ready delivery today june day received message amazon package would delivered would new datehow earth send package provide tt number customer way smell far away scamthis company way allowed sell product amazon,0.018931801860270377,0.9810681981397297,0.062254627033090294,0.2,0.8029850244764829,80.29850244764829,High Trust
Dave Mayson,/users/64833f8c40823900119be2d6,GB,3.0,2023-06-09 17:04:52+00:00,1.0,Great until they're not,"There's plenty to like about Amazon when it works. They sell more or less everything, and lots of it can be with you by tomorrow. But, for a company that is declaring profits bigger than some national budgets, they could shave just a little off that to provide actual customer service, for those occasions when it doesn't simply go right. There simply is no way to get hold of them. If you try to begin a complaint, or ask a question, the site will guide you through a million useless questions, in the assumption that you can only have a problem that they have foreseen, and that you can be guided to an automated procedure. If you really persist, this experience will become circular, as you glimpse buttons that you think will help, but actually take you back to an earlier point in the process. Eventually, you may spot the very well hidden 'contact us' button that appears if you go round three times, and insist each time that your problem isn't listed. Sadly this contact is a chat that is -without wanting to offend those who man cheap call centres - far less intelligent than a bot. Today I had the issue that a number of Kindle books have gone from my library. When you're removing them from a device, one button says, ""remove download"" whilst another says, ""delete,"" and the latter actually removes the book clean out of your library on the Amazon server. No idea why this would even be a possiblity, let alone so easy to do, but someone in our family managed to wipe a massive chunk of our library whilst emptying a Kindle. It took me about 10 attempts to explain to the guy on the other end that this is even possible - after each attempt he sent me a link to my library, insisting that the books must be there if I bought them. Eventually he pretended the chat had been quiet for too long (5 seconds) and passed it off to someone whose English and knowledge of Amazon was even worse. After reviewing the whole thing again with him, and receiving the same patronisation, he assured me there was nothing that can be done. I told him this isn't correct because I know people who have done it, by virtue of getting a slightly better assistant. Then I provided him with the order number for one of the books that is missing, so he could see that there is still a receipt in my order history, but that the book no longer appears in my library. At this point he told me that Amazon only archive invoices for a year or so, so he wouldn't be able to see a record of the order. I explained that I was looking at the record of the order, by logging into my Amazon account, which resides on their servers, so this was clearly a lie. At that point he simply closed the chat window. Normally I wouldn't go to the trouble of venting somewhere about this, but it's now about the tenth such experience I've had. This one is arguably partly my fault (although there's really no reason to have an option to completely remove books from your library, and certainly not to make it so easily done), but usually it's a complete screw up on their part, and you're still dealing with someone who can just hang up if they don't feel like helping.",2023-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,6.0,9.0,3134,582,23,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,there plenty like amazon work sell less everything lot tomorrow company declaring profit bigger national budget could shave little provide actual customer service occasion doesnt simply go right simply way get hold try begin complaint ask question site guide million useless question assumption problem foreseen guided automated procedure really persist experience become circular glimpse button think help actually take back earlier point process eventually may spot well hidden contact u button appears go round three time insist time problem isnt listed sadly contact chat without wanting offend man cheap call centre far less intelligent bot today issue number kindle book gone library youre removing device one button say remove download whilst another say delete latter actually remove book clean library amazon server idea would even possiblity let alone easy someone family managed wipe massive chunk library whilst emptying kindle took attempt explain guy end even possible attempt sent link library insisting book must bought eventually pretended chat quiet long second passed someone whose english knowledge amazon even worse reviewing whole thing receiving patronisation assured nothing done told isnt correct know people done virtue getting slightly better assistant provided order number one book missing could see still receipt order history book longer appears library point told amazon archive invoice year wouldnt able see record order explained looking record order logging amazon account resides server clearly lie point simply closed chat window normally wouldnt go trouble venting somewhere tenth experience ive one arguably partly fault although there really reason option completely remove book library certainly make easily done usually complete screw part youre still dealing someone hang dont feel like helping,0.003922779075747083,0.9960772209242529,0.32641615255187884,0.2,0.8633218409725022,86.33218409725022,High Trust
Lorraine Van Cott,/users/5ebc53ca0eea571e859d96ca,US,3.0,2023-06-09 15:50:36+00:00,2.0,Shame on you Amazon. I feel cheated& lied to.n,"Amazon has turned to products from China but as a buyer it's not information that is easily known prior to purchase. Amazon needs to change that. Maybe I'm offended doing business with China. Maybe I don't want to wait a long time for an item to arrive when shipped from China.  Maybe I ordered my regular size not knowing it's made in China & since their clothing runs small my order doesn't fit. Which lead me to returns. Since I have yet to use a return to China idk how long it takes to get my money back.Shame, shame Amazon.",2023-06-09 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,6.0,9.0,529,100,46,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon turned product china buyer information easily known prior purchase amazon need change maybe im offended business china maybe dont want wait long time item arrive shipped china maybe ordered regular size knowing made china since clothing run small order doesnt fit lead return since yet use return china idk long take get money backshame shame amazon,0.009637130155420141,0.9903628698445799,0.056085249579360626,0.4,1.106398484838162,110.63984848381621,High Trust
