Douglas Kelly,/users/5d5d372e3d6bf5efb759aaf0,US,6.0,2023-05-30 15:03:36+00:00,1.0,"Next day delivery...""NOT""","I can't say I don't buy lots of stuff from Amazon. But over the past year I have found that Amazon's delivery dates are near worthless. When you group packages to arrive on a specific date, Amazon changes the date or breaks up the package. On Friday I bought a prime sale item. "" Buy it today you'll have it tomorrow"" Once the order was placed and within a few hours my Saturday delivery became 6 days later on Friday. I often buy for a second home. Only about half our packages have arrived while we were taking a long weekend. On the packages that don't arrive, either a neighbor grabs them or they are lost or stolen. Amazon created the fast delivery but my recent experience has been anything but fast.",2023-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,30.0,706,132,25,3,4.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,cant say dont buy lot stuff amazon past year found amazon delivery date near worthless group package arrive specific date amazon change date break package friday bought prime sale item buy today youll tomorrow order placed within hour saturday delivery became day later friday often buy second home half package arrived taking long weekend package dont arrive either neighbor grab lost stolen amazon created fast delivery recent experience anything fast,0.012049855186048394,0.9879501448139516,0.07403252944475602,0.2,0.808781578295927,80.8781578295927,High Trust
