Michae Leschziner,/users/5d8fad95f378d143c9b373c8,GB,9.0,2023-05-28 13:46:19+00:00,2.0,"Amazon locker ""full""?","Amazon locker full?  Have you ever wondered why a range of items are not deliverable to lockers because the ""locker is full""?  In my experience, this is often a lie, designed to make you bear very high postal charges. I have experimented with various items, with various lockers, over a long period of time.  In many cases, especially smallish low-cost items, the lockers are ALWAYS ""FULL"", even though other items ordered at the same time from other suppliers are readily delivered to the ""full"" locker.  As a matter of principle, I DO NOT ORDER items which Amazoin does not deliver to its lockers.  This ""locker is full"" business is merely designed to enable the suppliers to increase their profits by levying high delivery charges.",2023-05-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,28.0,734,124,21,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon locker full ever wondered range item deliverable locker locker full experience often lie designed make bear high postal charge experimented various item various locker long period time many case especially smallish lowcost item locker always full even though item ordered time supplier readily delivered full locker matter principle order item amazoin deliver locker locker full business merely designed enable supplier increase profit levying high delivery charge,0.06883224036472446,0.9311677596352755,0.06954570947840717,0.4,1.0794930217133192,107.94930217133192,High Trust
