Frank Timberlake,/users/5c2dd8cca510ea489e299645,US,26.0,2023-05-25 05:01:57+00:00,1.0,It's got too bad to be worth it,"That's it for me.Amazon might have been decent in the past... but definitely, not anymore. I think I've been their customer for about 15 years, give or take.The last annoyance (out of many I've accumulated through the years) is regarding the fact that they don't price match their own stuff within the return window.I've recently bought an expensive computer, and the same day I received it, a 6% deal hit it. Now in order to get the discount... I'm supposed to send it back and order another one? In what mind is that good for anyone? Amazon would have a returned product worth less, and I would have to go through the logistics hassle... okay, maybe UPS would win with this stupid policy.I insist, it's a product where Amazon is the merchant. I would see it totally justified if the customer was hopping between vendors in their marketplace. That's not the case.I really regret not using Best Buy for this. I also stopped using Amazon when I'm in other countries, and it's not that difficult finding alternatives for many products. After leaving Amazon, some other niche products can be a PITA to find, though... specially if (like me) one has sworn off Aliexpress as well...But life goes on without Amazon. Bye, bye, Amazon US.It seems almost predictable how the customer experience would decay as a company starts becoming a monopoly.",2023-05-23 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,25.0,1338,230,31,8,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,thats meamazon might decent past definitely anymore think ive customer year give takethe last annoyance many ive accumulated year regarding fact dont price match stuff within return windowive recently bought expensive computer day received deal hit order get discount im supposed send back order another one mind good anyone amazon would returned product worth less would go logistics hassle okay maybe ups would win stupid policyi insist product amazon merchant would see totally justified customer hopping vendor marketplace thats casei really regret using best buy also stopped using amazon im country difficult finding alternative many product leaving amazon niche product pita find though specially like one sworn aliexpress wellbut life go without amazon bye bye amazon usit seems almost predictable customer experience would decay company start becoming monopoly,0.008851099653056797,0.9911489003469433,0.12899607403252944,0.2,0.8213736649799775,82.13736649799776,High Trust
Shaquille Fuller,/users/6053efefee1772001a145e08,US,3.0,2023-05-25 03:11:27+00:00,1.0,Amazon Logistics is terrible and can't be trusted,"I would like to get my packages on time. If you use technology to let customers know you are two stops away, the delivery driver shouldn't take a trip across town while passing your location! I am done with Amazon after this mess. Can't trust any of the logistic information. They don't care. I will spend my money locally going forward! I waited over an hour (30 mins in which the driver's location did not move) for them to show up at a delivery location closing at 6:30pm CST.",2023-05-24 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,25.0,479,89,49,8,1.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,would like get package time use technology let customer know two stop away delivery driver shouldnt take trip across town passing location done amazon mess cant trust logistic information dont care spend money locally going forward waited hour min driver location move show delivery location closing pm cst,0.26133126546827434,0.7386687345317257,0.04991587212563096,0.2,0.679317541690989,67.9317541690989,Medium Trust
