Christian S.,/users/6462b76055c27c0013aa3174,US,1.0,2023-05-16 00:51:49+00:00,1.0,Significant price increase on items purchased just last week,"Purchased same swim shirt in two different colors last Monday for $20.98 each. When I tried them on this afternoon they were a little too big, so wanted to exchange them for next size down. Since Amazon does not do exchanges and only refunds, so I would have had to purchase the shirts again in my new desired size while returning the previous ones I received. Unfortunately, the same exact shirts are now $29 each today! That is a pretty significant increase from just 7 days ago! Now I know you can receive a refund for the difference if an item/product you purchased days before goes DOWN in price, but what about those who have or will experience a similar scenario as mine? All I wanted to do was exchange them for a smaller size and pay more or less the same price as last week. How is this fair? It isn't. SMH...",2023-05-15 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,16.0,819,153,60,9,1.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,purchased swim shirt two different color last monday tried afternoon little big wanted exchange next size since amazon exchange refund would purchase shirt new desired size returning previous one received unfortunately exact shirt today pretty significant increase day ago know receive refund difference itemproduct purchased day go price experience similar scenario mine wanted exchange smaller size pay less price last week fair isnt smh,0.2827614048336765,0.7172385951663235,0.08581043185642176,0.2,0.6757813839544461,67.57813839544461,Medium Trust
