Blaze Mobile,/users/645a60709600510012db41b4,US,2.0,2023-05-09 17:41:55+00:00,1.0,After getting our brand approved,"After getting our brand approved, and our store, we had to pay advertising in order to get items noticed, fees were outrageous. We went with FBA. What a joke, they accepted and and all returns, even without the item in box. They lost over 170 of our SKU's, and delayed our opening a case for months, we still have non resolution. Bottom line, Amazon FBA completely failed us. We fulfilled our orders with no returns, FBA was a nightmare. We have stopped selling on Amazon and only do brick and mortar due to all of the fraud, and return expenses (Amazon says they incur this, but its the sellers!!). Goodbye online marketplaces, you're not worth it. The buyers are not people who go into retail stores, they are mostly scammers.",2023-04-10 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,9.0,728,130,32,5,29.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,getting brand approved store pay advertising order get item noticed fee outrageous went fba joke accepted return even without item box lost skus delayed opening case month still non resolution bottom line amazon fba completely failed u fulfilled order return fba nightmare stopped selling amazon brick mortar due fraud return expense amazon say incur seller goodbye online marketplace youre worth buyer people go retail store mostly scammer,0.129056159433753,0.870943840566247,0.07291082445316882,0.2,0.7500540851737573,75.00540851737573,High Trust
Matthew Reid Adams,/users/63e51a3169ff7f001261c777,ZA,1.0,2023-05-09 17:22:27+00:00,1.0,Returned an item but did not receive my refund,I bought a laptop from Amazon on the 19th of June 2022 [Order number 026-4932158-0409958] and returned this laptop the post office as instructed by Amazon on the 20th of June 2022. The laptop did not start even though it was plugged in and it refused to charge so I returned it because the product was clearly faulty. Royal Mail confirmed that the item was returned on the 21st of June 2022 to the Amazon Warehouse at 09:12 and an employee at Amazon signed for it. I have proof of delivery.One month past and I ordered a new laptop and still didn't get my refund for the faulty laptop so I queried with Customer Service and was told that my refund would take 5-7 business days. I have email proof from the Amazon employee stating that the item I returned has been received and that my refund would be issued in 5-7 business days.I'm still to receive my refund despite numerous incident reports filled out and hours of calls to customer service. It reached the point wear I wanted to make a claim against Amazon however I'm afraid the fees would be more than the value of the laptop [849.99 Value of the laptop] therefore decided to not take further action. I'm hoping this review finds and Amazon employee and they can get back to me on how to resolve this issue. I have all the documentation you require.- Order number and purchase receipt- Proof of delivery along with the Amazon employee signature- Email stating that I'll receive the refund with confirmation that the return has been received,2022-07-21 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,9.0,1496,268,46,9,292.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,bought laptop amazon th june order number returned laptop post office instructed amazon th june laptop start even though plugged refused charge returned product clearly faulty royal mail confirmed item returned st june amazon warehouse employee amazon signed proof deliveryone month past ordered new laptop still didnt get refund faulty laptop queried customer service told refund would take business day email proof amazon employee stating item returned received refund would issued business daysim still receive refund despite numerous incident report filled hour call customer service reached point wear wanted make claim amazon however im afraid fee would value laptop value laptop therefore decided take action im hoping review find amazon employee get back resolve issue documentation require order number purchase receipt proof delivery along amazon employee signature email stating ill receive refund confirmation return received,0.00013817218662509934,0.9998618278133748,0.15030846887268648,0.2,0.8299926076812247,82.99926076812247,High Trust
Continuity Concierge,/users/5cead56be51855796dacb107,US,26.0,2023-05-09 16:56:36+00:00,3.0,What ever happened to 2-day shipping…,"What ever happened to 2-day shipping for Amazon Prime membership?  And why isn't there a link somewhere about the Amazon website to contact customer service?  Why does it take about 5 minutes (not exaggerating) to drill down, answer questions, meet criteria and generally jump through hoops in order to get to the point where you can ask a question of a customer service rep?  I get that its HUGE but does that exonerate them from basic business practices and being available to their customers?  Is it impossible to imagine that there are some questions that can't be answered by the options they offer up in a list?The COVID pandemic wreaked havoc upon society worldwide and created new standards and expectations for and about work, workers, customers, customer services, etc. and during that time it was impossible to fulfill Prime membership benefits like 2-day shipping, but it's long since and they've not yet reinstated the 2-day shipping policy. Go to amazon and look up prime membership benefits and the list includes video and kindle and music benefits but, all of those come with a monthly subscription fee separate from the $139 annual fee for Prime membership.  The shipping benefits listed for Prime Membership reflect two-day shipping on ""select"" items, so perhaps just the ""select"" item list got pared back during COVID and has never been 're-augmented'?Whatever the answer, I'm not sure Amazon prime membership is worth it anymore - certainly not if you're paying for it monthly; but perhaps even the annual membership doesn't make sense?It's rare that I need anything the next day or even two-days later and I'll frequently select delivery on my amazon delivery day, but when I do need something within' two-days, I'm finding Walmart to be more receptive to those needs (and they often deliver the next day AND on Sundays). Me thinks Amazon has gotten too big for it's britches and forgets the trail-blazing they once did only to foist buggy service upon us now. And don't get me started on dropping Amazon returns at a Whole Foods, especially one in NYC  The Upper East Side Whole Foods at 87th & 3rd has a huge Amazon Returns sign with that big smiley swoosh beneath it, so you know you're in the right place, but there's no additional signage to tell you to go to the Mezzanine which is accessible only by elevator (don't take the escalator bc it bypasses the Mezz altogether).",2023-05-09 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,9.0,2399,407,37,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ever happened day shipping amazon prime membership isnt link somewhere amazon website contact customer service take minute exaggerating drill answer question meet criterion generally jump hoop order get point ask question customer service rep get huge exonerate basic business practice available customer impossible imagine question cant answered option offer listthe covid pandemic wreaked havoc upon society worldwide created new standard expectation work worker customer customer service etc time impossible fulfill prime membership benefit like day shipping long since theyve yet reinstated day shipping policy go amazon look prime membership benefit list includes video kindle music benefit come monthly subscription fee separate annual fee prime membership shipping benefit listed prime membership reflect twoday shipping select item perhaps select item list got pared back covid never reaugmentedwhatever answer im sure amazon prime membership worth anymore certainly youre paying monthly perhaps even annual membership doesnt make senseits rare need anything next day even twodays later ill frequently select delivery amazon delivery day need something within twodays im finding walmart receptive need often deliver next day sunday think amazon gotten big britches forgets trailblazing foist buggy service upon u dont get started dropping amazon return whole food especially one nyc upper east side whole food th rd huge amazon return sign big smiley swoosh beneath know youre right place there additional signage tell go mezzanine accessible elevator dont take escalator bc bypass mezz altogether,0.02215428651686043,0.9778457134831395,0.22826696578799777,0.6,1.4345762498991692,143.45762498991692,High Trust
