Pistol P,/users/645848cfefbe6d001597f634,CA,1.0,2023-05-08 02:56:57+00:00,1.0,Amazon Has Done Terrible Things To Me,"Amazon Has Done Terrible Things To Me. I have been an Amazon Prime Member for 12 years now. At the beginning their customer service was excellent and I even got their credit card. This past year, however, they have become a nightmare to deal with and have stolen money from me and permanently banned me from writing reviews because of ""suspicious activity"" on my account. Let me be clear, I have left maybe 3-4 reviews the entire 12 years I've had my account, and I only reviewed something if it was a terrible product and I tried to save others from buying it.Furthermore, I ordered a Razer Monitor a few months ago, and the package was ripped open when it arrived. I tested the monitor and it was not the model I ordered, so I sent it back. Shortly after I received an email stating that I was not getting a refund and they were keeping the monitor I sent back. This was a $1200 monitor, so I lost a lot of money. I tried going through the Better Business Bureau and Amazon laughed in my face and said they would be happy to speak to my legal team. Most recently I ordered 3 Limited Edition Nintendo Switch Tears of the Kingdom models, and they were stolen off my porch. I have specific delivery instructions I have left Amazon, that they are to knock and if no one answers to deliver another time, to make sure my packages didn't get taken by porch pirates. Well, they refused the refund without a Police Report, which I did. Even after the Police investigation was done and the Police Report was approved, I sent it to Amazon as instructed. They still denied me a refund or replacement, so I had to call and argue with them and they finally agreed to the refund. Amazon in its current state is a complete mess and they no longer know how to care for their long-term customers who have spent hundreds of thousands of dollars on their platform over 12 years. Stay away from this company if you can and order from other online retailers, as places like Walmart and BestBuy Online are stocking the same products now and they have much better delivery and customer service.",2023-05-01 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,8.0,2072,381,37,7,7.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon done terrible thing amazon prime member year beginning customer service excellent even got credit card past year however become nightmare deal stolen money permanently banned writing review suspicious activity account let clear left maybe review entire year ive account reviewed something terrible product tried save others buying itfurthermore ordered razer monitor month ago package ripped open arrived tested monitor model ordered sent back shortly received email stating getting refund keeping monitor sent back monitor lost lot money tried going better business bureau amazon laughed face said would happy speak legal team recently ordered limited edition nintendo switch tear kingdom model stolen porch specific delivery instruction left amazon knock one answer deliver another time make sure package didnt get taken porch pirate well refused refund without police report even police investigation done police report approved sent amazon instructed still denied refund replacement call argue finally agreed refund amazon current state complete mess longer know care longterm customer spent hundred thousand dollar platform year stay away company order online retailer place like walmart bestbuy online stocking product much better delivery customer service,0.005429180416906953,0.994570819583093,0.213684800897364,0.2,0.8400223699710193,84.00223699710193,High Trust
Dean Cragg,/users/62e17d3155eff30013b125e2,US,4.0,2023-05-08 00:36:32+00:00,1.0,Stop the bait and switch listings and fake reviews everywhere,"They need to stop the 2 types of bait and switch that is going on in the majority of listings before they get sued into oblivion because of how rampant this issue is and how much it is costing people. The first issue is when you see a product for instance “3 pack diamond grit polish $10.28” in the search results and then you click on it because it’s a good deal and then it shows you the horizontal row of “different sizes” but the exact item/size/title/description just the literal exact thing that it was advertising before you clicked on it says it’s $32.98 and the only “size”/the only product on that listing for the listed $10.28 is a piece of wool cloth. This is flat out ridiculously stupid and scummy and a waste of everyone’s time. The second and even worse thing is sellers will start selling a good product and once it gets good reviews or if they can no longer get that product or whatever they will simply delete the photos, title, and description of the original product and then replace it with a new product that is often in the same category or related to the original product but far worse quality and almost never even interchangeable with the original (for example they replace a belt sander with a palm sander or drill or just different size brand and quality belt sander) and all they did was change the title, description and photos but kept the same listing since all they technically did was “edit it” which also allows them to keep all the positive reviews so you will be buying a product that is rated 5 stars and had hundreds of reviews and thus probably won’t even question it but yet you may be the first person to ever buy it because in essence they’re all fake reviews since they’re for the other product. The only way to tell is by reading the reviews and even then unless it has dozens of reviews or reviews with pictures of the product you’ll never know. Not only is that scummy and definitely worthy of a class action it could also really cause severe harm to people physically and monetarily because a lot of people get a lot of tips and info on the use, maintenance, parts, and accessories of products from the reviews especially on Chinese products that have useless instructions. For instance, with 3d printing a lot of cheap and popular printers are from Chinese companies and come with poor instructions and if you don’t know what you’re doing it’s rough so say for instance someone says that they a hard time finding a thermister or heating element for the printer but XYZ is the correct one, well in 3d printing and especially with those parts if you don’t replace them with the correct ones and in the correct way you can easily start a fire and so if they change out the product and keep the reviews then some mom buying one for her kid won’t know any better and even doing all the research if she sees that review she could she will end up installing the wrong one and there is a high likelihood that it will catch on fire all because Amazon couldn’t care less about anything but profit, and no I’m not one of the eat the rich types but corporations are getting out of hand and this stuff is not only poor business practices and scams blatantly happening on a massive scale right in front of them it’s also 100% going to get someone killed.",2023-05-06 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,8.0,3290,605,61,10,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,need stop type bait switch going majority listing get sued oblivion rampant issue much costing people first issue see product instance “ pack diamond grit polish ” search result click it’s good deal show horizontal row “different sizes” exact itemsizetitledescription literal exact thing advertising clicked say it’s “size”the product listing listed piece wool cloth flat ridiculously stupid scummy waste everyone’s time second even worse thing seller start selling good product get good review longer get product whatever simply delete photo title description original product replace new product often category related original product far worse quality almost never even interchangeable original example replace belt sander palm sander drill different size brand quality belt sander change title description photo kept listing since technically “edit it” also allows keep positive review buying product rated star hundred review thus probably won’t even question yet may first person ever buy essence they’re fake review since they’re product way tell reading review even unless dozen review review picture product you’ll never know scummy definitely worthy class action could also really cause severe harm people physically monetarily lot people get lot tip info use maintenance part accessory product review especially chinese product useless instruction instance printing lot cheap popular printer chinese company come poor instruction don’t know you’re it’s rough say instance someone say hard time finding thermister heating element printer xyz correct one well printing especially part don’t replace correct one correct way easily start fire change product keep review mom buying one kid won’t know better even research see review could end installing wrong one high likelihood catch fire amazon couldn’t care less anything profit i’m one eat rich type corporation getting hand stuff poor business practice scam blatantly happening massive scale right front it’s also going get someone killed,0.009760544329531927,0.9902394556704681,0.3393157599551318,0.2,0.8629828798262603,86.29828798262604,High Trust
