Mrs June Webb,/users/62165e0a8b487a001396bf2a,GB,4.0,2023-05-03 16:29:23+00:00,1.0,If I could give less stars I certainly…,"If I could give less stars I certainly would. I ordered an iMac in March and waited at least 2 weeks for the item. I paid my £1479.00 and patiently waited. Eventually it arrived …… or did it. When I opened the battered box it was full of cabling and what looked like the inners of a computer or similar…… anyway it was certainly not an iMac. To cut the story short, customer services were useless and rude and after calling them and speaking with a manager several times, I decided to contact my bank. I opened a dispute and during this time, Amazon told me they had paid back the monies plus postage of £10. A few weeks later, Amazon decided to dispute the dispute saying I had received the goods. This went to appeal, and finally 2 months later I received my refund, thanks to my bank. PLEASE if you are sending for a valuable item, don’t buy it from Amazon. You may pay a few pounds more from a high street shop but at least it will be hassle free.",2023-05-03 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,3.0,951,183,39,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,could give less star certainly would ordered imac march waited least week item paid £ patiently waited eventually arrived …… opened battered box full cabling looked like inners computer similar…… anyway certainly imac cut story short customer service useless rude calling speaking manager several time decided contact bank opened dispute time amazon told paid back monies plus postage £ week later amazon decided dispute dispute saying received good went appeal finally month later received refund thanks bank please sending valuable item don’t buy amazon may pay pound high street shop least hassle free,0.020815954298091386,0.9791840457019086,0.10263600673022995,0.2,0.8101192241970003,81.01192241970003,High Trust
