Tanisha Kelly,/users/645066532736830012856000,US,1.0,2023-05-02 03:24:48+00:00,1.0,Ridiculous,"Literally, Amazon delivery drivers kept leaving my packages at the wrong buildings in my apartment complex. So I switched to hub lockers. Then, Amazon revoked my ability to write reviews, claiming that my previous reviews looked ""suspicious"". My reviews were actually wholesome, positive, and did not violate Amazon's policies. But their customer service and managers couldn't or wouldn't fix it. So I closed the account and opened a new one. Now, yesterday I created an order and used a virtual credit card that my employers gave me as a bonus. Amazon has now frozen my account and is ""investigating""because apparently using a virtual credit card is ""suspicious"" too. Amazon's customer service and managers are rude, defensive and completely unhelpful, making it painfully clear that they have no desire to help resolve Amazon's system glitches. Amazon is ridiculous and I'm not doing this anymore. I don't have to. There are too many other options.",2023-05-01 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,5.0,2.0,950,153,10,1,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,literally amazon delivery driver kept leaving package wrong building apartment complex switched hub locker amazon revoked ability write review claiming previous review looked suspicious review actually wholesome positive violate amazon policy customer service manager couldnt wouldnt fix closed account opened new one yesterday created order used virtual credit card employer gave bonus amazon frozen account investigatingbecause apparently using virtual credit card suspicious amazon customer service manager rude defensive completely unhelpful making painfully clear desire help resolve amazon system glitch amazon ridiculous im anymore dont many option,0.025558578160098096,0.9744414218399019,0.08581043185642176,0.2,0.8043827972912353,80.43827972912354,High Trust
