Rozan Loveday,/users/6436b1fd9648730012b850d3,US,1.0,2023-04-12 15:28:59+00:00,1.0,Jumping Through Hoops is BS,"My Mom and I have been faithful Amazon customers for over 20 years. Recently I got tangled up with a scammer that asked me to order apple gift cards from my Moms and my account. So Amazon blocked those accounts and really put me through the wringer trying to keep them open and state my case. They kept asking me to submit proof of the cards I was using and billing statements from the bank. Which I did to know avail. We lost all the Kindle books we’ve purchased over the years and both being avid readers that’s a lot of money, all the movies we’ve purchased on those accounts customer service told me they couldn’t be transferred. We would have to create a new account and repurchase. I finally created my mom a new account with a new email and I told her if I wanted something I’d just use her account. It’s been going well for about a month and a 1/2. Yesterday I ordered a movie from prime video and a charging cable for one of my devices. I paid with my moms debit card. An hour later she gets an email stating that they have put her account on hold due to suspicious activity…what suspicious activity? Since when is a movie and a charging cable suspicious activity? I was supposed to send them a copy of our bank statement and proof that we were the owner of the debit card used which I did. Only to get another email saying that what I provided wasn’t good enough. They wanted information on a credit card ending in 5719 but we don’t use credit cards on that site. I called the account change and issue department 800.388.5572 if anyone needs it and I was told that an email had been sent to them and they would respond within 24 hours. What sucks about a account being blocked is you can’t access anything, you can’t make orders, listen to music, watch videos you own or have rented your just dead in the water. All I can say about this is if everyone is being treated the same way I’m being treated they are going to lose customers fast. I’ve also had packages come to me opened, I’ve had things I’ve bought come broken. It’s taken a long time to get things refunded and or replaced. What is it about the bigger the company gets the worse they treat the people that made them successful to begin with? It’s the same with Wal-Mart.",2023-04-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,4.0,12.0,2241,423,27,5,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,mom faithful amazon customer year recently got tangled scammer asked order apple gift card mom account amazon blocked account really put wringer trying keep open state case kept asking submit proof card using billing statement bank know avail lost kindle book we’ve purchased year avid reader that’s lot money movie we’ve purchased account customer service told couldn’t transferred would create new account repurchase finally created mom new account new email told wanted something i’d use account it’s going well month yesterday ordered movie prime video charging cable one device paid mom debit card hour later get email stating put account hold due suspicious activity…what suspicious activity since movie charging cable suspicious activity supposed send copy bank statement proof owner debit card used get another email saying provided wasn’t good enough wanted information credit card ending don’t use credit card site called account change issue department anyone need told email sent would respond within hour suck account blocked can’t access anything can’t make order listen music watch video rented dead water say everyone treated way i’m treated going lose customer fast i’ve also package come opened i’ve thing i’ve bought come broken it’s taken long time get thing refunded replaced bigger company get worse treat people made successful begin it’s walmart,0.006504019408077709,0.9934959805919223,0.23724060572069547,0.2,0.8441961114401002,84.41961114401002,High Trust
Fady Anwar,/users/5e7771bcdffcf750c48f7d7b,IE,2.0,2023-04-12 14:36:35+00:00,2.0,Used to be great,"I'm not sure if I'm actually further wasting my time in here but here goes nothing. I confirmed with the agent on the phone that there are clear instructions for the delivery driver to call me upon arrival, yet, for some reason they didn't bother to do and simply left it with a shop owner on the street which I don't know. Then they put a comment saying they left it with a neighbour! They could have also left on the curb while they are it!! This is so ridiculous and undermine the heavily marketed principles of Amazon about customer obsession which appears by now to be just a cliché a middle manager would say to get into Amazon...",2023-04-12 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,4.0,12.0,636,119,16,4,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,im sure im actually wasting time go nothing confirmed agent phone clear instruction delivery driver call upon arrival yet reason didnt bother simply left shop owner street dont know put comment saying left neighbour could also left curb ridiculous undermine heavily marketed principle amazon customer obsession appears cliché middle manager would say get amazon,0.8409901858179383,0.15900981418206173,0.06674144699943915,0.4,0.6928531964909187,69.28531964909187,Medium Trust
