Jonathan Mueller,/users/5cf1b687edd84e2adfb6e7d9,EC,7.0,2024-03-01 00:26:54+00:00,1.0,I got scammed buying a DJI Mini 3 Pro…,I got scammed buying a DJI Mini 3 Pro from Amazon in January of 2023. The package delivered had been previously returned by someone that took out the drone and replaced it with a CPU cooler and aluminum foil shaped like the DJI remote along with a busted cellphone. Then they sealed it again to look unopened. After numerous attempts to talk to a person I finally gave up. I was instructed to return the item which I did. After Amazon received the box the sent an automated reply saying the parts were not returned and the contents would be discarded and no refund given. Hours more on the phone got nothing and nowhere. After this the only option was to file a credit card dispute for the amount. A nightmare and Amazon never got a manager to call me to discuss or even check into what I was saying to see who previously bought and returned the item. They don’t care. They don’t care even now losing me as a 10 year or more customer. I cancelled my Prime membership and all other Amazon service. They do not deserve or respect their customers. The worst experience buying something online. Amazon can not be trusted they will not look into or care at all when their own customer is scammed. Whoever did this knew exactly what to put in the box to fool the automated return system and will do it again I’m sure. Amazon won’t care because they will pass the scam on to you without spending 10 minutes to look into it. If only I could upload pictures of the day I received the false merchandise. Heart broken.,2023-01-30 00:00:00+00:00,2024.0,3.0,1.0,1507,280,38,9,396.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,got scammed buying dji mini pro amazon january package delivered previously returned someone took drone replaced cpu cooler aluminum foil shaped like dji remote along busted cellphone sealed look unopened numerous attempt talk person finally gave instructed return item amazon received box 