Sanjay Dalvi,/users/641ec570481a950013bcba7b,AE,2.0,2023-03-25 11:57:15+00:00,1.0,Horrible Exp from Amazon,"Good day, everyone.On March 22, 2023, a wooden plant stand that I had ordered was placed.which is scheduled to be delivered on March 25, 2023, on Saturday.I agreed with this plan.I received a call at 16:10 on the evening of the 24th from someone claiming to be an Amazon third party.And I have to send your order by today, and he added his comment that he is not sure that I will get this tomorrow?I told him it wasn't possible to accept the delivery on the 24th rather than the 25th as per the established schedule because I was a little surprised by his reply.I emailed Amazon about this on the 24th,  and they have yet to respond. They may be worried about their new bookings not the existing 's.I called customer support on the morning of the 25th, and a woman answered with the name Ms. Riama or Rima. She apologized for the oversight and promised to see to it that it was resolved today.I called again just to double-check, and this time Ms. Mona from the customer service representative answered the phone and said, ""Today we can't deliver, and she don't want to provide false hopes.""Is it offensive that the initial customer support representative toyed with the client?What a wonderful service! This will be my final purchase from Amazon.com.Just a quick question: what would happen if I had paid in advance. ?",2023-03-24 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,3.0,25.0,1319,234,24,4,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,good day everyoneon march wooden plant stand ordered placedwhich scheduled delivered march saturdayi agreed plani received call evening th someone claiming amazon third partyand send order today added comment sure get tomorrowi told wasnt possible accept delivery th rather th per established schedule little surprised replyi emailed amazon th yet respond may worried new booking existing si called customer support morning th woman answered name m riama rima apologized oversight promised see