R P,/users/617086ddc95cdd0012fb7d21,CA,18.0,2023-03-24 22:57:07+00:00,1.0,"Who is watching you, Amazon or Santa?","So I filled out a survey a few days ago where you can earn points. The survey asked about past purchases so I selected hairdryer from the list. Wouldn’t you know it, the next screen wanted to know the brand and I couldn’t remember the name so I searched Google. About an hour later Amazon sends me one of their email adverts with a selection of hair dryers. Well, I thought are they tracking me? I was sure I had all tracking turned off so I called them and was told that if you search any site the cookies that are still on your device can be used by Amazon. The only alternative is to Block All Cookies. The thing is I always clear the cache which includes websites, data and cookies whenever I close my browser and I had just opened the app for the survey so that means Amazon is more powerful than Santa.",2023-03-22 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,3.0,24.0,808,156,37,7,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,filled survey day ago earn point survey asked past purchase selected hairdryer list wouldn’t know next screen wanted know brand couldn’t remember name searched google hour later amazon sends one email advert selection hair dryer well thought tracking sure tracking turned called told search site cooky still device used amazon alternative block cooky thing always clear cache includes website data cooky whenever close browser opened app survey mean amazon powerful santa,0.031726674627131767,0.9682733253728683,0.08749298934380258,0.2,0.8016352605551946,80.16352605551947,High Trust
