michael hance,/users/641124085bbf3b001218c964,US,1.0,2023-03-15 03:55:27+00:00,1.0,Fraudulent Practices !!!,"Ordered a Bosch auto product.  Received product and removed from Bosch packaging and found the product was actually from an inferior  manufacturer. You had to look really close, but it was not a Bosch product. I examined the Amazon Packing , and it had a sticker that said "" thank you for giving this product a second life . ""  So amazon is restocking returns, not inspecting them, and then reselling them !!   How fraudulent !!  Beware !!",2023-03-01 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,3.0,15.0,439,78,24,3,14.0,0,6,1,0,Genuine,ordered bosch auto product received product removed bosch packaging found product actually inferior manufacturer look really close bosch product examined amazon packing sticker said thank giving product second life amazon restocking return inspecting reselling fraudulent beware,0.9973945474651238,0.002605452534876207,0.04374649467190129,0.2,0.31005202520181835,31.005202520181836,Low Trust
Linda Manas,/users/56791a710000ff0001f5dcec,GB,14.0,2023-03-15 08:43:51+00:00,1.0,Conned into signing up for Amazon Prime. BEWARE!,I don’t like Amazon because they advertise things for sale that are out of stock. I had a very bad experience just over a year ago when I bought a book. Like many people I ticked free postage.BEWARE! If you click Free Postage you will inadvertently sign up for Amazon Prime.I did not know I had done this until I had to change my bank card because of a security scare. I then had a phone call from Amazon saying they could not process my Amazon payments. I was horrified and thought it was a scam. I then rang the real Amazon and they told me I had signed up to Amazon Prime. I was appalled and cancelled my Amazon Prime account.I gave the card number of the expired card which was safe to do.  I then received a phone call from BT saying my call to Amazon had cost £80.BT refunded half of this as a goodwill gesture. Beware of signing up to Amazon Prime if you click Free postage. I lost several payments of £7.99 and £40 so lost about £80. Disgusting company who are conning and tricking people into signing up for Amazon Prime. I tried to download a kindle app the other day but discovered I could only use the app to read a book if I buy the book off Amazon. No chance!Other thing I hate about them: you can’t use PayPal.,2022-12-20 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,3.0,15.0,1225,237,48,8,85.0,0,2,0,0,Genuine,don’t like amazon advertise thing sale stock bad experience year ago bought book like many people ticked free postagebeware click free postage inadvertently sign amazon primei know done change bank card security scare phone call amazon saying could process amazon payment horrified thought scam rang real amazon told signed amazon prime appalled cancelled amazon prime accounti gave card number expired card safe received phone call bt saying call amazon cost £bt refunded half goodwill gesture beware signing amazon prime click free postage lost several payment £ £