Vince,/users/60f0aa04a497a60012ac5b5a,CA,2.0,2023-02-28 08:07:24+00:00,1.0,Amazon: Inaccurate Information,"Placed an order (#702-5928005-0311437) with Amazon on Feb 25th, 2023. Estimated and assured delivery was 2 business days i.e. Feb 28th. For being on a safer side, lets consider March 1st. I also checked for faster delivery options as I am okay to pay an extra charge to get a faster delivery. When I checked the tracking its showing March 7th, 2023. I contacted customer service (Shalu and Steven via chat) I was told that the item was not in stock (when placing order it showed 7 in stock) so they would have to backdate the order and get it from a different fulfillment center. Well, if this was known to me when placing the order, I would have not placed this order itself as the vendor could get it delivered much faster. All the time the agent-Steven kept saying the actual estimated delivery time is displayed on the checkout page and also when you get a confirmation email that order is placed. I had canceled the initial order and I am very sure of no such longer delivery date was suggested. However, I still placed a dummy order (#702-0941180-8361033) to check their claims, now I have screenshots which clearly suggests guaranteed delivery by March 3rd on checkout page and also the confirmation email they sent me. When contacted customer service, they offered me $5 as account credits. I am not interested in credits or extra money. I want the delivery timeline promised/ displayed to be kept which they later said “it cannot be guaranteed”. I even understand that due to weather and logistics, things can be delayed so I was even open for Friday (March 3rd, 2023) delivery. But instead this is further than promised and customer service is like trying to prove wrong. Amazon was so good before.  After this experience, I canceled my kindle and prime subscription. I would never be taking their services/ subscriptions again.",2023-02-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,28.0,1838,319,30,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,placed order amazon feb th estimated assured delivery business day ie feb th safer side let consider march st also checked faster delivery option okay pay extra charge get faster delivery checked tracking showing march th contacted customer service shalu steven via chat told item stock placing order showed stock would backdate order get different fulfillment center well known placing order would placed order vendor could get delivered much faster time agentsteven kept saying actual estimated delivery time displayed checkout page also get confirmation email order placed canceled initial order sure longer delivery date suggested however still placed dummy order check claim screenshots clearly suggests guaranteed delivery march rd checkout page also confirmation email sent contacted customer service offered account credit interested credit extra money want delivery timeline promised displayed kept later said “it cannot guaranteed” even understand due weather logistics thing delayed even open friday march rd delivery instead promised customer service like trying prove wrong amazon good experience canceled kindle prime subscription would never taking service subscription,0.010704361496023605,0.9892956385039764,0.17891194615816042,0.2,0.8304302084836203,83.04302084836202,High Trust
Jamie,/users/63e40282d5de190014a87906,GB,4.0,2023-02-28 06:11:57+00:00,2.0,You’ll get what you didn’t ask for,"A decent selection and they had what I was after but insisted on forcing me to sign up to Amazon Prime if I bought the item I was after. When I clicked that I didn’t want it, the website simply ignored me and did so repeatedly. I barely use Amazon and I hate companies trying to force these things on me so I ended up deleting my account and not buying the item instead. I’m sure they’re not bothered, what with all the taxes they’ve dodged over the years, but I’d rather pay a bit more elsewhere than have Amazon Prime forced upon me against my wishes.",2023-02-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,28.0,553,107,34,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,decent selection insisted forcing sign amazon prime bought item clicked didn’t want website simply ignored repeatedly barely use amazon hate company trying force thing ended deleting account buying item instead i’m sure they’re bothered tax they’ve dodged year i’d rather pay bit elsewhere amazon prime forced upon wish,0.018324384572123934,0.9816756154278761,0.06001121704991587,0.4,1.1028400511239211,110.28400511239211,High Trust
