Cara Dschaak,/users/62bc56a796481900130ae382,US,6.0,2023-02-24 00:08:00+00:00,1.0,If I could leave a negative star…,"If I could leave a negative star rating, I would. They have MAJOR PROBLEMS with their system! I had ordered a CPAP pillow last week, paid for it, received it with absolutely no problems. Then three days later I received an email telling me my payment was declined. Of course, I was confused to what was going on; I  didn't have to dig very long to see that a completely different order of the same CPAP pillow, made on my account with my name, and the reason they were saying my payment declined was bc they had used a credit card (marked as the default card for some reason) I had on the list of cards I've used in the past that no longer worked (I had closed the account a few months ago); this ""order"" even had an entirely DIFFERENT ORDER NUMBER! This is NOT a case of someone anonymously trying to scam a free CPAP pillow; this is a case of THEIR SYSTEM making a random second order for some strange reason, and even tried to collect payment for it a SECOND TIME! And no, I of course did not authorize or was even aware of this! Actually, this has happened twice before, and I of course contacted them immediately and explained what was going on; the customer service rep didn't know really what to say or do about it, as she is just an employee earning a paycheck. But she would not let me speak to a supervisor or anything! She did not do anything about it, and how is a person expected to feel safe shopping on their site when they make random multiple orders at the person's expense? All I can say is I think IT'S A VERY BIG DEAL, and I'm not done making ""noise"" about it either! I hope everyone reads this, bc it's bad enough with all thieves and scammers out there, but you also need to worry about these huge shopping websites (Amazon has been around a long time and they're supposed to guarantee that you're safe) making random repeated orders and taking your money, probably hoping you won't notice? They've gotten too big for themselves and something is going on with them! I'd watch out with Amazon if I were you!!",2023-02-17 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,24.0,2029,381,33,7,7.0,0,9,1,0,Genuine,could leave negative star rating would major problem system ordered cpap pillow last week paid received absolutely problem three day later received email telling payment declined course confused going didnt dig long see completely different order cpap pillow made account name reason saying payment declined bc used credit card marked default card reason list card ive used past longer worked closed account month ago order even entirely different order number case someone anonymously trying scam free cpap pillow case system making random second order strange reason even tried collect payment second time course authorize even aware actually happened twice course contacted immediately explained going customer service rep didnt know really say employee earning paycheck would let speak supervisor anything anything person expected feel safe shopping site make random multiple order person expense say think big deal im done making noise either hope everyone read bc bad enough thief scammer also need worry huge shopping website amazon around long time theyre supposed guarantee youre safe making random repeated order taking money probably hoping wont notice theyve gotten big something going id watch amazon,0.9998074729100256,0.0001925270899744147,0.213684800897364,0.2,0.34283322372446,34.283322372446,Low Trust
