Mackenzie,/users/5d8df18735c3dff62172af96,ES,4.0,2023-02-21 09:15:12+00:00,1.0,Infuriating and Unacceptable,"I have never felt more disrespected or abused by customer service in my entire life. I'm not even one to write bad reviews...but I have to vent out my frustration somehow because goodness knows the Amazon support team won't listen. Long story short (including several phone calls, being transferred to several departments, and hours on the phone), I was promised IN WRITING a refund for an item I ordered. I was instructed to give them a call when the item arrived, and ""rest assured"" I'd receive a refund. I even called again to confirm this would be the case before making the order...and was assured. Well, the item was delivered. I call them up. They literally said. ""Sorry, we have to BREAK OUR PROMISE to you and we can't process this refund. Sorry, there is nothing we can do. I'm going to disconnect the call."" CLICK. That was from a supervisor. I truly couldn't believe it. I actually cried from anger and frustration. SCAMAZON is right. Avoid like the plague.",2023-02-21 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,21.0,969,170,28,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,never felt disrespected abused customer service entire life im even one write bad reviewsbut vent frustration somehow goodness know amazon support team wont listen long story short including several phone call transferred several department hour phone promised writing refund item ordered instructed give call item arrived rest assured id receive refund even called confirm would case making orderand assured well item delivered call literally said sorry break promise cant process refund sorry nothing im going disconnect call click supervisor truly couldnt believe actually cried anger frustration scamazon right avoid like plague,0.025281057660218265,0.9747189423397817,0.09534492428491306,0.2,0.8064284560268734,80.64284560268734,High Trust
