Alana tovar,/users/63eb2c72a1eac50013d77154,US,1.0,2023-02-14 11:26:08+00:00,5.0,Amazon is a great choice for customers…,"Amazon is a great choice for customers looking for an online shopping experience that is both convenient and enjoyable. The user experience on the site is simple and efficient, with a comprehensive search function and an easy-to-navigate layout. Prices are competitive and there are plenty of options to choose from. Delivery is fast and customer service is reliable. Additionally, Amazon offers a variety of tools and services to help customers make the most of their shopping experience, including helpful reviews, answers to customer questions, and idea lists. Overall, Amazon is a great choice for customers looking for a convenient and enjoyable shopping experience.",2023-01-03 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,14.0,671,103,39,7,42.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon great choice customer looking online shopping experience convenient enjoyable user experience site simple efficient comprehensive search function easytonavigate layout price competitive plenty option choose delivery fast customer service reliable additionally amazon offer variety tool service help customer make shopping experience including helpful review answer customer question idea list overall amazon great choice customer looking convenient enjoyable shopping experience,0.01893042538042022,0.9810695746195798,0.05776780706674145,1.0,2.002088348723138,200.2088348723138,High Trust
sweetpea,/users/63eae824eaecf70012c87fe8,US,1.0,2023-02-14 03:47:56+00:00,2.0,Goodbye Amazon,"I went to my Amazon account to login. I could not remember my password. I clicked on the link for the forgotten password. It sent the code numbers to my cell phone. I entered those, Then it wanted my expiration date to the card I used six months ago to purchase items as a security question. The problem with that is I got an updated card with a new expiration date on it. I never set this up as a security question. And why would they even think that would be a good security question to start with. Now they want me to make a new account. No I don't think so.Vendors that I was going to buy from just lost a sale. Any future vendors that sell through amazon will also lose money cause I will not buy through amazon again.Went through a whole thing of name, address, email, last purchase, and still told me they could not unlock my account. Goodbye amazon",2023-02-13 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,14.0,856,164,14,2,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,went amazon account login could remember password clicked link forgotten password sent code number cell phone entered wanted expiration date card used six month ago purchase item security question problem got updated card new expiration date never set security question would even think would good security question start want make new account dont think sovendors going buy lost sale future vendor sell amazon also lose money cause buy amazon againwent whole thing name address email last purchase still told could unlock account goodbye amazon,0.022487824822517138,0.9775121751774829,0.09197980931015143,0.4,1.1071520494507716,110.71520494507716,High Trust
Tom Jonas,/users/63ead88b9683a1001393a93b,US,1.0,2023-02-14 02:40:55+00:00,1.0,No interest in helping customers,I live in a condominium community with 180 units. Amazon made a delivery and proudly showed a photo of our order outside the wrong door. So I called Amazon and having fought through the automated useless response got to speak to a person. Who could barely speak English and was on a line with so much interference it was almost impossible to communicate. Having said they could not communicate with the driver (total BS) they cut me off. I have been a long term Amazon Prime customer and its so easy to just order it from Amazon. But no more! Too many problems and no response. From now on until my auto membership reviews I will work at buying from elsewhere and then cancel Prime. Amazon would not publish this.,2023-02-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,14.0,713,130,32,5,3.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,live condominium community unit amazon made delivery proudly showed photo order outside wrong door called amazon fought automated useless response got speak person could barely speak english line much interference almost impossible communicate said could communicate driver total b cut long term amazon prime customer easy order amazon many problem response auto membership review work buying elsewhere cancel prime amazon would publish,0.07387899744437125,0.9261210025556288,0.07291082445316882,0.2,0.7776426661684482,77.76426661684482,High Trust
Jerry Pyzansky,/users/563670100000ff0001e744a1,US,3.0,2023-02-14 01:06:11+00:00,1.0,I've been an Amazon Prime member for a…,"I've been an Amazon Prime member for a long time.  And in all that time, I've witnessed and experienced a progressive erosion in the quality of service provided by, and an increased lack of professionaIism, diligence, understanding, and/or intelligence on the part of Amazon's Customer Service staff.  Today was the worst, most nightmarish experience yet.  I had to return a malfunctioning Fire TV.  Everything went smoothly until I received the replacement TV today.  It arrived without a remote, power cord, or legs. Now whether or not I was supposed to KEEP those parts from the TV I returned, I have no idea.  None of the reps I dealt with at the time said anything of the sort.   So I spent over 3 hours on the phone or chat with Amazon trying to figure out the easiest way to get a TV that was complete and works.  I was transferred to various individuals (11 at last count -- and I was disconnected or cut off from THREE of those) all saying they would fix the problem to my satisfaction.  However, nothing ever ever happened and the only solution that they could ultimately come up with is for me to return THIS TV as well, and they'd issue a refund (when they're good and ready). Some of the suggestions provided by some of the agents were frankly ludicrous.  One actually suggested that I go online (on Amazon, of course) and order the missing parts, purchase them, and then request a REFUND for those items FROM Amazon! When I asked if she could provide me those item numbers (since she was supposedly affiliated with their ""special"" Fire TV unit), or better yet JUST SEND ME those missing parts, she simply ignored my request.  Especially when I asked why she thought it would be acceptable for me to PAY again for something that should have been included WITH the TV to begin.Anyway, towards the end of all of this, having hit the end of my patience, the reps wouldn't even listen to me, went into some spiel about how they are entitled to terminate their calls, which several of them did.  The follow-up emails I received were just as abrupt and helpless/hopeless.  So I'm sitting here with a TV that is no use to me; waiting for UPS to pick it up to return it.  And then -- once Amazon in Lexington KY gets it -- I'll have to wait a good month or longer to see a penny of what I've paid.  Frankly, I'm not holding my breath.  I've read the postings here from people who PURPORTEDLY work for Amazon's Customer Support.  One says that most of their reps are located here in the US.  Color me suspicious, but I highly doubt it.  One also says they DO have a bit of autonomy and flexibility regarding what they can and cannot do for a customer.  Again, color me doubtful:  all I was told over and over again today (from 95% of those I spoke to or dealt with) is essentially their hands are tied, and they are limited to what they can or cannot do based on their systems and its policies.",2023-02-13 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,14.0,2898,529,39,8,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,ive amazon prime member long time time ive witnessed experienced progressive erosion quality service provided increased lack professionaiism diligence understanding andor intelligence part amazon customer service staff today worst nightmarish experience yet return malfunctioning fire tv everything went smoothly received replacement tv today arrived without remote power cord leg whether supposed keep part tv returned idea none rep dealt time said anything sort spent hour phone chat amazon trying figure easiest way get tv complete work transferred various individual last count disconnected cut three saying would fix problem satisfaction however nothing ever ever happened solution could ultimately come return tv well theyd issue refund theyre good ready suggestion provided agent frankly ludicrous one actually suggested go online amazon course order missing part purchase request refund item amazon asked could provide item number since supposedly affiliated special fire tv unit better yet send missing part simply ignored request especially asked thought would acceptable pay something included tv beginanyway towards end hit end patience rep wouldnt even listen went spiel entitled terminate call several followup email received abrupt helplesshopeless im sitting tv use waiting ups pick return amazon lexington ky get ill wait good month longer see penny ive paid frankly im holding breath ive read posting people purportedly work amazon customer support one say rep located u color suspicious highly doubt one also say bit autonomy flexibility regarding cannot customer color doubtful told today spoke dealt essentially hand tied limited cannot based system policy,0.01500431475288607,0.9849956852471139,0.2966909702748177,0.2,0.8518360366785205,85.18360366785205,High Trust
Christina,/users/5ece9dcada677acefed2b2df,GB,19.0,2023-02-13 21:40:29+00:00,1.0,"""AMAZING"" AMAZON","God... no comments. I made a very expensive purchase on Amazon from an original brand seller. In the end, I received a very used item, you could tell by many aspects. So Amazon offered me a return, but for some magical reason I couldn't bring it to my local Amazon fresh, but only Ervi, and that's it, from the 28th of Jan, my nightmare started. Ervi provided me with a receipt with an invalid tracking number, so neither I nor Amazon couldn't locate the parcel. At least at Ervi, you are talking to real robots, at Amazon you are talking to humans which are worst than robots. For almost 3 weeks, I was receiving misleading information that I am either getting a refund today, tomorrow I am not receiving it, contact Ervi, I have to wait 14 days and will get a refund, and in the end no, bla bla bla. Not only that people at Amazon are either rude or using pre-copied text messages. I even visited the shop where I dropped the parcel and a lady managed to get through to Ervi, Ervi couldn't locate it and said to contact Amazon. Amazon on that day told me 2 things, first get in contact with Ervi, report it as lost and we will give you a refund, second 14 days passed you will not get a refund. Hahahahha, my IQ dropped during these conversations dramatically. Thankfully, I have a proper bank, so I made a report and my bank will be dealing with these m*r*ns at Amazon. I am a customer of Amazon since 2017, and only after the pandemic, I started experiencing worse and worse deliveries in general. Either I am receiving used or broken things, or my parcels are simply lost. Amazon, Ervi, DPD you name it, deliveries are getting so much worse, it is better to get it by yourself.",2023-01-28 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,13.0,1682,314,16,2,16.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,god comment made expensive purchase amazon original brand seller end received used item could tell many aspect amazon offered return magi