Joshua Cairns,/users/63e4694d6447140016cc5d11,US,1.0,2023-02-09 05:32:37+00:00,1.0,Banned when trying to follow the rules,"I started selling on Amazon last year, but because of water damage in my warehouse, I had to dropship some of the orders I had previously received. I then closed all of my listings in order to organize my inventory. A few days later, I got a message from Amazon warning me that drop shipping may result in the cancellation of my account. I took it seriously and carefully studied the code of conduct and all the restrictions. They authorized my course of action, which called for shipping all of my product to Amazon's warehouse rather than doing it myself. I sorted my inventory over the course of 2.5 to 3 months with no action on my account.",2023-02-07 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,9.0,644,118,38,7,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,started selling amazon last year water damage warehouse dropship order previously received closed listing order organize inventory day later got message amazon warning drop shipping may result cancellation account took seriously carefully studied code conduct restriction authorized course action called shipping product amazon warehouse rather sorted inventory course month action account,0.027263013541167228,0.9727369864588328,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.7996046121301454,79.96046121301454,High Trust
