MC,/users/62b3663c7b2a800013a4560a,CA,2.0,2023-02-03 02:35:01+00:00,1.0,"ZERO Stars for Amazon's Customer Service, especially those in the Philippines","I would give Amazon's Customer Service, especially those in the Philippines, ZERO stars if it were an option.Amazon's Customer Service Agent used to be good and helpful, but it has gotten significantly worst nowadays. I was talking to a couple of Customer Service Agents and supposedly one Customer Service Supervisor from the Philippines. Both agents and supervisor were not only rude, but they also didn't care if I wanted to cancel my Amazon Prime Membership due to my frustrations with the issue at the time of the call. Some of these people don't have the honor your trust that we are accustomed to in the West, and when we try to arrange for a return, they blame the customers for having to return an item that doesn't serve our purpose and charge return fees. One of the reasons I buy from Amazon is because of the hassle-free and free returns, being a Prime Member.As an Amazon Customer, I think Amazon can better provide service by employing Customer Service Agents who are local rather than from other places in the world.Today, Feb 02, I called again and spoke with an agent, who hung up the phone. I called about an email dated Feb 01 that I saw today, and I wanted to find out why an Amazon specialist sent it to me. It's even more frustrating trying to reach Customer Service at Amazon.",2023-02-01 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,3.0,1300,232,77,11,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,would give amazon customer service especially philippine zero star optionamazons customer service agent used good helpful gotten significantly worst nowadays talking couple customer service agent supposedly one customer service supervisor philippine agent supervisor rude also didnt care wanted cancel amazon prime membership due frustration issue time call people dont honor trust accustomed west try arrange return blame customer return item doesnt serve purpose charge return fee one reason buy amazon hasslefree free return prime memberas amazon customer think amazon better provide service employing customer service agent local rather place worldtoday feb called spoke agent hung phone called email dated feb saw today wanted find amazon specialist sent even frustrating trying reach customer service amazon,0.011020112864534803,0.9889798871354651,0.13011777902411667,0.2,0.8205134993725559,82.0513499372556,High Trust
Mr Grant Dickins,/users/549ae45f00006400019ff1be,GB,44.0,2023-02-03 00:29:30+00:00,1.0,Ordered 3 items from Amazon and none of…,"Ordered 3 items from Amazon and none of them was delivered , said online that items was received by resident, which obviously never happened. They told me I need to get a police report for them , police told me that Amazon need to contact them as it’s there issue as there drivers didn’t deliver , I’ve asked Amazon repeatedly to send me proof ( photo, signature) that item was delivered, they  said they have none. Now because it’s more than sixty days Amazon are saying case closed and I’m not allowed a refund for items I’ve paid for and didn’t receive. Isn’t that theft ??? They drag the process out and don’t get back to you when they say they will do so the case goes over 60 days . Will never in my lifetime purchase anything of them again.",2022-11-27 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,3.0,747,141,40,8,68.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered item amazon none delivered said online item received resident obviously never happened told need get police report police told amazon need contact it’s issue driver didn’t deliver i’ve asked amazon repeatedly send proof photo signature item delivered said none it’s sixty day amazon saying case closed i’m allowed refund item i’ve paid didn’t receive isn’t theft drag process don’t get back say case go day never lifetime purchase anything,0.016885787894989554,0.9831142121050105,0.07908020190689849,0.2,0.807373146433885,80.7373146433885,High Trust
