Esterina Marziale,/users/63a691137efb6900131834ce,CA,8.0,2023-02-01 05:31:59+00:00,1.0,Sent a used item and won’t take responsibility,"I was sent an aquarium light on promotional code from the manufacturer to replace a light that was defective. This light was picked and shipped by Amazon.  The light I received was used, boxed sealed with packing tape, no bubble wrap, no glass strip protector and dirty. I called Amazon and they told me I can return it but I get nothing because it’s promotional.  I told them it was picked and shipped from Amazon warehouse.  They won’t take responsibility that they sent me a used item.   They told me in the system it is marked as new.  I simply asked to send this back and they can send me a new one like they were supposed to do in the first place. They blamed it on a third party seller.  It’s also an argument with them when I have to return an item.  They use to use canada post, but now they use purolator, knowing that purolator isn’t as available in some cities, like myself it is a 30 min drive.  I told them this over and over but they don’t care.  The customer service people, wow, horrible mostly from Philippines and Indian, are rude and they can’t answer your question they get frustrated and the last thing I get, I can’t help so I am ending the call, they just hang up and then send a survey, unreal!!!All I asked Amazon to do is to send me a new light as per the company who makes them and the promotion code and I will send the used one back. Thr response was from all 9 customer service people (9 because they hang up) I spoke to was we can’t do anything about it it’s a promotional item. You return it you get nothing.",2023-01-31 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,2.0,1.0,1541,295,46,8,1.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,sent aquarium light promotional code manufacturer replace light defective light picked shipped amazon light received used boxed sealed packing tape bubble wrap glass strip protector dirty called amazon told return get nothing it’s promotional t