Dude,/users/5d29f664a4257a36e49b2e97,US,16.0,2023-01-30 17:17:21+00:00,1.0,When I attempt to sign into Amazon,"When I attempt to sign into Amazon, I receive a pop-up that says “Password reset required” which states that an OTP {one time password) is required. This is a 2-step process, the first is they send an email to verify that my email address is indeed mine and the second step is send a text message via my cell phone for the second verification.My problem is that I no longer have that phone number; I changed it when I moved to a different state with a different area code, from 606 to 850.Since there is no way to contact Amazon via my computer I called them. When I explained my dilemma to the person that answered the phone,  I was told that he (the person on the  phone) did not have the means required to correct or change the phone number and I need to go on line to perform that task myself.“Hello:, I tried and it cannot be performed that way. So I was forced to purchase my items via ebay, which I loath to do. Amazon….the balls in your court.",2023-01-30 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,30.0,951,182,34,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,attempt sign amazon receive popup say “password reset required” state otp one time password required step process first send email verify email address indeed mine second step send text message via cell phone second verificationmy problem longer phone number changed moved different state different area code since way contact amazon via computer called explained dilemma person answered phone told person phone mean required correct change phone number need go line perform task myself“hello tried cannot performed way forced purchase item via ebay loath amazon…the ball court,0.034056846142004125,0.9659431538579959,0.10207515423443635,0.2,0.8033866077758852,80.33866077758852,High Trust
