Stan,/users/63d320ba4a5c91001259d857,US,2.0,2023-01-27 02:54:46+00:00,1.0,Amazon lack of time management and transparency.,"I was supposed to get my delivery 2 days ago. Weather was perfect. Amazon sent a message saying it was delayed and would be delivered yesterday or today and blamed the delay on weather. We had some snow yesterday.  Not enough to stop someone from doing their job... no plows were needed on the road. Today, no delivery, perfect weather and clean roads.Now I  am sure I will get another delay notice.  No one will be home tomorrow and I needed it for Saturday. With porch pirates... I am sure I would have more issues trying to get a stolen item replaced.I am done with Amazon. Shifty delivery dates. Poor customer service... laughing all the way to the bank.Guys, Alexa is not worth it.",2023-01-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,27.0,686,124,48,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,supposed get delivery day ago weather perfect amazon sent message saying delayed would delivered yesterday today blamed delay weather snow yesterday enough stop someone job plow needed road today delivery perfect weather clean roadsnow sure get another delay notice one home tomorrow needed saturday porch pirate sure would issue trying get stolen item replacedi done amazon shifty delivery date poor customer service laughing way bankguys alexa worth,0.045040340335608955,0.954959659664391,0.06954570947840717,0.2,0.7913889717278769,79.1388971727877,High Trust
Thera,/users/636b9a20e01f360013b30833,NL,2.0,2023-01-26 22:23:45+00:00,1.0,Amazon.com customer service: A nightmare!,"I ordered an e-book (amazon.com) last evening, but after I pushed the button ’buy this book’ a small window appeared with the message that I already had bought this book a couple of years ago. This morning (26-1-’23) I got an email with an invoice confirming they had charged me for an e-book I didn’t buy because according to Amazon’s records I owned it already. I cancelled the ‘order’ with a request for refund. Amazon immediately started the refund-process. So far so good, were it not that Amazon (.com where my initial account is registered and all e-book purchases) removed the book in the library of my device (the one I already owned). As a frequent customer of Amazon's very 1st hour I loved shopping there (mainly books, paper versions & e-books). Its Customer Service used to be excellent. It was approachable by email, people working there understood what the problem was. Now it turned into a sheer nightmare. There is a chat option which is a complete waste of time. Spent exactly 2 hours reading hollow niceties such as “I really apologize for the inconvenience” and “I understand your concern regard the e book” and repeated ad nauseum, but the person was unable to offer a solution because he/she just didn’t understand what the issue was. After exactly 2 hours I stopped the chat because I had to attend a meeting.  A company that sells products under its own responsibility should have a well-functioning customer service. Refunds are not always the only solution. In my case I want to know where the (paid for) ebook is I bought a couple of years ago. The amount Amazon refunded today is the amount they charged me yesterday. Not for the book I already had and which they removed today. Just imagine a transaction with a much higher-priced product and a de facto defunct customer service. Inadmissible practices, Amazon!",2023-01-26 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,26.0,1841,317,41,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,ordered ebook amazoncom last evening pushed button ’buy book’ small window appeared message already bought book couple year ago morning ’ got email invoice confirming charged ebook didn’t buy according amazon’s record owned already cancelled ‘order’ request refund amazon immediately started refundprocess far good amazon com initial account registered ebook purchase removed book library device one already owned frequent customer amazon st hour loved shopping mainly book paper version ebooks customer service used excellent approachable email people working understood problem turned sheer nightmare chat option complete waste time spent exactly hour reading hollow nicety “i really apologize inconvenience” “i understand concern regard e book” repeated ad nauseum person unable offer solution heshe didn’t understand issue exactly hour stopped chat attend meeting company sell product responsibility wellfunctioning customer service refund always solution case want know paid ebook bought couple year ago amount amazon refunded today amount charged yesterday book already removed today imagine transaction much higherpriced product de facto defunct customer service inadmissible practice amazon,0.01820001176689017,0.9817999882331099,0.1777902411665732,0.2,0.8264580423498695,82.64580423498695,High Trust
jackie heizenreter,/users/62d8a0db768cb40017e665bd,US,2.0,2023-01-26 18:03:12+00:00,1.0,"Delayed in transit, AGAIN!","I am waiting for an order that was supposed to be delivered on Monday.  No show.  I got an update it was delayed and would be delivered on Tuesday or Wednesday, and to call on Thursday if I hadn't received it and wanted a refund.  It is now Thursday and an update says I will receive it tomorrow or Saturday and to call if I don't receive it and want a refund.  Seriously?  I checked the tracking and the seller shipped it immediately.  It has been delayed in shipping twice.  As of 3:30 this morning, it was in a facility about 20 miles away, (it was only 75 miles away yesterday morning,) yet it doesn't show out for delivery.  Why not?  I had other sites where I could order this, and chose Amazon because of the delivery date.  They lied to me.  If I cancel this, I will have to start all over again and wait longer.  The seller fulfilled their commitment, and this is all on Amazon.  I am not impressed, and am done with them.",2023-01-23 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,26.0,931,177,26,4,3.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,waiting order supposed delivered monday show got update delayed would delivered tuesday wednesday call thursday hadnt received wanted refund thursday update say receive tomorrow saturday call dont receive want refund seriously checked tracking seller shipped immediately delayed shipping twice morning facility mile away mile away yesterday morning yet doesnt show delivery site could order chose amazon delivery date lied cancel start wait longer seller fulfilled commitment amazon impressed done,0.036014854455906575,0.9639851455440934,0.09927089175546831,0.2,0.8018467511231404,80.18467511231404,High Trust
