Rayan Antoun,/users/63cb211b08738d0013e00a96,US,1.0,2023-01-21 01:18:00+00:00,1.0,Amazon Delivery doesn't really know how to deliver anything,"I have been a loyal amazon prime customer for years. I ordered an XTERRA 4500 Treadmill on January 9th, 2023 and paid the additional $99 for assembly and room of choice delivery. On January 13th, a third party delivery service ""JB Hunt"" Arrived at my door, and the delivery drivers informed me that the treadmill was too heavy to take upstairs, and offered to leave it in the garage. I informed them that I had paid for the room of choice service, and they said to contact Amazon to establish different delivery options. I called Amazon that day, spending more than 3 hours on the phone being transferred between multiple departments from account services, to heavy and bulky, to home services. During that phone call, the customer service representative in Heavy and Bulky assured me that Jb Hunt had no right to refuse delivery because I had paid for room of choice, and the treadmill only weighed 213 lbs. He assured me that if I reschedule the delivery, they will redeliver it, and that he could not change the delivery company. Consequently, I rescheduled the delivery for Wednesday, January 18th. On that day,  The same Jb Hunt driver arrived and informed me that they could not take the treadmill up the stairs. I contacted Amazon for a second time and Amazon apologized profusely and provided me a 20% discount for my inconvenience issued as a gift card, And reassured me again that Jb Hunt should have delivered the package, and rescheduled a 3rd re delivery attempt for the following day. On January 19th, Jb Hunt did not even bother to show up. Instead, the order was cancelled, unilaterally and marked fraudulently by Jb Hunt and marked as undeliverable for lack of access to the front door, which is NOT true. I called Amazon, and they informed me that I could fill out a special form with their heavy and bulky department that would specify that I do not wish Jb Hunt to deliver products to me anymore, and to re-order the treadmill. After filling out that form, and attempting to re-order the treadmill, I found that Amazon refused to give me the 20% discount on the 2nd order for my inconvenience. Honestly, after 9 hours of waiting through their delivery windows, and spending more than 6 hours on the phone with Amazon customer service to figure out how this Treadmill should get this delivered, I found it shocking that Amazon refused to carry the 20% discount to my 2nd attempt at purchasing the treadmill, even though I would have been able to get that 20% if Jb Hunt would have delivered the package like they were supposed to. In summary, Amazon delivery and logistics is a mess. The left hand does not know what the right hand is doing, and their third party delivery contractors such as Jb Hunt refused to do what they are contractually obligated to do and the customer is caught in the middle. Amazon kept insisting that Jb Hunt must deliver, and Jb Hunt refused to deliver and I wasted more than 15 hours of my life trying to coordinate between the two. I cancelled my prime membership because honestly, prime delivery is more like crappy delivery.",2023-01-20 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,21.0,3075,541,59,9,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,loyal amazon prime customer year ordered xterra treadmill january th paid additional assembly room choice delivery january th third party delivery service jb hunt arrived door delivery driver informed treadmill heavy take upstairs offered leave garage informed paid room choice service said contact amazon establish different delivery option called amazon day spending hour phone transferred multiple department account service heavy bulky home service phone call customer service representative heavy bulky assured jb hunt right refuse delivery paid room choice treadmill weighed lb assured reschedule delivery redeliver could change delivery company consequently rescheduled delivery wednesday january th day jb hunt driver arrived informed could take treadmill stair contacted amazon second time amazon apologized profusely provided discount inconvenience issued gift card reassured jb hunt delivered package rescheduled rd delivery attempt following day january th jb hunt even bother show instead order cancelled unilaterally marked fraudulently jb hunt marked undeliverable lack access front door true called amazon informed could fill special form heavy bulky department would specify wish jb hunt deliver product anymore reorder treadmill filling form attempting reorder treadmill found amazon refused give discount nd order inconvenience honestly hour waiting delivery window spending hour phone amazon customer service figure treadmill get delivered found shocking amazon refused carry discount nd attempt purchasing treadmill even though would able get jb hunt would delivered package like supposed summary amazon delivery logistics mess left hand know right hand third party delivery contractor jb hunt refused contractually obligated customer caught middle amazon kept insisting jb hunt must deliver jb hunt refused deliver wasted hour life trying coordinate two cancelled prime membership honestly prime delivery like crappy delivery,0.005094431638462185,0.9949055683615378,0.303421200224341,0.2,0.858137024225637,85.8137024225637,High Trust
Danie,/users/63cb144708738d0013e003d4,US,1.0,2023-01-21 00:24:10+00:00,1.0,I am planning to leave Amazon behind.,"I have mostly enjoyed using Amazon.  That said, I have found it very disturbing that they are going out of their way to steal money from my account by sneakily putting me into a prime membership. This has gone on for almost a year now. When I realize and cancel,  then it happens again and I was only refunded for one month out of 10.  I don't use prime. I always order over the free shipping minimum and also use subscribe n save.  I am going to find my way out of Amazon over this. They are losing a customer here.  It really is pure evil to steal like that.    They are not the only company doing this. Wyze cameras also did, and some apps will make it look like you can do a one month trial but then say you locked yourself into a year and take the whole chunk out before you see what they're doing. I'm done with internet shopping! (They can apologize and refund my money if they want my business.)",2023-01-16 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,21.0,903,175,37,7,5.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,mostly enjoyed using amazon said found disturbing going way steal money account sneakily putting prime membership gone almost year realize cancel happens refunded one month dont use prime always order free shipping minimum also use subscribe n save going find way amazon losing customer really pure evil steal like company wyze camera also apps make look like one month trial say locked year take whole chunk see theyre im done internet shopping apologize refund money want business,0.056842925585354934,0.943157074414645,0.0981491867638811,0.2,0.7912083745600987,79.12083745600988,High Trust
