Monica Rolan,/users/63c8a267c9a77600134eef77,US,1.0,2023-01-19 03:52:50+00:00,1.0,Amazon screws their customers,"I ordered some smoke detectors in October 2022 for $89. They had a black Friday sale in November for $59. I called and asked if they could credit the difference and they told me no, I would have to reorder and return the ones I ordered in October. I did, stating I found it for a better price. It was weird when i went to drop the item off at UPS store. There was not a QR code to scan and i had to pay them to print the return label. When they recieved the smoke detectors, they credited the ones I just ordered and not the ones I began a return for. I contacted them numerous times and they told me they can not refund the $26.67+tax difference. I made a complaint with the BBB and their statement was the same; they can not refund the difference. Interesting how a multi-billion dollar company does not have the technology to refund a difference of $26.67+tax when they make an error and instead the consumer has to pay for their error. I spend alot online: Amazon was my go-to but not anymore! Amazon has lost a customer.",2023-01-18 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,19.0,1025,196,29,4,1.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,ordered smoke detector october black friday sale november called asked could credit difference told would reorder return one ordered october stating found better price weird went drop item ups store qr code scan pay print return label recieved smoke detector credited one ordered one began return contacted numerous time told refund tax difference made complaint bbb statement refund difference interesting multibillion dollar company technology refund difference tax make error instead consumer pay error spend alot online amazon goto anymore amazon lost customer,0.05198547226261424,0.9480145277373857,0.10992708917554683,0.2,0.7959926817038021,79.59926817038021,High Trust
