Tom McElroy,/users/63bf561f91fcff0012be2751,US,1.0,2023-01-12 02:37:00+00:00,4.0,Amazon is an often hated occasional necessity...,"Amazon is frequently a lifesaver, delivering what you need as soon as you need it. I leave in two weeks for the trip of a lifetime, backpacking in Cambodia and Laos. I'm a professional photographer sometimes, and it was time to upgrade to include a professional camera drone. The inexpensive EXO Cinemaster II sounded like a great deal, but CAREFULLY reading Amazon reviews, I concluded it was a well-marketed drone, but NOT a great drone. The DJI Mini had many more reviews, almost all positive, so at spme extra expense I went with the DJI. I don't want to give more money to Jeff Bezos, but Amazon -even if you hate it- has its upsides, especially on product reviews and on the sale of unusual items. So, use it when needed, shop local when you have the option.",2023-01-11 00:00:00+00:00,2023.0,1.0,12.0,764,138,48,7,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon frequently lifesaver delivering need soon need leave two week trip lifetime backpacking cambodia lao im professional photographer sometimes time upgrade include professional camera drone inexpensive exo cinemaster ii sounded like great deal carefully reading amazon review concluded wellmarketed drone great drone dji mini many review almost positive spme extra expense went dji dont want give money jeff bezos amazon even hate upside especially product review sale unusual item use needed shop local option,0.019105931764676752,0.9808940682353232,0.07739764441951767,0.8,1.7059265630015652,170.59265630015653,High Trust
