HJ,/users/63368876345fab0014c3d427,GB,2.0,2022-12-01 17:59:24+00:00,1.0,"Anything over £10, just don't do it!","Amazon is fine for buying low value items,  but they really like to con you on medium - higher value items and have no customer service to speak of. They have their own delivery network, so you'd think they'd be able to reflect deliveries that actually happen, not claim that things have been delivered when they haven't. By getting you to pay for items and then only delivering one or two parts of those items, while claiming that they have fully delivered the order is clearly theft. No two ways about it. Their customer serive is useless, and they just tell you to wait (until you are no longer eligible for a refund). AVOID for any values that you can't afford to throw away.",2022-12-01 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,12.0,1.0,679,124,36,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon fine buying low value item really like con medium higher value item customer service speak delivery network youd think theyd able reflect delivery actually happen claim thing delivered havent getting pay item delivering one two part item claiming fully delivered order clearly theft two way customer serive useless tell wait longer eligible refund avoid value cant afford throw away,0.013212730795778397,0.9867872692042216,0.06954570947840717,0.2,0.8073027764977923,80.73027764977923,High Trust
