Terry Tosky,/users/5682c9d40000ff0001f7d9e7,CA,6.0,2022-11-27 13:21:12+00:00,1.0,I would like to leave a review for my…Amazon shopping experience,"I would like to leave a review for my last Amazon experience. Yesterday, I wanted to find/buy a remote for my tv. Both Amazon and Walmart had the one I needed. I checked their prices and could see that Amazon's was ~$7 cheaper (after shipping). So for about 4 hrs I tried to buy it on Amazon. I gave up on trying and ended up buying it from Walmart after about a 4 hr period of failure, phone calls, and frustration. It took me 5 minutes to do the Walmart thing, so I ended up buying my remote there.The problem was:  I had just moved, and had gotten a new phone # (landline). I couldn't access my account. I wasn't even able to open a new account. The main problem was that I don't have a cell phone (they want to leave you a text with a sign in code). They emailed me some kind of instructions that didn't work - From what I could see, if you have a new address, a new phone number (landline), and you don't own a cell phone, you are a second class customer and will not be able to access  any existing account or even open a new one. Good going Amazon. Actually, this has happened to me before also, which explains why I haven't been able to buy anything from Amazon in the recent past.",2022-11-25 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,27.0,1189,233,64,11,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,would like leave review last amazon experience yesterday wanted findbuy remote tv amazon walmart one needed checked price could see amazon cheaper shipping hr tried buy amazon gave trying ended buying walmart hr period failure phone call frustration took minute walmart thing ended buying remote therethe problem moved gotten new phone landline couldnt access account wasnt even able open new account main problem dont cell phone want leave text sign code emailed kind instruction didnt work could see new address new phone number landline dont cell phone second class customer able access existing account even open new one good going amazon actually happened also explains havent able buy anything amazon recent past,0.016328413276360438,0.9836715867236395,0.13067863151991027,0.2,0.8179715196658018,81.79715196658019,High Trust
