Andre Sinclair,/users/63750c3f8c912400126722fc,CA,1.0,2022-11-16 18:14:38+00:00,1.0,Amazon culls negative reviews,"Amazon culls negative reviews. After trying multiple times to contact a vendor, and Amazon about a defective item WELL within the sellers stated warranty time, I posted a 1 star review. I never have before, and rarely review with only usually giving full stars. This time the review was rejected.. first time ever. When I asked why, all I got back was there was ""suspicious activity"" in my account pertaining to reviews. Nothing about why, just this generic response. Laughably they sent me a link to 'amazon.ca review-guidelines' which is a dead page. They said this is to ""Instill trust' in the reviews when what they are doing is simply culling reviews of negative ones. Amazon itself has no path for a warranty issue, or to report one. So the seller can say what they want. If it lasts outside of 30 days they simply don't need to reply and Amazon will have their back. Pathetic.",2022-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,16.0,883,156,29,4,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon cull negative review trying multiple time contact vendor amazon defective item well within seller stated warranty time posted star review never rarely review usually giving full star time review rejected first time ever asked got back suspicious activity account pertaining review nothing generic response laughably sent link amazonca reviewguidelines dead page said instill trust review simply culling review negative one amazon path warranty issue report one seller say want last outside day simply dont need reply amazon back pathetic,0.010575920467542787,0.9894240795324573,0.08749298934380258,0.2,0.8122106376349891,81.22106376349892,High Trust
