J. Shirey,/users/6373a0dab74d4e00123ab859,US,1.0,2022-11-15 16:23:38+00:00,1.0,I won't go into all the awful details,"I won't go into all the awful details, because it's frankly not worth more of my time. The broad strokes are someone hacked our account we've had for nearly 20 years, changed the email & phone # associated with the account, turned on 2 factor authentication, & ordered 4 (yes, FOUR) robotic vacuum cleaners totaling $1700. My husband spent over 20 hours in one week on the phone with Amazon trying to get them to let us back into our account, give us our money back, cancel the order, etc. Supposedly they were having their IT dept go thru code line-by-line because they were baffled as to how someone was able to hack our account. Never got any answers on that account. The phone number & email address associated with our account had only been changed once in nearly 20 years (by us) - that didn't raise any red flags?? We've never bought one let alone FOUR robotic vacuums... THAT didn't raise any red flags?? They eventually gave us our money back, but our account remained locked, even to us. We routinely spent over $10,000 per year with them, more when COVID hit. They could not have cared less about retaining us as customers. No compensation for massive amounts of our time wasted due to their lousy security. No explanation. No follow-thru. I'd give them zero stars if I could. Now we only buy thru them when we absolutely have to have something & we absolutely cannot find it anywhere else, which amounts to next to nothing. Forget this place. They are the absolute worst.",2022-02-07 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,15.0,1483,265,37,8,281.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,wont go awful detail frankly worth time broad stroke someone hacked account weve nearly year changed email phone associated account turned factor authentication ordered yes four robotic vacuum cleaner totaling husband spent hour one week phone amazon trying get let u back account give u money back cancel order etc supposedly dept go thru code linebyline baffled someone able hack account never got answer account phone number email address associated account changed nearly year u didnt raise red flag weve never bought one let alone four robotic vacuum didnt raise red flag eventually gave u money back account remained locked even u routinely spent per year covid hit could cared less retaining u customer compensation massive amount time wasted due lousy security explanation followthru id give zero star could buy thru absolutely something absolutely cannot find anywhere else amount next nothing forget place absolute worst,0.00044707898886187276,0.9995529210111381,0.14862591138530568,0.2,0.8295016427826302,82.95016427826302,High Trust
Ruddyuddy - Travel Reviewer,/users/5e657612baa5183d221295ca,GB,18.0,2022-11-15 16:15:03+00:00,5.0,Always deliver on time,"Always deliver on time, customer service 5 star whenever there is a problem",2022-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,15.0,75,13,22,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,always deliver time customer service star whenever problem,0.18666192767238185,0.8133380723276181,0.007291082445316881,1.0,1.9081272526528723,190.81272526528724,High Trust
James Yorke,/users/5b36072c4de5666d34c85f33,GB,10.0,2022-11-15 15:24:15+00:00,1.0,To Amazon or not to Amazon,"Being an Amazon customer (for many years) they either excel themselves or absolute hopeless... there's no middle ground in my experience.As soon as the item has been dispatched they charge you, and when it doesn't arrive, it takes a few phones calls to get things sorted as the first phone call they always state (even though it has been delivered according to their system) please wait for x number of days, or if it hasn't arrived by xx/xx/xxxx then call us back.And there we have it, we have to chase something that hasn't been delivered in order to get the item we ordered and paid for. Then have to wait for either the item to be re-ordered, OR, we have to wait for 1 business day for the refund to go to our Amazon account as a voucher OR we have to wait for the funds to reach our bank between 3 -5 days.What's the point of being a Prime member? If this was the first time it happened it wouldn't be a 1 star, but as this has happened 7 times this year, its obviously Amazon has too much money to care about issues like this.It's about time Amazon started investigating missing parcels, each parcel or order has a tracking number, that tracking number can be tracked back to the originator who packed it, what vehicle it went on and how many parcels were on that vehicle at that time.So why do parcels go missing at our expense?Whinging over... Get a grip Amazon please.",2022-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,15.0,1377,255,26,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer many year either excel absolute hopeless there middle ground experienceas soon item dispatched charge doesnt arrive take phone call get thing sorted first phone call always state even though delivered according system please wait x number day hasnt arrived xxxxxxxx call u backand chase something hasnt delivered order get item ordered paid wait either item reordered wait business day refund go amazon account voucher wait fund reach bank dayswhats point prime member first time happened wouldnt star happened time year obviously amazon much money care issue like thisits time amazon started investigating missing parcel parcel order tracking number tracking number tracked back originator packed vehicle went many parcel vehicle timeso parcel go missing expensewhinging get grip amazon please,0.00856287770969286,0.9914371222903071,0.1430173864273696,0.2,0.8243220384306276,82.43220384306275,High Trust
