Andreas Schwarzkopf,/users/5e6186cda201d40b562d7534,DE,3.0,2022-11-05 22:43:08+00:00,3.0,My experience with a missing item was…,"My experience with a missing item was really frustrating, for days nothing happened they didn't even took my case serious. Then day after day I annoyed the hell out of them. I wrote them multiple times a day while complaining. I contacted the delivery company which is in my eyes partly responsible. They ignored me for whole 7 days. I also did contact the manufacturer but Amazon still didn't really feel the pressure. So I decided to annoy again and again and again and again until I had another idea. Let's just directly mail Andy Jassy the ceo of Amazon which I did next. I did mention that in the customer support chat and 10 seconds later I got reconnected to someone from problem prevention or something like that and then I explained to them everything again and then 15 min later I'm not even joking they organized a replacement order just like that. Finally!!!!!? But I have really mixed feelings about all the hassle you have to go through first until you mention Andy Jassy and suddenly everything goes really fast. Don't know how to feel about that hence the 3 stars. You should be like that without that I feel I have to pressure Amazon in such a way and annoy them until something is happening. Being relentless paid off but shouldn't be necessary to be honest",2022-11-05 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,5.0,1275,229,38,7,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,experience missing item really frustrating day nothing happened didnt even took case serious day day annoyed hell wrote multiple time day complaining contacted delivery company eye partly responsible ignored whole day also contact manufacturer amazon still didnt really feel pressure decided annoy another idea let directly mail andy jassy ceo amazon next mention customer support chat second later got reconnected someone problem prevention something like explained everything min later im even joking organized replacement order like finally really mixed feeling hassle go first mention andy jassy suddenly everything go really fast dont know feel hence star like without feel pressure amazon way annoy something happening relentless paid shouldnt necessary honest,0.9275557609779931,0.07244423902200692,0.12843522153673584,0.6,0.9619091638183506,96.19091638183505,High Trust
Sergio Satta,/users/5ad4e1ab4de5666d3408e28a,GB,26.0,2022-11-05 19:34:53+00:00,1.0,"Shame on you, Amazon !!","This company whom I’ve used for years as yet again let its customers down.Friday 4th, I ordered some Lavazza coffee capsules promised delivery for Saturday the 5th of November as a paying prime customer, you get some slight preferential treatment.Today, Amazon Prime van pulled up outside my address with a small parcel in his hand, only to realise that he’d got the wrong address and in fact was for a neighbour across the road. he realised his mistake and delivered to the correct address.As I was expecting a delivery also I checked on the Amazon Site to see where mine was only to discover my parcel had been marked off as delivered.The all event was captured on the cams around the property.My phone call to Amazon resulted in excuses and a refund. NOT what I wanted.This company has let its paying prime customers down again for the 4th time.Shame on you Amazon.I’m now, considering pulling my subscription to Amazon Prime, and buying my items elsewhere",2022-11-05 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,11.0,5.0,959,165,23,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,company i’ve used year yet let customer downfriday th ordered lavazza coffee capsule promised delivery saturday th november paying prime customer get slight preferential treatmenttoday amazon prime van pulled outside address small parcel hand realise he’d got wrong address fact neighbour across road realised mistake delivered correct addressas expecting delivery also checked amazon site see mine discover parcel marked deliveredthe event captured cam around propertymy phone call amazon resulted excuse refund wantedthis company let paying prime customer th timeshame amazoni’m considering pulling subscription amazon prime buying item elsewhere,0.03468312055474335,0.9653168794452567,0.09254066180594504,0.2,0.8011665720838174,80.11665720838174,High Trust
