Dil Pat,/users/5c38a0fe6a347a0f687dfd63,SI,10.0,2022-10-02 09:26:03+00:00,1.0,Amazon promoting scamming retailers,"Amazon no longer allows bad review of rogue sellers even though they deliberately try to scam buyers! The details are a bit mundane but here they are for completeness:The photo and description of an item listed on Amazon was the legal ""UK"" labelled sticker for a UK car numberplate. Instead, this retailer deliberately shipped the no-longer-legal ""GB"" labelled sticker. Presumably the seller had a lot of old useless illegal ""GB"" labelled sticker stock to be disposed of! The seller is counting on the majority of buyers not bothering to return the stickers they did not order because of their relatively low value. When a review describing the above was left on Amazon, Amazon refused to post it, stating that their policies did not allow criticism of sellers even if they are scammers as in this case. Clearly Amazon is not prepared to let honesty and protection of their buyers from rogue sellers get in the way of their obscene levels of profits. Shame on you Amazon!",2022-10-01 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,10.0,2.0,971,166,35,4,1.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,amazon longer allows bad review rogue seller even though deliberately try scam buyer detail bit mundane completenessthe photo description item listed amazon legal uk labelled sticker uk car numberplate instead retailer deliberately shipped nolongerlegal gb labelled sticker presumably seller lot old useless illegal gb labelled sticker stock disposed seller counting majority buyer bothering return sticker order relatively low value review describing left amazon amazon refused post stating policy allow criticism seller even scammer case clearly amazon prepared let honesty protection buyer rogue seller get way obscene level profit shame amazon,0.8240587419857639,0.1759412580142361,0.09310151430173864,0.2,0.40659093186746575,40.659093186746574,Low Trust
