Anthony Dunn,/users/58987fdf0000ff000a745b5c,GB,33.0,2022-08-31 10:48:51+00:00,1.0,Nauseating Gaslighters,"I ordered a OnePlus8Pro.The phone arrived with the perspex case and SIM pin missing.The fingerprint function did not work. Numerous calls to Amazon Customer Service were excruciating. I was directed to One Plus (arguably even worse) who directed me back to Amazon; back and forth with their disconcerting responses couched in generic public relations language. It is nauseating. A return was arranged and someone from UPS picked up the phone the next day. UPS tracking was great and showed the phone delivered to Amazon the next day. This information did not show on my Amazon account and the umpteen calls and chats mentioned above Amazon admitted they had the phone but ""needed to be scanned."" Their promise of a refund within the legal 14 days did not happen and no matter how I appealed they ignored me. I escalated the matter and further exchanges with customer services left me realising that this corporation can do what they like to you. With many of their companies registered in places like Luxemburg the ordinary consumer will struggle to get real legal redress as they fall outside of UK law. Some aspects of their soulless and robotic responses are sinister and manipulative; it is the framework of abuse, rolling you over while using saccharine phrases about how valued you are and have a nice day etc. They ignored me completely when I told them I was entitled to a refund under the Consumer Rights Act. I also explained I was slightly out-of-pocket, having bought a leather case for the phone.I took legal advice and was refunded through my credit card; a few days after this Amazon paid up. Something has changed at Amazon. Having to deal with their soulless robotic customer services is like being abused and their claim to be ""the most customer centric company on the planet"" is pure Orwell double-speak. I have the unsettling feeling that I've been gaslit.",2022-08-09 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,8.0,31.0,1876,319,22,2,22.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered oneplusprothe phone arrived perspex case sim pin missingthe fingerprint function work numerous call amazon customer service excruciating directed one plus arguably even worse directed back amazon back forth disconcerting response couched generic public relation language nauseating return arranged someone ups picked phone next day ups tracking great showed phone delivered amazon next day information show amazon account umpteen call chat mentioned amazon admitted phone needed scanned promise refund within legal day happen matter appealed ignored escalated matter exchange customer service left realising corporation like many company registered place like luxemburg ordinary consumer struggle get real legal redress fall outside uk law aspect soulless robotic response sinister manipulative framework abuse rolling using saccharine phrase valued nice day etc ignored completely told entitled refund consumer right act also explained slightly outofpocket bought leather case phonei took legal advice refunded credit card day amazon paid something changed amazon deal soulless robotic customer service like abused claim customer centric company planet pure orwell doublespeak unsettling feeling ive gaslit,0.026227093565772897,0.9737729064342271,0.17891194615816042,0.2,0.8226688424487457,82.26688424487457,High Trust
