Michael Kaye,/users/630650521cedae001264df93,US,1.0,2022-08-24 18:23:14+00:00,1.0,Amazons investigation team frauded me,"August 9th I order a mystery box for my sister's birthday for $45 tax and all.  August 15th I get an email from them saying that the seller hasn't confirmed the oder, I replied to just refund my money then. An hour later Amazon emails saying yes, the seller has confirmed shipping.. and now it's on its way and should be here August 23rd.  Check the status on the 23rd and it says it's late, but should arrive around 8pm. Nothing. Today, the 24th I finally get to a live person at Amazon, ask him where's my box? He said Amazon has investigated and the seller turned out to be fraud. Ok, cool where's my money I ask.  Then he goes on to say how on August 10th, the day after I bought the box, their investigation team has found it to be fraud but didn't tell me, but kept up saying my package was on its way, just give them a little longer. If they knew the day after it's not coming why the hell did they keep sending emails saying it's on its way?",2022-08-24 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,8.0,24.0,949,186,37,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,august th order mystery box sister birthday tax august th get email saying seller hasnt confirmed oder replied refund money hour later amazon email saying yes seller confirmed shipping way august rd check status rd say late arrive around pm nothing today th finally get live person amazon ask wheres box said amazon investigated seller turned fraud ok cool wheres money ask go say august th day bought box investigation team found fraud didnt tell kept saying package way give little longer knew day coming hell keep sending email saying way,0.030742658284543634,0.9692573417154564,0.10431856421761077,0.2,0.8054923837012503,80.54923837012502,High Trust
