Michael K,/users/5bd849574de5666d3461290f,GB,11.0,2022-07-14 00:15:12+00:00,1.0,Amazon is a company that just doesn’t…,"Amazon is a company that just doesn’t care about its customers.As a Prime customer, I ordered a new toilet flush for next day delivery. Admittedly, it’s an odd product, but after mine broke and Amazon had it for next day delivery, I placed an order.Very late in the day on what should have been delivery day, I received a string of emails telling me delivery has been delayed by 2 days. There was no explanation or option to cancel or amend the order. It was assumed I was happy with their sloppy service.This wasn’t a junk purchase from the Prime sale, rather something essential, and an item that I desperately needed.The tracking tool on the Amazon app continued to show delivery by 10pm and the phone system by 8pm but emails still insisted there was a delay of two days.Confused, I tried the text chat service. I got nowhere. Clearly, English wasn’t the first language of the representative, and responses were the usual scripted sort. The same was the case on the phone. Offshore call centres where staff without much of a grasp of the English language tried to assist. It was a waste of time, achieving nothing.Amazon is a greedy company, focused only on making sales, and with zero regard for their customers - and especially not the obvious fools paying a £7.99 monthly premium for a Prime service.Prime membership now cancelled.",2022-07-14 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,7.0,14.0,1338,233,38,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon company doesn’t care customersas prime customer ordered new toilet flush next day delivery admittedly it’s odd product mine broke amazon next day delivery placed ordervery late day delivery day received string email telling delivery delayed day explanation option cancel amend order assumed happy sloppy servicethis wasn’t junk purchase prime sale rather something essential item desperately neededthe tracking tool amazon app continued show delivery pm pho