Recordgirlie,/users/62c5adcb421e0f0012dddfa0,US,1.0,2022-07-06 17:44:22+00:00,1.0,DON'T USE YOUR CREDIT CARD CASH BACK W…,"DON'T USE YOUR CREDIT CARD CASH BACK W AMAZON! THEY TAKE 20% OF SOME CARDS!! I've had a good experience w Amazon and returns but I just signed up my Chase cash back credit card to use my cash back CREDIT, just to realize Amazon is taking 20% of my money!!. (When I use my other card, Capitol One Spark card Amazon gives me 100% credit but on my new Chase card Amazon takes 20%! So I've decided just to redeem my cash back at the credit card site on all my cards, just in case!) Amazon takes 20%! EXAMPLE; On certain cards (Chase for sure) If you have a $100 cash back credit and use it to buy something on Amazon they will only credit you $80 and keep $20!! Is this legal!? (Look at the place on Amazon check out where you get your credit card redemption and you'll see something like this. ""$32 total credit. $26 available to use w Amazon!"") That tipped me off and then I looked it up. Buyer be aware!!",2022-07-06 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,7.0,6.0,903,177,39,8,0.0,0,14,2,1,Suspicious,dont use credit card cash back w amazon take card ive good experience w amazon return signed chase cash back credit card use cash back credit realize amazon taking money use card capitol one spark card amazon give credit new chase card amazon take ive decided redeem cash back credit card site card case amazon take example certain card chase sure cash back credit use buy something amazon credit keep legal look place amazon check get credit card redemption youll see something like total credit available use w amazon tipped looked buyer aware,0.9999999661457208,3.385427915780781e-08,0.09927089175546831,0.2,0.3198541952782332,31.98541952782332,Low Trust
