Kirst,/users/627871e41b82d500111b2785,AU,3.0,2022-07-01 10:58:19+00:00,1.0,Does not take cybercrime seriosly and no respect for customera,"I am not a heavy user of amazon. Mostly because the quality of goods that arent froma big brand supplier are questionable. I recently had my amazon account hacked and amazon proactivly locked down my account but not before allowing one of four transactions progress to shipped. This resulted in >$1000 being charged to my account. Amazon are not taking resolution of this seaiously as my financial institution have determined amazon should be responsible for the refund. It looks like amazon would prefer to make revenue on cybercrime and fraud than support their customers with timely, clear and relevant managment of these cases in stressful times. It appears amazon sees more profit in supporting organised crime and probably facilitating money laundering or financing terrorism than it does in legal businesses and legitimate consumers. Disgraceful.",2022-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,7.0,1.0,853,134,62,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,heavy user amazon mostly quality good arent froma big brand supplier questionable recently amazon account hacked amazon proactivly locked account allowing one four transaction progress shipped resulted charged account amazon taking resolution seaiously financial institution determined amazon responsible refund look like amazon would prefer make revenue cybercrime fraud support customer timely clear relevant managment case stressful time appears amazon see profit supporting organised crime probably facilitating money laundering financing terrorism legal business legitimate consumer disgraceful,0.008730030440560286,0.9912699695594397,0.07515423443634324,0.2,0.8106658316669885,81.06658316669885,High Trust
