VW Tax,/users/62a43f09d5935e001260fe2d,CA,1.0,2022-06-11 09:07:08+00:00,1.0,The Worse Customer Service,"The Worse Customer Service - AmazonI was guaranteed a delivery on June 10, 2022 by 10:00 pm but the parcel wasn't delivered  Talked to two Amazon representatives right away and it was confirmed that the delivery date was guaranteed.  When we talked to the Supervisor, Kathryn R, she said she couldn't see that it was guaranteed and implied that I was lying.    She claimed that I couldn't talk to anyone except herself as she was the top of the management team so no one was above her.  She was not helpful and very rude.  She didn't help but hung up on me.  Though Amazon is a fast growing company, it is a long run for Amazon to learn and   provide good services to customers. The bottom line is never make a promise you're not certain you can keep, admit your mistake and rectify it.  It is okay to make mistakes as no one is perfect!",2022-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,6.0,11.0,837,155,26,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,worse customer service amazoni guaranteed delivery june pm parcel wasnt delivered talked two amazon representative right away confirmed delivery date guaranteed talked supervisor kathryn r said couldnt see guaranteed implied lying claimed couldnt talk anyone except top management team one helpful rude didnt help hung though amazon fast growing company long run amazon learn provide good service customer bottom line never make promise youre certain keep admit mistake rectify okay make mistake one perfect,0.17573789635787013,0.8242621036421298,0.08693213684800898,0.2,0.7295174791906667,72.95174791906666,Medium Trust
Latasha Knight,/users/62a403556d0355001102b501,US,1.0,2022-06-11 04:52:25+00:00,1.0,multiple occasions of non processed orders,Amazon have on multiple occasions not process my order! When adding a new card I always make sure to place my card as a default payment. Especially if that’s the only debit card on file! Why would Amazon try to use a ebt card as a payment? The ebt card is use only for a discount for monthly payments for Amazon Prime. Why should I be hold accountable for the system error? The CSR stated my purchase never went through because of a inefficient funds.. which not true she kept putting me on MUTE and when returning back to the call she would over talk me. So unprofessional. Items that was supposed to be for a birthday gift is now not happening because I order it on Thursday to arrive Saturday. Well here it is Friday and I’m just finding out my order was never placed. There is no system in place to let you know right away this fck’n sucks.,2022-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,6.0,11.0,844,161,42,6,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,amazon multiple occasion process order adding new card always make sure place card default payment especially that’s debit card file would amazon try use ebt card payment ebt card use discount monthly payment amazon prime hold accountable system error csr stated purchase never went inefficient fund true kept putting mute returning back call would talk unprofessional item supposed birthday gift happening order thursday arrive saturday well friday i’m finding order never placed system place let know right away fck’n suck,0.2419198945485635,0.7580801054514366,0.09029725182277061,0.2,0.6970995030902725,69.70995030902725,Medium Trust
Afi,/users/62a3fc420ca7ed0012737600,US,1.0,2022-06-11 04:22:57+00:00,1.0,Amazon keeps disappointing!,"I am so frustrated with Amazon! They keep increasing the annual cost for Amazon Prime and the service keeps getting worse and worse. I am sick and tired of them promising me that an item will be delivered by a certain date and failing to do so! If it is an item that you really need by a certain date it really puts you in a bind. Not only does it leave stuck without the item, but then when the item arrives too late, you have to deal with the hassle of returning it! They either need to start delivering items on time or compensate their customers for the inconvenience! I will not be renewing my Prime membership.",2022-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,6.0,11.0,616,118,27,3,0.0,0,4,2,1,Suspicious,frustrated amazon keep increasing annual cost amazon prime service keep getting worse worse sick tired promising item delivered certain date failing item really need certain date really put bind leave stuck without item item arrives late deal hassle returning either need start delivering item time compensate customer inconvenience renewing prime membership,0.9119094280419897,0.08809057195801029,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.35728140487973425,35.72814048797343,Low Trust
Brenda Berry,/users/62a3e04801ef0a001191a200,US,1.0,2022-06-11 04:15:39+00:00,2.0,SEEMS LIKE AMAZON FINANCIAL ENTRAPMENT TO ME,"I received the wrong item from an Amazon purchase and returned it.  The total cost of the item was approx. $500.   I have returned purchases to Amazon many times and the returned funds have always posted against my Amazon credit card balance.  This time the credit posted to a non-existent Amazon gift card.  When returning the item, Amazon preselected “refund to your Amazon account balance”.  This in no way indicates it is returning the money to a non-existent gift card.  To add insult to injury purchases were posted against the gift card vs my Amazon credit card so they won’t refund the remaining gift card balance to my Amazon credit card!!  This seems to be entrapment, as Amazon’s messaging regarding where the funds are being returned to isn’t clear!  It seems Amazon is intentionally using vague language in their auto pre-selected option for returned funds to ensure customers spend the returned money through their company!  If this is unintentional, Amazon should add “gift card” to the auto pre-selected return funds option so customers understand the funds will not be returned to their Amazon credit card used to make the purchase, but instead be added to a non-existent gift card balance.  The gift card was created at the time of the refund!  As I stated above, this seems like financial entrapment to ensure returned funds remain with AMAZON vs being credited to the Amazon credit card used to make the purchase! I believe any reasonable person would assume “be returned to Amazon account balance” means being returned to your Amazon credit card balance.  Especially since at the time of the return there were no other Amazon account balances other than the credit card, there weren’t any gift cards on file, and every other refund processed through Amazon had been credited to my Amazon credit card balance. When “gift card” isn’t in the sentence of the pre-selected option, and Amazon has credit card options, it seems like it is an intentional action by Amazon to be vague in their messaging to entrap customer’s funds and ensure more funds are expended through Amazon!  I rarely write reviews, but felt people should know about Amazon’s ridiculous refund policy/messaging, as it could really cause harm to families already in financial distress due to the resent pandemic and resulting economic downturn.",2022-06-11 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,6.0,11.0,2329,385,44,7,0.0,0,7,2,1,Suspicious,received wrong item amazon purchase returned total cost item approx returned purchase amazon many time returned fund always posted amazon credit card balance time credit posted nonexistent amazon gift card returning item amazon preselected “refund amazon account balance” way indicates returning money nonexistent gift card add insult injury purchase posted gift card v amazon credit card won’t refund remaining gift card balance amazon credit card seems entrapment amazon’s messaging regarding fund returned isn’t clear seems amazon intentionally using vague language auto preselected option returned fund ensure customer spend returned money company unintentional amazon add “gift card” auto preselected return fund option customer understand fund returned amazon credit card used make purchase instead added nonexistent gift card balance gift card created time refund stated seems like financial entrapment ensure returned fund remain amazon v credited amazon credit card used make purchase believe reasonable person would assume “be returned amazon account balance” mean returned amazon credit card balance especially since time return amazon account balance credit card weren’t gift card file every refund processed amazon credited amazon credit card balance “gift card” isn’t sentence preselected option amazon credit card option seems like intentional action amazon vague messaging entrap customer’s fund ensure fund expended amazon rarely write review felt people know amazon’s ridiculous refund policymessaging could really cause harm family already financial distress due resent pandemic resulting economic downturn,0.9982432296003753,0.0017567703996247408,0.21592821088053843,0.4,0.64406402737592,64.40640273759199,Medium Trust
