Doug D,/users/58e426f00000ff000a89abb5,US,2.0,2022-06-02 16:54:16+00:00,1.0,Illegally charged sales tax on exempt items,"I normally have very pleasant transaction experience with Amazon, but today was different.  I have ordered several clothing and shoe items recently and noticed I was being charged state sales tax.  These items are exempt in my state, so either the items were miscategorized or there was some other systemic issue behind the scenes.  When I contacted customer service, both reps I spoke with insisted I should fill out a tax exempt form.  I've never had to do this for any other retailers, and I do not believe I qualify anyway.  I live in a state where clothing and footwear is exempt from state tax.  Period.  I told them to cancel my order if they could not refund the tax.  After cancelling the order, the rep told me they would forward my issue to the tax review department who could look into it further.  At this point my order was already cancelled and could not be re-released, so funds are tied up, I don't have shoes, nor is the tax issue resolved.  All of this took 40 minutes.  I'm not happy.",2022-06-02 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,6.0,2.0,1004,181,43,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,normally pleasant transaction experience amazon today different ordered several clothing shoe item recently noticed charged state sale tax item exempt state either item miscategorized systemic issue behind scene contacted customer service rep spoke insisted fill tax exempt form ive never retailer believe qualify anyway live state clothing footwear exempt state tax period told cancel order could refund tax cancelling order rep told would forward issue tax review department could look point order already cancelled could rereleased fund tied dont shoe tax issue resolved took minute im happy,0.006485083902577764,0.9935149160974223,0.10151430173864273,0.2,0.8170603183964397,81.70603183964397,High Trust
