J.,/users/5de12df9153b7eea598dff02,CA,26.0,2022-02-21 19:45:00+00:00,1.0,Poor customer service,"I walked an hour round trip in stormy weather to the post office to try and return an item, for the return qr code to not work, it still does not work now, it says 'image' where the code is supposed to be. i walked home and contacted an advisor who booked a collection return as requested but neglected to inform me i would need to print a label. i do not have a printer. so i once again contacted live chat, giving all the details for the 3rd time, to go around and around in circles, with the hassle repeating myself to be told my options were limited. eventually they linked me to parcel monkey and after waiting for the details and putting them all in, the website then said it was not available at one of the addresses sent. then had to wait for details for an address in wales for the parcel to go back to. in all i've now spent 3 hours of my day off trying to return a 13.99 item, because amazon insists on refunding me the 9.98 cost to return which hardly seems worth the hassle in the first place, on top of the stress, and time wasted repeating myself over and over and trying to arrange a collection which does not require a printer or me walking another hour for a code which may not work.the return is now arranged but in my opinion 3 hours to come to a solution, where the customer had to do all the work, is absolutely ridiculous and it has been infuriating. I submitted a complain and they said they would refund the item and the postage which I had already paid for, which was already going to happen",2022-02-21 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,21.0,1517,293,21,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,walked hour round trip stormy weather post office try return item return qr code work still work say image code supposed walked home contacted advisor booked collection return requested neglected inform would need print label printer contacted live chat giving detail rd time go around around circle hassle re