Ivu,/users/5ed6ca07ef55d6f75aefdecc,US,3.0,2022-02-16 22:09:46+00:00,1.0,Buyer beware!,Buyer beware!! Be aware that Amazon returns that show when you are making a purchase that it will be free is an untrue statement. The free return is nothing more than a shipping label or QR code. Amazon has found a way to charge for returns and hit the purchaser with a restocking fee even if an item is an absolutely perfect condition. So ultimately your refund is less than your purchase price and Amazon doesn't seem to care about customer satisfaction. I have to believe that Amazon got as big as they did as quick as they did by doing nothing more than take unnecessary money from the common people who can literally not afford to be charged undisclosed fees. The practice of saying free shipping and free returns is not what they are providing so that is either bait and switch or certainly unethical.,2022-02-16 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,16.0,807,146,13,2,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,buyer beware aware amazon return show making purchase free untrue statement free return nothing shipping label qr code amazon found way charge return hit purchaser restocking fee even item absolutely perfect condition ultimately refund less purchase price amazon doesnt seem care customer satisfaction believe amazon got big quick nothing take unnecessary money common people literally afford charged undisclosed fee practice saying free shipping free return providing either bait switch certainly unethical,0.3443514648429561,0.6556485351570439,0.08188446438586652,0.2,0.6442011604556952,64.42011604556951,Medium Trust
