ellipse4,/users/5c33851f7add8a51697a7f1e,ZA,9.0,2022-02-10 07:40:12+00:00,1.0,Amazon.com in decline,"Amazon.com used to be an amazing company. Nowadays it is almost impossible to contact a human being. You have to answer lots of auto-generated, unhelpful, irrelevant questions or read lots of vague, unhelpful ""Help"" documents when you have a specific question.They have discouraged me from buying from them because of all this drama. Their website also often lists items that are out of stock in the search results. What must I do with that? I waste time clicking on links to products they do not even have.Then there is Amazon Prime. I tried it again recently (I used to be a loyal member)  but they made my friend drive to collect his birthday present after a major courier company that Amazon Prime used was not bothered to deliver the item to his house. Why pay for a service that does not even deliver something to your house? You have to spend money getting to where the courier company randomly left the parcel.Amazon is opening itself to competition big time.",2022-02-10 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,10.0,967,169,21,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazoncom used amazing company nowadays almost impossible contact human answer lot autogenerated unhelpful irrelevant question read lot vague unhelpful help document specific questionthey discouraged buying drama website also often list item stock search result must waste time clicking link product even havethen amazon prime tried recently used loyal member made friend drive collect birthday present major courier company amazon prime used bothered deliver item house pay service even deliver something house spend money getting courier company randomly left parcelamazon opening competition big time,0.016435684227088698,0.9835643157729113,0.09478407178911946,0.2,0.8107389722442796,81.07389722442797,High Trust
