Lubos Laska,/users/61f9e712ba984a0012e03066,US,1.0,2022-02-02 02:06:21+00:00,1.0,Video prime and Kindle unlimited,"Our Family pays for Amazon prime, video prime to watch and Kindle to read and listen books. Our family is very disappointed with services of Amazon. We have an unexplained issues going around, nobody seems to be able to do anything to help.  Video prime kicked us  out of the movie we were watching previous day ( which was part of prime video a day before), next day we had only option to rent or buy the same movie if we wanted to finish the same movie. We had  no explanation why or way to finish our started movie. Similar stuff  happen week before with amazon kindle when I was listening an audiobook (part of a prepaid deal) when suddenly the download was removed from my library. Amazon ""support team"" explained to me (not a polite way) that I have to buy the same book again because apparently the book was never been a part of the Kindle unlimited (which it was because I was listening it). I feel like they force customers to pay twice for services we've already paid for. We don't think it's legal and we're gonna seek a professional consultations.",2022-02-02 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,2.0,1059,194,32,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,family pay amazon prime video prime watch kindle read listen book family disappointed service amazon unexplained issue going around nobody seems able anything help video prime kicked u movie watching previous day part prime video day next day option rent buy movie wanted finish movie explanation way finish started movie similar stuff happen week amazon kindle listening audiobook part prepaid deal suddenly download removed library amazon support team explained polite way buy book apparently book never part kindle unlimited listening feel like force customer pay twice service weve already paid dont think legal gonna seek professional consultation,0.008671433203850767,0.9913285667961492,0.10880538418395962,0.2,0.8174253602348666,81.74253602