Brenda Adorador,/users/61f8eb7aafedc20013d891dd,US,1.0,2022-02-01 08:13:41+00:00,1.0,Amazon does not deliver,"In truth I have ordered items from Amazon that have been delivered. But it has happened 3 times that my stuff has been delivered to someone else, evidenced by the fact that I got an email with a picture of my stuff lying somewhere that was not my house. When I called to complain, the customer service rep refunded my money. The third time this happened, I go an email from an ""account specialist"" insinuating that I was getting too many refunds and suggesting I read their refund policy. I wrote back explaining what had happened. This was their reply ""Hello,Thank you for writing to us. We contacted you so we could better understand the returns activity on your account to learn how to improve your shopping experience.""We noticed that you have requested multiple returns in the last few months, and some of the items that you have returned were damaged, used, or not in their original condition.""""If you have any further concerns about your orders or your account, please contact our Customer Service team via the link below:""Nothing could be further from the truth. You actually have to receive goods to be able to return them!",2022-02-01 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,1.0,1132,197,23,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,truth ordered item amazon delivered happened time stuff delivered someone else evidenced fact got email picture stuff lying somewhere house called complain customer service rep refunded money third time happened go email account specialist insinuating getting many refund suggesting read refund policy wrote back explaining happened reply hellothank writing u contacted could better understand return activity account learn improve shopping experiencewe noticed requested multiple return last month item returned damaged used original conditionif concern order account please contact customer service team via link belownothing could truth actually receive good able return,