Diana Brown,/users/5f492cc1f4f0f334b91934fe,GB,10.0,2022-01-30 19:36:29+00:00,1.0,Terrible Service,Where to start. I bought a pair of Doc Martens from one of their third party sellers. I returned the item on 27 Dec. I left several messages for the seller with no response. I then contacted Amazon on the phone and they promised their third party seller team would be back in touch and asked me to email them back on the email they had sent me if I hadn’t heard in a week. I emailed back and it was not receiving incoming emails !?! So I wrote a stinking review because at this juncture I’m over £200 out of pocket which I simply can’t afford. They sent it back 5 days later saying I wasn’t allowed to comment on the seller. So I wrote back and said what was I supposed to do then? I was in desperation. Then got another email saying it didn’t accept incoming emails. Absolutely shocking. So I am now left with the only option to claim through my credit card. Amazon are simply not interested. I will think twice before using them again. Seem to have got very complacent.,2022-01-30 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,1.0,30.0,971,186,16,2,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,start bought pair doc marten one third party seller returned item dec left several message seller response contacted amazon phone promised third party seller team would back touch asked email back email sent hadn’t heard week emailed back receiving incoming email wrote stinking review juncture i’m £ pocket simply can’t afford sent back day later saying wasn’t allowed comment seller wrote back said supposed desperation got another email saying didn’t accept incoming email absolutely shocking left option claim credit card amazon simply interested think twice using seem got complacent,0.3519491865635192,0.6480508134364809,0.10431856421761077,0.2,0.6448891195617626,64.48891195617627,Medium Trust
