Andrew Lloyd,/users/58010b0f0000ff000a4d9eaf,GB,133.0,2022-01-05 13:32:19+00:00,1.0,Missing Parcel!!!! Driver ignoring me!!!!,"Today's order was just 2 stops away, van stopped outside my property, driver was inside the van for over 10 minutes, eventually came out, took parcels to my neighbours house, got back into the van, I was by this time, standing on my doorstep, then the driver starts the van up, and starts to leave, ignoring my waving arms and my calling him, he just blatantly ignored me. That ssus customer service and delivery station liaison have been in touch, very apologetic, but still no parcel.",2022-01-05 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,1.0,5.0,486,86,41,5,0.0,0,0,2,1,Suspicious,today order stop away van stopped outside property driver inside van minute eventually came took parcel neighbour house got back van time standing doorstep driver start van start leave ignoring waving arm calling blatantly ignored ssus customer service delivery station liaison touch apologetic still parcel,0.6031936050257515,0.3968063949742485,0.04823331463825014,0.2,0.5080498604147743,50.80498604147743,Medium Trust
Christopher Baptiste,/users/61d4b29189a8df00125b6a5b,US,1.0,2022-01-04 21:25:17+00:00,1.0,Amazon CS Gives False Information and Fails to Find My Package,"Amazon Pickup Mix-Up 1/3/22I had two packages that were supposed to be shipped out to UPS, one of which was an Amazon return and the other of which would not go through. The package that did not go through contained photos I needed to get developed for a music festival I took pictures for. I owed the organizer images, as I was on the media team for the event. These were to be sent to Georgia. I called UPS to fix the issue with the latter package, and then the following day, someone came to pick up a package. I gave him the film in error, thinking UPS must have solved my issue, only to realize that he came for the Amazon return, not for the film.Calls 1/3/22Following this realization, I proceeded to call UPS, whose representative told me they could do nothing, and bounced me to Amazon, whose representative also told me they could do nothing. I asked her if they could leave something that would let the Amazon shipping center in Virginia (where it was headed) that when they got the package it should be returned to me. She said that Amazon had no such system and I would need to wait until the [package made it to the facility. I asked her if she could put me through to the facility in Virginia so I could tell them myself. She said she had no such ability. I asked if she could transfer me to someone who could contact them. She explained that there was no such person. I thanked her for her time and called UPS again. This time, UPS said they would issue an interception order to stop the package from arriving. I thanked the representative and concluded the call, feeling relieved.Calls 1/4/22The following day, I awoke to find a message from my Amazon app which stated that a refund was applied to my account for my return. Frustrated, I called Amazon again and spoke to someone about the issue. I explained the situation and asked if she could get the package sent back to me. She explained that she was sorry, but the person who spoke to me last gave me false information. There was, in fact, a system of tickets that could be created to notify a shipping facility of a package that should be returned to the sender upon arrival. She told me that since the package arrived at the facility that morning, it has likely been opened, inspected, and the contents thrown away without me being notified. I explained to her that this was a departure from what the other representative told me and that the pictures on the film were for a music festival and were irreplaceable She apologized and said she would file a ticket anyway, just in case, but that I should expect to not get my pictures back. Despite the package being there already (complete with a shipping label and tracking number to aid in its location), she said it would take up to 15 days for the facility to even view the ticket, meaning my package would likely be long gone. She sighed and stated that things ""could have been very different"" if the first Amazon representative gave me the correct information. I asked why the system takes 15 days when packages are delivered sometimes in less than 2 days. She did not have an answer to this question. Frustrated, I explained that what was originally a mixup due to my lapse of memory has become the imminent loss of irreplaceable photo work and film rolls which were valued at a combined $45. I asked who I should speak to to get compensation for this incident in the event that I never get my film rolls back. She said that there was no such department and that Amazon would not offer compensation because the rolls were no Amazon products. I thanked her for her time and concluded the call. Less than 10 minutes later, I called Amazon support again. I was determined to do everything I could to get my package back. The third representative told me some of the information the second representative gave me was incorrect. She explained that once the package is received by the facility, it is not opened immediately but is rather thrown in a pile with packages to be sorted. According to her, it could take the aforementioned 15 days to find the package and a whole month to return it to me if they succeeded in locating it. She too, however, stated that there was a chance I would never receive it, before doubling back and sending me an email that stated I would get a confirmation email when the package was found.AftermathI am beyond frustrated with Amazon Customer Service. I was given a wealth of false information and every representative had something different to say than the last. No information was consistent and I have barely been given any real help. I am now gearing up for another call to Amazon, in an attempt to speak to a supervisor of some sort. I pray this will bring some sort of positive conclusion to this incident. Those pictures are unbelievably important to myself and my roll as a designated photographer for the festival.",2022-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,1.0,4.0,4881,883,62,11,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon pickup mixup two package supposed shipped ups one amazon return would go package go contained photo needed get developed music festival took picture owed organizer image medium team event sent georgia called ups fix issue latter package following day someone came pick package gave film error thinking ups must solved issue realize came amazon return filmcalls following realization proceeded call ups whose representative told could nothing bounced amazon whose representative also told could nothing asked could leave something would let amazon shipping center virginia headed got package returned said amazon system would need wait package made facility asked could put facility virginia could tell said ability asked could transfer someone could contact explained person thanked time called ups time ups said would issue interception order stop package arriving thanked representative concluded call feeling relievedcalls following day awoke find message amazon app stated refund applied account return frustrated called amazon spoke someone issue explained situation asked could get package sent back explained sorry person spoke last gave false information fact system ticket could created notify shipping facility package returned sender upon arrival told since package arrived facility morning likely opened inspected content thrown away without notified explained departure representative told picture film music festival irreplaceable apologized said would file ticket anyway case expect get picture back despite package already complete shipping label tracking number aid location said would take day facility even view ticket meaning package would likely long gone sighed stated thing could different first amazon representative gave correct information asked system take day package delivered sometimes less day answer question frustrated explained originally mixup due lapse memory become imminent loss irreplaceable photo work film roll valued combined asked speak get compensation incident event never get film roll back said department amazon would offer compensation roll amazon product thanked time concluded call less minute later called amazon support determined everything could get package back third representative told information second representative gave incorrect explained package received facility opened immediately rather thrown pile package sorted according could take aforementioned day find package whole month return succeeded locating however stated chance would never receive doubling back sending email stated would get confirmation email package foundaftermathi beyond frustrated amazon customer service given wealth false information every representative something different say last information consistent barely given real help gearing another call amazon attempt speak supervisor sort pray bring sort positive conclusion incident picture unbelievably important roll designated photographer festival,0.003896300500414117,0.9961036994995859,0.4952327537857543,0.2,0.8970984005069438,89.70984005069438,High Trust
