JS New,/users/61cf8596149fa50012fba236,GB,3.0,2021-12-31 22:35:17+00:00,1.0,"Nobody wants the disabled to run amok, on a murderous rampage with sewing needles",".... and Amazon are doing their honest best to prevent this from happening. Seriously, though:I ordered tiny curved sewing needles (that could barely be used to stab a mouse to death- but *I doubt* any body was buying with that intended purpose) and had to cancel when I was told that my citizen card ID would not be accepted as it is not a passport or drivers licence. I have not had a passport for many years and do not have a drivers licence due to my disability. Because of these policies I would have been refused delivery of sewing needles (for goodness sake!!!). As a disabled person I suppose I should be used to being treated like a child. But it doesn't make it any less of an annoyance and a genuine inconvenience.Amazon, I doubt you'll listen as you make it so hard to contact you but on the off chance: do you know that you have more than a few customers-who are not able bodied wealthy people- who cannot afford to throw money away on passports just for the sake of your outdated policies? A lot of us cannot legally get driving licences so that avenue is closed to us too.  As well as the disabled, many elderly people and the working poor cannot afford passports and do not have drivers licences.Unfortunately this issue doesn't ever effect disabled people with a voice (ie wealthy celebrities) because, naturally, they can afford passports. So I suppose the issue will not get resolved any time soon. On the off chance this is published, further more a fair few economically comfortable, able bodied customers will probably snigger at this; but do you know how annoying, inconvenient, difficult it is to be shut out of the rest of the world (repeatedly) but for a little consideration on its part. If it happened to you I'm sure you'd find it a headache too- and wish that people would listen.",2021-12-31 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,12.0,31.0,1810,325,81,14,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,amazon honest best prevent happening seriously thoughi ordered tiny curved sewing needle could barely used stab mouse death doubt body buying intended purpose cancel told citizen card id would accepted passport driver licence passport many year driver licence due disability policy would refused delivery sewing needle goodness sake disabled person suppose used treated like child doesnt make less annoyance genuine inconvenienceamazon doubt youll listen make hard contact chance know customerswho able bodied wealthy people cannot afford throw money away passport sake outdated policy lot u cannot legally get driving licence avenue closed u well disabled many elderly people working poor cannot afford passport driver licencesunfortunately issue doesnt ever effect disabled people voice ie wealthy celebrity naturally afford passport suppose issue get resolved time soon chance published fair economically comfortable able bodied customer probably snigger know annoying inconvenient difficult shut rest world repeatedly little consideration part happened im sure youd find headache wish people would listen,0.691137887167134,0.308862112832866,0.18227706113292205,0.2,0.49088646864301744,49.088646864301744,Low Trust
