R.A.,/users/61becd51fa8e3d0012a785f0,US,1.0,2021-12-19 06:12:54+00:00,1.0,Customer Service and Executive Relations team are worthless.,"Review DetailMember Services/Executive Relations Staff are a jokeAmazon.com1/5original star-ratingwaiting - MODERATION TEAMThis review is waiting for approval by the ConsumerAffairs moderation team.We count on members like you to help consumers make well-informed decisions about businesses or products.Write a reviewReview HistorySubmitted12/19/2021PublishedwaitingPUBLICpublished review 12/19/21I have had numerous issues with Amazon not upholding their part of the terms regarding my Prime Membership. Specifically the 2 day shipping/arrival guarantee. I can not begin to tell you how many times I have had to contact the member services staff only for them to be uncaring and unprofessional about issue resolution. Sending emails to jeff puts me in touch with their Executive Relations staff. Most of the time it is a waste. They come up with almost every excuse in the book as to why they can not honor it. Sometimes going as far as to actually blame me for not knowing the terms. Their solution has always been to offer me a Amazon credit (which in its own right is a joke because you can only use this credit for items sold and shipped by Amazon themselves.) No, I do not want your useless credit. I want you to honor the terms of your membership agreement. 2 day shipping means that you, Amazon, must select the proper level of shipment service with UPS that will guarantee that I will receive it in 2 days. That is what your 2 day shipping guarantee means as it applies to Prime Members. Otherwise, what is the point of having a Prime Membership. NOBODY and I do mean NOBODY in this company understands that concept. The last correspondence I received from them about this issue even said, ""further inquiries won't receive a response.""How would that make you feel hearing that if you were a member? If you said ""not valued,"" then you're not alone.If Amazon treats their Prime Members this way, then maybe all these horror stories I hear from their employees and ex-employees are starting to sound true. I can just imagine what it was actually like for the employees who had to endure or parished in their warehouse in Illinois that they didn't provide tornado shelters for. I'm willing to bet the stories being told about that are true.Amazon USED to be a great company. Not any more and it seems that Bezos probably doesn't even care anymore.Well maybe he will care when there is a class action lawsuit against him and his company for not upholding their end of the terms in their Prime Membership agreement.",2021-12-19 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,12.0,19.0,2518,420,60,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,review detailmember servicesexecutive relation staff jokeamazoncomoriginal starratingwaiting moderation teamthis review waiting approval consumeraffairs moderation teamwe count member like help consumer make wellinformed decision business productswrite reviewreview historysubmittedpublishedwaitingpublicpublished review numerous issue amazon upholding part term regarding prime membership specifically day shippingarrival guarantee begin tell many time contact member service staff uncaring unprofessional issue resolution sending email jeff put touch executive relation staff time waste come almost every excuse book honor sometimes going far actually blame knowing term solution always offer amazon credit right joke use credit item sold shipped amazon want useless credit want honor term membership agreement day shipping mean amazon must select proper level shipment service ups guarantee receive day day shipping guarantee mean applies prime member otherwise point prime membership nobody mean nobody company understands concept last correspondence received issue even said inquiry wont receive responsehow would make feel hearing member said valued youre aloneif amazon treat prime member way maybe horror story hear employee exemployees starting sound true imagine actually like employee endure parished warehouse illinois didnt provide tornado shelter im willing bet story told trueamazon used great company seems bezos probably doesnt even care anymorewell maybe care class action lawsuit company upholding end term prime membership agreement,0.005658943734261544,0.9943410562657384,0.23555804823331464,0.2,0.8442821377795321,84.4282137779532,High Trust
