Mark Diorio,/users/54601ab70000640001956b4a,US,10.0,2021-12-13 01:39:25+00:00,1.0,Amazon Hides Contact Info,"Wrong Delivery, Won't Let Me File ComplaintToday, 12/12/2021, the Amazon driver once again delivered our package to the wrong house. When I called Amazon customer service to ask how I could file a formal complaint, the CSR agent would not give me any information. Not an email, form link, nothing. Why? Because I did not have the email address of the person who ordered. Never mind that I had the order number, name and physical address, I must have the email address. I gave my email that is linked to my Amazon account, but no, not good enough. Please tell me why having the sender's email account is relevant to filing a delivery complaint? If you do research, you will see Amazon hides almost every contact number except Customer Service, whose agents are apparently trained to stonewall and block every call. I made numerous attempts to resolve this issue with Amazon, and each attempt was thwarted by agents who just kept repeating tired script.",2021-12-13 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,12.0,13.0,951,164,25,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wrong delivery wont let file complainttoday amazon driver delivered package wrong house called amazon customer service ask could file formal complaint csr agent would give information email form link nothing email address person ordered never mind order number name physical address must email address gave email linked amazon account good enough please tell sender email account relevant filing delivery complaint research see amazon hide almost every contact number except customer service whose agent apparently trained stonewall block every call made numerous attempt resolve issue amazon attempt thwarted agent kept repeating tired script,0.02342683886603431,0.9765731611339656,0.09197980931015143,0.2,0.806682542429013,80.6682542429013,High Trust
