Dan S Tong,/users/5501effb0000ff0001b0ebd3,US,23.0,2021-12-09 23:09:45+00:00,1.0,Amazon Decrepitude,"Amazon DecrepitudeI had trouble deciding whether to choose one or two stars for my review.In the past you could count on Amazon customer reviews to help you sort out whether a particular item was any good or not. Reviews would tell you about user experiences; how well the product worked, whether there were warranty claim issues, whether the item was suitable for a task, or even if a particular  vendor was untrustworthy or not.However, Amazon started adding Ratings which are not Reviews, simply some useless, lazy person simply giving stars (1-5) without any reason for the rating. Some products have tons of ratings without a single useful note giving a reason for the rating. This is especially infuriating when it comes to reviewing books. You click on what you think is a review and it turns out to be a rating, meaning there is no reason given for the star assignment. This is not very helpful to help you decide if you would be interested in purchasing a book.Later on Amazon removed all of the Comments that customers used to give additional information or commentary on a particular Review. This meant that warning about certain vendors failure to ship products on time, substituting products, shipping used items that were supposed to be new, or explaining why the negative review was a user caused, rather than a product problem.Removing the Comments on Reviews means that a TON OF HELPFUL information is gone resulting in the customer REVIEWS, are no longer as informative and helpful.Of course the worse thing that Amazon had done starting at least 10 years ago is that they lump reviews of different products together, presumably to make it appear that there are more reviews than actually exist. Whenever you purchase an product, you are invited, and encourage to leave a review, which is tied to the purchase of the exact item you purchased so there is no reasonable excuse for claiming that it is hard to connect the review to the exact item purchased. Amazon has all of the data that is needed to do this right.One terrible example of product Review LUMPING are those for Computer Hard Drives (HDs). Amazon lumps the reviews for old generation small capacity 500 Gb HDs, with all hard drives   made by a particular manufacturer with the largest capacity 18TB HDs. Now, the lower capacity HDs were designed and manufactured many years ago, using very different designs and components than those  newest, ultra high capacity HDs. These newest HD's that are very different from the older HDs, and use components that were produced most recently. We know that batches of components of the same design made at different times in factories may have quality control issues, hence Amazon's LUMPING practice defies reason and is DISHONEST.  Amazon will no doubt claim that their filtering menu takes care of this issue, but in fact that is false. You cannot evaluate the percentage of negative reviews (such as adding the two lowest star ratings together) without having these required data easily available. These are not easily found without counting every review. I certainly do not have time to do that, nor should that be required of anyone wanting to understand the review ratings. This would not be a problem if products that are not identical were not LUMPED together.LUMPING is misleading, and seriously dishonest, making it extremely difficult to make choosing a reliable product from Amazon. This practice should certainly stop, and the Review Comments should be put back if possible, and certainly re-instated.I have complained vigorously with customers support and even tried contacting Amazon upper management without success. Do away with LUMPING and get rid of Ratings instead of having Reviews! What will it take to get Amazon to fix these issues ?",2021-12-09 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,12.0,9.0,3777,629,18,2,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon decrepitudei trouble deciding whether choose one two star reviewin past could count amazon customer review help sort whether particular item good review would tell user experience well product worked whether warranty claim issue whether item suitable task even particular vendor untrustworthy nothowever amazon started adding rating review simply useless lazy person simply giving star without reason rating product ton rating without single useful note giving reason rating especially infuriating come reviewing book click think review turn rating meaning reason given star assignment helpful help decide would interested purchasing booklater amazon removed comment customer used give additional information commentary particular review meant warning certain vendor failure ship product time substituting product shipping used item supposed new explaining negative review user caused rather product problemremoving comment review mean ton helpful information gone resulting customer review longer informative helpfulof course worse thing amazon done starting least year ago lump review different product together presumably make appear review actually exist whenever purchase product invited encourage leave review tied purchase exact item purchased reasonable excuse claiming hard connect review exact item purchased amazon data needed rightone terrible example product review lumping computer hard drive hds amazon lump review old generation small capacity gb hds hard drive made particular manufacturer largest capacity tb hds lower capacity hds designed manufactured many year ago using different design component newest ultra high capacity hds newest hds different older hds use component produced recently know batch component design made different time factory may quality control issue hence amazon lumping practice defies reason dishonest amazon doubt claim filtering menu take care issue fact false cannot evaluate percentage negative review adding two lowest star rating together without required data easily available easily found without counting every review certainly time required anyone wanting understand review rating would problem product identical lumped togetherlumping misleading seriously dishonest making extremely difficult make choosing reliable product amazon practice certainly stop review comment put back possible certainly reinstatedi complained vigorously customer support even tried contacting amazon upper management without success away lumping get rid rating instead review take get amazon fix issue,0.061223865058266574,0.9387761349417334,0.35277621985417834,0.2,0.8399433114417023,83.99433114417023,High Trust
