Lewis Black,/users/61ade1f6f91d7200126a7dda,GB,1.0,2021-12-06 10:12:13+00:00,1.0,Last weekend I realised that I had been…,"Last weekend I realised that I had been paying for Amazon prime on two Amazon accounts. I immediately cancelled prime on one account and deleted said account. Later during the day, I realised that I had deleted the wrong account (it had all of my audible content on it), and went to the live chat to ask if my mistake could be fixed. The support was most unhelpful. Calls were hung up on, chats were redirected. The people I spoke to spoke poor English. This morning, I received an email from Amazon, stating that my second account had now also been terminated because I had been violating the terms of service. I am appalled at the treatment. I had immediately acted as soon as I had realised my mistake and I had tried to fix it. Amazon seemed to have no problem charging me twice for prime each month, and were quick to refuse their help. This experience really was a wake up call for both me and my partner. It just is not worth it to get digital content because, at the end of the day, all of the books and films I used to own via Amazon, are now gone.",2021-12-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,12.0,6.0,1057,202,40,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,last weekend realised paying amazon prime two amazon account immediately cancelled prime one account deleted said account later day realised deleted wrong account audible content went live chat ask mistake could fixed support unhelpful call hung chat redirected people spoke spoke poor english morning received email amazon stating second account also terminated violating term service appalled treatment immediately acted soon realised mistake tried fix amazon seemed problem charging twice prime month quick refuse help experience really wake call partner worth get digital content end day book film used via amazon gone,0.008583616716577588,0.9914163832834224,0.11329220415030847,0.2,0.818366632471773,81.8366632471773,High Trust
