gary deboer,/users/619410988bd2370012a433a2,US,1.0,2021-11-16 20:12:17+00:00,1.0,Amazon is NOT customer obsessed!,"Amazon has changed the navigation to watch your prime videos.  The navigation has changed more than 3 times in the last month where each new change requires the customer to do more clicks and navigate past other products Amazon is attempting to push.  It is really annoying. They really do not care about the experience as much as they rather force you through a maze to get where you want to go.  I have the same experience when attempting to listen to my music I purchased through amazon. Each time I bring up their player, it forces me to opt out of purchasing more products or services.  Unfortunately, this is common with a company that gets so big they feel there is not any other choice for the customer.  Lack of competition allows them to push their agenda instead of being customer drive.  Ironically, Amazon requires all potential hires to know the 14 leadership principles and core values, the main piece of each is Customer Obsession.  If they were really driven by the customer, they would have on each of their web pages the ability for the customer to either ask for assistance (from that spot) or allow the customer to rank their experience with that page as well as provide comments. And then take action to improve the experience.  What would be even more impressive is to allow each customer to build their own experience when they sign ow so they can have all their favorites (movies, music, orders, etc in one place) thus allowing them to remove the noise they wish to not see.  This of course impacts their bottom line since customer's would likely not click into the services or products they want to push.  Bottom line... they are customer obsessed but not from the customer's perspective but from their profit perspective...",2021-11-16 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,16.0,1750,305,32,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon changed navigation watch prime video navigation changed time last month new change requires customer click navigate past product amazon attempting push really annoying really care experience much rather force maze get want go experience attempting listen music purchased amazon time bring player force opt purchasing product service unfortunately common company get big feel choice customer lack competition allows push agenda instead customer drive ironically amazon requires potential hire know leadership principle core value main piece customer obsession really driven customer would web page ability customer either ask assistance spot allow customer rank experience page well provide comment take action improve experience would even impressive allow customer build experience sign ow favorite movie music order etc one place thus allowing remove noise wish see course impact bottom line since customer would likely click service product want push bottom line customer obsessed customer perspective profit perspective,0.0071341814739762,0.9928658185260238,0.17106001121704992,0.2,0.830644911506422,83.0644911506422,High Trust
