Lisa,/users/4ebec24a00006400010e6c6d,GB,13.0,2021-11-14 13:39:39+00:00,5.0,Love everything Amazon,"Love everything Amazon, sure there has been the odd hiccup here and there with an item but deliveries are fast and always when they should be. Generally speaking anything ordered for Prime delivery is of good quality and rarely have an issue with a prime item. Amazon have really seen the niche in the market to get stuff to customers when they need it and the range over all is massive.",2021-11-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,14.0,387,71,22,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,love everything amazon sure odd hiccup item delivery fast always generally speaking anything ordered prime delivery good quality rarely issue prime item amazon really seen niche market get stuff customer need range massive,0.03545613257099843,0.9645438674290016,0.039820527201346045,1.0,1.99023603915477,199.023603915477,High Trust
Bridget May,/users/613f57c89381e40013bacc8b,GB,3.0,2021-11-14 12:06:03+00:00,1.0,It's painful that this is the biggest ecomerce company,"Amazon is useful for getting items that are difficult to come by, or if you need something relatively urgently. However, their ethics (in disregard for both human life in their employees and the environment I general) are appauling. Their customer service over the phone is absolutely ridiculous, and the employees clearly haven't been taught adequate English to handle complex situations. It's awful that they have to read from standardised lines instead of being able to give a human sounding response. I think my worst personal experience with this company is with their blatant discrimination against non-prime customers. I bought a high ticket item that claimed to be in stock as a present. When I ordered, it was claimed that it could be delivered within the next week. But then I got multiple emails to delay the delivery, claiming it was out of stock (even though I had bought it when it was in stock and could visibly see the item listed as being in stock). My father is a prime member, and offered to order one to see if it would come a little quicker with their prime next day delivery. It was a last stitch effort and we didn't expect anything, but he went ahead anyway. The thing came the next day. Out of stock my furry beaver. My emails still said they didn't have any in stock. When I called them up to get a refund and ask why this was, the representative on the phone didn't understand what I was saying  and kept (clearly reading form some sort of q card) telling me that amazon is the best company with the best prices- price was not up for discussion really?! I got my refund but this begs the question of how and why this can happen. It is a legal minefield considering consumer rights, but with Amazon being so massive, I wonder if this is just overlooked thanks to greasing the right palms. Food for thought indeed.",2021-11-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,14.0,1839,330,54,9,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon useful getting item difficult come need something relatively urgently however ethic disregard human life employee environment general appauling customer service phone absolutely ridiculous employee clearly havent taught adequate english handle complex situation awful read standardised line instead able give human sounding response think worst personal experience company blatant discrimination nonprime customer bought high ticket item claimed stock present ordered claimed could delivered within next week got multiple email delay delivery claiming stock even though bought stock could visibly see item listed stock father prime member offered order one see would come little quicker prime next day delivery last stitch effort didnt expect anything went ahead anyway thing came next day stock furry beaver email still said didnt stock called get refund ask representative phone didnt understand saying kept clearly reading form sort q card telling amazon best company best price price discussion really got refund begs question happen legal minefield considering consumer right amazon massive wonder overlooked thanks greasing right palm food thought indeed,0.0316640618570414,0.9683359381429586,0.1850813236118901,0.2,0.8211842337938574,82.11842337938575,High Trust
Mrs Kidd,/users/5bdae17e4de5666d34a71418,GB,4.0,2021-11-14 09:00:00+00:00,1.0,Poor service and no care for customers,This week I ordered 4 items from Amazon (spread across 2 deliveries) and none of them arrived. I had emails to say my orders had been processed and would be arriving on particular days but those days came and went without the items being delivered. A couple of days later after each order I had emails saying the carrier was returning my items to Amazon as with absolutely no explanation. It was frustrating as the reason I ordered from Amazon was that I needed the items quickly. I phoned Amazon today after the second 2 items didn’t arrive to see if the carrier was having problems finding my house. The customer services man told me the first 2 items had been out of stock (surely that should have been flagged up when I bought them rather than take my money snd waste my time??) and the second 2 items were damaged in transit. I realise these things happen but it would have been nice to get an explanation on the day so I could have reordered the items and not be left in the stressful situation that I need to buy/borrow these items from someone else now. The customer services man was difficult to understand and didn’t listen to what my issue was (ie. that the items hadn’t arrived and I hadn’t received satisfactory communication as to what was going on). He just kept saying I was getting a refund so to just reorder. I wanted some kind of reassurance that this wouldn’t happen again when I reorder but I’m so fed up with Amazon’s attitude that I will be ordering from elsewhere. I’m left feeling that they are all about making money and customer care isn’t important to them.,2021-11-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,14.0,1586,290,38,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,week ordered item amazon spread across delivery none arrived email say order processed would arriving particular day day came went without item delivered couple day later order email saying carrier returning item amazon absolutely explanation frustrating reason ordered amazon needed item quickly phoned amazon today second item didn’t arrive see carrier problem finding house customer service man told first item stock surely flagged bought rather take money snd waste time second item damaged transit realise thing happen would nice get explanation day could reordered item left stressful situation need buyborrow item someone else customer service man difficult understand didn’t listen issue ie item hadn’t arrived hadn’t received satisfactory communication going kept saying getting refund reorder wanted kind reassurance wouldn’t happen reorder i’m fed amazon’s attitude ordering elsewhere i’m left feeling making money customer care isn’t important,0.005512950491599547,0.9944870495084005,0.16264722378014582,0.2,0.8297729695102294,82.97729695102294,High Trust
CPR,/users/6190b744ebf38a0012a9d241,US,1.0,2021-11-14 07:14:39+00:00,2.0,Amazon has gone downhill,Amazon has gone downhill. My last several orders have been late and I even had to cancel some. It sucks to see something that's supposedly guaranteed to be delivered by a certain time be tracked to be sitting in their distribution center 30 minutes away but still be delivered three days late. They say you're recourse is to be refunded your delivery fee but it's supposedly free with prime so your stuff is late and you no recourse. Makes me wonder if it's worth keeping my prime membership. Maybe if everybody cancelled their membership they'd get the clue and start doing better.,2021-11-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,14.0,582,102,24,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon gone downhill last several order late even cancel suck see something thats supposedly guaranteed delivered certain time tracked sitting distribution center minute away still delivered three day late say youre recourse refunded delivery fee supposedly free prime stuff late recourse make wonder worth keeping prime membership maybe everybody cancelled membership theyd get clue start better,0.04414688870420469,0.9558531112957953,0.05720695457094784,0.4,1.0893679465620871,108.93679465620872,High Trust
