D F,/users/618d2788720ea900130dcccf,US,2.0,2021-11-11 14:25:06+00:00,1.0,Underhanded marketing,"Amazon disguised it's philanthropy through unwanted marketing. Amazon has a program called amazon smile, where part of your purchase can be donated to a charity of your choice if you opt into the program. However, Amazon only allows you to participate in donating to these charities if you have your notifications turned on, which allows Amazon to send marketing messages--a suggestive sales technique. If you turn off notifications, amazon turns off your ability to donate part of your purchase to charities.",2021-11-11 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,11.0,509,81,21,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon disguised philanthropy unwanted marketing amazon program called amazon smile part purchase donated charity choice opt program however amazon allows participate donating charity notification turned allows amazon send marketing messagesa suggestive sale technique turn notification amazon turn ability donate part purchase charity,0.028316894395421448,0.9716831056045786,0.045429052159282106,0.2,0.7949273632341457,79.49273632341458,High Trust
