Cindy Rella,/users/5babe24e4de5666d34a6ad78,FR,4.0,2021-11-09 07:31:39+00:00,1.0,Horrible Customer Service - Used Items Sold As New,"I used to love Amazon and I used to buy on the website on a regular. I am also a prime member and I have always enjoyed shopping on their website. However, early 2021, their customer support became very unfriendly, with a huge lack of knowledge about the company's policies.Amazon is also sending used items that are often defective to clients who purchased new items on their website. (These used items are those returned by previous customers, unhappy with their purchase). When the clients discover the plot and wants to return the used item, Amazon is now charging them with a 50% restocking fee. These fraudulent practices need to stop and Amazon need to be investigated. So beware of the ""Sent by Amazon"" as this is where it all takes place. One advice to the readers: if you have to purchase electronics or anything of value, try to locate the seller outside Amazon and purchase from them directly. This will prevent Amazon to send you used and defective items.",2021-11-08 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,9.0,968,169,50,9,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used love amazon used buy website regular also prime member always enjoyed shopping website however early customer support became unfriendly huge lack knowledge company policiesamazon also sending used item often defective client purchased new item website used item returned previous customer unhappy purchase client discover plot want return used item amazon charging restocking fee fraudulent practice need stop amazon need investigated beware sent amazon take place one advice reader purchase electronics anything value try locate seller outside amazon purchase directly prevent amazon send used defective item,0.003879964705028435,0.9961200352949716,0.09478407178911946,0.2,0.8170168320053097,81.70168320053097,High Trust
Mark Cregger,/users/618989851dbcc80012baaa1b,US,1.0,2021-11-08 20:33:19+00:00,1.0,Poor Customer Service. Broken Agreements,"Amazon charges for Prime service, then offers 2 and 3 day shipping as a benefit for your paying more that $100 annually for it.  However, they reserve the right to break this agreement when it suits them. If for whatever reason they can't get your item to you within the time stated (even though it's listed as a prime item) the excuses from customer service vary from ""The item wasn't in one of our depots"" to ""This item has been delayed and hasn't reached your local facility"" or just plain lies promising the delivery will make it the next day. So don't count on, or expect an item to be delivered when promised. And don't expect to be treated like a ""Prime"" customer when you call for answers. Their customer service supervisors will be rude when they feel like it, and just hang up on you if they want and apparently there's no path of escalation for this behavior. I've canceled all of my recurring subscriptions and will cancel my Prime membership before it renews. Amazon is very convenient, but it's not worth the frustration, stress and rude treatment I've received from their customer service team.",2021-11-08 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,8.0,1109,196,40,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon charge prime service offer day shipping benefit paying annually however reserve right break agreement suit whatever reason cant get item within time stated even though listed prime item excuse customer service vary item wasnt one depot item delayed hasnt reached local facility plain lie promising delivery make next day dont count expect item delivered promised dont expect treated like prime customer call answer customer service supervisor rude feel like hang want apparently there path escalation behavior ive canceled recurring subscription cancel prime membership renews amazon convenient worth frustration stress rude treatment ive received customer service team,0.010545822386357474,0.9894541776136425,0.10992708917554683,0.2,0.8167125066419305,81.67125066419305,High Trust
