Holly G McDonald,/users/5f9f2651f39a01001abf8c73,US,2.0,2021-10-29 23:04:32+00:00,1.0,This morning I found a group packages…,"This morning I found a group packages left on the corner of my yard right next to a public sidewalk. Five Amazon Prime packages, for addresses other than mine, had been dumped on my property by, I presume, the Amazon Prime delivery person. I called Amazon Customer Service and spoke to a representative who was argumentative and unhelpful. I explained that these were all Prime packages for people who were paying Amazon a subscription fee in order to ensure quick, safe, responsible delivery. I told her that I live a 15-minute drive away from the Robbinsville, NJ Amazon Warehouse Fulfillment Center at 50 Canton Way and did not understand why this problem could not be resolved today. The Customer Service rep said she would file a report, but did not ask for any of the tracking numbers for the packages. She then told me just to leave the packages outside and someone would be by-- sometime--to pick them up. I waited all day for that to happen.Late this afternoon I called Amazon Customer Service again. This representative was more pleasant and helpful. Apparently, the first Customer Service rep with whom I had spoken did not even file a report when this rep looked to find it. This second rep took tracking numbers with which to file a report and said it would take three days for a pickup to happen for redelivery, which is Amazon's policy, even for Prime subscribers! Again, I said that was unacceptable. For example, Amazon now delivers prescription medications and what if someone is waiting for a prescription to be delivered. I told the rep a three-day redelivery for Prime does not make sense, is bad business, and that I would deliver four of the five packages to the houses whose locations in my neighborhood I know. As for the fifth package, Amazon will actually have to have someone do their job and come to pick it up for redelivery. I also expressed that I do not work for Amazon. With that being said however, the four packages I said I would deliver are now at their correct addresses.Amazon Prime buyer/subscriber beware. I would have left a rating of ""zero"" if that had been an option. Perhaps Amazon's founder and former CEO, instead of now spending billions of dollars looking for a new planet on which to live (funded in part by Amazon Prime subscribers), should have ensured that Amazon's workforce is valued, not recklessly overworked, that the employees are responsible, and Amazon has logical, work-flow procedures in place in order to deal with problems that are not so difficult to solve.",2021-10-29 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,29.0,2524,436,38,7,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,morning found group package left corner yard right next public sidewalk five amazon prime package address mine dumped property presume amazon prime delivery person called amazon customer service spoke representative argumentative unhelpful explained prime package people paying amazon subscription fee order ensure quick safe responsible delivery told live minute drive away robbinsville nj amazon warehouse fulfillment center canton way understand problem could resolved today customer service rep said would file report ask tracking number package told leave package outside someone would sometimeto pick waited day happenlate afternoon called amazon customer service representative pleasant helpful apparently first customer service rep spoken even file report rep looked find second rep took tracking number file report said would take three day pickup happen redelivery amazon policy even prime subscriber said unacceptable example amazon delivers prescription medication someone waiting prescription delivered told rep threeday redelivery prime make sense bad business would deliver four five package house whose location neighborhood know fifth package amazon actually someone job come pick redelivery also expressed work amazon said however four package said would deliver correct addressesamazon prime buyersubscriber beware would left rating zero option perhaps amazon founder former ceo instead spending billion dollar looking new planet live funded part amazon prime subscriber ensured amazon workforce valued recklessly overworked employee responsible amazon logical workflow procedure place order deal problem difficult solve,0.02154339758630538,0.9784566024136946,0.24453168816601234,0.2,0.8381346388400498,83.81346388400497,High Trust
