A Kelley,/users/5dcc662917e36efd902ab30d,US,5.0,2021-10-30 12:33:39+00:00,2.0,"Nope, not me!","Was a customer for years, bought hundreds of items. Only returned maybe 3 things out of hundreds. Started receiving household items on order every few months (subscribe and save). Did this since start of pandemic. This last month, I received 2 of the 3 items on order (after a year and a half of no complaints from me to Amazon). So, as anyone who is busy does, I disputed the charge for the not received 3rd  item with my credit card company. Never done this with Amazon before, but I did not have an hour or more to deal with their customer service and just wanted it resolved. Received email threatening they would no longer sell to me until I removed the dispute with my credit card company and paid for the item I didn't receive. Sorry Amazon.. But I deleted my account immediately, ordered a new credit card, etc.. and will never order on your site again. After years, and hundreds of orders.. Being forced to pay for something I did not receive will NEVER happen. Keep doing this to people and pretty soon your customer base will dissipate. Good luck with that!",2021-10-27 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,30.0,1068,194,13,3,3.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,customer year bought hundred item returned maybe thing hundred started receiving household item order every month subscribe save since start pandemic last month received item order year half complaint amazon anyone busy disputed charge received rd item credit card company never done amazon hour deal customer service wanted resolved received email threatening would longer sell removed dispute credit card company paid item didnt receive sorry amazon deleted account immediately ordered new credit card etc never order site year hundred order forced pay something receive never happen keep people pretty soon customer base dissipate good luck,0.05381003314833886,0.9461899668516611,0.10880538418395962,0.4,1.0948560602626225,109.48560602626225,High Trust
