Robert Allen,/users/610483b1f713d20012c5930a,US,2.0,2021-10-21 07:18:03+00:00,1.0,Attempted ripoff,"I ordered a new Seiko watch and received a refurbished watch that wasn't good enough to return to the original owner after being repaired.  The watch I ordered was supposed to come in a nice box, suitable for gifting as I intended.  Instead I got a watch on a small pillow in a plastic bag.  Inside the bag with the watch were documents detailing repairs done for a customer about seven months ago.  In the comment box on a form entitled Inspection/Service/Repair Form, it states ""Scratches on crystal.  Scratches and dents on bezel and case.  Inspect, sending a replacement watch.""  UNBELIEVABLE.  The first purchaser got a NEW watch; I got the watch that was not good enough to send back to the original owner.  Amazon almost certainly shipped this junk watch on purpose, probably playing the odds that the recipient would be too lazy to return it.  Since it was not in a box as a new Seiko would be, it stood out like a sore thumb.  It's not like somebody at Amazon grabbed the wrong watch by mistake.  Obviously, I am sending the junk watch back, but Amazon's return policy doesn't make up for this attempted swindle.  I still have to take my time, effort, and gas to get to the UPS store so I can send it back.  I stopped using Amazon about 4 years ago because of repeated shipping problems and only recently decided to try again.  My mistake, I guess.",2021-10-21 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,21.0,1357,244,16,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered new seiko watch received refurbished watch wasnt good enough return original owner repaired watch ordered supposed come nice box suitable gifting intended instead got watch small pillow plastic bag inside bag watch document detailing repair done customer seven month ago comment box form entitled inspectionservicerepair form state scratch crystal scratch dent bezel case inspect sending replacement watch unbelievable first purchaser got new watch got watch good enough send back original owner amazon almost certainly shipped junk watch purpose probably playing odds recipient would lazy return since box new seiko would stood like sore thumb like somebody amazon grabbed wrong watch mistake obviously sending junk watch back amazon return policy doesnt make attempted swindle still take time effort gas get ups store send back stopped using amazon year ago repeated shipping problem recently decided try mistake guess,0.01253995713153277,0.9874600428684672,0.13684800897363994,0.2,0.8210996232289616,82.10996232289615,High Trust
Chirag,/users/615d5fbd30a1f90012ebc5ce,IN,6.0,2021-10-21 05:52:01+00:00,1.0,BOYCOTT AMAZON ALREADY!,"Amazon actually proves that the Customer is no longer the king and that you're only there to give them profits. Here's a breakdown of what Amazon stands for today:1. Absolute Garbage Customer Support, IF at all you do manage to get in touch with one.2. The CS Rep has probably not even seen the face of elementary school since all they do is copy and paste replies from FAQs. I don't know what they're being paid for.3. 99% of the products you receive will be in a flimsy plastic wrapper with absolutely no padding at all and your item will be damaged for sure - All in the name of being Eco Friendly. But then you return and ask for a replacement and repeat, more such materials are wasted. So much for being Eco Friendly. In one instance, I literally had to return an item 8 times before I could get one in working order. Not so Eco friendly, just a diplomatic way of making more profits by saving on packaging costs!4. The CS Reps are powerless, they won't help you because they have no power and those that can do something won't get in touch with you, they're the so called back end and no matter what the rep tells you, no one is passing on your comments to the back end, believe me, I know. THE BIGGEST MISMATCH! It's hilarious!5. Apparently, 95% of the stuff sold on Amazon is low quality sourced from China, India and other third world countries and none of them have any kind of health and safety approvals whatsoever and almost everyone is a seller on Amazon selling whatever garbage they desire. And then you see cases of lead poisoning and other health related issues from using that plastic item you just bought from Amazon. Yes that's the culprit. Try to spend a little more and buy Branded stuff Made in a Developed country with checks and licensing authorities if you have a desire to live longer. If only Amazon was 'responsible' enough to do that for us.6. Packaging Standards are the WORST of any online retailer out there. Their frustration free packaging is a scam, it gives you a lot of frustration when you see broken items inside. There's NO bubble wrap or Foam peanuts or any sort of padding at all. Just the item thrown inside a flimsy polybag or a thin crushed box. I don't know who the wise guy is behind the packaging team but there are times when I receive an item as it is with shipping slip stuck directly on to it and there's no Amazon branded packing at all. Not even that low quality plastic bag. Imagine that!7. You actually end up wasting time and in turn money when you have to return, then reorder and then repeat and then speak to customer rep and then still get no resolution and apparently now their 10 day return is changing into 7 days replacement on some items, clever move. Instead of mending own ways, it's better to screw the customer, Bravo Amazon!8. In the end, it's your money. Either you can give it to support a retailer that keeps growing big and keeps screwing your happiness with no concern for your health, expectations, feedback and your hard earned money OR you can choose to boycott them and support a better company or another retailer instead that might be charging similar or maybe a little higher for the same item but will deliver it right the first time and will also stand behind it's products and be there for it's customers. 9. And since I've been fighting for my rightful money and asking for them to improve their packaging standards and had to constantly return items everytime due to damage or cheap quality, my account was BLACKLISTED by them and now they won't let me open another account or even let me get in touch with them. So much for being the world's largest online retailer. This is their sorry state. The choice is yours, the money is yours...",2021-10-21 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,21.0,3728,680,23,3,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,amazon actually prof customer longer king youre give profit here breakdown amazon stand t