Greg Bishop,/users/5c54e655d6050697fcc44d70,US,3.0,2021-10-18 17:50:51+00:00,1.0,I was liking Amazon a few years back…,"I was liking Amazon a few years back but I've become increasingly disappointed in the company. There are things that any company can improve on such as delivery time, leaving packages at the wrong house, etc. But those I can move past.Ultimately, I'm disappointed in how they've removed all my past product review and not allowed me to make any new reviews. They have not provided any explanation, response (other than a generic, non specific response), or method of recourse. It has been months so I assume it is permanent. I honestly don't know what caused this but the only thing I can assume is that it was because of a negative review of a book that was pro-transgender training for children. I was respectful and factual and shared my perspective under the Amazon guidelines so I don't understand why this would have caused that reaction. I would guess that this is the result of an ideological employee that was allowed to take this course of action without review to save the credibility of a book that they support. Perhaps it is a glitch but then it is just bad customer service for a long time prime member.That was on my family's personal account. I've instructed several of my businesses and partners to no longer use Amazon wherever possible so this has cost them more than a couple hundred thousand per year in purchases.But is disappointing to have no response, explanation or recourse. Bad customer service in any case.",2021-10-18 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,18.0,1436,249,37,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,liking amazon year back ive become increasingly disappointed company thing company improve delivery time leaving package wrong house etc move pastultimately im disappointed theyve removed past product review allowed make new review provided explanation response generic non specific response method recourse month assume permanent honestly dont know caused thing assume negative review book protransgender training child respectful factual shared perspective amazon guideline dont understand would caused reaction would guess result ideological employee allowed take course action without review save credibility book support perhaps glitch bad customer service long time prime memberthat family personal account ive instructed several business partner longer use amazon wherever possible cost couple hundred thousand per year purchasesbut disappointing response explanation recourse bad customer service case,0.006007272630970166,0.9939927273690299,0.13965227145260797,0.2,0.8249268179750365,82.49268179750365,High Trust
