Scott Cauvel,/users/5a99e9fe4de5666d348393b7,US,2.0,2021-10-06 21:28:58+00:00,1.0,Fifth notice...Amazon needs to place my…,"Fifth notice...Amazon needs to place my Prime Video account back onto my new Amazon profile. I have requested contact from you on text, email, FB posts and via messenger notices.  No one, I repeat No one at Amazon has contacted me!!!  This a two week old issue that has never been addressed by Amazon!You are exhibiting the most shaudy customer service I have experienced by ANY major company in years!  Bazos should be damn ashamed, maybe he is spending more time on his space dreams that a reputable, customer oriented business!!!Thank you",2021-10-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,6.0,541,92,40,6,0.0,0,8,2,1,Suspicious,fifth noticeamazon need place prime video account back onto new amazon profile requested contact text email fb post via messenger notice one repeat one amazon contacted two week old issue never addressed amazonyou exhibiting shaudy customer service experienced major company year bazos damn ashamed maybe spending time space dream reputable customer oriented businessthank,0.9995930521117827,0.00040694788821726835,0.051598429613011774,0.2,0.310523159866711,31.052315986671097,Low Trust
Nuno G,/users/615e111c1c8cd100128e7572,US,2.0,2021-10-06 21:17:57+00:00,2.0,Amazon delivery service's quality is…,"Amazon delivery service's quality is going down hill. Fast! My last two orders have been a complete disaster.Last month I placed an order with 3 items and Amazon gave me a delivery day. I reschedule my appointments to make sure I would be at home that all day. Only 1 item was delivered and the other two got rescheduled to next day. Next day only one item arrived. I had to stay home a third day to receive a simple order that could and should have been delivered all at the same time.This month I placed another order. Again I stood at home the all day the order was to be delivered. Nobody rang the door bell and nothing was delivered. I checked the order's status to find it says it had been delivered. It did not. I contact Amazon, explained what happen and they told me the order should be delivered today or I would get a credit on my account or card. Still to be seen which of the two events (if any!) is to happen.",2021-10-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,6.0,923,178,37,5,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,amazon delivery service quality going hill fast last two order complete disasterlast month placed order item amazon gave delivery day reschedule appointment make sure would home day item delivered two got rescheduled next day next day one item arrived stay home third day receive simple order could delivered timethis month placed another order stood home day order delivered nobody rang door bell nothing delivered checked order status find say delivered contact amazon explained happen told order delivered today would get credit account card still seen two event happen,0.13970830705083256,0.8602916929491674,0.09983174425126191,0.4,1.050112195324836,105.01121953248361,High Trust
Jim Glaze,/users/615e000aa7b8bf0012b746ae,US,8.0,2021-10-07 16:55:33+00:00,1.0,"Amazon Believes In Lip Service, Not Customer Service","Amazon's customer service has decided to follow Facebook's playbook. They believe lip service is more important than customer service. Within one week I received two deliveries containing damaged items. I spent hours on the chat window. I was emailed that one item had shipped and was told to expect delivery today. Minutes after another hour plus chat ended today, I received an email telling me that my delivery for today was delayed for a day - or two. The clear lesson they want to teach - ""Don't bother us, we do lip service, not customer service."" BTW – they no longer email transcripts of customer service chats to the customer. I was told today that that is now their policy. They said I should take screenshots of chats. How many screenshots would it take to document chats lasting more than hour? I preserved the record, but a different way.",2021-10-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,7.0,851,149,52,8,1.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer service decided follow facebooks playbook believe lip service important customer service within one week received two delivery containing damaged item spent hour chat window emailed one item shipped told expect delivery today minute another hour plus chat ended today received email telling delivery today delayed day two clear lesson want teach dont bother u lip service customer service btw – longer email transcript customer service chat customer told today policy said take screenshots chat many screenshots would take document chat lasting hour preserved record different way,0.013781206299324942,0.9862187937006751,0.08356702187324734,0.2,0.8098228012249871,80.98228012249871,High Trust
Christine Anderson,/users/5d97cef7bb92741abdb78eeb,US,4.0,2021-10-06 16:56:52+00:00,3.0,Amazon is going DOWN HILL!!,"I have been an Amazon customer for several years now. Since Covid hit I have spent THOUSANDS of dollars with them. Throughout the entire shutdown Amazon NEVER missed a delivery date. In the past several months it has gone SERIOUSLY DOWN HILL!! What is going on?? If you can not deliver an item on time then why do you even put a delivery day on the items? It's ridiculous. I pay for PRIME SERVICE but I am no longer getting it. Sorry, but I don't go for that crap. When I order a product and it specifically gives me a date of arrival BEFORE I ORDER IT!! I consider that a contract! I pay for the service, I pay for the item...but do not receive my order on the promised date. In May of 2021 I had a little incident where some supplies for a customers order got damaged. I immediately ordered what I needed with the ""promise"" of it being delivered the next day. Sometime around 5:00pm (long after it should have already been delivered) I received a text message informing me that it would not be arriving when promised. It was to arrive on May 21st which still would have given me 2 1/2 days to complete my customers order which was to be delivered on the evening of Monday, May 24th.   I did not receive my supplies until the afternoon of May 24th!! Needless to say I could not deliver as promised because Amazon did not deliver as promised. The loss of that order cost me $300.00!! When I called to complain, they had the AUDACITY to offer me a $5.00 credit to my account. ARE YOU KIDDING ME!!?? You cost me $300.00 and you want to compensate that with a $5.00 credit? Talk about a slap in the face. As a matter of fact that was and is THE ONLY time that Amazon had the courtesy of letting me know. Usually they do not even do that much. It's not until I see UPS drive past my house that I realize that something is wrong and then I have to check. They are also starting to get really cheap with their packaging. I have been ordering my makeup from Amazon for quite a while now. It used to come wrapped in bubble wrap in a box. There were no problems. Now they have been sending it in really thin and cheesy mail bags/envelopes and it arrives in pieces. One time they sent 2 glass bottle of foundation, 2 2 compacts of face powder and a tube of mascara all together in a paper shipping bag. Absolutely no padding, bubble wrap or anything!! Well after shipping and UPS throwing it around for a day and a half, I had a real mess on my hands. How much common sense does it actually take for someone to know that 2 glass bottles and some fragile makeup needs to be packed properly with padding and a box?? I see that Amazon sells Waterford Crystal and Austrian crystal wine glasses at $400.00 -$500.00 per half dozen. I can just imagine how they would arrive!! You NEED to get it together Amazon. Have you ever heard the saying ""Your mouth needs to stop writing checks that your ass can't cash!""",2021-10-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,6.0,2893,549,27,5,0.0,0,16,2,1,Suspicious,amazon customer several year since covid hit spent thousand dollar throughout entire shutdown amazon never missed delivery date past several month gone seriously hill going deliver item time even put delivery day item ridiculous pay prime service longer getting sorry dont go crap order product specifically give date arrival order consider contract pay service pay itembut receive order promised date may little incident supply customer order got damaged immediately ordered needed promise delivered next day sometime around pm long already delivered received text message informing would arriving promised arrive may st still would given day complete customer order delivered evening monday may th receive supply afternoon may th needless say could deliver promised amazon deliver promised loss order cost called complain audacity offer credit account kidding cost want compensate credit talk slap face matter fact time amazon courtesy letting know usually even much see ups drive past house realize something wrong check also starting get really cheap packaging ordering makeup amazon quite used come wrapped bubble wrap box problem sending really thin cheesy mail bagsenvelopes arrives piece one time sent glass bottle foundation compact face powder tube mascara together paper shipping bag absolutely padding bubble wrap anything well shipping ups throwing around day half real mess hand much common sense actually take someone know glass bottle fragile makeup need packed properly padding box see amazon sell waterford crystal austrian crystal wine glass per half dozen imagine would arrive need get together amazon ever heard saying mouth need stop writing check as cant cash,0.9999999949854868,5.014513249079755e-09,0.30790802019068986,0.6,0.9615816065453945,96.15816065453944,High Trust
Richard Costello,/users/606dda460f5ae6001bea8919,CA,17.0,2021-10-06 16:56:43+00:00,1.0,Amazon has horrible service …,"Amazon keeps getting worse all the time. I have had multiple orders recently with most being late, even though Amazon blames the carrier it seems. I get messages like this right after it has been shipped ""Unfortunately, your delivery is running behind schedule. Canada Post is working to make sure the delay doesn’t affect your final delivery time."" That message has been posted right after I get the notification of shipment,  so why is it they blame the carrier when they never actually shipped the item for many days after the order. It's Amazon's fault it is slow not the carrier,  if Amazon would actually ship it out sooner it wouldn't be late. I had an item that was supposed to be delivered that day, that day came and gone and Amazon hadn't even shipped it yet. So obviously the email they send with your guaranteed delivery day means nothing. Why tell you a guaranteed when their guarantee means nothing. Amazon seems quick to blame others for their poor service. I'm expecting another parcel today that was just shipped last night. I highly doubt I will see this item as it was shipped from 1700 kilometers away. Well if they wouldn't have sat on the order for 6 days it would be here. I order from a lot of online companies and Amazon has the absolute slowest service in my opinion.",2021-10-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,10.0,6.0,1294,231,29,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon keep getting worse time multiple order recently late even though amazon blame carrier seems get message like right shipped unfortunately delivery running behind schedule canada post working make sure delay doesn’t affect final delivery time message posted right get notification shipment blame carrier never actually shipped item many day order amazon fault slow carrier amazon would actually ship sooner wouldnt late item supposed delivered day day came gone amazon hadnt even shipped yet obviously e