PATRICE W.,/users/5e9dbec70ebc96eb2707bbd8,US,3.0,2021-09-23 22:41:40+00:00,1.0,HORRIBLE CUSTOMER SERVICE!!!!!,"I bought a 4 pack of my favorite cookies so that I could give some to a friend who had never tried them, but they arrived in a paper envelope. Two of the boxes were crushed in multiple places; but when I tried to return them, I was told that ""This usually doesn't happen"" and that there would be no refund because ""the item is still usable"". I felt like they were calling me a liar, so I sent photos of the boxes and the envelope. I was more insulted that they told me that the cookies were ""still usable""; if I had seen these boxes in a grocery store, I would have left them there. The fact that they expected me to just suck it up only pissed me off; if I wouldn't accept it in a store, I'm not going to accept it online. Also, items that can be smashed during shipping should be placed in a box, so that this kind of thing doesn't happen again. After complaining loud enough (I tend to complain when I pay good money for something and it's not the way I expect it to be), I finally got offered a refund. In the end, I will probably keep one box, give one box to my friend and give the other two to kids in my building. Lesson learned; don't buy food from Amazon!!!!!",2021-09-23 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,23.0,1169,232,30,3,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,bought pack favorite cooky could give friend never tried arrived paper envelope two box crushed multiple place tried return told usually doesnt happen would refund item still usable felt like calling liar sent photo box envelope insulted told cooky still usable seen box grocery store would left fact expected suck pissed wouldnt accept store im going accept online also item smashed shipping placed box kind thing doesnt happen complaining loud enough tend complain pay good money something way expect finally got offered refund end probably keep one box give one box friend give two kid building lesson learned dont buy food amazo