James Davis,/users/613fae9680b0490012dcf551,US,1.0,2021-09-13 20:10:20+00:00,2.0,Not all that and a bag of chips,"Okay. Amazon is nice to have simply because of their depth of selection. However, since I became a Prime member, customer service and their delivery promises fail at every level. For the fourth time in two months, I have an order that will not be delivered as promised. It's due to arrive today, 9/13 @10:00pm. It's 4:05 and it hasn't even shipped yet. In the past, I have sent emails directly to Jeff Bezos in order to get resolution, but at this point I think things are beyond repair. The CSA's obviously read a scripted response and have little power to correct any given situation to the customer's satisfaction. And their typical response is to give the package a couple of days to arrive. Last time I had a problem Amazon refunded my Prime membership fees and kept my membership in place at no charge until renewal, saying, ""We hope to win back your trust"". Well...that didn't work out so well. Not sure how many more times I can give them to screw things up before I say ""Screw it"".",2021-09-13 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,13.0,990,180,31,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,okay amazon nice simply depth selection however since became prime member customer service delivery promise fail every level fourth time two month order delivered promised due arrive today pm hasnt even shipped yet past sent email directly jeff bezos order get resolution point think thing beyond repair csas obviously read scripted response little power correct given situation customer satisfaction typical response give package couple day arrive last time problem amazon refunded prime membership fee kept membership place charge renewal saying hope win back trust wellthat didnt work well sure many time give screw thing say screw,0.0068909012268617235,0.9931090987731382,0.10095344924284913,0.4,1.116745239235139,111.67452392351389,High Trust
