Sue,/users/5f008c6697bff058b63288dd,GB,9.0,2021-09-06 15:48:28+00:00,1.0,Unfounded Price increase,"Yesterday I had a pair of El Naturalista sandals in my basket which I ordered but then cancelled due to the delivery date not being convenient, so intended to re order later.   When I went back in to re order less than 1 hour later they went up in price from £62.40 then they were £71.00, then they went up to over £86.00  and this morning were over £91.00 and now they are over £95.00    How can a product change in less than 24 hours they started at 5 in stock and are now still at 5 in stock.   What is with Amazon they say it is the supplier but I have never had this happen before in such a short time.   Normally sale prices last until the next day.    Very disappointed customer not sure I want to use again after this episode.",2021-09-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,6.0,734,143,24,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,yesterday pair el naturalista sandal basket ordered cancelled due delivery date convenient intended order later went back order less hour later went price £ £ went £ morning £ £ product change less hour started stock still stock amazon say supplier never happen short time normally sale price last next day disappointed customer sure want use episode,0.0134079342426446,0.9865920657573554,0.08020190689848569,0.2,0.8093364142583748,80.93364142583748,High Trust
RB,/users/5f0072d223f4b01776234104,US,22.0,2021-11-22 16:16:15+00:00,2.0,This is just something I think...,"This is just something I think left unsaid that needs to be said-AMAZON-listen up! We are a very tired bunch of now awkward people trying to stay alive in the worst tragedy in human history-that aside, how was the play Mrs. Lincoln? Amazon has done EVERYTHING to upset their client base-however this last adjustment they made to searching on their site has me swearing them off at the first opportunity-if we search like I did today for something simple, like 34 x 6"" Washcloths-we don't get what we're looking for any longer nay, what we get is a plethora of other similar things even if a brand name is specified one has to look through ALL of what THEY want us to see, rather than simply buying quickly, and moving on-which was their key to success-remember folks, their original mottos and mantras? Well say goodbye and also too to the customer service that was so perfect, all of that is now just more hooks to advertise and lure us in to buy more-this writer seriously resents this-I am afraid too that other big stores are doing other annoying things, but many of them showing what isn't in the search too-Walmart has a new one-they send an email that your goods have arrived-so their customer is outside their home looking frantically as there's nothing there, after going to their site they have a disclaimer that basically says even if that email says ""delivered"" allow 24-48 hours before asking to speak with them-essentially it's ok with Walmart if their customers are outside their homes (a few of the last things we would do on their own during a worldwide crisis) and looking for something they know hasn't been sent yet-it is for these reasons this writer feels the big stores are on their way out and the ones that held on-the supermarkets and older die hard companies will profit immensely from the demise of these monopoliesAddendum: Nov 2021-FRESH with their name as such refuses to deliver frozen goods in a freezer bag-they all arrive melted-this last time I refuse the refund, and have called the board of health as someone got very ill-it's time to stop the madness-oh, but you can avoid all of this if you use Whole Foods, and pay up to 15.00 now even if you are Prime, which almost means nothing any more-let's see how they fare against some real class action types",2021-09-05 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,11.0,22.0,2291,405,33,6,78.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,something think left unsaid need saidamazonlisten tired bunch awkward people trying stay alive worst tragedy human historythat aside play mr lincoln amazon done everything upset client basehowever last adjustment made searching site swearing first opportunityif search like today something simple like x washclothswe dont get looking longer nay get plethora similar thing even brand name specified one look want u see rather simply buying quickly moving onwhich key successremember folk original motto mantra well say goodbye also customer service perfect hook advertise lure u buy morethis writer seriously resents thisi afraid big store annoying thing many showing isnt search toowalmart new onethey send email good arrivedso customer outside home looking frantically there nothing going site disclaimer basically say even email say delivered allow hour asking speak themessentially ok walmart customer outside home last thing would worldwide crisis looking something know hasnt sent yetit reason writer feel big store way one held onthe supermarket older die hard company profit immensely demise monopoliesaddendum nov fresh name refuse deliver frozen good freezer bagthey arrive meltedthis last time refuse refund called board health someone got illits time stop madnessoh avoid use whole food pay even prime almost mean nothing morelets see fare real class action type,0.017616669155510006,0.98238333084449,0.22714526079641054,0.4,1.1366207175815273,113.66207175815273,High Trust
