JMarley,/users/61085c69c3becc0012630cb2,US,2.0,2021-09-03 16:59:12+00:00,1.0,Customer Service worse than Government,"Word of advice.  Do not order multiple items with different shipping dates.  Amazon offers you a mediocre  credit if you select fewer shipments at a later date.  If one of your items in that order is due at a later date, and you don't opt for the credit, they will just send you an email at the close of business saying your shipment is delayed and give you the fewer shipment option anyways.  Amazon has done this to us every time.  So if you are expecting an item, rest assured, they will bone you.  To get around this now, we order separately if the shipping days don't concur.  And customer service at Amazon?  Yeah right, no such thing.  A garbage organization that has competition stifled due to a solid crony-capitalism relationship.  FU Amazon.",2021-09-03 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,3.0,752,133,38,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,word advice order multiple item different shipping date amazon offer mediocre credit select fewer shipment later date one item order due later date dont opt credit send email close business saying shipment delayed give fewer shipment option anyways amazon done u every time expecting item rest assured bone get around order separately shipping day dont concur customer service amazon yeah right thing garbage organization competition stifled due solid cronycapitalism relationship fu amazon,0.01302190050927153,0.9869780994907285,0.07459338194054964,0.2,0.8084077261334741,80.84077261334741,High Trust
