Rishi,/users/5d499aa36bc3c18c9b0a5a1b,US,4.0,2021-09-01 20:18:52+00:00,1.0,I am an Amazon prime since 2009,"I am an Amazon prime since 2009. However, lately, it has been series of worst experiences with Amazon. Almost no items come on time or get damaged during shipping. Lately, I am getting a lot of wrong items and have to go through the hassle of returning them. A few weeks ago they sent me the wrong item and  I got charged with restocking fees since the packaging was opened. Just before that, I received an empty package and Amazon customer care asked me to contact the police.It looks like Amazon is going downhill and it's the end of their run. Anyhow, I started buying from local stores more than often which is good for the local economy.",2021-09-01 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,1.0,642,118,31,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon prime since however lately series worst experience amazon almost item come time get damaged shipping lately getting lot wrong item go hassle returning week ago sent wrong item got charged restocking fee since packaging opened received empty package amazon customer care asked contact policeit look like amazon going downhill end run anyhow started buying local store often good local economy,0.01145289681630514,0.9885471031836949,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.8075096704925765,80.75096704925765,High Trust
october skye,/users/612f9b373efaca0013468593,US,1.0,2021-09-01 16:34:40+00:00,1.0,"2 ""lost"" PrIme orders in August","Twice in one month (August 2021) Amazon has ""lost"" my orders. One was intended as a birthday gift for a friend. A 2 day delivery vanished, and I have allegedly been issued a refund (still waiting). The second lost order just occurred. I urgently needed a product. They offered me 1 day shipping through Prime. I watched as this order was routed from one distribution center to another distribution center to another distribution center between FOUR states while they lied to me about ""delays"". Meanwhile, I went to a local Walmart and purchased the product. Today (6 days later), Amazon offers the option of a Replacement or Refund. I click Refund and Submit, then receive email informing me ""We are unable to process a refund through our automated system at this time."" Considering how frustrating (and useless) interaction with their customer service reps seems to be, I'm going to wait 24 hours before wading through this nightmare. Maybe their automated Refund system will mysteriously begin to function. One more item of interest: I've been an Amazon customer for more than a decade. I've always left honest reviews. Some were, frankly, quite negative - and I was astonished that the Sellers in question had such consistently highly rated merch. I'm not sure whether one or more of these Sellers complained, or - and here's an odd coincidence - I was asked to check out their requirements for Prime for EBT recipients, which I did. ONE DAY later (no exaggeration!) my ability to leave reviews was taken away without explanation, and every review I'd ever written was scrubbed from the site. Yet, all these glowing fake reviews for overpriced junk products persist in tricking buyers. Many reputable Sellers have left Amazon for this reason. Caveat emptor.",2021-09-01 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,9.0,1.0,1760,294,31,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,twice one month august amazon lost order one intended birthday gift friend day delivery vanished allegedly issued refund still waiting second lost order occurred urgently needed product offered day shipping prime watched order routed one distribution center another distribution center another distribution center four state lied delay meanwhile went local walmart purchased product today day later amazon offer option replacement refund click refund submit receive email informing unable process refund automated system time considering frustrating useless interaction customer service rep seems im going wait hour wading nightmare maybe automated refund system mysteriously begin function one item interest ive amazon customer decade ive always left honest review frankly quite negative astonished seller question consistently highly rated merch im sure whether one seller complained here odd coincidence asked check requirement prime ebt recipient one day later exaggeration ability leave review taken away without explanation every review id ever written scrubbed site yet glowing fake review overpriced junk product persist tricking buyer many reputable seller left amazon reason caveat emptor,0.03192101509403766,0.9680789849059623,0.16489063376332025,0.2,0.8170176192056453,81.70176192056454,High Trust
