Robert Sipes,/users/6104ac4af713d20012c59e47,US,5.0,2021-08-31 19:57:35+00:00,1.0,Scammers working within Amazon,"With no other venue to get this out there I hope someone who matters sees this. Within days of signing up for Amazon Prime I received the first call ever from a scammer claiming to be from Amazon. It was from Victoriavile Quebec Canada (819) 302-6734. The message claimed I made a purchase, which I did not, and directed me to connect to another department. Coincidence? No way. Someone on the inside of Amazon is feeding new client data to another bad actor outside of Amazon. I called Amazon to inform them and got a tutorial on how to avoid scams.",2021-08-31 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,8.0,31.0,550,101,30,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,venue get hope someone matter see within day signing amazon prime received first call ever scammer claiming amazon victoriavile quebec canada message claimed made purchase directed connect another department coincidence way someone inside amazon feeding new client data another bad actor outside amazon called amazon inform got tutorial avoid scam,0.020466792836972943,0.979533207163027,0.056646102075154234,0.2,0.8010958239965443,80.10958239965443,High Trust
