Diane Johnson,/users/611e602bdd87b100166e7d7f,US,1.0,2021-08-19 13:44:23+00:00,1.0,Shady business practices,"Shady business practices.  If you use Subscribe and Save, be sure to check the price before and after you add an item to your subscription.  I added an item that normally sells for around $75 to subscribe and save and was supposed to be saving 15% with my other subscribe and save items.  I purchased this item many times in the past, most recently just 1 month prior to adding it to subscribe and save and never paid more than $77 for it with tax on Amazon.  When I checked the price on my subscribe & save order page, the price was $5 higher than the normal price on Amazon.  The first person I talked to at Amazon tried to tell me the regular price was $99, while I had it up on my screen under my business account which showed $75.24 regular price. I said I never paid that much for it and went and looked at my previous orders and then called them back again,  The 2nd person I talked to told me the regular price was $106.  SHADY, SHADY Amazon.  Tack the price up on items after you add it to subscribe and save and hope the customers don't notice.",2021-08-19 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,8.0,19.0,1054,203,24,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,shady business practice use subscribe save sure check price add item subscription added item normally sell around subscribe save supposed saving subscribe save item purchased item many time past recently month prior adding subscribe save never paid tax amazon checked price subscribe save order page price higher normal price amazon first person talked amazon tried tell regular price screen business account showed regular price said never paid much went looked previous order called back nd person talked told regular price shady shady amazon tack price item add subscribe save hope customer dont notice,0.015962431867217176,0.9840375681327829,0.11385305664610207,0.2,0.8147893953956119,81.4789395395612,High Trust
