Rick,/users/60f610156c78840011f68615,US,1.0,2021-07-20 00:01:18+00:00,1.0,Late delivery and impossible return conditions,"I ordered an item and it said it would be 1 week for delivery, then 3 days later got an email saying it would be 3 weeks or more for delivery. Tried to cancel order that day and amazon says it's in transit and can't be cancelled. I contacted a representative and she said she would try to cancel it and would contact me next day. No contact but the charge was removed from my visa so I assumed it was cancelled. 4 weeks later they tell me it will be delivered within a week. Tried to cancel again with no luck, called my bank and disputed the charge, item tried to be delivered but I refused it so I wouldn't have to pay shipping charges to send it back. Now Amazon sent me a nasty email stating the terms of service regarding returns has change and now instead of arbitration I must now take them to court.I will never order a thing from them again because I can't risk going to court to returning an item by having to get a court order for them to return my money.",2021-07-20 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,7.0,20.0,966,190,46,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered item said would week delivery day later got email saying would week delivery tried cancel order day amazon say transit cant cancelled contacted representative said would try cancel would contact next day contact charge removed visa assumed cancelled week later tell delivered within week tried cancel luck called bank disputed charge item tried delivered refused wouldnt pay shipping charge send back amazon sent nasty email stating term service regarding return change instead arbitration must take courti never order thing cant risk going court returning item get court order return money,0.007607314609219565,0.9923926853907804,0.1065619742007852,0.2,0.8175087375355472,81.75087375355471,High Trust
