Sofia Coyle,/users/5d20fb4bb6ae917e922cc407,US,5.0,2021-06-30 17:32:16+00:00,1.0,Color of my Eliacher Women's casual spaghetti strap summer dress,"I just received the Eliacher Women's casual spaghetti strap summer dress in the mail today.  The material is great it, and it isn't see through, but I purchased the color ""Wine"" which looks on the website more like a burgundy (which I loved). I received the dress and its like a shade lighter than what I got.  What's worse is when I went to leave a review of the dress, Amazon wouldn't let me because of their policy of having to spend $50 dollars or more in order to review.  This is kind of deceiving because if someone doesn't like the product they should be able to review it.  It's our right to be able to review a product because it's a form of freedom of speech.  I don't mean to be a pain in the ass, but the color is not what I wanted. If I exchange it now it will either get here right before the wedding I need it for or it will come too late after the wedding.  Either way it's a gamble with time.  I also saw other peoples reviews and they got the same ""Wine"" dress as mine and THEIRS was the color I wanted...but another woman got the Wine dress and it was the same color as mine.  Consistency is way too much to ask, I guess. I went to Trust Pilot to actually provide a review since Amazon takes that right away from me.   I am more displeased with not being able to review.   I've had no prior reviews that were negative or filled with crude language about Amazon so I don't know why my review isn't allowed for a product I was displeased with.  If you're going to be a big (basically) monopoly company, then at least give your customers the right to review the products you provide.  You got nothing else to lose for a company who's revenue was $386 billion in 2020.",2021-06-30 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,30.0,1684,323,64,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,received eliacher womens casual spaghetti strap summer dress mail today material great isnt see purchased color wine look website like burgundy loved received dress like shade lighter got whats worse went leave review dress amazon wouldnt let policy spend dollar order review kind deceiving someone doesnt like product able review right able review product form freedom speech dont mean pain as color wanted exchange either get right wedding need come late wedding either way gamble time also saw people review got wine dress mine color wantedbut another woman got wine dress color mine consistency way much ask guess went trust pilot actually provide review since amazon take right away displeased able review ive prior review negative filled crude language amazon dont know review isnt allowed product displeased youre going big basically monopoly company least give customer right review product provide got nothing else lose company who revenue billion,0.013922867089649262,0.9860771329103507,0.18115535614133482,0.2,0.8292696376834423,82.92696376834424,High Trust
