Seb Tedd,/users/53a5d0e300006400017aaa53,GB,43.0,2021-06-30 10:58:54+00:00,1.0,Can't cancel order 8 days before it's due to be delivered,"Ordered a car battery from Amazon last week. Was not due to be delivered for 8 days. Tried to cancel the order 3 minutes after it was placed. Couldn't do it, as ""order was processing"". Had a chat session with CS, who told me to wait for status to change to ""Dispatch"" so that I could contact them again and cancel.Status changed to ""dispatch"" today (3 days after ordering). Contacted again CS and was told an order cannot be cancelled once dispatched. I should just reject delivery due in 5 days...which I usually can't since they dump parcels outside (and it will be a 20kg battery this time).Surely, if a (heavy) order takes 3 days to be dispatched and then 5 days to be delivered, it can be cancelled at some point without going onto a delivery truck, to be rejected or returned by me.Also, they keep referring as ""external vendor"" when the good is coming from...Amazon EU. It's not their fault, it's that unknown Amazon EU vendor...Shocking and not very green. They used to be proud of their advanced logistics and CS. Surely not that great anymore.",2021-06-28 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,30.0,1053,188,57,11,2.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered car battery amazon last week due delivered day tried cancel order minute placed couldnt order processing chat session c told wait status change dispatch could contact cancelstatus changed dispatch today day ordering contacted c told order cannot cancelled dispatched reject delivery due dayswhich usually cant since dump parcel outside kg battery timesurely heavy order take day dispatched day delivered cancelled point without going onto delivery truck rejected returned mealso keep referring external vendor good coming fromamazon eu fault unknown amazon eu vendorshocking green used proud advanced logistics c surely great anymore,0.02560266092213936,0.9743973390778606,0.10544026920919798,0.2,0.80828672338077,80.828672338077,High Trust
