Kristy Spakowski,/users/5f1f3b07c5a3067c5d58ec10,US,2.0,2021-06-24 12:44:58+00:00,1.0,So completely disappointed in what…,"So completely disappointed in what Amazon has become, which is completely unreliable with shipping, regardless of how you place your order. We placed a very large order before our vacation and had requested that our products be delivered on the same day in 1 package, as an Amazon prime member. The website stated that our products had been delivered when they had not actually arrived. When we called to see what the problem was, our order was cancelled leaving us scrambling to find the items we had ordered, the day before we leave. I have been a prime member for YEARS and have experienced this same problem too many times and should have known better than to trust this company. I will NEVER order from Amazon again and will be cancelling my prime membership. The stress that their lack of efficiency has created is not worth it to me. We will shop elsewhere. If I could give 0 stars, I would. Get your act together Amazon!!! People depend on you and you are FAILING!!!",2021-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,24.0,974,174,35,5,0.0,0,6,2,1,Suspicious,completely disappointed amazon become completely unreliable shipping regardless place order placed large order vacation requested product delivered day package amazon prime member website stated product delivered actually arrived called see problem order cancelled leaving u scrambling find item ordered day leave prime member year experienced problem many time known better trust company never order amazon cancelling prime membership stress lack efficiency created worth shop elsewhere could give star would get act together amazon people depend failing,0.9880561289155078,0.011943871084492241,0.0975883342680875,0.2,0.3254896023958636,32.548960239586364,Low Trust
Jaz,/users/5f486a739b2cb12f6efac625,US,2.0,2021-06-24 18:28:53+00:00,1.0,Monopolies have terrible customer service,"Of course Amazon is a giant mega corporation that everyone will continue to use no matter how bad the service or products are, but that’s only because they have a monopoly on most online retail. It’s unfortunate, but there are better places out there with cheap prices and just as fast shipment, without the need to pay for a useless membership. My issue with Amazon is that although I pay the membership, I don’t necessarily get membership “perks” when it comes to online purchases. Amazon doesn’t care if you select two day free shipping, because you’ll get it when they feel like sending it out and they expect you wouldn’t have a problem with that, because where else will you get a $20 bedsheet set?? (Spoiler alert: Walmart is a terrible company too, but they have lower prices than Amazon, offer two day shipping on most products AND they don’t require you pay monthly for a membership). If you happen to call Amazon with an issue like, “I never received my puppy play pen! It’s been a week and I selected TWO DAY shipping!”, you’ll most likely get a half hearted fake apology, a poor excuse, and then finally, they’ll help you (that’s only after keeping you on hold for 15 minutes out of the entire 30 minute call). When they finally “help” you with an issue they created, they offer no discounts, coupon, or refunds of any kind for your time and their mistake. No, you will have to haggle for that, because a $10-$20 credit will hurt the billion dollar business and how will they pay their poor employees??? (Btw most pet supplies can be found on chewy for the same price, and chewy also offers two day shipping!). All this to say, Amazon sucks, they only reason anyone would believe it to be even a half decent business, however, is because it’s taking over smaller companies and leaving consumers “no choice” but to buy from them. But that’s a lie, there are plenty of business out their that offer similar shipping with better service, we just need to look and support them more.Edit: turns out the chat option for customer service is somehow worse?? Its not accessible at all, so if you’re someone who cannot speak on the phone for whatever reason be it disability or other, you’re out of luck if you’re looking for service with customer service. I asked about it with the agent I chatted with, they also have no clue why they’re unable to perform the same tasks as an agent on the phone would. Also, you’ll never stay with the same agent because they always pass you around to a new agent. I’m not 100% sure, but I have a feeling this is because they’re not allowed to be on a single call (or in this case, chat) for longer than whatever allotted time. It’s not only screwed up to Amazons customers, but it’s really screwed up to the employees.Edit #2: I HAVE to update because this situation I’m going through with Amazon is surreal. I’ve been in chat with them for 3 hours now and have not received any help. They just regurgitate the info I gave them back to me as if they found some sort of secret I was unaware of. After consulting with maybe the 5th associate I’ve been bounced to, I asked him for someone higher up in hopes that I would receive a simple solution quicker and he tells me that associates are not able to do that through chat, which is why i made my first edit when I explained that the accessibility for chat was COMPLETELY different from a call. However, 3 hours and 21 chat associates later, my associate writes “…allow me a moment to transfer this chat to the concerned team.” And then does! Am I in the twighlight zone right now??? My issue is by no means resolved btw because each associate takes a good 10 minutes to respond only to come back and tell me they need to read my chat, but this happens maybe 5 times per associate, and they never come back with the right info anyway! As I’m writing this, the people I was transferred to and connected with just reconnected me to someone else. Hopefully I’ll have my issue resolved by the time I get to the 50th person.Edit #3: my last associate straight up lied to me, blamed me for my issue (an earlier associate had made the mistake of cancelling my prime membership rather than giving me a credit, this last associate kept referring to it as “your request for a cancellation” as if she was upset about it) and told me that the only way to resolve this was by signing up again. When I explained that I had no interest in signing up anymore after the service I received and the time Amazon had no issue wasting, and I just wanted the credit that was owed to me, she explained that she couldn’t do it and told me there was nothing more they can do.",2021-06-24 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,24.0,4637,853,41,5,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,course amazon giant mega corporation everyone continue use matter bad service product that’s monopoly online retail it’s unfortunate better place cheap price fast shipment without need pay useless membership issue amazon although pay membership don’t necessarily get membership “perks” come online purchase amazon doesn’t care select two day free shipping you’ll get feel like sending expect wouldn’t problem else get bedsheet set spoiler alert walmart terrible company lower price amazon offer two day shipping product don’t require pay monthly membership happen call amazon issue like “i never received puppy play pen it’s week selected two day shipping” you’ll likely get half hearted fake apology poor excuse finally they’ll help that’s keeping hold minute entire minute call finally “help” issue created offer discount coupon refund kind time mistake haggle credit hurt billion dollar business pay poor employee btw pet supply found chewy price chewy also offer two day shipping say amazon suck reason anyone would believe even half decent business however it’s taking smaller company leaving consumer “no choice” buy that’s lie plenty business offer similar shipping better service need look support moreedit turn chat option customer service somehow worse accessible you’re someone cannot speak phone whatever reason disability you’re luck you’re looking service customer service asked agent chatted also clue they’re unable perform task agent phone would also you’ll never stay agent always pas around new agent i’m sure feeling they’re allowed single call case chat longer whatever allotted time it’s screwed amazon customer it’s really screwed employeesedit update situation i’m going amazon surreal i’ve chat hour received help regurgitate info gave back found sort secret unaware consulting maybe th associate i’ve bounced asked someone higher hope would receive simple solution quicker tell associate able chat made first edit explained accessibility chat completely different call however hour chat associate later associate writes “…allow moment transfer chat concerned team” twighlight zone right issue mean resolved btw associate take good minute respond come back tell need read chat happens maybe time per associate never come back right info anyway i’m writing people transferred connected reconnected someone else hopefully i’ll issue resolved time get th personedit last associate straight lied blamed issue earlier associate made mistake cancelling prime membership rather giving credit last associate kept referring “your request cancellation” upset told way resolve signing explained interest signing anymore service received time amazon issue wasting wanted credit owed explained couldn’t told nothing,0.9521581434570964,0.04784185654290363,0.4784071789119462,0.2,0.41960236405384105,41.9602364053841,Low Trust
Joanne,/users/60d35867275662001a7a0403,CA,1.0,2021-06-23 15:53:55+00:00,1.0,Amazon Treats Seniors Poorly,"I am a working Senior Citizen and I ordered a sit-stand desk top riser, expensive, big model. It was a wait for it to ship then it was a lot of work to get it all set up with computer pieces and it did not work. So I talked to Amazon and we arranged a replacement but I had to return the beast. SO I could barely lift it and had to pack it down, pack it up, and haul it into the post office, stop to get a shipping label printed, and a drive to town from the country. My 78 year old mother had to help me move it and I realized as I reassembled my office again that I need a smaller version; so I called Amazon THE VERY NEXT MORNING and Amazon is like too bad, you are going to have to do it all over again and pack the next one back even though it is not due here for a week. Also I have to wait for a refund when all I want is to switch the order to the smaller version. How difficult can Amazon make things for Senior Citizens?!?",2021-06-23 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,23.0,932,197,28,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,working senior citizen ordered sitstand desk top riser expensive big model wait ship lot work get set computer piece work talked amazon arranged replacement return beast could barely lift pack pack haul post office stop get shipping label printed drive town country year old mother help move realized reassembled office need smaller version called amazon next morning amazon like bad going pack next one back even though due week also wait refund want switch order smaller version difficult amazon make thing senior citizen,0.08978709769360059,0.9102129023063994,0.11048794167134043,0.2,0.7772040394874679,77.72040394874679,High Trust
