Karen Wylie,/users/54c81ced0000ff0001a70f62,GB,27.0,2021-06-18 21:28:20+00:00,1.0,Loyal customer for years now disgusted with treatment!!!,"Decided that, as holidays are out of the window at the minute, I would buy a hot tub to ease the aching muscles and help with stress. I have Amazon prime and (even though you pay extra for the 'free' delivery) I always try to buy items with prime delivery as they do generally arrive quicker.I picked a hot tub I liked and the ad said it would arrive by Thursday if I ordered that day (Friday). A little longer than normal but it's a large item so I went for it and planned to have everything there ready for a family hot tub weekend.After ordering, the message changed to ""dispatch pending, we will email you when we have a delivery estimate"". I did panic a little bit thought as they haven't let me down before so I'll wait and see.The following day the message hadn't changed so I got onto chat and the man said it was definitely due for dispatch that day and they just had to arrange the courier as it's a large bulky item. I was reassured....Tuesday.... Still the same message. Customer services said they would personally speak to the dispatch department and get it sent asap.Wednesday.. Really starting to panic now. Check Argos to find I can order a different hot tub for delivery the following day. Attempt to cancel the Amazon order so I can order from Argos. Amazon cannot cancel the order as it is in the final stages of dispatch..... Thursday Argos sold out of hot tubs, still no change to dispatch message. Customer services again promise to have it sent out as quickly as possible....I don't believe them any more for some reason.Now Friday night. A day after the advert promised I would have my delivery. Guess what. Still pending!!I'm losing the will to live!I now have spare filters, chemicals, foot bath, gazebo and dip sticks but still no hot tub. My aches and pains are twice as bad and my anxiety is through the roof. Will I have a hot tub this year? Who knows. I and my money are in limbo. Does Amazon care? No because they know I need them more than they need me! I'd cancel my Amazon prime account if my entire house wasn't linked to it!! I just checked and the advert says ""in stock"" and ""delivery by Thursday June 24th for prime members"" ....... Don't believe it folks!!!I'm very disappointed with Amazon and have lost all the trust I had in them!",2021-06-18 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,6.0,18.0,2274,418,56,8,0.0,0,10,2,1,Suspicious,decided holiday window minute would buy hot tub ease aching muscle help stress amazon prime even though pay extra free delivery always try buy item prime delivery generally arrive quickeri picked hot tub liked ad said would arrive thursday ordered day friday little longer normal large item went planned everything ready family hot tub weekendafter ordering message changed dispatch pending email delivery estimate panic little bit thought havent let ill wait seethe following day message hadnt changed got onto chat man said definitely due dispatch day arrange courier large bulky item reassuredtuesday still message customer service said would personally speak dispatch department get sent asapwednesday really starting panic check argo find order different hot tub delivery following day attempt cancel amazon order order argo amazon cannot cancel order final stage dispatch thursday argo sold hot tub still change dispatch message customer service promise sent quickly possiblei dont believe reasonnow friday night day advert promised would delivery guess still pendingim losing livei spare filter chemical foot bath gazebo dip stick still hot tub ache pain twice bad anxiety roof hot tub year know money limbo amazon care know need need id cancel amazon prime account entire house wasnt linked checked advert say stock delivery thursday june th prime member dont believe folksim disappointed amazon lost trust,0.9999846320737459,1.5367926254117314e-05,0.23443634324172744,0.2,0.346894952611472