Nunya,/users/60ae7a1b4d27a400195718bd,US,1.0,2021-05-26 16:41:16+00:00,1.0,Don't waste your money on PRIME,"Amazon was once a fairly good service.  Then it got politicized and too big for it's britches. Their WOKE mentality has done more to damage the company than it has been to bolster their customer base.  They increased their annual premium to offset their incompetence and misinformation.  Their annual PRIME supposedly has video, which is all well except that I don't consider shows from 1975 ""NEWLY RELEASED."" The only things NEW in their video lines up are their incessant drive to make their customers WOKE as they are.  They further claim that their PRIME will allow you to get your packages quicker, but what has actually happened is that now you have to wonder if you will ever get your package.  I am still waiting for an order that I have done without for almost a year.  They have no clue where the package went, except that it was last seen in GA.  After repeatedly complaining that it still hadn't arrived, they issued a refund...and something that should have occurred a few days after the package didn't arrive took almost two months and multiple phone calls to their customer service before the refund was issued.  Additionally, Amazon considers it a WIN if the package arrives 5 days later, although it promises two-day shipping....and they don't take into account that it took 3-4 WEEKS to actually get your product shipped.Finally, their customer service, which you can spend days trying to find, is crass and belligerent.  After being with Prime for a long time, I finally had enough and cancelled my Prime membership.  Not paying a company for substandard service or quality, in their products or their service.",2021-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,26.0,1629,276,31,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon fairly good service got politicized big britches woke mentality done damage company bolster customer base increased annual premium offset incompetence misinformation annual prime supposedly video well except dont consider show newly released thing new video line incessant drive make customer woke claim prime allow get package quicker actually happened wonder ever get package still waiting order done without almost year clue package went except last seen ga repeatedly complaining still hadnt arrived issued refundand something occurred day package didnt arrive took almost two month multiple phone call customer service refund issued additionally amazon considers win package arrives day later although promise twoday shippingand dont take account took week actually get product shippedfinally customer service spend day trying find crass belligerent prime long time finally enough cancelled prime membership paying company substandard service quality product service,0.004724055735696074,0.9952759442643039,0.15479528883903534,0.2,0.828597029899959,82.8597029899959,High Trust
Kirill S.,/users/59dd1c930000ff000ad35fc6,IT,41.0,2021-05-26 15:50:45+00:00,3.0,Mixed bag,"Overall, my experience with Amazon has been a mixed bag. The first two purchases were packaged differently despite practically being the same product, and that is because I bought them from two different sellers. You'd think Amazon would have some consistency and standards even across different sellers, but no. In my case, the biggest complaint here is that the second order was packaged in an inadequate way (it was inside a plastic bag), which created a serious privacy situation I am not going to talk about and which caused me a little bit of embarrassment and fear. Nowadays, it seems like you can inadvertently buy an item from a non-Amazon seller and then end up having such an inconsistent customer service...Amazon should vet sellers more rigorously and enforce some standards. My third order was nothing short of infuriating, it was packaged even worse than my second one, it was a small paperback categorized as a magazine, which meant I could not leave a feedback on how it was handled, something I discovered only when I attempted to do so despite the fact I distinctly remember there being an option to leave an opinion somewhere in the package\receipt itself. And yeah, it was inside a bubble wrap envelope, so it arrived slightly damaged. If only Amazon packaged their products better, I'd seriously consider continuing being a customer, but as of right now, I have to shop from local sellers. Oh, and for God's sake, add the possibility of using PayPal accounts as payment methods, that's also one of the main obstacles.",2021-05-26 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,26.0,1539,260,9,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,overall experience amazon mixed bag first two purchase packaged differently despite practically product bought two different seller youd think amazon would consistency standard even across different seller case biggest complaint second order packaged inadequate way inside plastic bag created 