Pamela+Trenta,/users/5ad11bf04de5666d34a4afc4,GB,49.0,2021-05-25 19:29:32+00:00,1.0,Horrible customer service,"I got in touch about a delivery . I purchased the item a couple of hours ago . The website said delivered by 29th of May . When I did the check out it was 1st of June . I asked the agent which options I had because I needed it by 31st of May . I spoke with to agents … There was no solutions for them … I had to wait .  I found the solution on my own … I cancelled the order … I could have replaced it and pay for the next delivery, but because I received such a horrible service I will but it in a shop .",2021-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,25.0,505,114,25,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,got touch delivery purchased item couple hour ago website said delivered th may check st june asked agent option needed st may spoke agent … solution … wait found solution … cancelled order … could replaced pay next delivery received horrible service shop,0.0744806922605647,0.9255193077394352,0.06393718452047112,0.2,0.7755470907738119,77.55470907738119,High Trust
Mary and Martin Wood,/users/60a5646f31a9250019b1f129,NZ,2.0,2021-05-25 19:11:07+00:00,1.0,Amazon “dis” Service,"ResponseI purchased a USB-C Hub with Hard Drive Enclosure Hagibis Type-C Docking Station & Stand for Mac Mini M1 together with a Samsung 870 QVO SAYA III 2.5” SSD 2 TB on the 19th January this year. The cost including shipping was US $89.32 for the Hub and $236.59 for the SSD. I purchased this SSD as the Amazon page the Hub was listed on had this displayed at the bottom, stating that they were frequently purchased together, so I understood that this was the correct SSD to go with the Mac Mini.When the items arrived in February the SSD would not work with the Mac Mini, and the message “not compatible” came up. I made the mistake of contacting the Amazon Customer Service centre rather than simply returning the SSD. After much discussion and following the instructions from the person I was conversing with to try to “re-initialise” the SSD which did not help, I was told that a replacement was to be sent out to me. During this exchange I repeatedly informed this person that the Mac Mini was telling me that the SSD was not compatible but at no time was I advised to return it using the Amazon returns system during this contact.In March the “replacement” arrived, but what Amazon had sent me was another Hub rather than a replacement SSD. I again contacted the Amazon Customer Service Centre. This contact in March was very long and during the course of the conversation the staff member I was in discussion with changed several times, with the message “...has joined the conversation”. Each time this happened I had to start from scratch trying to explain what had happened. During this exchange I was initially told they would send me another Hub, and I could “keep or destroy” the (second) Hub that had been sent to me.I had to repeatedly explain that the Hub was not the problem, the SSD was, but of course by this time (March) the time frame for returning the SSD had passed. Eventually I was advised to return the Hub and to include the SSD in the Hub packaging, as I no longer had the SSD packaging. I was also advised that “special authority” had been granted in this situation for me to return the SSD. I returned both the second Hub and the SSD the following day in the package the Hub had arrived in, using the courier Amazon advised me to use.A couple of weeks later I received an email from Amazon informing me that if I didn’t return the Hub by the first week in April I would be charged for it!A third discussion with the Amazon Customer Service Centre followed and again, the person I was conversing with changing several times. The conversation ended with me being told that all I could do was to contact my bank and try to recover my money from BNZ Visa.I then contacted the BBB for help.From the subsequent contact with Amazon through the BBB process, Amazon told me that they would return the SSD to me, as I had stated that at least if they did that I could sell it to recoup some of the money it had cost me. However it was never returned.I have been a customer of Amazon for many years and have spent thousands of dollars with them over the years. I am unbelievably disappointed in this situation and would have expected more than this from a company such as Amazon. The Customer Service people I dealt with through this could simply have advised me to return the SSD at the start and none of this would have happened. Instead I have been put through months of time wasting nonsense and have achieved nothing. I am out of pocket to the tune of around NZ$500, have a Hub for my Mac Mini but with no SSD, it doesn’t actually work.This is the final response from Amazon!We aren't able to offer any additional insight or action on this matter and any further inquiries regarding this issue won't receive a response.",2021-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,25.0,3744,682,20,3,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,responsei purchased usbc hub hard drive enclosure hagibis typec docking station stand mac mini together samsung qvo saya iii ” ssd tb th january year cost including shipping u hub ssd purchased ssd amazon page hub listed displayed bottom stating frequently purchased together understood correct ssd go mac miniwhen item arrived february ssd would work mac mini message “not compatible” came made mistake contacting amazon customer service centre rather simply returning ssd much discussion following instruction person conversing try “reinitialise” ssd help told replacement sent exchange repeatedly informed person mac mini telling ssd compatible time advised return using amazon return system contactin march “replacement” arrived amazon sent another hub rather replacement ssd contacted amazon customer service centre contact march long course conversation staff member discussion changed several time message “has joined conversation” time happened start scratch trying explain happened exchange initially told would send another hub could “keep destroy” second hub sent mei repeatedly explain hub problem ssd course time march time frame returning ssd passed eventually advised return hub include ssd hub packaging longer ssd packaging also advised “special authority” granted situation return ssd returned second hub ssd following day package hub arrived using courier amazon advised usea couple week later received email amazon informing didn’t return hub first week april would charged ita third discussion amazon customer service centre followed person conversing changing several time conversation ended told could contact bank try recover money bnz visai contacted bbb helpfrom subsequent contact amazon bbb process amazon told would return ssd stated least could sell recoup money cost however never returnedi customer amazon many year spent thousand dollar year unbelievably disappointed situation would expected company amazon customer service people dealt could simply advised return ssd start none would happened instead put month time wasting nonsense achieved nothing pocket tune around nz hub mac mini ssd doesn’t actually workthis final response amazonwe arent able offer additional insight action matter inquiry regarding issue wont receive response,0.23092192396133962,0.7690780760386604,0.3825014021312395,0.2,0.761039318445578,76.1039318445578,High Trust
Anthony Frawley,/users/5d7c8eb6b1c85ca258937764,US,4.0,2021-05-25 18:03:11+00:00,1.0,Too big to hold accountable,"I bought a product and it never shipped.  Waited a week and it said I could cancel because it was so late.  Then I had to go through a hassle on that.  Then, and this really set me off, they won't post my negative transaction review.  This company needs to be held accountable as the Monopoly it is.  Nobody profited more from covid-19 than Jeff Besos... I wouldn't be surprised if he paid to have it developed... Just saying.",2021-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,25.0,426,79,27,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,bought product never shipped waited week said could cancel late go hassle really set wont post negative transaction review company need held accountable monopoly nobody profited covid jeff besos wouldnt surprised paid developed saying,0.04571262326862639,0.9542873767313736,0.0443073471676949,0.2,0.7860051577992258,78.60051577992257,High Trust
