Scott Ivey,/users/60a6dac5af5f550019d4d6d2,US,1.0,2021-05-20 21:55:34+00:00,1.0,Amazon not worth it,"I have been an Amazon Prime member for 7 years and in that time I have had many problems, all of which were handled professionally and promptly. With that said, in the past year I have had more problems than ever before and when you call customer service they are about as helpful as nothing at all. They claim that all the products are from third party sellers and that all they can do is have you contact them. In my opinion, if they the ones who are taking you money then they are the ones who should be correcting the problems, giving refunds and so on.  I believe that Amazon has gotten to big for their britches and needs to get knocked down a couple of rungs on the business ladder. I know as for me, my family and friends, Amazon Prime membership is going to be a thing of the PAST. It’s really not worth it. I will not be shopping with them anymore. I will buy directly from sellers. They don’t need to get rich being the middle man who does nothing but make money!",2021-05-20 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,20.0,974,188,19,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon prime member year time many problem handled professionally promptly said past year problem ever call customer service helpful nothing claim product third party seller contact opinion one taking money one correcting problem giving refund believe amazon gotten big britches need get knocked couple rung business ladder know family friend amazon prime membership going thing past it’s really worth shopping anymore buy directly seller don’t need get rich middle man nothing make money,0.0318171419721264,0.9681828580278736,0.10544026920919798,0.2,0.8051794828557765,80.51794828557765,High Trust
