Robert White,/users/608c30817f4c930019dc94eb,US,1.0,2021-04-30 16:29:59+00:00,1.0,Amazon doesn’t care about their customers,"I ordered items that stated a SPECIFIC delivery date and after the order, the delivery dates change.  I contacted customer service and they state that they are ESTIMATED dates.  It doesn’t say ANYTHING about estimated delivery.  It states if you order before “x” time, it will be delivered on a specific date.  I have been disconnected with customer service TWICE.  I’m sick and tired of the lack of accountability on Amazon’s part.  They deliver to the wrong address, deliver when they want, in spite of what their website states, their drivers will drive by your house multiple times before they actually deliver your package, their drivers park in the middle of the street and organize their trucks(police on my street have confronted the drivers multiple times), the drivers are on their phones while driving and delivering (which is disrespectful to the customer who is outside waiting for their package), the drivers blast their music as if they were teenagers trying to impress their peers. Amazon needs to get their vendors and drivers under control and build a professional image and take time to care about their customers.   Prime members do not receive prime benefits!!!!",2021-04-30 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,30.0,1183,194,41,6,0.0,0,4,2,1,Suspicious,ordered item stated specific delivery date order delivery date change contacted customer service state estimated date doesn’t say anything estimated delivery state order “x” time delivered specific date disconnected customer service twice i’m sick tired lack accountability amazon’s part deliver wrong address deliver want spite website state driver drive house multiple time actually deliver package driver park middle street organize truckspolice street confronted driver multiple time driver phone driving delivering disrespectful customer outside waiting package driver blast music teenager trying impress peer amazon need get vendor driver control build professional image take time care customer prime member receive prime benefit,0.7980039647608348,0.2019960352391652,0.10880538418395962,0.2,0.4227590944563745,42.27590944563745,Low Trust
Chris Drake,/users/608c17ff2087f7001a92be71,US,1.0,2021-04-30 14:45:33+00:00,1.0,Payment accepted Account Locked due to “Fraudulent activity”,"I ordered an expensive Drine to take progress reports for my jobsite, paid for next day delivery, payment was accepted and then Amazon locked my account. So, no next day delivery, no drone for 5 days and they will get back with me in 24 hrs. I used Amazon instead of buying directly from DJI MAVIC because of the delivery time.Save some trouble, order direct. At least no one there will “flag”your account and stop your purchase on their time. We are the customer hiring them to deliver and paying extra for their security algorithm. A week into this and no product and they will get back with me in 24 hrs. DEAL DIRECT. It’s cheaper. Amazon",2021-04-30 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,30.0,641,117,60,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered expensive drine take progress report jobsite paid next day delivery payment accepted amazon locked account next day delivery drone day get back hr used amazon instead buying directly dji mavic delivery timesave trouble order direct least one “flag”your account stop purchase time customer hiring deliver paying extra security algorithm week product get back hr deal direct it’s cheaper amazon,0.004228876486148026,0.995771123513852,0.06561974200785194,0.2,0.8110095101584964,81.10095101584965,High Trust
William Oakes,/users/608bf9a1aeb5d30019ec33de,US,1.0,2021-04-30 12:36:39+00:00,1.0,"1984 HAPPENED, JUST IN 1986","Seems to be the New Wave, like all those banker's SS ""security teams, that intercepted your calls, posed sets of questions designed to be failed; and then locked you down.  Why?  So they would have your head to show off, as yet another impostor, intercepted.  And all the time rifling the till themselves.  Ok.  THIS wave is shutting down your comments, if there's one their thought police don't happen to like.  And this after letting a psychotic president rave half the day and night at a time, and for four YEARS (thanks, guys; and that would be Twitter).  Some Bezos flunky (NEVER a specific REASON given; not as if they need any), decided to shut me down, perhaps because I disliked a movie that he did; or just had a kill quota to meet.  Like I say, they don't give reasons.  So far, Google, Quora, and now (finally) Amazon, consecutively.  is anyone detecting a pattern in this?  I don't see the advantage, but if media shut you down, then good luck saying anything about anything.  Also, between the supreme court and Vladimir Putin, they can omit news that you need, and substitute whatever they wish to invent (it's called propaganda, and seems to be making a switch from politics to any and all topics).  So I got 86'd by these (within months).  Bezos, Zuckerberg, Gates (our American Putin); the big boys  are showing off their ability to shut you up or down.  In the meantime, the all American developed, and public, internet got marketed away by Obama, to the telecoms that are now sucking your blood.  Yes, 1984 has happened; it was just a little late.  You are now living in a Surveillance State.  Big Brother is watching; everything from your correspondence, to your geographic location, to the motions of your eyes (your iphone can do this, and does).",2021-04-30 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,30.0,1769,309,27,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,seems new wave like banker s security 