Dan C,/users/608719798ab228001a745a05,CA,2.0,2021-04-26 19:50:51+00:00,1.0,Almost hacked trying to set up Prime Video,"The other day while ordering an item I was offered a free trial of Prime. A short time later I tried to install Prime Video. While trying I got a message on my Smart TV with a 6 digit code and was told to go to a site and use that code to start setting up Video.I went to my pc and as soon as I entered the code I got a pop-up chat balloon and an error message. The chat said I would be receiving a call from a technician to help with the install. That is when I should have hung up.The technician called and spent over 45 minutes with me, while he had full access to my pc content. You see, he explained that I had a serious virus and that was why I couldn't set up Prime Video. But he could fix it. I finally caught on and went to my online banking and made sure the password was not there. He saw me do that and told me not to worry. That made me Panic!!I said I think you should get out of my system and he hung up.All I got from Amazon was initially a promise of support. Today all I got was defensiveness from Amazon Customer Service. When I asked if she was going to be defensive or help me with the problem she said ""If you would let me finish.."" the defensive comment was my only interjection.She ended by telling me not to worry they would take care of it... but I don't know the when or the how.Meantime I have had to cancel online banking,, with a bunch of utility payments coming due. I will have to get someone to check my system out. I am stressed.",2021-04-26 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,26.0,1463,296,42,8,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,day ordering item offered free trial prime short time later tried install prime video trying got message smart tv digit code told go site use code start setting videoi went pc soon entered code got popup chat balloon error message chat said would receiving call technician help install hung upthe technician called spent minute full acces