L C,/users/5f14d4b3ed6cc33460b2729e,US,4.0,2021-04-14 11:18:11+00:00,1.0,Where do I begin,"Where do I begin? Amazon shipping has become a nightmare.  They use UPS, USPS, and now Amazon Drivers.  UPS and the Amazon Drivers have left my packages in the wrong place so many times that I contacted Amazon and was assured that I could put in a request to ONLY have USPS ship items if they are fulfilled by Amazon. And right at this moment I am waiting for a package to be delivered, tracking it every few minutes, because they sent it UPS. Their reps are very polite, and they assure you all will be taken care of, and then they drop the ball. Shipping has definitely taken a turn for the worst. Amazon is in over their heads.",2021-04-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,14.0,630,120,16,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,begin amazon shipping become nightmare use ups usps amazon driver ups amazon driver left package wrong place many time contacted amazon assured could put request usps ship item fulfilled amazon right moment waiting package delivered tracking every minute sent ups rep polite assure taken care drop ball shipping definitely taken turn worst amazon head,0.019440081273636885,0.9805599187263632,0.06730229949523275,0.2,0.8037404192622281,80.3740419262228,High Trust
Erick Fidell,/users/60767c9e348d93001ad4b40f,US,1.0,2021-04-14 06:42:03+00:00,1.0,Amazon doesn't vet their Sellers--BEWARE!!,"I contacted Amazon and asked if a Seller was legit, as they were selling an Ashley Furniture sofa for 1/3 the price. They said, ""ABSOLUTELY!"" On that recommendation, I purchased 3 sofas. The tracking number said they were delivered to an address in Maryland. I, however, live in Florida. They contacted the Seller twice, I contacted the Seller 3 times, with no response. I noticed Amazon also sold this item and asked if they could send replacements as after 1 month, I had no sofas, I had no explanation of why the incorrect address was given to the seller (address hasn't changed in 3 years and never even been to Maryland!) and was out $1,300 for a month with NOTHING to show for it. Of course, they declined. Every rep I spoke with at Amazon said, ""Nothing we can do about it. But you can give us more money with a different Seller and hope for the best..."" Um, #HardPass. AMAZON vouched for the Seller, AMAZON took my money, AMAZON is willing to take MORE MONEY, but couldn't guarantee I'd get the sofas from another Seller and wasn't willing to send replacements from their own inventory. I've never met such apathetic Customer Service reps or a company that won't stand behind what's sold on their website.",2021-04-14 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,14.0,1213,216,42,5,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,contacted amazon asked seller legit selling ashley furniture sofa price said absolutely recommendation purchased sofa tracking number said delivered address maryland however live florida contacted seller twice contacted seller time response noticed amazon also sold item asked could send replacement month sofa explanation incorrect address given seller address hasnt changed year never even maryland month nothing show course declined every rep spoke amazon said nothing give u money different seller hope best um hardpass amazon vouched seller amazon took money amazon willing take money couldnt guarantee id get sofa another seller wasnt willing send replacement inventory ive never met apathetic customer service rep company wont stand behind whats sold website,0.24479846129826696,0.755201538701733,0.12114413909141895,0.2,0.7018295971691504,70.18295971691504,Medium Trust
