Venus,/users/5bedf018e669312d52682d93,US,25.0,2021-04-13 00:39:45+00:00,2.0,Allowing scams on their site,"The company refused to take action when I sent them physical evidence in the form of emails and screenshots of one of their sellers scamming people and asking others (including me) to join in to help for a cut of free merchandise. I contacted them twice! First I received a ""does not go against guidelines"" spiel, because no-one obviously even read the message. I went through the steps that it said to take if I thought it needed a second review. The second time they didn't even bother to write me anything.    Almost immediately after, I guess I bothered them too much with not wanting people to get scammed, because they blacklisted me from being able to write reviews and took all my old ones down. Saying that my review activity was ""suspicious"". Oh yes, because detailed reviews and being nice are now signs of some sort of review conspiracy to make the world a better place! What's really suspicious, is that they are allowing (and by inaction encouraging) fraud on their customers. I think they don't care how they get the money, even if those products killed someone, they will ignore complaints because they want their cut of those sellers money.   I contacted them regarding my blacklisting with a very polite message, and yet again I have received no reply.  Just remember guys, anything you can get from Amazon, you can get anywhere else",2021-04-13 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,13.0,1351,235,28,5,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,company refused take action sent physical evidence form email screenshots one seller scamming people asking others including join help cut free merchandise contacted twice first received go guideline spiel noone obviously even read message went step said take thought needed second review second time didnt even bother write anything almost immediately guess bothered much wanting people get scammed blacklisted able write review took old one saying review activity suspicious oh yes detailed review nice sign sort review conspiracy make world better place whats really suspicious allowing inaction encouraging fraud customer think dont care get money even product killed someone ignore complaint want cut seller money contacted regarding blacklisting polite message yet received reply remember guy anything get amazon get anywhere else,0.35531128270544504,0.644688717294555,0.13180033651149747,0.4,0.9487044259495769,94.8704425949577,High Trust
