Steven,/users/561d346f0000ff0001e2b9cc,US,4.0,2021-04-12 14:48:44+00:00,2.0,I think the concept is a good business…,"I think the concept is a good business model. I am an Amazon Prime member and my number 1 problem with them is the delivery date. Often when ordering it tells me I will receive my order in 2 days (which is one of the reasons I pay to be a prime member). After not receiving some orders when promised I log into my account to find out delivery date has been extended, sometimes up to 2-3 weeks. I think this should be disclosed when looking to place the order not after the fact. I also noticed that now Walmart, Etsy and others have cheaper prices on products that I use quite often.",2021-04-12 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,12.0,583,113,39,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,think concept good business model amazon prime member number problem delivery date often ordering tell receive order day one reason pay prime member receiving order promised log account find delivery date extended sometimes week think disclosed looking place order fact also noticed walmart etsy others cheaper price product use quite often,0.0059557062608023795,0.9940442937391977,0.0633763320246775,0.4,1.1096974132745343,110.96974132745343,High Trust
