Lindsey,/users/5b634bde4de5666d34a19a29,US,4.0,2021-04-11 17:48:24+00:00,1.0,"For your Amazon,","For your Amazon,Been a customer for well over a decade. Lately,  you've hired local people to deliver packages and it's the worst business move you've made.  I've had nothing but issues for over a year.  Late packages,  lying about attempting to deliver,  and most of all,  GIVING ME THE WRONG PACKAGES ALL THE TIME.  That's not all though,  I wish it was.  How dare you ask your customers to drive to a Whole Foods or a Khols, spend time and gas money to drive to one of these stores to return an item that the customer had no part in delivering incorrectly.  THEN tell me that you'll make an EXCEPTION to refund my money because I refuse to drive to one of these places.  I'm quickly losing my desire to remain an Amazon customer.  That means not only discontinuing my shopping with you,  but deleting all of my Amazon accounts entirely.  Prime video,  audible,  grocery,  all of it.  I'm not going to keep pumping money into a company that makes billions and tells me that my refund is an exception to your poor business practices. Get it together,  Amazon.",2021-04-11 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,11.0,1060,189,16,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazonbeen customer well decade lately youve hired local people deliver package worst business move youve made ive nothing issue year late package lying attempting deliver giving wrong package time thats though wish dare ask customer drive whole food khols spend time gas money drive one store return item customer part delivering incorrectly tell youll make exception refund money refuse drive one place im quickly losing desire remain amazon customer mean discontinuing shopping deleting amazon account entirely prime video audible grocery im going keep pumping money company make billion tell refund exception poor business practice get together amazon,0.011346941114739151,0.9886530588852609,0.10600112170499158,0.2,0.8155267537836288,81.55267537836288,High Trust
