YLH,/users/5bbc467e4de5666d34ee9124,GB,6.0,2021-04-10 08:30:48+00:00,1.0,A cancer in our midst.,"I am an Amazon marketplace seller. I have also worked as an Amazon driver. It seems to me that Amazon does not care about its customers, it’s marketplace sellers or it’s drivers.  The place is run by robots. Robots do not empathise, know the difference between right and wrong, they don’t have morals or manners or care if you’re ill, need the loo, have been wronged, stolen from, overcharged, underpaid, been sent on a wild goose chase. Amazon are a cancer in our society and everyone is feeding it and allowing it to grow uglier and more invasive until one day we won’t be able to manage without them. EBay care about their customers and sellers. So do Onbuy and Etsy and all those independent retailers out there. Today I am sat here having been wronged once again by Amazon. It’s been how I earn my money. It’s been a very long, miserable hard slog for very little pay. Enough is enough. Goodbye Amazon. Neither me, my partner nor my children will be using you ever again.",2021-04-10 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,10.0,976,177,22,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon marketplace seller also worked amazon driver seems amazon care customer it’s marketplace seller it’s driver place run robot robot empathise know difference right wrong don’t moral manner care you’re ill need loo wronged stolen overcharged underpaid sent wild goose chase amazon cancer society everyone feeding allowing grow uglier invasive one day won’t able manage without ebay care customer seller onbuy etsy independent retailer today sat wronged amazon it’s earn money it’s long miserable hard slog little pay enough enough goodbye amazon neither partner child using ever,0.00934525395697323,0.9906547460430267,0.09927089175546831,0.2,0.8151815513726071,81.5181551372607,High Trust
