Sophie Emerson,/users/6069a9a1ebf30500197ecca5,GB,1.0,2021-04-04 11:57:30+00:00,1.0,Reduction in Amazon purchasing behaviour,"I was, up till recently a very active and avid Amazon customer, purchasing more than I could really afford to each month on very regular basis. Usually on frivolous items ordering just because I liked how something looked, or maybe because of the rave reviews. Etc..... Anyway, up until recently I would turn a blind eye to how Amazon made their money, because it suited me to. Well no more! I am appalled at the revised returns policy, yes it's bad enough that we have to pay to sometimes return items(although I do partially understand the reasoning behind, not that I am happy about it!) but it is the fact there were no CLEAR prior instructions that annoys the BeJesus out of me! These changes, these policy instructions should be made very clear and not hidden - so that it is clear to ALL concerned so they can make a WELL INFORMED decision whether they would still like to purchase the items or not. STOP BEING SO CONNIVING!!!!!!So, although there is a silver lining, it is with sadness that I have to inform Amazon, I shall only be purchasing essential items for the foreseeable future, items i cannot otherwise obtain elsewhere! (Good reason to save my money - many thanks for your assistance and consideration of my monetary wellbeing!!!)",2021-04-04 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,4.0,1248,219,40,5,0.0,0,13,2,1,Suspicious,till recently active avid amazon customer purchasing could really afford month regular basis usually frivolous item ordering liked something looked maybe rave review etc anyway recently would turn blind eye amazon made money suited well appalled revised return policy yes bad enough pay sometimes return itemsalthough partially understand reasoning behind happy fact clear prior instruction annoys bejesus change policy instruction made clear hidden clear concerned make well informed decision whether would still like purchase item stop connivingso although silver lining sadness inform amazon shall purchasing essential item foreseeable future item cannot otherwise obtain elsewhere good reason save money many thanks assistance consideration monetary wellbeing,0.9999997042943005,2.957056994823404e-07,0.12282669657879977,0.2,0.32456548716860967,32.456548716860965,Low Trust
Derrick Stringer Britford Display,/users/5b2660e64de5666d34a491aa,GB,5.0,2021-04-04 07:12:46+00:00,1.0,Let me start By saying. I like Amazon.,"Let me start. By saying. Normally. I think Amazon are great. And for this item. They gave me my money back. Straight away. But they ask for reviews. I gave one. This morning it was returned as they could not publish it on their site. You obviously. Cannot say. The truth.I purchased. I Percy pig. Easter egg for my wife. At a very high price I might add. But she wanted a Percy pig. I made the big mistake. Have open it. Just before I gave it to her. Not only was the box ripped. One of Percy's ears. Would broken off completely. And the packaging. Inside the box. Was almost nonexistent. In fact. It arrived. In bad condition. It was my fault for not checking it. When it arrived. But whoever packed it in this large box. Hadn't realised. There was just a bit of paper in there. Things move about. My headline. On their review. Was. I will never buy. An Easter egg. Online again. I also put having read. Other reviews. On their site. Which were all. Negative. I should have read them first as well. Once again. Amazon. Were great. On accepting, it should not. Have arrived like that. But it did. I also sent them photographs. Of the condition. Off the box. And of the egg.",2021-04-04 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,4.0,4.0,1173,221,38,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,let start saying normally think amazon great item gave money back straight away ask review gave one morning returned could publish site obviously cannot say truthi purchased percy pig easter egg wife high price might add wanted percy pig made big mistake open gave box ripped one percy ear would broken completely packaging inside box almost nonexistent fact arrived bad condition fault checking arrived whoever packed large box hadnt realised bit paper thing move headline review never buy easter egg online also put read review site negative read first well amazon great accepting arrived like also sent p