Minka,/users/605c731dcb1564001aebcdd1,GB,11.0,2021-03-25 12:01:26+00:00,1.0,Luring you to sign up for amazon prime without noticing,"Mixed experiences with Amazon overall, but one that outraged me recently that I want to warn of: My one star refers to amazon's sneaky way of making you a - of course paying - amazon prime member without you noticing.I discovered the charge on my credit card and started investigating since I did was not aware having signed up for Amazon Prime. It turns out that when finishing a regular amazon transaction, there is an ""offer"" to sign up for amazon prime. The way it is presented online, with colors, buttons etc. lures you easily into clicking that button. You think you are just confirming your transaction, while you actually signed up for a new service you did not want and that automatically starts charging monthly to your credit card. WATCH OUT!@amazon: very poor conduct",2021-03-25 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,3.0,25.0,780,135,55,10,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,mixed experience amazon overall one outraged recently want warn one star refers amazon sneaky way making course paying amazon prime member without noticingi discovered charge credit card started investigating since aware signed amazon prime turn finishing regular amazon transaction offer sign amazon prime way presented online color button etc lure easily clicking button think confirming transaction actually signed new service want automatically start charging monthly credit card watch outamazon poor conduct,0.03736389227004064,0.9626361077299593,0.07571508693213685,0.2,0.7964610712514071,79.6461071251407,High Trust
