Michael,/users/6043bec98c276200196ec89c,CA,2.0,2021-03-06 17:41:56+00:00,2.0,no way to give Amazon feedback,"A seller requested that I cancel an order with them; there is an Amazon bot that walks me down a decision tree but does not provide the right option or even an ""other"" option when cancelling the order. I tried finding a way to leave feedback about Amazon itself on the Amazon site to suggest how to correct the problem, but couldn't find anything. No option to leave feedback about Amazon through Amazon.",2021-03-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,3.0,6.0,404,73,30,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,seller requested cancel order amazon bot walk decision tree provide right option even option cancelling order tried finding way leave feedback amazon amazon site suggest correct problem couldnt find anything option leave feedback amazon amazon,0.032899426755345955,0.967100573244654,0.04094223219293326,0.4,1.0917387330609136,109.17387330609137,High Trust
AJ,/users/6043bd43dcb82000191f1299,ZA,2.0,2021-03-06 17:56:08+00:00,1.0,Run away,"Stay far, far away! Been a customer for many, many years, no problems, good service. Last week tried to buy something from the German site (I usually use the US site). In checkout, there was a message that I could earn a free credit if I topped up my gift card credit. Who wouldn't do that? So I topped up my gift card credit, returned to my purchase, completed checkout. All fine. Next day I received an email that I had ""violated the gift card terms"" and my account had been locked. Received a message that I had to prove I made the top-up. Did just that, sent a bank statement clearly showing the top-up transaction, my name and address. A day later got another message, ""we received your documents but we cannot unlock your account"". No reason given. Now I have no access to my account and Amazon basically still has my 88 euros. It's still there, in the account, loaded to my gift card, which they locked. To me that sounds a lot like they are simply taking money that is not theirs. Customer care keeps telling me they ""forwarded my request to the correct department"", followed by radio silence. If this is how they treat longtime customers I do not want to be a customer anymore. But I would really like my 88 euros back. Maybe this is how they got so rich, they simply take customer's money and then lock the accounts. Clever idea, but rather shady.",2021-03-06 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,3.0,6.0,1357,251,8,2,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,stay far far away customer many many year problem good service last week tried buy something german site usually use u site checkout message could earn free credit topped gift card credit wouldnt topped gift card credit returned purchase completed checkout fine next day received email violated gift card term account locked received message prove made topup sent bank statement clearly showing topup transaction name address day later got another message received document canno