MarkDw,/users/509ae620000064000126494d,BE,5.0,2021-03-03 17:31:32+00:00,1.0,Do not order here from abroad,"Do not order here from Belgium or other countries where your VISA or MC has a two step verification process!   I was trying to order something on AMAZON.COM, tried paying with it with VISA. That didn't work because AMAZON.COM has no permission to charge money on the card without the two step verification and their payment system isn't designed for the two-step-verification process.  MC was refused for the same reason.  So I bought online giftcards, redeemed them and ordered the product.  After 14 hours I received a mail that they saw 'suspicious' activity on my account concerning payments.   They closed my account, cancelled the order and didn't want to give a refund for the money.  Easy money for AMAZON I'd think.  Up to me now to file a complaint with a US authority, but from abroad it's not that simple.  I'll try my best.   But I wouldn't advise anyone to risk their money.",2021-03-03 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,3.0,3.0,888,153,29,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,order belgium country visa mc two step verification process trying order something amazoncom tried paying visa didnt work amazoncom permission charge money card without two step verification payment system isnt designed twostepverification process mc refused reason bought online giftcards redeemed ordered product hour received mail saw suspicious activity account concerning payment closed account cancelled order didnt want give refund money easy money amazon id think file complaint u authority abroad simple ill try best wouldnt advise anyone risk money,0.08278519646148652,0.9172148035385135,0.08581043185642176,0.2,0.7757694881405411,77.57694881405412,High Trust
