KIM,/users/5ee99a6abb64c0a0dd9c36a8,US,2.0,2021-02-21 06:59:20+00:00,1.0,Why does Amazon favor one race over the others?,"I used to love Amazon. I used AmazonSmile religiously, donating to the ASPCA. Now, they have a special category for black-owned businesses. Why is this not considered racist? Why don't they have the same option for other races? Better yet, why does the race of the business owner matter? Shouldn't the quality of the product be the primary concern? Why is it ok for them to favor one race over the others - which is, by the way, the very definition of racism. I will be taking my business elsewhere until Amazon realizes that the race of the business owner is not relevant... All businesses owners should be afforded the same treatment regardless of race.",2021-02-21 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,2.0,21.0,655,115,47,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used love amazon used amazonsmile religiously donating aspca special category blackowned business considered racist dont option race better yet race business owner matter shouldnt quality product primary concern ok favor one race others way definition racism taking business elsewhere amazon realizes race business owner relevant business owner afforded treatment regardless race,0.023594562123295894,0.9764054378767041,0.06449803701626472,0.2,0.8011023263416049,80.1102326341605,High Trust
