Marki,/users/6017c0c8a45078001a0c4b34,US,1.0,2021-02-01 09:02:09+00:00,1.0,Customer service has gone downhill,"Customer service has gone downhill. I’ve had multiple issues with returns, such as I shipped item back and Amazon didn’t process refund or said I didn’t return item. The issues were frustrating and it took unnecessary time to contact customer service, but usually in the past customer service was nice and able to resolve it quickly. This latest return was within the return window, processed on the last date and shipped on the last date (dropped off at ups the date it said to drop off, before the last shipment of the day) and I was still charged a restocking fee. I chatted customer service thinking maybe it was another glitch, since the last day of the return window and the last day to ship are cutting it close but are still within the window. This time customer service was terrible. Not only were the reps unfriendly, but they also kept stating the items needed to arrive at Amazon return center by that date. It doesn’t say that anywhere in the “free returns” policy or in the return label, it just says must be dropped off at ups by x date (which I did). The customer has no control over how long it takes for an item to get from the UPS store to the Amazon return center, but ok if that’s now the Amazon policy then fine just state it clearly when the order is placed and when the items are shipped back so the customer knows what to expect (I still don’t think this is the policy, I think it’s the date to have the item scanned at UPS, but the customer service rep was adamant that the ship by date was the date the item must arrive at Amazon return center - so maybe it truly has changed). Since the customer service rep was certain the ship by date for a return is when it must arrive at the Amazon return center and that’s why I was being changed a restocking fee, I then asked if I could provide feedback and share a screenshot from the return label showing that it stated to drop off at UPS by that date, not get to Amazon by that date. The customer service rep told me there was no way to provide feedback and didn’t seem to care at all. I asked about a chat transcript, rep said no way to get a transcript. I asked the rep to stay on a minute so I could grab screenshots to save, the rep promptly closed the chat and there was no way for me to get back to the chat. By this time I had wasted over an hour going in circles with the rep so I just gave up, if there’s no survey, no other way to provide feedback, no way to get a chat transcript then it seems like Amazon clearly doesn’t care how the customer service experience went anymore. I’ve considered getting prime for years and just never decided I needed it enough. Now I’m glad that I didn’t. Amazon used to pride itself on customer service and now they don’t seem to care at all since there was no avenue to provide feedback on the customer experience anywhere accessible. Even though I don’t have prime, I’ve had an Amazon account for many years and now I’m really thinking I’ll close it. Bugs and issues in the app, with shipping, returns, products etc. inevitably do happen sometimes so having the backbone of good customer service is key to feeling like I can trust a retailer. Maybe the experience is different if you’re not prime, but you’d still think that even a non prime account with many years worth of various purchases would be a valued enough customer and apparently is not valued anymore. I’d rather deal with other businesses that have much better customer service like target for day to day and Nordstrom for fashion. Ordering clothes online is always going to be hit or miss in terms of sizing so do yourself a favor and order from somewhere else with a much better return process and customer service in place to help if/when there are issues.",2021-02-01 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,2.0,1.0,3741,699,34,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,customer service gone downhill i’ve multiple issue return shipped item back amazon didn’t process refund said didn’t return item issue frustrating took unnecessary time contact customer service usually past customer service nice able resolve quickly latest return within return window processed last date shipped last date dropped ups date said drop last shipment day still charged restocking fee chatted customer service thinking maybe another glitch since last day return window last day ship cutting close still within window time customer service terrible rep unfriendly also kept stating item needed arrive amazon return center date doesn’t say anywhere “free returns” policy return label say must dropped ups x date customer control long take item get ups store amazon return center ok that’s amazon policy fine state clearly order placed item shipped back customer know expect still don’t think policy think it’s date item scanned ups customer service rep adamant ship date date item must arrive amazon return center maybe truly changed since customer service rep certain ship date return must arrive amazon return center that’s changed restocking fee asked could provide feedback share screenshot return label showing stated drop ups date get amazon date customer service rep told way provide feedback didn’t seem care asked chat transcript rep said way get transcript asked rep stay minute could grab screenshots save rep promptly closed chat way get back chat time wasted hour going circle rep gave there’s survey way provide feedback way get chat transcript seems like amazon clearly doesn’t care customer service experience went anymore i’ve considered getting prime year never decided needed enough i’m glad didn’t amazon used pride customer service don’t seem care since avenue provide feedback customer experience anywhere accessible even though don’t prime i’ve amazon account many year i’m really thinking i’ll close bug issue app shipping return product etc inevitably happen sometimes backbone good customer service key feeling like trust retailer maybe experience different you’re prime you’d still think even non prime account many year worth various purchase would valued enough customer apparently valued anymore i’d rather deal business much better customer service like target day day nordstrom fashion ordering clothes online always going hit miss term sizing favor order somewhere else much better return process customer service place help ifwhen issue,0.004626862354301367,0.9953731376456987,0.3920358945597308,0.2,0.8760937477347955,87.60937477347956,High Trust
