MC,/users/55c0bed30000ff0001d18f5d,GB,5.0,2021-01-30 13:04:01+00:00,1.0,Poor arrangement for delivery,"Someone purchased a surprise gift for me via Amazon but when they went to deliver, as I knew I hadn’t ordered it, and wasn’t expecting anything from Amazon I wasn’t sure. They were unable to advise me who placed  the order and insisted on taking UD / date of birth details.   Tried to explain i’ve been  a victim of fraud before hence as they couldn’t tell me who organised the delivery, I wasn’t comfortable giving date of birth. So he refused to let me have my gift, he then stormed off with my gift and slammed our gate very aggressively damaging paint work. His conduct was unacceptable. I would advise anyone purchasing a gift for delivery not to use Amazon- they don’t record who ordered the delivery (there are so many companies that put the name of the person the gift is from) and as a result leave you in a position of not knowing if it was genuine or fraud I am trying to see if the friend who made the purchase can get her money back",2021-01-30 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,1.0,30.0,945,178,29,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,someone purchased surprise gift via amazon went deliver knew hadn’t ordered wasn’t expecting anything amazon wasn’t sure unable advise placed order insisted taking ud date birth detail tried explain i’ve victim fraud hence couldn’t tell organised delivery wasn’t comfortable giving date birth refused let gift stormed gift slammed gate aggressively damaging paint work conduct unacceptable would advise anyone purchasing gift delivery use amazon don’t record ordered delivery many company put name person gift result leave position knowing genuine fraud trying see friend made purchase get money back,0.01755697260341889,0.9824430273965811,0.09983174425126191,0.2,0.8111878625485429,81.11878625485429,High Trust
