schvitzing,/users/600ca0d149f2830019289a11,US,1.0,2021-01-23 22:21:00+00:00,1.0,Amazon robbed me of $300,"My account was hacked. My P/W [changed] and Prime card (cancelled and replaced]  were used only with Amazon purchases. Five $100 gift card charges appeared on my bank statement, but NOT on my order history on Amazon.  Phone calls and chats all ended with promise to have ""security team"" contact me in 24-48 hrs.  Several 24-48 hr periods and phone call/ chats have passed since I contacted Amazon in November.  No response.Amazon temporarily credited my Prime card, then recharged my new card!Chase VISA, servicer of the Prime card, has billed me, and instructs me to resolve with non-responding Amazon.Amazon is totally opaque. There is no way to elevate communication beyond whomever takes your call or chat.Amazon hasn't acknowledge a breech of their system, which is the only way these gift cards could have been processed.I have stopped doing business with Amazon.  I also continue to pursue credits to my account.Walmart, Costco, Target, Ace Hardware, Chewy, Staples, or anyone else with on-line service will have my business.",2021-01-23 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,1.0,23.0,1032,166,24,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,account hacked pw changed prime card cancelled replaced used amazon purchase five gift card charge appeared bank statement order history amazon phone call chat ended promise security team contact hr several hr period phone call chat passed since contacted amazon november responseamazon temporarily credited prime card recharged new cardchase visa servicer prime card billed instructs resolve nonresponding amazonamazon totally opaque way elevate communication beyond whomever take call chatamazon hasnt acknowledge breech system way gift card could processedi stopped business amazon also continue pursue credit accountwalmart costco target ace hardware chewy staple anyone else online service business,0.04644132517636809,0.9535586748236319,0.09310151430173864,0.2,0.7953996402721