Sylvie Shultz,/users/5d500b776b4d2ef4382799c8,GB,2.0,2021-01-18 17:18:56+00:00,1.0,My review was censored,"My review was censored. I was checking some vide courses on amazon prime. Wrote 3 reviews of them. 2 with 5 stars and the last one with 4 because the course teacher mentions over and over a pdf file which supposed to be a great part of this french learning course but the pfd file is nowhere to be found. I noticed that one reviewer before me noticed the same. Other than that I was very polite and complimented the course teacher who was really great and the main reason why I wanted to write and post the review. Then amazon sent me an email that this last review did not meet their standards like the use of profanities and it might not be up to the point. I was shocked. Why bother writing a review if they can do whatever they want with it? Possibly this course is not very popular, had very few ratings and the point of it not having a pdf attached (as it should) would be quite discouraging for prospective buyers. Shame on amazon! every time when I manage to forget how horrible they are they manage to remind me.",2021-01-18 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,1.0,18.0,1021,195,22,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,review censored checking vide course amazon prime wrote review star last one course teacher mention pdf file supposed great part french learning course pfd file nowhere found noticed one reviewer noticed polite complimented course teacher really great main reason wanted write post review amazon sent email last review meet standard like use profanity might point shocked bother writing review whatever want possibly course popular rating point pdf attached would quite discouraging prospective buyer shame amazon every time manage forget horrible manage remind,0.2793182567429973,0.7206817432570027,0.10936623667975323,0.2,0.6822141189644519,68.22141189644519,Medium Trust
