Malvain,/users/5fef7102750ed7001936f9ac,US,1.0,2021-01-01 19:09:35+00:00,1.0,Racial Profiling of Customers at Amazon.com,"I recently contacted Amazon regarding my account being unable to review.  I was pointed to a paragraph on their ToS saying I broke their rules.  I've reviewed the ToS in depth and honestly did not break any rules.  The only thing that I can think of remotely being correlated is I'm chinese with obviously a chinese last name.  On their ToS they listed 5 reasons with regards to why they ban a customer.  Three reasons has to do with receiving product / discount for a review.  Since I didn't do that it couldn't be the reason.  One reason had to be someone took over my amazon account which did not happen.  So that just leaves the last reason (below) which leads me to believe Amazon.com actively utilizes racial profiling of their customers and sellers.-- Elements of the account indicate a relationship to sellers, publishers, or other reviewers of the products you review.Based on the above reason, Amazon thinks I have to be related to a seller.  I am of chinese descent with an extremely common chinese last name.  And because I've purchased inexpensive china made product sold by chinese sellers (which one of these sellers likely have the same last name as me) .  That allows Amazon to racially link me between those sellers and me.I think for an ecommerce platform being so big, to exhibit racial profiling is extremely unethetical and injust.  People need to speak up more about this type of poor behavior.",2021-01-01 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,1.0,1.0,1417,245,43,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently contacted amazon regarding account unable review pointed paragraph tos saying broke rule ive reviewed tos depth honestly break rule thing think remotely correlated im chinese obviously chinese last name tos listed reason regard ban customer three reason receiving product discount review since didnt couldnt reason one reason someone took amazon account happen leaf last reason lead believe amazoncom actively utilizes racial profiling customer seller element account indicate relationship seller publisher reviewer product reviewbased reason amazon think related seller chinese descent extremely common chinese last name ive purchased inexpensive china made product sold chinese seller one seller likely last name allows amazon racially link seller mei think ecommerce platform big exhibit racial profiling extremely unethetical injust people need speak type poor behavior,0.013616124803871575,0.9863838751961285,0.13740886146943354,0.2,0.820673709891951,82.0673709891951,High Trust
Wise Wolf,/users/5acee70b4de5666d34f3376b,US,29.0,2021-01-01 16:05:41+00:00,3.0,I wish that they would let me choose what packaging material I want to use for my order.,"Amazon.com is a website so huge that its impossible to ignore their impact on society and retail as a whole, they have driven several competitors into bankruptcy including mom and pop stores who cant compete on price, small/medium sized competitors by lowering their prices on products (like baby products) which forces their small/medium sized competitor to lower prices to compete with Amazon and then after they go out of business Amazon will raise their prices when there is no competition around (this has been in news articles). Amazon has also been in the news for things like their poor treatment of fulfillment center employees by timing how many seconds they take to pick an order and pack it, limiting bathroom breaks, and making workers work during Covid-19 even though several of their employees got Covid-19 in their fulfillment centers.  So why do you ask do i keep buying from a company like this? for one simple reason, convenience. Amazon has a huge selection of products, they allow for easy and FREE returns within 30 days where other competitors charge restocking fees for returns and make returns at customer expense for shipping costs. Amazon also has a presence in many countries, ive purchased stuff from Amazon Japan, Amazon UK and had the items shipped to the United States very easily.So why did I rate Amazon.com 3/5? well because while they may be very convenient to buy from they also have very poor packaging and dont let customers specify what kind of packaging they want their items shipped in. Amazon has gotten some heat from environmental groups trying to get them to cut down on plastic and cut down on cardboard boxes in the past and we still see petitions online constantly being opened about their packaging. A simple solution would be to let the customer choose what kind of packaging they want their items shipped in during the checkout process and if theres an extra costs associated with more packaging materials then the customer can decide if they want to pay the extra costs or not. I would totally welcome the ability to choose what packaging material Amazon uses for my orders because I would love to be able to order things like art books, movies, collectibles, and video games from Amazon but whenever I try to order any of these items from Amazon they ship the items in a plastic padded envelope 99% of the time or a cardboard box without any packing paper or void fillers and when I finally receive the item it will be all scuffed up or dented during shipping, have a loose disc (movies and video games), or be damaged in some other way so I would have to go through the trouble of returning the item back to Amazon which isnt good for the environment either since it would costs more fuel and packaging material to be sent back to Amazon. The combination of Amazon's business practices, their poor treatment of fulfillment center employees, and their poor quality packaging which prioritizes getting the package to the customer as fast as possible over the condition that the items arrive in at their destination are the reasons why I gave Amazon a 3/5 score.",2021-01-01 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,1.0,1.0,3114,538,88,18,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazoncom website huge impossible ignore impact society retail whole driven several competitor bankruptcy including mom pop store cant compete price smallmedium sized competitor lowering price product like baby product force smallmedium sized competitor lower price compete amazon go business amazon raise price competition around news article amazon also news thing like poor treatment fulfillment center employee timing many second take pick order pack limiting bathroom break making worker work covid even though several employee got covid fulfillment center ask keep buying company like one simple reason convenience amazon huge selection product allow easy free return within day competitor charge restocking fee return make return customer expense shipping cost amazon also presence many country ive purchased stuff amazon japan amazon uk item shipped united state easilyso rate amazoncom well may convenient buy also poor packaging dont let customer specify kind packaging want item shipped amazon gotten heat environmental group trying get cut plastic cut cardboard box past still see petition online constantly opened packaging simple solution would let customer choose kind packaging want item shipped checkout process there extra cost associated packaging material customer decide want pay extra cost would totally welcome ability choose packaging material amazon us order would love able order thing like art book movie collectible video game amazon whenever try order item amazon ship item plastic padded envelope time cardboard box without packing paper void filler finally receive item scuffed dented shipping loose disc movie video game damaged way would go trouble returning item back amazon isnt good environment either since would cost fuel packaging material sent back amazon combination amazon business practice poor treatment fulfillment center employee poor quality packaging prioritizes getting package customer fast possible condition item arrive destination reason gave amazon score,0.0039325280206630574,0.996067471979337,0.30173864273696016,0.6,1.4583814645370605,145.83814645370606,High Trust
