Amy,/users/5bfe18e35483f4b8a91906ea,US,7.0,2020-12-19 20:46:23+00:00,1.0,A crazy Amazon Xbox Gift card purchase saga,"I have purchased a total of $2520 Xbox gift cards from Amazon for a research project. During my purchase process, I was told that Amazon suspected some fake purchase activities on my account and cancelled my orders and locked my account. After calling them, I was told several times that my account was restored and that I was good to go. That repeated a couple of times but I was able to purchase a total of $2520 Xbox gift cards.Then the fun started: When I redeemed the codes, the Microsoft Xbox system told me that some of the codes were already redeemed. The unredeemable codes added up to $610.So I contacted Amazon and was told to contact Microsoft/Xbox. I then contacted Microsoft/Xbox. After Microsoft/Xbox investigated this, they said that the $610 worth of gift codes were deactivated by Amazon before being sold to me. In other words, I received deactivated codes from Amazon.I then contacted Amazon again and was told to either dispute the $610 with my credit card company or continue asking if Microsoft/Xbox would re-issue me new codes of $610.Why asking a third party to pay for your mistakes? As of today, after three months of repeated conversation with Amazon, I am still not refunded for the $610 in total. What an unprofessional company that takes advantage of consumers and charge their money without offering the goods!",2020-12-19 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,12.0,19.0,1342,229,43,8,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,purchased total xbox gift card amazon research project purchase process told amazon suspected fake purchase activity account cancelled order locked account calling told several time account restored good go repeated couple time able purchase total xbox gift cardsthen fun started redeemed code microsoft xbox system told code already redeemed unredeemable code added contacted amazon told contact microsoftxbox contacted microsoftxbox microsoftxbox investigated said worth gift code deactivated amazon sold word received deactivated code amazoni contacted amazon told either dispute credit card company continue asking microsoftxbox would reissue new code asking third party pay mistake today three month repeated conversation amazon still refunded total unprofessional company take advantage consumer charge money without offering good,0.10361490517164978,0.8963850948283503,0.12843522153673584,0.2,0.7738795917215222,77.38795917215222,High Trust
