denvecsr,/users/5bab8ee44de5666d3460bcdd,US,6.0,2020-12-14 21:17:13+00:00,1.0,"Amazon, the worst company in the world when something goes wrong.","What Amazon has done to me and my grandson is disgusting. My grandson asked me for something for Christmas. I immediately went to Amazon to purchase it. Being 65 it's better I buy online then visit stores during Covid19. I received emails from Amazon 1.) on Dec 1st, order confirmation. 2.) on Dec 7th, my item has shipped and I should expect it by Dec 8th. After a few days waiting for item to arrive I started contacting Amazon. From one customer service (CS) rep to another rep, then supposedly one cs team leader to another cs team leader, I got the same answer they don't know what happened to my grandson's Christmas gift. They kept telling me that they can no longer give me my item I payed for and was told I would receive it proof of emails received by Amazon. I tried all over the web to find Amazon's Executive contact information. I called the executive office's where they would not give me any executive to talk to about my problem. I sent emails to a few executives but no answer as of yet, jeff at amazon being one of them. The only thing I can see is that when I purchased my item on Dec 1st it was selling for $129.99, now it up to $400.00. They must have seized my item to make more money selling it to someone else. How much more money does Jeff Bezos and Amazon want to make? So beware when Amazon screws you no one will help you.",2020-12-14 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,12.0,14.0,1351,258,65,11,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon done grandson disgusting grandson asked something christmas immediately went amazon purchase better buy online visit store covid received email amazon dec st order confirmation dec th item shipped expect dec th day waiting item arrive started contacting amazon one customer service c rep another rep supposedly one c team leader another c team leader got answer dont know happened grandson christmas gift kept telli