Roxas Sora,/users/5fc79c0b0a6ce00019bfe6dd,US,1.0,2020-12-02 13:52:19+00:00,1.0,Avoid Purchases at ALL Costs!,"I've avoided anything under the Amazon umbrella all my life, vowing not to buy from Amazon due to ethical concerns I heard about the company. Since my phone provider grants my household free Amazon Prime & Amazon Video, I started to invest into their products/shopping app. I tried to figure out within the app itself without any help if 1 return item from an entire order made at the same time during the same check out process would be credited back to the newly applied Amazon credit card line I opened or if it would be reapplied/readjusted elsewhere witin the entire order. I couldn't find the pricing within the app's purchase feature. I scrolled through and it wouldn't show me any adjustments made to the order purchase or at least signal out the new price order adjustments made via their checkout systems. Asking the customer service assistant was a great mistake. The interaction between client and service assistant was deplorable. There was a superiority complex and verbal colloquialism I had to mine through while using the app's texting chat feature. Other sites have better help assistance features that allow for pulling up an orders history and allowing the client to interact with all the purchase history via chat features automated interface. All it did was show my previous order and didn't let me cycle to the other order I was seeking to quell out my worries. I opted to chat with a human to help through my troubles; it only aggrievated the problem and was just a cycle of jargon from the customer service assistant that didn't help the situation. I was just trying to reassure myself a cancellation problem would be resolved but they just kept saying look ""this order is complete,"" completely ignoring the fact I was not talking about an old order of the same item already managed a month ago. I had to explain there was already an order I cancelled under the ""cancelled orders"" section, as I could not see the proof the complete process of the cancellation for the single item, where as other major corporate shopping websites there is an implemented ability to verify the process. The assistant was just copy/pasting order number they can view from their screen and calling them individual orders where as I knew they were all under the same cart and were processed separately and given separate order numbers for some unknown illogical reason other than to reclassify the shipments into another column to create customer difficulties. I had to go radio silent for a while and go searching once more for the actual answer I was looking for. I had to find the partial answer to my question under the view order details AFTER clicking on a random column of orders that don't initially list the entire amount spent on one round of order applied to a single cart checkout. The operating system is designed to confuse the consumer and never really find out how the mechanics are being handled. I pointed out the order once more into the chat even though the auto reply bubble said it was inactive and another agent would help me. No, it was the same person who responded crassly as if they had a grudge against me for ordering from the company that pays their check. They gaslighted and snarkly insisted there were no such adjustments made to that segmented order being processed and it was always given the entire gift card at checkout. That would make no sense since the singular item I had cancelled was at a $0.00 balance meaning the gift card had been applied onto that item before it's cancelled status, having previously been part of the overall order as well. I pointed this fact out to the customer service rep and they quipped out a long winded statement pressing the matter in a negative tone that all orders are given a small window immediately credit back any cancellation orders to the respective card (though, less calmly explained and more so typed out as if gritting their teeth through out the text schpeel. I'm certain the rep made my questions into an unbearable task, causing it to be long winding on purpose to amount to conflict and waste a customer's/consumer's/client's overall time.The overall conversation could have been resolved if the interface was more transparent with all their consumer's purchase history. The in-real life interaction just felt as if asking simple questions is seen as the most stupidest thing to do rather than being seen as a matter to be resolved within seconds with courtesy and precision. This problem will only continue further as the reps seem to feel entitled to belittle their customers and gaslight through an entire conversation without any negative repercussions handed out to them. There isn't even a report rep button hovering nearby or a way to scramble the chat for another agent to assist. The worst business practices I have ever seen",2020-12-02 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,12.0,2.0,4827,829,29,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ive avoided anything amazon umbrella life vowing buy amazon due ethical concern heard company since phone provider grant household free amazon prime amazon video started invest productsshopping app tried figure within app without help return item entire order made time check process would credited back newly applied amazon credit card line opened would reappliedreadjusted elsewhere witin entire order couldnt find pricing within apps purchase feature scrolled wouldnt show adjustment made order purchase least signal new price order adjustment made via checkout system asking customer service assistant great mistake interaction client service assistant deplorable superiority complex verbal colloquialism mine using apps texting chat feature site better help assistance feature allow pulling order history allowing client interact purchase history via chat feature automated interface show previous order didnt let cycle order seeking quell worry opted chat human help trouble