Colin.wilson,/users/583d64d70000ff000a5c0fb3,GB,21.0,2020-11-29 12:16:08+00:00,1.0,False Trade description,"HiI attempted to order a webcam for my pc today The webcam I have has stopped working, and I have a zoom meeting tomorrow.I ordered a webcam from Amazon which said Prime delivery by 10pm tonight after I purchased the item it came up Delivery Tuesday 1st Dec I couldn't believe it.So I cancelled that order then I ordered another webcam prime delivery by 10pm tonight again after purchasing the item it came up delivery Tuesday Dec 1st I then contacted Amazon the advisor took my details put me on hold for ages when she came back she asked me where it said today 10pm  I told her it was next to the camera being advertised I also explained this was the second time this had happened. She said it isn't saying that.When I went back online to check,every camera that said 10pm delivery had been changed to Tuesday 1st December This is terrible and Amazon should be stopped from doing this It is breaking the Trade descriptions act IMO I am sure this has happened to many other customers. Amazon sales teamIf you read this review Hang your heads in shame.",2020-11-29 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,11.0,29.0,1052,192,23,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,hii attempted order webcam pc today webcam stopped working zoom meeting tomorrowi ordered webcam amazon said prime delivery pm tonight purchased item came delivery tuesday st dec couldnt believe itso cancelled order ordered another webcam prime delivery pm tonight purchasing item came delivery tuesday dec st contacted amazon advisor took detail put hold age came back asked said today pm told next camera advertised also explained second time happened said isnt saying thatwhen went back online checkevery camera said pm delivery changed tuesday st december terrible amazon stopped breaking trade description act imo sure happened many customer amazon sale teamif read review hang head shame,0.034416932560061356,0.9655830674399386,0.1076836791923724,0.2,0.8043282695584438,80.43282695584438,High Trust
