JoAnna,/users/5fc290eb37e9dd001aa96c53,CA,1.0,2020-11-28 18:03:30+00:00,1.0,I purchased 14 items yesterday for…,"I purchased 14 items yesterday for Christmas for my children. The order was split into three shipping orders. One of my order came back “payment declined”, I checked my bank and there were charges on my account for those items. I emailed customer service and was advised that these charges were authorization charges and it was going to be refunded to me and therefore I should revise my payment. Furthermore they said it was a banking issue.I contacted my bank and was told there was no authorization charges or pending charges or refunds in process, that this was a legitimate charges from Amazon.I emailed customer service again. Again I get the same response as the first rep. but this time they tell me one of my items in my order was successfully charged and on its way to advance shipping. Ok, no problem, I see that charge, valid. There were two other items in this order. One item was charged before the item that was sent to shipping. Five transactions before. I explained to the rep. and still received the same answer, that it was my bank. The rep. stated in their email that if I had further questions or anything to send to reply directly to this email. I had screenshots of my banking to show the charges. So I emailed, “Mail Delivery Subsystem: Address not found.”Email number three. I’m irritated at this time. To no avail, I get the same robotic response email back as the first two.So I go into my account to try to cancel the order, this way I know for sure I’ll get my money back. “Error cannot cancel order.”24 hrs later I’m calling into customer service this time. I get a very nice polite gentleman who seemed very eager to help. 20 mins later after a few minutes of silence, “Hello? Are you still working on my account?”, ‘click’, phone disconnects.Second call into customer service. Not a very happy shopper now. Explained the situation for a fifth time now. Lady seem genuinely concerned. After some time, “Have you called your bank?” “Yes, I have.” “Ok. So there’s nothing we can do because this is a banking issue. We can cancel your order and you can reorder again.” “Ok but I’m going to lose the Black Friday prices, is there anything you can do to help offset it?” “No, your order was a declined payment therefore it’s not Amazon’s fault so there’s nothing to credit.” “Btw one of the items is now out of stock.” What?!!! In short I’m out two gifts for my kids and also out the money Amazon took from my bank. The five representatives were of no help! There was no compassion.",2020-11-28 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,11.0,28.0,2508,452,35,6,0.0,0,4,2,1,Suspicious,purchased item yesterday christmas child order split three shipping order one order came back “payment declined” checked bank charge account item emailed customer service advised charge authorization charge going refunded therefore revise payment furthermore said banking issuei contacted bank told authorization charge pending charge refund process legitimate charge amazoni emailed customer service get response first rep time tell one item order successfully charged way advance shipping ok problem see charge valid two item order one item charged item sent shipping five transaction explained rep still received answer bank rep stated email question anything send reply directly email screenshots banking show charge emailed “mail delivery subsystem address found”email number three i’m irritated time avail get robotic response email back first twoso go account try cancel order way know sure i’ll get money back “error cannot cancel order” hr later i’m calling customer service time get nice polite gentleman seemed eager help min later minute silence “hello still working account” ‘click’ phone disconnectssecond call customer service happy shopper explained situation fifth time lady seem genuinely concerned time “have called bank” “yes have” “ok there’s nothing banking issue cancel order reorder again” “ok i’m going lose black friday price anything help offset it” “no order declined payment therefore it’s amazon’s fault there’s nothing credit” “btw one item stock” short i’m two gift kid also money amazon took bank five representative help compassion,0.8720075531082985,0.12799244689170153,0.25350532809871,0.2,0.4146972890655928,41.469728906559276,Low Trust
