Sally Peyton Castles,/users/5fb599be2548ff001a6ee0c8,US,1.0,2020-11-18 22:02:06+00:00,2.0,Amazon ignores filters,"Amazon is a great site to find almost anything out there. If you are looking for a specific item they neither have it or they don't, and if they don't they will have something very similar. I have 90% success/satisfaction in finding what I'm looking for. In the remaining 10% of the time its a different story. Case in point:  I'm currently shopping for a pair of blue light reading glasses. Im a petite woman with a narrow face. In search Bar I type in,""women's blue light reading glasses in narrow width."" I also select women's and narrow in  the filter and sort section to eliminate everything else, as there are THOUSANDS to choose from. So.....You would expect women's narrow blue light readers right?  NOPE! The very first selections are  men's/women's blue light readers. Now obviously if the glasses are unisex they would look ridiculous on a skinny 97 lb woman. They do list women's only glasses, but no matter how you word it, amazon simply ignores the so called filters and you end up having to scroll through thousands of unisex glasses instead of having the convenience of shopping for women's only glasses. Needless to say, I did NOT waste my time with amazon. I went to the eyebops site, where customized shopping was successful, and I found a great pair of glasses in under 10 minutes. I don't know why Amazon chooses to ignore what the customer specifically wants. Why do they even have the filters? This has happened on more than a couple of occasions, and its definitely steering me away from amazon.",2020-11-18 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,11.0,18.0,1519,266,22,3,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon great site find almost anything looking specific item neither dont dont something similar successsatisfaction finding im looking remaining time different story case point im currently shopping pair blue light reading glass im petite woman narrow face search bar type inwomens blue light reading glass narrow width also select womens narrow filter sort section eliminate everything else thousand choose soyou would expect womens narrow blue light reader right nope first selection menswomens blue light reader obviously glass unisex would look ridiculous skinny lb woman list womens glass matter word amazon simply ignores called filter end scroll thousand unisex glass instead convenience shopping womens glass needless say waste time amazon went eyebops site customized shopping successful found great pair glass minute dont know amazon chooses ignore customer specifically want even filter happened couple occasion definitely steering away amazon,0.09992967819492392,0.9000703218050761,0.14918676388109928,0.4,1.079872513678758,107.98725136787579,High Trust
