Mystery Rosebud,/users/59fd00100000ff000addd363,GB,21.0,2020-11-17 17:21:18+00:00,1.0,Mis-sold Prime and account hacked.,"I tried to buy a product I liked and the process was spoilt by having to get rid of a Prime subscription I didn't want. I don't like having my bank details stored either, so unchecked this option, to get rid of my payment details being stored. I thought that was my right in the UK with our data protection laws. I then had an unknown purchase deduct money from my bank account by Amazon. I am now out of pocket. I had no idea that simply wanting to buy a product on Amazon would leave me in such distress. I feel so let down by the experience. Phoned Amazon to explain the data they held on me- how could they use my payment details when I had unchecked them to be stored? had been used against me and they said they would sort it in 24 hours and email me and I have heard nothing. I feel like I have had a crime happen against me and no way of getting it sorted. Amazon don't seem to care about me as a customer.",2020-11-17 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,11.0,17.0,914,184,34,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,tried buy product liked process spoilt get rid prime subscription didnt want dont like bank detail stored either unchecked option get rid payment detail stored thought right uk data protection law unknown purchase deduct money bank account amazon pocket idea simply wanting buy product amazon would leave distress feel let experience phoned amazon explain data held could use payment detail unchecked stored used said would sort hour email heard nothing feel like crime happen way getting sorted amazon dont seem care customer,0.02080928487065011,0.9791907151293499,0.10319685922602355,0.2,0.8102347294098796,81.02347294098796,High Trust
