David Simister,/users/59b1303c0000ff000ac52230,GB,35.0,2020-11-05 00:46:03+00:00,1.0,Learning about customer service,So this year so far 25 deliveries lost late or refunded. I spent some hilarious time with the chat team finding out   All the various little Amazon tricks for customers. I found out that there is something called supplier managed prime deliveries. Basically when the mug .. sorry customer clicks on the prime delivery only button there is a mass of suppliers who actually manage these products without having to use Amazon prime infrastructure at all. They use this awesome delivery process called second class Mail. And when the mug.. sorry customer has the audacity to question where their prime delivery is. Amazon can say no idea talk to the supplier. When the mug sorry customer says but I used prime delivery Amazon say yes but it’s supplier delivered prime... how stupid of we mugs not to realise that simple yet effective con trick.. I meant clearly explained shift of responsibility...,2020-11-05 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,11.0,5.0,894,151,31,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,year far delivery lost late refunded spent hilarious time chat team finding various little amazon trick customer found something called supplier managed prime delivery basically mug sorry customer click prime delivery button mass supplier actually manage product without use amazon prime infrastructure use awesome delivery process called second class mail mug sorry customer audacity question prime delivery amazon say idea talk supplier mug sorry customer say used prime delivery amazon say yes it’s supplier delivered prime stupid mug realise simple yet effective con trick meant clearly explained shift responsibility,0.031633429849516566,0.9683665701504834,0.08468872686483454,0.2,0.8011210304482086,80.11210304482086,High Trust
