Bryn Kai-Hendricks,/users/5f7fda79198b1000190c9dc9,CA,10.0,2020-10-16 03:47:47+00:00,3.0,"Good pricing, bad screw ups.","Good pricing, good products, but when they mess up, they mess up bad with little to no compensation.I’ve bought from Amazon many times.  When their customer service agents say someone will get back to you, know that they will never get back to you.  Have heard that at least a dozen separate times and never once has anyone got back to me.They can usually correct things pretty quick, but the problems thst get them there are usually pretty bad and they do nothing or very little to mitigate the issue.Overall I still buy from them because of the pricing but I am starting to slow down on purchases because their poor resolution on multiple problems has had me spend way too much time on the phone with them correcting their mistakes while I am actually paying to correct them for them, by being a customer.I have also caught them in their own policy lies and have it recorded where the agent refuses to put in writing what he says on the phone, even though he will put other things in writing.  I asked him directly; why will you say it on the phone to me and not put it in writing, he said because he isn’t obligated to do that.  Unbelievable.I think this company is dealing with the massive influx of sales during the pandemic and though I have little sympathy for the trillions in profit... overall they do pretty good job... when they mess up it can be pretty bad... but usually they don’t mess up and usually things will sort out.  I wish I could more easily support Canadian retailers though.",2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,16.0,1499,273,28,5,3.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,good pricing good product mess mess bad little compensationi’ve bought amazon many time customer service agent say someone get back know never get back heard least dozen separate time never anyone got back methey usually correct thing pretty quick problem thst get usually pretty bad nothing little mitigate issueoverall still buy pricing starting slow purchase poor resolution multiple problem spend way much time phone correcting mistake actually paying correct customeri also caught policy lie recorded agent refuse put writing say phone even though put thing writing asked directly say phone put writing said isn’t obligated unbelievablei think company dealing massive influx sale pandemic though little sympathy trillion profit overall pretty good job mess pretty bad usually don’t mess usually thing sort wish could easily support canadian retailer though,0.020006558654600784,0.9799934413453992,0.1531127313516545,0.6,1.4206192669430304,142.06192669430305,High Trust
Erick Hazama,/users/5f86373455a2c9001abe541d,CA,1.0,2020-10-13 23:24:40+00:00,1.0,Horrible Customer Service,"Received a gift card for my birthday. No claim code was found behind the peelable sticker, and scratching even further just showed the bare cardboard underneath. Contacted Amazon support and gave all other information and numbers from the card and receipt. Told me someone would call me the next day, which never happened. Called back again the next week and re-explained my whole situation, only for the lady to suggest I email their gift card department with photos of the card and receipt. No reply. Called again to ask what I am supposed to do, was suggested to go to the retail store where the card was purchased. I had very high doubts that they could do anything about it. I was correct. Called again (and explained the whole story again) and said no one had contacted me back whether through email or phone call. With all of the information from the card (except the claim code itself) and the receipt, Amazon said they cannot find the card in their system and cannot do anything about it. Every phone call ended with a suggestion of emailing their gift card department, which oddly enough does not have a direct line that I could be transferred to. All of a sudden 5 individual representatives e-mailed me saying that they would look into it and asked for the exact same information that I have provided several times. Not one of them e-mailed me back after sending the information they requested. How does Amazon not have a record of a card that they manufacture, each with its own unique serial number and barcode? How is it that the only way to access the cards information is through the claim code, which is the very thing that I am missing, and the sole purpose of my issue? 3 weeks, 5 phone calls, and 7 email chains later, I have decided that this piece of cardboard belongs in the trash, just like the usefulness of their service center. Amazon will never fall, but everyone needs to know that their service is inadequate, and the knowledge that their representatives have is incompetent.",2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,13.0,2006,355,25,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,received gift card birthday claim code found behind peelable sticker scratching even showed bare cardboard underneath contacted amazon support gave information number card receipt told someone would call next day never happened called back next week reexplained whole situation lady suggest email gift card department photo card receipt reply called ask supposed suggested go retail store card purchased high doubt could anything correct called explained whole story said one contacted back whether email phone call information card except claim code receipt amazon said cannot find card system cannot anything every phone call ended suggestion emailing gift card department oddly enough direct line could transferred sudden individual representative emailed saying would look asked exact information provided several time one emailed back sending information requested amazon record card manufacture unique serial number barcode way access card information claim code thing missing sole purpose issue week phone call email chain later decided piece cardboard belongs trash like usefulness service center amazon never fall everyone need know service inadequate knowledge representative incompetent,0.009882339504612906,0.9901176604953871,0.19910263600673023,0.2,0.8348793574490396,83.48793574490396,High Trust
James Mulford,/users/5f86034c8bc2c800195a3867,US,1.0,2020-10-13 19:43:13+00:00,1.0,If I could give a zero I would have,"If I could give a zero I would have. I would guess that out of every 10 orders at least 2 do not let there gurantee delivery date, and a few are lost and never delivered. I placed a order on Thursday the ⁸th of October, the items had a gurantee delivery date of Saturday the 10th. Saturday it showed them out for delivery, but never were delivered. I checked later that evening to find out that the had been a delay in transit and now would be delivered between the 11th and 12th. Both days came and went and never delivered. Tracked via Amazon to find out if still says the same thing, and now states it may be lost. I contacted customer support to ask them, and they told me they would refund my account, but could not reship the items because they were from a outside vendor. I then asked what was the point of a Amazon gurantee if it was not fulfilled. He proceeded to tell me that this is what Amazon assumes it will be delivered. I then asked if he had ever opened a dictionary to read the definition of gurantee, because unless there is some other definition of gurantee it means something totally different than when Amazon assumes. He then left the chat, someone else entered, but had nothing relevant to say other than I'll pass this along too the proper department. I sure would like the contact for this other department to see if they are any help, although I highly doubt it will get myself or anyone else anywhere with this company.",2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,13.0,1447,271,35,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,could give zero would would guess every order least let gurantee delivery date lost never delivered placed order thursday ⁸th october item gurantee delivery date saturday th saturday showed delivery never delivered checked later evening find delay transit would delivered th th day came went never delivered tracked via amazon find still say thing state may lost contacted customer support ask told would refund account could reship item outside vendor asked point amazon gurantee fulfilled proceeded tell amazon assumes delivered asked ever opened dictionary read definition gurantee unless definition gurantee mean something totally different amazon assumes left chat someone else entered nothing relevant say ill pas along proper department sure would like contact department see help although highly doubt get anyone else anywhere company,0.007207410845231518,0.9927925891547685,0.1519910263600673,0.2,0.8267944998493977,82.67944998493977,High Trust
Jewels,/users/5d0cab15920ea3d37f387c27,US,8.0,2020-10-13 16:04:58+00:00,1.0,Cust. Service and Fraud Dept. What a JOKE!,"My account was hacked and someone was using my email account and writing terrible reviews under my name, I spoke to both departments because I now am not able to leave reviews and all reviews I have left have been removed. They said they would have their ""Team"" look into this and solve this issue for me! That's funny, what I did get was several emails telling me about their ""guidelines"" for reviews and fraudulent activity.And 1 very insulting email almost implying that my claims are false!I have since canceled my prime membership and will find an alternative company to order from. They are just getting to Big for there Pants!",2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,13.0,633,111,42,8,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,account hacked someone using email account writing terrible review name spoke department able leave review review left removed said would team look solve issue thats funny get several email telling guideline review fraudulent activityand insulting email almost implying claim falsei since canceled prime membership find alternative company order getting big pant,0.8125601796311221,0.18743982036887785,0.062254627033090294,0.2,0.406170835591057,40.6170835591057,Low Trust
shannon bellefleur,/users/598a2b8f0000ff000ab91d8f,US,6.0,2020-10-13 15:28:17+00:00,1.0,amazon support calls hacked - CAREFUL!,"I have now had calls to amazon support hijacked twice - hackers somehow intercept the transfer, or the call drops and the 'amazon' person who calls immediately after is not actually from amazon. So now I'm contesting 100s of dollars in fake purchases and cancelling credit cards again. cancelling prime also cost me dozens of digital movies and books I've purchased over the years. Amazon needs to clean house and secure their customers information!",2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,13.0,449,74,38,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,call amazon support hijacked twice hacker somehow intercept transfer call drop amazon person call immediately actually amazon im contesting dollar fake purchase cancelling credit card cancelling prime also cost dozen digital movie book ive purchased year amazon need clean house secure customer information,0.04214726955066652,0.9578527304493335,0.04150308468872686,0.2,0.7872269821624122,78.72269821624121,High Trust
Jennifer Herges,/users/5f85c12aabde140019cd8e13,US,1.0,2020-10-13 15:01:06+00:00,2.0,Trade-in failure,I attempted to trade-in a an old kindle for a new one. After they received my kindle I was told it was not in good enough condition to receive the credit. I was charged for the $30 credit I already used and asked to have my kindle sent back to me as it was still in working condition. Amazon sent me the wrong kindle back along with a speaker that was not mine. I attempted to contact customer service during the pandemic unsuccessfully. I recently made contact with them and the only thing I wanted was my kindle back. Unfortunately that was not an option and all I received was the $30 credit back. I’m lucky I received that back but ultimately am still out a perfectly good tablet. Overall I would caution people on trading items in as the company does not make it right if the item is lost.,2020-10-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,13.0,794,151,16,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,attempted tradein old kindle new one received kindle told good enough condition receive credit charged credit already used asked kindle sent back still working condition amazon sent wrong kindle back along speaker mine attempted contact customer service pandemic unsuccessfully recently made contact thing wanted kindle back unfortunately option received credit back i’m lucky received back ultimately still perfectly good tablet overall would caution people trading item company make right item lost,0.019046820014052977,0.980953179985947,0.08468872686483454,0.4,1.1074143353659402,110.74143353659403,High Trust
