J Rene,/users/5f7a45faedcf385f0df910eb,US,1.0,2020-10-04 23:38:43+00:00,1.0,Important Info when dealing with A to Z and Amazon,"At Amazon the customer service representatives are not trained well and Amazon does not care. For instance, I bought a $ 5373.98 zero turn motor from a third party seller on Amazon. I had to summit an A to Z claim because I received a damaged unusable mower due to a crushed mower deck underneath unit. I won the claim at first but an Amazon employee  told me that I won it and since my banking services (Amazon visa credit card) due date was in a day or two,  he told me to dispute it with credit card, because it was  refunded and I wouldn’t be penalized for the dispute.  So A to Z took refund back, if you dispute the amount on your credit card A to Z won’t honor their refund.   Amazon didn’t care even if I had submitted a  Notarized witness statement of a friend visiting and who heard speaker phone calls.  Also had an witness to mover problems. Then Amazon told me to cancel dispute again. That this change would get my refund back.  Again she witnessed the speaker phone conversation. I just got lucky she was here.  Amazon took no responsibility for their workers statements concerning making or canceling the  credit card dispute in the first place and then they just dropped it.  They would not pay the return shipping and the seller will not.  This seller had bad BBB score and complaints. So I have re disputed with credit card with no other recourse. So Amazon is not your friend. So started shopping others sites with free shipping and returns. Wow I beat Amazon prices to heck and back. From 50 to 15 percent on every item plus no tax, too.  I took a friends new monthly statement of $4376.00 and shopped  those items. (They paid their bill off every month like I do.) The same exacted items, He would of saved big nearly $1000.00by buying with other non Amazon sellers was amazing (with free shipping and returns! WOW This was a shock. I think he is returning most of them. I told him to be careful with too many returns, (he likes prime streaming services,) they would bar him from Amazon, if they received to many returns.  I have decided I want to help people wake up and see the real Amazon. I want them to use Amazon not let Amazon use them.  I have Several meetings arranged with different groups this month. I will address and make aware of the Ins and outs with Amazon. I call it “Amazon Ain’t Your Friend”. I compare Amazon to Sears in the late1800- 1930. And Amazon will fall too.  I just do not ever want Amazon to rip off another person. They obviously don’t check out their sellers. At the end of this month, I am canceling prime ASAP. I am not stupid, I want to finish using bonus points. Got 40 dollars to go. You can keep your Amazon-visa credit card and used your points against your statement balance. Amazon has become an American Bad Habit and addiction. It would be a Tragedy for Americans to be left with only Amazon, once every other retailer goes bust because of them! Then u will be at the mercy of Amazon the Almighty!   I got a car and truck sign ordered “Amazon ain’t your friend”. So a new adventure awaits me. Good Luck. If you would like for me to give a presentation for your group, just email me, no can’t leave an email  but here’s my phone number 870-723-3625, send me a text, Attention Amazon issues. The presentation is free in the continental USA at this time. Also if I can help let me know.  I will check it out, but my opinion is Amazon doesn’t want their real policies known. I didn’t know you would lose an A to Z refund if amount was disputed on Amazon credit card. Who would of known. I couldn’t find anything information concerning A toZ refunds. This has never happened on eBay or pay pal. I had an 7800.00 dispute due the purchase of a truck. The engine blew up after delivery. I got my money back. Guys,  we the customers created a monster retailer, they have sold our information and got rich doing it. So that’s why I am doing this. I Hope I can help.  I bought a vlogging equipment from another business and returned the one from Amazon. Saved 50 bucks! Maybe You Tube is next step for me. I am retired.  So again Amazon Ain’t Your Friend, Pal!",2020-10-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,4.0,4115,764,50,10,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,amazon customer service representative trained well amazon care instance bought zero turn motor third party seller amazon summit z claim received damaged unusable mower due crushed mower deck underneath unit claim first amazon employee told since banking service amazon visa credit card due date day two told dispute credit card refunded wouldn’t penalized dispute z took refund back dispute amount credit card z won’t honor refund amazon didn’t care even submitted notarized witness statement friend visiting heard speaker phone call also witness mover problem amazon told cancel dispute change would get refund back witnessed speaker phone conversation got lucky amazon took responsibility worker statement concerning making canceling credit card dispute first place dropped would pay return shipping seller seller bad bbb score complaint disputed credit card recourse amazon friend started shopping others site free shipping return wow beat amazon price heck back percent every item plus tax took friend new monthly statement shopped item paid bill every month like exacted item would saved big nearly buying non amazon seller amazing free shipping return wow shock think returning told careful many return like prime streaming service would bar amazon received many return decided want help people wake see real amazon want use amazon let amazon use several meeting arranged different group month address make aware in out amazon call “amazon ain’t friend” compare amazon sears late amazon fall ever want amazon rip another person obviously don’t check seller end month canceling prime asap stupid want finish using bonus point got dollar go keep amazonvisa credit card used point statement balance amazon become american bad habit addiction would tragedy american left amazon every retailer go bust u mercy amazon almighty got car truck sign ordered “amazon ain’t friend” new adventure awaits good luck would like give presentation group email can’t leave email here’s phone number send text attention amazon issue presentation free continental usa time also help let know check opinion amazon doesn’t want real policy known didn’t know would lose z refund amount disputed amazon credit card would known couldn’t find anything information concerning toz refund never happened ebay pay pal dispute due purchase truck engine blew delivery got money back guy customer created monster retailer sold information got rich that’s hope help bought vlogging equipment another business returned one amazon saved buck maybe tube next step retired amazon ain’t friend pal,0.8835377466143495,0.11646225338565053,0.4284913067863152,0.2,0.4439293880500883,44.39293880500883,Low Trust
No name,/users/5f7a3f8dc831f2500752e1bb,US,1.0,2020-10-04 21:34:35+00:00,1.0,Unnecessary negative return experience,"On phone approx 4.5 hours to resolve issue w/ladder-collapsed while my employee was on it. Bought ladder on Amazon,end of May. Alerted them to the issue 9-22-20. Waited for manufacture response for return, need money to buy replacement ladder. Tried return chat route, waste of time. First person talked to-helpful from NC-after 2 hours, put me on hold-got unintentionally disconnected. Emailed damaged ladder pictures to Amazon. Called Amazon CS back to complete what had to be done to get ladder money back, waste of time talking to Amazon foreign representatives, insisted transfer to US. Christol B answered-disdainful, disrespectful-helped me decide discontinue Amazon purchasing. Next day received email I would be getting my refund. What they put me through to get refund ridiculous and unacceptable. $80. Ladder was crappy, failed first time used it.",2020-10-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,4.0,858,133,38,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,phone approx hour resolve issue wladdercollapsed employee bought ladder amazonend may alerted issue waited manufacture response return need money buy replacement ladder tried return chat route waste time first person talked tohelpful ncafter hour put holdgot unintentionally disconnected emailed damaged ladder picture amazon called amazon c back complete done get ladder money back waste time talking amazon foreign representative insisted transfer u christol b answereddisdainful disrespectfulhelped decide discontinue amazon purchasing next day received email would getting refund put get refund ridiculous unacceptable ladder crappy failed first time used,0.005069403465062525,0.9949305965349374,0.07459338194054964,0.2,0.8123839746555787,81.23839746555787,High Trust
Julie,/users/5a957de60e7d9e41884d1d86,US,2.0,2020-10-04 21:25:43+00:00,1.0,"Amazon blocked my account, never even contacted me","I have had an Amazon account for YEARS!!  It sure would be nice and beneficial to know exactly which review(s) are supposed to be so ""unusual"", and that are supposed to be the problem!  I haven't even written any reviews for a month, probably more. I can't even remember the last time I wrote a review or for which products.  ALL REVIEWS have to go through an approval process by Amazon BEFORE they are even posted ""live"" on Amazon, so why weren't any of these ""suspicious"" &/or ""unusual"" reviews ""red flagged"" and ""kicked back"" during this initial approval process? To me, this entire supposedly suspicious and unusual review blocking of my account seems very suspicious to me. After YEARS of buying and leaving reviews, with ZERO problems on Amazon.......then BOOM, suddenly, I'm just blocked, no explanation, Amazon doesn't even bother to notify me about any of this. I have left a few UNBIASED reviews for a free or discounted product offer, that a seller has included an offer/promotional card or label on their product to do so for the product I ordered from them. HOWEVER, I have ALWAYS disclosed this information in my review (just as have a LOT of other buyers have done on product reviews they have left) and ALL of my reviews, no matter what I was offered or not offered have ALWAYS been true and unbiased! I, myself rely on HONEST, ACCURATE and UNBIASED reviews from other customers for products they have purchased on & off Amazon. I would NEVER leave a false, untrue, biased, or inaccurate review, never! There are already too many false, fake, and biased reviews out there for products &/or scammer sellers on and off Amazon!  That is another reason why I disclose in any review I write, if a seller has ""solicited"" me to write a review (because I feel this is somewhat unethical) AND in fact, I will leave a  more critical review for that product. I have several of these offerings right now, that I have NOT reviewed. If this is NOT allowed on Amazon, then why doesn't Amazon penalize and BLOCK the SELLER and their ACCOUNT from being able to sell their product on Amazon? Why is the buyer/customer being penalized? I have seen so much of this in other customer reviews for YEARS (obviously it wasn't/isn't a problem because all those reviews are visible and have not been removed or blocked by Amazon)! It seems like 80% of everything I have purchased in the past year has come with some sort of solicitation included......this is a SELLER problem and NOT a buyer problem!  BUYERS have ZERO control on what a SELLER includes with their product when it's shipped out to them! So again, why would Amazon be blocking the BUYERS?One more thing I just found out and would like to bring to everyone's attention! I just looked and every single product that I received a solicitation card with the product or solicitation directly on the product itself, and that I still have the solicitation info for was FULFILLED and SHIPPED directly from/by AMAZON! If this is against Amazon policy it would then seem that AMAZON needs to get their own ""house"" in order and stop penalizing their paying customers for solicitation material that their very own Amazon employees are putting in the product packages before shipping them! I have canceled my Prime account and other Amazon subscriptions and will not place any further orders through Amazon. As I am sure Amazon doesn't want to have any further business relationship, with an all of a  sudden, ""suspicious"" and ""unusual"" buyer.",2020-10-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,4.0,3484,602,50,8,0.0,0,12,2,1,Suspicious,amazon account year sure would nice beneficial know exactly review supposed unusual supposed problem havent even written review month probably cant even remember last time wrote review product review go approval process amazon even posted live amazon werent suspicious unusual review red flagged kicked back initial approval process entire supposedly suspicious unusual review blocking account seems suspicious year buying leaving review zero problem amazonthen boom suddenly im blocked explanation amazon doesnt even bother notify left unbiased review free discounted product offer seller included offerpromotional card label product product ordered however always disclosed information review lot buyer done product review left review matter offered offered always true unbiased rely honest accurate unbiased review customer product purchased amazon would never leave false untrue biased inaccurate review never already many false fake biased review product scammer seller amazon another reason disclose review write seller solicited write review feel somewhat unethical fact leave critical review product several offering right reviewed allowed amazon doesnt amazon penalize block seller account able sell product amazon buyercustomer penalized seen much customer review year obviously wasntisnt problem review visible removed blocked amazon seems like everything purchased past year come sort solicitation includedthis seller problem buyer problem buyer zero control seller includes product shipped would amazon blocking buyersone thing found would like bring everyones attention looked every single product received solicitation card product solicitation directly product still solicitation info fulfilled shipped directly fromby amazon amazon policy would seem amazon need get house order stop penalizing paying customer solicitation material amazon employee putting product package shipping canceled prime account amazon subscription place order amazon sure amazon doesnt want business relationship sudden suspicious unusual buyer,0.9999990607813081,9.392186919310319e-07,0.33763320246775097,0.2,0.3675271101028962,36.752711010289616,Low Trust
JW,/users/5f58b9fb1433b7e803aaf33e,GB,3.0,2020-10-04 20:31:12+00:00,5.0,Perfect site,"Perfect site, I know I am in good hands if something isn't right! I get refunded if something is wrong and its easy enough, just drop it off at the post office and get refunded not long after. If something does go wrong and I need to talk to someone, there is a live chat that helps, which allows you to go through it step-by-step. I haven't had any problems.",2020-10-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,10.0,4.0,359,70,12,2,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,perfect site know good hand something isnt right get refunded something wrong easy enough drop post office get refunded long something go wrong need talk someone live chat help allows go stepbystep havent problem,0.4226452918858026,0.5773547081141974,0.03925967470555244,1.0,1.7965292889982092,179.65292889982092,High Trust
