Hari Krishna,/users/5f2d97104813495f08864d28,US,1.0,2020-09-17 23:30:56+00:00,1.0,My experience as an amazon's customer,"I've written a review for one of the products I've purchased through Amazon. Amazon reviewed my message and didn't post my message, because I was not recommending that seller based on my experience. I was trying to share my genuine experience with what I've faced and didn't use any bad words in my message. Similarly Amazon might have NOT posted messages which gives negative feedback about their customers. Since then I don't trust amazon customer reviews because they hide lot of truth reviews and buyers like me get trapped to one of their seller customer products. And all the products from amazon are China products these days and also expensive with less quality. so I'm trying to share my review in another portal like here so that my message wil get to some people and not get trapped in amazon's bad online marketing strategy.",2020-09-17 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,9.0,17.0,836,144,37,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ive written review one product ive purchased amazon amazon reviewed message didnt post message recommending seller based experience trying share genuine experience ive faced didnt use bad word message similarly amazon might posted message give negative feedback customer since dont trust amazon customer review hide lot truth review buyer like get trapped one seller customer product product amazon china product day also expensive less quality im trying share review another portal like message wil get people get trapped amazon bad online marketing strategy,0.015950404511031087,0.9840495954889689,0.08076275939427931,0.2,0.8081773496233403,80.81773496233403,High Trust
Lucy Bouldin,/users/5f63aaa75d40203b7379fbda,GB,1.0,2020-09-17 18:35:07+00:00,1.0,In April I was a victim of fraud through Amazon,"In April I was a victim of fraud through Amazon, I contacted both Amazon (who said they would get back to me and didn’t!) and my bank (who managed to refund me for the transactions!). Amazon then locked me out of my account, and demanded payment for the fraudulent transactions. I went back and forth with Amazon for months about this while my account was on hold and they refused to unlock it. For 6 months I paid for my prime and kindle subscriptions, was unable to cancel them (not even customer service could cancel them), and was unable to use them. I spoke to amazon on numerous occasions, they kept saying they needed to pass my details to the accounts team - the accounts team never got back to me. Several amazon advisors told me to just create a new account - why would I do that when I want to use the one I’m paying for? I cannot even describe the frustration this has caused me for months. Everyone I spoke to was unhelpful, and nearly every email I sent was not replied to.",2020-09-17 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,9.0,17.0,987,186,47,10,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,april victim fraud amazon contacted amazon said would get back didn’t bank managed refund transaction amazon locked account demanded payment fraudulent transaction went back forth amazon month account hold refused unlock month paid prime kindle subscription unable cancel even customer service could cancel unable use spoke amazon numerous occasion kept saying needed pas detail account team account team never got back several amazon advisor told create new account would want use one i’m paying cannot even describe frustration caused month everyone spoke unhelpful nearly every email sent replied,0.1962396030968394,0.8037603969031606,0.10431856421761077,0.2,0.7227439112951025,72.27439112951025,Medium Trust
