Rosie,/users/5f5392896ce9b959172a0eea,GB,3.0,2020-09-05 13:28:58+00:00,1.0,"Boycott time: dishonest, disingenuous, ungenerous and more.","Dishonest, disingenuous, ungenerous and more.Amazon signed me up to a one month prime membership without my knowledge in Sep 2019, because I selected same day delivery for a replacement toothbrush head. In October, naturally, I did not cancel this membership because I had no idea that I was being charged it.I have requested a full refund for £95.88. This is how much same day delivery for a toothbrush will end up having cost me, if I do not receive it. That's the dishonest and disingenous bit. At the same time, I am cancelling my audible account. Although I have paid for two credits, they will not let me keep these and choose two books at my leisure. Instead I must choose two books now before cancelling it, otherwise I will lose access to the books I've bought but not yet chosen. Ungenerous and more!  Result: I have lost what little trust I had in Amazon. I will be making an effort over the coming months to use alternative, more sustainable suppliers wherever possible. I encourage others to join me.",2020-09-05 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,9.0,5.0,1013,179,59,7,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,dishonest disingenuous ungenerous moreamazon signed one month prime membership without knowledge sep selected day delivery replacement toothbrush head october naturally cancel membership idea charged iti requested full refund £ much day delivery toothbrush end cost receive thats dishonest disingenous bit time cancelling audible account although paid two credit let keep choose two book leisure instead must choose two book cancelling otherwise lose access book ive bought yet chosen ungenerous result lost little trust amazon making effort coming month use alternative sustainable supplier wherever possible encourage others join,0.02454311351059044,0.9754568864894095,0.10039259674705553,0.2,0.8078069625941158,80.78069625941157,High Trust
