Rick James Bish,/users/5e08c683361d6141ae095b9a,US,3.0,2020-08-12 01:16:36+00:00,1.0,Amazon filtering reviews with low rating,"I am a long time Amazon Prime member. My wife recently purchased me a macro flash setup from Amazon under her account login. The unit performed poorly and also stopped working. I wrote a review on the product under my account.  The next day Amazon emailed stating my review had been denied. They did not give s specific reason however the content of my review was factual and was not completely negative so it would appear Amazon chooses what reviews pass and will deny any negative review that might hurt sales. I signed into my wife's account, chose the product from her order history and chose the review option. Before I could even start typing, a message popped up that Amazon was not accepting reviews for the product on this account. In short...do not trust Amazon reviews. They are controlled.",2020-08-12 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,8.0,12.0,801,140,40,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,long time amazon prime member wife recently purchased macro flash setup amazon account login unit performed poorly also stopped working wrote review product account next day amazon emailed stating review denied give specific reason however content review factual completely negative would appear amazon chooses review pas deny negative review might hurt sale signed wife account chose product order history chose review option could even start typing message popped amazon accepting review product account shortdo trust amazon review controlled,0.018767968588813886,0.9812320314111861,0.07851934941110487,0.2,0.806319885587814,80.6319885587814,High Trust
