Carmen Rosa,/users/5f31a19aef67ac204e0e129f,US,1.0,2020-08-10 19:36:08+00:00,1.0,Amazon’s Billing Error,"I placed an order on Amazon for an item and they mistakenly processed it twice. This caused my account to go into overdraft and my bank would charge me the surcharges. Call the bank and they will not be held responsible for these tractions. I was calling  Amazon, which was the one who made the mistake and they tell me that they already reimbursed the money for the transaction that was not authorized but they were not responsible for the surcharges that they themselves caused. Terrible Customer Service. They do not honor the customer rights and don’t repair their mistakes. In the end, I had to make myself responsible for AMAZON'S BILLING ERRORS.",2020-08-10 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,8.0,10.0,652,113,22,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,placed order amazon item mistakenly processed twice caused account go overdraft bank would charge surcharge call bank held responsible traction calling amazon one made mistake tell already reimbursed money transaction authorized responsible surcharge caused terrible customer service honor customer right don’t repair mistake end make responsible amazon billing error,0.03368933937384526,0.9663106606261548,0.0633763320246775,0.2,0.7958305967180129,79.5830596718013,High Trust
BadBoy,/users/5f31751def67ac00fa0df69d,IN,1.0,2020-08-10 16:31:06+00:00,1.0,I’ve been shopping on Amazon for 3…,"I’ve been shopping on Amazon for 3 years on wards now. It is one of the best sites to shop I guess globally. I don’t know many other sites that provide this large of a product base. A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̳̾̾m̳̾̾b̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾i̳̾̾s̳̾̾ ̳̾̾+̳̾̾1̳̾̾ ̳̾̾8̳̾̾4̳̾̾4̳̾̾ ̳̾̾4̳̾̾2̳̾̾0̳̾̾ ̳̾̾0̳̾̾0̳̾̾7̳̾̾2̳̾̾A̳̾̾m̳̾̾a̳̾̾z̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾̾ ̳̾̾c̳̾̾u̳̾̾s̳̾̾t̳̾̾o̳̾̾m̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾ ̳̾̾s̳̾̾e̳̾̾r̳̾̾v̳̾̾i̳̾̾c̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾h̳̾̾e̳̾̾l̳̾̾p̳̾̾l̳̾̾i̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾p̳̾̾h̳̾̾o̳̾̾n̳̾̾e̳̾̾ ̳̾̾n̳̾̾u̾