Bob Sacamano,/users/5f2afe3598da517a1d295e4f,US,2.0,2020-08-05 18:46:42+00:00,1.0,Amazon is NOT policing fake or bribed reviews,"I now get offers weekly from Amazon sellers offering free stuff for good reviews.  Ok.  I have received LOTS of cameras, vacuums, etc AND I notify Amazon that this is going on.  They do not care.  For two weeks now I have a seller holding my refund hostage until I change a review.  This should be intolerable by Amazon.  They obviously do not like bad reviews (inhibits sales) and love good reviews even to the point of letting sellers intimidate customers to modify existing reviews.  I have notified Amazon on the phone and in writing with no comment from them on this practice.  (asking for the management or executive responses.",2020-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,8.0,5.0,633,110,45,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,get offer weekly amazon seller offering free stuff good review ok received lot camera vacuum etc notify amazon going care two week seller holding refund hostage change review intolerable amazon obviously like bad review inhibits sale love good review even point letting seller intimidate customer modify existing review notified amazon phone writing comment practice asking management executive response,0.024389140666819856,0.9756108593331801,0.06169377453729669,0.2,0.8001441845740495,80.01441845740494,High Trust
