Amazon Deceptiveness,/users/5f20af315471a43430e170c3,US,1.0,2020-08-05 23:51:02+00:00,1.0,Update Amazon Deceptiveness - Continues ( Purchases were for a 3 1/2 year old).,"I have been purchasing from Amazon since very early 2000's.  Currently, I am lied to about deliveries, merchandise quality and by Amazon reviews on their web site of quality.  Nearly 50% of my orders are now totally bogus in regards to delivery dates and quality.  I placed my order on 7/21/2020 and the Amazon ad had a delivery date of 7/28/2020 and sent me an E-Mail confirming a 7/28/2020 delivery.  This is a birthday present for a 3 1/2 year old boy.  I had to call Amazon on 7/27/2020 to find out if the item had shipped yet. Amazon support said no.  Today, 7/28/2020, I get an E-Mail from Amazon saying the delivery date will be August 7, 2020.  If I never called them; probably I would have been left hanging.  I asked the Amazon so-called support person what should I tell this 3 1/2 year old boy??  ------------------------------------------------------------- I now received an email today, 8/5/2020 stating Amazon has cancelled the order due to NOT HAVING THE ITEM.  Ordered on 7/21/2020 with a 7/28/2020 delivery.  I called on 7/27/2020 to find out if it shipped.  It did not.  I get an E-Mail on 7/28/2020 stating it would be delivered on 8/7/2020.  Today, 8/5/2020 I now get an E-Mail from Amazon stating THEY CANCELLED THE ORDER.  What a waste of time and what disappointment for a 3 1/2 old boy.   What should I tell a 3 1/2 year old????  He won't understand the lies by Amazon.The quality of the clothing is atrocious and 50% or more of items on Amazon seem to be Chinese crap and junk. I have seen articles claiming Amazon resellers are having people give reviews to up their reviews.  This, I tend to believe.  I am just about done with Amazon, their Prime and the lack of being trustworthy and professional.  I am clearly seeing that Amazon no longer cares about customers, professionalism and American made 