Kevin Heisey,/users/5f0a911753f8af247b64d1b9,US,1.0,2020-07-14 03:12:27+00:00,1.0,Prime services aren't what they used to…,"Prime services aren't what they used to be. I ordered Pistachios from Amazon expressly because it advertises, ""will be delivered by tomorrow"", all day today, ""it's on its way!"" Then 8:01 PM rolls around and I get a ""Package is still on its way, but running late"" and I'm supposed to get it in a few days.If I wanted them in 2-3 days, I'd go to the store. I was an early Amazon adopter and proud customer 10+ years ago and bought almost everything from them. Over the last 3-4 years I use them less and less as it's rare when something arrives, working on time and more times than not I end up disappointed or worse.UPDATE: Still haven't got my pistachios. According to Amazon tracking they sat in one facility for 12 hours and the next facility for 40+ hours (so far), both facilities are within an hour or so drive from me.I suspect they never intended to deliver them overnight. Why do I pay for Prime again?",2020-07-12 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,7.0,14.0,910,169,40,7,2.0,0,1,0,0,Genuine,prime service arent used ordered pistachio amazon expressly advertises delivered tomorrow day today way pm roll around get package still way running late im supposed get daysif wanted day id go store early amazon adopter proud customer year ago bought almost everything last year use less less rare something arrives working time time end disappointed worseupdate still havent got pistachio according amazon tracking sat one facility hour next facility hour far facility within hour drive mei suspect never intended deliver overnight pay prime,0.03152925289799301,0.968470747102007,0.09478407178911946,0.2,0.8031921879088274,80.31921879088274,High Trust
