1muflon1,/users/5bc104ea4de5666d34ab7839,NL,1.0,2020-07-07 23:56:44+00:00,1.0,I tried to purchase a kindle version of…,"I tried to purchase a kindle version of a book which showed on amazon.com priced at $61.76. So I decided to buy it with one click, I wasn’t logged in so I logged in and immediately clicked on the buy with one click button as I was not expecting logging in will have any effect on the order.Afterwards, I received in my email invoice with a completely different price than the one shown before ($81.59). When I brought this to the attention of amazon customer service they told me that is just a normal change in price across the time.However, then I noticed when I log out price drops back to $61.76. Every single time I log into my account price becomes $81.59 and every single time I log out it drops back to $61.76. I tested this about 8-10 times and even recorded one such attempt in case they change it later so I can bring this issue to the attention of local authorities and lawmakers because if this is legal it definitely should not be in the future.I am appalled by this for two reasons:The practice itself is incredibly deceitful. In fact, since I did not notice the change in price right away and at amazon.com you buy kindle books with one click I purchased the book at an increased price and now wasted my time going through the return process. Furthermore, I wonder how many shoppers might never even notice this happening and literary get scammed by amazon - I doubt that any customer expects the price of purely digital good changing after they log-in, and hence many might not check.Customer service laying to customers. When I wrote an email about this to the amazon customer service their reply was that Amazon prices change with time and tax rates might be different in different states.However, the price changes every time I log in log out - hence clearly the price is not a function of time but a binary function of whether I am logged in or out of my account. Claiming that’s changing with time is incredibly intellectually dishonest as the fact that the price is still even of the time of this writing shown to be $61.74 shows that at least today the price was completely unrelated to time but depended solely on my logged in/out status.Furthermore, this cannot be explained by taxes because when I log into my account the pre-tax price is changed as well! In fact from the order summary from my accidental purchase, I can see that the pre-tax price I was charged was $67.99. That is higher than the post VAT price shown before I log in.This is really low! If amazon sets different prices based on the login of a customer they should at least be transparent about it and put a big warning sign under each price! Furthermore, they should at least transparently say that price depends on the customer and not time as is the case here!All future customers of amazon should be beware of this practice! You might get billed completely different price than the one they pretend to offer!",2020-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,7.0,7.0,2907,524,40,8,0.0,0,6,2,1,Suspicious,tried purchase kindle version book showed amazoncom priced decided buy one click wasn’t logged logged immediately clicked buy one click button expecting logging effect orderafterwards received email invoice completely different price one shown brought attention amazon customer service told normal change price across timehowever noticed log price drop back every single time log account price becomes every single time log drop back tested time even recorded one attempt case change later bring issue attention local authority lawmaker legal definitely futurei appalled two reasonsthe practice incredibly deceitful fact since notice change price right away amazoncom buy kindle book one click purchased book increased price wasted time going return process furthermore wonder many shopper might never even notice happening literary get scammed amazon doubt customer expects price purely digital good changing login hence many might checkcustomer service laying customer wrote email amazon customer service reply amazon price change time tax rate might different different stateshowever price change every time log log hence clearly price function time binary function whether logged account claiming that’s changing time incredibly intellectually dishonest fact price still even time writing shown show least today price completely unrelated time depended solely logged inout statusfurthermore cannot explained tax log account pretax price changed well fact order summary accidental purchase see pretax price charged higher post vat price shown log inthis really low amazon set different price based login customer least transparent put big warning sign price furthermore least transparently say price depends customer time case hereall future customer amazon beware practice might get billed completely different price one pretend offer,0.9841785602066383,0.015821439793361702,0.2938867077958497,0.2,0.36668806145585076,36.66880614558507,Low Trust
Jess C,/users/5e7ba0848cd2bc21520867b2,CA,7.0,2020-07-07 19:16:20+00:00,2.0,Ive been a prime member for years,"Ive been a prime member for years. Ordering an item/items on average every two weeks. I’ve never had any issues and customer service seemed to be great until recently. I ordered an item recently that was on sale but back ordered, once it became available in stock, the price went back up but my item was shipped out and I was charged the discount price because I had made the order beforehand. Tracking said it would be delivered on time and then all of the sudden, it said it would be delayed. I was fine with waiting however, the package was apparently sent back while in transit and I received a refund from amazon with no explanation. Amazon now expects me to pay full price on an item that I paid for 50% off. I find it very convenient that the item was sent back mid transit. Been a week and no response from customer service. My prime membership ended and I will not be renewing it. If I can help it, I will order somewhere else and not on amazon.",2020-07-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,7.0,7.0,954,181,33,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ive prime member year ordering itemitems average every two week i’ve never issue customer service seemed great recently ordered item recently sale back ordered became available stock price went back item shipped charged discount price made order beforehand tracking said would delivered time sudden said would delayed fine waiting however package apparently sent back transit received refund amazon explanation amazon expects pay full price item paid find convenient item sent back mid transit week response customer service prime membership ended renewing help order somewhere else amazon,0.008410657893827483,0.9915893421061726,0.10151430173864273,0.4,1.1160975314008148,111.60975314008148,High Trust
