Sunshine Palomides,/users/5efdd66ac3bb91d36ea2ecd1,DE,1.0,2020-07-02 12:43:34+00:00,1.0,"Direct Debit payments stopped working, no reason given by Amazon","So after having been an active private Amazon customer for as long as the shop's existed, across 3 countries, and having purchased more items than usual recently due to being off work (sick) and bored at home, my direct debit payment method stopped working. This happened a few months ago and any payment I try to make via direct debit gets automatically declined. Only credit card is accepted.So clearly, there's been a security flag set on my account of some sort. Unfortunately, contacting Amazon customer service has not lead to any improvement (let alone resolution), only a robotic repetition of the phrase 'We are sorry for your inconvenience, but sometimes Amazon declines direct debit payments. We cannot disclose reasons. Please switch to credit card payment instead.'What I want is a dialogue to address any concerns which may have lead to the flag being set on my account, and a way to resolve it.w o r s t   c u s t o m e r   s e r v i c e   e v e r",2020-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,7.0,2.0,962,176,64,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,active private amazon customer long shop existed across country purchased item usual recently due work sick bored home direct debit payment method stopped working happened month ago payment try make via direct debit get automatically declined credit card acceptedso clearly there security flag set account sort unfortunately contacting amazon customer service lead improvement let alone resolution robotic repetition phrase sorry inconvenience sometimes amazon decline direct debit payment cannot disclose reason please switch credit card payment insteadwhat want dialogue address concern may lead flag set account way resolve itw r c u e r e r v c e e v e r,0.01193388140294058,0.9880661185970594,0.09871003925967471,0.2,0.8137750671504645,81.37750671504645,High Trust
