Myiah Grizzard,/users/5efd1da3616e55f85131cef5,US,2.0,2020-07-01 23:35:20+00:00,1.0,misinformation & a stolen package.,"I had a package delivered while I was at work yesterday and the delivery said “handed directly to a resident” even though i’m not home. When I got home, obviously the package wasn’t there. I reached out to Amazon and a representative told me that sometimes deliveries are accidentally marked as delivered early and that I should give it to tomorrow, she also said that she looked it up and actually saw that my package hadn’t actually been delivered yet. I could tell she didn’t know what she was talking about and I should’ve went with my gut but i’m always trying to give someone the benefit of the doubt, so I waited before I confronted my neighbor. Today, I got home from work and of course, no package. I called and was told that my package was in fact delivered yesterday, which I knew it was. To make a long story short, my neighbors got a free JBL Speaker and Xbox controller charger. Untrained and stupid customer service, AND automated support system which also told me to wait until the end of the day on Jul 1 (today, a day after my package was delivered).",2020-07-01 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,7.0,1.0,1068,196,34,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,package delivered work yesterday delivery said “handed directly resident” even though i’m home got home obviously package wasn’t reached amazon representative told sometimes delivery accidentally marked delivered early give tomorrow also said looked actually saw package hadn’t actually delivered yet could tell didn’t know talking should’ve went gut i’m always trying give someone benefit doubt waited confronted neighbor today got home work course package called told package fact delivered yesterday knew make long story short neighbor got free jbl speaker xbox controller charger untrained stupid customer service automated support system also told wait end day jul today day package delivered,0.030184295207648464,0.96981570479235