Thomas Thomson,/users/5ebef37a242795387f4b2cc6,US,3.0,2020-06-26 20:12:03+00:00,1.0,I got it fixed but I am still avoiding them.,"I had an Amazon account which I have not used in 5 years.  They just reminded me of why.  Bought a Amazon Fire 7, great price, got here ahead of schedule. I found that unless I renewed my Amazon account (I bought it from Target) I could not register it.  And if I cannot register it I can not set up my facebook account or my email account. I have spent hours trying to update my Amazon account on their customer service web page. Although they know my email address and cell phone # (which have not changed in five years, they will not accept my current zip code (I moved within the same county) and I can not remember the last tour digits of a debit card I had five years ago (because my bank twice has issued me new debit cards because they had determined my old one had been compromised.  Long story short I can not get past these challenges to update ""my"" account on their web page and they referred me to a vendor of their's (Expert/Help) who hit my bank account for a fee and then disappeared 5 minutes into a ""chat"" discussion about ""my"" problem. Amazon customer service is who and what be, a company who does not want to talk to their customers and they don't want to deal with their emails on their web site either. Now I remember why I haven't used them in five years.  June 20 Spent the whole week calling Amazon's customer service number and a recorded message said they were not (even) taking calls because of the virus. Their employees may have been out protesting, shopping at stores where the glass was broken and they didn't have to use the front door, who knows. Pulling down statues, etc. On Sat. morning I called and a guy answered the phone.  He knew an end run around my problem, pushed a button and deleted my old account with the old info, and let me set up a new account and my problem was solved. Also, remember (Expert/Help, there in San Francisco) who charged me $1.00 to solve my problem and then ditched me?  A couple of days later they charged me $48.00 for an annual subscription. I got their phone number off of my on-line bank account and called them and told them it was an unauthorized charge and I wanted it credited.  The young Asian woman who spoke faster than a 50 caliber machine gun wanted to argue with me until I told her if she wanted to argue about it, I would just call Bank X and they would run a belated stop pay and debit their account at the bank.  Works every time.  So I found a live person at Amazon who knows what he is doing and found another crooked California company. That state (where I lived for 13 years) is becoming the Miami of the nation. I am now a happy camper but they still only deserve one star. I'm still avoiding the them. Life is too short.",2020-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,6.0,26.0,2714,514,44,10,14.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,amazon account used year reminded bought amazon fire great price got ahead schedule found unless renewed amazon account bought target could register cannot register set facebook account email account spent hour trying update amazon account customer service web page although know email address cell phone changed five year accept current zip code moved within county remember last tour digit debit card five year ago bank twice issued new debit card determined old one compromised long story short get past challenge update account web page referred vendor experthelp hit bank account fee disappeared minute chat discussion problem amazon customer service company want talk customer dont want deal email web site either remember havent used five year june spent whole week calling amazon customer service number recorded message said even taking call virus employee may protesting shopping store glass broken didnt use front door know pulling statue etc sat morning called guy answered phone knew end run around problem pushed button deleted old account old info let set new account problem solved also remember experthelp san francisco charged solve problem ditched couple day later charged annual subscription got phone number online bank account called told unauthorized charge wanted credited young asian woman spoke faster caliber machine gun wanted argue told wanted argue would call bank x would run belated stop pay debit account bank work every time found live person amazon know found another crooked california company state lived year becoming miami nation happy camper still deserve one star im still avoiding life short,0.007363559304721598,0.9926364406952785,0.2882781828379136,0.2,0.853973856915222,85.3973856915222,High Trust
