Maria S.,/users/5ecb38412b4bf6db785ab164,US,1.0,2020-05-25 03:29:11+00:00,1.0,Terrible Customer Service & Greedy Co.,"Attempted to order multiple items from a baby gift registry.  I was prompted to remove the items from the registry after selecting them but then the items disappeared without giving me the opportunity to add them to my cart.  Then I searched again for the items only to find out they were no longer on the registry even tho I never got the opportunity to add them to my cart.  I called customer service since I wanted to ship them to the recipient's address but I got disconnected.  Then I called the main customer service number only to hear that due to COVID19, they can't help customers at this time and was instructed via a machine to chat online. I went online to chat then someone called me but I got disconnected again.  After several attempts I found out one of the products wasn't approved for shipment to my State. Additionally, I was told I wasn't the only call experiencing those issues and the gift registry dept was inundated with these types of calls...i.e. being prompted to remove items from a registry without getting the opportunity to add them to my cart.  Since there were only 3 other items on the registry, I attempted to get a gift card only to find out I can't use my amazon credit for that.  This was absolutely the worst customer service I ever encountered for an online company that supposedly is closing retail shops left and right!  I hope consumers wake up and realize what is happening...they are trying to create a monopoly so customers don't have other options.  I urge people to support retail businesses that are more customer service friendly rather than support a company that only hires people to ship overpriced items.",2020-05-25 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,5.0,25.0,1658,292,38,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,attempted order multiple item baby gift registry prompted remove item registry selecting item disappeared without giving opportunity add cart searched item find longer registry even tho never got opportunity add cart called customer service since wanted ship recipient address got disconnected called main customer service number hear due covid cant help customer time instructed via machine chat online went online chat someone called got disconnected several attempt found one product wasnt approved shipment state additionally told wasnt call experiencing issue gift registry dept inundated type callsie prompted remove item registry without getting opportunity add cart since item registry attempted get gift card find cant use amazon credit absolutely worst customer service ever encountered online company supposedly closing retail shop left right hope consumer wake realize happeningthey trying create monopoly customer dont option urge people support retail business customer service friendly rather support company hire people ship overpriced item,0.04260878655108959,0.9573912134489104,0.16376892877173305,0.2,0.8114493924788019,81.14493924788019,High Trust
