Michael Bascom,/users/5ec893b42b4bf620ff599189,US,1.0,2020-05-23 03:08:48+00:00,1.0,1 day guarantee that you are paying for…,"1 day guarantee that you are paying for a prime membership for that doesn't end up being guaranteed...whats the point of amazon slapping the word guaranteed on many items when they don't end up following through. No apology, just asking if I can wait another full day for delivery. I trusted in paying for an amazon prime membership that when the website says guaranteed next day delivery on an item I intentionally order for an event the next day that they should be standing by their guarantee..if not, then that is intentional false advertising.",2020-05-23 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,5.0,23.0,548,94,40,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,day guarantee paying prime membership doesnt end guaranteedwhats point amazon slapping word guaranteed many item dont end following apology asking wait another full day delivery trusted paying amazon prime membership website say guaranteed next day delivery item intentionally order event next day standing guaranteeif intentional false advertising,0.01995988963722495,0.980040110362775,0.05272013460459899,0.2,0.8005640821023073,80.05640821023073,High Trust
Lynn,/users/5ead8a4b995ff2d27cfdeed0,US,14.0,2020-06-09 05:50:08+00:00,1.0,Lame Excuses,"I realize that they are probably literally 'pitching and catching' to keep up, but when it comes to the lame excuses... enough is enough! Although after a recent shipping blunder on their part, I was reluctant to place another order, but because a family member made a request for a specific item, I ordered again. The item was to have been shipped to them (they live in another state) in mid-May. I looked up the tracking for the item to see where the package was in transit. I saw that the item was received in the local area days earlier, but that it did not go out for delivery due to 'weather or natural disaster.' Bear in mind that happened in mid-May, long before the advent of tropical storms in June. Curious about the delay, I called the family to find out what was actually going on - it's not unusual for there to be really bad storms/ tornadoes in their area in late spring. They said everything was just fine, just only that the weather was hot.  So why would Amazon's system say the package was delayed due to weather? I decided to check with Amazon by chat. Long story short, first the agent kept side-stepping the issue and when I said that I would send a copy of the text that said it was delayed due to weather, she replied 'it's been automated' - and with that, the previous day's tracking information disappeared! Yes, disappeared! It just said that it was ""in transit today."" How convenient for them! They need to be completely HONEST about things. Why not have a designation that says something like 'limited capacity' or 'circumstances beyond our control' or something like that? Why LIE about the weather?  The bottom line is that Amazon Prime can't deliver on its already over-extended beyond the 2-day delivery promises and they probably cover things up to boot.After a bit more investigating, it turns out that the falsehood about the weather as the reason for delayed delivery was made by UPS and UPS is perhaps the party responsible for the suddenly disappearing 'update.'   The over-due item arrived damaged and was returned. There was confusion at Amazon about the refund. In looking up details on the refund, I was surprised to be greeted by a gratuitous political statement emblazoned across a banner heading on their website. Isn't it enough to put up with Amazon's poor service? Must we endure grandstanding as well?",2020-05-22 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,6.0,9.0,2352,412,12,2,18.0,0,4,1,0,Genuine,realize probably literally pitching catching keep come lame excuse enough enough although recent shipping blunder part reluctant place another order family member made request specific item ordered item shipped live another state midmay looked tracking item see package transit saw item received local area day earlier go delivery due weather natural disaster bear mind happened midmay long advent tropical storm june curious delay called family find actually going unusual really bad storm tornado area late spring said everything fine weather hot would amazon system say package delayed due weather decided check amazon chat long story short first agent kept sidestepping issue said would send copy text said delayed due weather replied automated previous day tracking information disappeared yes disappeared said transit today convenient need completely honest thing designation say something like limited capacity circumstance beyond control something like lie weather bottom line amazon prime cant deliver already overextended beyond day delivery promise probably cover thing bootafter bit investigating turn falsehood weather reason delayed delivery made ups ups perhaps party responsible suddenly disappearing update overdue item arrived damaged returned confusion amazon refund looking detail refund surprised greeted gratuitous political statement emblazoned across banner heading website isnt enough put amazon poor service must endure grandstanding well,0.659743546392