Mrs G,/users/5ebba858242795a3e348c939,GB,1.0,2020-05-13 07:57:57+00:00,1.0,I'd give less than one star if I could,"I'd give less than one star if I could. I had an issue so contacted Amazon support to be put through to a representative to chat to. The representative was dismissive, derogatory and very rude. I was put through to another rep who treated me in the same way.I decided to try and contact Amazon again, this time to complain about the terrible service. Again, I was treated rudely and stonewalled.They promise to escalate your complaint but refuse to say who to. They won't put you through to anyone higher up, instead saying that there isn't anyone higher up. They offer the same £5 goodwill credit, which after treating me so badly and wasting an hour and a half of my time and still not resolving my initial issue nor that of the terrible customer service, feels entirely unsatisfactory. The only resolution they give is a copy and pasted 'I will escalate your claim. This will not happen again'. I didn't even get a sorry.I've always received excellent service via Amazon before, even when there's been a problem. I don't know what's changed, I did ask but this wasn't met with a response.I asked for a copy of the original transcript detailing the first round of terrible customer service. I was told that they couldn't provide one and that one would be available in the message centre. This was a lie. There isn't a copy in the message centre. I let the rep know and was again told I wasn't allowed a copy of the transcript.Once again I left the chat with a bad taste, feeling very frustrated and still my original issue hasn't been resolved and nor do I feel any better about the very poor service I initially received. I'm a Prime customer. They used to treat Prime customers really well. That is no longer the case.",2020-05-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,5.0,13.0,1722,309,38,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,id give less one star could issue contacted amazon support put representative chat re