Destiny Bryant,/users/5eafbb9046f4d08486f9bc26,US,1.0,2020-05-04 06:56:27+00:00,1.0,Customer Service Straight Lied to Me.,"Look, I set up a baby registry with a multitude of items on it. (Crib, change table, and chester drawers set included.) Only to be told by their customer service that they would not ship to my state unless the item is under 108inches in length, and weighs less then 80lbs. Those were my states “restrictions.” HOWEVER; my crib is 80inches and 68lbs! It comes dismantled in a square box. So how are they unable to ship this item to me if it meets the requirements? Why would your registry customer service give me a bold face lie? I’m  livid, displeased, and very much unhappy with the treatment I received. Bonus; customer service told me, bluntly, they don’t ship oddly shaped items to my state. Yet, the number of people I now that buys legitimate full sets of big truck tires off of amazon prime, and they ship just fine. As well as I know people, family, who have ordered their cribs from them. “Great customer service” they say, “they are so helpful and honest” they say. Yeah, no they aren’t. Do not use Amazon!",2020-05-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,5.0,4.0,1017,185,37,6,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,look set baby registry multitude item crib change table chester drawer set included told customer service would ship state unless item inch length weighs less lb state “restrictions” however crib inch lb come dismantled square box unable ship item meet requirement would registry customer service give bold face lie i’m livid displeased much unhappy treatment received bonus customer service told bluntly don’t ship oddly shaped item state yet number people buy legitimate full set big truck tire amazon prime ship fine well know people family ordered crib “great customer service” say “they helpful honest” say yeah aren’t use amazon,0.21704760321443392,0.782952396785566,0.10375771172181716,0.2,0.7122277407371465,71.22277407371465,Medium Trust
