Nightmare with Amazon,/users/5ea7b47d84263175091f607a,US,1.0,2020-04-28 04:44:20+00:00,1.0,I am having a nightmare with Amazon’s…,"I am having a nightmare with Amazon’s customer service. My packages were swapped with another one while I got the notification that my packages were successfully delivered. I contacted Amazon and they picked up the wrong package the next day, while opening an investigation on my own packages. It’s been 2 weeks since the delivery was messed up. I have contacted Amazon 3 times and each time I was asked to come back later: the first time in 2 business days, 2nd time for 4 business days and the most recent one I was asked to come back in 7-8 business days!!! I cannot cancel my order nor getting refund for something that I have not received. The representatives were rude, the last one opted out of the chat room - not saying a word - when I started to complain about my frustration on the service. I have read so many bad reviews about Amazon’s customer service these days. Just one more from me. Amazon is going downhill compared to other online retailers. A sad thing to see, given how I used to love this platform.",2020-04-28 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,28.0,1021,187,38,7,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,nightmare amazon’s customer service package swapped another one got notification package successfully delivered contacted amazon picked wrong package next day opening investigation package it’s week since delivery messed contacted amazon time time asked come back later first time business day nd time business day recent one asked come back business day cannot cancel order getting refund something received representative rude last one opted chat room saying word started complain frustration service read many bad review amazon’s customer service day one amazon going downhill compared online retailer sad thing see given used love platform,0.5318558773906634,0.4681441226093366,0.10487941671340438,0.2,0.5550479446473492,55.50479446473492,Medium Trust
RR LL,/users/5ea7aebe842631cea31f5f55,US,1.0,2020-04-28 04:19:16+00:00,1.0,Amazon is force people to buy without letting people know,"First of all, I've been enjoying amazon until today. I purchased something cost about $1500. When I selected the payment, I selected to pay full in 18 months. After two weeks, today I see my bank statement, I found the payment is there and it's from amazon. So I went back to my amazon to check, the system says they used one of my another cards as a back up to process the order in order to avoid any delay. It sounds reasonable right? BUT the truth is, if I know I have to pay $1500 for one time, I would not purchase at all. Because it's too much for me, especially now everyone is suffering from covid19. I never get a notice to let me know they are using a back up card to process the order, and I never get the option to choose if I want to use the back up card to proceed or I want to drop the purchase either.At last, after contacting amazon customer service, their conclusion is "" it's sold, I'm sorry you need to pay this much for one time, but that's your problem."" I just don't know how is this fair?",2020-04-28 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,28.0,1012,200,57,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,first ive enjoying amazon today purchased something cost selected payment selected pay full month two week today see bank statement found payment amazon went back amazon check system say used one another card back process order order avoid delay sound reasonable right truth know pay one time would purchase much especially everyone suffering covid never get notice let know using back card process order never get option choose want use back card proceed want drop purchase eitherat last contacting amazon customer service conclusion sold im sorry need pay much one time thats problem dont know fair,0.006907668313300347,0.9930923316866996,0.11217049915872125,0.2,0.8189802656750941,81.8980265675094,High Trust
T C (Gempic),/users/5ea78a68949c72e2735750d7,US,1.0,2020-04-28 01:52:54+00:00,1.0,Amazon riding on the back of coronavirus,"I have been a Prime member for two decades and I never experienced such horrible CS for the past month (3/1/20-4/27/20). I have always loved Amazon for their top-notch CS but in the last month or so they have went from being the best CS on the internet to the worst CS in a matter of a month and all on the back of the corona-virus. It seems they decided they would dump their CS and take advantage of the pandemic and ride this as best they can while trying to make money on their prime members. I fully support what they are saying about supporting the first responders (bravest people on the planet), just not what they (Amazon) are doing because they are NOT selling a thing that is helping in this pandemic. Try and find N95 masks, PPE's, disinfectant wipes, disinfectant hand soap...etc... You cannot find it on Amazon so I don't know what they are trying to push on us as if they are doing something or making a difference other than contributing to the problem. Yeah, I have had it with Amazon and I wish there were a way to contact and let the share-holders know how bad Amazon has become within a months time without helping anyone but themselves. Yeah, time to get rid of my echo devices, prime membership and move on.  I know its going to be hard but this is a total let-down of Amazon and how they decided to treat and milk their prime customers.",2020-04-28 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,28.0,1359,254,40,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,prime member two decade never experienced horrible c past month always loved amazon topnotch c last month went best c internet worst c matter month back coronavirus seems decided would dump c take advantage pandemic ride best trying make money prime member fully support saying supporting first responder bravest people planet amazon selling thing helping pandemic try find n mask ppes disinfectant wipe disinfectant hand soapetc cannot find amazon dont know trying push u something making difference contributing problem yeah amazon wish way contact let shareholder know bad amazon become within month time without helping anyone yeah time get rid echo device prime membership move know going hard total letdown amazon decided treat milk prime customer,0.01929698829032022,0.9807030117096798,0.142456533931576,0.2,0.818842812641155,81.8842812641155,High Trust
Todd Proulx,/users/5ea779faada65c41aa0b498f,US,5.0,2020-04-28 00:34:31+00:00,1.0,Customer service has gone right down…,"Customer service has gone right down hill and they are very sneaky on what they say.  Oh no sir, you are still getting one and two day shipping it just takes 20 or more days to ship it.  We tell you that at time of ordering, but not at time of research nor actual order, just the very last step.  I have also noticed they are out of about 20 % of items I normal would get, not toilet paper or disinfectant, but golf push carts and a cooking brush.If you are not going to deliver on your promise, refund people.   I call customer services and they said, there is nothing we can do, senior customer service, we have actual beat the deliver time we gave you on the item  you asked for, we said 30 days and we are delivering in 26.  I said hoe about the 4 other orders...   Well we are keeping our commitment of 2 day shipping.Finally when I gave them poor reviews on the email response, I got a $5.00 credit, Big Jeff, your brand is sucking!",2020-04-28 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,28.0,938,182,37,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,customer service gone right hill sneaky say oh sir still getting one two day shipping take day ship tell time ordering time research actual order last step also noticed item normal would get toilet paper disinfectant golf push cart cooking brushif going deliver promise refund people call customer service said nothing senior customer service actual beat deliver time gave item asked said day delivering said hoe order well keeping commitment day shippingfinally gave poor review email response got credit big jeff brand sucking,0.030930904495108016,0.969069095504892,0.10207515423443635,0.2,0.8049495785993331,80.49495785993331,High Trust
