Vee C,/users/5bb8fdae4de5666d34cf8e79,US,7.0,2020-04-27 17:47:08+00:00,1.0,Amazon deserves negative stars,"Amazon deserves negative stars.  I have (had) been a customer for DECADES.  Today I had my credit card information stolen.  Someone used my credit card that is tied to my bank account to place several online orders with various vendors.  I contacted three of them to report the issue, after I contacted the bank that issues my credit card.  All three vendors immediately stopped payment on the fraudulent orders and assured me that my bank account would be reimbursed within 48 hours.  However, when I contacted Amazon Customer Support to report fraudulent use of my credit card, this is what I encountered:  (1) Asked for last 4 digits of credit card used; (2) name on card; (3) date and amount of charge - I provided all of this information.  Support indicates that yes my card was used for that amount on the date provided, but the name on the account was different, and that I had to provide any ""guesses"" as to the name that was used on the account.  Seriously, take a guess.  Hello, you are asking me to identify someone that stole my credit card information!  When I could not take a ""guess"" as to the name on the account, I asked for the name that was used and I was denied this information because Amazon had to ""protect the name used"".  So let's just protect the person that stole my information and not provide me with any help.  This went back and forth for several minutes.  I asked for the name and contact information for an Amazon Supervisor and this was denied.  I indicated I wanted the charge taken off of my credit card - denied - told it was my bank's responsibility, not Amazon's.  I explained how other vendors immediately did not question the fraudulent charges, and removed them ASAP.  Oh and let's not forget.  Last week I placed an order with Amazon, and afterI reported the fraudulent issue, I received an email that my payment was being denied for fraudulent use.  Just brilliant - the order I did place is denied payment, yet the order I did not place goes through, and I cannot dispute the charges.  After this fiasco, I immediately closed my Amazon account  and I will never do business with them again.",2020-04-27 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,27.0,2135,380,30,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon deserves negative star customer decade today credit card information stolen someone used credit card tied bank account place several online order various vendor contacted three report issue contacted bank issue credit card three vendor immediately stopped payment fraudulent order assured bank account would reimbursed within hour however contacted amazon customer support report fraudulent use credit card encountered asked last digit credit card used name card date amount charge provided information support indicates yes card used amount date provided name account different provide guess name used account seriously take guess hello asking identify someone stole credit card information could take guess name account asked name used denied information amazon protect name used let protect person stole information provide help went back forth several minute asked name contact information amazon supervisor denied indicated wanted charge taken credit card denied told bank responsibility amazon explained vendor immediately question fraudulent charge removed asap oh let forget last week placed order amazon afteri reported fraudulent issue received email payment denied fraudulent use brilliant order place denied payment yet order place go cannot dispute charge fiasco immediately closed amazon account never business,0.038497468133370134,0.9615025318666298,0.2131239484015704,0.2,0.8233760556136289,82.33760556136289,High Trust
