Sarah Hochstetler,/users/58f4d36b0000ff000a8ded8f,US,14.0,2020-04-21 14:38:32+00:00,1.0,I will say I have gotten lots of good…,I will say I have gotten lots of good things from Amazon but on 4-20-20 I had a really horrible experience with Amazon. I am posting this as I have free speech rights in this country. Anyhow back to my experience with Amazon. Early this month I ordered a package of toilet paper from a third-party seller because I was running a little low on toilet paper. Anyhow it was supposed to be in yesterday thru USPS but when postal service showed up no package. I got on Amazon chat and all the rep could do is say many I'm sorrys only to see no results. I was told at first I would have to wait 35 days for a refund. I can't wait 35 days for toilet paper. I specifically asked to chat with a supervisor and was transferred to several reps before getting a supervisor. All the supervisor could do is I'm sorry. Not good enough. I happened to be a Paraplegic on a fixed low income who needs such items or I'm vulnerable to serious health issues like UTI. Also there has been what appears to be price gouging with toilet paper sold by third party sellers which is illegal. But Amazon is allowing it. I don't have funds to be giving price gouging people for toilet paper. What I want to see as a remedy to the problem is my order gets replaced with a 8 pack of toilet paper from Amazon fresh a few hour window for the delivery. As for price gouging that needs to stop.,2020-04-21 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,21.0,1358,262,38,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,say gotten lot good thing amazon really horrible experience amazon posting free speech right country anyhow back experience amazon early month ordered package toilet paper thirdparty seller running little low toilet paper anyhow supposed yesterday thru usps postal service showed package got amazon chat rep could say many im sorrys see result told first would wait day refund cant wait day toilet paper specifically asked chat supervisor