Evy Munro,/users/5d8037a31933cfa22712e428,US,2.0,2020-04-07 04:31:55+00:00,1.0,Nonexistent and Unreliable Customer Service,"Customer service has gone downhill fast in the past few years from personal experience. Don't get me wrong, I appreciate what Amazon is doing to adjust and accommodate the changes as part of coronavirus pandemic but my issue with Amazon has been going on awhile now. Starting a few years ago I started getting lost packages and receiving other people's packages. Once I even received a package that had my name and address label on one side and another person's name and address on the other of the same package! Amazon has made missing packages relatively easy to deal with by replacing them or refunding them. However, it does make me wonder where the money is coming from, somebody has to pay for the lost packages. Each time I try to contact Amazon asking if they wanted me to return those packages that didn't belong to me the representatives would at first be puzzled and when they realized what I was asking would laugh me off and simply tell me to keep the packages. That was problem number one that got me a bit cautious about Amazon as a company and the Amazon culture. Then it began to become more and more difficult to reach Amazon cuatomer service. The website and app links to reach actual people was convoluted and seemed to change location quite often. There was no easily searchable customer service phone number. Even if you did manage to locate a phone number, the robotic phone tree was impossible to navigate. What made me decide to quit Amazon was when I ordered some textbooks, which mind you, was what got Amazon started in the first place. I ordered the books after school semester had just started and I got the actual textbook list from the professors. Usually campus bookstores are more expensive than Amazon. I hadn't had issues with ordering textbooks from Amazon before (as long as I had the right ISBN code from the professors) until this last time, which was for fall 2019 semester. I ordered the textbooks within the first week of the semester staring. I had Amazon prime and had elected to receive my shipment as soon as possible. A week later, nothing. As I anxiously waited, I got impatient by the end of the second week and called up Amazon. They looked into and said that I had ordered from third party sellers and that there was nothing they could do. They advised that I order only from Amazon and not third party sellers, regardless of what the estimated shipment or delivery showed. This striked me as odd because it sound like Amazon was sabotaging its third sellers even though these third sellers are using Amazon as a platform and paying Amazon (technically speaking the third sellers are Amazon customers in that sense). In any case, I cancelled the long-delayed textbook orders and repurchased them through a seller that I thought was Amazon. It was listed as Book Depository, which when I looked said it was part of Amazon. Turned out that wasn't much better. My books took over a month to arrive. One book was delayed for two months, after which Amazon automatically cancelled the order without recourse. Since those last textbook orders I have vowed to boycott Amazon. It hasn't been entirely successful however. Having been a heavy Amazon customer (my yearly Amazon purchase was probably easily north of 4k) for the last nearly ten years, it has been hard to quit. And I hate it but I have been able to cut my spending on Amazon by about two thirds and aim to cut it down to zero. I think Amazon started off with a simple concept that was utilitarian and expanded to take control of every aspect of consumer life. I suppose it has been successful in making convenience an expectation of many and hence allowing Amazon to tighten its grip. Now that it has a strong grip on so many people, it has cut back or woefully neglected the human aspect of consumption and purchase. It's a shame but I don't think we should continue to award Amazon with our trust.",2020-04-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,7.0,3906,693,43,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,customer service gone downhill fast past year personal experience dont get wrong appreciate amazon adjust accommodate change part coronavirus pandemic issue amazon going awhile starting year ago started getting lost package receiving people package even received package name address label one side another person name address package amazon made missing package relatively easy deal replacing refunding however make wonder money coming somebody pay lost package time try contact amazon asking wanted return package didnt belong representative would first puzzled realized asking would laugh simply tell keep package problem number one got bit cautious amazon company amazon culture began become difficult reach amazon cuatomer service website app link reach actual people convoluted seemed change location quite often easily searchable customer service phone number even manage locate phone number robotic phone tree impossible navigate made decide quit amazon ordered textbook mind got amazon started first place ordered book school semester started got actual textbook list professor usually campus bookstore expensive amazon hadnt issue ordering textbook amazon long right isbn code professor last time fall semester ordered textbook within first week semester staring amazon prime elected receive shipment soon possible week later nothing anxiously waited got impatient end second week called amazon looked said ordered third party seller nothing could advised order amazon third party seller regardless estimated shipment delivery showed striked odd sound like amazon sabotaging third seller even though third seller using amazon platform paying amazon technically speaking third seller amazon customer sense case cancelled longdelayed textbook order repurchased seller thought amazon listed book depository looked said part amazon turned wasnt much better book took month arrive one book delayed two month amazon automatically cancelled order without recourse since last textbook order vowed boycott amazon hasnt entirely successful however heavy amazon customer yearly amazon purchase probably easily north k last nearly ten year hard quit hate able cut spending amazon two third aim cut zero think amazon started simple concept utilitarian expanded take control every aspect consumer life suppose successful making convenience expectation many hence allowing amazon tighten grip strong grip many people cut back woefully neglected human aspect consumption purchase shame dont think continue award amazon trust,0.004818158513162405,0.9951818414868376,0.38867077958496915,0.2,0.8753250766604127,87.53250766604127,High Trust
Alan Jackson,/users/5e8bcaef6251454d49ec3944,US,1.0,2020-04-07 00:36:32+00:00,1.0,"Do not care about people, only profits.","One of the only ways to get hired on at Amazon is to apply through Integrity Staffing Solutions. I had applied and was supposed to start Monday at 630pm at the Chattanooga Amazon site (Chat 1). I got there a half hour early and waited for orientation. An Amazon worker met me outside entrance 7 and said it was a first come first serve basis. They hired 10 people, asked 15 to come and be prepared for work, and turned away 5. I told them I needed a job because I lost my job at the school because of the Coronavirus. They said they hire more people than is needed just in case some do not show up. Here I thought I had a job and had been waiting for weeks to start, only to be turned away. What is even worse, I had turned down a job at AutoZone because Amazon paid more. Interestingly, I told an old man about my excitement getting a job at Amazon, and he said, ""be careful, they do not care about you, they only care about money"". Now I understand what he meant.",2020-04-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,7.0,965,190,39,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,one way get hired amazon apply integrity staffing solution applied supposed start monday pm chattanooga amazon site chat got half hour early waited orientation amazon worker met outside entrance said first come first serve basis hired people asked come prepared work turned away told needed job lost job school coronavirus said hire people needed case show thought job waiting week start turned away even worse turned job autozone amazon paid interestingly told old man excitement getting job amazon said careful care care money understand meant,0.018369342491224055,0.981630657508776,0.1065619742007852,0.2,0.812127723594545,81.2127723594545,High Trust
Amy Lafave,/users/5e0bf34b98483680b77b8237,US,3.0,2020-04-06 20:12:52+00:00,1.0,Id leave zero stars if able,I would leave zero stars if able. They have become such giants that customer service has fallen by the wasteside...they dont care about customers anymore like they used to. Cant even honor a price difference from a product they fulfill and ship that was ordered a day ago...same exact item offered but cheaper. Prime members are wasting their money dealing with this ungrateful company. Cancelling my longstanding prime membership and suggest other wise folks follow unless you enjoy being treated poorly and wasting your hard earned money.,2020-04-06 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,6.0,540,87,27,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,would leave zero star able become giant customer service fallen wastesidethey dont care customer anymore like used cant even honor price difference product fulfill ship ordered day agosame exact item offered cheaper prime member wasting money dealing ungrateful company cancelling longstanding prime membership suggest wise folk follow unless enjoy treated poorly wasting hard earned money,0.025614987011292563,0.9743850129887074,0.04879416713404375,0.2,0.7969513399211624,79.69513399211624,High Trust
nik,/users/5b30aaa94de5666d345e0c97,GB,5.0,2020-04-06 18:02:06+00:00,1.0,Why mr Bezos made cool 50 billion lasy year,"Why mr . Bezos ( owner of Amazon) made cool 50 billion last yearI have some friends selling on Amazon and their opinion was cool place to sell. So few weeks ago i decided to sell on Amazon. I didn't even sell anything yet and they took 50 pounds out of my debit card and post it as a credit on the account. On the seller account they have an option to upgrade it to pro for 30 pounds every 4 weeks so they will not charge you for posting items, like eBay does.I pay for this option and was very exited to sell on Amazon.Before that i need a verified account. I upload copy of my passport, state id, banks statement ..etc. Everything they ask me.And here where started the HORROR.Its not exactly same horror like in the books of Steven King but its most unpleasant experience on internet.I have to send countless emails, explaining what is the situation and the stuff from Amazon keep asking me to upload my document.Meantime like in every good horror movie the link where i was suppost to upload the documents stop working- simply got frozen and to make long story short , i got rip off 30 pounds and wasn't able to sell anything on Amazon.I still have 50 pounds credit on the account so i can buy the cheap and useless stuff, floating on Amazon.I learn 1 lesson from this : big companies can do anything and take you money and you can do nothing.There is no Strike back. You will bitten, robbed and thrown out, like in the good old days in The wild west.Because the internet now you are using is like the Wild West.If you are small company , you can get knok-knok on the door from Uncle Sam and they will be checking your taxes really carefully but if you are Amazon you can get away with off-short companies and steal billion of pounds from the local economy by not paying the taxes.I think is time ti say NO to mr. Bezos and avoid Amazon like the Devil avoid the holly water.Dont give your hard earn money to the scammers.",2020-04-06 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,4.0,6.0,1925,363,43,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,mr bezos owner amazon made cool billion last yeari friend selling amazon opinion cool place sell week ago decided sell amazon didnt even sell anything yet took pound debit card post credit account seller account option upgrade pro pound every week charge posting item like ebay doesi pay option exited sell amazonbefore need verified account upload copy passport state id bank statement etc everything ask meand started horrorits exactly horror like book steven king unpleasant experience interneti send countless email explaining situation stuff amazon keep asking upload documentmeantime like every good horror movie link suppost upload document stop working simply got frozen make long story short got rip pound wasnt able sell anything amazoni still pound credit account buy cheap useless stuff floating amazoni learn lesson big company anything take money nothingthere strike back bitten robbed thrown like good old day wild westbecause internet using like wild westif small company get knokknok door uncle sam checking tax really carefully amazon get away offshort company steal billion pound local economy paying taxesi think time ti say mr bezos avoid amazon like devil avoid holly waterdont give hard earn money scammer,0.00589164047546498,0.994108359524535,0.2035894559730791,0.2,0.8377720709568832,83.77720709568833,High Trust
