-MaS-,/users/5e52e9a25aec3f2b5ed3ea0c,EG,3.0,2020-03-09 05:39:12+00:00,1.0,The worst online shopping experience ever,"I've an order from Amazon which I've placed on 17 Feb for international  shipment.The order have been shipped on 20 Feb and was estimated by the carrier to be delivered on 25 Feb and by Amazon on 3 March (Also this was inaccurate because one of my items was not available then it became available the next day).Until 24 Feb there was no tracking updates for my order, since then I've contacted Amazon customer service 10th of times, but keep saying ""Please wait your order will be delivered before 3rd March"".I've waited but nothing arrived on the date, contacted them again after 3rd March, but now they tell to wait until 11 March!!!I've paid for 7-10 days delivery and I had to wait for 19 days and still nothing delivered and all they tell it's not our issue but the carrier!!!Even I haven't chosen the carrier they still blame the carrier and me as I've to contact the carrier not them!!After a lot of chat with their bad customer service all they want to do to give me a 5$ promo for my next order!!!The worst service you can ever get, and they don't want to cancel and refund or at least compensate for the waste of time and money they caused to me.I'll never shop on Amazon again, even I was amazed by their service in the past.Now we have lots of other great online markets, who cares for their customers not like the very bad Amazon.",2020-03-09 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,3.0,9.0,1343,248,41,6,0.0,0,11,2,1,Suspicious,ive order amazon ive placed feb international shipmentthe order shipped feb estimated carrier delivered feb amazon march also inaccurate one item available became available next dayuntil feb tracking update order since ive contacted amazon customer service th time keep saying please wait order delivered rd marchive waited nothing arrived date contacted rd march tell wait marchive paid day delivery wait day still nothing delivered tell issue carriereven havent chosen carrier still blame carrier ive contact carrier themafter lot chat bad customer service want give promo next orderthe worst service ever get dont want cancel refund least compensate waste time money caused meill never shop amazon even amazed service pastnow lot great online market care customer like bad amazon,0.9999926801859202,7.319814079753684e-06,0.13909141895681434,0.2,0.32782194369840273,32.782194369840276,Low Trust
Jean M.,/users/5e65c7034c154f46f8289e77,US,1.0,2020-03-09 04:33:33+00:00,1.0,Repeated Failure to Deliver Within Time Frame,"This is the second or third time Amazon does not honor their delivery commitment.  I ordered (Order# 114-4637355-9134643) a Galaxy S20 case to be delivered on March 8, 2020.  Notification on my app says the delivery have not been made but after consulting with a representative over the phone, I was told that it was delivered based on notification they saw from the USPS website.  In fact, they were correct.  It read, ""March 8, 2020 at 12:10 pm. Delivered, In/At Mailbox. AURORA, CO 80014"" I found out later.  However, when I went back to my mailbox, there were no keys and nothing was delivered.  This is seriously starting to ruin the whole Amazon experience.  What I found more difficult is the ability to file a complaint with Amazon directly, or to leave a general review of  Amazon because I am confident the seller isn't responsible for this.  Leaving a negative review on the product will ruin the seller's reputation but would not serve the responsible parties, Amazon and its delivery partners.  After reading the review of another customer, it is becoming clear that this is Amazon's doing.  The customer's, Katherine of Baltimore, MD, comments on consumer affairs read, ""I've recently noticed a pattern in ordering from Amazon where when an order is placed within several minutes' cutoff for next or two day Prime delivery, the system stalls in placing the order so it will miss the cutoff and be bumped to the following day's delivery time from what it originally quoted. This is something that has happened multiple times and in a way that has caused me to be suspicious.""",2020-03-09 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,3.0,9.0,1588,270,45,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,second third time amazon honor delivery commitment ordered order galaxy case delivered march notification app say delivery made consulting representative phone told delivered based notification saw usps website fact correct read march pm delivered inat mailbox aurora co found later however went back mailbox key nothing delivered seriously starting ruin whole amazon experience found difficult ability file complaint amazon directly leave general review amazon confident seller isnt responsible leaving negative review product ruin seller reputation would serve responsible party amazon delivery partner reading review another customer becoming clear amazon customer katherine baltimore md comment consumer affair read ive recently noticed pattern ordering amazon order placed within several minute cutoff next two day prime delivery system stall placing order miss cutoff bumped following day delivery time originally quoted something happened multiple time way caused suspicious,0.003982096607917343,0.9960179033920826,0.1514301738642737,0.2,0.8282949864688961,82.8294986468896,High Trust
Henrik Nielsen,/users/4db6bcaa0000640001081023,DK,304.0,2020-03-09 00:52:33+00:00,1.0,Saturday 07/03 I receive a message from…,"Saturday 07/03 I receive a message from Amazon stating that they could not direct debit my account (due to my mistake) and they ask me to transfer the amount to their IBAN before 21/03.Anyway, I transfer the funds immediately upon receiving this message, but a bank transfer takes at least 1 banking day (not Saturday and not Sunday). Anyways, Sunday evening, I receive a new email that Amazon blocked my account until money is received.Hmm really? I thought I had until 21/03 to transfer the funds? I expect the transfer to go through immediately on Monday morning, but Amazon really shows its true colors here - a greedy company (who does not pay taxes and exploits its workforce to top it off). A leech on society.",2020-03-09 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,3.0,9.0,717,126,40,7,0.0,0,0,2,1,Suspicious,saturday receive message amazon stating could direct debit account due mistake ask transfer amount iban anyway transfer fund immediately upon receiving message bank transfer take least banking day saturday sunday anyways sunday evening receive new email amazon blocked account money receivedhmm really thought transfer fund expect transfer go immediately monday morning amazon really show true color greedy company pay tax exploit workforce top leech society,0.997291675575023,0.0027083244249770377,0.07066741446999439,0.2,0.3154876451064874,31.54876451064874,Low Trust
