mr elio tavernese,/users/53844140000064000175c3a4,GB,17.0,2020-02-29 10:10:40+00:00,1.0,First time (and last time) I have ordered with Amazon.com,"First time I have ordered, paid for and used Amazon.com. Purchased a descendants doll (hard to find in the uk) to arrive in time for daughters birthday. Got a message the day after the delivery was due to say it was going to be delayed. Next message to say they have refunded the money paid as they can not deliver the item. Sent an email to advise this was really poor service and was offered £10 credit and fast free shipping on next purchase. 1: do you think I wonder order again from you and 2: don’t think my daughter will take that as consolation for the gift she was expecting. Really disappointed and 1 star is a very generous rating.",2020-02-29 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,2.0,29.0,642,121,57,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,first time ordered paid used amazoncom purchased descendant doll hard find uk arrive time daughter birthday got message day delivery due say going delayed next message say refunded money paid deliver item sent email advise really poor service offered £ credit fast free shipping next purchase think wonder order don’t think daughter take consolation gift expecting really disappointed star generous rating,0.010087294618905427,0.9899127053810945,0.06786315199102635,0.2,0.8085289830887524,80.85289830887524,High Trust
chd,/users/54a433990000640001a14968,FR,16.0,2020-02-29 09:00:08+00:00,1.0,"How Amazon pollute the planet and why customers pay a lot of money for a home ""free delivery""","I wanted to report a largely exaggerated price and amazon deleted my comments and questions. I took an example on the product ""green curry blue elephant"" sold by an Indian company, but I suppose that there are many products in this case because many products sold on amazon are sent directly from China or from Asia in general.The same package of ""green curry blue elephant"" - 70 grams is sold:- about 4 euros on a French delicatessen site, this is where I bought this excellent product and then I checked if it was offered on Amazon. And the result is amazing:- 24 euros on the Amazon.fr site- 12.40 USD on Amazon.com therefore 11 euros- 230 Indian rupees on Amazon.in therefore 3 eurosOn the French price on Amazon.fr, the delivery costs are included for this Green Curry - and this is false because there is always a delivery price so this notion must disappear from Amazon because how a consumer can understand that for the price of 24 euros he buys a product worth 3 euros shipped from India, but there are 21 euros of shipping costs or additional margin because European consumers can pay an additional cost. And that consumers who want to protect the planet do not have the information of this additional cost and of the pollution it generates by having an object sent to them for 3 euros in Europe from India. And if he does not check the buyer he does not know that the product is shipped from India.The only solution is that Amazon removes its Premium, and displays for all products sold: the price of the product itself and the shipping costs so that the customer is aware of a purchase polluting for the planet and also so that it check if this same product is not sold locally with a quantity shipment therefore less costly per unit for the planet and for the customer. The country of shipment of the product must also be mentioned in order to alert the customer to the pollution caused if the distance is great.In addition, this product ""green curry blue elephant"" sold by the company ""Sun Ark Services Private limited"" based in Mumbai has obtained Indian opinions which are published on the French site. And it is not normal for Amazon to post an opinion from an Indian client on a French site because we cannot compare the price paid in India (3 euros) with the price asked in France (24 euros) for the same product because a customer's opinion integrates product quality and also value for money. And a European pays 21 euros for postage or additional margin for a product whose value is 3 euros. These Indian opinions completely bias the perception of a European customer who thinks that he is going to have a good product, which is the case, at the right price, completely false because too expensive, and there it is a scam because he pays 21 euros of shipping costs for 70 grams of curry.if I sum up Amazon protects an opportunistic Indian seller who lies by claiming that the port is free and who misinforms Amazon customers with a product 8 times more expensive than the Indian site, and 6 times more expensive than another French site (edelices.fr) because it does not display the shipping costs which are 21 euros for a 70 gram package of curry for a product that costs 3 euros (230 INR) shipped from India to Europe to unity - which is shocking for the preservation of the planet and for the customer who mostly buys shipping costs without knowing it. It is written that the delivery is free, in fact it never is and the price of the port has been added, but there it is exorbitant.In addition, this seller had my opinion deleted, because I know this product, because I informed Amazon customers of the abnormal price compared to a local purchase. Who pays the kilo of curry at 344 euros? it's ridiculous but people who don't know the price will make the mistake of buying and will pollute the planet without knowing it.Amazon have to give 2 prices : the price of the product and the price of delivery as there is always a delivery cost",2020-02-29 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,2.0,29.0,3962,713,93,18,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wanted report largely exaggerated price amazon deleted comment question took example product green curry blue elephant sold indian company suppose many product case many product sold amazon sent directly china asia generalthe package green curry blue elephant gram sold euro french delicatessen site bought excellent product checked offered amazon result amazing euro amazonfr site usd amazoncom therefore euro indian rupee amazonin therefore euroson french price amazonfr delivery cost included green curry false always delivery price notion must disappear amazon consumer understand price euro buy product worth euro shipped india euro shipping cost additional margin european consumer pay additional cost consumer want protect planet information additional cost pollution generates object sent euro europe india check buyer know product shipped indiathe solution amazon remove premium display product sold price product shipping cost customer aware purchase polluting planet also check product sold locally quantity shipment therefore less costly per unit planet customer country shipment product must also mentioned order alert customer pollution caused distance greatin addition product green curry blue elephant sold company sun ark service private limited based mumbai obtained indian opinion published french site normal amazon post opinion indian client french site cannot compare price paid india euro price asked france euro product customer opinion integrates product quality also value money european pay euro postage additional margin product whose value euro indian opinion completely bias perception european customer think going good product case right price completely false expensive scam pay euro shipping cost gram curryif sum amazon protects opportunistic indian seller lie claiming port free misinforms amazon customer product time expensive indian site time expensive another french site edelicesfr display shipping cost euro gram package curry product cost euro inr shipped india europe unity shocking preservation planet customer mostly buy shipping cost without knowing written delivery free fact never price port added exorbitantin addition seller opinion deleted know product informed amazon customer abnormal price compared local purchase pay kilo curry euro ridiculous people dont know price make mistake buying pollute planet without knowing itamazon give price price product price delivery always delivery cost,0.02357956886244668,0.9764204311375533,0.3998878295008413,0.2,0.8681877814689449,86.81877814689449,High Trust
