Alissa Ormond,/users/5e51e2fa6ca715dae082427f,US,1.0,2020-02-23 02:28:19+00:00,1.0,Lazy Scums Don't Help,"I would give it zero stars if I could. In December (two months ago), I went to a post office not knowing how bad it really was. Somehow the incompentent douche there managed to swap the packing lists/labels and sent the wrong textbooks to the wrong location. Long story about that one alone, but I will skip details and keep it relevant to how much of a joke Amazon is.  Anyway, after I have been informed from the college that they had the wrong books (which UW-Superior is also a major disappointment, save your money and pick literally anything else), I contacted Amazon Customer service. I had used the chat before and they were right on and so helpful. However, this time was so different. I started off with one person who said he going to transfer me...at least that was somewhat common courteous. Anyway, from there, about four or five other people kept connecting and then leaving the chat as soon as they were connected without a single word. The last one, Glen (Glenn?), said he would put in a form and I would get an email confirming when  it sent back. So anyway, since I lost faith in ALL of the Amazon world, I called customer support and they just kept hanging up. Four phone calls later, I officially decided that if they are too lazy that they can't make a lame a** excuse to not help me, they don't need me as a customer. Needless to say, I am no longer a Prime member and have not ordered since. Oh yeah, two months later and still have not had my books returned. Goodbye Amazon!!",2020-02-23 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,2.0,23.0,1500,277,21,4,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,would give zero star could december two month ago went post office knowing bad really somehow incompentent douche managed swap packing listslabels sent wrong textbook wrong location long story one alone skip detail keep relevant much joke amazon anyway informed college wrong book uwsuperior also major disappointmen