Rosie Brocklehurst,/users/5874d2ad0000ff000a6ab287,GB,53.0,2020-02-06 13:24:08+00:00,1.0,Unusually Bad Customer Service,"Small issue. Small amount of money involved. But Amazon Customer Service this time have been very poor indeed. Twice! It's the principle of the issue. I bought a small sturdy 8"" folding standing step so I could reach blinds in my hallway . I am partially disabled. The step arrived from Nubiru via Amazon with a broken hinge, with a leaflet saying do not use if damaged. I had to repackage the item and arrange to get to a post office which is difficult for me, given my disability, and all the inconvenience you can just imagine! The post office is half a mile away. On top of this, I had to pay for return postage as this item was not under the Prime Membership for which I pay £7.99 per month. I don't use any other Amazon services (as I don't know how to or whether it is worth it, other than Prime for postage). I did not receive any notification that the seller had received the item (which was only worth £5.74pence. Not a lot I know. So I chased. They then wanted proof of postage. I had to use my camera to sort this out and sent proof of postage to them via my email. (It goes to Amazon and is then forwarded). I received the £5.74 but not the postage reimbursement so I am out of pocket for a broken item by £3.00!  I sent a message to the seller and rang Amazon customer service. They also sent a message to the seller on Monday last. They said if I had not heard back in 48 hours I was to contact Amazon again. I did this today It was a call centre in India I believe. I called this morning and the person I spoke to wanted to have a copy of the post office receipt I photographed. I found it on my system and sent it and then she said she could not read it , and I needed to photograph it again. I am so fed up. I obviously would not have got even £5.74 back if I had not sent the proof of postage to Nubiru, the market place seller. I have had to to sort out my camera and then upload the picture  as I do not have or use a suitable smartphone. I feel like closing down  my account with Amazon, where I have spent many £thousands over 20 or more years, and speak to someone higher up about this. And Customer Service used to be so good at Amazon. I think it is attrition -their new policy - to be so unhelpful  they don't have to reimburse the money themselves and want me to give up. Thousands of small amounts unclaimed  add up to a lot of money for Mr Bezos.",2020-02-06 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,2.0,6.0,2376,471,30,4,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,small issue small amount money involved amazon customer service time poor indeed twice principle issue bought small sturdy folding standing step could reach blind hallway partially disabled step arrived nubiru via amazon broken hinge leaflet saying use damaged repackage item arrange get post office difficult given disability inconvenience imagine post office half mile away top pay return postage item prime membership pay £ per month dont use amazon service dont know whether worth prime postage receive notification seller received item worth £pence lot know chased wanted proof postage use camera sort sent proof postage via email go amazon forwarded received £ postage reimbursement pocket broken item £ sent message seller rang amazon customer service also sent message seller monday last said heard back hour contact amazon today call centre india believe called morning person spoke wanted copy post office receipt photographed found system sent said could read needed photograph fed obviously would got even £ back sent proof postage nubiru market place seller sort camera upload picture use suitable smartphone feel like closing account amazon spent many £thousands year speak someone higher customer service used good amazon think attrition new policy unhelpful dont reimburse money want give thousand small amount unclaimed add lot money mr bezos,0.8874402700503504,0.11255972994964958,0.2641615255187886,0.2,