Ivan,/users/568f609d0000ff0001fa5e57,RU,2.0,2020-01-30 16:46:24+00:00,1.0,"Worst customer service in europe, keep away from amazon es","My review is regarding customer service of amazon.es. I tried to buy a laptop from amazon.es on 28th of january, payment was declined due to ""suspicious actions"" perfomed, maybe because i was shopping from Czech republic on spanish amazon with my russian credit card, but i'm not sure. I was asked to provide billing address of the credit card, which i did. Then i tried to place my order again and payment was declined again. Account was blocked and i was asked to provide banking statement which contains billing address, but you can not get it from any russian bank, because we just do not ever receive statement via post or email, so there is no term ""billing adress"" in any card statement of russian bank. After that i created another amazon account and tried to do the purchase again ( it was not stated in email that i'm not allowed to do so), that account was also blocked again. This time amazon es customer service acted even worse, in the application they say i should follow instructions received via email, but in email they say i should follow instructions in the application!  Because of reversive conversion from RUB to EUR and back i lost approximately 100 EUR. Why does amazon charge me with the amount and then sends it back even though payment should have been declined? I don't know, but i really doubt now that will ever use service from amazon since they cant even make their customer service work as it should be!",2020-01-30 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,30.0,1437,256,58,10,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,review regarding customer service amazones tried buy laptop amazones th january payment declined due suspicious action perfomed maybe shopping czech republic spanish amazon russian credit card im sure asked provide billing address credit card tried place order payment declined account blocked asked provide banking statement contains billing a