Sandra Colquhoun,/users/5d48a732ccdcd10c9dd04bc9,GB,10.0,2020-01-27 07:01:16+00:00,1.0,I used Amazon customer service by text…,"I used Amazon customer service by text wish I hadn't bothered. I had ordered an Alexa beginning of January for 24.99 but it wasn't get delivered for another month. After ordering this I had taken on a free prime trial so wondered if I would get my order quicker with this. The rep said only way would be to cancel and order again I said ok didn't realise they couldn't order it but thought ok they've checked it's in stock so go ahead. When I went back to buy the Alexa it is now doubled in price from 24.99 to 49.99. I would expect a customer service person who had any sense would notice the difference in price and not advice someone to cancel an item they can then not afford to reorder. Please do not wrongly presume these people are efficient at their jobs and double-check what they saying before confirming , I wish I had.",2020-01-27 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,27.0,830,157,39,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used amazon customer service text wish hadnt bothered ordered alexa beginning january wasnt get delivered another month ordering taken free prime trial wondered would get order quicker rep said way would cancel order said ok didnt realise couldnt order thought ok theyve checked stock go ahead went back buy alexa doubled price would expect customer service person sense would notice difference price advice someone cancel item afford reorder please wrongly presume people efficient job doublecheck saying confirming wish,0.016559244652462446,0.9834407553475375,0.08805384183959619,0.2,0.8093311460416879,80.9331146041688,High Trust
