hayley Phillips,/users/5e1c60434c24534971ff48d6,GB,1.0,2020-01-13 12:20:11+00:00,1.0,Amazon are thieves.,"i have been in contact with Amazon since the end of November trying to sort out a complaint as they were taking THREE payments of Prime off me a month for nearly four years.I was lied to, accused of lying and had 0 help at all. My Prime payment was taken from my debit card on 28.11.19it was also taken from a Credit Card never used or linked to Amazon.i complained and was told i would receive a refund of £7.99 for four months for the inconvenience.i didn't receive this payment on time. so i complained again. It then came to light i was being charged for Prime three times a month since my account was opened on 05.09.2016. they claimed i opened two accounts with the same email address, postal address and contact number - definitely can't do this. I was told i would receive a refund of 29 months worth of prime (insulting considering i'd paid three times a month for 3 years, however i was so drained by the process and the incompetent staff members i just wanted to call it a day)i only received 13 of these.I contacted them again to see where the additional 16 were and i was told i would never have them. so i was lied to about that.I have had no help, empathy or sympathy from any one i have spoken to at Amazon considering they have been knowingly stealing from me for 3.5 years. Please, everyone check exactly how much they are taking from you monthly as tehy will definitely not return it. i am seeking legal advise for this and will ensure i tweet it so everyone can see what a thieving, horrible company Amazon really is.",2020-01-13 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,13.0,1537,288,19,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,contact amazon since end november trying sort complaint taking three payment prime month nearly four yearsi lied accused lying help prime payment taken debit card also taken credit card never used linked amazoni complained told would receive refund £ four month inconveniencei di