Kristen perez,/users/5e17b49a53022f600b6e6d07,US,2.0,2020-01-09 23:26:51+00:00,1.0,Worst company to back up their delivery…,"Worst company to back up their delivery services.  Does not provide refunds to customers if it's a 3rd party company,  even though they should stand by a product they are delivering and they are promoting!! Their drivers are very lazy. Dont even ring the bell when dropping at a residence they just drop at the location,  not to mention usually in plain sight. If it wasn't for the email alerts 9/10 times I wouldn't even know my package arrived and I'm almost always home awaiting its arrival due to this exact reason! I have been trying to locate one package with 2 some items for 8 days now and Amazon associate have been giving me the run around. Every time they admit it is lost and state they will give me a refund they then transfer me to a different department that contradicts their statements.  I never know whether I'm speaking to a human or a computer.  Not that it matters the humans are reading off a script. After 8 days of all this hastle of my lost items they now inform me they wont give me a refund unless I file a police report. Online they told me I could do it online or in person but then emails me and states in person only with strict guidelines.  All this for a simple $40 item I've already wasted 8 days of my life trying to locate, which on day one they should of instructed me on obtaining a police report.  I will be canceling my prime membership and will no longer be ordering any further items from them. At least target, walmart, Burlington,  use ups and they all RING the bell and at the very least attempt to hide the packages from plain site. My mailman was astonished with how my last 2 deliveries were just dropped right at the top of my stairs for all to see. Shame on your delivery people they are lazy",2020-01-09 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,9.0,1742,327,40,7,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,worst company back delivery service provide refund cu