Robert Allen,/users/5e14c06dffc8641a1c44bb27,US,1.0,2020-01-07 17:32:04+00:00,1.0,I am writing this message in regards to…,"I am writing this message in regards to a Stolen amazon account. I log in my amazon account on the morning of Sept 18 2019 and to my surprise someone had taken over the account and had charged 3 items, one being a amazon gift card for $500, to me and sent to an unrecognized email address. My email address was changed along with the phone number.Notice how i said the phone and email were changed, with that information the guy owns the account and amazon can do nothing to fix the issue in less than 72 hours or so i'm told. Now the interesting part I am able to tell them everything else to include credit card numbers and provide any identifying information they need but because my phone/email were changed I get treated very rudely.I was told by corporate receptionist that Amazon ""certainly doesn't need my money"" while im drastically trying to secure all my credit and bank cards that were tied to it, Amazon is rude and oblivious to what happened. I never received any information that my information was being changed within amazon. No email like you customer service over and over called me a liar for. I NEVER RECEIVED AN EMAIL!!! or any info that my info was being changed. I have been a customer for a very long time and 80-90% of products i have searched or bought off of Amazon.com. As a disabled vet living on fixed income it is horrendous how i was treated and certainly seems like i need to reevaluate doing business with Amazon.I have recorded message from employees laughing at me and telling me how it was my fault. Very unprofessional. I am disgruntled, said some things i'm not proud of as well but the audacity of a ""customer service rep"" or a ""corporate receptionist"" to chastise me at my lowest is disgusting. Very Dissapointed,",2020-01-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,7.0,1755,316,40,8,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,writing message regard stolen amazon account log amazon account morning sept surprise someone taken account charged item one amazon gift card sent unrecognized email address email address changed along phone numbernotice said phone email changed information guy owns account amazon nothing fix issue less hour im told interesting part able tell everything else include credit card number provide identifying information need phoneemail changed get treated rudelyi told corporate receptionist amazon certainly doesnt need money im drastically trying secure credit bank card tied amazon rude oblivious happened never received information information changed within amazon email like customer service called liar never received email info info changed customer long time product searched bought amazoncom disabled vet living fixed income horrendous treated certainly seems like need reevaluate business amazoni recorded message employee laughing telling fault unprofessional disgruntled said thing im proud well audacity customer service rep corporate receptionist chastise lowest disgusting dissapointed,0.46476899135323624,0.5352310086467638,0.1772293886707796,0.2,0.6030613820575379,60.30613820575379,Medium Trust
Craig R.,/users/5b6cd6fb4de5666d349fdcbc,US,4.0,2020-01-07 16:14:24+00:00,1.0,I'm done with Prime. No more paying for crap service!,"5 months of failed deliveries. This is ridiculous and yesterday was the final straw. I reside in a secure apartment community that has 24/7 call box access. Even a 2-year-old could figure it out! Look up the name, then key in 3 digit code and press the call button. Resident answers and presses 9 to open door. All of that info is in the delivery instructions. I even put the 3 digit code so they don't have to look me up. So what happens? Every time they show up when the office is closed they just drive off. They never even attempt to use the call boxes, NEVER! I complain every time and all the useless support staff does is put on their fake sincerity claiming they understand how upset I am. No, that's impossible. I spend a lot of money on Amazon. Over $3,000 in 2019 alone. Enough to make the cost of Prime worth it, but WTH good is it if it takes 2 or 3 delivery attempts every single time? It's basically paying them to screw me over. Yesterday was it, the last freaking straw! On Saturday my electric shaver broke. Now I could have gone to the mall or Walmart, but no, I chose to buy on Amazon and it was an Amazon sold item so next day (Sunday) delivery was guaranteed (that was manure)! So, what happens? As always the crappy delivery service shows up after 6 pm when the leasing office is closed and they just drive off, never even attempting to use the call boxes (there are two) that are in plain sight! As always I call and complain and get the same fake apologies and promises that it won't happen again. I'm even told that this time they will add instructions to call me prior to delivery if any issues. Well, the next day came and went with no delivery attempt and no phone call. Two damn days of dealing with a manual razor and useless people at Amazon logistics has me infuriated. Then they try to argue saying the driver said no access because the office is closed. I actually asked them if they were F-ing stupid because I have explained multiple times there is 24/7 access via call boxes. I demanded they explain how Dominos, Pizza Hut, Door Dash, Uber Eats and everyone else can deliver food with no issues, but a fracking damn near trillion-dollar company can't hire drivers willing to get off their lazy butts and use a call box? Of course no answer to that. Now I'm demanding they cancel the order and refund me, but they are trying to talk me into giving them another try. No, hell no, you are NOT getting a 3rd delivery attempt, just so the same a-hole can do another drive-by without trying. That was it. I was done. After getting it canceled I ended the call, went online and canceled Prime. I am not wasting another dime on a service that is impossible to receive. The extra 2% discount with Prime isn't worth it either as you need to spend at least $800 every month for that extra 2% to offset the cost of Prime. Free shipping you say? No that's nothing either because the standard shipping on in-stock items is never more than two days anyway. Well, 4-5 when you consider the moron drivers won't even try...",2020-01-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,7.0,3043,568,53,10,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,month failed delivery ridiculous yesterday final straw reside secure apartment community call box access even yearold could figure look name key digit code press call button resident answer press open door info delivery instruction even put digit code dont look happens every time show office closed drive never even attempt use call box never complain every time useless support staff put fake sincerity claiming understand upset thats impossible spend lot money amazon alone enough make cost prime worth wth good take delivery attempt every single time basically paying screw yesterday last freaking straw saturday electric shaver broke could gone mall walmart chose buy amazon amazon sold item next day sunday delivery guaranteed manure hap