John Crenshaw,/users/5e140e63361d61d3380e4c69,US,11.0,2020-01-07 05:30:23+00:00,2.0,I am a Prime member and normally I have…,"I am a Prime member and normally I have nothing but good things to say.  Not everything gets delivered within the Prime timetable but more than enough to keep me happy.  This morning I found a charge of $128.49 on my bank statement from Amazon that I could not justify with the orders that I had placed.  In this day of fraud and identity theft, I immediately called Amazon's customer service.  After having gone through the hoops and hurdles of validating who I am I got around to the matter of my concern.  The charge, as I discovered, was for my Prime membership fee for the new year.  Imagine how much time, not just mine but your rep's time as well, would have been saved if you had done a better job of declaring the nature of your fees and amount BEFORE hand.  I'll file this one under ""p**s poor"" consideration and communication on your part and hope that you, Amazon, will make improvements next year.",2020-01-07 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,7.0,910,166,40,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,prime member normally nothing good thing say everything get delivered within prime timetable enough keep happy morning found charge bank statement amazon could justify order placed day fraud identity theft immediately called amazon customer service gone hoop hurdle validating got around matter concern charge discovered prime membership fee new year imagine much time mine rep time well would saved done better job declaring nature fee amount hand ill file one p poor consideration communication part hope amazon make improvement next year,0.0073089596525235815,0.9926910403474765,0.09310151430173864,0.4,1.114965823034086,111.4965823034086,High Trust
