Lesley,/users/5e1008aa31bb5a9bee951742,US,1.0,2020-01-04 03:39:50+00:00,2.0,Delivery has gone badly since Amazon…,"Delivery has gone badly since Amazon decided to start doing their own deliveries.  Never had a problem when they were using 3rd party vendors (UPS, USPS).  My biggest complaint is that now  when you order, they give you a delivery date (usually w/in  day or two) and then the date gets changed (sometimes more than once).  Today, I was notified that my package was delivered, but it wasn't there.  When I contacted their ""chat assistant"", it stated that the package was delivered.  When I made the next choice that it didn't arrive, it immediately responded with some B.S. that the delivery must have been posted too soon, and that I should expect it 3 days from now!  WTH???  3 more days, Really???  Anti-Trust laws will catch up with Amazon at some point, and we will have choices for such services.  (In my lifetime - not sure).",2020-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,4.0,831,146,37,6,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,delivery gone badly since amazon decided start delivery never problem using rd party vendor ups usps biggest complaint order give delivery date usually win day two date get changed sometimes today notified package delivered wasnt contacted chat assistant stated package delivered made next choice didnt arrive immediately responded b delivery must posted soon expect day wth day really antitrust law catch amazon point choice service lifetime sure,0.03546102085565529,0.9645389791443447,0.08188446438586652,0.4,1.0986463824493455,109.86463824493455,High Trust
Mariner Hain,/users/5d8dd63035c3df5885729d08,AU,3.0,2020-01-04 01:30:04+00:00,1.0,impossible to get a refund.,Bought an item off amazon that was defective. Went online and got a swap of product and I clicked the dhl pick up return. The airwave bill did not exist. Called amazon they could not help only sent me an email that directed me to another number. Called that number they said it’s the wrong amazon number and could not help. Then got sent an email to rate there service. Pressed no it said sorry your account dose not exist. First and last perchase from amazon.,2020-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,4.0,460,86,27,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,bought item amazon defective went online got swap product clicked dhl pick return airwave bill exist called amazon could help sent email directed another number called number said it’s wrong amazon number could help got sent email rate service pressed said sorry account dose exist first last perchase amazon,0.029636170985553427,0.9703638290144466,0.04823331463825014,0.2,0.7948285774348733,79.48285774348733,High Trust
Paul Vobach,/users/5e0fe418361d615b9d0c9c95,US,1.0,2020-01-04 01:04:08+00:00,1.0,Amazon's customer service for sellers…,"Amazon's customer service for sellers is beyond horrible.  There is not an adjective in the English language to describe how bad they are.  I had what I thought was a pretty simple and fundamental question on changing the return address on the shipping labels that I produce as I have recently relocated.  The first call I made, after I navigated through the automated system, the rep I talked to I could barely understand first of all.  Secondly, he could not grasp what I was trying to do.  I had to explain it 5 times and beg to speak to another rep that I could understand and that could understand what I was trying to do.  After 25 minutes and nearly having a breakdown and him refusing to let me speak to someone else, he said that he would have someone return my call.  Three hours later I do get a call back from a ""SUPERVISOR.""  She was as clueless as he was, I had to explain it to her 3 times and she had to put me on hold to find a solution.  We did finally get the address changed after a total of 50 minutes on the phone (this is after I tried their ""chat"" service, which also sucks).  Holy cow...this wasn't a question of quantum physics or rocket science, I thought it was a pretty easy question that any competent customer service rep could spit out without having to go through the frustration of nearly an hour on the phone and wait 3 hours for a call back.  Not the first nor will it be the last frustrating I have with their extreme incompetence.  I know these people try their best and I am wrong in taking my frustrations out on them.  I fault AMAZON as a company for sending their customer service to a third world country.  #1) it lowers the quality of service we as sellers get,  #2)  It takes jobs away from the US where (I assume) most of their revenue comes from.  C'mon Jeff, there are millions of people here that are willing to work for 12.00 an hour, I know you got crushed in your divorce but give us the quality of service we deserve for the fees you charge us!",2020-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,4.0,1997,378,38,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer service seller beyond horrible adjective english language describe bad thought pretty simple fundamental question changing return address shipping label produce recently relocated first call made navigated automated system rep talked could barely understand first secondly could grasp trying explain time beg speak another rep could understand could understand trying minute nearly breakdown refusing let speak someone else said would someone return call three hour later get call back supervisor clueless explain time put hold find solution finally get address changed total minute phone tried chat service also suck holy cowthis wasnt question quantum physic rocket science thought pretty easy question competent customer service rep could spit without go frustration nearly hour phone wait hour call back first last frustrating extreme incompetence know people try best wrong taking frustration fault amazon company sending customer service third world country lower quality service seller get take job away u assume revenue come cmon jeff million people willing work hour know got crushed divorce give u quality service deserve fee charge u,0.04014453592517314,0.9598554640748269,0.21200224340998317,0.2,0.82232818071941,82.23281807194101,High Trust
Johnny,/users/5deba2b91ef7dc4a63dabef7,GB,2.0,2020-01-04 00:59:22+00:00,1.0,Lies lies lies,I placed an order in November 2019 that I was charged for over £500It was about a week before I got a delivery date window. On the final day of the delivery window amazon emailed a new dateI then went through and got written confirmation that the order would be delivered on 17th December. Then within the same hour of confirmation the delivery window changed this cycle continued I did get written confirmation that the order was cancelled from amazon but still no refundLot of lies being told and have lost all trust and confidence in amazonEvery customer service send you in circles with bad information and tell you the order will be delivered etc again and again but still no refund,2020-01-04 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,4.0,687,122,14,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,placed order november charged £it week got delivery date window final day delivery window amazon emailed new datei went got written confirmation order would delivered th december within hour confirmation delivery window changed cycle continued get written confirmation order cancelled amazon still refundlot lie told lost trust confidence amazonevery customer service send circle bad information tell order delivered etc still refund,0.007778415560790368,0.9922215844392096,0.06842400448681997,0.2,0.8097955931169688,80.97955931169687,High Trust
