CFD,/users/5d85190dd56ada01e46c1ebf,US,9.0,2020-01-10 05:33:38+00:00,1.0,Excuses & convenient Glitches for Amazon that they use to cover up their wrong actions!,"Apparently, Amazon does not like nor respect Customers that combe left over Amazon Balance/Gift Cards on their Orders placed when there is also a Credit Card used to pay for the remaining amount due on the Orders.   Amazon would rather Boycott & take off Amazon Balance/Gift Cards that we use & apply to our Orders without any permissions, for no apparent reasons & behind their Customers Backs!  This to then, fully charge our Credit Cards for the full amount of our Orders & then cover themselves up with excuses like, (""It was a Glitch in the System that caused this to happen & your Order can't be canceled now because it is already shipping soon.  Sorry about the inconvenience"")...I experienced what I explained above just recently on one of my Orders where I placed an Order on Amazon & specifically chose at & during Checkout to apply my remaining Amazon Balance/Gift Card to my Order to deduct that much Money off from what was due to be charged to my Credit Card.  All looked good until later that evening when I logged into my Checking Account & unexpectedly & shockingly saw a full pending charge from Amazon for my Order that did not look or sound quite right.  I did some looking into & investigating on this & found out that Amazon without my permission & behind my Back, took off my remaining Amazon Balance/Gift Card of $7.24 from my Order that I applied & then charged my Credit Card for the full amount as if they were trying to hold or freeze my remaining Amazon Balance & did not want it to be used up or applied to my Order that I placed with them.  Amazon then had my remaining now unused Amazon Balance/Gift Card of $7.24 showing up in my Amazon Account as $0.00 & (Pending) under Gift Cards even though, they took it off my Order & charged my Credit Card in full behind my back for no real apparent reason!  I contacted Amazon via Online Chat in hopes of making them fix this & making it right for me which of course did not happen.I Chatted with them regarding this issue, was hoping for & trying to get them to fix this problem that went wrong on their end with my Order & my remaining now (not applied) Amazon Account Balance of $7.24 that was clearly supposed to be applied towards this Order that I placed on Amazon.  Amazon's response was: ""There is nothing we can do to change or fix the issue with the Payment Method to apply your Account Balance to that Order like you are requesting, it was a Glitch in the System & unfortunately, your Order cannot be Canceled now as for it is already shipping out soon"".In my opinion, I am suspecting & thinking that this was a convenient Amazon planned or performed Glitch if you would call it, to take the full amount of Money for my Order from my Credit Card only, then Boycott & not let me use my remaining Amazon Account Balance on or towards this Order which (I did apply at Checkout) & then call it a System Glitch to cover themselves? I suspect & feel that that Amazon may be conveniently & purposely doing this to lots of their Customers in this way behind our Backs even though, we are choosing at Checkout to (Apply our remaining Amazon Account Balance/Gift Cards to & on our Orders that we are placing at the time). That is pretty greedy & crooked of Amazon to be doing this & playing this kind of actions on us in hopes that most of us will not notice nor even become aware of this!  Please do be aware & watch your Credit Cards when you've applied & used partial Amazon Balance/Gift Card remainders on Amazon Orders & then paid for the rest of your Order using a Credit or Debit Card like I did because they may do or try to do the same to you out of greediness & orneriness.",2020-01-01 00:00:00+00:00,2020.0,1.0,10.0,3659,680,87,15,9.0,0,3,1,0,Genuine,apparently amazon like respect customer combe left amazon balancegift card order placed also cre