Lora Eighmey,/users/5e0b5063361d6186940a8336,US,1.0,2019-12-31 13:43:06+00:00,1.0,I purchased a gift for my parents,"I purchased a gift for my parents. It came with a piece missing. I talked to customer service and could barely understand the lady because her accent was so thick and she had kids screaming in the background. She had a new item sent to my parents house and sent me a code on how to send back the damaged item. The new item arrived at me parents house a few days later and it looked like someone took a baseball bat to the item it was dented so bad. I called customer service and I got the same lady. I couldn’t understand her, and told her numerous times she needed to slow down and that she had too much background noise with the kids. She said ok. I asked her to send a new item to my parents house and had her repeat the address back to me (Still lots of noise). She sent me another code and my parents returned the item (I live out of town)Yesterday, the new item arrived at my house; not my parents house.Horrible experience with this lady. If you are going to be in customer service out of your house, make sure you speak clearly and there isn’t any background noise. Ugh",2019-12-31 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,31.0,1077,209,33,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,purchased gift parent came piece missing talked customer service could barely understand lady accent thick kid screaming background new item sent parent house sent code send back damaged item new item arrived parent house day later looked like someone took baseball bat item dented bad called customer service got lady couldn’t understand told numerous time needed slow much background noise kid said ok asked send new item parent house repeat address back still lot noise sent another code parent returned item live townyesterday new item arrived house parent househorrible experience lady going customer service house make sure speak clearly isn’t background noise ugh,0.01980460837570335,0.9801953916242967,0.117218171620863