E Dabrak,/users/5e021fcd31bb5ae8c08f5579,GB,2.0,2019-12-24 15:08:37+00:00,1.0,Order has been cancelled without any reasons and customer service didn't help,"I have ordered a WD My Cloud EX2 Ultra, 20 TB on Amazon.co.uk through a seller that is vouched by Amazon.co.uk. A few hours later my order was cancelled without any reasons even though the bank transaction has been authorised.I have contacted the Amazon.co.uk customer service to get to know why my order was cancelled and without any reasons. They replied to me that the seller has cancelled the order and that they couldn't do anything about it since the seller has cancelled it. I found it quite upsetting that Amazon.co.uk is vouching for sellers that have the possibility to cancel orders without giving any prior reason or just because they feel like it...It doesn't give me any reasons to trust to order in the future to Amazon.co.uk since they cannot do anything about it and they are not reassuring at all since they cannot promise it won't happen in the future and all they can say is ""I'm sorry this happened to you"".Thank you but this doesn't help me in this kind of situation.",2019-12-24 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,24.0,989,175,77,12,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered wd cloud ex ultra tb amazoncouk seller vouched amazoncouk hour later order cancelled without reason even though bank transaction authorisedi contacted amazoncouk customer service get know order cancelled without reason replied seller cancelled order couldnt anything since seller cancelled found quite upsetting amazoncouk vouching seller possibility cancel order without giving prior reason feel like itit doesnt give reason trust order future amazoncouk since cannot anything reassuring since cannot promise wont happen future say im sorry happened youthank doesnt help kind situation,0.011593618158758522,0.9884063818412415,0.0981491867638811,0.2,0.813833028273397,81.3833028273397,High Trust
