Maureen Meadows,/users/5df52a3c214ad898a772d7dc,US,3.0,2019-12-14 18:31:03+00:00,2.0,Increased delivery issues with property damage from driving on my grass,"I have been an Amazon customer since 2010 and an Amazon Prime customer since it began. I have placed at least 400 orders with them. All deliveries were perfect with no issues until now, delivery service begin to have horrible service the last 4 weeks. I notice all my delivery issues is when the carrier in a contract and is not a core carrier like FedEx or UPS. Three times in the month of December they have run off my driveway, ran over my sprinkler heads and put huge ruts in newly planted grass. It has cost me money to repair each time. I have entered 3 complaints for claims, attached photos and am still waiting on reimbursement. Also, these sub-contractors are not reading my very specific instructions that say, bring packages to front door only, do not leave by the garage where they are seen and can be stolen. DO not run off the driveway into my grass, do not run over my sprinkers. However, the problem is getting worse. I guess I will cancel Amazon Prime, go back to placing orders and choosing my own freight options. Not a happy customer at this time.",2019-12-14 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,14.0,1068,196,71,11,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer since amazon prime customer since began placed least order delivery perfect issue delivery service begin horrible service last week notice delivery issue carrier contract core carrier like fedex ups three time month december run driveway ran sprinkler head put huge rut newly planted grass cost money repair time entered complaint claim attached photo still waiting reimbursement also subcontractor reading specific instruction say bring package front door leave garage seen stolen run driveway grass run sprinkers however problem getting worse guess cancel amazon prime go back placing order choosing freight option happy customer time,0.01581395144718595,0.984186048552814,0.1