saj mahmood,/users/5956271d0000ff000aa9e979,ES,18.0,2019-12-12 20:54:09+00:00,1.0,Amazon can’t be trusted !!,"Amazon a brand you can trust right? NO!So, my brother ordered 4 x Gtech Airram 2 vacuum cleaners, 1 was for him, the other for me and the last 2 were going to be presents. When Black Friday came along who better to take advantage of with their special Black Friday offers than Amazon, after all their customer service is supposedly excellent and they are a reputable company - NOT THIS TIME!!The 4 items were ordered and paid for on their website and we waited for the 1 week deliver date, we are Prime customers and use Amazon frequently for many items. We were excited having bagged a bargain at £120 each, the delivery date came and went and that’s when the problems started. Amazon were contacted to enquire about the whereabouts of the items, after several calls they finally informed us that the items had been delivered! Apparently they had been left at the address in a safe place, we hadn’t received anything. On checking the tracking it appeared that the items had been delivered to somewhere in Scotland and not to us in London. Many stressful days passed and there seemed to be no resolution, Amazon have 3rd party sellers on their websites and apparently the vendor wasn’t bothering to respond to their messages. We kept stressing to them that we wanted the items and not a refund, Amazon decided to refund us anyway! Hooray! We didn’t lose out right? Well, according to Amazon no we didn’t. Amazing, no compensation no nothing! The said vendor is still happily trading on Amazon and selling the vacuums at £200 now. We had many options of purchasing the Gtechs from various places on Black Friday, instead we wrongly trusted Amazon and have now missed out on the Black Friday offers, they suggested that we buy again if we wanted. Well, the whole point of Black Friday is to pick up a bargain and not be forced into paying for something and missing out on a bargain. So, they now think that through no fault of our own we should pay £320 more to buy the same again!I genuinely believe that the Vendor didn’t send anything, they obviously realised that they had priced the item too cheap and decided to pretend that they had sent them to a wrong address, wait for the customer to complain and then refund the customer the original cost, meantime they continue to use the Amazon platform to sell the vacuum cleaners at the normal non discounted price of £200. It’s unbelievable that Amazon allow this kind of practice where their customers lose out!I’ll never be using Amazon again, do so at your own peril.",2019-12-12 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,12.0,2519,448,26,5,0.0,0,9,2,1,Suspicious,amazon brand trust right noso brother ordered x gtech airram vacuum cleaner last going present black friday came along better take advantage special black friday offer amazon customer service supposedly excellent reputable company timethe item ordered paid website waited week deliver date prime customer use amazon frequently many item excited bagged bargain £ delivery date came went that’s problem started amazon contacted enquire whereabouts item several call finally informed u item delivered apparently left address safe place hadn’t received anything checking tracking appeared item delivered somewhere scotland u london many stressful day passed seemed resolution amazon rd party seller website apparently vendor wasn’t bothering respond message kept stressing wanted item refund amazon decided refund u anyway hooray didn’t lose right well according amazon didn’t amazing compensation nothing said vendor still happily trading amazon selling vacuum £ many option purchasing gtechs various place black friday instead wrongly trusted amazon missed black friday offer suggested buy wanted well whole point black friday pick bargain forced paying something missing bargain think fault pay £ buy againi genuinely believe vendor didn’t send anything obviously realised priced item cheap decided pretend sent wrong address wait customer complain refund customer original cost meantime continue use amazon platform sell vacuum cleaner normal non discounted price £ it’s unbelievable amazon allow kind practice customer lose outi’ll never using amazon peril,0.999912333101842,8.766689815797868e-05,0.2512619181155356,0.2,0.3502962170721861,35.02962170721861,Low Trust
All About Food First (Gale),/users/5df291fe2ed7ce9c27fb2d8f,US,2.0,2019-12-12 19:16:22+00:00,2.0,Amazon have gotten very messy,"Amazon have gotten very messy with their services. Mixing up orders, delivering the wrong packages I’ve ordered with Amazon for years and they are not the same they’ll tell you your package is coming one day and will come on a different day I called Customer Service and it took almost a hour fo handle a very simple solution   The Amazon Prime is supposed to a 2 day’s delivery it could be 4 days before you get your package I’m done with them!",2019-12-12 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,12.0,445,83,29,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,amazon gotten messy service mixing order delivering wrong package i’ve ordered amazon year they’ll tell package coming one day come different day called customer service took almost hour fo handle simple solution amazon prime supposed day’s delivery could day get package i’m done,0.04059999042525486,0.9594000095747451,0.04655075715086932,0.4,1.0890101562175465,108.90101562175465,High Trust
Sven M,/users/5df28059815b048f54757b26,US,1.0,2019-12-12 18:01:44+00:00,1.0,Contractors and Business Customers…,"Contractors and Business Customers Beware:Amazon’s Guarantee delivery is actually not a Guarantee.  It is through whatever carrier they decide to send your package. I am flipping a house while I live in it.  I have contractors and suppliers who all meet their deadlines. Not one contractor or supplier has cost me the time nd money this has.I have been doing business with Amazon for years.  I have an account through one of my businesses. I am seriously contemplating shutting this account down. I ordered a shower system, 2 faucets and 2 bath lights for the finishing touches on the bath.  The most important product is the shower valve as the Plumber and tile guys are waiting for it.  Everyone is shut down because Amazon cannot get the delivery to me or find out where it is. Unfortunately I will have to spend my time finding new products at local a supplier, Home Depot or Lowes after spending hours looking for what I wanted and finally thinking I found it on Amazon.Unfortunately my contractors may have to move to other jobs and our job will have to be put off a month or 2.  Luckily the toilet is working.I won’t bore you with the 2 hrs on the phone with Amazon and 1 with UPS the 8 people who where powerless to help.  Yes 8 people. The interesting thing was the first girl in the beginning had the most solutions.  The supervisors by the way as the highest Amazon person us little customers are permitted to talk to are a person on the “membership leadership team” Chelsy.  What a joke.  According to her Amazon gives them absolutely no ability to be leaders with us the customers/members. No ability to get needed products or answers.I was informed by Amazon that they cannot and will not call UPS to get my items delivered. I ended up spending another 1 hour on the phone with UPS so far. I am now on hold for the second time.  All this time and my goal is to drive 45 minutes each way the UPS distribution center to pick up and deliver my own package.  I estimate this will be 2+ additional hours my time plus gas and milage on my vehicle.  ALL FOR A SHOWER VALVE.  In hopes of getting the supplies for the plumber and tile guys so the job does not get postponed and/or additional labor charges will be applied to the job.  Amazon will not compensate for your time is what Chelsy stated to me. So they do not value their customers time obviously.  At the time of this post I have been on hold for the second time with UPS. As of now 30 more minutes.DONT BUY YOUR CONSTRUCTION OR TOOLS THROUGH AMAZON IF YOU NEED THEM FOR A JOB ANY TIME SOON.It would seem Amazon is getting so big they dont even have to advertise the truth or they dont understand what the definition of guarantee is. To enlighten them;guar·an·tee/ˌɡerənˈtē/￼Learn to pronouncenoun1. 1. a formal promise or assurance (typically in writing) that certain conditions will be fulfilled, especially that a product will be repaired or replaced if not of a specified quality and durability.""we offer a 10-year guarantee against rusting""2. provide a formal assurance or promise, especially that certain conditions shall be fulfilled relating to a product, service, or transaction.",2019-12-12 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,12.0,3154,559,35,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,contractor business customer bewareamazon’s guarantee delivery actually guarantee whatever carrier decide send package flipping house live contractor supplier meet deadline one contractor supplier cost time nd money hasi business amazon year account one business seriously contemplating shutting account ordered shower system faucet bath light finishing touch bath important product shower valve plumber tile guy waiting everyone shut amazon cannot get delivery find unfortunately spend time finding new product local supplier home depot lowes spending hour looking wanted finally thinking found amazonunfortunately contractor may move job job put month luckily toilet workingi won’t bore hr phone amazon ups people powerless help yes people interesting thing first girl beginning solution supervisor way highest amazon person u little customer permitted talk person “membership leadership team” chelsy joke according amazon give absolutely ability leader u customersmembers ability get needed product answersi informed amazon cannot call ups get item delivered ended spending another hour phone ups far hold second time time goal drive minute way ups distribution center pick deliver package estimate additional hour time plus gas milage vehicle shower valve hope getting supply plumber tile guy job get postponed andor additional labor charge applied job amazon compensate time chelsy stated value customer time obviously time post hold second time ups minutesdont buy construction tool amazon need job time soonit would seem amazon getting big dont even advertise truth dont understand definition guarantee enlighten themguar·an·teeˌɡerənˈtē￼learn pronouncenoun formal promise assurance typically writing certain condition fulfilled especially product repaired replaced specified quality durabilitywe offer year guarantee rusting provide formal assurance promise especially certain condition shall fulfilled relating product service transaction,0.005930462931473104,0.9940695370685269,0.3135165451486259,0.2,0.8597380775639886,85.97380775639886,High Trust
