Karlie Huff,/users/5decba67741d5f2d7036078f,US,1.0,2019-12-08 08:59:12+00:00,1.0,"Only if I’m desperate, will I order from Amazon again!","I recently ordered an electronic and a few other items from Amazon for Christmas presents.  When I hadn’t received any info regarding the purchase, I tried to look into it from my account.  I was locked out of my Amazon account for no apparent reason.  Despite having numerous security codes sent to my phone and email account, I couldn’t get passed the added security question, which I could not answer.  The security question was asking the expiration date on an old debit card that they had on file.  Not the last card I used, but one that was on file.  It was a card that I had canceled due to fraud almost a year ago.  I called customer service and told them that I just wanted to see about my most recent purchase.  I told them the credit card I used, , as well as the items purchased. All of this was to no avail.  The customer service rep would not unlock my account and she told me my order had been canceled.  She told me the credit card company canceled my order.  After a long wait on hold with the credit card company, I was told they had not declined my purchase, nor do they cancel people’s  orders.   I ended up ordering the electronic directly from Apple, which is what I should have done in the first place.  Low and behold, a few days later, I received a text that my amazon order was on the way!  Ugh!  Now I will have the headache of having to send it back when it arrives!  I’m so done with Amazon!",2019-12-08 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,8.0,1420,269,54,10,0.0,0,4,2,1,Suspicious,recently ordered electronic item amazon christmas present hadn’t received info regarding purchase tried look account locked amazon account apparent reason despite numerous security code sent phone email account couldn’t get passed added security question could answer security question asking expiration date old debit card file last card used one file card canceled due fraud almost year ago called customer service told wanted see recent purchase told credit card used well item purchased avail customer service rep would unlock account told order canceled told credit card company canceled order long wait hold credit card company told declined purchase cancel people’s order ended ordering electronic directly apple done first place low behold day later received text amazon order way ugh headache send back arrives i’m done amazon,0.794948582848858,0.20505141715114195,0.15086932136848008,0.2,0.43269957284926697,43.2699572849267,Low Trust
