Sarah Cochran,/users/5dea66b7153b7e1647929b91,DO,1.0,2019-12-06 14:33:34+00:00,1.0,There is absolutely NO ACCOUNTABILITY…,"There is absolutely NO ACCOUNTABILITY for not delivering on time. They continually say “sorry for the misunderstanding” when an item is delayed...I’m not talking a day late, but more like 5 days or more. So patronizing to say it was a misunderstanding! When we purchase an item with a “guaranteed” delivery date, what does that mean? To Amazon, nothing. I’m not talking about extenuating circumstances for the delivery to be late. No accountability.  What’s the point in Paying for prime if there’s the “guarantee” means nothing. I hope Amazon gets this. I wouldn’t want them to think this is a “misunderstanding”.",2019-12-06 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,6.0,614,101,38,5,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,absolutely accountability delivering time continually say “sorry misunderstanding” item delayedi’m talking day late like day patronizing say misunderstanding purchase item “guaranteed” delivery date mean amazon nothing i’m talking extenuating circumstance delivery late accountability what’s point paying prime there’s “guarantee” mean nothing hope amazon get wouldn’t want think “misunderstanding”,0.13326407950615027,0.8667359204938497,0.056646102075154234,0.2,0.7446971806619557,74.46971806619557,Medium Trust
