Ann Horst,/users/5de7f6b8741d5ff57433be12,US,2.0,2019-12-04 18:11:12+00:00,1.0,"Lord, help us. Amazon, you are fired!","Lord, help anyone who places an order or receives an order from Amazon that requires customer service.  They don't make anxiety meds powerful enough for what I am experiencing.  It's as though I have been calling a plumbing service to help me find my Amazon gift.  I have been at this since last night!  The gift is here - at my apartment complex - in a locker - and yet, six calls or transfers later, and I still have no idea which locker or what code to use.  Apparently plumbers can't help with Amazon orders.  Just letting you know up front.  And, they emailed my mother letting her know they canceled her Prime account when it was mine that never should have been charged in the first place.  Actually, you know what?  A plumber probably would have found my gift by opening the darned locker for me and they would have understood that a mother and a daughter are not the same person.  Please use small business instead.  Put the gift in a box. Go to the post office, use their kiosk, and get the item shipped with a tracking code.  Old fashioned shipping still works.  We don't need Amazon and their unpaid and terribly trained workforce.  Bezos, You are not getting any more of my money.",2019-12-04 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,12.0,4.0,1193,217,37,7,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,lord help anyone place order receives order amazon requires customer service dont make anxiety med powerful enough experiencing though calling plumbing service help find amazon gift since last night gift apartment complex locker yet six call transfer later still idea locker code use apparently plumber cant help amazon order letting know front emailed mother letting know canceled prime account mine never charged first place actually know plumber probably would found gift opening darned locker would understood mother daughter person please use small business instead put gift box go post office use kiosk 