Ling Zao Po,/users/5ddb20ebfe6f624b5de88651,AU,1.0,2019-11-25 00:32:20+00:00,1.0,Amazon sucks - big time!,"Using my debit card, I bought a product from Amazon au, then found out it was being fulfilled from China. PayPal debited the amount immediately (authorisation). Two days later I received an email from the Seller (Assi) that the order HAD BEEN SHIPPED and would arrive in the next 27 days! My statement then reflected that the amount was fully debited, i.e. the ""authorisation"" condition was withdrawn. Four days later, I received an email from the Seller ""Assi"" (funny how phonetically that could be confused by the unwary as ""Aussie""), that the item was out of stock, and I would receive a full refund within the next 10-20 days!Question: How can I be told FIVE DAYS LATER that an item which has actually been PAID FOR AND DISPATCHED is now ""out of stock"" and a refund is pending for nearly a month to be paid?Where are you now Steve Bezos?",2019-11-25 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,25.0,841,150,24,5,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,using debit card bought product amazon au found fulfilled china paypal debited amount immediately authorisation two day later received email seller assi order shipped would arrive next day statement reflected amount fully debited ie authorisation condition withdrawn four day later received email seller assi funny phonetically could confused unwary aussie item stock would receive full refund within next daysquestion told five day later item actually paid dispatched stock refund pending nearly month paidwhere steve bezos,0.16115451432878639,0.8388454856712136,0.08412787436904094,0.2,0.736248317709415,73.6248317709415,Medium Trust
