Mark,/users/5dd3c81e041053cffb435a9e,JP,1.0,2019-11-19 10:47:36+00:00,1.0,I am a Prime member of Amazon and I…,"I am a Prime member of Amazon and I ordered memory sticks from Amazon and the item was sold and fulfilled by Amazon directly.The original packaging of the RAM had a new label placed over the original, stating what I ordered online and expecting.  However the contents of the package contained the memory which was stated on the original packaging (Not what I ordered).Someone purposely relabeled the RAM falsely representing the RAM and it was sold to me.  Amazon refused to help me with a refund or credit, regardless of whether I had pictures of the original unaltered packaging, and regardless of having the direct proof of the item packaging which had the correct label covered over by an erroneous one (representing what I actually wanted and ordered).Amazon's p!ss poor excuse.  ""Because you used a Freight Forwarder""So this means if Amazon knows you will use a Freight Forwarded, Amazon could simply ship you a Jelly Bean instead that new camera you wanted, and you have NO LEGAL RECOURSE in their eyes.   It's a cowardly policy and treats customers guilty until proven innocent.  Yet they won't even allow use to prove innocence!Disgraceful business tactic and poor customer service.BEWARE OF AMAZON'S SHADY UNDERHANDED TACTICS!",2019-11-19 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,19.0,1236,202,36,9,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,prime member amazon ordered memory stick amazon item sold fulfilled amazon directlythe original packaging ram new label placed original stating ordered online expecting however content package contained memory stated original packaging orderedsomeone purposely relabeled ram falsely representing ram sold amazon refused help refund credit regardless whether picture original unaltered packaging regardless direct proof item packaging correct label covered erroneous one representing actually wanted orderedamazons ps poor excuse used freight forwarderso mean amazon know use freight forwarded amazon could simply ship jelly bean instead new camera wanted legal recourse eye cowardly policy treat customer guilty proven innocent yet wont even allow use prove innocencedisgraceful business tactic poor customer servicebeware amazon shady underhanded tactic,0.5262478218667567,0.47375217813324333,0.11329220415030847,0.2,0.5595345298966834,55.95345298966834,Medium Trust
