Donald Bogden,/users/5dcf19f9e78ec4552c6269e2,US,1.0,2019-11-15 21:42:16+00:00,1.0,Amazon Customer Service Is Incompetent,"Amazon Customer Service Is Incompetent; Having a payment dispute with these people is drip torture. I had my credit card information hacked and the person used it to buy products via amazon marketplace. Amazon notified me that since my credit card company disputed the charges with them, they were subsequently holding me responsible. Amazon simultaneously froze my prime account (blocking my access and alerting me in a 4 sentence email) and told me the only way to reactivate it was to pay in full for the fraudulent activity (amazing considering the charges were not even made through my amazon account, just with the credit card I have saved in amazon).The kicker is, of course, that it’s not possible to directly speak with an amazon representative to explain their rationale or the process, let alone to resolve. So 4 phone calls and 5 days later I’m still waiting for a return phone call from amazon to explain how this is even possible.So basically you can get a 100lb piece of heavy machinery delivered to your doorstep in two days via AmazonPrime, but if you’re the victim of fraud, you're guilty until proven innocent (and that’s going to take atleast a coupe weeks).FML",2019-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,15.0,1181,201,38,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon customer service incompetent payment dispute people drip torture credit card information hacked person used buy product via amazon marketplace amazon notified since credit card company disputed charge subsequently holding responsible amazon simultaneously froze prime account blocking access alerting sentence email told way reactivate pay full fraudulent activity amazing considering charge even made amazon account credit card saved amazonthe kicker course it’s possible directly speak amazon representative explain rationale process let alone resolve phone call day later i’m still waiting return phone call amazon explain even possibleso basically get lb piece heavy machinery delivered doorstep two day via amazonprime you’re victim fraud youre guilty proven innocent that’s going take atleast coupe weeksfml,0.012303501550761714,0.9876964984492382,0.11273135165451487,0.2,0.816394519555522,81.6394519555522,High Trust
autumn Hall,/users/5dcef5516cc9f93858c8589b,US,1.0,2019-11-15 18:58:53+00:00,1.0,Amazon gives an AWFUL experience.,"I recieved an email from Amazon stating that I had received a 10$ e-book coupon, there was even a button that said ""claim your 10$ reward."" When I tapped on the button it led me to a web page that says I'm not eligible. No where in the entire email does it say only certain people are eligible, it even says those who recieved the email were rewarded the coupon. I started a live chat with an Amazon employee and I've never had a representative lash out on me like he did. I still have screenshots too. He straight up told me, exact words, ""I'm not going to help you"" and refused to put me through to anyone else. Isn't that his job?? He didn't help me or give any info the entire chat. Later I recieved a direct email from someone higher-up letting me know that I indeed WAS eligible for the coupon, when the guy in the chat told me I was not. The whole experience over something so miniscule was awful and the jacka** representative shouldn't be working at a job that's meant to help people and be nice if it's so difficult for him. Also, you can't review a product unless you've spent 50$ on Amazon. IF YOU BUY A PRODUCT, FOR ANY PRICE, YOU SHOULD BE ABLE TO LEAVE A REVIEW ON THAT PRODUCT. This company is shady as fu*k.",2019-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,15.0,1224,235,33,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recieved email amazon stating received ebook coupon even button said claim reward tapped button led web page say im eligible entire email say certain people eligible even say recieved email rewarded coupon started live chat amazon employee ive never representative lash like still screenshots straight told exact word im going help refused put anyone else isnt job didnt help give info entire chat later recieved direct email someone higherup letting know indeed eligible coupon guy chat told whole experience something miniscule awful jacka representative shouldnt working job thats meant help people nice difficult also cant review product unless youve spent amazon buy product price able leave review product company shady fuk,0.0424745184707501,0.9575254815292499,0.13180033651149747,0.2,0.8051228080669244,80.51228080669244,High Trust
Ivan,/users/5dcef2bc87f09f4c0622fd37,US,1.0,2019-11-15 18:47:30+00:00,1.0,Amazon.com representative are abusers.,"I called for the Air-pods, cable lightning and cover for the items. These items do not function accurately with Android devices, which is not describe on its manual. After communicating to customer services, they dismissed the return. They expressed that I need to reach the manufacture to return the items, manufacture explained that i need to contact Amazon.com. In addition. I was very respectful. I was transfer to another representative because no one could help. The last representative hang up the phone call on me. I had been an Amazon Prime Member for many years. I don’t appreciate how Amazon.com is conducting business, but that action was absolutely abusive, onslaught and offensive from their representative.",2019-11-15 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,15.0,721,115,38,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,called airpods cable lightning cover item item function accurately android device describe manual communicating customer service dismissed return expressed need reach manufacture return item manufacture explained need contact amazoncom addition respectful transfer another representative one could help last representative hang phone call amazon prime member many year don’t appreciate amazoncom conducting business action absolutely abusive onslaught offensive representative,0.01759116187376155,0.9824088381262385,0.06449803701626472,0.2,0.8041040264663721,80.41040264663721,High Trust
