Sally Nightmare,/users/5dbf6898e6bff76e692684e7,US,1.0,2019-11-03 23:54:11+00:00,5.0,My wife and I had an issue of being…,"My wife and I had an issue of being charged for Amazon Prime membership when She wasn't a Prime member. We noticed the charge after it made that checking account overdraft and, get a $29.00 overdraft fee. We then back tracked how long it had been happening. It happened for seven months. She contacted customer service and spoke to a man named Jake. He was very courteous and compassionately professional with his behavior. He fully reimbursed us for the mistake plus the overdraft fee. I respectfully say thank you for your great customer service representatives. 5 stars indeed.",2019-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,3.0,580,98,36,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wife issue charged amazon prime membership wasnt prime member noticed charge made checking account overdraft get overdraft fee back tracked long happening happened seven month contacted customer service spoke man named jake courteous compassionately professional behavior fully reimbursed u mistake plus overdraft fee respectfully say thank great customer service representative star indeed,0.03998011583068941,0.9600198841693106,0.054963544587773416,1.0,1.99100265100221,199.100265100221,High Trust
Baja John,/users/5dbf3abaf223d81602f126cf,MX,1.0,2019-11-03 20:38:22+00:00,1.0,Dismal if things go wrong. Website is part of the problem.,"Never had a problem with Amazon in the US but I now suspect that was because things never went wrong. Their international shipping and foreign websites are another story because more problems are encountered which their websites and customer service aren't dealing with effectively. I think the sites are evolving as features seem to change. First, the international shopping feature on the US site had issues when I last used them. At least to Mexico. They claim hassle-free shipping and refunds if things don't arrive on one web page but their agreement page states that the buyer is responsible for customs fees and shipping. Confusing and contradictory if not a legal loophole and certainly not 'hassle free"". They claim that entering a foreign address for delivery will only allow sale of items that can be mailed to that address. I have had 3 failed deliveries due to orders blocked by Customs. Secondly, their problem resolution via web pages and customer service is difficult, time-consuming and at times ineffective. On one occasion I spent 5 weeks of wrangling for a refund over a $600 order which Amazon Mexico reported had been lost in the (Mexican) mail system. After 5 weeks I gave up on Amazon and went to my credit card company which immediately issued a refund that wasn't contested by Amazon. (Note that refunds of Amazon purchases from third-party vendors are discretionary since they are not coveted by the same rules as direct purchases). Both US and Mexican site had no way of requesting a refund for a lost package. Their AI interface restricts selections and the one page which comes up with a button for lost packages brings up a previous page to repeat an endless and futile cycle. The only page that allows unfiltered contact to customer service is at the very bottom of the first displayed when you select the 'contact customer service"" link on the US site. The Mexican site doesn""t allow unfiltered contact. Perhaps Amazon needs to pay heed to the message on their customer service feedback at the end of customer service messages, noting that feedback is helping them construct the 'most customer-centered business on earth.' There are no customer service email addresses or telephone numbers displayed on the Amazon web pages. They can be found for the US and Mexico by doing a web search. Customer service (CS) were always polite and often helpful. However, on one occasion a lost package in Mexico suggests significant chaos and inattentiveness. An ongoing problem isn't followed up by a single person, even when I replied to the specific, numbered email address of the CS representative who emailed me. On each of 5 occasions the reply was from a different individual who, in each case promised that they would personally take care of the problem. I also called a few times and the CS representatives who answered always asked for time to review the case and get back to me, suggesting there wasn't an easily accessible record of the problem or any progress to resolve it. There is a message system embedded in your account information that I wasn't even aware of until a CS representative told me and provided a link. It took a few more days to find a link to it through the Amazon web pages. You can find it by selecting the 'my account' menu. It depends on the app where you will find it on the congested page which is displayed. On some apps it is displayed in the 'My Account' menu. It is an easy way to pick up and reply to messages from vendors but is 'read only' for Customer Service, once again foiling any option of continuity for an ongoing problem. Amazon Mexico fails to correctly identify mail carriers in Mexico, doesn't always update tracking information and later deletes all carrier information. One package was delivered by FedEx, with a FedEx label. My Amazon Mexico order details identified the carrier as Estafeta and provided a tracking number which the Estafeta tracking page said was invalid. My Amazon pages correctly tracked the package and when I used the tracking number on the FedEx tracking, it was accepted and gave identical information to Amazon and more. The expensive lost package was also reported as carried by Estafeta, but with an invalid tracking number. I couldn't check the number on FedEx pages because Amazon had deleted the tracking information from my order details. WHY??? In another case I followed up with a third party vendor on an internationally shipped order through Amazon US because it was a couple of weeks late. Amazon tracking information hadn't changed over the 2 week, indicating that it had 'left the carrier facility in Mexico City'. The vendor reported that a delivery had been attempted and also noted that it was better to track on the carrier's website as Amazon was notoriously poor at updating tracking information.And yes, this account reports Only my own experiences - over about the last six months",2019-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,3.0,4904,835,58,11,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,never problem amazon u suspect thing never went wrong international shipping foreign website another story problem encountered website customer service arent dealing effectively think site evolving feature seem change first international shopping feature u site issue last used least mexico claim hasslefree shipping refund thing dont arrive one web page agreement page state buyer responsible custom fee shipping confusing contradictory legal loophole certainly hassle free claim entering foreign address delivery allow sale item mailed address failed delivery due order blocked custom secondly problem resolution via web page customer service difficult timeconsuming time ineffective one occasion spent week wrangling refund order amazon mexico reported lost mexican mail system week gave amazon went credit card company immediately issued refund wasnt contested amazon note refund amazon purchase thirdparty vendor discretionary since coveted rule direct purchase u mexican site way requesting refund lost package ai interface restricts selection one page come button lost package brings previous page repeat endless futile cycle page allows unfiltered contact customer service bottom first displayed select contact customer service link u site mexican site doesnt allow unfiltered contact perhaps amazon need pay heed message customer service feedback end customer service message noting feedback helping construct customercentered business earth customer service email address telephone number displayed amazon web page found u mexico web search customer service c always polite often helpful however one occasion lost package mexico suggests significant chaos inattentiveness ongoing problem isnt followed single person even replied specific numbered email address c representative emailed occasion reply different individual case promised would personally take care problem also called time c representative answered always asked time review case get back suggesting wasnt easily accessible record problem progress resolve message system embedded account information wasnt even aware c representative told provided link took day find link amazon web page find selecting account menu depends app find congested page displayed apps displayed account menu easy way pick reply message vendor read customer service foiling option continuity ongoing problem amazon mexico fails correctly identify mail carrier mexico doesnt always update tracking information later deletes carrier information one package delivered fedex fedex label amazon mexico order detail identified carrier estafeta provided tracking number estafeta tracking page said invalid amazon page correctly tracked package used tracking number fedex tracking accepted gave identical information amazon expensive lost package also reported carried estafeta invalid tracking number couldnt check number fedex page amazon deleted tracking information order detail another case followed third party vendor internationally shipped order amazon u couple week late amazon tracking information hadnt changed week indicating left carrier facility mexico city vendor reported delivery attempted also noted better track carrier website amazon notoriously poor updating tracking informationand yes account report experience last six month,0.003497583718160764,0.9965024162818392,0.46831183398766124,0.2,0.8919135749384519,89.19135749384519,High Trust
Speechless,/users/5dbef174bc30ad137b9020b7,US,3.0,2019-11-03 15:29:26+00:00,2.0,Amazon Delivery a Disaster,"My experience with Amazon has usually been good, with one obvious exception.  When I order something that is shipped and delivered by Amazon, it's always a disaster.  Additionally, their customer service now seems to be non existent.  Getting lost orders replaced is a headache and they'll manage to ship a replacement after you jump through their hoops.  But it will take a week or more for them to ship it.",2019-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,3.0,408,70,26,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,experience amazon usually good one obvious exception order something shipped delivered amazon always disaster additionally customer service seems non existent getting lost order replaced headache theyll manage ship replacement jump hoop take week ship,0.018245001531825285,0.9817549984681747,0.03925967470555244,0.4,1.0987294341751979,109.87294341751979,High Trust
Christine,/users/5dbecaaebc30adea1190117b,US,1.0,2019-11-03 12:40:17+00:00,1.0,I wish I could give no stars,"I wish I could give no stars. I bought the Amazon Kindle fire 7 thinking it was a great value. It's not connected to Google. It's connected to their search engine. Nobody wants their search engine we want Google. The other thing is there's an Alexa built-in. I was kind of excited about that. But again she's not hooked up to Google! So she don't know Jack jackshit! She's only connected to their library or something so every time you ask her something she says ""I don't know the answer to that!"" What is the point of an Alexa who knows nothing? What a piece of junk I would throw it in the trash but now I just use it as an extra device to take notes on like a notebook for $50 what a piece of junk worthless piece of crap. I would have tried to return it but it was past the 30 Days by the time I had a chance to open it and do anything with it. You can't even download regular apps off of this thing! Such a waste of money it's a $50 electronic notebook now! Don't buy this piece of crap! This is Amazon's attempt to monopolize! You lose Google wins! I would never buy another electronic device from you again!",2019-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,3.0,1114,218,28,7,0.0,0,9,2,1,Suspicious,wish could give star bought amazon kindle fire thinking great value connected google connected search engine nobody want search engine want google thing there alexa builtin kind excited shes hooked google dont know jack jackshit shes connected library something every time ask something say dont know answer point alexa know nothing piece junk would throw trash use extra device take note like notebook piece junk worthless piece crap would tried return past day time chance open anything cant even download regular apps thing waste money electronic notebook dont buy piece crap amazon attempt monopolize lose google win would never buy another electronic device,0.9999441015843142,5.589841568576226e-05,0.12226584408300617,0.2,0.3244811180244441,32.448111802444416,Low Trust
John Kuzyk,/users/5d66940083274083a77cc8db,CA,6.0,2019-11-03 00:57:24+00:00,1.0,"Amazon Takes Money, blames everyone else","Amazon.com advertised item, took the money. Then AMAZON removed there name on the the feed back and put it on supplier.  Supplier request I remove my feed back. Then USPS Usless Postal did not deliver item. They claim it was delivered but customer did not receive. USPS classification it was not a letter, billed as package, size determined it as a package. USPS put PKG in a box not delivered to resident. Customer resolved with Postal Carrier. AMAZON did nothing to resolve.",2019-11-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,11.0,3.0,476,82,40,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazoncom advertised item took money amazon removed name feed back put supplier supplier request remove feed back usps usless postal deliver item claim delivered customer receive usps classification letter billed package size determined package usps put pkg box delivered resident customer resolved postal carrier amazon nothing resolve,0.028471790885092094,0.9715282091149079,0.045989904655075714,0.2,0.794962085488469,79.49620854884691,High Trust
