Willis Domingo,/users/5db9b22f7354d7127d81be2d,US,1.0,2019-10-30 15:55:18+00:00,1.0,Amazon's fraudulent practices,"I am an individual who has been selling products on Amazon for over ten years. I order products through a drop ship wholesaler who represents hundreds of manufacturers and over 13,000 products. Our wholesale outlet is one of the most respected in the country and purchases only from verified trademark holders for redistribution. Because of the numbers involved, the manufacturers might not know my name. However, I have an account in good standing with the wholesaler. I list my products on Amazon by means of a data feed directly from the wholesaler. Occasionally a manufacturer/trademark holder may grow concerned about counterfeit products offered on Amazon and submit blanket complaints about every retailer they see on Amazon whose name they do not recognize. This happened to me. When this happens I immediately contact the wholesaler to ask for a letter of verification and an introduction to the manufacturer/trademark holders as proof that I sell products sourced only from the trademark holder - not counterfeits. I also request and receive letters of verification from the manufacturer/trademark holder. At Amazon's request I also submitted invoices from the wholesaler to show that I purchase products from the legitimate source. These letters and invoice are attached as Exhibits to this complaint. Once these documents have been submitted Amazon stopped communicating with me. All I received were automated e-mails stating that I need to submit the documents I already submitted. Using automation Amazon repeats the same complaint and document request over and over ignoring the documentation sent to them. After several automated e-mails, Amazon stopped replying altogether. After several weeks of sending automated e-mails Amazon suspended my account and held the funds for the sales I had already completed. The unpaid balance due to me is $312.68. When I requested the release of the funds, Amazon sent one automated e-mail saying I could expect a response in 7 days. I contacted them again after 14 days and received an automated response saying Amazon will not release the funds, they will not provide the reason and will no longer communicate with me. The customer paid me, not Amazon,for the merchandise I delivered. This money does not belong to Amazon. The maneuver of not transmitting to me the proceeds of my sales does not seem to be even legal. The use of robot e-mail replies on Amazon's part hints to my mind at fraudulent intent.Additional Information: I believe this process of (1) Accusing a seller of wrongdoing (2) Ignoring a seller's defense (3) Holding the seller's balance due presumably for be kept as Amazon's personal business property - this process is a generalized fraudulent scheme. The basis for my belief is the number of complaints by sellers on Amazon who has voiced the same complaint.",2019-10-30 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,30.0,2836,457,29,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,individual selling product amazon ten year order product drop ship wholesaler represents hundred manufacturer product wholesale outlet one respected country purchase verified trademark holder redistribution number involved manufacturer might know name however account good standing wholesaler list product amazon mean data feed directly wholesaler occasionally manufacturertrademark holder may grow concerned counterfeit product offered amazon submit blanket complaint every retailer see amazon whose name recognize happened happens immediately contact wholesaler ask letter verification introduction manufacturertrademark holder proof sell product sourced trademark holder counterfeit also request receive letter verification manufacturertrademark holder amazon request also submitted invoice wholesaler show purchase product legitimate source letter invoice attached exhibit complaint document submitted amazon stopped communicating received automated email stating need submit document already submitted using automation amazon repeat complaint document request ignoring documentation sent several automated email amazon stopped replying altogether several week sending automated email amazon suspended account held fund sale already completed unpaid balance due requested release fund amazon sent one automated email saying could expect response day contacted day received automated response saying amazon release fund provide reason longer communicate customer paid amazonfor merchandise delivered money belong amazon maneuver transmitting proceeds sale seem even legal use robot email reply amazon part hint mind fraudulent intentadditional information believe process accusing seller wrongdoing ignoring seller defense holding seller balance due presumably kept amazon personal business property process generalized fraudulent scheme basis belief number complaint seller amazon voiced complaint,0.011901437445241808,0.9880985625547581,0.25630959057767805,0.2,0.8453111993929147,84.53111993929147,High Trust
