David,/users/5db3793eec398951fe155302,US,1.0,2019-10-25 22:37:52+00:00,1.0,Horrible delivery experience,"Horrible delivery experience.  I kept checking the tracking and when I showed a map where the driver was, less than a mile from us and I was 4th in line, I went and waited in the front room.  I checked again and the tracking said I was next.  I checked again and it said delivery was attempted at 4:51 pm and that I can give permission through the app to leave it somewhere like in the mailbox or in a bush.  Probably because they wanted it to be on me if it got stolen because it is a pricey item.  They are probably doing this to a lot of deliveries so they can cut down on man hours of delivery drivers.  It takes more time to actually take a pricey item to a resident to find that there is no one home.  No one ever came to the door!  It was a pricey item for a birthday tomorrow morning.  I called Amazon to tell them the situation.  I get transferred to this carrier and they tell me he will come back before 9 pm.  I needed to go to bed because I work nights. I called Amazon to keep the item and I will go to Best Buy to purchase it.  Thanks a lot Amazon!  I love how your customer service says “thank you so much for being a Prime member.”  What a bunch of malarky!!!  You lost a 514$ sale Amazon.  No wonder so many people hate you!",2019-10-25 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,25.0,1242,249,28,3,0.0,0,6,2,1,Suspicious,horrible delivery experience kept checking tracking showed map driver less mile u th line went waited front room checked tracking said next checked said delivery attempted pm give permission app leave somewhere like mailbox bush probably wanted got stolen pricey item probably lot delivery cut man hour delivery driver take time actually take pricey item resident find one home one ever came door pricey item birthday tomorrow morning called amazon tell situation get transferred carrier tell come back pm needed go bed work night called amazon keep item go best buy purchase thanks lot amazon love customer service say “thank much prime member” bunch malarky lost sale amazon wonder many people hate,0.9926636567658569,0.007336343234143117,0.13965227145260797,0.2,0.33159862590759315,33.15986259075932,Low Trust
