Meghan,/users/5da7a7ea1f564d16d5872b08,CA,5.0,2019-10-23 00:28:43+00:00,4.0,I like their Customer Service,"Personally, I really enjoy using Amazon.My items ship quickly, and I have gotten used to the rotation of delivery drivers. Some of the delivery drivers are better than others but in general they are all pretty good.If I have ever had an issue with a delivery not being delivered, they have refunded me absolutely no problem. Or, if they were not able to refund they re-sent a product and I received it within a normal amount of time. I really like that I can e-mail the company and get a response back shortly. I do not always like to use the phone to speak to customer service so this option is just a lot easier for me.",2019-10-17 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,23.0,621,117,29,5,6.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,personally really enjoy using amazonmy item ship quickly gotten used rotation delivery driver delivery driver better others general pretty goodif ever issue delivery delivered refunded absolutely problem able refund resent product received within normal amount time really like email company get response back shortly always like use phone speak customer service option lot easier,0.025272378529544365,0.9747276214704557,0.06561974200785194,0.8,1.7004877591367982,170.0487759136798,High Trust
Karin Clements,/users/5da7793e94a12f496ea58204,US,1.0,2019-10-16 20:10:46+00:00,1.0,My Amazon account was hacked,"My Amazon account was hacked.  I contacted Amazon customer service last week to tell them I am unable to get into my account at all. They told me someone changed my password and said they locked the account.    I was told Amazon would get back to me in 1-2 days.  No calls, no emails, nothing from Amazon at all.   I called again on Monday, again I told them I was still locked out of my account AND was unable to make a payment. Was told the account was safe AND again was told someone would get back to me in 1-2 days. Still no response, no email, no calls, nothing.   Since then, someone bought an Apple watch AND used my points to pay for it.  On the phone with Amazon right now, my third call to them and spent over an hour getting the exact same ""someone will get back to you"" story as the last two times and NOTHING has been resolved. Hope whoever hacked my account enjoys stolen goods, thanks to AMAZON!    Good to know the safeguards you put in place keep the account owners out but allow thieves in!  Do yourself a favor, avoid Amazon at ALL COSTS!",2019-10-16 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,16.0,1058,201,28,5,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,amazon account hacked contacted amazon customer service last week tell unable get account told someone changed password said locked account told amazon would get back day call email nothing amazon called monday told still locked account unable make payment told account safe told someone would get back day still response email call nothing since someone bought apple watch used point pay phone amazon right third call spent hour getting exact someone get back story last two time nothing resolved hope whoever hacked account enjoys stolen good thanks amazon good know safeguard put place keep account owner allow thief favor avoid amazon cost,0.663689710867607,0.336310289132393,0.11273135165451487,0.2,0.49070141489709945,49.07014148970995,Low Trust
Belle Morte,/users/5da74da48455a37b60c2e710,US,3.0,2019-10-16 17:04:46+00:00,1.0,Delivery Caused Injury,"On October 9, 2019, Order# 111-2361737-4892233 was marked as out for delivery with the estimate showing before 9PM. Typically the drivers will knock or ring the doorbell to notify me that the packages have been delivered and will put it to the side of the door or on the chair next to my front door. NOTE: I have a storm door and external front door. The storm door has a solid bottom, meaning I have ZERO visibility of my front step and since the door swings outward, you have to step out to get it to swing fully outward and exit the home.  However, I hadn't received any knock, doorbell ring, text, or any other notification that the package was delivered, so when I went to step outside of my home around 8PM that evening, my foot ended up right inside of the package which caused me to fall, twisting both legs and causing two sprained ankles, strained knees and hips, and contusions to my knee and ankle. I struggled to get up, but was able to do so with the help of my daughter who came running when she heard the fall. After she got me inside and I was able to get things cleaned up and while waiting for my friend to bring larger bandages so I wouldn't bleed all over my home, and for my daughter's Grandmother to come to my home to take me to the ER since I couldn't put ANY weight on my left foot, I decided to call Amazon customer support to report what had happened. The agent on the other line was apologetic, and advised that she would get in contact with the shipping team, and began asking me questions such as if I felt the driver did it on purpose. I told her I don't think they did it maliciously, but, their negligence in not notifying me that the package was there, and putting it directly up against the step/in front of my door caused injury. I was asked to send in photos so I sent in pictures of the injury, videos of the fall and the delivery driver showing he just dropped the package and walked away taken by my security camera, and photos of my ER visit. I have been asking people repeatedly about what they plan on doing about this situation since I shouldn't be out hundreds, potentially thousands of dollars for an ER visit because one of your drivers didn't do their due diligence to notify the customer of the delivery. I have received nothing but half-hearted sympathetic emails in response with zero action save for the slap in the face refund for the $30.00 package whose contents were miraculously okay, and I didn't ask for a refund on.. Because that $30.00 order is going to cost me much more than that due to medical bills even after insurance coverage, and weeks, if not months of healing since sprains take a long time to heal. As a single mom, I sincerely doubt I can afford a legal team to combat Amazon and their customer service agents into covering medical costs that are destroying my budget, but, I feel that it was necessary to make sure people know just how far Amazon has fallen in relation to their delivery and customer services. I made one last ditch effort to try to see how we can make this right, because I do not feel it is fair that I have to suffer the burden of medical bills caused by no fault of my own, but their corporate team hasn't responded back. It has been a week now and I have received zero positive resolution.",2019-10-16 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,16.0,3286,615,22,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,october order marked delivery estimate showing pm typically driver knock ring doorbell notify package delivered put side door chair next front door note storm door external front door storm door solid bottom meaning zero visibility front step since door swing outward step get swing fully outward exit home however hadnt received knock doorbell ring text notification package delivered went step outside home around pm evening foot ended right inside package caused fall twisting leg causing two sprained ankle strained knee hip contusion knee ankle struggled get able help daughter came running heard fall got inside able get thing cleaned waiting friend bring larger bandage wouldnt bleed home daughter grandmother come home take er since couldnt put weight left foot decided call amazon customer support report happened agent line apologetic advised would get contact shipping team began asking question felt driver purpose told dont think maliciously negligence notifying package putting directly stepin front door caused injury asked send photo sent picture injury video fall delivery driver showing dropped package walked away taken security camera photo er visit asking people repeatedly plan situation since shouldnt hundred potentially thousand dollar er visit one driver didnt due diligence notify customer delivery received nothing halfhearted sympathetic email response zero action save slap face refund package whose content miraculously okay didnt ask refund order going cost much due medical bill even insurance coverage week month healing since sprain take long time heal single mom sincerely doubt afford legal team combat amazon customer service agent covering medical cost destroying budget feel necessary make sure people know far amazon fallen relation delivery customer service made one last ditch effort try see make right feel fair suffer burden medical bill caused fault corporate team hasnt responded back week received zero positive resolution,0.007268200579181783,0.9927317994208182,0.34492428491306787,0.2,0.8653507566930226,86.53507566930226,High Trust
Extremerecluse Fallows,/users/5da72ea91f564d312786ea4a,US,2.0,2019-10-16 14:52:34+00:00,1.0,Since Amazon has instituted in-house…,"Since Amazon has instituted in-house shipping, things have continually declined. I recently enrolled in Prime. I ordered an air tool. It has been a week since I placed my order. I spoke to customer service and they admitted they had no clue. In the old shipping system, a customer could go online, click on the shipping number and instantly know where there items were. Now, all you see is ordered, shipped and arrived. This tells the customer nothing. That is why customer service had no clue. Once the order leaves the warehouse, their is no way to accurately track it's progress.",2019-10-16 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,16.0,582,101,37,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,since amazon instituted inhouse shipping thing continually declined recently enrolled prime ordered air tool week since placed order spoke customer service admitted clue old shipping system customer could go online click shipping number instantly know item see ordered shipped arrived tell customer nothing customer service clue order leaf warehouse way accurately track progress,0.019257492575916895,0.9807425074240831,0.056646102075154234,0.2,0.8017004741270723,80.17004741270723,High Trust
