Shelby Roberson,/users/5d9d35c369ec705fe6fd47f0,US,1.0,2019-10-09 01:20:38+00:00,1.0,Amazon has gone downhill fast,"Amazon has gone downhill fast.  We have prime and pay a lot for it.  When we ordered we will have a delivery date, but you can’t go with that. All we can do is sit and wait to see if it shows up on time.   We are currently waiting on a item we purchased for my parents which was supposed to have been delivered on October 7th.  We checked to see the status to see if was delayed, it could be delivered either the 8th or 9th is October.  So we checked again today and it showed they tried to deliver it at 3:17 a m this morning (oct 8th).  Yes, it shows 3:17 am, they said they attempted to deliver and will have try again.  At this point I’m upset with amazon (this is not the only time this as happened).  I called today to get told “ sorry all we can at is they can’t find a driver to deliver it and it will be delivered as soon as they can). I lost it at his point and told them this is not acceptable.    I finally got to a supervisor who said she was sending a message to find out what was going on. She said we would hear something within 2 hours.  Well it’s been 5 hours and again nothing from amazon. No phone call, no message or package.    Buyer beware just because you have prime and pay a lot for it don’t mean you will receive your packages as they state when you purchase it.",2019-10-09 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,9.0,1289,259,29,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon gone downhill fast prime pay lot ordered delivery date can’t go sit wait see show time currently waiting item purchased parent supposed delivered october th checked see status see delayed could delivered either th th october checked today showed tried deliver morning oct th yes show said attempted deliver try point i’m upset amazon time happened called today get told “ sorry can’t find driver deliver delivered soon lost point told acceptable finally got supervisor said sending message find going said would hear something within hour well it’s hour nothing amazon phone call message package buyer beware prime pay lot don’t mean receive package state purchase,0.012239653145921537,0.9877603468540784,0.14526079641054404,0.2,0.822932332709148,82.2932332709148,High Trust
Dr H,/users/5cd489bc763a2b490c310c8f,US,8.0,2019-10-08 22:10:51+00:00,1.0,"From ""great"" to ""in the toilet"" in three months.","The most impressive thing about Amazon.com used to be its unparalleled customer service.  That's the key thing that has kept me a member for 15 years and a Prime member for the last several years.I'm not sure what changed, or why it changed, but since August 2019 that customer service has taken a nose-dive right into the toilet.In 15 years I've only had a handful of Amazon purchases go awry, and in every case I was able to shoot an email to customer service, and within 72 hours Amazon had made good, either by issuing a refund or over-nighting a replacement order at no extra charge.Apparently those days are gone.  Beginning this past summer the email contact option went away.  Also, you can no longer call Amazon directly about an order issue.  The only form of contacts left are on-line ""chat"", or you can leave them a message and ask THEM to call YOU, at their convenience.Right off the bat this is Amazon telling us that THEIR time is more valuable than OUR time.With email, I could make a report, and check for replies at my convenience.  With ""chat"" I have to sit by the computer and interact with an Amazon chat person, sometimes for half an hour or more.  In the past 3 months my experience has been that the person you chat with is never able to help you with your issue, without ""escalating"" your case 2 or 3 times, meaning you get shuffled from one chat-person to the next several times in every chat -- and you get to retell your story 3 or 4 times.Did I mention that before you even get to a chat \person\, you first have to play 20 questions with the chat 'bot?The phone situation is even more ridiculous.   You used to be able to dial an actual customer service rep.  Now you call in a request for them to call you back -- and they return your call, once again, at THEIR convenience, not yours.Even all this might be tolerable had Amazon maintained the same level of service they used to have.  Unfortunately, that also seems to be gone with the wind.Recently I ordered a dozen items in a single order which, for reasons best known to Amazon, was split into two shipments.  One was sent by UPS, and arrived 2 days later without incident.  The other was shipped by USPS and never arrived.  On the third day I contacted Amazon ""chat"" about the missing shipment and was told that it had ""been delivered on Wednesday (the day before).  It hadn't.Amazon chat advised me to wait another day, and then contact them again if the shipment still hadn't arrived.  I waited; it didn't, and I contacted Amazon again.At this point, as recently as last July, customer service would have offered me my choice of a replacement shipment or a refund.This time, I was told to ""wait three business days, and contact us again if the shipment doesn't arrive.""I waited three more days; the shipment didn't arrive.  I checked with USPS and they told me they had left the shipment ""in your garage"".  I don't have a garage.  I checked with neighbors up and down the street; none of them had seen the shipment.So, I contacted Amazon chat again.  I was told that I needed to wait three more business days and contact them again.  I did this, and by this point I had waited 10 days for a ""2-day shipping"" Prime order, which still had not arrived.Since there had been dated birthday items in the shipment, I told Amazon I no longer needed the items, and requested a refund.They told that I -I- needed to initiate an investigation with the USPS, before they could issue a refund.  Excuse me?  -I- was not the shipper of those items; Amazon was the shipper.  Seems like THEY were the one's who should have initiated the investigation.So I said, ""fine I'll initiate the investigation, and if you can't issue a refund until that's complete, then please send me a replacement order.""I was told they couldn't issue a refund OR a replacement until the results of the investigation were complete.  If you have ever had to have the Post Office investigate a package that you mailed which got lost in the mail, you know such an investigation can take anywhere from several weeks to several months.Everyone of these ""chat"" sessions lasted a half-hour or longer, and involved at least 4 different Amazon reps.Meanwhile, the bottom line is, I ordered and PAID FOR $200 worth of goods from Amazon which they failed to deliver, and they will not make good on this order until -I- have the Post Office investigate what had to be either Amazon's or the Post Office's screw-up.If someone makes a shipment which doesn't arrive, it is almost always considered the responsibility of the SHIPPER to investigate and make good on the shipment.  Virtually every other on-line seller I use follows this protocol; Amazon used to, as well -- up to this past August.Now it appears their customer service policy is, ""we'll take your money, and screw you.""Very disappointing.",2019-10-08 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,8.0,4835,855,48,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,impressive thing amazoncom used unparalleled customer service thats key thing kept member year prime member last several yearsim sure changed changed since august customer service taken nosedive right toiletin year ive handful amazon purchase go awry every case able shoot email customer service within hour amazon made good either issuing refund overnighting replacement order extra chargeapparently day gone beginning past summer email contact option went away also longer call amazon directly order issue form contact left online chat leave message ask call convenienceright bat amazon telling u time valuable timewith email could make report check reply convenience chat sit computer interact amazon chat person sometimes half hour past month experience person chat never able help issue without escalating case time meaning get shuffled one chatperson next several time every chat get retell story timesdid mention even get chat person first play question chat botthe phone situation even ridiculous used able dial actual customer service rep call request call back return call convenience yourseven might tolerable amazon maintained level service used unfortunately also seems gone windrecently ordered dozen item single order reason best known amazon split two shipment one sent ups arrived day later without incident shipped usps never arrived third day contacted amazon chat missing shipment told delivered wednesday day hadntamazon chat advised wait another day contact shipment still hadnt arrived waited didnt contacted amazon againat point recently last july customer service would offered choice replacement shipment refundthis time told wait three business day contact u shipment doesnt arrivei waited three day shipment didnt arrive checked usps told left shipment garage dont garage checked neighbor street none seen shipmentso contacted amazon chat told needed wait three business day contact point waited day day shipping prime order still arrivedsince dated birthday item shipment told amazon longer needed item requested refundthey told needed initiate investigation usps could issue refund excuse shipper item amazon shipper seems like one initiated investigationso said fine ill initiate investigation cant issue refund thats complete please send replacement orderi told couldnt issue refund replacement result investigation complete ever post office investigate package mailed got lost mail know investigation take anywhere several week several monthseveryone chat session lasted halfhour longer involved least different amazon repsmeanwhile bottom line ordered paid worth good amazon failed deliver make good order post office investigate either amazon post office screwupif someone make shipment doesnt arrive almost always considered responsibility shipper investigate make good shipment virtually every online seller use follows protocol amazon used well past augustnow appears customer service policy well take money screw youvery disappointing,0.002059059095510022,0.9979409409044899,0.4795288839035334,0.2,0.8948762472329516,89.48762472329516,High Trust
Maree Rexroad,/users/5d9ceae8d5e7685398271c40,US,1.0,2019-10-08 20:00:49+00:00,1.0,I used to love Amazon,"I used to love Amazon.  Not anymore.  The products are dollar store quality.  Pay the extra money at another website and get what you're paying for.  Review after review after review are from people getting the bate and switch.  Isn't bate and switch illegal?  Why does Amazon get away with it?  The picture shows one product and what the customer receives is another product.  I used to buy manufacturers that I know have a reputation, but those products are now not cost effective through Amazon.  Again, you can get a better prices at other websites.  About the only thing I buy from Amazon anymore are books, Amazon can't bait and switch a book too badly.",2019-10-08 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,10.0,8.0,659,115,21,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,used love amazon anymore product dollar store quality pay extra money another website get youre paying review review review people getting bate switch isnt bate switch illegal amazon get away picture show one product customer receives another product used buy manufacturer know reputation product cost effective amazon get better price website thing buy amazon anymore book amazon cant bait switch book badly,0.020952093120754814,0.9790479068792451,0.06449803701626472,0.2,0.8024235608428755,80.24235608428755,High Trust
