Cindy W.,/users/5b3ba3a04de5666d341b29c5,US,7.0,2021-05-27 18:12:28+00:00,1.0,"Yep, Amazon says YOU are responsible for the actions of the people they employ.","Just got off the phone with Amazon. If you ever follow their instructions to cancel a shipment that has been shipped via Amazon Logistics, don't. If they always ship to you via their Amazon Logistics, think about it seriously. If the courier marks the package as ""refused"" and doesn't return it to an Amazon facility, Amazon will try to refuse the refund if one of their ""top notch"" couriers decides you don't need the item but they do. According to Amazon Customer Service, I am responsible for THEIR courier. I don't remember that job interview..",2019-09-28 00:00:00+00:00,2021.0,5.0,27.0,548,95,79,14,607.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,got phone amazon ever follow instruction cancel shipment shipped via amazon logistics dont always ship via amazon logistics think seriously courier mark package refused doesnt return amazon facility amazon try refuse refund one top notch courier decides dont need item according amazon customer service responsible courier dont remember job interview,9.971545466013815e-06,0.999990028454534,0.0532809871003926,0.2,0.8106512116473454,81.06512116473455,High Trust
