KareBear,/users/5d8eed26ee6821352667261e,US,1.0,2019-09-28 05:18:33+00:00,3.0,"Two-day shipping, really?","At first, I really loved using Amazon.  Their two-day delivery was spot on, and I could order anything and trust the product.  Now, it feels like I’m always trying to check with myself as to why I’m paying this membership!  Two-day delivery is bs.  I’ve had several two-day delivery packages be delayed.  One was a birthday present for my 6 year old nephew.  We postponed leaving until the next morning because Amazon said the delivery would be there in two days.  Right at the 9pm end of day delivery mark, Amazon sends a shipment delay note saying it may not be for another 5 days.  The tracking showed it was in my city.  Why would that take 5 days?!  Im beginning to wonder what I pay this membership for.  The two day shipping has gone to the wayside, and I’m beginning to not believe in Amazon’s promise any more...or the quality of the products sold.  Don’t say you can do something if you can’t.  False advertising, Amazon.  Maybe I should take my membership to Walmart, Amazon.  What do you think about that?  I’m not a fan, but they seem to be getting themselves squared away to be completion.",2019-09-28 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,28.0,1103,198,25,3,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,first really loved using amazon twoday delivery spot could order anything trust product feel like i’m always trying check i’m paying membership twoday delivery b i’ve several twoday delivery package delayed one birthday present year old nephew postponed leaving next morning amazon said delivery would two day right pm end day delivery mark amazon sends shipment delay note saying may another day tracking showed city would take day im beginning wonder pay membership two day shipping gone wayside i’m beginning believe amazon’s promise moreor quality product sold don’t say something can’t false advertising amazon maybe take membership walmart amazon think i’m fan seem getting squared away completion,0.22379343529370246,0.7762065647062976,0.11104879416713405,0.6,1.3103130411865755,131.03130411865754,High Trust
Dhill7,/users/5d8eaeb2e15f9ce5c7f88d73,US,1.0,2019-09-28 00:52:05+00:00,1.0,Bring back delivery drivers who care,"Fed up.  Amazon, please bring back delivery drivers who actually care about honoring your “guaranteed” delivery dates.  Since your “guaranteed” delivery dates have failed miserably for the past month, it gives me no reason to keep paying monthly for a prime membership.",2019-09-28 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,28.0,269,42,36,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,fed amazon please bring back delivery driver actually care honoring “guaranteed” delivery date since “guaranteed” delivery date failed miserably past month give reason keep paying monthly prime membership,0.04329662369346238,0.9567033763065376,0.023555804823331465,0.2,0.7830628491179351,78.30628491179351,High Trust
Jing Chan,/users/5d8e716de15f9c71b6f87d67,US,1.0,2019-09-27 20:32:10+00:00,1.0,Ban Customer Reviews BUT Allow Vendors to Getaway with Bait-N-Switch,"So I'll start off by saying that while I am an Amazon prime member, I was deemed not a great customer in their eyes.  I was prohibited from leaving reviews on their website or even asking questions about products since 2017.  There was no communication from them explaining what happened.  Roughly estimating about 3-5% of my 300+ reviews were free products.  Regardless, I don't hold a grudge even though that was before Amazon changed their policy.  I didn't even bother emailing or pleading the case because Amazon had 100% right to what they did.  I was just glad that Amazon allowed me the privilege of continuing as a customer.Fast forward to Sept 2019, I'm looking for a screen protector for a new Samsung Galaxy S10. I found a lot of screen protector with over 100+ reviews and 4-5 stars.  I was really happy with so much choice.  But when I started to read the reviews, I noticed that most reviews weren't for screen protectors.  It was often things that were highly non-related (i.e. reviews for  christmas tree lighting, wrist bands, belt buckles, batteries etc).  The item ""AILIBOTE Glass Screen Protector for Samsung Galaxy S10"" had over 7,700+ reviews at an average of 4+ stars.  ONLY 67 was related to the Galaxy S10 screen protector.  This doesn't equate to even 1% of the reviews.There are many other examples like I listed above.  I ended up spending over 3 hours sifting through the different reviews to find a screen protector that was accurately reviewed and still deemed a viable product to purchase.  My complaint and why I'm leaving a one-star review for Amazon.com is that they rely only on an algorithm to ban a 9+ year customer from leaving reviews.  But when it comes to the bad vendors, Amazon.com continuously allows them to get away with anything.  Even selling products that are non-related to the 4+ star reviews and essentially cheating the unsuspecting customers.  I hope something can be done to fix this.",2019-09-27 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,27.0,1941,331,68,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ill start saying amazon prime member deemed great customer eye prohibited leaving review website even asking question product since communication explaining happened roughly estimating review free product regardless dont hold grudge even though amazon changed policy didnt even bother emailing pleading case amazon right glad amazon allowed privilege continuing customerfast forward sept im looking screen protector new samsung galaxy found lot screen protector review star really happy much choice started read review noticed review werent screen protector often thing highly nonrelated ie review christmas tree lighting wrist band belt buckle battery etc item ailibote glass screen protector samsung galaxy review average star related galaxy screen protector doesnt equate even reviewsthere many example like listed ended spending hour sifting different review find screen protector accurately reviewed still deemed viable product purchase complaint im leaving onestar review amazoncom rely algorithm ban year customer leaving review come bad vendor amazoncom continuously allows get away anything even selling product nonrelated star review essentially cheating unsuspecting customer hope something done fix,0.010152556571427449,0.9898474434285726,0.1856421761076837,0.2,0.832052156935823,83.2052156935823,High Trust
