consumer advocate,/users/5d88f0c022d2dc68712b5af1,US,1.0,2019-09-23 16:20:18+00:00,1.0,I would give Amazon zero stars if I…,"I would give Amazon zero stars if I could. In my opinion, based on personal experience and review of articles and publications, their customer service and ethics are appalling. How about these examples. Your package shows delivered but you didn't receive it ... Amazon tells you to ask your neighbors and any family members living at other addresses to see if they received your package ... You ordered and paid for an item, at a discounted price, and have not received it ... Amazon tells you that it was mistakenly sent to the wrong Amazon Hub and is no longer available, you need to cancel and reorder the item at the regular price; Your ordered and paid for an item and never received it ... Amazon states that your physical address of many years, at which you have received many deliveries as well as receive mail, doesn't exist; Ethically ... Amazon's pricing algorithm also steers customers to Amazon's own products, even if they are higher priced, and Amazon promotes its own products in merchant listings. While this might be best for Amazon, is it ethical to steer your customers toward paying more for the same thing? I could go on and on but there is no point. Since I have stopped buying from Amazon I have found better prices, along with much better service from virtually everyone else I have purchased from. While I never-say-never, I will say that it is very unlikely I will purchase anything from Amazon in the future ... I WOULD STRONGLY RECOMMEND THAT YOU CONSIDER LOOKING AT OTHER RETAILERS, BOTH ONLINE AND RETAIL, AS YOU ARE LIKELY TO RECEIVE A BETTER PRICE AND MUCH BETTER SERVICE.  Keep in mind that Amazon adds ""zero value"" to anything you purchase. Think about it ... perhaps, it is for this reason that their profits are so high. To make matters even worse, if you have their ""Prime"" service, as I did, you pay Amazon an ""annual fee"" for higher prices on many items and very poor customer service. Just my opinion for your consideration.",2019-09-23 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,23.0,1965,346,36,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,would give amazon zero star could opinion based personal experience review article publication customer service ethic appalling example package show delivered didnt receive amazon tell ask neighbor family member living address see received package ordered paid item discounted price received amazon tell mistakenly sent wrong amazon hub longer available need cancel reorder item regular price ordered paid item never received amazon state physical address many year received many delivery well receive mail doesnt exist ethically amazon pricing algorithm also steer customer amazon product even higher priced amazon promotes product merchant listing might best amazon ethical steer customer toward paying thing could go point since stopped buying amazon found better price along much better service virtually everyone else purchased neversaynever say unlikely purchase anything amazon future would strongly recommend consider looking retailer online retail likely receive better price much better service keep mind amazon add zero value anything purchase think perhaps reason profit high make matter even worse prime service pay amazon annual fee higher price many item poor customer service opinion consideration,0.0160674532940947,0.9839325467059054,0.19405496354458776,0.2,0.8307772660618702,83.07772660618701,High Trust
