Edd,/users/5d0900c2e3812383bc381cb1,US,4.0,2019-09-18 16:39:59+00:00,2.0,Amazon Is Not What It Used To Be,"Amazon is one misstep from losing me as a long-time Prime customer. Once they moved to their contracted courier services (and fired FedEx and UPS) it has been nothing but issues regarding delivery, for which Amazon refuses to take responsibility (even though checkout literally 'Guarantees' delivery on a certain date).Packages will be mishandled, delayed for no reason, lost a lot more often than they used to be, or will supposedly be delivered without actually being delivered. And you quickly realize there's no actual guarantee from Amazon. Unless you initiate contact with them for an undelivered/unreceived package, you won't get a refund. Nor are they willing to offer anything to back-up the guarantee, such as an account credit, without the customer asking. And even then, it's $5, which is nothing especially if a large item is ordered.And try contacting Customer Service. You might as well be talking to a wall. They don't care. They all read off the same script and will keep you in ridiculous loop just so you get frustrated and quit your battle. They don't WANT the customer to be happy...they just want them to be frustrated enough to stop bothering them.The company just doesn't care about customers anymore. They are massive and their income in almost guaranteed, aside from millions deciding to boycott them. This will just get worse over time, and I think the company is going to be in trouble this holiday season. People just need to start taking stands against the company and start shopping elsewhere.",2019-09-18 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,18.0,1524,252,32,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon one misstep losing longtime prime customer moved contracted courier service fired fedex ups nothing issue regarding delivery amazon refuse take responsibility even though checkout literally guarantee delivery certain datepackages mishandled delayed reason lost lot often used supposedly delivered without actually delivered quickly realize there actual guarantee amazon unless initiate contact undeliveredunreceived package wont get refund willing offer anything backup guarantee account credit without customer asking even nothing especially large item orderedand try contacting customer service might well talking wall dont care read script keep ridiculous loop get frustrated quit battle dont want customer happythey want frustrated enough stop bothering themthe company doesnt care customer anymore massive income almost guaranteed aside million deciding boycott get worse time think company going trouble holiday season people need start taking stand company start shopping elsewhere,0.010376121949928261,0.9896238780500718,0.14133482893998878,0.4,1.1230789048130336,112.30789048130336,High Trust
