Marcass Carcass,/users/5466181c00006400019689fd,US,10.0,2019-09-11 10:12:04+00:00,1.0,Amazon.com is running a bait and switch false advertisement scam for Prime terrorists.,"Amazon.com is running a bait and switch false advertisement scam...  The ad said that shipping was free, no not free if I sign up for Prime, or free if I spend more than $25, I mean, actually free shipping, but when I got to check out it tried to charge me for shipping.  I then noticed that I needed to select free shipping, no, not free shipping if I sign up for Prime, actual free shipping, but no, they signed me up for Prime and made me have to stick with it after I tried contacting them to dispute the matter. The chat person was named Muhammad, on 9/11, can't help but feel as if I've been hacked through the Amazon.com website.  I knew I should've stayed away from this website, always hated it, but my family insisted on using it.",2019-09-11 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,11.0,740,141,86,13,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazoncom running bait switch false advertisement scam ad said shipping free free sign prime free spend mean actually free shipping got check tried charge shipping noticed needed select free shipping free shipping sign prime actual free shipping signed prime made stick tried contacting dispute matter chat person named muhammad cant help feel ive hacked amazoncom website knew shouldve stayed away website always hated family insisted using,0.027542104433626837,0.9724578955663732,0.07908020190689849,0.2,0.8020449881645663,80.20449881645662,High Trust
