PurpleBean,/users/4e7a581000006400010c56c1,GB,7.0,2019-09-06 12:24:19+00:00,1.0,Amazon processes fundamentally flawed,"I posted the following review following the supply of a box set of Avengers DVDs.  The review was declined by Amazon so I am posting it here:The product is probably great - I bought it as a present for someone. What really got me annoyed, though, is the Amazon process. The product was advertised on the web site at £24.99. When the pre-order acknowledgement came through it showed £25. Not a huge difference, I know, but, on principle, the price advertised should be the price charged. Had a web chat and was assured that the correct price would be charged when the product was despatched. When the product was despatched I was charged £25 and so had to get back in touch again. The customer service team offered me compensation but, in a sense, that’s not the point. I suspect (possibly incorrect) that this has arisen because of rounding on VAT. There are two principles here - firstly charge the customer what you promised and then pay over the correct amount of VAT (to be compliant). The net is your income. If Amazon can get away with this enough times then that’s a significant amount of money. It is fundamentally (on principle) wrong to overcharge your customer, however much that may be.",2019-09-06 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,6.0,1198,212,37,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,posted following review following supply box set avenger dvd review declined amazon posting herethe product probably great bought present someone really got annoyed though amazon process product advertised web site £ preorder acknowledgement came showed £ huge difference know principle price advertised price charged web chat assured correct price would charged product despatched product despatched charged £ get back touch customer service team offered compensation sense that’s point suspect possibly incorrect arisen rounding vat two principle firstly charge customer promised pay correct amount vat compliant net income amazon get away enough time that’s significant amount money fundamentally principle wrong overcharge customer however much may,0.06651973080869325,0.9334802691913068,0.11890072910824454,0.2,0.7905202804173023,79.05202804173022,High Trust
Christian,/users/5cbc77b6710f030e91e56e53,US,2.0,2019-09-06 12:00:57+00:00,1.0,Lately I'm really disappointed with Amazon.,"Lately I'm really disappointed with Amazon,, I have a membership and before I had never had any problems with my deliveries, my deliveries  were always on time,, lately there have been a lot of delays/ and reschedules with my deliveries and I am seriously considering to cancelled my membership. Before most of my deliveries were Ups or the USPS now they been using lasership and Amazon and I always have a problem or delay/Reschedule with my deliveries. Really hope I ain't the only one going thru this. Soon I will be cancelling my membership. 👎🏽",2019-09-06 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,6.0,548,95,43,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,lately im really disappointed amazon membership never problem delivery delivery always time lately lot delay reschedules delivery seriously considering cancelled membership delivery ups usps using lasership amazon always problem delayreschedule delivery really hope aint one going thru soon cancelling membership 👎🏽,0.00861489313064243,0.9913851068693575,0.0532809871003926,0.2,0.8063487508547573,80.63487508547573,High Trust
