Christopher Aslett,/users/57ab1d250000ff000a398374,GB,9.0,2019-09-01 13:33:24+00:00,1.0,Oxymoronic A to Z Guarantee,"If you purchase something from Amazon, you are guaranteed to get reasonable service and the law will be adhered to. Challenges arise when you have purchase something from an independent seller on Amazon. Then you are at the mercy of their A to Z guarantee which only protects the customer when the seller fails to respond. Effectively, the seller could respond to all correspondence for the next ten years and they will be able to keep your item and your money. Also, the A to Z team appear unable to read any correspondence between you and the seller and they will ask you to provide information that is already there. They will then ignore the messages you send them and close the case without issuing a refund. I have had many instances when this has occurred. My recent confirmation of their ineptitude is not an isolated incident. Avoid using Amazon if you want great service and require protection. Additionally, most items on Amazon are more expensive than elsewhere.",2019-09-01 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,1.0,974,168,27,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,purchase something amazon guaranteed get reasonable service law adhered challenge arise purchase something independent seller amazon mercy z guarantee protects customer seller fails respond effectively seller could respond correspondence next ten year able keep item money also z team appear unable read correspondence seller ask provide information already ignore message send close case without issuing refund many instance occurred recent confirmation ineptitude isolated incident avoid using amazon want great service require protection additionally item amazon expensive elsewhere,0.012552529802902841,0.9874474701970971,0.09422321929332586,0.2,0.8125683789572137,81.25683789572136,High Trust
