Mr P Evans,/users/52c99f0a00006400015d0120,GB,40.0,2019-09-01 08:31:41+00:00,1.0,Ok unless your item breaks after 1 month 😡,"My wife bought a really expensive toothbrush on Amazon.com as not available in the UK. (£350 + £75 import and postage).Yes I can tell her big waste of money 6 months in the brush has stopped working but Amazon don't comply to the sale of goods act, they are not a shop you can take your product back if faulty, I am now having to go direct to the manufacturer in South Korea, who incidentally is not responding to emails to try and get it repaired or replaced. Amazon therefore is a multibillion $ waste of time if you are let down by the product. After also seeing first hand how they treat their factory workers I will be thinking twice about convenience verses the bitter taste of disappointment and moral concerns.",2019-09-01 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,9.0,1.0,718,132,42,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,wife bought really expensive toothbrush amazoncom available uk £ £ import postageyes tell big waste money month brush stopped working amazon dont comply sale good act shop take product back faulty go direct manufacturer south korea incidentally responding email try get repaired replaced amazon therefore multibillion waste time let product also seeing first hand treat factory worker thinking twice convenience verse bitter taste disappointment moral concern,0.03370139172601038,0.9662986082739896,0.07403252944475602,0.2,0.797955810025946,79.7955810025946,High Trust
