Nicole Doe,/users/56e4302a0000ff000a0e2033,DK,9.0,2019-08-09 16:12:14+00:00,1.0,Stealing my intellectual property/ unwillingness to cooperate,"My royalties are theirs now?Two weeks ago for some reason I got locked out of my account and it asks me for an old phone number.Mail works, my address was given in total to 8 agents who verified me, send me a password link ( although I told them THAT was not the problem), resetted the password and then ...it asks me for a very old phone number.Two weeks of mails, phone calls and suggestion to ""make a new account"".I have written two books associated with that account. The account changing department asked me for the numbers of an old credit card I had on it and ofc I couldnt remember so I asked them to please send me a mail or search for my books, then you can see I am who I say I am.The woman on the other end, refused. Then she refused to transfer the call to her supervisor, in order to make that decision she could not make. Then she refused to regenerate a different question in the system, or call me back and told me to go to retail.Meanwhile, my royalties and books are mine and amazon is illegally keeping them from me, when they could easily check and verify my info, with just a bit of good faith.Shame on amazon, shame on that woman.",2019-08-09 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,8.0,9.0,1153,221,61,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,royalty nowtwo week ago reason got locked account asks old phone numbermail work address given total agent verified send password link although told problem resetted password asks old phone numbertwo week mail phone call suggestion make new accounti written two book associated account account changing department asked number old credit card ofc couldnt remember asked please send mail search book see say amthe woman end refused refused transfer call supervisor order make decision could make refused regenerate different question system call back told go retailmeanwhile royalty book mine amazon illegally keeping could easily check verify info bit good faithshame amazon shame woman,0.01023073645654812,0.9897692635434518,0.12394840157038699,0.2,0.8196743120858033,81.96743120858034,High Trust
David J Hammond,/users/5d4d7de815bfc7380d05dca6,US,1.0,2019-08-09 14:08:14+00:00,1.0,Things happen for a reason,"I'm happy dealing with Amazon as a customer, but not as someone who's applied to work for amazon. Watching videos on YouTube I heard nothing but bad things working with Amazon. Despite those negative reviews I just looked at it as a opportunity. Anyway make long story short my drug test was screwed up I made arrangements to take another one, gave up six hours of my day, and since I just been getting the run around. Well todays the deadline. I don't even work for them and I'm having problems, I can only imagine the problems I would have if I do work for them. But I'm done with trying to get a job with them, things work out for the better and this is a sign that this probably isn't the job for me. Anyway it's time to let go and move on.",2019-08-09 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,8.0,9.0,744,145,26,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,im happy dealing amazon customer someone who applied work amazon watching video youtube heard nothing bad thing working amazon despite negative review looked opportunity anyway make long story short drug test screwed made arrangement take another one gave six hour day since getting run around well today deadline dont even work im problem imagine problem would work im done trying get job thing work better sign probably isnt job anyway time let go move,0.019614465049708252,0.9803855349502918,0.08132361189007291,0.2,0.8064574898531605,80.64574898531605,High Trust
