Ms. Overall,/users/5b108d404de5666d344f935b,US,6.0,2019-08-05 15:18:02+00:00,1.0,Horrible Shipping,"I have constantly had horrible shipping and delivery issues with Amazon. When reaching out to customer service there is no accountability. You cannot review their shipping and delivery because Amazon will refuse to post the review as they do not want to be called out on their terrible failure to meet their own set 2-day turnaround service. I pay for prime membership and I notice if I have something set to deliver on a Sunday, it rarely comes. I have had my address marked as, ""Business Closed"" even though it is a house because USPS did not want to deliver. ONTRAC has delivered items to the wrong address, after hours, the next day (after the date scheduled for delivery) or not at all, and Amazon will tell me to reach out to them. Amazon is the one that chose the shipping company, not I, they need to reach out. Amazon has gotten progressively worse over the years and meeting the 2-day commitment that Prime members pay for does not seem to be something they can adhere to. They breach that contract frequently and I see a class action lawsuit looming in their future.",2019-08-05 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,8.0,5.0,1077,193,17,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,constantly horrible shipping delivery issue amazon reaching customer service accountability cannot review shipping delivery amazon refuse post review want called terrible failure meet set day turnaround service pay prime membership notice something set deliver sunday rarely come address marked business closed even though house usps want deliver ontrac delivered item wrong address hour next day date scheduled delivery amazon tell reach amazon one chose shipping company need reach amazon gotten progressively worse year meeting day commitment prime member pay seem something adhere breach contract frequently see class action lawsuit looming future,0.019624217818997258,0.9803757821810027,0.10824453168816602,0.2,0.8118367974281345,81.18367974281345,High Trust
Tori Medina,/users/5d4752ba80a67209192286d2,US,1.0,2019-08-04 21:48:45+00:00,1.0,Shipping issues,"I have used amazon for years and have generally had reliable service however, the last year I have had multiple hiccups with the delivery of my items. One item was sent to a walmart distribution center in a different city- still not sure how fedex messed that up. About 2 weeks ago I ordered a product that I order pretty frequently (every other month or so) but the packaging was terrible and the lid on one of the items cracked and product was seeping out. I sent amazon a review (with photos) of the issue and they wouldn't acknowledge their fault and told me I needed to return the leaky product via mail.. pretty sure usps wont accept liquids that are not contained.Today, I was supposed to receive 4 orders of the same item, all purchased/ordered at the same time. Well of course only 3 arrive. I keep checking the status of the last item and about 2 hours after the other items were delivered I get an email saying my last item has been delayed.... How is it delayed when it should have gone out with the other 3 items that are all the same product?! Same product, color, purchased on the same order. Now I have to prolong the maintenance I had planned.",2019-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,8.0,4.0,1160,215,15,2,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,used amazon year generally reliable service however last year multiple hiccup delivery item one item sent walmart distribution center different city still sure fedex messed week ago ordered product order pretty frequently every month packaging terrible lid one item cracked product seeping sent amazon review photo issue wouldnt acknowledge fault told needed return leaky product via mail pretty sure usps wont accept liquid containedtoday supposed receive order item purchasedordered time well course arrive keep checking status last item hour item delivered get email saying last item delayed delayed gone item product product color purchased order prolong maintenance planned,0.07510595862587116,0.9248940413741289,0.12058328659562535,0.2,0.7865636780061894,78.65636780061894,High Trust
Phil A,/users/5d474cf780a672668f22856b,US,4.0,2019-08-04 21:24:46+00:00,1.0,uSPS delivery failures (and lies),"This review concerns prime delivery when Amazon chooses to use the USPS for delivery, especially when the delivery is scheduled for a Sunday.  I was expecting a delivery today, Aug 4, 2019 and received a notification that the delivery occurred at 11:14 am.  But, where is the package?  I searched but did not find any.  I have a motion detection video camera and it was not triggered.  This makes the 7th Sunday delivery by the USPS that did not make it.  I’ve had zero issues with delivery on other days or when delivery is made by an Amazon vehicle.  If Amazon continues to use the USPS, I will probably stop ordering anything that is scheduled for a Sunday.",2019-08-04 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,8.0,4.0,660,118,33,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,review concern prime delivery amazon chooses use usps delivery especially delivery scheduled sunday expecting delivery today aug received notification delivery occurred package searched find motion detection video camera triggered make th sunday delivery usps make i’ve zero issue delivery day delivery made amazon vehicle amazon continues use usps probably stop ordering anything scheduled sunday,0.009736880318640232,0.9902631196813597,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.8083676787414089,80.83676787414089,High Trust
