Gian Piero,/users/5b277a194de5666d343ba7a9,ES,26.0,2019-07-24 10:32:37+00:00,5.0,21 years using Amazon,"I am surprised by some many bad reviews. I must be extraordinarily lucky. My first Amazon order was in 1998. Since then I have used Amazon virtually every week, for books and videos in the early days and now for virtually anything. In the last 21 years I have had deliveries in France, Italy and Spain. I have never encountered a serious problem. Once a book arrived damaged, used the same box, I printed the labels, went to Post Office and sent it back, a new book arrived 3 days later. Another time my mobile phone under guarantee stopped working, I got a small box, printed the appropriate labels and went to the Post Office. After 10 days I go my phone back repaired. I do not believe that I am particularly lucky. I believe our world is full of people that love to complain.",2019-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,7.0,24.0,779,145,21,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,surprised many bad review must extraordinarily lucky first amazon order since used amazon virtually every week book video early day virtually anything last year delivery france italy spain never encountered serious problem book arrived damaged used box printed label went post office sent back new book arrived day later another time mobile phone guarantee stopped working got small box printed appropriate label went post office day go phone back repaired believe particularly lucky believe world full people love complain,0.036664059031193116,0.9633359409688069,0.08132361189007291,1.0,1.997932692862418,199.79326928624178,High Trust
Matt Andrews,/users/5d38210790717e3e4a20a6a3,US,1.0,2019-07-24 09:59:32+00:00,1.0,"Terrible experience! I lost over $30,000 to fraudulent seller accounts","I can't begin to express my anger towards Amazon. I'm absolutely appalled by the rude, offensive, belittling comments and lack of assistance. I bought three furniture pieces for my apartment in upstate New York. One was QLED 8K television, which was bought on May 5th. I received the item in practically a hollow box. Upon inspection, surprisingly, there were no noticeable signs of damage, so I decided to plug it into my wall. The second I did, I smelled an awful odor coming from the back of the set which smelled like something died inside. The television would not power on or respond to button presses. I decided to speak to Amazon personally, which I couldn't get in touch with a human for over an hour. When I finally got a hold of someone they had me on hold for another 30 minutes. At first, he was polite, but as I explained what happened, he would cut in and not let me get any other words in. He shouted MA'M!...MA'M!...MA'M!..then gave me an annoyed tone of why the television wasn't under warranty. If that wasn't enough, he would paraphrase me and use words ""power cord"" ""tv remote"" and others in a shrill voice clearly making fun of me because I'm a female. I told him if he would hold on the line I can put my boyfriend on, which suddenly ended the call prematurely. This is so unprofessional! I've reached out to Amazon customer service at least 4 times last and this month, which had I never received a reply. I can't return the television, and it has been in the living room the entirety of this ordeal! I have tried everything but it seems I'm on my own. I don't want to start a lawsuit against Amazon but I might not have a choice.",2019-07-24 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,7.0,24.0,1654,305,70,10,0.0,0,5,2,1,Suspicious,cant begin express anger towards amazon im absolutely appalled rude offensive belittling comment lack assistance bought three furniture piece apartment upstate new york one qled k television bought may th received item practically hollow box upon inspection surprisingly noticeable sign damage decided plug wall second smelled awful odor coming back set smelled like something died inside television would power respond button press decided speak amazon personally couldnt get touch human hour finally got hold someone hold another minute first polite explained happened would cut let get word shouted mammammamthen gave annoyed tone television wasnt warranty wasnt enough would paraphrase use word power cord tv remote others shrill voice clearly making fun im female told would hold line put boyfriend suddenly ended call prematurely unprofessional ive reached amazon customer service least time last month never received reply cant return television living room entirety ordeal tried everything seems im dont want start lawsuit amazon might choice,0.9686701043273488,0.03132989567265121,0.17106001121704992,0.2,0.34987695007973557,34.98769500797356,Low Trust
