John Simon,/users/59d560ee0000ff000ad11a9e,CA,4.0,2019-07-16 13:34:26+00:00,1.0,I thinks their products,"I thinks their products, pricing, and delivery are great.  However, I never leave my credit card information saved for any company.  So I was surprised after not using Amazon for over a year when I suddenly started receiving charges from them.  Upon calling I discovered they had reactivated my prime account and charged my credit card which they kept on file - even though I chose not to save the information for future pusposes.They agreed to reverse the charges but how can I trust a company which keeps financial data without permission and ""mistakenly"" starts charging you for services you didn't buy?",2019-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,7.0,16.0,606,102,23,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,think product pricing delivery great however never leave credit card information saved company surprised using amazon year suddenly started receiving charge upon calling discovered reactivated prime account charged credit card kept file even though chose save information future pusposesthey agreed reverse charge trust company keep financial data without permission mistakenly start charging service didnt buy,0.024909406583728647,0.9750905934162714,0.05720695457094784,0.2,0.7989866876223253,79.89866876223253,High Trust
