Claude Larimer,/users/5d13cfeb3fc1c8284c359ed3,US,13.0,2019-06-26 20:22:56+00:00,1.0,appears to becoming Amabay/ebay,"Bought an item from a third party seller in CA to be delivered by the 28th, went out for delivery on the 25th, never delivered. received email from amazon that there was a problem with the order,""contact seller"", which I did; they told me to be patient as it had until the 28th, I explained and forwarded the email that there was a problem. Their reply was to refuse delivery. Fedex delivered it on the 29th when I was not home to refuse it, and I could see why it was not delivered, so I cancelled the order. The seller had sent the 110lb item in the standard box that you would see it in in the retail store, Fedex had taped it, using a what would appear to be a whole roll of tape. I filed a claim under the A-Z warranty policy, bottom line is that I was lied to the whole process saying they would cover the cost and evan return shipping and kept asking for documents that I had already sent them: (playing games). I repackaged the item and sent it back via Fedex ground (110lbs) for $121.58 at their instruction,  the seller indicates that when they got the package it was 15lbs. Amazon has closed the case and I am out roughly $150.00 on this deal since Fedex is saying that they are only responsible for $221.58. No problem closing the account and buying elsewhere.",2019-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,6.0,26.0,1272,240,31,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,bought item third party seller ca delivered th went delivery th never delivered received email amazon problem ordercontact seller told patient th explained forwarded email problem reply refuse delivery fedex delivered th home refuse could see delivered cancelled order seller sent lb item standard box would see retail store fedex taped using would appear whole roll tape filed claim az warranty policy bottom line lied whole process saying would cover cost evan return shipping kept asking document already sent playing game repa