Benzo Advisor,/users/5c389cb1a33add91b4dcdc24,US,3.0,2019-06-25 19:37:56+00:00,1.0,lazy drivers,Horrible delivery service. First of all I’m disabled it’s very hard to leave the apartment. I have it in my Amazon delivery instructions to deliver the package to my home since I’m home every day. Do they do this? Rarely what do they do? They pull into the apartment Leasing office and dump all the packages on them. They make zero attempt to actually deliver the packages to the customers at least that’s how it works here in Atlanta. The leasing office has told them that they need to attempt to deliver before taking it to the office but they never are rarely do. Because of This I will no longer be using Amazon. I pay for prime for two day delivery And rarely getting it. Dumping packages out and a leasing office because you’re too lazy to do your job isn’t delivery.,2019-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,6.0,25.0,773,143,12,2,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,horrible delivery service first i’m disabled it’s hard leave apartment amazon delivery instruction deliver package home since i’m home every day rarely pull apartment leasing office dump package make zero attempt actually deliver package customer least that’s work atlanta leasing office told need attempt deliver taking office never rarely longer using amazon pay prime two day delivery rarely getting dumping package leasing office you’re lazy job isn’t delivery,0.026593756243591955,0.973406243756408,0.08020190689848569,0.2,0.8027435032579011,80.27435032579011,High Trust
Emily,/users/5d122d94ea39084e53cea67e,US,1.0,2019-06-25 14:20:06+00:00,1.0,Why is student prime only 4 years?,"Why is student prime only 4 years?! I am a graduate student, which means I am now in my 6th year of school and student prime was super affordable and a helpful option for my textbooks. However, being on a tight budget I am unable to afford the $119 fee for regular prime. I understand you do not want people to ""mooch"" off of this discount but with what you use to determine if someone is a student should show that they are still a student! Use broke college students cannot afford $119 when we have other fees that need to be paid as well. I sadly had to cancel my subscription because I cannot afford that $119.",2019-06-25 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,6.0,25.0,614,118,34,7,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,student prime year graduate student mean th year school student prime super affordable helpful option textbook however tight budget unable afford fee regular prime understand want people mooch discount use determine someone student show still student use broke college student cannot afford fee need paid well sadly cancel subscription cannot afford,0.4700619472564314,0.5299380527435686,0.06618059450364554,0.2,0.5782051452725134,57.82051452725134,Medium Trust
