Quinetta James,/users/5cf5c7fb99e21804c5cd4ce9,US,1.0,2019-06-04 01:23:18+00:00,1.0,Done with Amazon. Horrible !,"I purchased 2 Amazon Fire Tv’s sticks in November. Both remotes went out Janurary. I have been buying batteries every since thinking that there was an issue with the battery. Finally I got around to some free time to contact Amazon for the 2nd time about the remotes and the agent said that they were unable to replace the remotes because of a warranty being outdated. There is obviously an issue with the devices themselves being that BOTH REMOTES ARE NOT WORKING JO MATTER WHAT AAA BATTERIES I PURCHASE. Instead of apologizing for the inconvenience and assisting me with replacing 2 products that I bought from Amazon, the agent said “Download the app and use that for my TV’s”. How inconsiderate to tell me to pass my phone around the house so me or my guests can play hot potato me with my cell phone, and God forbid I need to talk on my phone while someone wants to watch TV. I will be discontinuing ALL SERVICES that has to do with Amazon and so will others that I recommend Amazon to. Very distasteful experience!!!",2019-06-04 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,6.0,4.0,1022,185,28,5,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,purchased amazon fire tv’s stick november remote went janurary buying battery every since thinking issue battery finally got around free time contact amazon nd time remote agent said unable replace remote warranty outdated obviously issue device remote working jo matter aaa battery purchase instead apologizing inconvenience assisting replacing product bought amazon agent said “download app use tv’s” inconsiderate tell pas phone around house guest play hot potato cell phone god forbid need talk phone someone want watch tv discontinuing service amazon others recommend amazon distasteful experience,0.7914102835580699,0.20858971644193014,0.10375771172181716,0.2,0.4250464005653285,42.50464005653285,Low Trust
