Victor Adkins,/users/5cf496c70d0a0c6d80bb830d,US,1.0,2019-06-03 03:41:06+00:00,1.0,Amazon delivery and customer service fails,"Amazon has become a giant machine that does not care about their customers or about their guaranteed deliveries. I have been a prime customer for quite a while and have had recently multiple shipments that have not come on their scheduled delivery date. Those dates are the only reason to buy with Amazon and pay extra money for prime. The only response from Amazon customer service is ""sorry"" or here is a $5 credit. They could care less that I needed those items on the promised date and their failure to follow through cost me extra money, time and hassle. This is unacceptable and it won't happen again. I will not order anything from Amazon again once my rewards credit from my Amazon card are used up and I will not be renewing my prime membership. I will just use Wal-Mart instead as they offer FREE expedited shipping without a membership. Sad and disappointed as a long term customer and wish it wasn't so. Enjoy your snake oil status Amazon and I know losing one customer won't affect you but I do hope you read this review and care again one day for all your other customers sake.",2019-06-03 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,6.0,3.0,1091,198,42,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon become giant machine care customer guaranteed delivery prime customer quite recently multiple shipment come scheduled delivery date date reason buy amazon pay extra money prime response amazon customer service sorry credit could care less needed item promised date failure follow cost extra money time hassle unacceptable wont happen order anything amazon reward credit amazon card used renewing prime membership use walmart instead offer free expedited shipping without membership sad disappointed long term customer wish wasnt enjoy snake oil status amazon know losing one customer wont affect hope read review care one day customer sake,0.012868318173221028,0.987131681826779,0.11104879416713405,0.2,0.8157755997468162,81.57755997468162,High Trust
