Steve,/users/5b6489c24de5666d34a0b147,US,3.0,2019-05-16 15:22:01+00:00,1.0,Amazon automated return system screws customer!,"Recently I place an order through Amazon.com. Order# 114-1442158-54*****.All the items were purchase from one (1) order.  The order included some items that were the wrong size from what I thought I was ordering.I did a search on 4 AWG terminal lugs.  Amazon search engine took me to 4/0 AWG terminal lug.  I didn't know that 4/0 terminal lugs were about twice the size as 4 AWG terminals.  So I returned the 4/0 and 2/0 terminal lugs. Amazon's automated return system would not let me return these items in one shipment, instead it issues three separate return labels. The amount I paid for these items totaled at $39.62, the refund I received was $21.65.  Amazon charged me 54% of the original price.These items combined weight was 1.03 lbs, they took up less than 1/5 of a cubic foot. Yet Amazon forced me to make three separate shipping, and charged me 50% of the purchase price.THIS IS A SCAM BY ANY STANDARDS, and Amazon should rethink their return policy... it's designed to screw the customer.",2019-05-16 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,5.0,16.0,1001,174,47,6,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently place order amazoncom order item purchase one order order included item wrong size thought orderingi search awg terminal lug amazon search engine took awg terminal lug didnt know terminal lug twice size awg terminal returned terminal lug amazon automated return system would let return item one shipment instead issue three separate return label amount paid item totaled refund received amazon charged original pricethese item combined weight lb took less cubic foot yet amazon forced make three separate shipping charged purchase pricethis scam standard amazon rethink return policy designed screw customer,0.007490143885083233,0.9925098561149168,0.0975883342680875,0.2,0.8157725949110759,81.57725949110758,High Trust
