Earnest,/users/5a551f190000ff000afdb327,GB,71.0,2019-05-15 08:38:44+00:00,1.0,Avoid Amazon Wardrobe,"Amazon used to set the benchmark for customer service, not any more. They got too big and still think they have that reputation, they don't, it's been going downhill for years, next day delivery is a joke and customer service although polite are just reading from a list of answers. Amazon Wardrobe is their latest failing. I ordered 3 pairs of walking boots so I could find the correct fit at home. I sealed the other 2 back up in the mailing bag and stuck the returns label on. When I took it to the post office I was told they couldn't accept it due to an issue with the barcode. This meant dragging the parcel containing 2 heavy pairs of walking boots around the town with me to get my shopping. On returning home I contacted Amazon and was told the barcode was fine, they blamed the post office scanner. The only 2 options they gave me was to print another label and try again, or they suggested I could book a collection with a courier, pay for it myself and wait in at home for it to be collected. They said they would reimburse me when they received it. I stated this wasn't an acceptable resolution and asked to escalate the matter as a formal complaint, and their manager to contact me. When that happened I was told that the only 2 options available were the same as I had been told already. They weren't interested. I printed the label, which had exactly the same barcode as before, and set off for the post office once again with fingers crossed. I spoke to the manager who informed me the problem was a glitch in Amazon's system and it had been happening all day with their return parcels, not all of them just some. Luckily the scanner accepted the barcode this time otherwise I would once again have to lug the package home......Amazon are in denial and the policy is to blame anyone else for their failings, including their long term loyal customers. Will I be using Amazon Wardrobe again? No way",2019-05-15 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,5.0,15.0,1913,353,21,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon used set benchmark customer service got big still think reputation dont going downhill year next day delivery joke customer service although polite reading list answer amazon wardrobe latest failing ordered pair walking boot could find correct fit home sealed back mailing bag stuck return label took post office told couldnt accept due issue barcode meant dragging parcel containing heavy pair walking boot around town get shopping returning home contacted amazon told barcode fine blamed post office scanner option gave print another label try suggested could book collection courier pay wait home collected said would reimburse received stated wasnt acceptable resolution asked escalate matter formal complaint manager contact happened told option available told already werent interested printed label exactly barcode set post office finger crossed spoke manager informed problem glitch amazon system happening day return parcel luckily scanner accepted barcode time otherwise would lug package homeamazon denial policy blame anyone else failing including long term loyal customer using amazon wardrobe way,0.050585220583671146,0.9494147794163289,0.19798093101514302,0.2,0.8143035759111931,81.4303575911193,High Trust
