Hina Ansar,/users/5cda5bfca5274ec1621c64cf,US,2.0,2019-05-14 06:11:16+00:00,1.0,Recurring charges without justification: Amazon Prime Video,"I have had the worst experience ever with this Amazon Prime Video. They have repeatedly charged me for transactions I have not performed with their account. Then when I call and talk to them, they give me the go around by telling me the issue will be resolved and you would not be charged anymore. But they never stop chargung me. When I call for refund, they would refund me only for one of almost 20 charges that they may have charged me. They would claim for a gift card which is never processed. I am told that I have watched a video while I was on my job. Each time, every manager claims to be taking care of the issue but nothing happens. When I ask if they have any record of the previous call, they never have it. Sick and tired of these recurring charges. I would never recommend it to anyone and if anybody has any idea of how to challenge them from being in Indiana and refund my charges, please offer some help. Thank you!",2019-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,5.0,14.0,934,179,59,7,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,worst experience ever amazon prime video repeatedly charged transaction performed account call talk give go around telling issue resolved would charged anymore never stop chargung call refund would refund one almost charge may charged would claim gift card never processed told watched video job time every manager claim taking care issue nothing happens ask record previous call never sick tired recurring charge would never recommend anyone anybody idea challenge indiana refund charge please offer help thank,0.03883196180999806,0.961168038190002,0.10039259674705553,0.2,0.800662538444412,80.0662538444412,High Trust
Andrew Evenson,/users/5cda1e8094dddb2d748949cd,US,1.0,2019-05-14 01:48:59+00:00,1.0,Customer Service Reps have no ability to help,"I don't know what the role of customer service reps is since they don't seem to have the ability to help beyond the standard buttons you can access yourself.I placed an order with 2-day shipping, but due to the quantity I ordered, I ultimately got an email stating the delivery date was now going to be over 3 weeks out. This was not acceptable for my timeline so I requested to cancel within an hour. I was told it was too far along in the shipping process to cancel. I questioned how that could be when it wasn't shipping for 3 weeks. No one could give me an answer to that. Every time they would respond with the same generic response that when items are shipping very soon, they can't be cancelled. I don't know how 3 weeks is soon. One rep had kids crying in the background and just said ""ummm"" for 10 minutes without providing any meaningful information at all. The ""supervisor"" had dogs barking in the background and gave the exact same generic response that didn't actually apply to my situation or order. Never got any resolution as no one was empowered to do anything more than try the same cancel button I have access to on my account.Really a baffling experience that this is the type of service Amazon provides.",2019-05-14 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,5.0,14.0,1224,224,45,8,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,dont know role customer service rep since dont seem ability help beyond standard button access yourselfi placed order day shipping due quantity ordered ultimately got email stating delivery date going week acceptable timeline requested cancel within hour told far along shipping process cancel questioned could wasnt shipping week one could give answer every time would respond generic response item shipping soon cant cancelled dont know week soon one rep kid cry background said ummm minute without providing meaningful information supervisor dog barking background gave exact generic response didnt actually apply situation order never got resolution one empowered anything try cancel button access accountreally baffling experience type service amazon provides,0.009406578580565667,0.9905934214194343,0.1256309590577678,0.2,0.8204229025212706,82.04229025212706,High Trust
