Kelsey,/users/5c85e768a452db187bf984c3,CA,2.0,2019-03-11 04:43:23+00:00,1.0,Don’t believe everything,"I recently wrote an honest review for a product I had received from amazon. It did not contain any profanity but simply stated that situation and that was that they sent me the wrong product and when asked to return, they wanted me to pay to send back the wrong product they sent me- which is unacceptable. As a paying customer I am not going to spend more money on a mistake they made. Amazon sent me an email saying they wouldn’t publish my review- which leads me to believe that many products on amazon for the majority only accept positive reviews and little negative ones - which scews the knowledge about how good the product actually is. I don’t find this to be a trustworthy act from amazon and because of this I’ve lost an enourmous amount of respect.",2019-03-11 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,3.0,11.0,760,140,24,3,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently wrote honest review product received amazon contain profanity simply stated situation sent wrong product asked return wanted pay send back wrong product sent unacceptable paying customer going spend money mistake made amazon sent email saying wouldn’t publish review lead believe many product amazon majority accept positive review little negative one scews knowledge good product actually don’t find trustworthy act amazon i’ve lost enourmous amount respect,0.04506135395031351,0.9549386460496865,0.07851934941110487,0.2,0.7931731929070642,79.31731929070642,High Trust
