Nosey Mae Parker,/users/5c8146b5f46be341a633dc94,US,1.0,2019-03-07 16:28:48+00:00,1.0,Inflated Price/Misleading Seller Info,"I put a book (100 Flowers and How They Got Their Names - hardback version) into my cart. It was priced at $16 and showed that it was being sold and shipped by Amazon and that there was only one left in stock. I added some additional books and items, an order that totaled well over $100. As I was reviewing my order prior to purchase I noticed that the price of this book had jumped to over $29! I removed the book from my cart and waited for a couple of minutes. I went back to the original page and found that the price had again been adjusted, this time to $9.99 and the seller had changed from Amazon to an affiliate. Not nice, Amazon! I immediately removed every item from my cart. I found all the books and items on a couple of your competitor's websites and ordered from them. I was able to get 100 Flowers at a more reasonable price as well. So for the sake of around $13 you lost out on a $100+ order. A drop in the bucket to a company the size of Amazon, I know. Still, bad business is bad business......",2019-03-07 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,3.0,7.0,1014,200,37,4,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,put book flower got name hardback version cart priced showed sold shipped amazon one left stock added additional book item order totaled well reviewing order prior purchase noticed price book jumped removed book cart waited couple minute went back original page found price adjusted time seller changed amazon affiliate nice amazon immediately removed every item cart found book item couple competitor website ordered able get flower reasonable price well sake around lost order drop bucket company size amazon know still bad business bad business,0.22880594813930705,0.771194051860693,0.11217049915872125,0.2,0.7080311257620908,70.80311257620909,Medium Trust
