Mark Shortt,/users/5c7f2f89785a58e57e069ca1,US,1.0,2019-03-06 02:25:22+00:00,1.0,If I could give them a zero I would,"If I could give them a zero I would. I had an old debit card get hot carded 1 year ago. I updated my primary payment method for Amazon with my new card I got from my bank. The new card worked for a month or two and then I noticed a part that I had ordered did not arrive when I expected. I went into Amazon and checked and it said order cancelled. Did I get an email, text notification or phone call.....NO! So after some digging and contacting their customer service they stated it was using my old card, I told them to remove it and ensure that my new card was set as default card. So another couple months go by and now another package is not shipping when I expect and so I login and check Amazon again and it states payment needs revision....It was trying to use my old card yet again! I called this time as I was upset and needed the order before I left out of town. I call to see if they can fix what is going on and also get my order shipped ASAP. The original order (Tuesday Morning) stated with my prime membership that they would have it to me Wednesday evening. However, since they messed up my payment method yet again, now when fixing the order after losing the whole day it states my order will not arrive until Friday evening, when I will be out of town! So their mistake and it cost me delivery time and do they offer to fix it. No!! They instead tell me all the reasons why I could have messed up the payment, which is absolute lie! They tell me after about 45 seconds that they cannot do anything about the shkpping to get it to me sooner. I cancelled membership and then they tell me I would not get a refund because I used up shipping credits, IT IS PRIME! When asking for when I used these credits they could not provide me any information....this was management.. They are going downhill and customer service is horrible.",2019-03-06 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,3.0