Niki jfr,/users/5b485f3f4de5666d34efe902,US,5.0,2019-03-04 22:52:28+00:00,1.0,Delivered but never received,"I ordered two electric toothbrushes off of Amazon valued at ~$300. Their tracker showed the item as delivered, but I never received it. I reached out to customer service with my concerns, and was asked to submit a police report. Once the report was verified by the police department and issued an incident number, then to reach out to customer service with the information so I can be refunded. It has been 9 days since the police department issued the incident #, and I reached out to Amazon Customer Service three times, and on each occasion they asked me to validate the information. Share the department name, assigned officer, department #, etc. Which I did. They then assured me I'd be refunded within 24-48 hours every time, and I have yet to be refunded. I reached out once again today, and the rep said ""We have tried to validate the police report, however we are unable to validate the report."" What does that suppose to mean? I have the police report with the incident # in my hands. The rep also continued to accuse me with blatant lies that ""you've ordered with us a number of times, but most of the packages are being stolen or lost even though tracking shows delivered."" This is a disgraceful lie since the only other time I reached out to them regarding a missing item was when I ordered neck pillows back in December of 2018. Ever since then I've ordered hundreds of items with varied price tags that I've received without a problem. It appears that this rep is indirectly accusing me of theft. That I took the toothbrushes and now I'm lying about never having received them. Why would I file a false police report then? It's a federal crime, morons. I'm not going to risk prison time over toothbrushes. Since this is such a huge deal for them, I don't understand why they don't require signatures for items valued above a certain threshold rather than just throwing the package somewhere and calling it a day. Overall, I'd recommend working with vendors directly, and ordering from them, and cutting Amazon out of the picture. If your item is ""lost or stolen"" they call you a thief and send you on a wild goose chase. I'll be relaying this to my credit card company as a fraud charge, but don't recommend spending another penny with this company and their nasty behavior towards loyal customers.",2019-03-04 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,3.0,4.0,2313,411,28,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,ordered two electric toothbrush amazon valued tracker showed item delivered never received reached customer service concern asked submit police report report verified police department issued incident number reach customer service information refunded day since police department issued incident reached amazon customer service three time occasion asked validate information share department name assigned officer department etc assured id refunded within hour every time yet refunded reached today rep said tried validate police report however unable validate report suppose mean police report incident hand rep also continued accuse blatant lie youve ordered u number time package stolen lost even though tracking show delivered disgraceful lie since time reached regarding missing item ordered neck pillow back december ever since ive ordered hundred item varied price tag ive received without problem appears rep indirectly accusing theft took toothbrush im lying never received would file false police report federal crime moron im going risk prison time toothbrush since huge deal dont understand dont require signature item valued certain threshold rather throwing package somewhere calling day overall id recommend working vendor directly ordering cutting amazon picture item lost stolen call thief send wild goose chase ill relaying credit card company fraud charge dont recommend spending another penny company nasty behavior towards loyal customer,0.00798500647026306,0.992014993529737,0.23051037577117217,0.2,0.842109571919103,84.2109571919103,High Trust
