Katie Webster,/users/5c34e83fbc638bd689d6c10b,US,1.0,2019-01-08 18:13:31+00:00,1.0,Amazon is a sneaky sneaky company that…,"Amazon is a sneaky sneaky company that is on the same bandwagon as the monthly product subscriptions that automatically renew without your consent. Amazon asks if you would like to try out prime for free shipping, then, without any question, they use the credit card you have on file one month later to extract the yearly membership for a prime account which you assumed was ended after your free trial month. They send a sneaky email that is not from Amazon.com but from sales-news@amazon which makes you think it is a phishing scam and you immediately double delete. I am so disappointed in this aspect of the company and will definitely think 3 times before ever purchasing from this site again. I hate shady companies that auto renew- should be illegal to do this without permission.",2019-01-08 00:00:00+00:00,2019.0,1.0,8.0,787,136,39,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon sneaky sneaky company bandwagon monthly product subscription automatically renew without consent amazon asks would like try prime free shipping without question use credit card file one month later extract yearly membership prime account assumed ended free trial month send sneaky email amazoncom salesnewsamazon make think phishing scam immediately double delete disappointed aspect company definitely think time ever purchasing site hate shady company auto renew illegal without permission,0.021867182331257756,0.9781328176687423,0.07627593942793046,0.2,0.8043215967199572,80.43215967199572,High Trust
