kim,/users/5c11d3ff6b8fe698e48f30ca,US,1.0,2018-12-13 03:37:37+00:00,1.0,I pay for Prime,"I pay for Prime. Part of that service is 2 day free delivery. In the past when I did not receive the item in 2 days (and it was important) I called and Amazon gave a 1 month extension on my prime membership. I only had this issue twice in the many years I have been a member. I have had late deliveries all the time, but did not care. I had an important delivery today, and Amazon informed me they no longer extend the membership. So, I have paid for two day delivery and they do not have to make good on that part of the contract.Looks like a class action law suit to me. Sign me up",2018-12-13 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,12.0,13.0,583,119,15,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,pay prime part service day free delivery past receive item day important called amazon gave month extension prime membership issue twice many year member late delivery time care important delivery today amazon informed longer extend membership paid two day delivery make good part contractlooks like class action law suit sign,0.011278628888181064,0.9887213711118189,0.06674144699943915,0.2,0.8077089749557973,80.77089749557973,High Trust
