Yashira Robles,/users/5c08453ec574bfa3883121bd,US,2.0,2018-12-05 21:42:20+00:00,1.0,Amazon misleading/ false promotions,"For the past few days a promotion had been popping up on my account, ""Save $15 with your first sign in on the app"". I have a Prime membership and consistently place orders on Amazon but through my regular browser so I proceeded to download the app. After downloading the app I add an item to the cart that meets their requirement of $30. However, the $15 are not automatically deducted off the total. So I decide to reach out to customer service through the available chat option only to be given the runaround.My first complain is that I switch off from a representative to representative. If you do not respond back within a minute or god forbid 2. You will have a new representative that will need to read the complete conversation to catch up.Then a representative decided to focus on whether I received an email with the promotion? In which I respond, it doesn't seem to me that I need one when the promotion clearly states, ""the eligible customers should have received this offer directly from Amazon through the Amazon website OR by email. My favorite was when a representative told me I was not eligible because unbeknownst to me. I downloaded the app already in March 2018. Yet, I have several emails from Amazon throughout the summer with a similar promotion asking me to download the app.I am extremely disappointed in the customer service I received from Amazon. I had a more serious matter  resolved with Best Buy resolved through chat in less than 8 minutes. While, I had close to a 4 hour conversation through chat with more than a handful of Amazon representative only for my time to be wasted. A representative finally informed me a complaint will be placed after over 3 hours of me speaking with representatives and that I would hear back in 48 hours. 4 hours later over six representatives later, my matter was never resolved. My household spends thousands every year through Amazon. Just for them to not be able to honor a $15 promotion they themselves promoted to me on my account. I hardly ever use promo codes when shopping on Amazon but if they will be promoting a discount for downloads of their app they should honor it. Amazon will surely be losing much business from our end and I will be doing my research in other websites now instead of immediately going through Amazon.",2018-12-05 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,12.0,5.0,2301,407,35,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,past day promotion popping account save first sign app prime membership consistently place order amazon regular browser proceeded download app downloading app add item cart meet requirement however automatically deducted total decide reach customer service available chat option given runaroundmy first complain switch representative representative respond back within minute god forbid new representative need read complete conversation catch upthen representative decided focus whether received email promotion respond doesnt seem need one promotion clearly state eligible customer received offer directly amazon amazon website email favorite representative told eligible unbeknownst downloaded app already march yet several email amazon throughout summer similar promotion asking download appi extremely disappointed customer service received amazon serious matter resolved best buy resolved chat less minute close hour conversation chat handful amazon representative time wasted representative finally informed complaint placed hour speaking representative would hear back hour hour later six representative later matter never resolved household spends thousand every year amazon able honor promotion promoted account hardly ever use promo code shopping amazon promoting discount downloads app honor amazon surely losing much business end research website instead immediately going amazon,0.00938244058948386,0.9906175594105161,0.22826696578799777,0.2,0.8409621728628576,84.09621728628576,High