Debra Jean,/users/5b9f60084de5666d3458e621,US,2.0,2018-09-17 08:24:42+00:00,1.0,I think I'm in shock,"I think I'm in shock.  I have been an Amazon shopper for 20 years and I buy practically everything at Amazon.com.  I haven't been able to leave product reviews for about 8 months.  I keep getting an error message that says I violated Amazon rules and my reviews are biased which is totally untrue.  I called Amazon 2 times during the past 8 months about this problem and was sent an email 2 times from Amazon apologizing for the inconvenience and they were very sorry and I should be able to leave product reviews now.  I tried again and kept getting the same error message.  Yesterday 9/16/18 I called Amazon again about the problem because I got the most horrible, nasty, disgusting email from Amazon.com that I have ever received in my life.  It was dated 9/10/18 and said:We have determined that you have violated our Community Guidelines. As a result, we have suppressed all of your reviews, and you will no longer be able to post community content on Amazon. This includes Customer Reviews.Customer Reviews are meant to give customers unbiased product feedback from fellow shoppers. Because our goal is to provide Customer Reviews that help customers make informed purchase decisions, any accounts and reviews that could be viewed as advertising, promotional, or biased will be removed.Your community privileges may have been revoked for one or more of the following reasons:-- Elements of your account indicate a relationship to sellers, publishers, or other reviewers of the products you review.-- Your reviews were posted in exchange for compensation, such as gift cards to purchase the product, product refunds, review swaps, or free or discounted products.-- You requested free or discounted products in exchange for reviews.We made this decision after carefully considering your account. This decision is final, and your community privileges will not be reinstated.We cannot share any further information about this decision, and we may not reply to further emails about this issue.Review Moderator Amazon.comSo I called Amazon again yesterday and spoke with a supervisor and she was very nice and couldn't figure out why I got this email.  An Amazon Rep wrote an email for me to the appeals department and I got so mad and upset at Amazon that I notified my family attorney and he told me Amazon has committed Defamation of Character/Slander and my Attorney sent an email to Amazon Appeals requiring proof of the false accusations they are making about me and required them to send me an apology email and stopped me from shopping at Amazon until he clears this up and he is ready to take them to Court for saying these horrible, untrue things about me. I can't believe Amazon.com would do this.  I have never taken any compensation from any seller for a review and I never violated any of Amazon's stupid guidelines whatever they are. I guess you can't leave a review that says your item is ""beautiful and lovely"" because that's all the Amazon reps see.I don't know what to say except I am in shock and they obviously have the wrong person because what they emailed me is not about me at all.Debra Jean",2018-09-17 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,9.0,17.0,3116,527,20,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,think im shock amazon shopper year buy practically everything amazoncom havent able leave product review month keep getting error message say violated amazon rule review biased totally untrue called amazon time past month problem sent email time amazon apologizing inconvenience sorry able leave product review tried kept getting error message yesterday called amazon problem got horrible nasty disgusting email amazoncom ever received life dated saidwe determined violated community guideline result suppressed review longer able post community content amazon includes customer reviewscustomer review meant give customer unbiased product feedback fellow shopper goal provide customer review help custo