Pooja Brijmohan Singh,/users/5b981bd24de5666d346aa946,IN,1.0,2018-09-11 19:47:48+00:00,1.0,Pathetic Amazon,"Pathetic AmazonI ordered L'Oreal Professionnel Serie Expert Liss Unlimited Evening Primrose Oil, 125ml and De Fabulous Shampoo, 250ml and Conditioner Reviver Set, 250ml on 05/09/2018 and both delivered to me on 06/09/2018 through Amazon Prime Delivery.When I opened the packet, I found that the bottles were not properly packed (sellotaped here and there) and there was leakage also. Oil was coming out of bottle. In fact it seems that these bottles were packed by someone from Amazon after getting them returned by any other customer. In my opinion I had been delivered product already used/returned by someone else.I had clearly read the policy regarding return/refund at the time of placing the order and I knew that product was not eligible for return/refund but I was not sure that I would be delivered such kind of already used/returned by some else product. I needed these product on urgent basis therefore I decided to get them delivered through Amazon Prime delivery and I paid extra money for that but what I got? Already used products… I never expected it from Amazon.I have paid my hard earned money to Amazon for these products and now I got defective products. I sent an e-mail to Amazon mentioning the issues I faced and attached pictures of the same. Next day I got an e-mail that ""on verification it was found that the products were damaged therefore refund would be issued"" and I was asked to update my account details, I updated my account details and on the very next day I was informed that the refund could not be issued as pictures are not clear.I sent pictures and numerous e-mails again and again but all in vain. I tried to contact customer care but my number was blocked. I tried chat option and they informed me that after examining pictures they haven't found any damage in the products. Amazon already examined the pictures and accepted that the products were 