Paul Kirby,/users/57cc59820000ff000a40f5c7,US,13.0,2018-07-18 20:06:16+00:00,1.0,Amazon = The Worst of Corporate Globalism,"Amazon represent some of the worst corporate behavior in online companies.  They seek to monopolize various platforms (e.g. video streaming - try buying an online video from anywhere else... it's almost impossible - that's called a monopoly and it's bad because it prevents competition - competition keeps the market prices fair and keeps the customer in control, not the corporation).  Also, it's almost impossible to close your Amazon account without jumping through 30 hoops (try it and see...).  They out-sourced billions of dollars to Asia - which isn't bad in itself, but they didn't do it to ""invest"" in Third World economies, the did it to save a buck (aka ""greed"") and they dramatically cut back on investing in a US workforce.  Jeff Bezos, as the CEO and owner, is very clearly driven by greed and has no national loyalties.  He's out-sourced to the cheapest labor force in the world, which means he's taken jobs away from Americans.When any company reaches the status of Corporate Giant, you lose that attention-to-detail that small local companies are so good at providing.  Here's an example of a product I bought recently through Amazon:I bought a 39 inch wide drip pan. Amazon Services are listed as the seller (no third party). I was mailed a 29 inch wide drip pan. Amazon totally screwed up and sent me the wrong product. When you live in a rural area, receiving the wrong product in the mail is incredibly frustrating. You then have to take the extra time to go into town to a USPS drop-off and mail it back and then wait for your refund. So much wasted time and money in ""limbo"" while you're waiting.I would discourage anyone from ordering a product from Amazon Services that requires anything other than them putting a product in box or envelope and mailing it - once you get into different sized products they don't have the Quality Controls in place to prevent very simple mistakes like this. Sadly, the fact that they are a big corporation means attention to detail like this will inevitably get overlooked. With that in mind, I would encourage people to pay the extra to buy products locally and not have to deal with very basic but time-consuming and costly mistakes.",2018-07-18 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,7.0,18.0,2192,377,41,7,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,amazon represent worst corporate behavior online company seek monopolize various platform eg video streaming try buying online video anywhere else almost impossible thats called monopoly bad prevents competition competition keep market price fair keep customer control corporation also almost impossible close amazon account without jumping hoop try see outsourced billion dollar asia isnt bad didnt invest third world economy save buck aka greed dramatically cut back investing u workforce jeff bezos ceo owner clearly driven greed national loyalty he outsourced cheapest labor force world mean he taken job away americanswhen company reach status corporate giant lose attentiontodetail small local company good providing here example product bought recently amazoni bought inch wide drip pan amazon service listed seller third party mailed inch wide drip pan amazon totally screwed sent wrong product live rural area receiving wrong product mail incredibly frustrating take extra time go town usps dropoff mail back wait refund much wasted time money limbo youre waitingi would discourage anyone ordering product amazon service requires anything putting product box envelope mailing get different sized product dont quality control place prevent simple mistake like sadly fact big corporation mean attention detail like inevitably get overlooked mind would encourage people pay extra buy product locally deal basic timeconsuming costly mistake,0.00933089100250987,0.9906691089974902,0.21144139091418956,0.2,0.837622832681583,83.7622832681583,High Trust
