Ian Tipany,/users/5b38ec1b4de5666d34fb6272,GB,6.0,2018-08-04 09:12:32+00:00,2.0,"Amazon UK not talking to Amazon elsewhere, leaving me with goods I no longer  want.","I ordered goods from Amazon and when they didn't arrive by the date needed I tried contacting Amazon - not easy, as it turned out. When I did catch up with them I was told I had not ordered anything and they had not taken anything from my  account, so nothing to worry about. I called my card provider and they informed me that the money had been taken from my account. I then looked at my options and decided I would be better with nothing to do with Amazon. Then I received a message in German from the supplier of the goods. I still don't know what the messages were about as my German isn't up to much, but they seemed to be trying to get in touch and I presumed this was about delivery of the goods, now two days late. At that point I went back to my card provider. Their grounds for contesting a charge seem quite limited, and the only one open to me was non-delivery. I contested the charge on that basis, pointing out that Amazon said I hadn't paid anything, while their accounts showed the contrary. the day after I sent off the formal notice to my card provider the goods were left on my doorstep. Nobody signed for them. Next day I sent Amazon a message bringing them up to date and got a reply telling me I would have to log into my account but that is still non-existent as far as Amazon UK is aware. To log into my account I need information which I do not have and they say does not exist. They don't even recognise the email on which we have exchanged several messages in the past few days and want me to find a lot of further information which they say they don't have and which doesn't exist anyway, so that I can get rid of the goods they say I don't have,  that I now don't want. Somewhere there's a simple failure to communicate between Germany where the supplier is based, and the UK where I am based. But I am aware that some supplier in Germany is short of goods and money, which is unfair. And I have heard recently that Amazon's treatment of its junior employees is pretty rough, so I don't want to put any of the staff I have been dealing with into the firing line. What is to be done?Three weeks later Amazon have responded adequately, accepting that they should have realised that my email ending .googlemail.com, which they had, was the same as .gmail.com which i have been using since google changed it. They offered a way of returning the goods which is so  complicated that I have given them to charity, their alternative suggestion.",2018-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,8.0,4.0,2466,466,83,15,19.0,0,0,0,0,Genuine,ordered good amazon didnt arrive date needed tried contacting amazon easy turned catch told ordered anything taken anything account nothing worry called card provider informed money taken account looked option decided would better nothing amazon received message german supplier good still dont know message german isnt much seemed trying get touch presumed delivery good two day late point went back card provider ground contesting charge seem quite limited one open nondelivery contested charge basis pointing amazon said hadnt paid anything account showed contrary day sent formal notice card provider good left doorstep nobody signed next day sent amazon message bringing date got reply telling would log account still nonexistent far amazon uk aware log account need information say exist dont even recognise email exchanged several message past day want find lot information say dont doesnt exist anyway get rid good say dont dont want somewhere there simple failure communicate germany supplier based uk based aware supplier germany short good money unfair heard recently amazon treatment junior employee pretty rough dont want put staff dealing firing line donethree week later amazon responded adequately accepting realised email ending googlemailcom gmailcom using since google changed offered way returning good complicated given charity alternative suggestion,0.005460194715490061,0.9945398052845099,0.26135726303982054,0.4,1.1495413552502192,114.95413552502191,High Trust
Ron,/users/5b42e6224de5666d34b17b84,US,3.0,2018-07-16 07:43:27+00:00,1.0,Worst Online Company,"Perhaps Amazon.com was a great company in the past, but I learned the hard way that my recent horrible experience with them was far from an isolated incident, as I have seen numerous other 1 star reviews for them lately. Everything that could go wrong....did go wrong. Took hours to sign up again, even though I was supposed to already be a member. They blatantly lied about the laptop I ordered. Said it had 4.0Ghz when it actually had 1.8. Screwed up my shipment numerous times and still tried to ship the order long after I cancelled it. Their customer service people were very rude in a matter of fact sort of way...as if their jobs were secure no  matter how bad they treat the customer. Big THUMBS DOWN TO THIS ROTTEN COMPANY!",2018-07-16 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,7.0,16.0,732,133,20,3,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,perhaps amazoncom great company past learned hard way recent horrible experience far isolated incident seen numerous star review lately everything could go wrongdid go wrong took hour sign even though supposed already member blatantly lied laptop ordered said ghz actually screwed shipment numerous time still tried ship order long cancelled customer service people rude matter fact sort wayas job secure matter bad treat customer big thumb rotten company,0.05157032488167987,0.9484296751183201,0.07459338194054964,0.2,0.7891335139472699,78.91335139472699,High Trust
