Shaun Peter,/users/565a7abe0000ff0001ee7f51,PH,4.0,2018-06-26 07:05:57+00:00,1.0,Amazon: Too big to care,"My issue has finally been resolved, after 20 hours of stress, after 18 customer service reps who refused to look into the fact I had been charged for cancelled orders. Finally, I was correct, and a refund from Amazon appeared in my account. A month after my purchase.Your service reps make assumptions, have not been trained well, and assume the way Amazon SHOULD work is the way it always DOES work. 16 of 18 service reps told me my card was only preauthorized, without even knowing that Amazon can't preauth pinless debit cards and charges the full amount when preparing for shipping. Everyone just assumed I was wrong and didn't look into it or handle it. I learned more from reading Amazon's FAQ than the service reps had learned from training.I'm a writer currently writing an article about this, I feel I have to. This was the worst customer service experience I have ever had in my life. The title of the article is ""Too Big To Care"".I especially dislike the service rep who told me in different words that Amazon doesn't make mistakes, and to never contact amazon customer service about this issue again or I won't receive a reply.The bank was on my side. I had submitted proof from my bank. The transactions were the exact amount of my cancelled orders. I had verified with my bank five times that these were not preauthorizations. Still, I was not believed and I slipped through the cracks because nobody believes Amazon could make a mistake. I requested my case be escalated to a manager or ombudsman and it was not. You truly do not care and think every customer is an idiot. I have a 148 IQ and a Master's degree and I was treated like a stupid mistaken child.After spending a huge chunk of my income with Amazon for a large portion of my life, I am done. I will no longer buy anything from Amazon. You treated me like crap and didn't believe me, and even after the bank told me you had refunded me one month later, you didn't acknowledge your mistake or apologize.Thanks for the refund. However, due to the stress and wasted time you caused me I'm devoting the rest of my life to let everyone know on social media and in the real world how much Amazon sucks, doesn't care, steals money and refuses to fix it, then when they finally do realize and fix it, I have to hear about it from my bank.Amazon has truly become #toobigtocare. Keep an eye out for that hashtag in the future, because I will put it everywhere. Charging loyal customers 265 USD for 60 dollars of merchandise and then refusing to acknowledge the possibility that Amazon made a mistake is no way to go through life, Amazon.",2018-06-26 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,6.0,26.0,2603,471,23,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,issue finally resolved hour stress customer service rep refused look fact charged cancelled order finally correct refund amazon appeared account month purchaseyour service rep make assumption trained well assume way amazon work way always work service rep told card preauthorized without even knowing amazon cant preauth pinless debit card charge full amount preparing shipping everyone assumed wrong didnt look handle learned reading amazon faq service rep learned trainingim writer currently writing article feel worst customer service experience ever life title article big carei especially dislike service rep told different word amazon doesnt make mistake never contact amazon customer service issue wont receive replythe bank side submitted proof bank transaction exact amount cancelled order verified bank five time preauthorizations still believed slipped crack nobody belief amazon could make mistake requested case escalated manager ombudsman truly care think every customer idiot iq master degree treated like stupid mistaken childafter spending huge chunk income amazon large portion life done longer buy anything amazon treated like crap didnt believe even bank told refunded one month later didnt acknowledge mistake apologizethanks refund however due stress wasted time caused im devoting rest life let everyone know social medium real world much amazon suck doesnt care steal money refuse fix finally realize fix hear bankamazon truly become toobigtocare keep eye hashtag future put everywhere charging loyal customer usd dollar merchandise refusing acknowledge possibility amazon made mistake way go life amazon,0.010585032526673215,0.9894149674733268,0.2641615255187886,0.2,0.8475397888404211,84.75397888404211,High Trust
