Aaron,/users/529eefb70000640001580537,GB,5.0,2018-06-12 10:01:17+00:00,1.0,Appalling service from Amazon.com as a UK buyer,"Outside of the US? Do not rely on Amazon(.com) to support your transaction all the way through to delivery!This 1 star doesn't represent the item in any way, because I didn't receive it!After receiving the delivery slip through the door by Yodel (of all people) stating it had been left in a safe place, but failed to specify where, I went through a two week back and forth with Amazon about where my item was. They couldn't (or wouldn't) provide the details of the delivery or be bothered to investigate Yodel properly to find out where my parcel had gone. In the end they they said would refund me if I provided a crime report, however my report was refused by my local police department due to the item failing to be delivered. My country's laws state that as the item wasn't received it cannot be classed as potentially stolen therefore no crime occurred. But Amazon seems to think they're above such laws and had the audacity to blame me for the failure of delivery, churning the same old statement about their terms and conditions to me over and over again that once an item has been ""delivered"" it becomes my responsibility. I'm pretty sure the onus is on them to actually use a half decent and competent courier service when handling such expensive goods.First and last item I will attempt to purchase with Amazon.com as a UK buyer, and pretty sure I'll avoid buying such high value items with Amazon in general in future.F YOU, Amazon.",2018-06-12 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,6.0,12.0,1444,257,47,8,0.0,0,2,1,0,Genuine,outside u rely amazoncom support transaction way deliverythis star doesnt represent item way didnt receive itafter receiving delivery slip door yodel people stating left safe place failed specify went two week back forth amazon item couldnt wouldnt provide detail delivery bothered investigate yodel properly find parcel gone end said would refund provided crime report however report refused local police department due item failing delivered country law state item wasnt received cannot classed potentially stolen therefore crime occurred amazon seems think theyre law audacity blame failure delivery churning old statement term condition item delivered becomes responsibility im pretty sure onus actually use half decent competent courier service handling expensive goodsfirst last item attempt purchase amazoncom uk buyer pretty sure ill avoid buying high value item amazon general futuref amazon,0.11858598717350591,0.8814140128264941,0.1441390914189568,0.2,0.7695348246970384,76.95348246970384,High Trust
