Irene,/users/5ad9fe2c4de5666d34cf4766,GB,1.0,2018-04-20 15:09:27+00:00,1.0,Amazon: sort yourselves out! No words for your shocking service.,"Shocking service. If I could give no stars, I definitely would. My partner bought a Samsung s8 from Amazon with a Third party seller called ""Power Tech"". We bought the phone knowing it could be a risk, as the reviews were not good to start with. We ordered the phone. After one day already, we received an email telling us the delivery was delayed. With a bad gut-feeling, we waited another week. One week later, the delivery was (AGAIN) being delayed another week. Patient as we are, we waited. One week later, 2 weeks after buying the phone, the delivery was once again delayed by a week. That was it, we straight away knew it was a scam. Called up Amazon's customer service and spoke to a man with an extremely strong accent. The agent told us that Power Tech had left Amazon A DAY AFTER WE'D ORDERED THE PHONE. No one decided to maybe phone up the CUSTOMERS who had PAID 500 POUNDS FOR A PRODUCT. No apologies. We simply got a refund. As I was not satisfied, we rang up again to then speak to ANOTHER agent with a very strong accent. Hard to understand and very unhelpful. After we had given our explanation, he simply asked 'whats your email address?'. No apologies, no decent manners, nothing. Amazon clearly recruits agents based upon their robotic and inhuman skills. I insisted to speaking with a manager. The ""manager"" picked up the phone. Another person who was un-understandable. He claimed that they had done everything they could to help the situation. The person I spoke to, who was clearly incapable of any managing position or satisfying a customer, did not understand my story and said: ""we refunded you so I do not understand what the issue is."". This made our blood boil even more. I decided to hang up the phone as wasting time to incapability is not something I wish to be doing all day. No issue resolved. We have spent 3 weeks waiting for a phone that was never going to come. On top of that, we spent another week waiting to be refunded. Amazon: if you claim to be a market leading website, please sort out your business and make sure you work with reliable third parties. Plus, please employ humans who 1) can speak proper English and 2) aren't socially awkward to solve a bloody issue. Sort yourselves out.",2018-04-20 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,4.0,20.0,2233,403,64,10,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,shocking service could give star definitely would partner bought samsung amazon third party seller called power tech bought phone knowing could risk review good start ordered phone one day already received email telling u delivery delayed bad gutfeeling waited another week one week later delivery delayed another week patient waited one week later week buying phone delivery delayed week straight away knew scam called amazon customer service spoke man extremely strong accent agent told u power tech left amazon day wed ordered phone one decided maybe phone customer paid pound product apology simply got refund satisfied rang speak another agent strong accent hard understand unhelpful given explanation simply asked whats email address apology decent manner nothing amazon clearly recruit agent based upon robotic inhuman skill insisted speaking manager manager picked phone another person ununderstandable claimed done everything could help situation person spoke clearly incapable managing position satisfying customer understand story said refunded understand issue made blood boil even decided hang phone wasting time incapability something wish day issue resolved spent week waiting phone never going come top spent another week waiting refunded amazon claim market leading website please sort business make sure work reliable third party plus please employ human speak proper english arent socially awkward solve bloody issue sort,0.00816502708444107,0.9918349729155589,0.22602355580482333,0.2,0.8411221976187441,84.11221976187441,