Retail shopper,/users/5aa044694de5666d342af9ae,US,5.0,2022-02-03 18:10:21+00:00,1.0,The good the bad and the ugly!,"I starting using Amazon about 2 years ago. I found myself buying more out of convenience. I'm a Prime member which is the only way I would use them due to  shipping & return policys on 3rd party sellers,trying to return items usually doesn't go well & most don't accept returns for any reasons even if it's damaged on arrival. Then they raised the price to 140$ a year!A couple of things that bothered me:#1 Reviews---They only publish positive or netural reviews. Sellers are allowed to delete your review. That's like having the fox guard the hen house! If you say anything negative they reject them. I've probably written a couple hundred or more reviews. Anytime I've said anything negative,meaning giving constructive criticism it's rejected and deleted. So, I no longer write them and do not shop as often as I did before. I was always careful & followed community guidelines when writing any reviews but as long as sellers are allowed to decide what's appropriate reviews will be untrustworthy. #2 Scammers are everywhere! I bought laundry soap from a 3rd party seller,they added water to it to make more money. The factory seal was gone. I've used that brand for decades & could tell upon opening it was tampered with. Amazon does try to get rid of these disgusting creeps, but they pop up daily mostly because Amazon's weak vetting.Amazon has let thousands of low quality 3rd party sellers use the platform which has ruined the platform. #3. Recently I noticed an e-mail thanking me for my order but I realized I never bought this item. I went to the sight,it showed I had purchased a 14$ item & paid with my CC. I never ordered that item,I never received the item I was charged for. Amazon did credit me with a full refund, BUT had I not seen this charge I would have been out this money. How could this even happen? Check your bank account. Again buyer beware.#4 Fake merchandise-- Everything from shampoos to phone charging cords. There are 10's of thousands of sellers,many selling counterfeit goods,fake products that can potentially harm. Amazon doesn't vet all the sellers properly so be careful. Scammer will offer items very cheap,you order it,they debit your bank account & you never get it. *They fake shipping tracking numbers so it looks like it's on the way so they can get paid but the merchandise never comes. Always check the seller- if they are New beware. If they have negative ratings beware. I've caught a few of them. They are shut down only to pop back up days later. **Edited Feb 2022**I continued to buy occasionally after my initial review until I was banned from leaving any reviews at all. I was black listed. That was a year ago. They deleted every single review I had ever written and sent me an e-mail claiming I had not followed community guidelines. They gave no examples. I spent alot of time and effort writing reviews of products I'd purchased going out of my way to take great pictures and give praise to the sellers who have great stuff. Not all my reviews were negative. The review system has been hijacked,no longer a system that works on Amazon. Why would Amazon delete all my hundreds of reviews? I've lowered my rating from 3 to 1 star here on trust P. I no longer use Amazon.",2018-03-09 00:00:00+00:00,2022.0,2.0,3.0,3228,570,30,7,1427.0,0,3,1,0,Genuine,starting using amazon year ago found buying convenience im prime member way would use due shipping return policy rd party sellerstrying return item usually doesnt go well dont accept return reason even damaged arrival raised price yeara couple thing bothered reviewsthey publish positive netural review seller allowed delete review thats like fox guard hen house say anything negative reject ive probably written couple hundred review anytime ive said anything negativemeaning giving constructive criticism rejected deleted longer write shop often always careful followed community guideline writing review long seller allowed decide whats appropriate review untrustworthy scammer everywhere bought laundry soap rd party sellerthey added water make money factory seal gone ive used brand decade could tell upon opening tampered amazon try get rid disgusting creep pop daily mostly amazon weak vettingamazon let thousand low quality rd party seller use platform ruined platform recently noticed email thanking order realized never bought item went sightit showed purchased item paid cc never ordered itemi never received item charged amazon credit full refund seen charge would money could even happen check bank account buyer beware fake merchandise everything shampoo phone charging cord thousand sellersmany selling counterfeit goodsfake product potentially harm amazon doesnt vet seller properly careful scammer offer item cheapyou order itthey debit bank account never get fake shipping tracking number look like way get paid merchandise never come always check seller new beware negative rating beware ive caught shut pop back day later edited feb continued buy occasionally initial review banned leaving review black listed year ago deleted every single review ever written sent email claiming followed community guideline gave example spent alot time effort writing review product id purchased going way take great picture give praise seller great stuff review negative review system hijackedno longer system work amazon would amazon delete hundred review ive lowered rating star trust p longer use amazon,4.8560297342130266e-09,0.9999999951439703,0.31968592260235557,0.2,0.8639371820924563,86.39371820924563,High Trust
