Simon,/users/5a620a970000ff000b0327bd,GB,32.0,2018-07-22 14:05:28+00:00,1.0,Beware: Amazon try to charge for items which have been returned!,"This has now happened twice. Bought some items via Amazon. An item breaks or is no good, so I return the item and get a refund. A few weeks later, Amazon then debits my card again for the item which has been returned! When I last phoned to kick off - I was told that the wrong return postage sticker had been attached - which is funny because guess who supplies the returns post stickers? You got it - Amazon! In other words, the excuse offered was complete B/S. Amazon staff are trying to get away with sticking through fraudulent bills/debits! Make sure you check your bank/card statements very carefully!",2018-02-14 00:00:00+00:00,2018.0,7.0,22.0,607,110,64,11,158.0,0,4,1,0,Genuine,happened twice bought item via amazon item break good return item get refund week later amazon debit card item returned last phoned kick told wrong return postage sticker attached funny guess supply return post sticker got amazon word excuse offered complete b amazon staff trying get away sticking fraudulent billsdebits make sure check bankcard statement carefully,0.7532179702731269,0.24678202972687313,0.06169377453729669,0.2,0.4357297697708959,43.57297697708959,Low Trust
