Michael Crouchen,/users/59e658030000ff000ad6381b,GB,3.0,2017-10-17 19:20:51+00:00,1.0,Disgusted and appalled,"I noticed a charge on my bank statement of £7.99 that said ""Amazon Digital Svc"".  The retailer locator was amazon.com. I wanted to query this so I requested a call back online and an unknown number called me. The advisor asked for the details and said that because it was from amazon.com and not amazon.co.uk she'd need to transfer me to amazon.com. The advisor at amazon.com was rude and blunt!! She asked for the amount in dollars. I explained that the payment was in £ pound sterling and she said she couldn't help me unless the amount was in US dollars. Again I explained that the payment was in £ sterling, because I live in ENGLAND!  She said I would need to speak to amazon.co.uk. After a few minutes of getting absolutely nowhere with this incompetent person, I asked to speak to a manager. She promptly put me on hold and then hung up on me. Absolutely disgusted by the phone manners and want to know how I am going to get my money back.",2017-10-17 00:00:00+00:00,2017.0,10.0,17.0,946,175,22,3,0.0,0,3,2,1,Suspicious,noticed charge bank statement £ said amazon digital svc retailer locator amazoncom wanted query requested call back online unknown number called advisor asked detail said amazoncom amazoncouk shed need transfer amazoncom advisor amazoncom rude blunt asked amount dollar explained payment £ pound sterling said couldnt help unless amount u dollar explained payment £ sterling live england said would need speak amazoncouk minute getting absolutely nowhere incompetent person asked speak manager promptly put hold hung absolutely disgusted phone manner want know going get money back,0.799932875513714,0.20006712448628605,0.0981491867638811,0.2,0.41966339959591925,41.96633995959193,Low Trust
