Marc,/users/57c454fb0000ff000a3f140b,KR,2.0,2016-08-29 16:03:58+00:00,1.0,Low prices at what cost?,"The way a company treats its employees should be factored into the buying decisions we make. The BBC Panorama documentary (and other YouTube videos) expose the inhumane working conditions at Amazon distribution centers. These modern day high tech sweatshops dehumanize workers and supervisors alike and  undoubtedly lead to physical and psychological damage.  It is high time for our governments to act before  there is a tragedy that will be compared to the Triangle shirtwaist factory fire of 1911, which claimed the lives of 146 young workers and paved the way for 20th Century labor reforms.",2016-08-29 00:00:00+00:00,2016.0,8.0,29.0,595,95,24,5,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,way company treat employee factored buying decision make bbc panorama documentary youtube video expose inhumane working condition amazon distribution center modern day high tech sweatshop dehumanize worker supervisor alike undoubtedly lead physical psychological damage high time government act tragedy compared triangle shirtwaist factory fire claimed life young worker paved way th century labor reform,0.03641122733803629,0.9635887726619637,0.0532809871003926,0.2,0.7924505837510604,79.24505837510604,High Trust
