Patrick Dolan,/users/5233398c00006400014c1e70,GB,5.0,2016-02-22 17:12:26.289000+00:00,1.0,Amazon Vs High Street,"I bought an Abus lock holder for my bicycle on Amazon. The seller stated it would fit an Abus 53 lock, which is what mine is, but it does not. I wrote a review on Amazon to warn other Amazon customers about this but Amazon refused three times to allow me to post this polite review. It also looks like I will never get my money back from either the seller or Amazon. My advice to anyone reading this is to try your best to buy the items you need from the High Street first. This way if you have any problems you, 1) don't incur postage returns cost, 2) your local high street store will be more than happy to refund it and 3) will allow you to leave a honest review on the matter on their website.  Whereas Amazon can do none of the above three, or will only do it if and when it suits their needs. So think very carefully before you decide to buy anything online, especially from Amazon.",2016-02-22 00:00:00+00:00,2016.0,2.0,22.0,893,174,21,4,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,bought abus lock holder bicycle amazon seller stated would fit abus lock mine wrote review amazon warn amazon customer amazon refused three time allow post polite review also look like never get money back either seller amazon advice anyone reading try best buy item need high street first way problem dont incur postage return cost local high street store happy refund allow leave honest review matter website whereas amazon none three suit need think carefully decide buy anything online especially amazon,0.01715019462942917,0.9828498053705709,0.0975883342680875,0.2,0.810942569538903,81.0942569538903,High Trust
