Ken Fitzpatrick,/users/557d6bc10000ff0001c5dca2,US,5.0,2015-10-08 17:48:24.352000+00:00,2.0,Are all Customer Service Agents outside the United States?,"Recently when I call Amazon customer service I cannot understand the agent that is answering the phone.  I have nothing against any other nationality, we are all human beings and must work to make a living. Amazon has every right to employ agents around the world, however they should have those agents assist the country they are from.  It makes for better communications all around.  When a customer cannot understand what an agent is trying to tell them mistakes can happen.  At one point in my conversation the agent said she would cancel my order and then correct the quantity in a new order.  This would delay the product that I purchased. I subscribe to Amazon Prime for the free quick shipping.  The last thing I need is someone changing my order because I couldn't understand what they are saying. Finally, if Amazon were to hire agents in their respective countries it would help the economy in each country and not take it away from another country. This contributes to stable employment and a sound economy for all.",2015-10-08 00:00:00+00:00,2015.0,10.0,8.0,1028,178,58,9,0.0,0,0,1,0,Genuine,recently call amazon customer service cannot understand agent answering phone nothing nationality human being must work make living amazon every right employ agent around world however agent assist country make better communication around customer cannot understand agent trying tell mistake happen one point conversation agent said would cancel order correct quantity new order would delay product purchased subscribe amazon prime free quick shipping last thing need someone changing order couldnt understand saying finally amazon hire agent respective country would help economy country take away another country contributes stable employment sound economy,0.03416534014477996,0.96583465985522,0.09983174425126191,0.4,1.1028836787778624,110.28836787778624,High Trust
