iamcool,/users/5314d4e3000064000166ea95,US,1.0,2014-03-03 19:19:17+00:00,3.0,"Free shipping is INTENTIONALLY, and unreasonably slow","It has become very obvious that Amazon intentionally delays their free shipping, probably so people upgrade shipping methods and pay more.  I just recently ordered something they have in stock sold from amazon, and was told it would ship from amazon a week(7days) later. What is up with that? Two days later I cancelled my amazon order, ordered from somewhere else(shipped same day), and still got my package delivered 3 days before amazon was to even ship it! You can read all about this on amazons own forum, hundreds of people wondering WHY amazon has become so slow past couple years.  All i can say is im not going to wait if better service is out there for basically same price, people will catch on, and go somewhere else, naturally.",2014-03-03 00:00:00+00:00,2014.0,3.0,3.0,740,130,53,7,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,become obvious amazon intentionally delay free shipping probably people upgrade shipping method pay recently ordered something stock sold amazon told would ship amazon weekday later two day later cancelled amazon order ordered somewhere elseshipped day still got package delivered day amazon even ship read amazon forum hundred people wondering amazon become slow past couple year say im going wait better service basically price people catch go somewhere else naturally,0.0650930208116259,0.9349069791883741,0.07291082445316882,0.6,1.3820356544848207,138.20356544848207,High Trust
