Mikkel Lund,/users/489cae2f0000640001004723,DK,125.0,2013-04-09 12:43:53+00:00,1.0,Pay in your own currency = robbery at high noon,"What might seem like a nice service is in fact charged at a whopping 4% premium at amazon.com. Most credit cards charge 1.5 to 2% - this is at least double. The concept is called Dynamic Currency Conversion and is entirely legal, however, it is a steep price to pay for doing the math for you. There is no limit to what the company can add onto the official exchange rate - the only rule is that they advice you of the actual exchange rate applied and the total added cost up front - which does not happen. Dear friends at Amazon, please stay honest - this isn't it ...",2013-04-09 00:00:00+00:00,2013.0,4.0,9.0,571,110,47,10,0.0,0,0,2,1,Suspicious,might seem like nice service fact charged whopping premium amazoncom credit card charge least double concept called dynamic currency conversion entirely legal however steep price pay math limit company add onto official exchange rate rule advice actual exchange rate applied total added cost front happen dear friend amazon please stay honest isnt,0.7174824714699257,0.2825175285300743,0.06169377453729669,0.2,0.45359751917249647,45.359751917249646,Low Trust
