Hefin,/users/4f36a442000064000113dc7e,GB,4.0,2012-12-10 02:44:29+00:00,5.0,Amazon.com US accepts a return from UK late!,"I live in the UK, but on a visit to the US I brought a rather expensive keyboard which on return to the UK I inspected the keybaord and found the US keyboard layout was different to the standard UK keyboard layout.  D'oh the mistake was my fault I should have checked the keyboard immediately on receipt, as should be done with all mail order goods. I looked to send the keyboard back from the UK to the US but the cost was too much.  Two months went by with the unused keyboard sitting in the box, (with me very much considering putting it on eBay), when found that I was taking a trip back to the states in  a couple of weeks. I wasn't really expecting the Amazon.com to do anything, after all I was well outside the the return time frame of 30 days, but I'd thought I'd ask. To my sheer delight customer service got back to me saying that they would accept this late return, providing it was unused and new (of course). I'm delighted with this amazing good natured and helpful customer service, willing to bend the rules for me. Thanks Amazon.com.  BTW Amazon.co.uk rocks to!",2012-12-10 00:00:00+00:00,2012.0,12.0,10.0,1083,201,44,8,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,live uk visit u brought rather expensive keyboard return uk inspected keybaord found u keyboard layout different standard uk keyboard layout doh mistake fault checked keyboard immediately receipt done mail order good looked send keyboard back uk u cost much two month went unused keyboard sitting box much considering putting ebay found taking trip back state couple week wasnt really expecting amazoncom anything well outside return time frame day id thought id ask sheer delight customer service got back saying would accept late return providing unused new course im delighted amazing good natured helpful customer service willing bend rule thanks amazoncom btw amazoncouk rock,0.13519931387480572,0.8648006861251942,0.11273135165451487,1.0,1.9549466133935,195.49466133935002,High Trust
Linda Tran,/users/50b6aca00000640001286d7b,US,5.0,2012-11-29 03:38:52+00:00,5.0,I love Amazon.com!,"I use Amazon.com when I'm shopping for prices on almost anything. If I'm searching for a good deal on a specific product, I compare prices on Amazon.com against other sources, and most of the time, Amazon.com offers it at a lower price and free shipping. I never have a problem adding stuff to my cart for the free shipping option, $25 on Amazon.com is a breeze! I've purchased kitchen stuff, electronics, pet supplies, and other random stuff. The user reviews are extremely helpful when I'm comparing products. Sometimes I use Amazon.com user reviews when I'm shopping at other stores or websites to gauge if it's worth buying. The only negative point I have about Amazon.com is the clutter on their website. It's pretty overwhelming when they have tons of products and the website has a lot going on. It's not a big problem for me though since I'm usually looking for something specific.",2012-11-29 00:00:00+00:00,2012.0,11.0,29.0,889,153,18,3,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,use amazoncom im shopping price almost anything im searching good deal specific product compare price amazoncom source time amazoncom offer lower price free shipping never problem adding stuff cart free shipping option amazoncom breeze ive purchased kitchen stuff electronics pet supply random stuff user review extremely helpful im comparing product sometimes use amazoncom user review im shopping store website gauge worth buying negative point amazoncom clutter website pretty overwhelming ton product website lot going big problem though since im usually looking something specific,0.1619491323850638,0.8380508676149362,0.08581043185642176,1.0,1.9361875201787524,193.61875201787524,High Trust
