David Bond,/users/4ff19f2100006400011c5953,GB,10.0,2012-07-02 13:48:50+00:00,2.0,"Mostly reliable, but Ooooh...","Firstly I must say that I've found Amazon to be mostly reliable, but Ooooh when they get something wrong... I recently pre-ordered a videogame from them and when it had failed to arrive by the Monday after release I phoned contacted them, only to hear that I'd have to wait the usual (11?) working days before reporting it lost. Nothing arrived so I complained again, and a replacement was finally sent. In the meantime, because it was a birthday gift, I had to buy a second copy elsewhere (from shopto.net incidentally) which was ordered at 7pm on the Monday and arrived the NEXT morning! FIVE days after the original 11-day wait the replacement arrived from Amazon, and then, a week later what I could only presume was the original order arrived, post dated well after it should have been shipped (it was a pre-order remember?), but before the replacement was posted. This of course I returned which was a simpleprocess that cost me nothing extra but was an unwanted hassle nonetheless. So WHERE had it been? WHY wasn't it posted First Class as I paid for (the time it took to get here I imagine it was sent by Airmail-pigeon post), and WHY couldn't it be tracked? SHOULD this review be on Royal Mails' site? I DON'T KNOW the answers to any of these questions, but I do know that I won't be using Amazon again anytime soon for videogames, no matter what tempting pre-order bonuses they offer.",2012-07-02 00:00:00+00:00,2012.0,7.0,2.0,1395,248,29,4,0.0,0,1,1,0,Genuine,firstly must say ive found amazon mostly reliable ooooh get something wrong recently preordered videogame failed arrive monday release phoned contacted hear id wait usual working day reporting lost nothing arrived complained replacement finally sent meantime birthday gift buy second copy elsewhere shoptonet incidentally ordered pm monday arrived next morning five day original day wait replacement arrived amazon week later could presume original order arrived post dated well shipped preorder remember replacement posted course returned simpleprocess cost nothing extra unwanted hassle nonetheless wasnt posted first class paid time took get imagine sent airmailpigeon post couldnt tracked review royal mail site dont know answer question know wont using amazon anytime soon videogames matter tempting preorder bonus offer,0.08917788535323282,0.9108221146467672,0.13909141895681434,0.4,1.0832293411147467,108.32293411147467,High Trust
